        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Nearby post card and post detail, Pantopus-authored variant · f9-curator-chip\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screens “Nearby feed post card” and “Post detail”, plus the “Pulse card” (as in the attached screenshot) and the Nearby “map card” callout. The Pulse and map cards share this data but not the card component. This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed.\n1. On posts Pantopus wrote, a “From Pantopus” chip replaces the whole identity block.\n2. A SourceCaption line goes under the body.\n3. The overflow menu gains “Why am I seeing this?”, which expands in place. (The earlier half-sheet idea is replaced by this inline expansion.)\n4. The mute action writes to the existing Feed preferences.\nReport and neighbor posts are unchanged.\n\nATTACH: the Nearby feed with a neighbor card and a system card (web 1440, web 390, iOS, Android) · post detail with the overflow menu open (web and iOS) · the Pulse card in its current host screen · the Nearby map card callout · Feed preferences.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: Web 1440x900 (left sidebar) and 390x844 (bottom tab bar). iOS 393x852: native list; overflow is a “…” button that opens a pull-down menu (UIMenu); long-press is not used. Android 412x915: Material 3 cards, a “⋮” button that opens a dropdown menu.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Nearby tab → feed card → post detail. The same variant appears on:\n- the Pulse card, in the host screen shown in its attached screenshot (host tab listed as an assumption on Notes);\n- the Nearby map card callout;\n- Saved posts;\n- a post opened from a notification deep link.\nTo open the explainer, a person taps “Why am I seeing this?” in the overflow menu, or taps the chip itself (hit area 44pt iOS / 48dp Android / 44px web). No journey in the flow spec hands anything to this card, so it must stand alone.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: It is Mon 19 Oct 2026, 6:10 PM. Maya Chen at HOME A scrolls Nearby after last night’s wind and sees a power-outage post. She wants to know whether a neighbor wrote it and, if not, whether she can hide posts like it.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Let a reader tell at a glance that Pantopus, not a neighbor, posted this, and understand exactly what muting would hide.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: The eye lands first on the “From Pantopus” chip where a face would be, second on the body, and third on the Source line. Primary action: none on the card. Inside the explainer, the one action is the “Show Pantopus posts in Nearby” toggle.\n\nCONTENT (house style fixtures; only the deltas are listed). Draw a real feed with the three card kinds stacked, not one card alone.\n- Neighbor card, unchanged: avatar, “Marcus R. · Vancouver, WA · 4h”, “Anyone else lose power around 164th? Ours came back at 11.”, “6 replies”. The location part of a neighbor’s header is the city, as in the attached screenshot, never a street.\n- Pantopus card:\n  - identity slot: chip “From Pantopus” · “2h”;\n  - body: “Clark Public Utilities reports 412 customers without power near NE 164th Ave after last night’s wind. Their current estimate for power back is 8:30 PM tonight.” (The body may name a street because it describes a place, not a person’s home.)\n  - SourceCaption: “Source: Clark Public Utilities · outage map · as of 5:45 PM ↗”, linking to the publisher’s own outage page;\n  - overflow menu: “Report” · “Mute posts from Pantopus” · “Why am I seeing this?”.\n- System card: “Online or mail voter registration for Nov 3 must arrive by Oct 26 in Washington.” Keep its existing treatment.\n- Explainer: the heading “Why am I seeing this?”, then four lines:\n  1. “Pantopus shared this from a public source. No neighbor wrote it.”\n  2. “It came from Clark Public Utilities.”\n  3. “You’re seeing it because it’s about an area near your place in Vancouver.”\n  4. “It doesn’t count as neighborhood activity in Nearby.”\n  Then the toggle row “Show Pantopus posts in Nearby” (on) with the caption under it “Turning this off hides them in the Nearby feed and map. Posts you saved stay in Saved posts.”, the text button “Report this post”, and the text button “Show less” to collapse. Line 4 appears only once Pantopus posts are actually excluded from neighborhood counts. Draw a three-line inset beside the explainer (lines 1-3) to show the variant without it.\n- Post detail (densest version):\n  - a 16:9 photo captioned “Photo: Clark Public Utilities”;\n  - the headline “Crews working to restore power along NE 164th Ave and nearby streets after overnight wind”;\n  - topic chips “Power” · “Weather”;\n  - the SourceCaption line;\n  - the overflow menu open.\n- Worst case: the source “Washington State Department of Transportation” wraps to two lines; a 6-line body truncates with the existing “More”.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\nThe Pantopus row has no avatar-plus-name shape at all. The chip replaces the whole identity block: no avatar circle, no initials disc, no reserved 40px slot and no empty space where a face would be.\n\nChip:\n- ScopeChip geometry: pill, 24pt tall, hit area 44pt iOS / 48dp Android / 44px web;\n- fill surface.sunken, label in text.strong in label type;\n- a 12pt Pantopus mark glyph in text.secondary;\n- in dark mode, the dark raised fill and dark text primary;\n- no tick, star or badge glyph; it must not look like a verification badge;\n- sits on the byline baseline and reads as a label, not a person;\n- draw it so it cannot be confused with a selected topic chip (topic chips in post detail keep their own ChoiceChip look).\n\nThe Source line is SourceCaption in a proposed “post source” variant: no ProvenanceMark, because the post is Pantopus’s summary, not a confirmed fact; the external-link glyph trails it. It sits under the body. Keep it separate from the chip: who posted and where the fact came from are two different facts.\n\nThe explainer expands inline under the chip and pushes the body down. It is four lines plus a toggle row at least 44pt tall (48dp on Android), so it doesn’t warrant a sheet, and a sheet would cover the post being explained.\n\nVariants:\n- Pulse card: the chip takes the avatar position, left of the title.\n- Map card callout: the chip, a one-line title and the SourceCaption line.\n- Reported card: a persistent caption “Reported · reviewing” under the SourceCaption line.\n- No record of who posted (older cached copies): draw the body and the time only. Show no chip, no name, no placeholder identity, and no “Why am I seeing this?” item in its overflow menu.\n- Media failed: the image box keeps its 16:9 size and shows “Photo didn’t load · Retry”.\n- Cold load: one WarmingSkeleton row for a Pantopus card: a chip-width bar, body bars and the image box, with no avatar circle.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- Tapping the chip or the overflow item toggles the explainer. It expands over 200ms and the chevron rotates. Under Reduce Motion it cross-fades. “Show less” collapses it; on web, Escape does the same as “Show less”.\n- Turning the toggle off saves to Feed preferences. What it hides: Pantopus posts in the Nearby feed and on the Nearby map. Saved posts keep them. Whether the Pulse card and the map callout are also filtered is an open question (Notes); draw them unchanged.\n- In the feed, after the mute: the card collapses in place to InlineUndo, and other Pantopus cards fade out of the feed behind it over 200ms. Focus moves to Undo. The InlineUndo row keeps the card’s scroll position; removed cards above it do not move it.\n- Choosing “Mute posts from Pantopus” in the overflow menu does the same as turning the toggle off.\n- On the Pulse card: the mute collapses that card in place to InlineUndo, with focus on Undo.\n- In post detail: the detail stays open. The toggle row is replaced in place by InlineUndo, focus moves to Undo, and the feed is filtered when the person goes back.\n- Undo stays until the person leaves the screen where the mute happened.\n- One light haptic tick when the mute is confirmed, and nothing else.\n- “Report” and “Report this post” open the existing report flow; on return the card shows “Reported · reviewing”.\n- Every action is a tap; nothing depends on swipe, long-press or hover.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: SourceCaption (proposed “post source” variant: no ProvenanceMark, because the post is Pantopus’s summary, not a confirmed fact; external-link glyph; add to the Foundations board) · InlineUndo (removed-row variant: “Posts from Pantopus are hidden in Nearby · Undo”) · InlineErrorRow (save-failed variant, for the mute write) · OfflineNotice · WarmingSkeleton (row skeleton; chip bar and image box only, no avatar circle for Pantopus cards). The chip uses ScopeChip geometry only, and its text follows the glossary term “From Pantopus”.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Card reading order: chip → time → body → Source → actions.\n- Chip: spoken label “From Pantopus, not a neighbor”, hint “Shows why you’re seeing this”, button trait, with an expanded or collapsed state (aria-expanded on web).\n- The source link is read as “Source: Clark Public Utilities, outage map, as of 5:45 PM, opens their website”.\n- The explainer is announced politely when it opens, and focus moves to its heading. “Show less” has the spoken label “Close explanation”; focus returns to the chip.\n- The toggle’s spoken label is “Show Pantopus posts in Nearby, on”, followed by its caption.\n- The mute confirmation and the error are live regions. After a mute, focus is on Undo.\n- Retry on the mute failure has the spoken label “Retry hiding posts from Pantopus”.\n- Targets: 44pt on iOS, 48dp on Android with 8dp gaps, 44px on web.\n- The chip is told apart by its shape, glyph and words, not colour.\n- At AX5, the chip and time stack, and the explainer lines wrap without truncating.\n\nCOPY: Use every string above, plus these:\n- “Turn them back on in Feed preferences.”\n- Mute failed: “We couldn’t hide posts from Pantopus. Your feed hasn’t changed. Retry”.\n- Reported: “You reported this post. We’ll review it by Mon 26 Oct (in 7 days) and tell you here.”\n- Offline, under the disabled toggle and under Report: “Changing this needs a connection.”\n- Already muted, when the post is opened from a link: the toggle shows off, with the caption “Pantopus posts are hidden in your Nearby feed.”\n\nEDGE CASES\n- Long source names wrap to two lines and never ellipsise.\n- A 6-line body truncates.\n- Many Pantopus posts in a row each carry the chip, and muting removes them all behind one undo.\n- Zero Pantopus posts: nothing changes.\n- Slow media: reserve the image box, never an avatar.\n- Offline: the toggle and Report are disabled, with reasons.\n- Rows with no author record show no chip and have no “Why am I seeing this?” item.\n- A post in Saved posts stays there after a mute and keeps its chip.\n- A household member and an owner see the same card.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of an avatar, initials disc or logo circle, put the “From Pantopus” chip where the whole identity block goes — because an avatar-plus-name shape reads as a person.\n- Instead of a blue selected-style or ticked chip, draw a neutral sunken pill with the mark glyph — because a coloured chip reads as a selected filter or an endorsement badge.\n- Instead of “Pantopus curator”, write “From Pantopus” — because “curator” is internal vocabulary readers don’t know (NN/g heuristic 2).\n- Instead of a sheet or modal for the explanation, expand four lines in place — so the post being explained stays visible.\n- Instead of a collapse button called “Hide” next to a mute toggle, write “Show less” — because “Hide” would be mistaken for the mute.\n- Instead of a guessed byline when the app doesn’t know who posted, draw no identity at all — because a placeholder could make a Pantopus post look like a neighbor’s.\n- Instead of the source as a tooltip or chip, draw a SourceCaption linking to the publisher, with its as-of time — so a reader can check the fact itself.\n- Instead of a mute that only closes the menu, or line 4 before exclusion from counts ships, save the mute to Feed preferences with InlineUndo in the card’s place, and draw the three-line variant — because every line must be literally true.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- In the three-card frame, a reader can tell which card a neighbor wrote without reading the body.\n- The chip never reads as a person, a selected filter or a badge.\n- The explainer says who posted, where it came from and why this person sees it; every line is literally true and comes with its control.\n- The reader can tell from the toggle caption exactly what muting hides and what it keeps.\n- Mute takes one tap, from the toggle or the overflow item, with undo, focus on Undo and a failure path.\n- Cached rows with no record of who posted show neither a chip, a byline nor a “Why” item.\n- The Pulse and map variants match the card.\n- No neighbor header shows a street.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f9-curator-chip · web-1440 · 01-feed-three-kinds · light: neighbor, Pantopus and system cards stacked.\n2. f9-curator-chip · ios · 02-feed-collapsed · light: the same feed on iOS, explainer collapsed, “…” overflow button visible.\n3. f9-curator-chip · ios · 03-why-expanded · light: the four lines, the toggle and its caption, Report this post, Show less, and the three-line inset.\n4. f9-curator-chip · android · 04-muted-undo · light: InlineUndo in the card’s place with focus ring on Undo, the feed re-filtered behind it.\n5. f9-curator-chip · web-1440 · 05-post-detail-overflow · light: photo, headline, topic chips, SourceCaption, overflow menu open.\n6. f9-curator-chip · web-390 · 06-feed-three-kinds · light: the three cards at 390.\n7. f9-curator-chip · android · 07-no-author-record · light: a cached row with no chip, no byline, and its overflow menu open without “Why am I seeing this?”.\n8. f9-curator-chip · ios · 08-mute-failed · light: InlineErrorRow, toggle back on.\n9. f9-curator-chip · web-390 · 09-reported-and-already-muted · light: the reported card with its review line and the persistent “Reported · reviewing” caption, and a linked post with the toggle off and its caption.\n10. f9-curator-chip · android · 10-loading-and-media-failed · light: one WarmingSkeleton Pantopus row (chip bar, body bars, image box, no avatar), one image box loading, one failed with Retry.\n11. f9-curator-chip · ios · 11-pulse-and-map-variants · light: stacked: the Pulse card in its host context (as in the attached screenshot) above the Nearby map callout over its map.\n12. f9-curator-chip · android · 12-offline · light: OfflineNotice, toggle and Report disabled with reasons.\n13. f9-curator-chip · web-1440 · 13-worst-case · light: the long source name, a truncated body, three Pantopus cards in a row.\n14. f9-curator-chip · ios · 14-ax5 · light: frame 3 at AX5.\n15. f9-curator-chip · web-1440 · 15-greyscale · light: frame 1 in greyscale.\n16. f9-curator-chip · web-1440 · 16-feed-three-kinds · dark: the dark twin of frame 1.\n17. f9-curator-chip · ios · 17-why-expanded · dark: the dark twin of frame 3.\n18. f9-curator-chip · web-1440 · 18-notes · light: Notes.\n   - Invented strings: Marcus R., his post and “6 replies”, the outage body, 412, 8:30 PM, “outage map”, 5:45 PM, the headline, the photo caption, the topic chips, Mon 26 Oct review date, “Reported · reviewing”, the WSDOT example, “Report this post”, “Show less”, “Close explanation”, the toggle caption, the already-muted caption, the new explainer lines, the Retry spoken label.\n   - Design doc says “Pantopus curator”; renamed to “From Pantopus” per the glossary; the card snapshot tests and the f9-nearby-cells-map copy must follow.\n   - Each explainer line is generated from who posted, the source feed, the real ranking reason (line 3) and the exclusion from counts, and each is enforced by code. Line 4 depends on that exclusion being live.\n   - Contract change request: SourceCaption “post source” variant, drawn without a ProvenanceMark on posts; add to the Foundations board.\n   - Assumptions: a neighbor’s header shows the city, never a street (matches f9-privacy-mirror); the Pulse card’s host tab (confirm before sending; do not move Pantopus content onto Today without confirmation); the 7-day review time needs product confirmation.\n   - Flag, do not redesign: whether the existing system card shows a human-looking byline.\n   - Open questions: Does the mute also filter the Pulse card and the map callout? Where does the reporter see the outcome of the review beyond “Reported · reviewing”?\n   - Omitted states: web and Android explainer expanded, same as iOS frame 3. List any others.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for “continue”. Turn 2: artboards 7-12, then wait for “continue”. Turn 3: artboards 13-18.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Explainer lines rewritten so they answer why this post is shown (location reason in line 3) and no longer repeat 'not a neighbor'; three-line inset kept; Notes record line 3 comes from the real ranking reason (review major).",
          "Mute scope stated in a toggle caption: hides Pantopus posts in the Nearby feed and map, Saved posts keep them; mute behaviour defined for the feed, the Pulse card and post detail; open question on filtering Pulse and the map callout (review major).",
          "Collapse control renamed 'Show less' with spoken label 'Close explanation' (review major).",
          "SourceCaption no-mark usage declared as a proposed 'post source' variant and a contract change request on Notes (review major and minor).",
          "Pulse card no longer placed on the Today tab; referenced by its attached screenshot, host tab listed as an assumption; frame 11 now stacked instead of side by side (review minors).",
          "iOS overflow is a '…' button opening a pull-down menu; long-press not used (review minor).",
          "Focus moves to Undo after a mute, scroll position kept, chip carries expanded/collapsed state (review minor).",
          "Reported copy changed to 'We'll review it by Mon 26 Oct (in 7 days) and tell you here.'; persistent 'Reported · reviewing' caption added and drawn in frame 9; 7-day time flagged for product confirmation (review minors).",
          "Rows with no author record have no 'Why am I seeing this?' item; frame 7 shows it (review minor).",
          "Notes record the 'Pantopus curator' to 'From Pantopus' rename and its downstream effects (review minor).",
          "Omitted states listed: web and Android explainer expanded (review minor).",
          "Added Retry spoken label for the mute failure and the Saved posts edge case."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f9-earn-removal",
        "name": "Earn entries removed + a calm landing for old links",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 19,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Mailbox drawer, Today status strip and old Earn links · f9-earn-removal\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of three existing designed screens: “Mailbox drawer” (the mailbox left nav on web 1440), the Today status strip (the strip at the top of the Today tab in the attached screenshot) and “Earn Wallet”. This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed:\n1. The Earn section and its row appear only for accounts that have Earn history (money available or already paid).\n2. The Today status strip loses its offers chip. For everyone without Earn history it is gone; for people with Earn history it becomes a neutral wallet chip.\n3. Old Earn links land on the Mail root with one neutral line.\n4. The wallet stays open, read-only, for people with Earn history.\n\nATTACH: the mailbox nav on web 1440 and the drawer on web 390, iOS and Android, each with its Earn section · the Today status strip with its offers chip (web Today tab; iOS; Android) · the Earn Wallet (web and iOS) · the Mail root on web 390 and iOS, including the existing mailbox-arrival pill · the existing support or contact screen.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: Web 1440x900 (left sidebar plus the mailbox nav) and 390x844 (bottom tab bar, drawer). iOS 393x852 (native drawer as in the screenshot). Android 412x915 (Material 3 navigation drawer).\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE\n- Mail tab → mailbox drawer, Earn section.\n- Today tab → the status strip at the top.\n- Old links: /app/mailbox/earn, /app/mailbox/earn/wallet and pantopus://mailbox/earn, from bookmarks, shared URLs and pushes sent before this change.\nAn old link hands over only the destination. Eligibility decides the landing:\n- An account with at least one Earn transaction that is available or paid goes to the wallet.\n- Everyone else goes to the Mail root.\n- While eligibility is unknown, the screen holds: under 1s, show nothing new; after 1s, show the Mail root with the Mail tab selected and a WarmingSkeleton row list, with no landing line and no Earn row. Then either land on the wallet or show the line.\n- A signed-out person goes through sign-in, which keeps the destination, and then continues to the same decision.\nNo journey in the flow spec passes through here.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: It is Mon 19 Oct 2026, 6:10 PM. Maya Chen at HOME A never earned anything. She taps an old September bookmark to /app/mailbox/earn. Sam Ortega, a member of HOME A, earned $18.50 this summer. He is the exception: he opens the drawer on Android and still finds his wallet.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Take the cash-Earn promise off every surface for people who never earned, without hiding money from the few who did.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS\n- Drawer: an ordinary list with nothing that looks missing.\n- Landing: the eye goes first to the Mail tab selected, second to the one neutral line, third to the mailbox list. The landing is already the Mail tab, so the only action on the line is “Hide this”.\n- Wallet: first the balance, second the history, third the footer and its one text button.\n\nCONTENT (house style fixtures; only the deltas are listed)\n- Drawer for most people: the rows in the screenshot minus the Earn section. The expected rows are Mail Day · Map · Vacation hold · Stamps · Unboxing · Vault · Records · Settings. If the screenshot differs, keep the screenshot and note the difference.\n- Drawer for someone with Earn history: the same rows, plus the section header “Earn” and the row “Earn Wallet” with the balance trailing (“$18.50” for Sam, “$0.00” for someone fully paid out).\n- Today status strip before (removed): “3 mail pieces waiting” · “Recycling and garbage tomorrow” · “2 offers available”.\n- After, most people: “3 mail pieces waiting” · “Recycling and garbage tomorrow”.\n- After, has Earn history (Sam): “3 mail pieces waiting” · “Recycling and garbage tomorrow” · “Earn Wallet · $18.50”, which opens the read-only wallet. It uses the same neutral chip style as the others: no offer count, no money glyph, no highlight.\n- Old-link landing: the Mail root with the Mail tab selected. The line is a LandingBannerSlot in the proposed “old Earn link” variant: a neutral 16pt info glyph, the sentence “Earn isn’t part of Pantopus right now. Everything else in your mailbox is where you left it.” and the trailing text button “Hide this”.\n- Wallet, read-only (Sam): title “Earn Wallet”, then:\n  - balance “$18.50”;\n  - “Mail scan bonus · Fri 14 Aug · $6.00”;\n  - “Referral bonus · Thu 2 Jul · $12.50”;\n  - footer “Your $18.50 stays in your account. Payouts are paused for now.”;\n  - one text button, “Ask about your balance”, which opens the existing support or contact screen.\n  No offers, no “earn more” and no withdraw button.\n- Wallet, fully paid out: balance “$0.00”, history rows such as “Referral bonus · Tue 9 Jun · $10.00 · Paid”, the footer “Your past Earn payments are listed here.” and no button.\n- Eligibility check failed on an old link: the Mail root with InlineErrorRow “We couldn’t check your Earn history. Retry”.\n- Worst case: a balance of “$1,204.75” with 40 history rows and the footer “Your $1,204.75 stays in your account. Payouts are paused for now.”, and a drawer with the Earn section and all 8 other rows at AX5.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\nDraw the drawer in both variants side by side, on one shared baseline grid, aligned row for row. Label them above the frames (not in the UI) “Most people” and “Has Earn history, the exception”. The rows below Earn move up by exactly one section height. Leave nothing behind:\n- no divider stranded above Settings;\n- no 48px gap;\n- no “Earn” header with nothing under it;\n- no stale badge.\n\nThe Today status strip reflows: two chips share the strip’s full width, or the native strip scrolls as the screenshot shows. There is never a hole or a ghost chip. In frame 2, draw three strips stacked, each with a visible label above it outside the UI: “Before (removed)”, “After, most people”, “After, has Earn history (Sam)”.\n\nThe landing is the ordinary Mail root. The LandingBannerSlot takes the pill geometry of the existing mailbox-arrival pill, in its position. Its sentence is text.primary with no semantic fill, never text.muted. It is not an error banner, not red and not a notice card. Exactly one banner shows: for this one landing, the old-Earn-link line ranks above mailbox arrival, and the mailbox-arrival pill waits until the next visit.\n\nThe wallet keeps its existing layout, with the history as plain rows, the footer as a caption in text.secondary, and “Ask about your balance” as a 44pt text button under the footer.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- While eligibility loads, draw the most-people drawer and the most-people strip. For an eligible person the Earn section and the wallet chip are inserted without animation once the answer arrives, and only while the drawer is closed. If the drawer is already open, the section appears the next time the drawer opens.\n- The landing line fades in once over 200ms and is static under Reduce Motion.\n- “Hide this” removes the line in place with a 150ms collapse (a cross-fade under Reduce Motion). It dismisses the line for good on this account; later old-link arrivals land on the Mail root with no line.\n- “Ask about your balance” opens the existing support or contact screen; back returns to the wallet.\n- Retry refetches in place.\n- The wallet rows are not tappable unless they already are in the screenshot.\n- No haptics.\n- The drawer opens by its menu button, and its existing edge swipe is an extra.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: LandingBannerSlot (proposed “old Earn link” variant: neutral glyph, text.primary sentence, no semantic fill, trailing action “Hide this”; ranked above mailbox arrival for this landing) · InlineErrorRow (provider-unreachable variant for the old-link check: no errorBg fill, the error hue on the glyph only, text in text.primary, Retry button; and the fail-closed rule: the Earn row renders nothing when the lookup fails) · WarmingSkeleton (Mail root row list during the old-link hold; never used for the Earn row) · OfflineNotice with FreshnessLine (offline variant).\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- The drawer is announced with its real count: 8 items for most people, 9 for someone with Earn history.\n- The landing line is a polite status message, announced once. “Hide this” has the spoken label “Hide note about Earn”.\n- Retry has the spoken label “Retry Earn history”.\n- The wallet chip on the strip is read as “Earn Wallet, 18 dollars 50 cents”.\n- Wallet reading order: balance → history, as a list read as “Mail scan bonus, Friday 14 August, 6 dollars” → footer → “Ask about your balance”. The list announces its count (2 items for Sam, 40 in the worst case).\n- Targets: 44pt on iOS, 48dp on Android with 8dp gaps, 44px on web.\n- Text contrast is 4.5:1 or better, and no state relies on colour.\n- At AX5, amounts drop below their labels, drawer rows wrap, and the landing line wraps to several lines with “Hide this” below it.\n\nCOPY: Use every string above, plus these:\n- Offline, for someone with Earn history: FreshnessLine “You’re offline · as of 5:52 PM” above the cached wallet; “Ask about your balance” is disabled with “Contacting us needs a connection.”\n- Offline, on an old link while eligibility is unknown: show the cached Mail root with FreshnessLine “You’re offline · as of 5:52 PM”, and hold the Earn line until eligibility is known.\nNo upsell, no gating copy, no “coming back”, and no promise of future earnings.\n\nEDGE CASES\n- Eligibility loading: the most-people drawer, with no skeleton row held for Earn.\n- Old link, eligibility slow: the hold described above; never a full-page spinner.\n- Lookup failed: hide the row and the wallet chip, and show no error in the drawer.\n- Offline with a cached Today payload that still carries the offers item: show no offers chip. The strip follows the eligibility answer, not the cache.\n- Long balances and 40 history rows scroll.\n- Someone whose Earn money was all paid out sees balance “$0.00”, their history, and the footer “Your past Earn payments are listed here.”\n- A household member and an owner are treated the same: eligibility belongs to the person, not the home.\n- Signed-out: sign-in, then the same landing.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a 404 or a “no longer available” page, land on the Mail root with one neutral LandingBannerSlot line — because a 404 on a link the app sent last week reads as a broken product.\n- Instead of a greyed or disabled Earn row, remove the section and close the gap — because an inert row promises something that isn’t there.\n- Instead of a skeleton row while eligibility loads, draw the drawer without Earn — because a row that flashes and vanishes looks broken.\n- Instead of “coming back soon” or “Earn has closed”, write “Earn isn’t part of Pantopus right now” — because it is true today and promises nothing.\n- Instead of hiding the wallet from everyone, or a wallet that only says payouts are paused, keep it read-only with “Ask about your balance” — because locking someone out of their own money with no next step is the worst outcome here.\n- Instead of “2 offers available” for Sam, draw “Earn Wallet · $18.50” — because nothing may invite anyone to earn, but Sam’s money must stay reachable.\n- Instead of the neutral line when the check failed, show the provider-unreachable InlineErrorRow with Retry, never a red save-failed row — because this person may hold a balance, nothing was written, and an old link never shows a red state.\n- Instead of the landing line stacked under the mailbox-arrival pill, show one banner only — because the contract never allows two banners.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- Placed side by side, the two drawers differ by exactly one section and nothing else.\n- The strip never shows an offers chip to anyone, including offline; Sam sees only the neutral wallet chip.\n- An old link never produces a 404, a red state, a full-page spinner or two banners.\n- Sam can still reach his $18.50 and has a next step, and a paid-out person can still see their history.\n- Nothing on any frame invites anyone to earn.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f9-earn-removal · web-1440 · 01-mailbox-nav-both · light: both variants side by side on one baseline grid, labelled “Most people” and “Has Earn history, the exception”.\n2. f9-earn-removal · web-1440 · 02-status-strip-before-after · light: three strips stacked with outside labels “Before (removed)”, “After, most people”, “After, has Earn history (Sam)”.\n3. f9-earn-removal · web-390 · 03-old-link-landing · light: Mail root, Mail tab selected, the old-Earn-link LandingBannerSlot with “Hide this”, no mailbox-arrival pill.\n4. f9-earn-removal · ios · 04-drawer-most-people · light: iOS drawer without Earn.\n5. f9-earn-removal · android · 05-drawer-has-history · light: Sam’s drawer with Earn Wallet $18.50.\n6. f9-earn-removal · ios · 06-wallet-read-only · light: Sam’s balance, two history rows, footer, “Ask about your balance”.\n7. f9-earn-removal · ios · 07-eligibility-loading · light: the most-people drawer, no Earn row, no skeleton.\n8. f9-earn-removal · ios · 08-old-link-holding · light: after 1s on an old link, Mail root with the Mail tab selected and a WarmingSkeleton row list, no line.\n9. f9-earn-removal · android · 09-offline-cached-strip · light: offline, the cached Today status strip with two chips and no offers chip.\n10. f9-earn-removal · web-390 · 10-check-failed-old-link · light: Mail root with the provider-unreachable InlineErrorRow and Retry, no red fill.\n11. f9-earn-removal · web-390 · 11-drawer-most-people · light: the 390 drawer without Earn.\n12. f9-earn-removal · web-390 · 12-offline-old-link · light: cached Mail root, FreshnessLine offline, no Earn line yet.\n13. f9-earn-removal · ios · 13-offline-wallet · light: Sam’s cached wallet under FreshnessLine “You’re offline · as of 5:52 PM”, “Ask about your balance” disabled with its reason.\n14. f9-earn-removal · web-1440 · 14-wallet-worst-case · light: $1,204.75 with 40 rows scrolling, its footer and button, plus an inset of the $0.00 paid-out wallet with its footer and no button.\n15. f9-earn-removal · ios · 15-ax5-landing-and-drawer · light: the landing line and the drawer with Earn at AX5.\n16. f9-earn-removal · web-1440 · 16-greyscale · light: frame 1 in greyscale.\n17. f9-earn-removal · web-1440 · 17-mailbox-nav-both · dark: the dark twin of frame 1.\n18. f9-earn-removal · ios · 18-wallet-read-only · dark: the dark twin of frame 6, with “Ask about your balance”.\n19. f9-earn-removal · web-1440 · 19-notes · light: Notes.\n   - Invented strings: “3 mail pieces waiting”, “Recycling and garbage tomorrow”, “2 offers available”, “Earn Wallet · $18.50” chip and its spoken label, the landing line, “Hide this”, “Hide note about Earn”, Sam’s $18.50 and his earnings, “Mail scan bonus · Fri 14 Aug · $6.00”, “Referral bonus · Thu 2 Jul · $12.50”, the paid-out rows, “Your $18.50 stays in your account. Payouts are paused for now.”, “Ask about your balance”, “Contacting us needs a connection.”, “Your past Earn payments are listed here.”, the check-failed line, $1,204.75, 5:52 PM.\n   - Any drawer rows that differ from the screenshot.\n   - Assumptions: “Hide this” dismissal is stored per account, server-side. “Ask about your balance” opens the existing support or contact screen.\n   - Deviations: research asked for a verb-led action back to a tab; not needed because the redirect already lands on the Mail tab, so the action is “Hide this”. The design doc keeps the inbox_offers strip item for eligible people; this design relabels it “Earn Wallet · $18.50” and routes it to the read-only wallet. The design doc specified 404 for old Earn routes; this design redirects ineligible accounts to the Mail root instead.\n   - Contract change request: LandingBannerSlot gains an “old Earn link” variant (no actor name first, text.primary, trailing “Hide this”), used on the Mail root, ranked above mailbox arrival for this landing.\n   - Engineering: the Today payload, the web mailbox nav and the iOS and Android Earn routes all gate on the same eligibility answer (an Earn transaction that is available or paid), default hidden, on both client and server. Native route entries that outlive the payload item would open a dead area. Confirm Android has the pantopus://mailbox/earn branch. The footer “Payouts are paused for now” ships only after engineering confirms the real payout status for people with a balance.\n   - Open questions: What does the eligible strip item say and where does it go (proposed above)? Does “Payouts are paused” match the real payout status?\n   - Omitted states: iOS and Android old-link landing at default size, same as frame 3; web old-link holding, same as frame 8. List any others.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for “continue”. Turn 2: artboards 7-12, then wait for “continue”. Turn 3: artboards 13-18, then wait for “continue”. Turn 4: artboard 19.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Strip for people with Earn history decided: the offers chip becomes a neutral 'Earn Wallet · $18.50' chip to the read-only wallet; drawn as a third strip in frame 2; deviation from the design doc and open question on Notes (review major).",
          "Old-link line is now a LandingBannerSlot 'old Earn link' variant with 'Hide this', ranked above mailbox arrival so only one banner shows; 'sits directly under it' removed; contract addition on Notes (review major).",
          "Wallet no longer a dead end: footer 'Your $18.50 stays in your account. Payouts are paused for now.' plus 'Ask about your balance' in frames 6, 13, 14, 18; footer gated on engineering confirmation (review major).",
          "Old-link holding state specified (nothing under 1s, then Mail root with WarmingSkeleton rows) and added as frame 8 (review minor).",
          "'Hide this' per-account server-side dismissal recorded as an assumption (review minor).",
          "Notes record why no verb-led back-to-tab action is needed (two review minors).",
          "Frame 2 strips carry outside labels 'Before (removed)', 'After, most people', 'After, has Earn history (Sam)' (review minor).",
          "Pickup string changed to 'Recycling and garbage tomorrow' per glossary and fixture (review minor).",
          "Manifest reordered: offline wallet before worst case, AX5, greyscale and dark twins; Notes last; omitted landing and holding variants listed; now 19 frames in 4 turns (review minor).",
          "ATTACH now says '(web Today tab; iOS; Android)' instead of the internal hub route; support screen added to ATTACH (review minor)."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f9-verification-promise-copy",
        "name": "Verification promise lists (one name per thing, no withdrawn fee promise)",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 20,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Verification promise lists · f9-verification-promise-copy\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of four existing designed surfaces: the \"Verify this address\" sheet (web sheet; the iOS and Android sheet drawn by f3b-verify-address-sheet), \"Verified success\" (web page; the last step of the iOS and Android verify flow), the Place file \"Proof\" row, and the \"Meet the block\" mover row. This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed.\n\nATTACH: (1) The web Verify this address sheet at 1440 and 390, with the unlock list open. (2) The web Verified success page. (3) The iOS verify flow: the unlock-list step and the final step. (4) The Android verify sheet and final step, if already drawn by f3b; otherwise the Android inline verify banner. (5) The Place file Proof row on web 390 and iOS. (6) The \"Meet the block\" mover row on web, iOS and Android. (7) The Block Founders panel on Nearby, for the rank badge and date pill shapes.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: web 1440x900 and 390x844 · iOS 393x852 · Android 412x915. On Android, the unlock list inside the f3b Verify this address sheet uses exactly the same GrantLimitList strings as web and iOS. Android also changes the mover row, the Place file Proof row and the success step. f3b draws the sheet itself; this prompt fixes its strings.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE\n- The verify sheet opens from: Place tab → Place file → Proof row → \"Verify\"; the Place dashboard verify banner; the \"Verify address\" link on any LockedActionRow; the invitation-accepted screen; and the members roster capability caption. The caller supplies the reason line in the header. Keep that line exactly as the host draws it (for Sam's household case: \"To send neighbor messages, we need to confirm you live here.\").\n- Verified success is reached three ways. On web, a correct postcard code redirects to pantopus.com/app/place?verified=1. On iOS and Android, it is the flow's last step. When a document or landlord check finishes later, a notification lands here.\n- f1-claim-receipt adds a receipt list under the success headline after a claim. When both appear, the receipt comes after the method line and before the rank. On the success frames, mark that position with a thin labelled bracket in the margin, \"Claim receipt (drawn by f1-claim-receipt)\". Draw no receipt rows.\n- The mover row sits in the Place file's mover section while the move-in date is within 60 days. The old Just Moved card on Today was merged into these Place file rows, so draw the row in the Place file, not on Today.\n- Hand-off: success leads to Nearby → Block Founders panel, where the rank, the tier and the invite allowance also live. After that, the Proof row shows how and when the address was confirmed.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Maya Chen owns HOME A, 2418 NE Larkspur Loop. She moved in Mon 28 Sep 2026 (assumed). On Mon 19 Oct 2026 at 6:10 PM, her postcard has arrived. She opens Place file → Proof, reads what verifying adds, enters the code and lands on success. Two homes on her block verified before her. Her block's Founding window opened Mon 5 Oct, had 3 of 5 slots open and closes Sun 25 Oct, so she takes slot 3. Sam Ortega is a household member who joined by invite; his address is not verified. On Mon 12 Oct he opened the sheet from the household reason header and chose the postcard, so on Mon 19 Oct his check is pending.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Wherever verification is offered, say plainly what it adds and what it doesn't. Use one name per thing (Block Founder is the rank, Founding Neighbor is the first-5 badge), and never show the withdrawn fee promise.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: On the sheet, the eye lands first on the heading \"What needs address verification\", then on the two visible rows, then on the host's existing primary action (unchanged). The first method card, Postcard code, stays fully visible above the fold at 390x844. On success, the eye lands first on \"Address verified\" and its method-and-date line, then on the rank badge, then on the existing primary action.\n\nCONTENT (fixture deltas only)\n- Maya's rank after verifying: Block Founder #3. Her tier: Founding Neighbor, slot 3 of 5.\n- Invite allowance for a new verifier with 0 converted referrals: 3 postcard invites this week. Rule: the weekly cap is 3 plus 1 for each neighbor who joins through your invite, up to 6 in total.\n- Pending example (Sam): postcard mailed Mon 12 Oct, expected Thu 22 Oct (in 3 days from Mon 19 Oct).\n- Worst case: Block Founder #148, 6 invites (3 base + 3 earned), address wrapping to two lines at 390.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\n- Unlock list on the sheet (web, iOS, Android): GrantLimitList, V4 verify-unlock variant, drawn exactly as the Foundations board defines it. Heading \"What needs address verification\". It has the five lock rows from the shared string set, no sub lines, 44pt rows, a 16pt lock glyph in text.secondary and a verb phrase in body text.primary. Two rows are visible, then the 44pt disclosure row \"and 3 more\" with a chevron. The labels are now shorter, so each row is one or two lines at default text size, never three. Every host (f3b-verify-address-sheet, f3b-invitation-decision, attestation) shows this same list.\n- Collapsed sheet: directly under the list, draw one plain text.secondary line: \"Verifying confirms you live here. It doesn't change fees or anything that's free.\" Then the host's method cards.\n- Expanded sheet, and success: below the list (on success, below the allowance row), draw an overline \"WHAT STAYS THE SAME\" and three plain text rows with no glyphs.\n- Success, top to bottom: title, address, method line, [claim receipt position], rank row, tier row (conditional), allowance row, what stays the same, actions. The rank condition, the invite formula and the Founding tier appear here, where they are granted, and never on the sheet.\n- Rank row: the SlotMeter RankBadge (squared, radius md, surface.sunken, overline \"BLOCK FOUNDER\", numeral \"#3\"), with the label \"Your rank on this block\" beside it and, under the label, the caption \"Your number is set when your address is confirmed.\" in text.secondary.\n- Tier row: a neutral pill (surface.sunken, text.strong) with no warning tint, and its caption under it. Rank and tier are never the same shape, never side by side in one sentence, and each has its own row, at least 24pt apart.\n- Founding tier rule: the tier row appears on success only when this viewer's home holds the slot. It never appears as an offer. When the window is closed or the lookup failed, draw no Founding offer anywhere. A tier the home already holds still shows on success.\n- If the rank lookup fails on success, put an InlineErrorRow in the rank slot.\n- Before/after frame: the same row at its old three-line height beside its new two-line height, with the rhythm measurements labelled. The list gets shorter, so draw it shorter.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS: \"and 3 more\" expands in place with a 200ms height change; under Reduce Motion it appears instantly. The whole Proof row is the tap target and opens the sheet. The mover row keeps its existing tap. On iOS, success plays one light haptic tick; on Android, one light confirm haptic. There are no other haptics, no confetti and no badge animation. Success announces \"Address verified\" as a status message.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED\n- GrantLimitList: V4 verify-unlock, contract strings unchanged.\n- SlotMeter: RankBadge shape and its neutral pill only; no meter is drawn on this surface.\n- FactRow for the Proof row: missing (unverified), not-at-this-tier (saved place) and known. The pending Proof row uses the FactRow known layout with the LockedActionRow pending sentence as its value and no ProvenanceMark. The verified rows use FactRow known with a FILLED ProvenanceMark (confirmed) beside the method-and-date value, and no check badge.\n- LockedActionRow: pending variant, for Sam.\n- InlineErrorRow · WarmingSkeleton (row skeleton, rank and allowance rows only) · OfflineNotice (read-only cached screen variant, with per-control reason captions).\n\nACCESSIBILITY: Reading order on success: title, address, method line, claim receipt (when present), rank, rank caption, tier, allowance, what stays the same, actions. Spoken labels: the badge reads \"Block Founder number 3 on this block\"; the pill reads \"Founding Neighbor, slot 3 of 5\"; Retry reads \"Retry block details\". The lock glyph is decorative; the list heading carries the meaning. The disclosure is a button that announces its expanded state. Disabled method cards offline stay focusable and read their reason. Targets are 44pt / 48dp / 44px. In greyscale, rank and tier differ by shape alone. At iOS AX5 and Android 200%, rows wrap past two lines, the badge stacks above its caption, and the sheet scrolls.\n\nCOPY (sentence case, identical on web, iOS and Android)\nSheet list heading (from GrantLimitList V4): \"What needs address verification\"\nSheet list, visible: \"Message your neighbors\" · \"Get a residency letter\" · disclosure \"and 3 more\"\nExpanded: \"Show your Residency Pass\" · \"Share what you pay in rent (Real Rent)\" · \"Earn a Block Founder rank\"\nCollapsed sheet line: \"Verifying confirms you live here. It doesn't change fees or anything that's free.\"\nWhat stays the same (expanded sheet and success): overline \"WHAT STAYS THE SAME\" · \"Readings, reminders and dates work the same whether or not you verify.\" · \"Verifying doesn't change any fees.\" · \"It confirms you live here. It isn't a background check.\"\nSuccess: title \"Address verified\" · \"2418 NE Larkspur Loop, Vancouver, WA 98684\" · \"Address confirmed by postcard · Mon 19 Oct 2026\" · badge + \"Your rank on this block\" / \"Your number is set when your address is confirmed.\" · pill \"Founding Neighbor · slot 3 of 5\" / \"One of the first 5 verified homes on this block.\" · \"3 postcard invites this week\" / \"Each neighbor who joins through your invite adds 1 more a week, up to 6.\" · text link \"See your block on Nearby\"\nRank failed: \"We couldn't load your block details\" + \"Retry\"\nProof row: unverified \"Verify this address to become a Block Founder here.\" + \"Verify\" · pending \"We're checking your postcard code — expected in 3 days · Thu 22 Oct\" with caption \"Postcard mailed Mon 12 Oct\" · verified \"Address confirmed by postcard · Mon 19 Oct 2026\" · confirmed by the owner \"Confirmed by Maya Chen · Mon 19 Oct 2026\" · saved place \"Claim this address first\" (grey, no action)\nSam's LockedActionRow, pending: \"We're checking your postcard code — expected in 3 days · Thu 22 Oct\" (no link)\nMover row payoff, before: \"Verify this address to become a Block Founder here.\" After: \"You're Block Founder #3 on this block.\"\nOffline: notice \"You're offline. You can still read what verifying adds.\" · reason caption under each disabled method card \"Verifying needs a connection.\"\nRemoved from every surface: \"Permanent 0% marketplace fee\", \"permanent\"/\"permanently\", \"The Nearby cells map in detail\", \"Post to your block\", \"6 postcard invites a week instead of 3\".\n\nEDGE CASES\n- Wrap the long address; never truncate it. A 3-digit rank widens the badge, and the numeral is never cut.\n- Maximum allowance: \"6 postcard invites this week\" / \"3 base + 3 from neighbors who joined\".\n- Window closed or lookup failed: no tier row on success and no Founding offer anywhere. A household member whose home already holds the slot sees no Founding offer.\n- Slow network: the title and method line render from the verify response; the rank and allowance rows show row skeletons; the tier row has no skeleton and appears only once loaded.\n- Offline: OfflineNotice \"You're offline. You can still read what verifying adds.\" above the list; the list stays readable; the method cards (Postcard code and the others) are disabled, each with the caption \"Verifying needs a connection.\" No silent dead buttons.\n- Pending (Sam): the Proof row and his LockedActionRow show the pending line and carry no Verify link, so the sheet does not reopen from them until the check resolves. If another host still opens the sheet, it shows the LockedActionRow pending line in place of the method cards.\n- Mover row: shown only while the move-in date is within 60 days (HOME A: until Fri 27 Nov with the assumed Mon 28 Sep move-in); after that the row is gone.\n- Document method: \"Address confirmed by document · Mon 19 Oct 2026\". Already verified: the sheet never opens.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of \"your permanent rank\", draw \"Your rank on this block\" plus its condition line — because a verification can lapse, and nothing yet guarantees the rank survives that.\n- Instead of showing \"#3\" before verifying, draw \"Earn a Block Founder rank\" — because the number can change before the code is entered, and the Block Founders panel shows no rank to people who haven't verified.\n- Instead of a warning-tinted countdown pill, draw a neutral pill — because the badge is a perk, not an obligation.\n- Instead of one chip shape for both names, draw the squared RankBadge and the round tier pill — because the rename only works if readers can see the difference.\n- Instead of a bare \"Verified\" or a check badge, draw the method and date with a filled ProvenanceMark — because a bare badge gets read as an endorsement.\n- Instead of sub lines, invite rows or a Founding row in the sheet list, draw the V4 five rows under \"What needs address verification\" and put those facts on success — because every host must show one identical unlock list.\n- Instead of the full what-stays-the-same block on the collapsed sheet, draw one line — because the method cards must stay above the fold.\n- Instead of padding rows back to three lines, draw the shorter two-line rows and let the list end sooner — because a shorter list is the point of the rename.\n\nDONE WHEN: No frame contains \"permanent\", \"0%\", the cells-map row or \"instead of 3\". \"Block Founder\" and \"Founding Neighbor\" never share a sentence. In greyscale, rank and tier differ by shape. Every verification mention names its method and date. Web, iOS and Android show exactly the same strings, and the sheet list matches GrantLimitList V4 exactly, heading included. No row goes past two lines at default size. The invite numbers follow 3 + 1 per converted referral, up to 6. The rank row states its condition. No viewer is offered a Founding slot their home already holds. At 390x844 the Postcard code card is fully visible on the collapsed sheet. The offline frame has no control disabled without a reason.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f9-verification-promise-copy · web-1440 · 01-verify-sheet-expanded · light: Maya, Mon 19 Oct; heading \"What needs address verification\", all five rows, the what-stays-the-same list, the method cards below.\n2. f9-verification-promise-copy · web-1440 · 02-verified-success · light: Maya's full success page with the rank row and its condition caption, tier and allowance rows, and the claim receipt bracket.\n3. f9-verification-promise-copy · web-390 · 03-verify-sheet-collapsed · light: Sam, Mon 12 Oct, before he chooses a method; reason header \"To send neighbor messages, we need to confirm you live here.\" as the host draws it, the heading, two rows plus \"and 3 more\", the one-line note, and the Postcard code card fully visible above the fold at 390x844.\n4. f9-verification-promise-copy · web-390 · 04-rhythm-before-after · light: one row at the old three-line height beside the new two-line height, measured.\n5. f9-verification-promise-copy · ios · 05-verify-sheet-expanded · light: iOS unlock-list step, expanded, same heading.\n6. f9-verification-promise-copy · ios · 06-verified-success · light: iOS final step with badge, condition caption and pill.\n7. f9-verification-promise-copy · android · 07-verify-sheet-expanded · light: Android f3b sheet with the identical expanded list.\n8. f9-verification-promise-copy · android · 08-verified-success · light: Android final step with badge, condition caption and pill.\n9. f9-verification-promise-copy · web-390 · 09-founding-closed-success · light: success with no tier row; rank and allowance unchanged.\n10. f9-verification-promise-copy · web-390 · 10-place-file-proof-rows · light: five stacked Proof rows: unverified with Verify; pending (known layout, no mark) with caption; verified by postcard with filled mark; confirmed by Maya Chen with filled mark; saved place.\n11. f9-verification-promise-copy · ios · 11-mover-row · light: \"Meet the block\" row before and after verifying, in the Place file mover section (move-in Mon 28 Sep, within 60 days).\n12. f9-verification-promise-copy · android · 12-mover-row-200pct · light: the mover row before and after, at 200% text.\n13. f9-verification-promise-copy · web-390 · 13-rank-failed · light: success with InlineErrorRow in the rank slot.\n14. f9-verification-promise-copy · web-390 · 14-slow-network · light: success with title and method line, row skeletons for rank and allowance, no tier skeleton.\n15. f9-verification-promise-copy · web-390 · 15-offline · light: sheet with OfflineNotice \"You're offline. You can still read what verifying adds.\", list readable, method cards disabled with \"Verifying needs a connection.\"\n16. f9-verification-promise-copy · ios · 16-ax5 · light: success at AX5, stacked and scrolling.\n17. f9-verification-promise-copy · web-390 · 17-greyscale · light: success in greyscale.\n18. f9-verification-promise-copy · web-1440 · 18-verify-sheet-expanded · dark: dark twin of 1.\n19. f9-verification-promise-copy · ios · 19-verified-success · dark: dark twin of 6.\n20. f9-verification-promise-copy · Notes:\n- Assumptions: HOME A move-in Mon 28 Sep 2026; Founding window Mon 5 Oct to Sun 25 Oct (21 days).\n- Every invented string: the collapsed-sheet line; the what-stays-the-same overline and rows; the pending lines \"expected in 3 days · Thu 22 Oct\" and \"Postcard mailed Mon 12 Oct\"; the rank caption \"Your number is set when your address is confirmed.\"; the allowance caption \"Each neighbor who joins through your invite adds 1 more a week, up to 6.\"; the rank-failed line; the success link; \"Confirmed by Maya Chen\"; the offline notice and \"Verifying needs a connection.\"; Sam's Mon 12 Oct timeline; plus any string you added.\n- Replaced v1 strings with reasons: \"Confirmed by postcard code\" became \"Address confirmed by postcard\"; \"stays free\" became \"work the same\"; \"and 4/5 more\" became \"and 3 more\"; the heading \"What this unlocks\" became \"What needs address verification\" to match GrantLimitList V4. Proposed change (not applied): if the founder prefers \"What this unlocks\", change prompt 00c V4 first.\n- Deviation: the pending date puts the relative count first (\"in 3 days · Thu 22 Oct\") per the house style; prompt 00c's LockedActionRow pending string uses the range \"expected Thu 22–Thu 29 Oct\". Proposed: align 00c and f3b-locked-action-row with one form.\n- \"Proposed change to the shared GrantLimitList lock set: add 'Send postcard invites' (6 rows, 'and 4 more') on every host (invitation decision, verify sheet, attestation); not applied until prompt 00 is updated.\"\n- The rank condition \"Your number is set when your address is confirmed.\" appears on success and on the Block Founders panel. The window close date \"Closes Sun 25 Oct\" moved off the sheet; it lives on the Block Founders panel and f9-founding-meter-preview.\n- Fixture conflict: prompt 00b's SlotMeter uses \"Closes Tue 27 Oct\", which is inconsistent with a 21-day window from Mon 5 Oct. Proposed change: 00b uses Sun 25 Oct.\n- Conflict: the saved-place Proof row follows the contract (\"Claim this address first\"), while x-place-file says \"Not here — this is a saved place\".\n- Build note: the copy check must cover the web, iOS and Android apps, or the native apps will keep the old names.\n- Flags for the founder: any \"free\" wording needs a pricing decision; is the Founding Neighbor tier per home or per person; which notification category carries a finished document or landlord check (one settings page has Security, the other doesn't); add \"kept even if you move\" to the rank caption only if the data model guarantees it; confirm whether posting to your block needs verification; run a confusion test on Founding Neighbor vs \"First 5 on this block\".\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for continue. Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue. Turn 3: 13-18, then wait for continue. Turn 4: 19-20.",
        "changeLog": [
          "List heading changed to GrantLimitList V4's \"What needs address verification\" in FIRST FIVE SECONDS, LAYOUT and COPY; \"What this unlocks\" is kept on Notes as a proposed 00c change (major, review).",
          "Added the rank condition caption \"Your number is set when your address is confirmed.\" under \"Your rank on this block\" on success. Notes now say it appears on both success and the Block Founders panel, and keep the \"kept even if you move\" flag (major, review).",
          "Pending strings now put the relative count first, \"expected in 3 days · Thu 22 Oct\", per house style and 00c ordering. Notes record the mismatch with 00c's range string (minor, review).",
          "Offline now reads \"You're offline. You can still read what verifying adds.\", and the method cards are disabled with the reason \"Verifying needs a connection.\" Updated in EDGE CASES, COPY, frame 15 and Notes (minor, contract OfflineNotice).",
          "The mover row now shows only while the move-in date is within 60 days, with an assumed HOME A move-in of Mon 28 Sep 2026 (minor, x-place-file).",
          "Frame 3 is now dated Sam, Mon 12 Oct, before he chooses a method, with the host reason header quoted. Added a pending edge case: no Verify link, the sheet does not reopen, and any other host shows the pending line in place of the method cards (minor, review ×2).",
          "Allowance caption now reads \"Each neighbor who joins through your invite adds 1 more a week, up to 6.\", matching the doc's cap of 3 + min(referrals, 3). Listed as invented (minor, doc §F9).",
          "Specified the FactRow treatment: the pending row uses the known layout with no ProvenanceMark, and the verified rows use the known layout with a filled ProvenanceMark and no check badge (minor, contract).",
          "Kept Sun 25 Oct as the close date and added a Notes item proposing that 00b's Tue 27 Oct fixture change to match (minor, 00b).",
          "Stated the Founding window start (Mon 5 Oct) and the 24pt rank/tier separation from 00b; all other substance unchanged."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f9-founding-meter-preview",
        "name": "Founding slots meter in the address preview (honest, fails closed)",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 19,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Founding slots meter on the preview density card, plus the sticky wall line · f9-founding-meter-preview\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed \"density card\" in the signed-out address preview (web /start; the iOS and Android preview sections) and of the existing sticky wall bar on web /start. This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed.\n\nATTACH: (1) The web /start preview with the density card, at 1440 and 390. (2) The iOS preview sections with the density card. (3) The Android preview sections with the density card. (4) The web sticky wall bar (\"Keep this address handy.\" + Continue + the share/app-download footer) at 390. (5) The web compare arrival header (/start?vs=). (6) The existing preview loading skeleton. (7) The legacy free-tiles fallback. (8) The /start form's existing offline state, if drawn.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: web 1440x900 and 390x844 · iOS 393x852 · Android 412x915. The wall line is web only: native compare links open web /start, and there is no native compare screen.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: This happens before sign-in and outside the four tabs; add no tab or nav entry. The density card sits in the preview that appears after someone types an address at pantopus.com/start and taps \"See your place\". The same preview also opens from a shared pantopus.com/start?address= link, a postcard link pantopus.com/start?r=, a tap on a share card, a friend's compare link pantopus.com/start?vs=, and the signed-out Place launch preview on iOS and Android. The previous step hands over only the typed address and, on a compare arrival, the sender's card: readings and a city, never an address. Next, on web, the wall's \"Continue\" asks for an account; the card's \"Claim this address\" is the other way forward.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Someone new, not signed in, on Mon 19 Oct 2026 at 6:10 PM, types PLACE B, 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas, WA 98607. They are not Jordan Lee, who saved PLACE B privately on Sat 10 Oct; a saved place claims nothing, so the address is still unclaimed. The block's window opened Mon 5 Oct and is on day 15 of 21: 2 slots taken, 3 open, closes Sun 25 Oct.\n- Plain arrival (frames 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 14, 15, 16, 17): the visitor came to pantopus.com/start with no vs token, so the wall reads \"Keep this address handy.\"\n- Compare arrival (frames 6 and 18): Dana (Camas, WA) sent this visitor her compare card, dated Sat 12 Sep. PLACE B is on the same block as Dana's card, so the wall reads the slot line.\n- Compare arrival, different block (frame 7): the same Dana link, but the visitor types an unclaimed address on another block, 4410 SE Cascade Dr, Vancouver, WA 98683 (invented). That block's window shows 2 of 5 open with the same close date (assumed).\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Show a Founding Neighbor slot only when the system has confirmed that one is open for this address, and show nothing when it can't confirm that.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: The eye lands first on the density line \"A few verified homes nearby\", second on the slot meter with \"3 of 5 open\", third on the forward action. On web, the sticky wall's Continue is the single filled primary. The card CTA \"Claim this address and be one of the first here\" keeps the host's existing button style exactly as the screenshot shows; do not promote it. On iOS and Android (no wall), the card CTA is the primary.\n\nCONTENT (deltas only)\n- Density, text unchanged: \"A few verified homes nearby\", level 3 of 4, plus the card's existing source line.\n- Slots: 2 taken, 3 open. 21-day window, 15 days elapsed. Closes Sun 25 Oct.\n- Frame 7 block: 3 taken, 2 open, same close date.\n- Worst cases: \"1 of 5 open\"; closing today; 5 of 5 open in a brand-new window; the typed address already holds a Founding slot or is already claimed and verified (HOME A is such a home: Maya Chen verified it at 6:10 PM and holds slot 3); the long address 4410 SE Cascade Dr, Vancouver, WA 98683 wrapping at AX5 and 200%.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\n- The card keeps its density block on top, then a divider, then the slot block, then the CTA. Each block has its own label, so the two can never merge.\n- Density glyph: replace the four filled/hollow dots with four rising bars. Reached bars are solid in text.secondary ink. Unreached bars are a short baseline tick with no outline. The glyph can then no longer be read as provenance or as slots, and the qualitative words still carry the meaning. Never print a count.\n- Slot block: the SlotMeter V1 preview-card variant, exactly as on the Foundations board: the heading \"Founding Neighbor\", the five segments, the \"3 of 5 open\" numeral to the right of the segments, the elapsed bar and the neutral date pill, then the caption. This surface sets only the values: 2 taken, 3 open, 15 of 21 days elapsed, \"Closes Sun 25 Oct\". Under the caption, add the \"What's this?\" disclosure. The numeral is the only place the count is printed. The pill has no warning tint and no relative count.\n- Dark mode (frames 17 and 18): the taken fill stays primary.600 with the Foundations dark edge; the hatch, the open-segment edges and the elapsed bar use dark text.secondary on dark base; taken segments keep at least 3:1 against dark raised.\n- Degrade:\n  - Zero slots open, the window has ended, or this address already holds a slot or is already claimed and verified: draw the density block only, with no meter, no heading, no caption and no divider. The CTA follows the host's normal state for that address (\"Claim this address\" when unclaimed; the host's claimed-address state otherwise), never \"be one of the first here\".\n  - Lookup failed: draw no density card at all, and close the gap between the neighbouring cards.\n  - Loading: use the existing whole-preview skeleton, with no shape for the density card or the meter. The whole payload arrives together, so nothing shifts.\n  - Legacy fallback (no density object): no card and no meter.\n  - Wherever something renders nothing, draw the Foundations C5 gutter annotation box at the gap.\n- Wall line (web): on a compare arrival where the typed address is on the sender's block and slots are open, the SlotMeter V3 line \"3 Founding Neighbor slots are still open on this block.\" replaces \"Keep this address handy.\". It does not stack on top of it. The benefit line \"Today and a night-before pickup reminder run on it.\", the Continue button and the footer row stay. The wall reserves scroll padding.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS: The card as a whole is not a target; only the CTA and \"What's this?\" are. \"What's this?\" expands in place in 200ms, instantly under Reduce Motion. The meter does not animate, pulse or count. The wall line changes without animation. No haptics.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: SlotMeter (V1 preview card; V3 wall line replacement) · WarmingSkeleton (existing preview skeleton; no meter shape) · InlineErrorRow (fail-closed: render nothing) · OfflineNotice (native read-only; web form-offline variant) · LandingBannerSlot (unchanged, above the compare arrival). ProvenanceMark appears only in the frame 3 specimen, as a labelled contrast row, and never on the card. Filled vs hollow appears nowhere on the card.\n\nACCESSIBILITY: Reading order: density words, heading, meter, date, caption, \"What's this?\", CTA. The meter is one element, spoken as \"Founding Neighbor slots: 3 of 5 open, closes Sunday 25 October.\" The elapsed bar is hidden from assistive tech. The density glyph is decorative, and the words carry the meaning. The open count and the closing date are printed as text beside the meter, which serves as the summary and the list. Contrast: segment edges and hatch at least 3:1 in light and dark, text at least 4.5:1. Targets are 44pt / 48dp / 44px. At iOS AX5 and Android 200%, the numeral moves below the segments, the pill wraps, and the CTA wraps. In greyscale, taken vs open reads as solid vs hatch.\n\nCOPY\nHeading: \"Founding Neighbor\" · numeral \"3 of 5 open\" · pill \"Closes Sun 25 Oct\" (on the last day, \"Closes today\")\nCaption: \"A badge — no money or fee change. You can still claim this address.\"\nDisclosure: \"What's this?\" → \"A badge for the first 5 homes on this block to verify their address. Slots count only homes that verify.\"\nCTA when open: \"Claim this address and be one of the first here\". Otherwise: \"Claim this address\" (or the host's claimed-address state). The CTA reads the same open value as the meter.\nWall, same block with slots open: \"3 Founding Neighbor slots are still open on this block.\" With one slot left: \"1 Founding Neighbor slot is still open on this block.\" All other cases: \"Keep this address handy.\"\nNever: \"You two are on the same block\", any mention of the sender, percentages, \"60% claimed\", a live clock.\n\nEDGE CASES\n- The long address wraps above the card.\n- \"1 of 5 open\": four solid segments and one hatched. A new window at 5 of 5 open is a real confirmed reading, so draw all five hatched.\n- On the closing day, the pill reads \"Closes today\" and the elapsed bar is full.\n- Typed address already holds a Founding slot, or is already claimed and verified: no meter, and the CTA follows the host's claimed-address state, never \"be one of the first here\". The wall line stays ordinary.\n- Different block: the ordinary wall. Same block with zero slots: the ordinary wall. No compare token: the wall is unchanged.\n- Slow network: the skeleton stays, and no meter shape appears.\n- Offline on native: the existing offline notice, and no card.\n- Web offline: the /start form's OfflineNotice form-offline variant, \"You're offline. We can't look up an address right now.\"; no preview, no card.\n- Signed-in viewers skip the wall; the compare header owns that case.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of filled vs hollow segments, draw solid vs hatched — because filled vs hollow means provenance everywhere in Pantopus.\n- Instead of a grey, empty or skeleton meter on failure, draw no card with the C5 annotation — because an empty meter reads as \"five open\".\n- Instead of \"closes in 6 days\" in warning amber, draw the neutral pill \"Closes Sun 25 Oct\" — because a badge must not borrow a deadline's urgency.\n- Instead of reusing the density dots as slots, draw rising bars for density and the SlotMeter segments for slots — because two quantities need two shapes.\n- Instead of \"You two are on the same block\", draw the block's slot count only — because the sender shared readings and a city, not where they live.\n- Instead of a percent bar, draw five segments with the numeral — because percentages are banned and five segments show the total.\n- Instead of a second filled button on the card on web, keep the card CTA in the host's existing style — because the wall's Continue is the one primary at the sign-up moment.\n- Instead of an open-slot offer on a home that is already claimed and verified, draw no meter and the host's claimed-address state — because nobody can take a slot that home already holds.\n\nDONE WHEN: A failed lookup shows no density card. Zero open, a closed window, or an address that already holds a slot shows no meter and no \"be one of the first here\". The CTA and the meter can never disagree. Density and slots can't be confused in greyscale in frame 16. The wall line replaces the old line, never stacks on it and never names the sender. No warning tint and no clock appear. No web frame shows two filled primary buttons. The heading and caption match SlotMeter V1 exactly, and the caption states that you can still claim this address.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f9-founding-meter-preview · web-1440 · 01-open · light: plain arrival; full preview for PLACE B with density bars, SlotMeter V1, date pill, caption, open CTA in the host style, and the wall \"Keep this address handy.\" with Continue as the only filled primary.\n2. f9-founding-meter-preview · web-390 · 02-open · light: the same plain arrival at mobile width.\n3. f9-founding-meter-preview · web-390 · 03-density-vs-slots-specimen · light: density bars and SlotMeter side by side, labelled, plus a labelled ProvenanceMark contrast row.\n4. f9-founding-meter-preview · web-390 · 04-no-slots-or-closed · light: density block only, plain \"Claim this address\", with the C5 gutter annotation at the removed slot block.\n5. f9-founding-meter-preview · web-390 · 05-lookup-failed · light: no density card; the neighbouring cards close the gap; C5 annotation between the neighbouring cards.\n6. f9-founding-meter-preview · web-390 · 06-wall-same-block · light: compare arrival from Dana, PLACE B, with the slot line replacing \"Keep this address handy.\".\n7. f9-founding-meter-preview · web-390 · 07-wall-different-block · light: compare arrival from Dana; 4410 SE Cascade Dr typed; its card shows its own meter at 2 of 5 open with the open CTA; the wall line is the ordinary \"Keep this address handy.\".\n8. f9-founding-meter-preview · web-390 · 08-loading · light: existing skeleton, no meter shape.\n9. f9-founding-meter-preview · web-390 · 09-legacy-fallback · light: free tiles, no card, C5 annotation between the neighbouring cards.\n10. f9-founding-meter-preview · web-390 · 10-edge-meters · light: three stacked cards: 1 of 5 open; 5 of 5 open; closing today with \"Closes today\" and a full elapsed bar. Below them, the wall with the singular line.\n11. f9-founding-meter-preview · ios · 11-open · light: plain arrival; iOS preview section; card CTA is primary.\n12. f9-founding-meter-preview · android · 12-open · light: plain arrival; Android preview section; card CTA is primary.\n13. f9-founding-meter-preview · android · 13-offline · light: offline notice, no card.\n14. f9-founding-meter-preview · ios · 14-ax5 · light: numeral below the segments, pill wrapped, caption and CTA wrapped.\n15. f9-founding-meter-preview · android · 15-200pct · light: the same at 200%.\n16. f9-founding-meter-preview · web-390 · 16-greyscale · light: frames 2 and 3 in greyscale, side by side.\n17. f9-founding-meter-preview · web-1440 · 17-open · dark: dark twin of 1.\n18. f9-founding-meter-preview · web-390 · 18-wall-same-block · dark: dark twin of 6 (Dana compare arrival).\n19. f9-founding-meter-preview · Notes:\n- Invented strings: the disclosure sentence, the singular wall line, \"Closes today\", the address 4410 SE Cascade Dr, Vancouver, WA 98683 and its 2 of 5 open with the same close date, plus any string you added.\n- Replaced v1 strings: the heading \"Founding Neighbor slots on this block\" became \"Founding Neighbor\", and the caption \"A badge for the first 5 homes here to verify. No fees change. You can claim this address either way.\" became the SlotMeter V1 caption. \"For the first 5 homes on this block to verify\" moved into the disclosure. If the founder prefers the longer wording, propose it as a change to 00b V1; it is not applied here.\n- The v1 disclosure sentence \"You can claim this address whether or not a slot is open.\" is covered by the visible caption \"You can still claim this address.\".\n- Deviation: \"closes {date}\" was dropped from the wall line (the contract string omits it); the date stays on the card's pill.\n- Fixture conflict: prompt 00b's SlotMeter fixture closes Tue 27 Oct, which is inconsistent with a 21-day window from Mon 5 Oct. Proposed change: 00b uses Sun 25 Oct.\n- The viewer is an anonymous visitor, not Jordan Lee, who saved PLACE B privately. HOME A is never typed by a stranger here; it appears only as the already-claimed edge case.\n- Flags for the founder: showing the line only on same-block compare arrivals itself hints that the sender lives nearby, so consider showing it on every wall where slots are open. The same-block check needs the sender's geohash-6, which the readable compare token must not carry: resolve it server-side (for example with an opaque token lookup) or drop the same-block condition. Also flag the dropped derive label \"Be one of the first verified here\" (a softer promise, rejected) and the dropped relative day count.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for continue. Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue. Turn 3: 13-18, then wait for continue. Turn 4: 19.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Frame 7 no longer previews HOME A, which Maya already claimed and holds slot 3 for. It now uses an unclaimed invented address on another block (4410 SE Cascade Dr, 2 of 5 open), listed on Notes. Added an edge case and a degrade rule: an address that already holds a slot, or is already claimed and verified, gets no meter and never shows \"be one of the first here\" (major, review ×2).",
          "Replaced the redefined slot anatomy with SlotMeter V1 exactly as on the Foundations board. This surface now sets only the values: 2 taken, 3 open, 15 of 21 days, Closes Sun 25 Oct. Removed the full-width track, the 10pt radius-sm segments, the 2px gaps and the 2px elapsed bar (major, 00b).",
          "The heading and caption now use the V1 strings \"Founding Neighbor\" and \"A badge — no money or fee change. You can still claim this address.\" The first-5 wording moved into the disclosure. Updated the spoken label, DONE WHEN and Notes (major, 00b + per-surface).",
          "Marked frames 1, 2, 11 and 12 (and the other non-compare frames) as plain /start arrivals with no vs token. Frames 6 and 18 are the Dana compare arrival (minor).",
          "Added a founder flag on Notes: the same-block check needs the sender's geohash-6, which conflicts with the readable token (minor, doc §F8).",
          "Added dark-mode ink for the hatch, edges and taken segments, with 3:1 against dark raised (minor).",
          "Frames 4, 5 and 9 now carry the Foundations C5 gutter annotation (minor, 00b C5).",
          "Renumbered the state slugs to match their manifest positions. Added a web offline edge case using the OfflineNotice form-offline variant, and an attachment for it (minor).",
          "Recorded that 00b's Tue 27 Oct close date conflicts with the Sun 25 Oct used here, and stated the window start (Mon 5 Oct). All other substance unchanged."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f8-positioning-copy",
        "name": "Positioning line and contrast line in the hero",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 17,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Positioning line and contrast line · f8-positioning-copy\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screens \"/start funnel hero\", \"Marketing homepage hero\", \"Place launch (iOS)\" and \"Place launch (Android)\", plus the link unfurl of the \"Place OG share card\". This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed.\n\nATTACH: (1) The web /start hero at 1440 and 390. (2) The /start?vs= compare arrival header at 390. (3) The marketing homepage hero at 1440. (4) The iOS Place launch. (5) The Android Place launch, and its offline state if drawn. (6) The current share card and how it unfurls in a chat. (7) The expired-compare-link banner on /start, if drawn.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: web 1440x900 and 390x844, plus a 320x568 check · iOS 393x852 · Android 412x915 · a 360px-wide link unfurl.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Web /start is signed-out and has no tab bar. On native, the Place launch is the Place tab's root for someone with no place; keep the tab bar exactly as the screenshot shows it. The marketing homepage (pantopus.com) sits outside the app shell. People arrive from a search result, from a friend's compare link pantopus.com/start?vs=, from a mailed postcard link, or cold. This is step 1 of the stranger journey. Nothing before the address field asks for an account, a location or notifications. Apart from the sender strip and the landing banner, the field is the first interactive element. Any existing header \"Sign in\" link stays but comes after the field in focus order. Next, the person types an address and taps \"See your place\", which opens the preview. A plain pantopus.com/start link also unfurls: its title uses the H1 string, and its description uses the contrast line.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Someone new to PLACE B, 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas, has never heard of Pantopus. On Mon 19 Oct 2026 at 6:10 PM they arrive cold from a search result and see the default hero. A second visitor opens Dana's compare link from a chat at the same time (frame 4).\n\nTHE ONE JOB: In two lines, say what Pantopus is and what it is not, so a stranger knows this isn't another neighborhood app.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: On the default hero, the eye lands first on the H1, second on the lede, third on the address field. The single primary action is the existing \"See your place\". The contrast line reads as a caption on the lede. On the compare arrival, the eye lands on the sender strip, then the field, then \"See your place\"; the contrast line is read last.\n\nCONTENT: The H1 is one shared string everywhere. The contrast line is one shared string everywhere. The web lede, native lede and marketing lede are listed under COPY. The marketing eyebrow, the address field, \"See your place\" and the privacy proof line stay unchanged. The compare arrival uses Dana's collapsed sender strip from the attached header, unchanged.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\n- Three type ranks stacked directly, with 8pt between the H1 and the lede and 8pt between the lede and the contrast line.\n  - H1: h1 30/36/700, text.primary, at every width. The system has no larger display size, so do not invent one.\n  - Lede: body 16/24/400, text.secondary, max 46ch.\n  - Contrast line: label size 13/18. Clause one, \"Nextdoor is what your neighbors say.\", is weight 400 in text.secondary. Clause two, \"Pantopus is what's on record about your address.\", is weight 600 in text.strong. The weight carries the contrast between the clauses, and both clauses pass 4.5:1. In dark mode, clause one uses dark text.secondary and clause two uses dark text.primary.\n- Then, unchanged: the field, \"See your place\" and the privacy line, with 16pt above the field.\n- At 640px and wider, the contrast line fits on one line. At 390 it may wrap to two lines; at 320 it wraps to two or three lines. In every case the field stays fully inside the first viewport (390x844, and 320x568).\n- Compare arrival: the contrast line moves below the field, after the privacy line, so the sender strip and the input keep the first viewport.\n- Expired-link arrival: LandingBannerSlot shows the expired-compare banner above the hero; then the ordinary hero follows, with the contrast line under the lede.\n- Marketing homepage: keep its existing serif display type and paper background (the house-style exception). Set the contrast line in the homepage's existing caption sans, with the same two weights, at 4.5:1 or better on paper.\n- Share unfurl: the contrast line travels as the link's description text under the image and title (og:description, together with the sources). The image itself carries no contrast sentence; the share card prompt (f8-og-compare-card) owns the image, og:title, og:description and og:image:alt, and this surface's unfurl strings must match it. The named unfurl title reads \"What's on record at Dana's place. Yours?\"; the anonymous one reads \"A place in Camas, WA · Yours?\". Both use the same description. Draw each unfurl as a generic, unbranded link-preview bubble (image, title, description, domain \"pantopus.com\") with no messaging-app chrome, logos or colours.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS: The lines are static text. They render with the page, with no skeleton or fade-in. Focus lands on the field; on native, only after a tap, and the keyboard never opens automatically. No haptics.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: None change. LandingBannerSlot stays above the hero on web for the expired-link banner, and the contrast line stays under the lede in that state. OfflineNotice, form-offline variant, sits below the field on native offline (frame 11). The address field, primary button and privacy line belong to the host.\n\nACCESSIBILITY: Reading order: H1 (heading level 1), lede, contrast line (one paragraph; the weight change is not announced), field, button, privacy line, then any header \"Sign in\" link. On the compare arrival: sender strip, field, button, privacy line, contrast line. Text is never truncated. At iOS AX5 and Android 200%, all three lines wrap, the page scrolls, and the field comes directly after the contrast line with nothing in between. Mobile text is never below 13px. In greyscale, the difference between the clauses still reads through weight. The unfurl image's alt text reads out the four readings with no address.\n\nCOPY (verbatim, sentence case)\nH1: \"See what's true about your address.\"\nWeb /start lede: \"Flood zone and wildfire hazard, today's air, radon, water, who represents you, and the neighbors who've proven they're real. Free, no account.\"\nNative lede: \"Your flood zone, wildfire hazard, today's air and county assessed value, plus verified homes nearby — free, no account.\"\nMarketing eyebrow: \"Your address, answered · Early access\"\nMarketing lede: \"Public records, flood and wildfire hazard, today's air, and the neighbors who've proven they're real — free, no account. Then claim it: every address has exactly one page.\"\nContrast line: \"Nextdoor is what your neighbors say. Pantopus is what's on record about your address.\"\nUnfurl title (named): \"What's on record at Dana's place. Yours?\" · unfurl title (anonymous): \"A place in Camas, WA · Yours?\" · unfurl description: \"Flood, wildfire, air and radon from FEMA, USFS, AirNow and EPA. Nextdoor is what your neighbors say. Pantopus is what's on record about your address.\"\nPlain /start unfurl: title \"See what's true about your address.\" · description \"Nextdoor is what your neighbors say. Pantopus is what's on record about your address.\"\nExpired-link banner (unchanged contract string): \"That comparison link has expired. Type an address to see your own place.\"\nNative offline (OfflineNotice form-offline): \"You're offline. We can't look up an address right now.\"\nWrite \"Nextdoor\" as plain text only: no logo, colour, link or emphasis, and no claim about Nextdoor.\n\nEDGE CASES: At 320px, the lede runs to five lines and the contrast line wraps to two or three lines; draw frame 3 at the three-line worst case, with the field still fully inside 320x568. At 1440, the contrast line is one line. On the compare arrival with an expired link, the banner shows and the ordinary hero follows. On a slow network, all text is present at first paint and only the autocomplete waits. On native offline, the hero is unchanged and OfflineNotice (form-offline) sits below the field. If the native Place launch has no assessed-value reading, drop that clause (see Notes). For signed-in viewers, the hero is unchanged.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of text.muted for clause one, draw text.secondary — because text.muted fails contrast at caption size.\n- Instead of 31/37 or 42/48 H1 sizes, draw h1 30/36 — because the system has no display size.\n- Instead of a second lede-sized paragraph, a pill or a quote block, draw one caption line under the lede — because three prose blocks push the field below the fold.\n- Instead of an us-vs-them table or a coloured \"Nextdoor\", draw one plain sentence at caption weight — because a comparison must stay a truthful description, and a loud competitor name reads as defensive.\n- Instead of \"your home's value\", draw \"county assessed value\" — because modelled values are often wrong and we show only sourced records.\n- Instead of \"Wildfire and flood risk\" or \"local risks\", draw \"flood zone and wildfire hazard\" — because those are the authorities' terms.\n- Instead of the contrast line inside the share image, draw it as the unfurl description — because text inside a preview image becomes unreadable at bubble size.\n- Instead of a real messaging app's bubble, draw a generic unbranded link preview — because the frame must not imitate another product.\n\nDONE WHEN: At 390 and 320, the field is fully visible without scrolling, including with a three-line contrast line at 320. The contrast line reads as a caption, not a paragraph. Both clauses pass 4.5:1 in light and dark. The H1 and the contrast line are identical on every platform, and each lede matches its COPY entry exactly. On the compare arrival, the contrast line sits below the field and the privacy line is visible. Nothing above the field asks for anything, and the field comes before any header link in focus order.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f8-positioning-copy · web-1440 · 01-start-hero · light: H1, lede, one-line contrast line, field, button, privacy line.\n2. f8-positioning-copy · web-390 · 02-start-hero · light: the same at mobile width, contrast line wrapped.\n3. f8-positioning-copy · web-390 · 03-narrow-320 · light: artboard size 320x568, not 390x844; contrast line at its three-line worst case, field still fully in view.\n4. f8-positioning-copy · web-390 · 04-compare-arrival · light: Dana's sender strip, field, button, privacy line, then the contrast line.\n5. f8-positioning-copy · web-1440 · 05-marketing-hero · light: homepage hero with the new marketing lede and the contrast line under it.\n6. f8-positioning-copy · ios · 06-place-launch · light: native lede and contrast line.\n7. f8-positioning-copy · android · 07-place-launch · light: the same on Android.\n8. f8-positioning-copy · web-390 · 08-link-unfurls · light: two stacked 360px generic, unbranded link-preview bubbles (image, title, description, domain \"pantopus.com\"; no messaging-app chrome, logos or colours) with the same description, one named (\"What's on record at Dana's place. Yours?\") and one anonymous (\"A place in Camas, WA · Yours?\"), plus a third, smaller plain /start unfurl.\n9. f8-positioning-copy · web-390 · 09-slow-network · light: full text at first paint, autocomplete pending.\n10. f8-positioning-copy · web-390 · 10-expired-link-banner · light: LandingBannerSlot expired-compare banner, then the ordinary hero with the contrast line under the lede.\n11. f8-positioning-copy · android · 11-offline · light: hero unchanged, OfflineNotice \"You're offline. We can't look up an address right now.\" below the field.\n12. f8-positioning-copy · ios · 12-ax5 · light: wrapped lines, field right after the contrast line.\n13. f8-positioning-copy · android · 13-200pct · light: the same at 200%.\n14. f8-positioning-copy · web-390 · 14-greyscale · light: frame 2 in greyscale.\n15. f8-positioning-copy · web-1440 · 15-start-hero · dark: dark twin of 1.\n16. f8-positioning-copy · web-390 · 16-compare-arrival · dark: dark twin of 4.\n17. f8-positioning-copy · Notes:\n- 03-narrow-320 is sized 320x568 on purpose.\n- The replaced v1 strings (old web and native ledes, the \"local risks\" marketing lede, 31/37 and 42/48 sizes, text.muted) with reasons.\n- Replaced doc string: the unfurl title \"What's true about Maya's place. Yours?\" became \"What's on record at Dana's place. Yours?\", to match the contrast line's \"on record\" and because the sender is Dana; this comes from the share card research changes.\n- The compare unfurl title, description and og:image:alt strings must match f8-og-compare-card exactly; og:image:alt reads out the four readings with no address.\n- Deviation from design doc §F8: the contrast line moves from the OG image footer to og:description (text-heavy OG image rule, Apple TN3156); the share card prompt must drop its footer line, and the founder should confirm.\n- Invented strings: the unfurl description, the plain /start unfurl pairing, plus any string you added. The time is the fixture's 6:10 PM.\n- The assessed-value dependency. The optional privacy-line wording \"No location tracking — just the address you type.\" for the founder. The share card prompt owns the image.\n- Context for the founder: naming a competitor in the hero can read as defensive and costs a line on a phone, which is why the line is caption weight and moves below the field on compare arrivals.\n- Build note: there is no shared copy file yet, so \"one string per platform\" means creating one and updating every copy (the /start page metadata, the /start H1, the marketing hero, iOS and Android Place launch), not a quick find-and-replace.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for continue. Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue. Turn 3: 13-17.",
        "changeLog": [
          "At 320 the contrast line now wraps to two or three lines, and frame 3 is drawn at the three-line worst case with the field fully inside 320x568 (minor, derive f8-7).",
          "Notes now say the unfurl title, description and og:image:alt must match f8-og-compare-card, and that alt text reads the four readings with no address. Added the alt text to ACCESSIBILITY (minor, brief).",
          "Unfurls are now drawn as generic, unbranded link-preview bubbles with no messaging-app chrome. Added a matching INSTEAD OF line (minor).",
          "Frame 3 now states its artboard size is 320x568, not 390x844, and Notes explain that the size is intentional (minor).",
          "Added an Android offline artboard using the OfflineNotice form-offline variant, and added OfflineNotice to the components. Frame count went from 16 to 17 and BATCH PLAN was rebalanced (minor).",
          "Added that any header \"Sign in\" link comes after the field in focus order, in WHERE IT LIVES, ACCESSIBILITY and DONE WHEN (minor, flows-spec).",
          "Renumbered the state slugs to match their manifest positions (09b became 10). All other substance unchanged."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "x-provenance-sheet",
        "name": "Where this fact comes from (provenance sheet + \"This isn't right\")",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": true,
        "frameCount": 38,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Where this fact comes from · x-provenance-sheet\n\nTYPE: NEW. This is the ProvenanceSheet component from the Foundations board, drawn with real payloads and every state. Draw ProvenanceMark, SourceCaption, ScopeChip, ScaleStrip and AqiBand exactly as they appear on the Foundations board. This prompt says only how this sheet uses them.\n\nATTACH: the Foundations board (prompt 00); Today with its PickupCard, FourteenDayStrip and AqiBand; Place risk details with its ScaleStrips; the compare reveal; the DateSheet. If a host is not designed yet, attach the current Today or Place screenshot from the published design system and draw only a dimmed backdrop behind the sheet.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS\n- iOS 393x852: a sheet at the medium detent (about half the screen, about 420pt). Close button top right.\n- At the iOS medium detent and default text size, these are all visible without scrolling: the mark, the value, the SourceCaption, the confidence sentence, the Covers line and the sticky foot. If a payload's content is taller than that, the sheet opens at the large detent instead. At AX sizes the sheet opens at the large detent and scrolls.\n- Android 412x915: ModalBottomSheet with a drag handle and a visible Close. Back closes it.\n- Web 390x844: a bottom sheet. Web 1440x900: a centred modal 560 wide over the dimmed host. Escape closes it.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE\nThe sheet has no tab and no URL of its own. It opens over the screen the person was reading (in Place, Today or Nearby) and closes back to it, with focus returning to the row that opened it. Ways in:\n- A DateRow on Today, in the household calendar or in the place file. The whole 56pt row is the target, and so is its \"Where this fact comes from\" custom action.\n- The FourteenDayStrip. On native apps the strip scrolls to its rows, and a row opens the sheet. Only on desktop web does a whole day cell open it.\n- The PickupCard's SourceCaption row.\n- The whole AqiBand row on Today (hit area at least 44pt).\n- A ScaleStrip row (Flood, Wildfire, Radon) in Place risk details or in the compare reveal.\n- A YearBand month row in the place file. The row is the target, not the marker.\n- The \"Your reports\" row in the place file, which opens the sheet at the report status.\n- A seeded civic or tax row.\n- Phase 2: the bill provenance block.\n- \"Where this fact comes from\" inside the DateSheet. Here the content swaps in with Back, and no second sheet stacks.\nEvery host hands over the value, its bands, the authority, the as-of time, the confidence, the source link (if any), which fact it is and the scope. The sheet shows the same authority string the host showed, and draws at once, with no loading screen. The schedule path hands on to the DateSheet (pickup kind, weekday prefilled, frequency Not set) and comes back to this sheet's receipt.\n\nWHO AND WHEN\n- Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM. Maya Chen is on Today for HOME A. The PickupCard shows \"Recycling and garbage · Tue 20 Oct\" next to a ring and the words \"City schedule, not yet confirmed\". She taps the source row to see who says so.\n- At 7:10 AM that morning she tapped the air row.\n- Jordan Lee (PLACE B) reopens the report he sent on Mon 12 Oct.\n- A signed-out viewer of Dana's compare card taps a Flood row.\n\nTHE ONE JOB\nAnswer three questions about one fact: where it came from, how sure anyone is and what it covers. Then show how to fix it or report it.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS\nThe eye lands on three things, in this order:\n1. The large mark with the value beside it.\n2. The legend, with the current word emphasised.\n3. The source, the confidence sentence and the Covers line.\nThe sticky foot always shows the fact type's action:\n- A schedule gets two outlined peer buttons of equal weight, \"Yes, Tuesday is right\" and \"Set my pickup day\" (the same pair as the PickupCard).\n- Radon gets \"Get a free test kit\".\n- A lease gets \"Edit this date\".\n- A bill gets \"Fix what we read\".\n- Anything else gets only the quiet \"This isn't right\".\n\nCONTENT\nUse the house FIXTURES. Draw one payload per frame. Every payload except P3, P7 and the compare rows carries a ScopeChip.\n- P1, on record, not confirmed (HOME A pickup). Mark: hollow.\n  - Value: \"Pickup day · Tuesday\". Detail: \"Tomorrow · Recycling and garbage\".\n  - SourceCaption: \"Waste Connections · city pickup schedule · as of Mon 19 Oct\" (identical to the PickupCard).\n  - Covers: \"The city pickup route that includes this address\".\n  - ScopeChip \"Your household\". No address line (Today already shows it).\n  - Source row: \"Waste Connections · Pickup schedule ↗\".\n- P2, official (flood). Mark: filled. ScopeChip \"Your household\".\n  - Value: \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\". SourceCaption: \"FEMA · area zone · effective Sep 2021\".\n  - Covers: \"The FEMA map area that includes this address\". Method: \"FEMA flood map, area zone\".\n  - Source row: \"FEMA flood map ↗\".\n- P3, you added (lease). Mark: tick.\n  - Value: \"Lease ends Wed 31 Mar 2027\". Detail: \"Tell your landlord in writing by Mon 1 Mar 2027\".\n  - SourceCaption: \"You · added Mon 14 Sep 2026\". Covers: \"Your household\".\n- P4, official, no link (HOME A air, drawn at 7:10 AM Mon 19 Oct). Mark: filled. ScopeChip \"Your household\".\n  - Value: \"Air quality index (AQI) 42 — Good\". Detail: \"PM2.5 · nearest monitors\".\n  - AqiBand detail: \"AQI 42 · Good · PM2.5\". SourceCaption: \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM\".\n  - Covers: \"The area around the nearest AirNow monitors\".\n  - EPA text, word for word: \"Air quality is satisfactory, and air pollution poses little or no risk.\"\n  - In place of the source row, draw the flat caption \"No public page for this reading\".\n- P4 alert (PLACE B, drawn at 4:10 PM). ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\".\n  - Value: \"AQI 118 — Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups\". AqiBand alert: \"AQI 118 · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups · PM2.5\", with the threshold rule \"Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM\". SourceCaption: \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 4:00 PM\".\n  - EPA text: \"Members of sensitive groups may experience health effects. The general public is less likely to be affected.\"\n- P5, official (radon). Mark: filled. ScopeChip \"Your household\".\n  - Value: \"Radon Zone 1 — highest potential (county)\". SourceCaption: \"EPA · county-wide · zone map as published\".\n  - Covers: \"All of Clark County\". Method: \"EPA county-level estimate\".\n  - One outbound TextActionRow: \"Get a free test kit · Washington Dept of Health ↗\".\n- P6, seeded deadline, on record, not confirmed. Mark: hollow. ScopeChip \"Your household\".\n  - Value: \"Property tax 2nd half due Mon 2 Nov\". Detail: \"in 14 days · moved from Sat 31 Oct\".\n  - SourceCaption: \"Clark County Treasurer · county-wide · as of Thu 1 Oct\". Covers: \"All of Clark County\".\n  - Source row: \"Clark County Treasurer ↗\".\n- P7, phase 2, read from your photo, now committed. Mark: tick.\n  - Value: \"Clark Public Utilities · $142.18 due Fri 23 Oct\". Detail: \"in 4 days\".\n  - SourceCaption: \"We read this from your photo · You confirmed the amount on Sat 17 Oct\".\n  - Covers: \"This bill only\".\n  - In place of a ScopeChip, the line \"You and Sam can see this bill\".\n  - Only people allowed to see bills can reach this sheet.\n- Wildfire (no frame of its own; same layout as P2). Mark: filled. Value \"Wildfire hazard potential: Moderate · 3 of 5\". SourceCaption \"USFS · modelled · 2023\". Covers \"The quarter-mile area around this address\". Five named bands Very low · Low · Moderate · High · Very high. Only reason: \"We matched the wrong spot\".\n- Worst case (PLACE B, at AX5). Mark: hollow.\n  - Value: \"Pickup day · Thursday\". SourceCaption: \"City of Camas · city pickup schedule · as of Sat 10 Oct\".\n  - ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\". Address \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas, WA 98607\" (shown because this viewer's host may not show it).\n  - Foot: \"Yes, Thursday is right\" and \"Set my pickup day\".\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\nDraw the sheet in this order, top to bottom:\n1. The title.\n2. The header row: ProvenanceMark L (56pt) at the leading edge; beside it, top-aligned, the value in h3 and one caption line of detail. The mark is visual only and is not a target.\n3. The legend, directly under the header row. Draw three ProvenanceMark M glyphs, each followed by its word: Official / On record, not confirmed / You added this. Use drawn marks, not text characters.\n   - The current item is semibold text.primary on a surface.sunken pill. The other two are text.secondary. Do not underline anything.\n   - At 393pt the legend takes two lines. At AX sizes, each item gets its own row.\n4. One SourceCaption line (authority · scope · as-of). Use \"as of\" for schedules and seeded rows, \"effective\" for FEMA, and \"observed\" for AirNow.\n5. The confidence sentence, in body text.\n6. \"Covers\" (label) with its value.\n7. The ScopeChip (and the address only when the host did not show it).\n8. The detail block for the fact type:\n   - Hazards: a ScaleStrip at detail size with every band named, and the occupied band outlined.\n     - Flood bands: Minimal (X) · 0.2% a year (shaded X) · 1% a year or more (A/V).\n     - Wildfire bands: Very low → Very high, five named.\n     - Radon bands: Zone 3 → Zone 2 → Zone 1.\n     - Then a \"Method\" label with its value.\n   - Air: AqiBand detail plus the EPA statement.\n   - Inside this sheet the ScaleStrip and AqiBand are read-only: not tappable.\n9. The source row: 44pt, with an external-link glyph. With no link, draw a flat caption that is not a target.\n10. The sticky foot: the type's action, then the quiet \"This isn't right\". It is a sticky footer with scroll padding under the content.\n\nKeep confidence and scope apart. FEMA, USFS and EPA data use the FILLED mark, and the Covers line states their limit (for USFS, the quarter-mile resolution). HOLLOW is only for facts a household can confirm (pickup, seeded deadlines). Never show a number, bar or meter for confidence.\n\nWhy it is shaped this way: this sheet replaces three older pieces: the calendar row's \"where it's from\" and dispute on event detail, the \"how we know\" captions on risk rows, and the \"we read this from a photo\" explanation on bills. It also replaces the two different \"this isn't right\" controls. Host rows already carry any caveat that changes what someone does. This sheet is the audit trail, so it states each thing once. Push is the only place a mark cannot travel, so there the caveat rides the front of the title. The schedule report and the self-fix event are what the pilot's honesty counter (\"not my schedule\" reports) reads.\n\nDegraded states:\n- No link: draw the flat caption.\n- Not on record: draw no mark and no legend. The value reads \"Not on record\" (flood: \"FEMA hasn't mapped flood hazard here\"). Draw a greyed ScaleStrip with no marker, and the SourceCaption \"FEMA flood map · checked Mon 19 Oct 2026\".\n- Stale: the same mark in text.primary at 50%, as on the Foundations board (3.39:1 on base, so it stays above 3:1). Never dim text.secondary ink. The age is carried by the FreshnessLine words \"Observed 7:00 AM · AirNow — 11 hours ago\".\n\nReport area, by fact type. Tapping \"This isn't right\" swaps in the report view. Reason pickers are single-select rows: the chosen row shows a trailing check, and the other rows show nothing. Never draw radio circles on any platform.\n- Schedule, default foot: \"Yes, Tuesday is right\" and \"Set my pickup day\", outlined peers side by side (stacked at AX5), then \"This isn't right\".\n  - \"Yes, Tuesday is right\" writes the rule in place: the ring becomes a tick, and the SourceCaption reads \"You set this · Mon 19 Oct\". It gives one light haptic, and the sheet stays open.\n- Schedule, report view:\n  - The sticky foot leads with the filled button \"Set my pickup day\". It hands off to the DateSheet with the pickup kind and weekday Tuesday prefilled, and frequency Not set. The DateSheet does not infer recycling.\n  - In the body, the checkbox \"Also tell us the city's schedule looks wrong\". Ticking it reveals the rows \"Wrong pickup day\" and \"Not my service\", and adds an outlined \"Send report\" to the foot.\n  - When the box is ticked and a reason is chosen, the filled button reads \"Set my pickup day and send report\". The DateSheet's saved status then reads \"Pickup day saved · Report sent — we'll check it and tell you here — in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" (role=status). If the report fails, the DateSheet still saves, its status reads \"Pickup day saved. We couldn't send your report · Retry\", and the reason is kept.\n  - \"Send report\" is for someone who wants to report without changing the day.\n  - After Save, reopening this sheet shows: the tick mark; value \"Pickup day · Tuesday\"; detail \"Tomorrow · Recycling and garbage\"; SourceCaption \"You set this · Mon 19 Oct\"; Covers \"Your household\"; the status \"You reported this · checking\" with \"We'll tell you here — in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\".\n- Flood and Wildfire:\n  - The body line \"Only FEMA can change this. If you think the map is wrong for your building, you can ask FEMA to review it.\" (Wildfire: \"Only USFS can change this.\")\n  - Flood only: the outbound row \"Ask FEMA to review the map (Letter of Map Amendment) ↗\".\n  - Then one row, \"We matched the wrong spot\" (Pantopus checks this one), and \"Send report\".\n  - Never promise to check the zone itself.\n- Radon: the test-kit row, then the reason \"We matched the wrong county\" and \"Send report\".\n- Air: one reason, \"This reading looks wrong\", and \"Send report\".\n- Seeded deadline: the reasons \"Wrong date\" and \"Doesn't apply to this address\", and \"Send report\".\n- You added: no report. The foot shows \"Edit this date\", which opens the DateSheet.\n- Read from your photo: no \"This isn't right\". The foot shows the text action \"Fix what we read\" (it reopens Confirm what we read) and \"View the photo\".\n\nReceipts. After a report is sent, a status block replaces the report area. Use the string for the type:\n- Schedule: \"Reported Mon 19 Oct. We'll check it against Waste Connections and tell you here — in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct.\"\n- Flood: \"Reported Mon 19 Oct. We'll check which spot we matched to this address and tell you here — in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct. Only FEMA can change the zone.\" (Wildfire: \"Only USFS\".)\n- Radon: \"Reported Mon 19 Oct. We'll check which county we matched to this address and tell you here — in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct. Only EPA can change the zone.\"\n- Air: \"Reported Mon 19 Oct. We'll look at this reading and tell you here — in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct.\"\n- Seeded deadline: \"Reported Mon 19 Oct. We'll check it against the Clark County Treasurer and tell you here — in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct.\"\nReopening shows one status string everywhere: \"You reported this · checking\", with the date line under it.\nCheck slipped (PLACE B, reported Mon 12 Oct, first due Mon 19 Oct): \"Still checking. It's taking longer than we said. New date: in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov.\"\nResolved (PLACE B, reported Mon 12 Oct), drawn as two separate frames:\n- Fixed: \"Fixed Thu 15 Oct: City of Camas moved this street to Friday routes. Your pickup day now shows Friday.\" Value \"Pickup day · Friday\", SourceCaption \"City of Camas · city pickup schedule · as of Thu 15 Oct\". Mark: still hollow (the household has not confirmed the city schedule).\n- No change: \"No change · Thu 15 Oct: City of Camas still lists Thursday for this street.\" with \"See their page ↗\". Mark: hollow.\n\nCompare entry (web-390, over the compare reveal):\n- The viewer's own live Flood row. The signed-out viewer typed 1107 NE Birchfield Ct.\n  - Draw no ScopeChip.\n  - Draw the P2 content with its ScaleStrip, the FEMA body line and the \"Ask FEMA to review the map\" row.\n  - The reason \"We matched the wrong spot\" shows the caption \"Sign in to send a report\" and the text button \"Sign in\". After sign-in, the person returns to this sheet with that reason still chosen.\n- The sender's frozen row.\n  - The header line \"Dana · Camas, WA — what's on record for this area\" and the SourceCaption \"FEMA · area zone · as of Sat 12 Sep 2026\".\n  - The filled mark, Covers, and the source row \"FEMA flood map ↗\".\n  - No report area and no ScopeChip, because this is not the viewer's address.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- \"This isn't right\" and \"Where this fact comes from\" inside the DateSheet swap the content in place and add a Back control. They never open a second sheet.\n- \"Set my pickup day\", \"Edit this date\" and \"Fix what we read\" dismiss this sheet, then present the next one. Sheets never stack.\n- \"Yes, Tuesday is right\" updates in place with no dismissal.\n- The foot is sticky at every detent, with scroll padding, so the action is always visible.\n- The source row opens a new tab on web, SFSafariViewController on iOS and a Custom Tab on Android.\n- Close is always visible. Android Back and web Escape close the sheet. Drag-to-dismiss is never the only way out.\n- The content swap is a 250ms horizontal push, matching Back navigation. With Reduce Motion it becomes a 150ms cross-fade.\n- One light haptic tick when a report sends or a pickup day is confirmed (Android: the confirm haptic), and none anywhere else.\n- The report status refreshes in place. Show nothing for the first second, then the FreshnessLine \"Updating…\" on the status line only.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED\nProvenanceSheet, ProvenanceMark (L/M/S/XS; stale in text.primary at 50%; reported), SourceCaption (including no-URL), ScopeChip, AqiBand (detail, alert, stale), ScaleStrip (detail, no data, frozen), FreshnessLine, OfflineNotice, InlineErrorRow, TextActionRow (outbound), LockedActionRow, DateRow, FourteenDayStrip, PickupCard (host), KindGlyph (specimen), DateSheet (handoff target). Reason pickers are single-select check rows, not ChoiceChip and not radio circles.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Reading order:\n  1. The title.\n  2. The value with its mark name (\"Pickup day, Tuesday, Waste Connections, on record, not confirmed\"). ProvenanceMark L is hidden from assistive tech; its name is read in this label.\n  3. The legend: one accessibility element.\n  4. The source, the confidence sentence, Covers, then the scope (\"Visible to your household\").\n  5. The detail block, the source link, then the foot actions.\n- Mark names are spoken as \"official\", \"on record, not confirmed\" and \"you added this\".\n- The legend reads: \"Key: filled disc, official; ring, on record, not confirmed; disc with tick, you added this.\"\n- AqiBand is one read-only element: \"Air quality index 42, Good, category 1 of 6. AirNow, observed 7 AM.\" The visible value spells out \"Air quality index (AQI)\" once.\n- ScaleStrip is one read-only element: \"Flood zone: Zone X, minimal flood hazard, scale Minimal to 1% a year or more. FEMA, effective September 2021. Official.\" The named bands serve as its text list.\n- Reason rows sit in a radio group (web role=radiogroup with role=radio; Android RadioButton semantics with no drawn ring; iOS selected trait). The selected state is the check plus the spoken \"selected\".\n- The report status and receipts are a polite live region (role=status).\n- Retry is labelled \"Retry sending report\".\n- Focus is trapped in the sheet, and the title is unique.\n- Targets are 44pt on iOS, 48dp on Android and 44px on web.\n- Disabled controls stay focusable and read their reason aloud.\n- Outbound links name their destination.\n\nCOPY\n- Title: \"Where this fact comes from\"\n- Labels: \"Covers\" · \"Method\"\n- Controls: \"This isn't right\" · \"Back\" · \"Close\" · \"Send report\" · \"Yes, Tuesday is right\" · \"Set my pickup day\" · \"Set my pickup day and send report\" · \"Edit this date\" · \"Fix what we read\" · \"View the photo\" · \"Sign in\"\n- Confidence sentences:\n  - P1: \"On record, not confirmed. This is the schedule for your area. Nobody in your household has confirmed it for this address yet.\"\n  - P2: \"Official. FEMA publishes this zone for the mapped area, not for one building.\"\n  - Wildfire: \"Official. USFS models hazard potential for a quarter-mile area, not for one building.\"\n  - P3: \"You added this. Only you or your household can change it.\"\n  - P4: \"Preliminary reading from AirNow, observed 7:00 AM. It hasn't had EPA's full checks yet.\" The alert uses the same sentence with 4:00 PM.\n  - P5: \"County zone from EPA. It says nothing about your home's level; only a test does.\"\n  - P6: \"On record, not confirmed. We copied this from the county and haven't checked it by hand yet.\"\n  - P7: \"You added this. We read it from your photo, and you confirmed the amount.\"\n- Failed: \"We couldn't send your report. Your answer is saved · Retry\"\n- Offline: \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\", then the reasons \"You can report this when you're back online.\", \"You can change your pickup day when you're back online.\" and \"The schedule page needs a connection.\"\n- Photo deleted: \"The photo was deleted; the bill stays\"\n\nEDGE CASES\n- AX5: the header row stacks (mark above value), pairs stack, the legend stacks, and the sheet scrolls at the large detent with the foot still sticky.\n- The largest value is the AQI 118 alert. It keeps the same layout, and its only reason is still \"This reading looks wrong\".\n- A Zone AE viewer row reads \"Zone AE — 1% chance each year (about 1 in 4 over 30 years)\", in the same layout.\n- Only one report per fact is shown: the latest.\n- A guest in HOME A sees \"Yes, Tuesday is right\" and \"Set my pickup day\" disabled, with the LockedActionRow \"Maya or Sam can change the pickup day here\". The checkbox reasons and \"Send report\" stay live.\n- P7 with the photo deleted: hide \"View the photo\" and show the caption \"The photo was deleted; the bill stays\". No dead link.\n- On a slow network, only the status line waits.\n- Offline: cached content stays. The report control, the source row, the confirm and the self-fix are disabled, each with its reason.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of an \"Unverified\" suffix or an amber chip, draw the 56pt ring and the emphasised legend word — because shape plus one word is the product-wide code, and amber reads as an error.\n- Instead of radio circles, draw check rows — because a ring means on record, not confirmed.\n- Instead of the same two reasons on every fact, draw reasons for that fact type with the self-fix first — because owners fix their own copy and authorities own their data.\n- Instead of \"Thanks — we'll check it\" or \"We'll check it against FEMA\", draw the type's dated receipt and the checking and resolved states — because a report needs a receipt, a date and an honest promise.\n- Instead of a hollow mark on FEMA, USFS or EPA data, draw it filled with a Covers line — because their limit is scope, not doubt.\n- Instead of a percentage, meter or stars, draw the confidence sentence — because a number fakes a precision nobody has.\n- Instead of a red or confirm-gated \"This isn't right\", draw a quiet text button — because reporting is routine.\n- Instead of a second sheet on top, swap the content and add Back — because stacked sheets strand screen-reader focus.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- At the iOS medium detent and default text size, someone can say who published the fact, how sure anyone is and what it covers, and can see the foot action, without scrolling. Draw frame 1 at the detent where P1 fits and print that height on the frame.\n- The sheet's authority string matches the host's exactly.\n- The schedule foot offers \"Yes, Tuesday is right\" and \"Set my pickup day\"; a ticked box plus the self-fix shows a dated receipt at once, in the DateSheet.\n- The flood view never promises to check the zone, and shows the FEMA body line with the review link.\n- The air report offers only \"This reading looks wrong\".\n- Every report ends in a dated receipt for its type that is still there when the sheet is reopened.\n- No drawn circle other than ProvenanceMark appears on the sheet.\n- The greyscale and accented columns still tell the three marks apart.\n- No frame has a dead link or a target smaller than 44pt.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 01-unconfirmed-schedule · light — P1 over Today: header row, legend, caption, confidence, Covers, sticky foot with the peer pair.\n2. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 28-confirmed-in-place · light — after \"Yes, Tuesday is right\": tick, \"You set this · Mon 19 Oct\", sheet still open.\n3. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 07-report-schedule · light — report view: box ticked, \"Wrong pickup day\" checked, filled \"Set my pickup day and send report\", outlined \"Send report\".\n4. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 26-self-fix-and-report-handoff · light — DateSheet after Save (Every other week, next recycling Tue 20 Oct) with \"Pickup day saved · Report sent — …\".\n5. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 26b-handoff-report-failed · light — the same DateSheet with \"Pickup day saved. We couldn't send your report · Retry\", reason kept.\n6. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 09-reported-checking · light — HOME A schedule receipt after \"Send report\".\n7. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 21-after-self-fix-reported · light — tick, \"You set this · Mon 19 Oct\", Covers \"Your household\", \"You reported this · checking\".\n8. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 02-official-flood · light — P2 at the large detent, with ScaleStrip and Method.\n9. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 08-report-authority-flood · light — FEMA body line, review row, \"We matched the wrong spot\" checked.\n10. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 09b-reported-flood · light — the flood receipt, ending \"Only FEMA can change the zone.\"\n11. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 04-no-link-air · light — P4 at 7:10 AM, AqiBand, flat caption.\n12. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 24-report-air-alert · light — AQI 118, threshold rule, \"Saved place · Only you\", report view with \"This reading looks wrong\".\n13. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 05-official-radon · light — P5 with ScaleStrip and the test-kit row.\n14. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 06-seeded-deadline · light — P6 report view with date reasons.\n15. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 03-you-added-lease · light — P3 with \"Edit this date\".\n16. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 20-read-from-photo · light — P7: tick, \"You and Sam can see this bill\", \"Fix what we read\", \"View the photo\".\n17. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 11-check-slipped · light — PLACE B, \"Still checking…\" with the new date.\n18. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 10-resolved-fixed · light — PLACE B, Friday, hollow mark, fixed status.\n19. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 10b-resolved-no-change · light — PLACE B, Thursday, hollow mark, \"See their page ↗\".\n20. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 14-opened-from-date-sheet · light — content swap with Back inside the DateSheet.\n21. x-provenance-sheet · web-390 · 22-compare-own-row · light — the viewer's live flood row, review row, sign-in caption.\n22. x-provenance-sheet · web-390 · 23-compare-frozen-row · light — Dana's row, \"as of Sat 12 Sep 2026\", no report area.\n23. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 27-guest-locked · light — guest view: confirm and self-fix disabled, LockedActionRow.\n24. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 18-not-on-record · light — no mark, \"FEMA hasn't mapped flood hazard here\", greyed track.\n25. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 19-status-loading · light — cached content with \"Updating…\" on the status line only.\n26. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 12-report-failed · light — InlineErrorRow, reason kept, self-fix live.\n27. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 13-offline · light — cached P1, controls disabled with reasons.\n28. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 25-stale-air · light — HOME A air at 6:10 PM: mark in text.primary at 50%, \"— 11 hours ago\".\n29. x-provenance-sheet · android · 01-unconfirmed-schedule · light — ModalBottomSheet with sticky foot.\n30. x-provenance-sheet · android · 07-report-schedule · light — single-select rows with check, and checkbox.\n31. x-provenance-sheet · web-1440 · 01-unconfirmed-schedule · light — 560 modal over Today.\n32. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 15-ax5 · light — worst case (PLACE B), stacked header and legend, large detent, sticky foot.\n33. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 16-greyscale · light — frame 11 (air, AqiBand) in greyscale; the separators and printed category name carry meaning.\n34. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 17-marks-in-context · light — copied from the Foundations board.\n    - Columns: light, accented widget, greyscale.\n    - Rows: XS 12pt in a FourteenDayStrip cell, S 16pt in a DateRow, M 24pt legend, L 56pt, the PickupCard source row, a widget glyph, 28px on an OG card, and an AX5 row.\n    - Hit-area overlays show the row or cell as the target. The tick stays knocked out.\n    - Caption: \"Marks are visual only. Below 12pt no mark is drawn; the row prints the words instead.\"\n35. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 17-marks-in-context · dark — the same board.\n36. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 01-unconfirmed-schedule · dark — dark twin.\n37. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 04-no-link-air · dark — dark twin; check the AQI keyline.\n38. x-provenance-sheet · ios · 99-notes · light — Notes:\n    - Every invented string: the Covers values, Method values, \"as of Thu 1 Oct\", \"zone map as published\", \"USFS · modelled · 2023\", the Wildfire confidence and Covers, the P7 sentence, the Sign-in caption, the offline reasons, the guest persona and \"Maya or Sam can change the pickup day here\", every receipt string, the combined DateSheet statuses, the FEMA/USFS body lines and the review row wording, the resolved texts, \"The photo was deleted; the bill stays\", the 7:10 AM and 4:10 PM draw times, and the EPA sensitive-groups statement (to verify).\n    - The city seed names both bins for Tue 20 Oct, but the DateSheet starts frequency at Not set and does not infer recycling. Frames 4 and 7 assume Maya chose Every other week with next recycling Tue 20 Oct.\n    - Frames 18 and 19 are alternatives; only frame 18 moves PLACE B to Friday. Everywhere else the fixture's Thursday holds. Frame 17 assumes Jordan's check was first due Mon 19 Oct.\n    - The P4 alert assumes Jordan chose the 101 threshold; the settings default is 151.\n    - Both schedule reasons are tagged not_my_schedule for the honesty counter.\n    - \"Get a free test kit · Washington Dept of Health ↗\" deliberately replaces the contract's \"Free test kits\" wording (verb-led, per the research change).\n    - Contract clarification: the stale mark is text.primary at 50%, never text.secondary at 50%, so it stays at 3:1 or better.\n    - Reason rows use check rows, not radio rings (circles are reserved for ProvenanceMark).\n    - The report service does not exist yet; its states are drawn anyway.\n    - The measured height of frame 1 and whether P1 fits the medium detent.\n    - \"Open: whether Change pickup day opens the DateSheet directly (contract) or this sheet first (the pickup loop). Drawn here: only the SourceCaption entry.\"\n    - \"Open: does a self-fix without the ticked box count as a not-my-schedule report?\"\n    - Omitted states: web-390 air, a separate Wildfire frame (same layout as flood), and Android 200% (covered by iOS AX5).\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 2: 7-12, then wait.\nTurn 3: 13-18, then wait.\nTurn 4: 19-24, then wait.\nTurn 5: 25-30, then wait.\nTurn 6: 31-36, then wait.\nTurn 7: 37-38.",
        "changeLog": [
          "P1 authority unified with the host PickupCard and Foundations crop: SourceCaption 'Waste Connections · city pickup schedule · as of Mon 19 Oct'; source row and receipt stay Waste Connections; spoken label updated (review major 1; supersedes the minor 'City of Vancouver (Waste Connections)' suggestion, which conflicted).",
          "P1 detail now 'Tomorrow · Recycling and garbage' (matches fixture and host; 'Tomorrow' stands alone); DateSheet does not infer recycling; frames 4/7 assume Every other week, next Tue 20 Oct, listed on Notes (review major 1 + minor date format; the 'P1 omits recycling' note was dropped as it conflicts with the major fix).",
          "PLACE B worst case and resolved captions now use the Foundations string 'City of Camas · city pickup schedule · as of …'.",
          "Reason pickers are single-select check rows on all platforms with radiogroup semantics and no drawn ring; Android artboard renamed; INSTEAD OF line added (review major 2, Foundations B8).",
          "Added a dated receipt string for every report type (schedule, flood, wildfire, radon, air, seeded deadline) with no promise to check FEMA/EPA designations; added artboard 09b-reported-flood (review major 3).",
          "Fold rule fixed: mark L moved into a header row beside the value; ScopeChip/address moved below Covers and address dropped when the host shows it; sticky foot with scroll padding; large detent when content is taller; frame 1 height printed and recorded on Notes (review major 4).",
          "Combined self-fix + report path: button reads 'Set my pickup day and send report'; DateSheet shows combined saved/reported status and a failed variant; new artboards 26 and 26b (review major 5).",
          "Schedule default foot now has peer buttons 'Yes, Tuesday is right' / 'Set my pickup day' with in-place confirm (ring to tick, 'You set this · Mon 19 Oct', light haptic); new artboard 28-confirmed-in-place; FIRST FIVE SECONDS updated; guest variant disables confirm too.",
          "Dates reordered to house pattern ('in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct', 'in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov'); 'Updated' replaced with 'as of' / 'effective' / 'observed'.",
          "Added Wildfire (USFS) payload: filled mark, value, caption, quarter-mile Covers, five bands, confidence sentence, reason and receipt; listed on Notes.",
          "P4 and alert now have h3 value lines, with 'Air quality index (AQI)' spelled out in visible copy.",
          "P2, P4, P5, P6 carry ScopeChip 'Your household'; P5 caption gains an as-of ('zone map as published').",
          "Flood body line rewritten in plain words; outbound row now 'Ask FEMA to review the map (Letter of Map Amendment) ↗'.",
          "Resolved states split into separate artboards (10-resolved-fixed, 10b-resolved-no-change) with the hollow mark stated; slipped check split out (11-check-slipped); reported status unified to 'You reported this · checking'.",
          "Stale mark specified as text.primary at 50% per Foundations B7 (stays ≥3:1); recorded as a contract clarification on Notes.",
          "Accessibility: L mark hidden from AT; ScaleStrip/AqiBand read-only inside the sheet; Retry labelled 'Retry sending report'; offline self-fix reason added; sign-in returns with reason kept.",
          "Greyscale artboard now uses the air (AqiBand) frame.",
          "Restored the merge acknowledgement (F12 dispute, F8 captions, F10 photo explanation, two old report controls) and the push-exception reasoning.",
          "Added photo-deleted edge case for P7 (no dead 'View the photo').",
          "Notes additions: invented guest persona, 101 vs 151 threshold assumption, not_my_schedule tagging of both schedule reasons, deliberate radon test-kit wording, frame 17 check-by assumption, measured frame 1 height.",
          "Artboards grew from 32 to 38; batch plan rebalanced to 7 turns of at most 6."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "x-date-sheet",
        "name": "The Date sheet (one sheet, three modes, ten kinds)",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": true,
        "frameCount": 34,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: The Date sheet · x-date-sheet\n\nTYPE: NEW. This one sheet replaces seven: add a date, pickup quick-set, the pickup editor, the voter step sheet, the date detail sheet, the remove-date confirm, and the reminder picker. Draw ONE component, DateSheet. The mode (create / view-mine / view-seeded) and the kind change the body. Scope decides only whether the visibility choice appears.\n- At a saved place there is no choice, and the footer always reads 'Only you will see this.'\n- At a home, for kinds other than Bill and the seeded kinds, the footer sentence and the saved message follow the selected chip. With Only you selected, they read 'Only you will see this.' and 'Saved to your calendar. Only you.' With Household selected, they read 'Everyone in this household will see this.' and 'Saved to your household calendar.' A new date at a home starts on Only you.\n- Bill at a home shows no visibility chips. Its footer names the people who can see it: 'You and Sam can see this bill.' Never write 'Everyone in this household' on a bill.\n- Seeded kinds (voter registration, property-tax appeal, property-tax due) never show visibility chips. The mailing date, plan and reminders a person enters are Only you, so their footer reads 'Only you will see this.'\n\nATTACH: screenshots of the place file (Dates section), Today with the 14-day strip and the pickup card, the provenance sheet ('Where this fact comes from'), and the Foundations board from prompt 00. In every frame, draw the host dimmed behind the sheet exactly as it appears in its screenshot.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS\n- iOS 393x852: a .sheet at the large detent.\n  - Header control: in create mode, and in view-mine once something has been edited, the header shows a leading 'Cancel' and Save sits in the sticky footer. In view-seeded, and in view-mine with no edits, the header shows 'Done'.\n  - When a Back control is present, Back is leading and Cancel/Done moves to the trailing edge. Arriving from the provenance sheet, the sheet grows from the medium to the large detent with a cross-fade.\n  - The date field is the compact date pill. Tapping it opens the system calendar with its month/year jump. That is a system control, not a second sheet.\n- Android 412x915: a Material 3 ModalBottomSheet with a close (X) icon button labelled 'Close' at the top start.\n  - For Lease ends, Notice deadline, Insurance renews and Warranty ends, embed the M3 DatePicker inside the sheet in Input display mode. It is an outlined text field 'MM/DD/YYYY' with a trailing calendar-toggle icon button (48dp, labelled 'Switch to calendar').\n  - All other kinds, including Next recycling, use the inline calendar mode with the same input toggle. The calendar always expands inline inside the sheet and is never a dialog.\n- Web 1440x900: a right-side SlidePanel, 480 wide, over the place file. Web 390x844: a bottom sheet. Both use a typeable date input and put the same Cancel/Done text button at the top right.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE\nThe sheet opens over Place (the place file) or Today. It never has a route of its own. Entry points:\n- Place file: a missing-fact row such as 'When does your lease end?' opens create mode with that kind already picked. A known-fact row opens view-mine.\n- Place file: the mover row for voter registration leads to the civic registration block. The F8 seasonal headline goes there too: /app/place/civic?focus=registration or pantopus://place/{homeId}/civic.\n- Civic registration block: 'Remind me', or the deadline row, opens view-seeded voter registration. 'Check or update at VoteWA ↗' stays outbound, both in the block and in this sheet.\n- Today: the '+ Add a date' row at the foot of the 14-day strip opens create mode with no kind picked. A strip list row opens view-mine or view-seeded. Strip cells are not targets.\n- Today pickup card: 'Change pickup day' and the no-rule line 'Set your pickup day' open the Pickup day kind with the city weekday already selected, so one tap on Save confirms it. FirstWeekRow 'Next: set your pickup day →' does the same.\n- Settings > Notifications: the pickup status row opens the Pickup day kind the same way.\n- Provenance sheet: 'Not my schedule', then 'Set my pickup day', replaces the provenance sheet's content with this sheet and adds a header Back control, '‹ Where this fact comes from'. The two sheets never stack.\n- Household calendar: its rows are read-only there, so editing opens this sheet.\n- Mail: with no claimed home, 'Mail snap needs a claimed address' opens the Bill kind as plain manual entry.\n- Reminder push: the app lands on the date's row (the strip list row if the date is within 14 days, otherwise the place file Dates row). The row is highlighted and takes focus, then view-mine opens. A bill reminder lands on the bill's row. Web: /app/place/today?rule=cal_7f3a2 (home) or /app/today?rule=cal_7f3a2 (saved place). Native: pantopus://place/today?rule=cal_7f3a2.\n- Create links: web /app/place/today?add=date&kind=lease_end at a home and /app/today?add=date at a saved place. Native pantopus://place/today?add=date and pantopus://place/today?add=date&kind=lease_end.\nHanded over from the caller: the scope (home or saved place), any preselected kind, and the rule id.\nHanded on after saving:\n- The sheet returns the person to where they came from. The calling row updates in place with the ProvenanceMark you-added.\n- The pickup card shows 'You · Thursday' with no caveat. The FirstWeekRow advances, and the widget snapshot is rewritten.\n- 'I did this' on voter registration also ticks the place file mover row 'Update your voter registration' as you-added. That tick stays Only you. Undo un-ticks it.\n- On native only: if notification permission was never asked and this is the first pickup day saved, the sheet closes and then the notification primer opens. The two are never stacked, and the primer never opens after a failed save. If permission was already granted or denied, nothing opens.\n\nWHO AND WHEN\n- Mon 19 Oct 2026, 6:10 PM. Maya Chen at HOME A has her lease PDF open: it ends Wed 31 Mar 2027 and requires 30 days' notice. She taps 'When does your lease end?' in the place file.\n- Jordan Lee at PLACE B moved in ten days ago. The provenance sheet says Thursday per the City of Camas, but he wants to set it himself and say how often recycling comes. He taps 'Not my schedule', then 'Set my pickup day', and picks Weekly. He tapped 'Not now' on the first notification ask.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Tell the app a date once, see exactly when you'll be reminded, and see who else can see it.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS\n1. The date, spelled out: 'Wed 31 Mar 2027'.\n2. The action date it creates: 'Notice deadline · in 133 days · Mon 1 Mar 2027'.\n3. The reminder timeline, with real dates.\nThe single primary action is Save. The footer scope sentence sits directly above it.\n\nCONTENT (house style fixtures; deltas only)\n- Sheet title: 'Add a date' in create mode; otherwise the kind name.\n- Kind tiles (KindGlyph tile variant): Pickup day · Move-in date · Lease ends · Notice deadline · Insurance renews · Warranty ends · HOA dues · Property-tax appeal · Voter registration · Bill. Bill is phase 2: draw it, and label it phase 2 on Notes.\n- Default leads: 14 days for Lease ends; 30 for Warranty, Insurance and HOA; 7 for Bill. If the default has already passed, the segment shows the passed reason and the suggestion.\n- Lease ends (HOME A):\n  - Date Wed 31 Mar 2027.\n  - 'How much notice does your lease require?' with ChoiceChips 20 days (WA minimum) · 30 · 60 · Other, captioned 'Check your lease.' Maya picks 30.\n  - This creates the linked DateRow 'Notice deadline · in 133 days · Mon 1 Mar 2027', titled 'Tell your landlord in writing by Mon 1 Mar'. Reminders attach to that row.\n  - Other notice lengths: 20 days gives Thu 11 Mar 2027. 60 days gives Sat 30 Jan 2027, a Saturday, so the sheet suggests 'That's a Saturday. Plan to send it by Fri 29 Jan.'\n- Lease reminders: segments 60 / 30 / 14 / 7 / 1 days before the notice deadline, 14 selected. Ticks: Mon 15 Feb 2027 · Sun 28 Feb 2027 · Mon 1 Mar 2027.\n- Warranty ends: 'Water heater warranty — Rheem 40-gal', Sat 12 Dec 2026, reminder 30 days. Ticks: Thu 12 Nov · Fri 11 Dec · Sat 12 Dec.\n- HOA dues: $285, Sun 1 Nov 2026, in 13 days.\n- Insurance renews with 'Not sure of the day': 'Renters insurance — PEMCO · about Jan 2027', reminder Fri 1 Jan 2027.\n- Move-in date (PLACE B): Fri 9 Oct 2026. It is in the past, and that is valid.\n- Pickup day (PLACE B):\n  - Thursday arrives preselected with a hollow mark and the SourceCaption '○ City of Camas · city schedule · 2026 calendar'. The legend word 'On record, not confirmed' is printed once beside it.\n  - Recycling frequency: Not set / Weekly / Every other week. Jordan picks Weekly. 'Next recycling' appears only for Every other week.\n  - Read-only preview: 'Thu 22 Oct · Thu 29 Oct · Thu 5 Nov'. Under it: 'Next holiday move: Thanksgiving — Thu 26 Nov moves to Fri 27 Nov · City of Camas 2026 calendar', with a struck ghost 'Thu 26 Nov'.\n  - Preview dates after the last published City of Camas calendar (Dec 2026) carry the caption 'projected', never a confirmed look.\n- Pickup day (HOME A), already set: 'Set by Sam Ortega · Tuesday · confirmed Sat 3 Oct 2026'. The household rule wins and the row says who set it. Every other week, 'Next recycling' Tue 20 Oct, preview Tue 20 Oct · Tue 3 Nov · Tue 17 Nov, no holiday moves.\n- Voter registration (seeded, statewide, person-scoped):\n  - Checked caption: '● Washington Secretary of State · statewide · checked Oct 2026'. Unconfirmed caption: '○ Washington Secretary of State · statewide · added Sep 2026'.\n  - Headline 'General election · Tue 3 Nov 2026'.\n  - Method DateRows, titles exactly: 'Online or by mail — must arrive by Mon 26 Oct 2026' (line 2: 'in 7 days') and 'In person, Clark County Elections — until 8:00 PM Tue 3 Nov 2026' (line 2: 'in 15 days').\n  - Line: 'Registration is per address. We can't see whether you're registered.'\n  - Plan: 'How will you register?' Online / Mail / In person.\n  - Then the outlined 'I did this' button, TextActionRow 'Check or update at VoteWA ↗', and the footer 'Only you will see this.'\n- Property-tax appeal (seeded, county, phase 2 data; SourceCaption 'Clark County Board of Equalization · county · checked Oct 2026'):\n  - 'Your county lets you challenge the assessed value your tax is based on.'\n  - DateRow conditional rule: 'Closes July 1, or 60 days after your value notice was mailed.' Then 'Late appeals can't be accepted.'\n  - Input 'When was your notice mailed?' with the option 'I haven't gotten one yet'.\n  - After Mon 14 Sep 2026 is entered: 'Closes in 25 days · Fri 13 Nov 2026', with the you-added mark.\n- Property-tax due row opened from the strip: 'Property tax, 2nd half — due Mon 2 Nov', with 'moved from Sat 31 Oct' in the detail.\n- Bill (HOME A): Clark Public Utilities $142.18, due Fri 23 Oct (in 4 days, so the 7-day default has passed).\n- Worst case: a 68-character title, 'Water heater warranty — Rheem 40-gal, installed by Columbia Plumbing', wrapping to two lines.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\nTop to bottom:\n- Header: title and Cancel/Done (Close on Android), with Back leading when present.\n- Kind grid: 2 columns × 5 rows, with no step before it.\n  - Each tile is a whole-tile target at least 56pt tall (48dp minimum on Android), with 8pt gaps, holding the KindGlyph tile variant (42pt) and its label, which wraps to two lines.\n  - Selected tile: the KindGlyph contract's filled radio dot plus a bold label, with a focus ring that looks different from it.\n  - Before a kind is picked, only the grid and a disabled Save show.\n  - After a pick, the grid collapses in place to one row, '[glyph] Lease ends · Change kind'. That row re-expands the grid.\n- HOA dues and Bill: an Amount field above the date.\n- Date field, with the spelled-out weekday date under it, then the 'Not sure of the day' toggle, which swaps the field for month and year.\n- The kind-specific block.\n- Optional title.\n- The 'Remind me' switch row: iOS Toggle, M3 Switch or web switch, 44pt/48dp.\n- ReminderLeadControl, shown only while the switch is on. Under it, a mini timeline: three ticks back from the action date, each labelled with a real date, and a leader line to the event. Caption: 'We'll also remind you the day before and on the day.' Second line: 'Reminders arrive at 7:00 AM.' With the switch off, it collapses to 'No reminders. This date still shows on Today and in your place file.'\n- With 'Not sure of the day' on, the segments hide and one tick shows at the start of the month, captioned 'We'll remind you at the start of Jan 2027.'\n- At a home only, for non-bill, non-seeded kinds: ChoiceChips 'Visible to: Only you · Household'.\n- ScopeChip in sentence form, then the footer. The body keeps scroll padding for it.\nFOOTER BY MODE (sticky):\n- Create: ScopeChip sentence plus filled Save, disabled until a kind and a valid date are set.\n- View-mine with no edits: ScopeChip sentence only. 'Mark done' is an outlined button in the body; 'Remove this date' is a text button.\n- View-mine after an edit: filled Save appears, and the header switches to Cancel.\n- View-seeded: ScopeChip sentence only until Remind me, the plan or the mailing date changes; then filled Save appears. 'I did this' is an outlined body button, never filled.\nPer kind:\n(a) Lease ends, Notice deadline, Insurance renews, Warranty ends, HOA dues and Bill: date field, 'Not sure of the day', title, switch and ReminderLeadControl.\n  - Switch default: on for Lease ends, Notice deadline, HOA dues and Bill; off for Insurance and Warranty.\n  - Bill at HOME A is pre-filled from a mail snap. Fields read from the photo carry the read-from-your-photo mark and the flag 'We weren't sure — check this', and each becomes you-added on Save. No Visible to chips; footer 'You and Sam can see this bill.' A member without finance permission sees Save disabled and a LockedActionRow 'Maya or Sam can add bills here'. No bill string says Paid until Mark paid is tapped.\n  - Bill at a saved place is plain manual entry with no photo wording, saved as a you-added date, not a household bill.\n(b) Move-in date: the date field only. No 'Not sure of the day', no switch, no reminder block.\n(c) Pickup day has no single date field. It has:\n  - A weekday chooser of seven ChoiceChips, Mon to Sun, spoken as full day names; radio rows at AX5.\n  - Then frequency, then 'Next recycling' (inline calendar, Every other week only), then the preview.\n  - In place of the lead control, one line, chosen by state: 'We'll remind you the night before, with your evening briefing (6:00 PM).' (notifications and evening briefing on); 'Notifications are off. Pickup still shows on Today the night before.' (notifications or evening briefing off); 'After you save, we'll ask to remind you the night before (6:00 PM).' (native, permission never asked).\n(d) Voter registration: method rows, then the plan, then the switch and ReminderLeadControl, which appear only after a plan is picked.\n  - Online: 1 day selected; 60/30/7 disabled with 'Too close to set'. Ticks Sun 25 Oct · Mon 26 Oct, captioned 'We'll remind you the day before and on the day.'\n  - Mail: 'Mail takes a few days. Send it by Wed 21 Oct.' 1 day selected; 60/30/7 disabled with 'Too close to set'. Ticks Tue 20 Oct · Wed 21 Oct, captioned 'We'll remind you the day before and on the day.'\n  - In person: 7 days selected. Ticks Tue 27 Oct · Mon 2 Nov · Tue 3 Nov.\n(e) Property-tax appeal: the rule plus the mailing-date input.\n  - Before a mailing date is entered, the h2 date slot shows the rule, not a date: 'July 1, or later' with the caption 'may be later'.\n  - 'I haven't gotten one yet' keeps the rule and shows 'Closes Thu 1 Jul 2027 or later · we'll ask again when your notice comes'. It sets no computed date and fires no reminder.\n  - The switch and ReminderLeadControl appear only once a date is computed.\nView modes:\n- The date shows large (h2) with its SourceCaption and mark. One legend word is printed at first use.\n- View-seeded: fields are locked and drawn as plain text with no outlines. Remind me and 'This isn't right' stay live.\n- A seeded row uses the filled mark only when its source has been checked. Otherwise it uses the hollow mark, its 'added' caption, and a line such as 'Not yet checked against the Washington Secretary of State site'.\nCollision: the existing row is drawn inline with its mark. 'Replace it' is previewed: the old row struck through above the new values, which are labelled 'New'.\nTimeline rules: a reminder date that has already passed is disabled, with the reason. Two ticks on the same day draw as one tick.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- Tapping a tile collapses the grid in 200ms. Under Reduce Motion it cross-fades.\n- Date entry: web accepts 03/31/2027, 31 Mar 2027 and March 31 2027, and paste works. Android input mode takes MM/DD/YYYY. iOS uses the compact date pill; tapping it opens the system calendar with the month/year jump, which is a system control and not a second sheet.\n- Save shows a spinner inside the button, then the status message, then the sheet closes. A successful save gives one light haptic tick; nothing else does.\n- Unsaved edits block swipe-to-dismiss. Cancel, Android Back or web Escape opens a native action sheet (an M3 dialog on Android, a small panel dialog on web) with 'Discard this date' / 'Keep editing'.\n- 'Remove this date' closes the sheet and the calling row collapses to an InlineUndo that stays until the person leaves the screen. Every removal cancels that date's reminders. For an Only-you date it reads 'Removed \"Water heater warranty — Rheem 40-gal\" · Undo'. For a Household-visible date it reads 'Removed for everyone in this household: \"Renters insurance — PEMCO\" · Undo', and the household is not told until Undo is gone. At HOME A the pickup kind reads 'Clear household pickup day' and behaves the same way.\n- 'Mark done' ('I gave notice' on a notice deadline, 'I did this' on voter, 'Mark paid' on a Bill at a home) cancels the remaining reminders.\n  - The status line shows with an InlineUndo 'Undo' until the person leaves.\n  - Reopened later, view-mine reads 'You marked this done Mon 19 Oct · Undo', and Undo restores the remaining reminders.\n  - Offline, the voter tick is queued on the device and uses the same copy.\n- 'This isn't right' opens the ProvenanceSheet in place, with Back. It ends at the dated receipt 'Reported Mon 19 Oct. We'll check it against the Washington Secretary of State by Mon 26 Oct and tell you here.', and the row then shows 'You reported this · checking'.\n- 'Check or update at VoteWA ↗' opens an in-app browser on native and a new tab on web.\n- Reminder push tray action 'Done' marks the date done without opening the app and cancels the remaining reminders. In the foreground there is no banner; the matching row is highlighted instead.\n- Nothing works by swipe alone.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED\nDateSheet (create, view-mine, view-seeded, bill mode, conditional seeded) · KindGlyph (tile and row) · ReminderLeadControl (date sheet and lease variants; the lease variant here adds the 14 segment; the extraction confirm default is 7) · DateRow (deadline, conditional rule and holiday moved variants) · ProvenanceMark (S and M; official, unconfirmed, you-added, read-from-your-photo) · SourceCaption · ScopeChip (footer sentence form) · ChoiceChip (visibility, notice length, voter plan, frequency, weekday) · InlineUndo · InlineErrorRow (save failed, load failed) · OfflineNotice (form offline) · LockedActionRow (names-who-can-act variant, with no 'Verify address' link) · TextActionRow (outbound) · WarmingSkeleton (row skeleton) · ProvenanceSheet · PushCopy (date reminder).\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Reading order: title, kind, date, action date, reminders, visibility, footer, Save.\n- The sheet has a unique title and traps focus.\n- After a tile pick, focus stays on the collapsed row '[glyph] Lease ends · Change kind', in the same position, and 'Lease ends selected' is announced.\n- The timeline is spoken as one sentence: 'Reminders on Mon 15 Feb, Sun 28 Feb and Mon 1 Mar.'\n- Marks are spoken as 'official', 'on record, not confirmed' or 'you added this'.\n- Selection looks different from focus in every control. ChoiceChips use a check plus primary.50 fill.\n- Errors sit next to their field and are announced politely. Saved, Removed, Reported and Marked done are status messages.\n- Targets are 44pt on iOS and web and 48dp on Android.\n- At AX5, the kinds become a one-column list, the reminder control and the weekday chips become radio rows, pairs stack, and the sheet scrolls.\n\nCOPY\n- Buttons: 'Save' · 'Change kind' · 'Remove this date' · 'Clear household pickup day' · 'Mark done' · 'I gave notice' · 'I did this' · 'Mark paid' · 'Replace it' · 'Open it' · 'Add as a separate calendar event' · 'Cancel' · 'Try again' · 'Done' · 'Undo' · 'This isn't right' · 'Discard this date' · 'Keep editing' · 'Keep it on file' · 'Change the date' · 'Use Wed 31 Mar 2027' · 'Remind 7 days before' · 'Remind 1 day before'.\n- Switch: 'Remind me'. Visibility: 'Visible to: Only you · Household'.\n- Saved: 'Saved to your calendar. Only you.' / 'Saved to your household calendar.' / bill: 'Saved. You and Sam can see this bill.'\n- Done: 'You marked this done · Only you' (voter and Only-you dates) or 'You marked this done · Your household' (Household dates), then 'We won't remind you again about this.'\n- Removed: 'Removed \"Water heater warranty — Rheem 40-gal\" · Undo' / 'Removed for everyone in this household: \"Renters insurance — PEMCO\" · Undo'.\n- Report receipt: 'Reported Mon 19 Oct. We'll check it against the Washington Secretary of State by Mon 26 Oct and tell you here.' Row: 'You reported this · checking'.\n- Past date: 'That date has passed. Did you mean Wed 31 Mar 2027?'\n- Lead passed (HOA): 'That's already passed — remind 7 days before (Sun 25 Oct)?' Bill: 'That's already passed — remind 1 day before (Thu 22 Oct)?'\n- Warranty in the past: 'This warranty already ended. Keep it on file?' with 'Keep it on file' / 'Change the date' at equal weight.\n- Save failed: 'Couldn't save that date. Try again.' Typed values are kept.\n- Remove failed: 'Couldn't remove that date. Try again.'\n- Load failed: 'Couldn't load that date.' with 'Try again'.\n- Offline, viewing: 'You're offline. You can read this date; saving needs a connection.' Offline, creating: 'You're offline. Saving a new date needs a connection.' Remind me and 'This isn't right' are disabled.\n- Guest: 'Maya or Sam can change dates at this home.' Bill without finance permission: 'Maya or Sam can add bills here'.\n- Unreadable bill: 'We couldn't read this one automatically. Add the amount and due date yourself.'\n- Unconfirmed seed: 'Not yet checked against the Washington Secretary of State site'.\n- Reminder push (PushCopy date reminder, on Notes): 'Lease notice due in 14 days' / 'Tell your landlord by Mon 1 Mar', action 'Done'.\n\nEDGE CASES\n- Collision at a home: 'Warranty ends is already on file: Water heater warranty — Rheem 40-gal · Sat 12 Dec 2026.' Choices: Replace it (previewed) / Add as a separate calendar event / Cancel.\n- Collision at a saved place: before typing, the tile's subline reads 'One per kind for now · already set for Sat 12 Dec'. After the tap: 'You can keep one Warranty ends date per place for now. Water heater warranty — Rheem 40-gal · Sat 12 Dec 2026 is already on file.' Choices: 'Open it' / 'Replace it' (previewed) / 'Cancel'.\n- A reminder opened for a removed date lands on Today with 'That date was removed.' No error modal, no blank page.\n- Notifications off: the timeline caption reads 'Notifications are off. These show on Today and in your place file.' Pickup uses its own notifications-off line.\n- Slow open from a push: a row skeleton appears inside the sheet only if the open takes 1s or longer; static under Reduce Motion.\n- Bills never show $0.00 or today's date in place of a blank.\n- Voter deadline passed for online: 'You can still register in person until 8:00 PM Tue 3 Nov.' Both passed: 'The deadline for Tue 3 Nov has passed.'\n- No seeded voter rule for the state: 'We don't have this state's deadline yet.' The outbound link appears only if we hold the office URL, never with a guessed date.\n- Many items and the longest title: the 68-character title wraps. The largest amount is $285.\n- Tiers: a saved place shows no visibility chips and no household words. A guest sees every field and Remind me disabled, plus the LockedActionRow. A pickup already set by Sam shows who set it. A member without finance permission cannot save a bill.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a multi-step wizard, draw the kind as one tap that collapses in place — because the kind is a choice, not a stage.\n- Instead of a calendar you page through for 31 Mar 2027, draw a typeable field (web, Android) or the compact pill with the month/year jump (iOS) — because document dates are far away and copied, and sheets never stack.\n- Instead of one lead with one leader line, draw all three ticks with real dates — because three reminders fire.\n- Instead of anchoring the lease reminder to the lease end, anchor it to the Notice deadline — because that is the day she must act.\n- Instead of a date field and lead control on Pickup day, draw a weekday chooser and the night-before line — because pickup repeats and rides the evening briefing.\n- Instead of working out recycling from the garbage day, draw an explicit frequency, a Next recycling field and a preview — because Not set is a real value.\n- Instead of a single seeded tax date, draw the rule with 'may be later' until a mailing date exists — because the deadline is conditional.\n- Instead of a filled mark and a 'checked' caption on every seeded row, draw hollow with 'added Sep 2026' until checked — because unverified must look unverified.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- A saved-place user can set a pickup day and a lease date.\n- Every reminder that will fire is visible with its date, the lease reminder lands before Mon 1 Mar, and a date can be saved with no reminder.\n- 31 Mar 2027 is reachable in 2–3 taps on each platform.\n- Recycling is never inferred, and pickup never promises a push that cannot fire.\n- Scope and visibility are stated at the moment of input, the footer always matches the selected chip, and a bill names who can see it.\n- A guest cannot write.\n- Seeded and you-added dates can be told apart in greyscale.\n- Marking done stops the reminders, says so, and can be undone.\n- A report ends on a dated receipt.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. x-date-sheet · ios · 01-create-lease-dense · light — HOME A, Lease ends, 30-day notice, linked Notice deadline row, lease segments with 14 selected, three ticks, Only you selected, footer 'Only you will see this.' Inset: the iOS month/year wheel set to March 2027, with taps numbered 1 (pill), 2 (month/year), 3 (day 31).\n2. x-date-sheet · ios · 02-create-empty · light — full kind grid, nothing chosen, disabled Save, over the Today strip.\n3. x-date-sheet · ios · 03-pickup-weekly · light — PLACE B, arrived from the provenance sheet with Back '‹ Where this fact comes from' leading and Cancel trailing; Thursday hollow; Weekly; preview Thu 22 Oct · Thu 29 Oct · Thu 5 Nov; holiday line with struck ghost Thu 26 Nov; line 'After you save, we'll ask to remind you the night before (6:00 PM).'\n4. x-date-sheet · ios · 04-view-mine-warranty · light — Remind me on, 30 selected, 60 disabled, ticks, outlined Mark done, Remove this date, footer sentence only.\n5. x-date-sheet · ios · 05-view-seeded-voter · light — '● … checked Oct 2026', method rows with 'in 7 days' / 'in 15 days' line 2, plan Online, two ticks, outlined I did this, VoteWA link, filled Save (plan changed), 'Only you will see this.'\n6. x-date-sheet · ios · 06-view-seeded-voter-unconfirmed · light — hollow mark, '○ … added Sep 2026', 'Not yet checked against the Washington Secretary of State site', no plan yet, footer sentence only.\n7. x-date-sheet · ios · 07-view-seeded-tax-appeal · light — HOME A (Maya rents), footer 'Only you will see this.'; left: rule, 'July 1, or later' with 'may be later', question empty; right: after 'I haven't gotten one yet'.\n8. x-date-sheet · ios · 08-tax-appeal-computed · light — HOME A, filled Board of Equalization caption, you-added 'Closes in 25 days · Fri 13 Nov 2026', reminders, Save, 'Only you will see this.'\n9. x-date-sheet · ios · 09-collision-warranty-home · light — HOME A, existing row inline, Replace it previewed, three choices.\n10. x-date-sheet · ios · 10-collision-warranty-saved-place · light — PLACE B, tile subline, full message, Open it / Replace it / Cancel.\n11. x-date-sheet · ios · 11-lead-passed-hoa · light — HOA $285 Sun 1 Nov, default 30 selected but disabled with its reason, suggestion 'That's already passed — remind 7 days before (Sun 25 Oct)?' and button 'Remind 7 days before'.\n12. x-date-sheet · ios · 12-past-date-lease · light — 31 Mar 2026 typed, with 'Use Wed 31 Mar 2027'.\n13. x-date-sheet · ios · 13-lease-notice-weekend · light — 60 days gives Sat 30 Jan; suggests Fri 29 Jan.\n14. x-date-sheet · ios · 14-not-sure-of-day · light — PLACE B, 'about Jan 2027', switch on, segments hidden, one tick Fri 1 Jan with 'We'll remind you at the start of Jan 2027.', no chips, footer 'Only you will see this.'\n15. x-date-sheet · ios · 15-view-mine-insurance-visibility · light — HOME A, Renters insurance switched Only you → Household, household footer, Remind me off with its caption, Cancel in header.\n16. x-date-sheet · ios · 16-saved · light — inset: Save with its spinner (saving); then 'Saved to your calendar. Only you.'; then the place file row with the you-added mark.\n17. x-date-sheet · ios · 17-notice-marked-done · light — HOME A Household notice: 'I gave notice' done, 'You marked this done · Your household', reminders cancelled, InlineUndo; inset shows the later 'You marked this done Mon 19 Oct · Undo'.\n18. x-date-sheet · ios · 18-removed-undo · light — place file warranty row collapsed to InlineUndo; inset: 'Removed for everyone in this household: \"Renters insurance — PEMCO\" · Undo'.\n19. x-date-sheet · ios · 19-discard-unsaved · light — typed lease date, action sheet with Discard this date / Keep editing.\n20. x-date-sheet · ios · 20-loading-from-reminder · light — left: highlighted row and the sheet's row skeleton; right: 'Couldn't load that date. · Try again'.\n21. x-date-sheet · ios · 21-save-failed · light — typed values kept, InlineErrorRow.\n22. x-date-sheet · ios · 22-offline · light — view-mine read-only date; Save, Remind me and 'This isn't right' disabled, each with its reason; inset: create mode with 'You're offline. Saving a new date needs a connection.'\n23. x-date-sheet · ios · 23-permission-denied-guest · light — viewer Alex Rivera, guest at HOME A; fields and Remind me disabled; LockedActionRow 'Maya or Sam can change dates at this home.'\n24. x-date-sheet · ios · 24-bill-prefilled · light — HOME A, Clark Public Utilities $142.18 due Fri 23 Oct, read-from-your-photo marks, one 'We weren't sure — check this' flag, 7 default passed with the 'Remind 1 day before' suggestion, no chips, footer 'You and Sam can see this bill.'\n25. x-date-sheet · ios · 25-bill-unreadable · light — HOME A, snap of Clark Public Utilities, amount and due date blank (never $0.00), Save disabled until both are filled, footer 'You and Sam can see this bill.'\n26. x-date-sheet · ios · 26-pickup-home-set-by-sam · light — HOME A, 'Set by Sam Ortega', Tuesday, Every other week, Next recycling Tue 20 Oct, preview Tue 20 Oct · Tue 3 Nov · Tue 17 Nov, night-before line, Clear household pickup day.\n27. x-date-sheet · android · 27-create-lease-dense · light — embedded input picker with 03/31/2027 and the calendar toggle, Close (X).\n28. x-date-sheet · web-1440 · 28-create-lease-dense · light — right SlidePanel over the place file, typed '31 Mar 2027'.\n29. x-date-sheet · web-390 · 29-view-seeded-voter · light — bottom sheet, checked caption.\n30. x-date-sheet · ios · 30-ax5-create-lease · light — left: create-empty as a one-column kind list; right: lease chosen, scrolled to reminder radio rows and stacked visibility options.\n31. x-date-sheet · ios · 31-greyscale-marks · light — frames 3 (hollow Thursday) and 8 (filled caption plus you-added date) side by side in greyscale, legend words visible.\n32. x-date-sheet · ios · 32-create-lease-dense · dark — dark twin of frame 1.\n33. x-date-sheet · ios · 33-view-seeded-voter · dark — dark twin of frame 5, checked caption.\n34. x-date-sheet · Notes — the Notes board, with:\n  - The PushCopy date-reminder tray preview (7:00 AM): Done marks the date done without opening the app and cancels the remaining reminders. Active/DEFAULT. Also listed in the in-app notifications. In the foreground there is no banner; the row is highlighted instead. A bill reminder lands on the bill.\n  - Hand-offs: close, then the notification primer on native for a first pickup save; the FirstWeekRow advances; the widget is rewritten; 'I did this' on voter ticks the place file mover row 'Update your voter registration' as you-added, Only you, and Undo un-ticks it.\n  - Assumptions:\n    - Seeded rows are filled only when checked, and seeds launch hollow.\n    - Thu 12 Nov is unmoved: the City of Camas 2026 calendar moves only the Wednesday route, Veterans' Day Wed Nov 11 → Thu Nov 12.\n    - Camas collects recycling weekly, so every-other-week is shown at HOME A (Vancouver).\n    - The tax-appeal seed appears at any Clark County address, including a rental. Property-tax appeal seeds are F12 phase 2 data. Bill is phase 2.\n    - Backend blockers: saved-place scope must outrank the city rule, or a saved-place correction is dropped; reminder leads must allow 0–60 days; saved-place Bill and Move-in date need a kind or storage (not in the F5 kind list).\n    - Deep-link paths follow whatever Today route f1-today-tab settles on; the ?event= alias is folded into ?rule=.\n    - Done replaces the voter sheet's 'Not now'.\n    - 'Confirm Tuesday / Pick a different day' became the preselected chooser plus Save.\n    - InlineUndo, with a consequence prefix for household dates, replaces the household remove-confirm.\n    - 'Visible to' is the label.\n    - Alex Rivera is an invented guest; Priya's invite is still pending.\n  - For prompt 00:\n    - Add the 14 segment to the lease variant.\n    - Add the 'Remind me' switch and its off state to ReminderLeadControl/DateSheet.\n    - The contract sample Thu 24 Sep is replaced by Sun 25 Oct.\n    - PushCopy date-reminder body and DateRow sample Sun 31 Jan become Mon 1 Mar ('Tell your landlord by Mon 1 Mar'), the HOME A fixture.\n    - flow-03 step 4 (60 days, Sat 30 Jan) is superseded by the Mon 15 Feb fixture.\n    - Flow-02's Luis is shown as Jordan at PLACE B.\n  - Invented strings: PEMCO; the Rheem title; Columbia Plumbing; Mon 14 Sep 2026; Alex Rivera; 'Mail takes a few days. Send it by Wed 21 Oct.'; Tue 27 Oct; 'checked Oct 2026'; 'added Sep 2026'; cal_7f3a2; 'Too close to set'; 'Reminders arrive at 7:00 AM.'; 'Clear household pickup day'; 'You marked this done · Your household'; 'You and Sam can see this bill.'; 'Saved. You and Sam can see this bill.'; 'Maya or Sam can add bills here'; 'Remind 7 days before'; 'Remind 1 day before'; 'We'll remind you at the start of Jan 2027.'; the three pickup reminder lines; 'Next holiday move: …'; the report receipt; every error, suggestion, discard and collision string.\n  - Omitted states: notifications-off caption; pickup notifications-off line; 'That date was removed.'; remove failed; voter deadline passed; no seeded voter rule; offline voter tick queued; report submitted (dated receipt, then 'You reported this · checking'); saved-place manual Bill; saved-place Lease ends (same footer as frame 14); bill Save disabled for a member without finance permission; Mark paid on a bill; projected pickup dates after Dec 2026; property-tax due (view-seeded, moved from Sat 31 Oct); Mail voter plan.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for continue.\nTurn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue.\nTurn 3: 13-18, then wait for continue.\nTurn 4: 19-24, then wait for continue.\nTurn 5: 25-30, then wait for continue.\nTurn 6: 31-34.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Report path now ends on the dated receipt naming the Washington Secretary of State and Mon 26 Oct, and the row then shows 'You reported this · checking'. 'Report submitted (dated receipt)' is in Omitted states (review, major).",
          "Bill at a home: no visibility chips, footer 'You and Sam can see this bill.', and a LockedActionRow 'Maya or Sam can add bills here' with Save disabled for members without finance permission. That variant is listed under Omitted states (review, major).",
          "Removing a date always cancels its reminders. Household-visible removals get the consequence prefix 'Removed for everyone in this household: …', shown as an inset on frame 18 (review, major).",
          "New hand-off: 'I did this' on voter ticks the place file mover row as you-added and Only you, and Undo un-ticks it. Added to the Notes hand-offs (review, major).",
          "Pickup reminder line now has three variants: on, notifications or evening briefing off, and permission never asked. The never-asked variant is drawn in frame 3 (review, major).",
          "'Mark paid' added for a Bill at a home, with a no-Paid-until-marked rule, in COPY buttons (review, major).",
          "iOS date entry: the compact pill opens the system calendar with the month/year jump. Web and Android input formats are separated. INSTEAD OF is rewritten. Frame 1 gets a numbered 1–3 tap inset of the month/year wheel (review, major).",
          "Every-other-week demo moved from Camas to HOME A in frame 26. Jordan now picks Weekly, with preview Thu 22 Oct · Thu 29 Oct · Thu 5 Nov and a Thanksgiving next-holiday line. WHO AND WHEN is updated (review, major).",
          "Voter captions split: checked ('● … checked Oct 2026', frames 5, 29, 33) and unconfirmed ('○ … added Sep 2026', frame 6) (review, major).",
          "New FOOTER BY MODE list. Seeded kinds never show chips and their footer reads 'Only you will see this.' Frames 7 and 8 are set at HOME A with that footer (review, major).",
          "Mail voter plan: 1 day selected, 60/30/7 disabled, ticks Tue 20 Oct and Wed 21 Oct with the day-before caption (review, minor).",
          "Default leads stated per kind (lease 14; warranty, insurance, HOA 30; bill 7). 'Remind 7 days before' button added and shown in frame 11. The bill's passed-default suggestion is in frame 24 (review, minor).",
          "Back is leading and Cancel/Done is trailing when Back is present, with the medium-to-large detent cross-fade. Jordan's path now goes 'Not my schedule' → 'Set my pickup day' (review, minor).",
          "Guest frame uses the invented Alex Rivera, listed on Notes. Priya's pending invite is noted (review, minor, two findings reconciled).",
          "'You marked this done · Your household' for Household dates, used in frame 17 (review, minor).",
          "Added: the before-kind state (grid plus disabled Save), the Amount field for HOA and Bill, Android inline calendar for other kinds, the Not-sure-of-the-day tick rule, and the create-mode offline copy, shown as an inset in frame 22 (review, minor).",
          "Saving state drawn as an inset in frame 16 (review, minor).",
          "Projected caption for pickup dates after Dec 2026, listed under Omitted states (review, minor).",
          "Notes updated: property-tax appeal marked F12 phase 2; saved-place Bill and Move-in storage added as a backend blocker; the PushCopy/DateRow Sun 31 Jan → Mon 1 Mar change flagged for prompt 00; property-tax due and Mail voter plan added to Omitted states (review, minor).",
          "Notification details on Notes: Done works in the background and cancels the remaining reminders, Active/DEFAULT, listed in-app, highlight with no banner in the foreground, and a bill reminder lands on the bill (review, minor).",
          "Voter method row titles now match the contract strings exactly, with 'in 7 days' / 'in 15 days' on line 2 (review, minor).",
          "Added the Settings > Notifications pickup entry point and the full web create paths (/app/place/today?add=date&kind=lease_end, /app/today?add=date) (review, minor).",
          "All v1 substance kept: the ten kinds, lease notice math, collision handling, tax-appeal rule, voter person-scoping, AX5, greyscale and dark twins, deep links, and the Notes assumptions."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "x-place-file",
        "name": "Your place file",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": true,
        "frameCount": 24,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Your place file · x-place-file\n\nTYPE: NEW. Nothing like it exists yet. Build it only from the Foundations components and the existing row and card styles.\n\nATTACH: the current Place tab root on web 1440 (with the left sidebar), web 390, iOS and Android (including any section switcher it shows); the current Today tab on iOS (so the band's 14-day window matches the FourteenDayStrip geometry); the Foundations board from prompt 00. These Place tab screenshots are for the chrome only: the sidebar, the bottom tab bar, the navigation bar and any section switcher. Keep those exactly. Everything below them is replaced by this screen, so do not keep the old dashboard cards (including the old Just Moved card).\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: web 1440x900 (sidebar) and 390x844 (bottom tab bar); iOS 393x852 with the large title \"Your place file\" that collapses on scroll; Android 412x915 with the Material 3 large top app bar.\n\nWHY IT IS SHAPED THIS WAY (do not optimise this away)\nThis is one list replacing four: the first-week checklist, Just moved, Your dates and the keeper's list of facts. Draw them as sections of one file, with one tick and one dismissal per row. Never split \"Set up your place\", \"Just moved\" or Dates back into separate cards. Ticks and dismissals are stored on the server and sync across devices; the sync banner is the only visible sign of that. A date more than 14 days away is visible only on this screen. In the current app, a lease end 5 months out would be saved, confirmed and then hidden until 2 weeks before it fires. This screen also gives the Place tab a job before an address is claimed.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE\nThis screen is the index of the Place tab (Place · Today · Nearby · Mail) on every platform: web /app/place, and the Place tab root on iOS and Android. It needs a place; a person with no saved place sees the Your places empty state instead. Arrivals:\n1. Tapping Place in the tab bar or sidebar.\n2. Today's FirstWeekRow (\"Next: set your pickup day →\", shown for 7 days). It lands on \"Set up your place\" with that step highlighted. Both use the same step set and agree on what is done.\n3. The claim receipt's \"See your place file\" button (formerly \"See what we know\"). The receipt hands over the carried items, which appear here once as a banner and stay in the \"What moved when you claimed\" row.\n4. The keeper strip's count (phase 2). The number there equals the number here.\n5. A reminder push with no specific date lands at the top. A reminder for a date more than 14 days away lands on that date's row: highlighted, focus moved to it, then the DateSheet opens in view mode. Links: web /app/place?rule=notice-deadline · pantopus://place?rule=notice-deadline.\n6. The large widget's year strip lands on the year band: web /app/place?section=year · pantopus://place?section=year.\nExits: rows open the DateSheet, the ProvenanceSheet, Your places, the home dashboard (read-only variant for members), the members roster, the invite composer, the bills list, Mail Day triage, the bill trend, the home documents list, the verify sheet, the privacy mirror, the keeper naming sheet, the Civic registration block, the widget how-to sheet and the claim receipt. \"Next 14 days\" opens Today's 14-day strip. Risk & readiness and Civic stay reachable (see LAYOUT).\n\nWHO AND WHEN\nDense frames: Maya Chen, owner of HOME A, Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM. She moved in 23 days ago, claimed on Sat 17 Oct; Sam Ortega joined Sun 18 Oct. She wants to check nothing in the year ahead is missing, including the lease notice.\nPLACE B frames: the fixture's Jordan Lee, never named on screen. Delta: Jordan saved PLACE B on Sat 17 Oct (not Sat 10 Oct), so the first week runs until Sat 24 Oct.\n\nTHE ONE JOB\nSee every fact on file for this address in one list, including dates months away, and add the few that are missing.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS\nHOME A (every first-week step done): 1. address, ScopeChip \"Your household\", \"11 on file\". 2. Band summary \"Next: voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\". 3. The first Just moved row, \"Update your voter registration\", whose filled button \"See how to update\" is the one primary action. The two remaining asks (widget, insurance) are quiet rows in their own sections, below the fold.\nPLACE B (first week): 1. address, ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\", \"2 on file\". 2. The band. 3. \"Set up your place\", primary action \"Set your pickup day\".\nPromoted asks follow the activation order: pickup day, then a reminder or the widget, then one date or one person. Never more than 3. On native, ask 2 is \"Turn on a reminder or add the widget\"; on web (no widget) it is \"Turn on a reminder\".\n\nCONTENT (house style fixtures; deltas only)\nHOME A deltas: moved in Sat 26 Sep 2026, so Just moved shows until Wed 25 Nov. Maya set Tuesday pickup on Sat 10 Oct while it was a saved place; it carried at the claim (Sat 17 Oct) with the lease end, notice deadline, warranty and Ollie. Maya set the move-in date on the home on Sun 18 Oct, after the claim. The warranty is \"Only you\"; everything else is \"Your household\". Priya invite sent Mon 19 Oct. Bills came from mail snaps (tick). Address not verified.\nCount rule: \"on file\" counts what this household holds plus address-specific records such as the pickup weekday. County and state rules are shown, not counted. HOME A = 11: Place 3 (address, pickup day, moved in) · Dates 4 (HOA dues, warranty, notice deadline, lease ends) · Money 3 bills · People 1 (Sam). PLACE B = 2: address and the Thursday pickup weekday (on record, not confirmed; \"Set your pickup day\" stays undone because nobody confirmed it or set how often).\n\nHeader, in order: \"Your place file\"; \"2418 NE Larkspur Loop\" / \"Vancouver, WA 98684\"; ScopeChip \"Your household\"; FreshnessLine \"Updated 4m ago\"; FactCount \"11 on file\" with pips Place · Dates · Money · People; legend \"● Official · ○ On record, not confirmed · ✓ You added this\", printed once.\n\nYear band \"The year ahead\", Oct 2026–Sep 2027:\n- You (tick): Nov (HOA dues) · Dec (warranty) · Mar with count \"2\" (notice deadline, lease ends).\n- Your city: Tuesday service rhythm with tick for Oct–Dec, dashed with the word \"projected\" from Jan (last published hauler calendar is Dec 2026). No Tuesday holiday move is published for Oct–Dec.\n- Your county (filled): Nov (property tax 2nd half) · Apr (1st half) · Jul (appeal, caption \"may be later\").\n- Your state (filled, full-lane-height bars): Oct (Mon 26 Oct) · Nov (Tue 3 Nov).\n- Summary \"Next 12 months: 9 dates, plus pickup every Tuesday. Next: voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct.\" Caption \"Every date is listed below.\" Link row \"Next 14 days · See them on Today ›\".\n\nJUST MOVED, caption \"Shown until Wed 25 Nov, 60 days after you moved in\". Undone rows first, done last:\n- \"Update your voter registration\" · \"Registration is per address · in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · button \"See how to update\" opens the Civic registration block (per-method dates and \"Check or update at VoteWA ↗\"). Never state or imply whether Maya is registered.\n- \"Move your utilities\" · Clark Public Utilities, NW Natural, City of Vancouver.\n- \"Forward your mail\" · USPS · done and quiet: \"You marked this done Sat 3 Oct\".\n\nPLACE:\n- Your home · \"Larkspur Loop ›\" opens the home dashboard (absent on a saved place).\n- Address · full address · chevron to Your places · tick.\n- Pickup day · \"You · Tuesday\" · \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow · carts out by 6:30 AM\" · SourceCaption \"Waste Connections · recycling every other Tuesday · you confirmed Sat 10 Oct\". Opens the DateSheet pickup kind.\n- Moved in · \"Sat 26 Sep 2026\" · tick · helper \"Shows your moving list for 60 days\".\n- What neighbors see · \"Same spot every time, about 0.3 mi\" (opens the privacy mirror).\n- Keeper (phase 2): named: \"Keeper · Ollie\" with chevron to the keeper naming sheet. Unnamed or skipped: quiet FactRow \"Give your place a keeper\" with text \"Add\", no badge, never promoted.\n- Put today on your home screen · \"Pickup, air and your next date. No notifications needed.\" iOS and Android only, with a small thumbnail of Maya's own widget (live snapshot: Tuesday pickup, AQI 42, HOA dues) at the leading edge. Quiet for HOME A.\n- What moved when you claimed · \"Pickup day, 3 dates and Ollie · Sat 17 Oct\". A move-in date saved on a saved place also carries at claim and is listed here when present.\n- Your reports · \"1 checking\".\n\nDATES: DateRows in date order, relative count first:\n- Voter registration · \"Online or by mail — in 7 days · must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\" · second line \"In person, Clark County Elections — in 15 days · until 8:00 PM Tue 3 Nov\" · the DateRow's statewide tag \"Statewide — WA\" (its optional tag, not the visibility ScopeChip; no person or house glyph) · filled · Washington Secretary of State · \"Remind me\". Directly below, a separate TextActionRow (outbound) \"Check or update at VoteWA ↗\", not nested in the row target.\n- HOA dues · \"$285 · in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov\" · \"Every year\" · tick.\n- Property tax, 2nd half · \"Due in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov\" · \"Every year\" · filled · Clark County Treasurer. Detail one tap away: \"moved from Sat 31 Oct\".\n- Water-heater warranty ends · \"in 54 days · Sat 12 Dec\" · \"Reminders Thu 12 Nov, Fri 11 Dec and Sat 12 Dec\" · Only you.\n- \"Tell your landlord in writing by Mon 1 Mar 2027\" · \"in 4 months · Mon 1 Mar 2027\" · \"Reminders Mon 15 Feb, Sun 28 Feb and Mon 1 Mar\" · \"From your lease: 30 days' notice\".\n- Lease ends · \"in 5 months · Wed 31 Mar 2027\" · link line \"Notice deadline: Mon 1 Mar 2027\". No reminder on this row.\n- Property tax, 1st half · \"Due in 6 months · Fri 30 Apr 2027\" · \"Every year\" · filled.\n- Property-tax appeal · \"in 8 months · Thu 1 Jul 2027, or 60 days after your value notice was mailed\" · \"Every year\" · Clark County Board of Equalization · filled · text action \"Add the mailing date\".\n- Quiet ask \"When does your insurance renew?\" · \"Add a date\".\n- \"Open household calendar\".\nVisibility: on user-entered dates the glyph and word (person + \"Only you\", or house + \"Your household\") is a control that opens the DateSheet's visibility choice; scope changes only when someone picks. Seeded county and state rows show their source and carry no household scope.\n\nMONEY (phase 2): Bills · \"3 upcoming · $306.17 through Mon 2 Nov\" · \"Next: Clark Public Utilities $142.18 · in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\" · \"You and Sam can see these.\" Below, quiet rows \"Mail Day ›\" (Mail Day triage) and \"How your bills compare ›\" (bill trend).\n\nPEOPLE: hosts the household block (own prompt). With 2+ members it collapses to MemberRow \"Maya and Sam live here · View\". Below, InviteRow \"priya@example.com · Member · sent Mon 19 Oct · Expires Mon 26 Oct · Resend\".\n\nMORE YOU CAN ADD, collapsed \"More you can add (3)\": \"Verify this address\" (verify sheet), \"Your gas bill · NW Natural\" (bills), \"A home document, like your lease\" (home documents list). Proof has no section until something is known.\n\nWorst case: 9 dates, 3 mover rows, 3 bills and a pending invite in one phone scroll, with November marks in three lanes.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\n- Phones: one column, 16pt gutter. Order: header → LandingBannerSlot (only when it holds a banner) → year band card → Set up your place (PLACE B, first 7 days) → Just moved → Place → Risk & readiness and Civic → Dates → Money → People → Proof (only when known) → More you can add → footer.\n- Existing sections: if the attached host shows a section switcher (e.g. Risk & readiness · Civic), keep it unchanged above the title and make this file its first section. If not, add two navigation FactRows \"Risk & readiness\" and \"Civic\" directly after Place. Say on Notes which you drew.\n- Year band on phones and web-390: each lane label (You · Your city · Your county · Your state) is a caption line above its lane. 12 month columns share the card width (about 27pt each), three-letter labels, \"2027\" above Jan. Lanes on surface.raised with ink dividers. One XS ProvenanceMark per month cell per lane, plus a count numeral at 2+; never exact-day placement on a phone. Statewide rules are full-lane-height bars. Today rule 1.5px text.primary labelled \"Today\". The 14-day window is a primary.50 sliver at least 8pt wide with an ink edge, starting at the today rule, with a bracket above the month labels; its label sits outside the band as the link row. City lane: light service-week rhythm, dashed and \"projected\" after Dec 2026. A holiday move = mark plus a small \"moved\" glyph in its month cell; the moved date is written in the pickup row. Bills are not drawn on the band.\n- YearBand anatomy is fixed by prompt 00. If a phone cell cannot hold mark, count and \"moved\" glyph, draw 2 cluster options side by side on Notes and use the first in the frames.\n- Web 1440: band spans full content width with exact-day marks. A holiday move sits on its new day with a faint struck ghost on the usual day (web-1440 only). A leader line runs from the notice-deadline mark back to a reminder tick \"Reminder Mon 15 Feb\". Below: a 720 column (Just moved, Place, Risk & readiness and Civic, Dates, Money, People) and a 320 column (More you can add, open by default; Your reports; What moved when you claimed). No widget row.\n- Rows: FactRow 56pt, label above value. Annual and self-entered DateRows get the 2px home pillar token (home) left rule plus their recurrence caption.\n- Missing data: no rules → all 12 columns, 4 empty labelled lanes, QuietDayReceipt line \"Checked — nothing on file for the next year\". Whole-screen error → no band. County rules fail alone → county lane not drawn, InlineErrorRow in the band. Saved place → county lane reads \"County dates aren't available for a saved place\".\n- PLACE B header: ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\"; FactCount \"2 on file\", Place pip only (T1 can show only Place and Dates).\n- PLACE B \"Set up your place\" (caption \"For your first week · until Sat 24 Oct\", Dismiss): \"Save your address\" (ticked), \"Set your pickup day\" (primary), \"Turn on a reminder or add the widget\", \"Add one date that matters\". No fraction. Below, grey LockedActionRow (not at this tier) \"Add the people you live with · Claim this address first\", no button, not counted. These are the promoted asks, so the same facts show only a quiet \"Not set\" in sections below.\n- PLACE B Place: pickup \"Thursday · how often: Not set\", hollow mark, caption \"City of Camas · pickup Thursdays · 2026 calendar\", opens the DateSheet pickup kind. Below: \"Thanksgiving — moved to Fri 27 Nov · City of Camas 2026 calendar\"; the band's Nov city cell shows the \"moved\" glyph. \"Moved in · Not set · Add\" with helper \"Add it to see a moving list for 60 days\". Keeper row in skipped form.\n- Saved place with a move-in date: Just moved appears with the same rows; ticks and dismissals are stored against the saved place (frame 18).\n- PLACE B Dates: the voter row and VoteWA link, plus \"More you can add (4)\" (Lease ends, Insurance renews, Warranty ends, HOA dues).\n- PLACE B other sections: one grey row \"Money, people and proof · Not here — this is a saved place · Claim this address first\". While a claim is pending, the Proof block (below) replaces it; Money and People stay absent. Footer \"Only you will see this.\" and text link \"Claim this address\".\n- Proof pending (PLACE B): LockedActionRow (pending, no link) \"Postcard mailed Mon 19 Oct · expected Fri 23 Oct–Mon 2 Nov · code expires Wed 18 Nov\"; below it a separate FactRow \"Enter your code\" with chevron; below that a disabled, focusable button \"Send a new code\" with reason \"You can ask for a new code after Mon 2 Nov.\"\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- Targets: 44pt iOS, 48dp Android (8dp gaps), 44px web. Custom actions: Edit, Remind me, Where this comes from, Mark done.\n- One target per row: only the first promoted ask shows a filled button, and that button is the row's only target. Asks 2 and 3 show their verb as the row label with a chevron. \"Not now\" and \"Skip\" sit on one line of small text buttons under each promoted ask (44pt each, 8pt apart) and are also custom actions. On mover rows, dismiss and Mark done live in a 44pt overflow button and in custom actions; the row body is the single target. Quiet asks offer Skip through their overflow button and a custom action.\n- \"Not now\" turns a promoted ask into a quiet row that is never auto-promoted again. \"Skip\" collapses the row to InlineUndo, is stored on the server, and can be reopened from More you can add.\n- Year band: a tap anywhere scrolls to Dates. Native: one adjustable element; swipe up/down moves by month. Web: month columns are buttons in tab order; click or Enter highlights that month's rows, Escape clears. Link row opens Today.\n- Widget row: promoted at most once in any 24 hours, otherwise quiet. Android: opens the how-to sheet whose primary \"Add to home screen\" calls the system pin dialog. iOS: how-to sheet with the Edit → Add Widget steps. Disappears once a widget is placed.\n- Dismissed mover row collapses to InlineUndo until she leaves the screen. When all three are gone: \"You can show these again in home settings.\"\n- \"More you can add\" expands in place. Deep-link landing scrolls once, then fades the highlight; a deleted date lands at the top with a status line. Count updates silently, no count-up.\n- Motion 300ms or less; Reduce Motion uses cross-fades and a static skeleton.\n- Haptics: one light tick on \"Mark done\" only (iOS light impact; Android confirm haptic).\n- DateSheet: right SlidePanel web 1440, bottom SlidePanel web-390, large sheet iOS, ModalBottomSheet Android. ProvenanceSheet: centred modal 560 web 1440, bottom sheet web-390, medium detent iOS, ModalBottomSheet Android. Sheets never stack.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED\nYearBand (place file; empty checked), FourteenDayStrip (window geometry only), ProvenanceMark (XS band, S rows), SourceCaption, ScopeChip, FactCount (place file header; T1), FactRow (known, missing, not at this tier, done ask, declined, permission-disabled, \"What moved when you claimed\", \"Your reports\"). \"Set up your place\" is a group of FactRows (missing, done ask) using FirstWeekRow's step set and 7-day window; draw no FirstWeekRow here. DateRow (deadline, money, pickup, holiday moved, conditional rule, done; statewide tag), KindGlyph, LockedActionRow (names who can act; pending; not at this tier), InlineUndo (removed row; declined ask), LandingBannerSlot (sync merge; one-time claim receipt), FreshnessLine, OfflineNotice, InlineErrorRow (provider unreachable), QuietDayReceipt, WarmingSkeleton (instrument, row), MemberRow (collapsed), InviteRow, TextActionRow (outbound), DateSheet, ProvenanceSheet.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Reading order: title → address → scope → freshness → count → banner → band summary → band → link row → Set up your place → Just moved → Place → Risk & readiness → Civic → Dates → Money → People → Proof → More you can add → footer.\n- FactCount: \"11 things on file: place, dates, money, people.\"\n- Band: its summary plus \"The Dates list below has every date.\" A month reads: \"November: You, HOA dues Sunday 1 November, you added this. Your county, property tax second half due Monday 2 November, official. Your state, in-person voter registration until 8 PM Tuesday 3 November, official. Your city, pickup every Tuesday, you added this.\" A moved pickup is spoken with its new date.\n- Marks are never targets alone. Provenance = shape plus legend word; \"projected\" = word plus dash; statewide = bar shape. None rely on colour.\n- Visibility control: \"Visible to: Only you. Change who can see this.\"\n- Disabled Resend, Add and Send a new code stay focusable and read their reason. Banners, the deleted-date line and InlineUndo are status regions.\n- AX5: band keeps its lanes but scrolls sideways at readable scale, lane labels pinned, visible \"Earlier\" and \"Later\" buttons. FactRows stack label and value. Text wraps. \"Not now\" and \"Skip\" stack.\n\nCOPY (sentence case)\nEverything quoted above, plus:\n- Banners: \"Synced 3 items from your other device\" · \"Your pickup day, 3 dates and Ollie came with you. · See what moved\" · \"That date was removed.\"\n- Undo: “Hid “Move your utilities” · Undo” · “Skipped “When does your insurance renew?” · Undo”\n- All known: \"Everything we can hold about this place is on file\" (shown only when no asks remain).\n- Reports: \"Voter registration deadline · Checking · reported Sun 18 Oct · we'll check by Sun 25 Oct\" · \"Pickup day · Fixed Fri 16 Oct · recycling is every other Tuesday · Waste Connections\" · \"Property-tax appeal date · No change Wed 14 Oct · Clark County Board of Equalization lists Thu 1 Jul 2027, or 60 days after your notice\"\n- Member view: \"Maya can add bills here.\" · \"Maya can invite people here.\" · \"Maya can rename Ollie.\" · \"Maya can add and change dates here.\"\n- Voter done (Notes sample, Sat 24 Oct): \"You marked this done Sat 24 Oct · Only you\" · \"We can't check registration status.\"\n- Voter after online deadline (Notes sample, Tue 27 Oct): \"Voter registration · In person, Clark County Elections — in 7 days · until 8:00 PM Tue 3 Nov\", online line removed. After Tue 3 Nov the row leaves Dates and Civic reads \"No upcoming election\".\n- Appeal computed (Notes sample, Mon 10 May 2027, tick): \"Property-tax appeal · closes in 53 days · Fri 2 Jul 2027\" · \"60 days after your notice was mailed Mon 3 May\"\n- Offline: \"You're offline · as of 6:04 PM\" · \"Adding a date needs a connection.\" · \"Resending needs a connection.\" · after Mark done: \"Saved on this device. It'll sync.\"\n- Notifications off: \"Notifications are off. This date still shows here and on Today.\"\n- Errors: \"We couldn't load your place file just now · Retry\" · \"We couldn't reach Clark County's calendar just now · Retry\"\n- Done row: \"Done · You marked this done Tue 16 Feb · Reminders off\"\n\nEDGE CASES\n- Longest address \"Unit 1204, 10417 NE Hazel Dell Avenue, Vancouver, WA 98685\" wraps to two lines, never cut.\n- A month cell with 12 marks shows \"12\".\n- No dates: empty You lane; promoted ask \"Add one date that matters\".\n- Reminder link for a deleted date: top of screen, \"That date was removed.\", no modal, no blank.\n- Reminder dates show on rows whether notifications are on or off. If notifications are denied, ask 2 reads \"Add the widget\" (native) and the widget row ranks ahead of the reminder ask.\n- Slow network: skeleton only after 1 second; cached content never goes blank.\n- County rules fail to load: county lane not drawn, InlineErrorRow \"We couldn't reach Clark County's calendar just now · Retry\"; the rest of the file stays.\n- Approximate date: \"about Dec 2026\", counts as known, offers \"Add the exact day\".\n- A seeded rule not yet checked against its authority is hollow.\n- Widget placed: widget row gone (frame 17).\n- Member view (Sam): the Only-you warranty is hidden and not counted (\"10 on file\"); the Dec mark is gone from the You lane; summary \"Next 12 months: 8 dates, plus pickup every Tuesday. Next: voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct.\" Mover ticks are Sam's own, so \"Forward your mail\" is undone for him. Bills caption \"You and Maya can see these.\" Resend and the claim-receipt row are absent. \"Your home\" opens the read-only dashboard. Sam's Just moved runs Sun 18 Oct–Thu 17 Dec.\n- Guest: \"Bills · 3 on file\" with \"Maya can see and add bills here.\" A Guest without calendar.edit sees Dates rows with no Edit or Remind actions and one line \"Maya can add and change dates here.\"\n- Web: no widget row; ask 2 is \"Turn on a reminder\".\n- Phase-2 rows (Bills, Mail Day, bill compare, Keeper) are absent until shipped; the layout still works.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of keeping the old Place dashboard cards under the file, draw the file as the whole tab body — because this screen replaces them.\n- Instead of a five-segment ring or \"3 of 6\", draw \"11 on file\" with pips only for known categories — because any denominator reads as an unfinished task.\n- Instead of a button on every missing fact, draw one filled button, at most 3 promoted asks and the rest behind \"More you can add (3)\" — because about ten competing asks lowers completion.\n- Instead of day-accurate dots and an in-band \"Next 14 days\" label on phones, draw month clusters with counts, an 8pt sliver and the label as a link row — because about 0.8pt per day makes Mon 26 Oct, Mon 2 Nov and Tue 3 Nov overlap.\n- Instead of an even pickup rhythm all year, draw holiday moves and \"projected\" after Dec 2026 — because the hauler publishes one year at a time.\n- Instead of a dot or a visibility chip for a statewide deadline, draw a full-lane-height bar in \"Your state\" and the DateRow's statewide tag — because it is not a fact about this house.\n- Instead of the lease reminder on the lease-ends row, put the three reminders on the notice row — because a reminder tied to the lease end fires after the last day to act.\n- Instead of red X's, failure rows or an empty band on error, draw neutral invitations, one grey \"Not here\" row, and no band plus an InlineErrorRow — because missing is not broken and an empty band means \"checked, nothing found\".\n\nDONE WHEN\n- A lease end 5 months away is visible on the band and editable in Dates; the notice row holds the reminders.\n- Each frame has one obvious primary action above the fold, and each row has one target. Nothing reads as percent complete. A saved place looks smaller, not failing.\n- This count equals the keeper's count; Today's first-week row agrees about what is done.\n- Every statewide or county date shows its source and cannot be read as a claim about this house.\n- Scope is stated in the header, on each user-entered date and in the saved-place footer.\n- A reminder for a date beyond 14 days lands on that row; a deleted date lands with \"That date was removed.\"\n- Every ask can be declined and found again; the claim receipt, report outcomes and keeper re-entry can be found again.\n- A saved-place mover sees \"Update your voter registration\" once a move-in date is set.\n- The all-clear line appears only when no asks remain. The widget row disappears once placed.\n- Greyscale and AX5 frames still read correctly.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. x-place-file · ios · 01-dense-home · light — HOME A, Just moved open, all content above.\n2. x-place-file · ios · 02-saved-place-first-week · light — PLACE B: Set up your place, holiday move, skipped keeper row, grey \"Not here\" row.\n3. x-place-file · web-390 · 03-member-view · light — Sam's view: \"10 on file\", no Dec mark, 8-date summary, his own mover ticks, reasons naming Maya.\n4. x-place-file · ios · 04-dismissed-and-declined · light — \"Move your utilities\" collapsed to Undo; the insurance row's overflow open on Skip, then its collapsed InlineUndo.\n5. x-place-file · ios · 05-sync-merge · light — the sync banner, shown once.\n6. x-place-file · ios · 06-claim-receipt-banner · light — the one-time banner plus \"What moved when you claimed\".\n7. x-place-file · ios · 07-reminder-landing · light — Mon 15 Feb 2027, 7:00 AM. Band Feb 2027–Jan 2028; window Mon 15 Feb–Sun 28 Feb, so Mon 1 Mar sits just outside. No Just moved. Dates: \"Tell your landlord in writing by Mon 1 Mar 2027\" · \"in 14 days · Mon 1 Mar 2027\" (highlighted, focused) · \"Lease ends · in 44 days · Wed 31 Mar 2027\" · \"Property tax, 1st half · Due in 74 days · Fri 30 Apr 2027\" · \"Property-tax appeal · in 4 months · Thu 1 Jul 2027, or 60 days after your value notice was mailed\" · \"Property tax, 2nd half · Due in 8 months · Mon 1 Nov 2027\" · \"HOA dues · $285 · in 8 months · Mon 1 Nov 2027\".\n8. x-place-file · ios · 08-notice-done · light — Tue 16 Feb 2027: notice row quiet with tick and \"Reminders off\"; Lease ends stays.\n9. x-place-file · android · 09-postcard-pending · light — PLACE B, claim pending: the pending LockedActionRow, the \"Enter your code\" FactRow and the disabled \"Send a new code\" with its reason replace the \"Not here\" row.\n10. x-place-file · web-390 · 10-your-reports · light — the three reports expanded.\n11. x-place-file · ios · 11-all-known · light — Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM, variant where Maya's claim was completed by postcard: all three Just moved rows done and quiet (\"You marked this done …\"); \"Insurance renews · in 5 months · Sat 13 Mar 2027\" (Mar cell count 3, summary 10 dates); NW Natural $38.40 due Mon 9 Nov (Bills \"4 upcoming · $344.57 through Mon 9 Nov\"); Proof \"Address confirmed by postcard · Sat 17 Oct 2026\"; lease document; widget placed; appeal row shows its rule with no ask; More you can add absent. \"15 on file\", and \"Everything we can hold about this place is on file\" sits where More you can add was. No celebration.\n12. x-place-file · ios · 12-empty-year · light — layout premise: a claimed home with no seeded county or state rules, no pickup weekday on record and no dates; header \"Your household\" and \"1 on file\" (Place pip only); four empty labelled lanes plus \"Checked — nothing on file for the next year\"; promoted asks \"Set your pickup day\" and \"Add one date that matters\".\n13. x-place-file · ios · 13-loading · light — header plus instrument and row skeletons at full height.\n14. x-place-file · web-390 · 14-error · light — no band, InlineErrorRow \"We couldn't load your place file just now · Retry\".\n15. x-place-file · android · 15-offline · light — cached content, disabled actions with reasons, one offline Mark done with \"Saved on this device. It'll sync.\"\n16. x-place-file · web-1440 · 16-dense-home · light — exact days, leader line, two columns, no widget row.\n17. x-place-file · android · 17-dense-home-widget-placed · light — HOME A with no widget row.\n18. x-place-file · web-390 · 18-saved-place-mover · light — PLACE B after Jordan adds \"Moved in · Fri 9 Oct 2026\": \"3 on file\"; Just moved appears with caption \"Shown until Tue 8 Dec, 60 days after you moved in\" and its three rows, \"Update your voter registration\" first. Set up your place still shows, ask 2 reads \"Turn on a reminder\". Scope stays \"Saved place · Only you\".\n19. x-place-file · android · 19-deleted-date-landing · light — top of screen with \"That date was removed.\"\n20. x-place-file · ios · 20-ax5 · light — band scrolls sideways with pinned labels; rows stacked.\n21. x-place-file · ios · 21-greyscale · light — frame 1 in greyscale.\n22. x-place-file · ios · 01-dense-home · dark — dark twin of frame 1.\n23. x-place-file · ios · 02-saved-place-first-week · dark — dark twin of frame 2.\n24. Notes — Assumptions: Vancouver holiday calendar; seeded rules treated as checked; the count rule; frame 12's premise; frames 7–8 dated 2027; frame 11 as a postcard variant with all asks done; which Risk & readiness/Civic treatment you drew; Maya set the home move-in date on Sun 18 Oct after the claim, and a saved-place move-in date carries at claim; the 14-day notice lead is a custom lead set with ReminderLeadControl's \"other\" option; the helper \"Shows your moving list for 60 days\" must be used in home settings too; \"Open household calendar\" replaces \"Everyone here can see these\" to keep scope wording to the two ScopeChip strings. Row samples: voter done, voter after Mon 26 Oct and after Tue 3 Nov, appeal computed. Invented strings: PLACE B save date Sat 17 Oct; Tuesday set Sat 10 Oct; Sam's move-in = join date Sun 18 Oct; Fri 9 Oct move-in on PLACE B and Tue 8 Dec; postcard dates and \"Send a new code\"; longest address; deep-link URLs; frame 7, 11 and 12 rows; the Your reports dates; member-view lines; \"You can show these again in home settings.\"; \"Money, people and proof · Not here — this is a saved place\"; \"See how to update\"; \"Your home · Larkspur Loop\"; \"Mail Day\" and \"How your bills compare\"; offline, error and county-error lines; undo lines; notifications-off line; \"Open household calendar\"; widget thumbnail content; any cluster options. Omitted states: Guest bills and Guest dates rows (described in edge cases), all three mover rows dismissed.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: artboards 1–6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: 7–12, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 3: 13–18, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 4: 19–24.",
        "changeLog": [
          "ATTACH: screenshots now scoped to chrome only; old dashboard cards and old Just Moved card explicitly replaced; added matching INSTEAD OF line (review major)",
          "Exits and rows: added 'Your home · Larkspur Loop' row to the home dashboard, Money rows 'Mail Day' and 'How your bills compare', and the home documents list as the destination for the document ask (review major; FINAL f3-member-home-dashboard, f10-mail-day-triage, f10-bill-trend entries)",
          "Frame 18 now draws the flow-13 step 2 saved-place mover state (PLACE B with move-in Fri 9 Oct, Just moved until Tue 8 Dec, voter row first, web ask 2 'Turn on a reminder'); removed from omitted list (review major)",
          "Frame 11 all-known made consistent: all mover rows done, appeal ask removed, More you can add absent, all-clear line only when no asks remain; also stated in COPY and DONE WHEN (review major)",
          "Frame 12 empty year given an explicit premise (no seeded rules, no pickup weekday, '1 on file', two promoted asks) and listed on Notes",
          "Single-target rule: only first promoted ask has a filled button; asks 2-3 are chevron rows; Not now/Skip as small text buttons plus custom actions; mover dismiss/Mark done in overflow; quiet-ask Skip via overflow; frame 4 shows overflow",
