      {
        "id": "f1-today-air-band",
        "name": "Air quality band (and the alert landing)",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 24,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Air quality band and alert landing · f1-today-air-band\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Today\" (its air section). This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed.\n\nATTACH: The current Today air section and the sections above and below it (weather, alerts) on iOS 393, Android 412, web 390 and web 1440. Also attach Today's location row in both the \"Your household\" and \"Saved place · Only you\" versions, and the Foundations board from prompt 00.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852 (primary). Android 412x915. Web 390x844 and 1440x900. Draw the tray at true truncation on iOS 393 and Android 412.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE\nToday tab → Today → the air section, between weather and alerts. It is always drawn, on clean-air days too.\nEntry points:\n- Scrolling Today.\n- An air alert push (iOS and Android). It opens pantopus://today?section=air, scrolls this section into view and highlights it once. The push is sent when AQI crosses the person's chosen threshold (101, 151 or 201; the default is 101), for claimed homes and saved places alike. Widening alerts to saved places never widens pickup pushes.\n- Web has no push today. The web URL /app/today?section=air exists for links and email; on web the crossing is seen in-app.\n- NOAA warning pushes land on the alerts section directly below. The same scope-chip rule applies there.\n- A tap on the widget's air hero, via ?src=widget&section=air.\n- The \"Air today\" row of the Nearby compare scale strip.\n- While a crossing is active, Today shows one row under the location row: \"Unhealthy air now · AQI 176 · See air quality\", which scrolls here (that row is drawn in the Today tab prompt).\nHand-offs:\n- Tapping the band row opens the ProvenanceSheet air variant, reading \"Preliminary reading from AirNow, observed 4:00 PM\" and \"Covers: nearest monitors\", with the report control \"This reading looks wrong\".\n- The overflow button in the air section header has one item, \"Change alert level\". It opens Notification settings at Air & weather alerts. Changing it there never touches the pickup reminder.\n\nWHO AND WHEN\n- Maya Chen at HOME A, Mon 19 Oct. She sees Good at 7:40 AM and gets a Gorge-smoke alert at 4:00 PM (AQI 118, her threshold 101). She also saved her mother's address, \"Mom's house\", 415 NE Dogwood St, Camas, WA 98607, which reads AQI 176 at the same time.\n- Jordan Lee at PLACE B, his only place, gets the first push Pantopus has ever sent him (AQI 176, his threshold 151), about an address he only saved.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Show where today's air sits on EPA's scale at a glance, and make an alert land on the crossing, and the address, that caused it.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: The eye should land on three things, in this order: (1) the value line \"AQI 118 · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups · Fine particles (PM2.5)\", (2) the band with its marker, plus the threshold rule \"Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM\", (3) EPA's health statement. The address label and ScopeChip sit above the band in alert frames. The only action is tapping the row for the source.\n\nCONTENT (deltas to FIXTURES)\nIn every frame, the first value line writes the pollutant as \"Fine particles (PM2.5)\". Any later mention in the same frame says \"PM2.5\" alone.\n- Good. Dated 7:40 AM.\n  - Value line \"AQI 42 · Good · Fine particles (PM2.5)\".\n  - Health statement \"Air quality is satisfactory, and air pollution poses little or no risk.\"\n  - SourceCaption \"● AirNow · nearest monitors · today · observed 7:00 AM\".\n- Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups alert, HOME A. Dated 4:10 PM.\n  - Address row \"2418 NE Larkspur Loop\" with ScopeChip \"Your household\".\n  - Value line \"AQI 118 · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups · Fine particles (PM2.5)\".\n  - Threshold rule at 101, labelled \"Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM\".\n  - EPA statement \"Members of sensitive groups may experience health effects. The general public is less likely to be affected.\"\n  - Sensitive groups for PM2.5: \"People with heart or lung disease, older adults, children, and people of lower socioeconomic status.\"\n  - A separate line labelled \"Pantopus note\": \"Smoke from the Gorge. Keep windows shut tonight.\" Under it, the caption \"NOAA smoke forecast · 3:00 PM\".\n  - Caption \"● AirNow · nearest monitors · today · observed 4:00 PM\".\n- Unhealthy alert, PLACE B. Jordan chose 151.\n  - Address row \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\" with \"Saved place · Only you\".\n  - Value line \"AQI 176 · Unhealthy · Fine particles (PM2.5)\", with the rule labelled \"Crossed 151 at 4:00 PM\".\n  - EPA statement \"Some members of the general public may experience health effects; members of sensitive groups may experience more serious health effects.\" Below it, the same sensitive-groups line and the Pantopus note with its caption.\n- Alert about another saved place (frame 4), Maya, dated 4:05 PM. Today opens on Mom's house instead of HOME A.\n  - Location row \"415 NE Dogwood St · Saved place · Only you\", with a 44pt text action \"Back to Larkspur Loop\".\n  - Value line \"AQI 176 · Unhealthy · Fine particles (PM2.5)\", with the rule at Maya's own level, labelled \"Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM\".\n  - The same EPA statement, sensitive-groups line, Pantopus note and caption as the PLACE B alert.\n- Still unhealthy, PLACE B. Dated 6:10 PM.\n  - Value line \"AQI 182 · Unhealthy · Fine particles (PM2.5)\", with the rule still labelled \"Crossed 151 at 4:00 PM\".\n  - Caption \"Still above your alert level. We won't send another alert until it drops below 151 and crosses again.\"\n  - Beside the frame, the delivered notification updated in place to \"Unhealthy air: AQI 182\" / \"AirNow 6:00 PM\".\n- Stale. Dated 6:10 PM: \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM today — 11 hours ago\".\n- Hazardous, worst case: \"AQI 612 · Hazardous · Fine particles (PM2.5)\". The marker is clamped at the right end of the 301+ segment and the number is printed. Statement: \"Health warning of emergency conditions: everyone is more likely to be affected.\"\n- Pushes (PushCopy, iOS and Android only). Use one separator style everywhere: \"AirNow 4:00 PM\", with no comma.\n  - Jordan, PLACE B, at 151 or above: \"Unhealthy air: AQI 176\" / \"AirNow 4:00 PM\". Time Sensitive (iOS) / HIGH (Android). He has one place, so there is no street label.\n  - Maya, HOME A, below 151: \"Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups\" / \"AQI 118 · AirNow 4:00 PM · Larkspur Loop\" (40 characters). Active / DEFAULT. She has more than one place, so her bodies carry the street label.\n  - Maya, Mom's house, at 151 or above: \"Unhealthy air: AQI 176\" / \"AirNow 4:00 PM · Dogwood St\". Time Sensitive / HIGH.\n  - NOAA warning pushes are Time Sensitive / HIGH. Only a real threshold crossing or a NOAA warning may use that level.\n  - A worsening reading updates the existing alert instead of stacking a new one.\n  - Placeholder \"Air quality alert\". Android public version \"Pantopus · Air quality alert\".\n  - Show the street label only when the person has more than one place.\nOn Notes, flag every EPA sentence (Good, Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups, Unhealthy, Hazardous) and the PM2.5 sensitive-groups line with \"verify verbatim against EPA's AQI technical document before build\", and list every string you invent.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\nDraw one AqiBand at detail size, in this order: address row with ScopeChip (alert frames only), then the value line, then the track, then the EPA statement, then the Pantopus note and its caption, then the SourceCaption. Spell out \"air quality index (AQI)\" once, in the section title. The overflow button sits in the section header, outside the row target, at 44pt/48dp/44px.\n- The track has six equal-width segments in EPA ColorVision Assist hues: Good, Moderate, Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups, Unhealthy, Very Unhealthy, Hazardous (end label 301+).\n- Put 2px surface gaps between segments and a keyline of at least 3:1 in both themes.\n- The marker is a two-tone halo marker. Its position inside its segment follows the value within that category's range.\n- The band name and number are printed in text.primary beside the marker, never on a fill. Label the segment ends 0, 51, 101, 151, 201 and 301+.\n- The threshold rule is a 1.5px text.primary line at the person's own chosen value, with its crossing time.\n- Degraded states:\n  - No reading: the same track greyed, with no marker, and \"No reading for this address right now\".\n  - Provider failed: the greyed track plus InlineErrorRow.\n  - Stale: values stay and only this row greys, with its age in words.\n  - Loading: WarmingSkeleton track outline at the final height.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- The band row (everything below the section header) is one target and opens the ProvenanceSheet.\n- An alert arrival scrolls once, moves accessibility focus to the band and fades a highlight within 300ms. Under Reduce Motion, jump there, then fade.\n- When an alert is about a saved place other than the one in view, Today opens on the alerted place; \"Back to Larkspur Loop\" returns to the usual place with a cross-fade.\n- The marker does not animate on refresh.\n- \"Change alert level\" lives in the header overflow and is also a custom accessibility action on the row.\n- No haptics.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: AqiBand (variants: detail, no reading, alert, still above threshold with no new push; states: ready, stale, offline), ScopeChip, SourceCaption (live variant), FreshnessLine (per-fact stale), InlineErrorRow (provider unreachable), OfflineNotice, WarmingSkeleton (section), ProvenanceSheet (air reading), PushCopy (air).\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Reading order: section header and overflow, address and scope, value line, band, statements, Pantopus note, source.\n- Spoken band label: \"Air quality index 118, Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups, category 3 of 6. Your alert level 101, crossed at 4 PM. AirNow, observed 4 PM.\"\n- Chart summary sentence (visible to screen readers): \"Air is in category 3 of 6 on EPA's scale.\" Follow it with a list of the six categories and their ranges.\n- The separators and printed names carry the meaning in greyscale.\n- Targets: row 44pt on iOS, 48dp on Android, 44px on web; overflow button and \"Back to Larkspur Loop\" the same, with 8dp spacing.\n\nCOPY: Use every string listed in CONTENT, plus the following.\n- Section title: \"Air quality index (AQI)\".\n- Provider failed: \"We couldn't reach AirNow just now\" with \"Retry air quality\".\n- Offline: \"You're offline · as of 6:02 PM\".\n- Alerts blocked by the phone: amber glyph, text.primary line \"Air alerts are on, but notifications are off for Pantopus\", button \"Open settings\". Draw it only when the person turned Air & weather alerts on, or changed the alert level, in Notification settings, and the phone now blocks Pantopus. A default-on setting after a decline at the phone's prompt draws nothing extra.\n- No place: \"Today starts with a place\" / \"Save an address and Today will show its weather, air, alerts and dates.\" / \"Preview an address\".\n\nEDGE CASES\n- AX5: the value line wraps above a full-width track and the category labels move into the list below.\n- Values over 500 are clamped, with the number printed.\n- A claimed home always shows \"Your household\", and a saved place always shows \"Saved place · Only you\".\n- An alert about one saved place while Today uses another: Today opens on the alerted address (frame 4) and offers the way back.\n- A long address such as \"12817 NE Fourth Plain Blvd Unit 204\" wraps above the ScopeChip; the chip moves to its own line and never truncates.\n- With no place, the section is not drawn and no alert is ever sent.\n- If notifications are denied at the phone's prompt, the band renders fully in-app, with no amber line.\n- On a slow network, keep the last reading and its age. Show a skeleton only on a cold load.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a proportional 0–500 track, draw six equal segments with a 301+ end, because proportional widths squeeze the everyday 0–100 range to about a fifth of the bar.\n- Instead of the standard EPA hues or a brand-blue ramp, draw ColorVision Assist hues with gaps and a keyline, because neighbouring standard hues fall below 3:1.\n- Instead of writing the band name on the fill, print it in text.primary beside the marker, because text on yellow or maroon fails contrast.\n- Instead of a paraphrased health line such as \"satisfactory for everyone\", print EPA's statement and put Pantopus context on its own \"Pantopus note\" line with a source, because EPA lists inaccurate cautionary statements as a reporting error.\n- Instead of a fixed 101 line, mark the threshold the person chose, because the landing must match the rule that actually fired.\n- Instead of hiding the band on a clean day or when a fetch fails, draw Good with its marker, and No reading as a greyed track, because silence and failure must look different.\n- Instead of landing an alert about Mom's house on Larkspur Loop's band, open Today on the alerted place with a way back, because the screen must agree with the push about the address.\n- Instead of a settings link for someone who declined notifications, draw nothing extra, because repeated pressure after a denial goes against platform guidance.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The alert landing agrees with the push about the address, the threshold and the time: Jordan's 176 push has no label and lands on Birchfield Ct; Maya's 118 push says Larkspur Loop and lands on HOME A; Maya's Dogwood St push lands on Mom's house.\n- The push level matches the event: Time Sensitive only at 151 or above or for a NOAA warning.\n- Good, No reading, Stale and Offline are four visibly different pictures.\n- Every frame reads correctly in greyscale, and the marker reaches 3:1 on every segment, including maroon, in light and dark.\n- The still-unhealthy frame shows that no second push was sent and the first was updated in place.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f1-today-air-band · ios · 01-good · light — dense default at 7:40 AM inside Today\n2. f1-today-air-band · ios · 02-alert-usg-household · light — arrived from push, highlight, rule at 101\n3. f1-today-air-band · ios · 03-alert-unhealthy-saved-place · light — PLACE B, rule at 151\n4. f1-today-air-band · ios · 04-alert-other-saved-place · light — Maya lands on 415 NE Dogwood St, Saved place · Only you, \"Back to Larkspur Loop\", rule at 101\n5. f1-today-air-band · ios · 05-still-unhealthy-no-new-push · light — AQI 182, plus the same notification updated in place\n6. f1-today-air-band · ios · 06-stale · light\n7. f1-today-air-band · ios · 07-no-reading · light\n8. f1-today-air-band · ios · 08-provider-failed · light\n9. f1-today-air-band · ios · 09-offline · light\n10. f1-today-air-band · ios · 10-alerts-on-os-blocked · light — amber line with Open settings\n11. f1-today-air-band · ios · 11-no-place · light — Today starts with a place, no air section\n12. f1-today-air-band · ios · 12-hazardous-over-500 · light\n13. f1-today-air-band · ios · 13-loading · light\n14. f1-today-air-band · ios · 14-tray · light — Time Sensitive 176 (no label), Active 118 (Larkspur Loop), Time Sensitive 176 (Dogwood St), hidden preview\n15. f1-today-air-band · android · 14-tray · light — collapsed, expanded, public version\n16. f1-today-air-band · android · 02-alert-usg-household · light\n17. f1-today-air-band · web-390 · 02-alert-usg-household · light — opened from Today during an active crossing, no highlight\n18. f1-today-air-band · web-1440 · 01-good · light\n19. f1-today-air-band · ios · 15-ax5 · light — alert at AX5\n20. f1-today-air-band · ios · 16-greyscale · light — frame 2 in greyscale\n21. f1-today-air-band · ios · 01-good · dark\n22. f1-today-air-band · ios · 03-alert-unhealthy-saved-place · dark\n23. f1-today-air-band · ios · 12-hazardous-over-500 · dark — marker contrast on maroon\n24. f1-today-air-band · Notes — must list: assumptions (stale after 2 hours; PM2.5 is the dominant pollutant at 7:40 AM; Maya's saved place \"Mom's house\" at 415 NE Dogwood St, Camas, and its 176 reading; the Pantopus note source \"NOAA smoke forecast · 3:00 PM\"); every invented string; the EPA text to verify; that \"Pantopus note\" is used instead of \"From Pantopus\" because the glossary reserves \"From Pantopus\" for the curated-post chip (open naming decision); that the default threshold is 101 per the research brief and f4-notification-settings must select 101, not 151; that \"Change alert level\" is used where flow-10 says \"Turn these off\", so the flow needs updating; that the push body drops the comma in \"AirNow 4:00 PM\" to fit 40 characters; that air alert pushes on web assume a new web-push channel, which does not exist today, and without it web shows the crossing only in-app (and by email, if built); that frame 4 is the proposed answer to the open product decision of how Today switches to an alerted place other than the one in view; that the backend currently alerts only the newest saved place per user, so Mom's house is assumed to be Maya's newest, and the team must decide whether other saved places alert; that the review suggested marking 151 on frame 4 but the rule marks Maya's own level, 101; omitted states: \"OS permission denied — in-app only\" (renders identically to frames 1 and 2) and \"location source none\" (covered by frame 11)\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: 1-6, then wait for continue.\nTurn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue.\nTurn 3: 13-18, then wait for continue.\nTurn 4: 19-24.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Added frame 4 '04-alert-other-saved-place': Maya's alert about her saved place 'Mom's house' (415 NE Dogwood St, Camas) opens Today on that place with 'Back to Larkspur Loop'; push 'Unhealthy air: AQI 176' / 'AirNow 4:00 PM · Dogwood St'; Notes calls it the proposed answer to the open decision (review major, flow-10 moment of truth)",
          "Rule on frame 4 marks Maya's own level (101), not 151 as the review text suggested, to keep 'mark the threshold the person chose'; recorded on Notes",
          "Web push assumption made explicit: pushes are iOS/Android only; web-390 frame 17 is now 'opened from Today during an active crossing, no highlight'; Notes records the missing web-push channel (review major + minor)",
          "Notes records default threshold 101 and that f4-notification-settings must select 101, not 151 (flows-spec flow-10)",
          "Renamed the context line label to 'Pantopus note' because the glossary reserves 'From Pantopus'; logged as an open naming decision",
          "Pollutant gloss now plain meaning first: 'Fine particles (PM2.5)' on each frame's first value line; FIRST FIVE SECONDS updated; PM2.5-dominant-at-7:40 assumption on Notes",
          "Notes adds the backend newest-saved-place audience rule and the decision it needs",
          "Notes lists 'OS permission denied — in-app only' and 'location source none' as omitted states",
          "Amber line condition reworded so a default-on setting after an OS decline draws nothing",
          "Replaced 'Today's pinned slot' with the concrete active-crossing row 'Unhealthy air now · AQI 176 · See air quality' drawn in the Today tab prompt",
          "Still-unhealthy frame now shows the delivered notification updated in place to 'Unhealthy air: AQI 182'; long-address edge case added",
          "Renumbered artboards to follow manifest order (24 frames)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f4-briefing-optin-card",
        "name": "Briefing opt-in (morning + night-before, one card)",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 29,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Briefing opt-in card · f4-briefing-optin-card\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Today\". You are adding one card. This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed. On iOS and Android this card is net-new; no briefing control exists outside Settings today. On web, this card replaces the old morning-only opt-in that sat in the home-only Place > Today detail. In that old location (frame 11 only), draw one FactRow (known variant, trailing chevron) with the label \"Briefings\" and the value \"Now on Today and in Notification settings\"; the row opens Notification settings, so home users who used the old opt-in are not stranded.\n\nATTACH:\n- Populated Today on web 390, iOS 393, Android 412 and web 1440, at HOME A and at PLACE B, with the pickup card and the first-week row visible.\n- The old web Place > Today detail with its morning opt-in.\n- The Today empty state \"Today starts with a place\".\n- The Foundations board from prompt 00.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: Web 390x844 (primary). iOS 393x852. Android 412x915. Web 1440x900.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE\nToday tab → Today, below the day's content and above the FirstWeekRow (\"Next: …\"). It shows for anyone with a place: a saved place or a claimed home. Neither owning nor verifying a home is required.\nEntry points:\n- Scrolling Today.\n- Coming back to Today after the pickup card's reminder ask.\n  - If the person said yes there, the night-before row is already collapsed to \"The night before pickup · 6:00 PM · Change\", showing the time they never chose so they can change it. The card does not re-ask or scroll.\n  - While that ask is open, the night-before row here is hidden.\n  - If the person chose \"Not now\" or \"No thanks\" there, the night-before row stays hidden, with the same meaning. The card shows only the morning row.\n- Its durable twin is Notification settings. The card's \"Notification settings\" link and each row's \"Change\" open it at Briefings.\nHand-offs: \"Yes\" on a row opens the system permission dialog directly (on web, the browser's). There is never a second primer. On grant, the row expands into time chips. A grant from either row also turns the evening briefing on (see INTERACTION).\n\nWHO AND WHEN\n- Maya Chen at HOME A, Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM, scrolling past tomorrow's pickup card. For this card, HOME A's pickup is the household rule Sam confirmed (Recycling and garbage, Tuesday).\n- Jordan Lee at PLACE B, who has only saved an address and has not set his pickup day (the City of Camas Thursday is shown hollow).\n- Maya again on her iPhone after turning briefings on in the web app (web-to-native move).\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Let anyone with a place turn on the night-before and morning briefings right here, show exactly what will arrive, and say honestly what won't.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: The eye should land on three things, in this order: (1) the top row question \"The night before pickup?\", (2) its caption \"Pickup comes with the evening briefing (6:00 PM)\" and the small tray preview under it, (3) the \"Yes\" / \"Not now\" / \"No thanks\" buttons under row 1. Each row has one decision, \"Yes\", with equal-weight declines beside it.\n\nCONTENT (deltas to FIXTURES)\nThe card has no title. It holds two list rows and one footer.\n- Row 1: \"The night before pickup?\" with the caption \"Pickup comes with the evening briefing (6:00 PM)\". In the never-asked state only, a compact PushCopy tray preview sits under the caption: \"Recycling + garbage tomorrow\" / \"Bins out tonight · curbside by 6:30 AM\", captioned \"This is the whole thing.\" Buttons: \"Yes\", \"Not now\", \"No thanks\". Chips after Yes: 5:00 PM · 6:00 PM (selected) · 7:00 PM · 8:00 PM.\n- Row 2: \"A morning heads-up?\" with the caption \"Date reminders at 7:00 AM\". Same three buttons. Chips after Yes: 6:30 AM · 7:00 AM (selected) · 7:30 AM · 8:00 AM.\n- Silence line, printed once for the whole card: \"Only when something needs you. No news means nothing's up.\"\n- Footer link: \"Notification settings\".\n- Collapsed on-rows: \"The night before pickup · 6:00 PM · Change\" and \"Morning briefing · 7:00 AM · Change\".\n- Quiet-night receipt, shown only when every check succeeded. Frame dated Wed 21 Oct, 6:10 PM: \"Checked 6:00 PM · nothing needs you tonight\". It is spoken as \"Checked at 6 PM: weather, air, alerts, your calendar. Nothing needs you tonight.\"\n- Saved place, PLACE B, no pickup day set by Jordan (city weekday only, hollow). Row 1 caption: \"Pickup is included once you set your pickup day. Until then, it only covers dates you've added.\" Trailing text action \"Set your pickup day\", which scrolls to the pickup card (or opens the DateSheet in pickup mode if the card is not on screen). The row 1 tray preview shows a date example instead: \"Tomorrow: truck rental return\" / \"Due by 10:00 AM · you added this\". Footer adds \"Briefings follow your saved place, 1107 NE Birchfield Ct.\" The caption and the text action disappear once Jordan sets his weekday, even if frequency is still Not set.\n- Declined in the card, per row: InlineUndo \"No night-before briefing · You can turn it on in Notification settings · Undo\" and \"No morning briefing · You can turn it on in Notification settings · Undo\". \"Not now\" shows \"No night-before briefing for now · Undo\" or \"No morning briefing for now · Undo\".\n- On in the app but blocked by the system: an amber glyph with the text.primary line \"Notifications are off for Pantopus\" and the button \"Open settings\". On web, the line is \"Notifications are off for Pantopus in this browser\" with \"How to turn them on\".\n- Declined at the system dialog (native): the card collapses to one text.secondary line, \"Pickup still shows here on Today · Or put it on your home screen\", with \"Show me how\". Shown once.\n- Declined at the browser dialog (web): the card collapses to one text.secondary line, \"Pickup still shows here on Today\", with no widget offer. Shown once.\n- On for web, not on this phone (iOS): \"The night before pickup · On in your browser\" and \"Turn on for this iPhone\".\n- Timezone caption \"Pacific Time\", placed beside the times. Show it only when the device is outside Pacific time.\n- FirstWeekRow on frames 3 and 4: \"Next: add one date or person →\".\nList every string you invent on the Notes artboard.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\nDraw one card on surface.base with two stacked list rows, each at least 56pt tall, night-before first.\n- Each row holds the question in body, the caption in bodySmall text.secondary, the tray preview (row 1, never-asked only) as a small inset on surface.raised, and a button row beneath.\n- Draw \"Yes\", \"Not now\" and \"No thanks\" as three equal outlined buttons, each at least 44pt/48dp/44px.\n- On grant, a row expands in place into one ChoiceChip row directly beneath it. The card grows and Today reflows below it. Do not use a modal or a separate time picker.\n- When both rows are on, each collapses to one value + Change line, night-before first. The card shrinks to about a third of its expanded height, so Today gets quieter as the person commits.\n- The amber line sits above both rows, full width, and only when a row is on and the system blocks delivery. A switch can never read on beneath an unread warning.\n- The silence line and the receipt sit at the foot of the card, above the settings link.\n- Loading: until the permission state is known, the card slot is a WarmingSkeleton (section) at the height of two rows. No row claims on or off.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- \"Yes\" opens the system dialog.\n  - If permission is already granted, \"Yes\" turns the row on and expands the chips with no dialog.\n  - On grant, the row expands its chips (under 300ms; cross-fade under Reduce Motion) and focus stays on the row.\n  - A grant from the morning row also turns the night-before row on, collapsed to \"The night before pickup · 6:00 PM · Change\", unless the night-before row was declined. A grant from the night-before row leaves the morning row asking.\n  - On Android, after a first denial the row stays with \"Yes\", which re-asks once. It collapses after the second denial, and only \"Open settings\" is offered if a row is on.\n  - On Android 12 and below, \"Yes\" turns the row on with no dialog.\n  - On iOS, \"Open settings\" opens the Pantopus notification page.\n  - On web, a browser decline collapses the card to its web line with no widget offer.\n- Tapping a chip saves at once. Show \"Saving…\", then \"Saved\" as polite live-region text on the row.\n- An expanded chip row collapses to its value + Change line when the person leaves Today.\n- \"Not now\" hides the row and never asks again on its own. \"No thanks\" records a lasting decline, stored on the server and reversible in settings. Both show the per-row InlineUndo until the person leaves Today. After that, the slot closes.\n- Once any briefing is on, the FirstWeekRow below moves on to its next step.\n- Play one light haptic tick only when a chip save succeeds (native).\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: NotificationAsk (card row form; time chips expansion; states: never asked, granted, declined, switch on but OS blocked, saving/Saved/Couldn't save; Android denied once), PushCopy (tray preview, compact), ChoiceChip (time), QuietDayReceipt (widget one-liner variant), InlineUndo (declined ask), InlineErrorRow (save failed), OfflineNotice, WarmingSkeleton (section), FactRow (known, old web location pointer), FirstWeekRow (neighbour; moves on to \"Next: add one date or person →\" once a briefing is on).\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Reading order: amber line (if present), row 1 (night before), its caption, its tray preview, its buttons or chips, row 2 (morning), its chips, silence line, receipt, settings link.\n- Each time chip has a hit target of at least 44pt / 48dp / 44px, with 8dp gaps. Chips show selection with a check and a fill, not colour alone. The focus ring must look different from selection.\n- At AX5, chips become radio rows and the three buttons stack.\n- Spoken row labels:\n  - \"Night-before briefing, off. Pickup comes with the evening briefing at 6 PM.\"\n  - \"Night-before briefing, on, 6 PM. Change.\"\n  - \"Morning briefing, off. Date reminders at 7 AM.\"\n- The tray preview is spoken as \"Example notification: Recycling and garbage tomorrow. Bins out tonight, curbside by 6:30 AM.\"\n- Spoken button labels: \"Turn on the night-before briefing\", \"Not now, night-before briefing\", \"No thanks, night-before briefing\"; \"Turn on the morning briefing\", \"Not now, morning briefing\", \"No thanks, morning briefing\". Retry is spoken as \"Retry saving briefing time\".\n- Status is announced without moving focus.\n\nCOPY: Use every string listed in CONTENT, plus the following.\n- Save error: \"We couldn't save your briefing time\" with \"Retry\". The row keeps its last saved value.\n- Offline: \"You're offline · as of 6:02 PM\", with \"Changing briefings needs a connection.\" under the disabled controls.\n- No place: the card is absent, and Today shows \"Today starts with a place\" / \"Save an address and Today will show its weather, air, alerts and dates.\" / \"Preview an address\".\n\nEDGE CASES\n- Both rows expanded at once at 390 wide: the chips wrap to two lines rather than scroll.\n- One row on and one off; both on; both declined (the card is absent).\n- A saved place without a set pickup day: the evening row still works for dates the person adds, and pickup is never promised. Air alerts are a separate setting and are not promised here.\n- The device is outside Pacific time.\n- The system permission is granted on web but not on this phone.\n- A decline in the pickup card's ask: only the morning row shows.\n- A slow save keeps the chip selected with \"Saving…\" and shows no spinner card.\n- The receipt is never shown while a check is pending or failed.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of two separate opt-in cards or a modal, draw one card with two rows that expand in place, because two competing asks create a ranking problem, and a modal trains dismissal.\n- Instead of the morning row on top, put the night-before row first, because it is the pickup trigger and the ask a person with a pickup rule needs most.\n- Instead of a primer with its own \"Yes\" or \"Allow\" before the system dialog, send \"Yes\" straight to the system dialog and show the exact notification inside the row, because a second yes is redundant and the preview is what makes the ask clear.\n- Instead of a permanent amber banner for someone who declined, collapse the card to one neutral line plus a one-time widget offer (native only), because repeated pressure after a denial goes against Android guidance.\n- Instead of a toggle that reads on while the system blocks delivery, show the amber line above the rows, because the card must match what the phone will actually deliver.\n- Instead of gating either row behind claiming or verifying a home, show both to anyone with a saved place, because turning on either briefing is how a saved-place user counts toward activation.\n- Instead of a caption promising bills, alerts or pickup to a saved place without a set day, name only what the evening briefing carries, because a saved place has no bills, air alerts are a separate setting, and pickup waits for the person's own day.\n- Instead of \"6:00pm\" and an always-on \"Pacific Time.\" caption, write \"6:00 PM\" and show the timezone only outside Pacific time, because the research brief's microcopy rules say so.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- A saved-place user can turn on either briefing from Today in two taps: \"Yes\", then the system prompt.\n- The person sees the exact notification before the system prompt.\n- What each row shows always matches the device's real permission, and nothing claims on or off before the permission is known.\n- Today never asks the night-before question twice, whether the answer came from this card or the pickup card.\n- A declined ask names the row that was declined, never reappears on its own, and can be turned on again from settings.\n- The silence line and receipt make a quiet night read as finished work.\n- Every frame reads correctly in greyscale and at AX5.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 01-never-asked · light — dense default under a populated Today at HOME A, night-before row first with its tray preview\n2. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 02-yes-time-chips · light — night-before row expanded, 6:00 PM selected\n3. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 03-one-on-one-off · light — night-before collapsed on top, morning row still asking, FirstWeekRow moved on\n4. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 04-both-on-collapsed · light — Wed 21 Oct quiet-night receipt, FirstWeekRow moved on\n5. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 05-granted-from-morning · light — morning chips expanded, night-before already collapsed to \"6:00 PM · Change\"\n6. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 06-saved-place · light — PLACE B, set-your-pickup-day caption and action, date tray preview, footer names Birchfield Ct\n7. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 07-saving · light\n8. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 08-save-error · light\n9. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 09-on-but-blocked · light — amber line above rows\n10. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 10-declined-undo · light — \"No night-before briefing · …\" InlineUndo, morning row still asking\n11. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 11-slot-closed · light — Today with the card absent, plus the old Place > Today location with its Briefings FactRow\n12. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 12-loading · light — WarmingSkeleton at two-row height\n13. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 13-no-place · light — Today starts with a place\n14. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 14-offline · light\n15. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 15-declined-at-browser · light — one neutral line, no widget offer\n16. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 16-after-pickup-decline · light — only the morning row\n17. f4-briefing-optin-card · ios · 01-never-asked · light\n18. f4-briefing-optin-card · ios · 17-declined-at-os-widget-offer · light\n19. f4-briefing-optin-card · ios · 09-on-but-blocked · light — Open settings\n20. f4-briefing-optin-card · ios · 18-this-phone-not-on · light — device set to Eastern Time; the times keep the caption \"Pacific Time\" because briefings follow the place's time zone\n21. f4-briefing-optin-card · android · 04-both-on-collapsed · light\n22. f4-briefing-optin-card · android · 09-on-but-blocked · light\n23. f4-briefing-optin-card · android · 19-denied-once-reask · light — row kept with Yes after the first denial\n24. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-1440 · 01-never-asked · light\n25. f4-briefing-optin-card · ios · 20-ax5 · light — chips as radio rows, stacked buttons\n26. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 21-greyscale · light — frame 2 in greyscale\n27. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 01-never-asked · dark\n28. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 09-on-but-blocked · dark\n29. f4-briefing-optin-card · Notes — must list: every invented string (including the saved-place caption, action and footer, the date tray preview, and the Briefings FactRow); that HOME A's pickup rule here is Sam's confirmed rule so the tray preview says \"Recycling + garbage\"; that the Briefings FactRow is drawn only if Place > Today still ships before the Today merge; that a grant from the morning row turns the evening briefing on, per the research brief's default-after-grant rule; that the quiet-night receipt is the one-line variant with a spoken check list, and the full per-provider receipt lives on Today's quiet-day state; that loading is also covered by the Today cold-load frame; that web rows assume a new web-push channel for briefings (backend plus service worker), which does not exist today, and that without it the web rows are not drawn and web relies on Today and an email trigger (flow-01 failure branch); that the \"Why didn't I get one?\" link is omitted because the receipt line here and the skipped-night row in Notification settings carry that answer; omitted states\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: 1-6, then wait for continue.\nTurn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue.\nTurn 3: 13-18, then wait for continue.\nTurn 4: 19-24, then wait for continue.\nTurn 5: 25-29.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Added the research brief's default-after-grant rule: a grant from the morning row also turns the night-before row on (collapsed, unless declined); new frame 5 '05-granted-from-morning' (review major; ux-research-brief §3)",
          "Saved-place condition now keyed to 'no pickup day set by Jordan' (not frequency); caption rewritten to 'Pickup is included once you set your pickup day. Until then, it only covers dates you've added.' with trailing 'Set your pickup day' action; caption disappears once the weekday is set (review major + minor; design doc F4/F5)",
          "Added a compact PushCopy tray preview under row 1 in the never-asked state ('Recycling + garbage tomorrow' / 'Bins out tonight · curbside by 6:30 AM', 'This is the whole thing.'), a date example for PLACE B, PushCopy in FOUNDATIONS, preview in reading order (review major; brief P6)",
          "Time chip hit targets stated as 44pt / 48dp / 44px with 8dp gaps",
          "Old-location pointer is now a FactRow (known, chevron) 'Briefings' / 'Now on Today and in Notification settings', drawn only if Place > Today survives the merge (two review findings conflicted: TextActionRow outbound vs FactRow; chose FactRow because the link is internal, not outbound)",
          "Timezone INSTEAD OF reason now cites the research brief's microcopy rules",
          "Quiet-night receipt keeps the one-liner but gets a spoken check list; Notes says the full receipt lives on Today's quiet-day state",
          "Timezone frame clarified: device on Eastern Time, times captioned 'Pacific Time'",
          "Decline InlineUndo strings are now per row (night-before / morning), for both Not now and No thanks",
          "FIRST FIVE SECONDS third item now the button row; FirstWeekRow moves on to 'Next: add one date or person →' on frames 3 and 4 and is listed as changed",
          "Added loading: WarmingSkeleton (section) at two-row height with no on/off claim; new frame 12 and a Notes entry",
          "Renumbered artboards to follow manifest order; frame count 27 → 29"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f4-notification-primer",
        "name": "Notification permission primer",
        "platforms": [
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": true,
        "frameCount": 17,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Notification permission primer · f4-notification-primer\n\nTYPE: NEW. Nothing like it exists in the Pantopus design system yet. Build it only from existing tokens, sheet styles and Foundations components.\n\nATTACH: The Mail tab notification list showing its push-off banner ('Push is off. You'll still see these here.'). Today on iOS and Android, showing the PickupCard (confirmed and confirmed-just-now states) and the briefing card (NotificationAsk in its card-row form). The place file (Place tab) showing its pickup row. The Date sheet on its pickup-day kind. Draw these hosts exactly as the screenshots show. Change them only where a state below says so. Where you draw the PickupCard, use the Foundations PickupCard button labels.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852: a sheet at medium detent with a grabber and a top bar with Close. It may scroll at large text sizes. Android 412x915: a Material 3 modal bottom sheet with a drag handle. Draw no web version: the web briefing card asks for browser permission itself.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: The sheet belongs to no tab. It opens over the screen where the person acted. It has no deep link, and it never opens at launch, sign-up or save. This sheet replaces the system prompt that iOS fires at cold launch today; that launch-time request is removed, so nothing asks on first launch. The primer never opens by itself. It opens only when the person taps an ask on an indirect entry.\nEntry points (the only two):\n1. Over Mail, when the person taps 'Turn on' in the push-off banner to get household updates on this phone. Never asked: the default Mail variant. iOS denied, Android denied once or Android blocked: the matching denied variant.\n2. Android only, denied once (the system says a reason should be shown): 'Turn on reminders' in the host's inline reminder ask opens the sheet in its denied-once pickup variant. The host is Today (the PickupCard) or the place file (the line under the pickup row).\nWhere it does not open:\n- After a pickup day saves in the Date sheet, the Date sheet closes first. The host then shows its own inline ask, 'Remind you the night before? 6:00 PM · Turn on reminders': on Today, the PickupCard's confirmed-just-now state; in the place file, the same line under the pickup row. On a phone never asked, tapping it opens the system dialog directly. The primer never stacks on the Date sheet and never follows the save. If the save failed, no ask appears; the card keeps its hollow mark and shows Retry.\n- iOS denied or Android blocked: the PickupCard and place file show no inline reminder ask. Only the Mail banner's 'Turn on' and the Notifications settings page lead to Open Settings.\n- Yes on the briefing card opens the system dialog directly, because the card already explains the request and a second screen would be a second 'Yes'.\nWhat it receives: the entry (Mail or pickup), the phone's permission state, and for pickup the confirmed weekday and the place's street label. What happens next: Continue opens the system dialog. After Allow, the person is back on the host. From Mail, Allow also switches Household activity on (it is off until switched on) and the banner reads 'Household updates are on · Change'. After any grant, Today's briefing card evening row reads '6:00 PM · Change', because evening is on by default after a grant; the morning row keeps asking. Focus returns to the control that opened the sheet: the Mail banner's Turn on, or the host's inline ask.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM. Maya Chen is at HOME A on her iPhone. She opens Mail and sees 'Sam marked Clark PUD paid' in the notification list under the banner 'Push is off. You'll still see these here.' She wants that kind of update on her phone and taps 'Turn on'. She has never been asked about notifications on this iPhone.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Show the exact notification the person is about to allow, then hand them to the system dialog without asking 'Yes' a second time.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: First, the title and the tray preview directly under it (the tray is the largest element). Second, the one-sentence body. Third, 'Continue' with 'Your phone will ask next.' under it. Continue is the only primary action.\n\nCONTENT (fixtures apply; these are the deltas)\nDelta: Maya also has a saved place, 'Grandma's', at 5200 SE Columbia River Dr, Vancouver. That second place is why each tray shows a street label.\nMail entry (default). Title: 'Household updates on this phone'. Body: 'Quiet updates from your household. Pickup the night before. Air alerts when it's unhealthy. Sign-in alerts for your account. Nothing else unless you turn it on.' Tray preview (PushCopy, bill paid): app name 'Pantopus', time '6:00 PM', title 'Sam marked Clark PUD paid', body 'Due Fri 23 Oct · Larkspur Loop'. Caption under the tray, line 1: 'This is the whole thing.' Line 2: 'Arrives quietly — no sound.' No amount appears on any tray.\nPickup entry (Android denied once only). Title: 'A reminder the night before pickup'. Body: 'Pickup the night before. Air alerts when it's unhealthy. Sign-in alerts for your account. Nothing else unless you turn it on.' Tray preview (PushCopy, confirmed pickup, the canonical string): title 'Recycling + garbage tomorrow' (28 characters), body 'Bins out tonight · Larkspur Loop'. Caption: 'This is the whole thing.'\nWorst case: the longest street labels, 'Due Fri 23 Oct · Columbia River Dr' and 'Bins out tonight · Columbia River Dr'. If a body does not fit, the preview truncates it at true width with a trailing ellipsis. Titles never truncate, because they stay within 30 characters.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION: Stack from top to bottom: grabber and top bar with Close (iOS) or drag handle (Android), title (h3), tray preview, caption (one or two lines), body (body 16/24), actions, caption under the button. The tray preview is the hero. Draw it at true tray proportions, inset on surface.raised over a surface.sunken well, with the platform's own notification anatomy. On iOS: rounded app icon, 'Pantopus', time, bold title, one body line. On Android: small monochrome icon, app name, a bullet, time. Frame it as an in-app illustration inside the sheet, with rounded corners and no system shadow. It must never look like a system alert or a live banner. The caveat-first rule protects honesty: an unconfirmed pickup's title is 'Unconfirmed: pickup tomorrow', so truncation can never cut the caveat. The specimen artboards prove this. If the street label is missing (one place only), drop it and keep 'Bins out tonight' or 'Due Fri 23 Oct'. Denied variants keep the same stack, replace the body with the two denied lines for that entry, and swap the actions.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\niOS default: one filled button, 'Continue', which opens the system dialog. The sheet has no 'Not now' button. Close sits in the top bar only, and swipe-down also closes. Closing does not fire the system dialog, and the sheet never reopens on its own.\niOS denied: one filled 'Open Settings' button, which opens Pantopus's notification page in iOS Settings. Close stays only in the top bar.\nAndroid default: 'Continue' and 'Not now' as peer buttons of the same height and weight. 'Not now' is this sheet's visible close: it closes the sheet and never fires the system dialog, so no denial is spent. It never re-presents the sheet on its own; the ask returns only when the person taps an ask again. Back behaves like 'Not now'. The permanent decline lives on the briefing card and in Settings.\nAndroid denied once: 'Continue' (fires the system dialog again) and 'Not now', as peers. Android blocked: 'Open Settings' (opens the Pantopus notification page) and 'Not now', as peers.\nThe sheet presents with the platform's standard sheet motion (300ms or less). Under Reduce Motion it cross-fades. The tray preview does not animate. Continue, Close, Open Settings and Not now have no haptic.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: NotificationAsk (variants primer iOS, primer Android, iOS denied, Android denied once, Android blocked; card-row form on the host). PushCopy (tray preview: bill paid, confirmed pickup, unconfirmed pickup, hidden-preview placeholders). PickupCard (host: confirmed, confirmed-just-now with the inline ask, error). NotificationRow (host: push-off banner and its granted line). OfflineNotice (queued writes). InlineErrorRow (save failed).\n\nACCESSIBILITY: Reading order: title, tray preview, caption, body, buttons, caption under the button. The tray is one element, spoken as 'Example notification: Sam marked Clark PUD paid. Due Friday 23 October, Larkspur Loop.' (pickup: 'Example notification: Recycling plus garbage tomorrow. Bins out tonight, Larkspur Loop.'). The sheet title is unique, focus stays inside the sheet, and focus returns to the control that opened it when the sheet closes. Buttons are 44pt on iOS and 48dp on Android, with 8dp between them. Button labels carry the meaning, never colour.\n\nCOPY\nButtons: 'Continue' · 'Not now' (Android only) · 'Open Settings' · 'Close' (iOS top bar only).\nCaption under Continue: 'Your phone will ask next.'\nDenied line 1 (both entries): 'Notifications are off for Pantopus on this phone.'\nDenied line 2, Mail entry: 'Household updates still show here in Mail.' Pickup entry: 'Pickup still shows on Today.'\nHost inline ask: 'Remind you the night before? 6:00 PM · Turn on reminders'.\nSave error, pickup entry: 'Couldn't save your reminder · Retry'. Save error, Mail entry: 'Couldn't turn on household updates · Retry'.\nOffline caption, Mail entry: 'You're offline. Household updates will turn on when you're back online.' Pickup entry: 'You're offline. Your reminder will save when you're back online.'\nMail banner after a grant: 'Household updates are on · Change'.\n\nEDGE CASES: Already granted: the sheet never appears. Mail 'Turn on' when the phone is already granted: no sheet; Household activity switches on in place, the banner reads 'Household updates are on · Change', and Change opens Notifications settings at /app/settings/notifications?group=household. A save that failed: no ask and no sheet. Offline: Continue still works, and the preference write is queued. Android denied once: Continue fires the system dialog again. A second denial blocks, and after that only Open Settings is offered. Android before version 13 needs no runtime prompt, so the sheet never appears. Large text: the tray preview grows with its own text and wraps its body to two lines. Hidden previews on the lock screen: the tray shows 'Pantopus · Household update' or 'Pantopus · Pickup reminder'.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a 'Yes' or 'Allow' button, draw 'Continue' with 'Your phone will ask next.' under it — because the system dialog is the decision and a lookalike Allow is manipulative.\n- Instead of a bell illustration, benefit bullets, or arrows toward the system dialog's Allow, draw the real tray preview — because people decide better when they see the actual notification.\n- Instead of styling the preview as a system alert, draw it as an inset illustration on raised-over-sunken — because the primer must never be mistaken for the system dialog.\n- Instead of a ghost 'Not now' beside a filled button on Android, draw two peer buttons — because a decline is a survivable outcome.\n- Instead of a long title with the caveat at the end, draw the canonical title of 30 characters or fewer — because tray truncation cuts the end of a title.\n- Instead of opening this sheet after a Date-sheet save or a PickupCard confirm, draw the host's own inline ask — because asks sit inline where they belong, and sheets never stack or open by themselves.\n- Instead of a persistent amber nag after a decline, draw the host with the widget offered once — because the widget is a return trigger that needs no permission.\n- Instead of a second Close button in the iOS denied sheet, keep Close in the top bar only — because one exit is enough.\n\nDONE WHEN: The primer never follows a card 'Yes', a Date-sheet save or an inline ask on a never-asked phone, and never opens by itself. Its only forward label is Continue (or Open Settings when denied). The trays match the canonical strings and fit at 393pt and 412dp with the caveat intact. Android 'Not now' spends no denial and never re-presents. Every denial frame names what still works for its entry, and every denial frame is reachable from a stated entry. Nothing asks at cold launch. The body names every default that sends, including sign-in alerts. A grant lands on '6:00 PM · Change' without Maya ever choosing a time, so she can change it.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f4-notification-primer · ios · 01-mail-entry · light: Maya's sheet over dimmed Mail after tapping Turn on in the push-off banner: 'Sam marked Clark PUD paid' tray, both caption lines, the body, Close in the top bar and Continue only.\n2. f4-notification-primer · android · 02-mail-entry · light: the same sheet on Android with Continue and Not now as peers.\n3. f4-notification-primer · android · 03-denied-once-pickup · light: over Today (PickupCard confirmed-just-now with its inline ask), the pickup title, 'Recycling + garbage tomorrow' tray, the pickup denied lines, Continue and Not now.\n4. f4-notification-primer · ios · 04-granted · light: back on Mail, banner reads 'Household updates are on · Change'; inset beside it shows Today's briefing card with the evening row '6:00 PM · Change' while the morning row still asks.\n5. f4-notification-primer · ios · 05-declined-at-os · light: left, Mail unchanged with its push-off banner; right, Today the next time it opens, with the briefing card slot closed and the PickupCard unchanged, its footer offering 'Put today on your home screen' once (at most once every 24 h). No amber, and no extra line.\n6. f4-notification-primer · android · 06-not-now · light: Mail unchanged after Not now. No system dialog fired. The banner still reads 'Push is off. You'll still see these here.'\n7. f4-notification-primer · ios · 07-denied-open-settings · light: over Mail, from Turn on: the Mail denied lines, one filled 'Open Settings' button, Close only in the top bar.\n8. f4-notification-primer · android · 08-denied-once-mail · light: over Mail, from Turn on: the Mail denied lines, Continue (asks again) and Not now.\n9. f4-notification-primer · android · 09-blocked · light: over Mail, from Turn on: the Mail denied lines, Open Settings and Not now.\n10. f4-notification-primer · ios · 10-never-shown · light: Today and Mail side by side with five annotations: 'Already granted: primer skipped'; 'Save failed: card shows Retry, no ask'; 'Mail Turn on while granted: banner reads Household updates are on · Change'; 'Date-sheet save: Date sheet closes, inline ask on the host, no primer'; 'iOS denied: no inline reminder ask on the PickupCard'.\n11. f4-notification-primer · ios · 11-offline-and-save-error · light: the Mail-entry sheet with the Mail offline caption, beside Mail with the InlineErrorRow 'Couldn't turn on household updates · Retry'.\n12. f4-notification-primer · ios · 12-tray-specimen · light: collapsed iOS trays at 393pt only: 'Recycling + garbage tomorrow' / 'Bins out tonight · Larkspur Loop'; worst case 'Bins out tonight · Columbia River Dr'; 'Unconfirmed: pickup tomorrow' / 'Recycling + garbage · city schedule'; 'Sam marked Clark PUD paid' / 'Due Fri 23 Oct · Columbia River Dr'; hidden previews 'Pantopus · Pickup reminder' and 'Pantopus · Household update'.\n13. f4-notification-primer · ios · 13-ax5 · light: frame 1 at AX5. The sheet scrolls, the tray wraps, and the button is full width.\n14. f4-notification-primer · android · 14-greyscale · light: frame 2 in greyscale, beside the same five tray strings drawn as collapsed Android trays at 412dp.\n15. f4-notification-primer · ios · 15-mail-entry · dark: dark twin of frame 1.\n16. f4-notification-primer · android · 16-denied-once-mail · dark: dark twin of frame 8.\n17. Notes:\n- Assumptions: Maya's second place 'Grandma's', 5200 SE Columbia River Dr; Maya skipped the inline reminder ask earlier, so her phone was never asked.\n- Annotation: 'Date-sheet save → Date sheet closes → inline ask on the host (Today PickupCard or place-file pickup row) → system dialog directly. No primer.'\n- Every invented string: both titles, both bodies, 'Arrives quietly — no sound.', all four denied lines, the inline ask, both save errors, both offline captions, 'Household updates are on · Change', 'Due Fri 23 Oct · Larkspur Loop', both Columbia River Dr worst cases, 'Pantopus · Household update' spoken form.\n- Changed from the contract: the primer body adds 'Sign-in alerts for your account.' because sign-in alerts are on by default; flag this for the NotificationAsk copy rule.\n- Omitted states: web (the card asks directly); Android before 13.\n- Decisions: provisional authorization is not used for pickup and is a possible test for the Mail (household) entry only. Android 'Not now' is the sheet's close; the permanent decline lives on the briefing card or in Settings. On Android the research says to show an educational screen only when the system says a reason should be shown, so the first-request Android frame (2) is a founder call.\n- Open questions: (a) flow-01 step 12 and flow-02 still place the primer after the first pickup confirm; this prompt follows the brief (inline ask, no primer), so the flows need updating. (b) The iOS visible Close conflicts with Apple's single-button pre-alert guidance. (c) PickupCard labels: the contract says 'Yes, Tuesday is right' / 'Change pickup day'; the brief and flows say 'That's my day' / 'Not my schedule'. The hosts are drawn with the Foundations PickupCard labels; the founder must reconcile them. (d) The Mail banner wording when the phone is allowed but Household activity is off still reads 'Push is off'; consider 'Household updates are off on this phone · Turn on'. (e) Pickup confirmer: settings shows 'confirmed by Sam'; pick one fixture across prompts.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for 'continue'.\nTurn 2: artboards 7-12, then wait for 'continue'.\nTurn 3: artboards 13-17.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Removed the auto-open after a Date-sheet save (brief P4, house-style AVOID asks in modals, no stacked sheets): the Date sheet closes and the host shows its inline ask 'Remind you the night before? 6:00 PM · Turn on reminders', which fires the system dialog directly; entries are now only Mail Turn on and the Android denied-once inline ask (review major)",
          "Rebuilt the manifest around the Mail entry: artboard 1 is the iOS Mail sheet, 2 its Android twin; granted (4) and dark (15) follow the Mail entry; the old pickup default frame became a Notes annotation and a frame-10 annotation (review major)",
          "WHO AND WHEN rewritten: Maya taps Turn on in the Mail push-off banner at 6:10 PM (review major)",
          "Stated that the host is Today or the place file, and that the Date sheet closes first; focus returns to the invoking control (review minor)",
          "Added iOS-denied and Android-blocked rule: no inline reminder ask on the PickupCard; only Mail Turn on and settings lead to Open Settings (review minor)",
          "Tray caption keeps 'This is the whole thing.' on both entries; 'Arrives quietly — no sound.' is a second line (PushCopy contract)",
          "Denied line 2 now depends on entry: Mail 'Household updates still show here in Mail.' / pickup 'Pickup still shows on Today.' (review minor)",
          "Frame 5 redrawn: briefing slot closed, PickupCard unchanged with the widget footer offered once, no extra line (NotificationAsk declined state)",
          "iOS denied: one filled Open Settings, Close only in the top bar (review minor)",
          "Bodies add 'Sign-in alerts for your account.' (brief section 3 defaults); flagged for the NotificationAsk contract on Notes",
          "Split the tray specimen: 393pt trays on iOS frame 12, 412dp trays moved into the Android greyscale frame 14; added bill-paid worst case and household hidden preview",
          "Added Mail-entry offline caption and save error; frame 4 shows the Mail banner after Allow",
          "Notes record: Android 'Not now' as the sheet's close with the permanent decline on the card or Settings (glossary), PickupCard label mismatch, banner wording when OS granted but group off, pickup confirmer fixture conflict, flows needing update",
          "Added an INSTEAD OF line against opening after a save or confirm, and one against a duplicate iOS Close"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f4-notification-settings",
        "name": "Notifications settings (five groups)",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 22,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Notifications settings · f4-notification-settings\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen 'Notification Preferences'. This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed.\nChanged, kept and merged on this page:\n- The page title becomes 'Notifications'.\n- 'Weather Alerts' and 'Air Quality Alerts' merge into one group, AIR & WEATHER ALERTS.\n- 'Home Reminders' becomes DATES & BILLS, with three switches.\n- Keep 'Gig Updates', 'Mail Summary' and 'Beacon Notifications' exactly as the screenshot shows, in one section below Account & security titled 'Other notifications'.\n- Replace 'Quiet Hours' with the 'Pause briefings' row.\n- Replace 'Briefing Location' and its three modes with one caption, 'Briefings follow <home or saved place>'. Draw no Device Location option.\n- Add the pinned master switch. It is the push switch that used to sit in the Mail account area; remove it there and put one row, 'Notifications · Open', in its place.\n\nATTACH: The existing Notification Preferences page on web 1440, iOS and Android. The Mail account area that holds today's push switch. The Today briefing card (for the 'More options' entry). A Mail notification row with its overflow menu open. The existing home settings page that still shows the per-home notification switches, which this change removes.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: Web 1440x900 uses the settings layout inside the left sidebar. Web 390x844. iOS 393x852 uses a grouped inset list. Android 412x915 uses a Material 3 preference list with group headers.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Settings > Notifications. On mobile, Settings opens from the account area in the Mail tab. On desktop, it opens from the sidebar. There is one page, and it has no tab of its own. Entry points:\n- Settings > Notifications, and the 'Notifications · Open' row in the Mail account area.\n- 'More options' on the Today briefing card.\n- 'Turn these off' in the overflow menu of any in-app notification row. The page scrolls once to that row's group and fades a highlight on it.\n- The first household 'marked paid' notification.\n- 'Change' on the Mail banner 'Household updates are on'.\n- The 'Manage reminders' link beside the Date sheet's 'Remind me' control.\n- The iOS Settings link 'Pantopus Notification Settings'.\n- Android's in-app settings link from the system notification page.\n- The 'Notifications · Open' row on the home settings page.\n- The deep link /app/settings/notifications, with ?group=briefings, ?group=air, ?group=dates, ?group=household or ?group=account for the group landing.\nWhat this page receives: from a notification row or ?group=, the group to highlight. What it hands on: 'Set it' opens the Date sheet on the pickup-day kind; 'Open Settings' opens the system notification page for Pantopus; 'Open' opens that Android channel; 'Turn on' on the device line asks this phone for permission; 'Add a place' opens place search; 'Show me how' opens the browser's own notification-permission help in a new tab.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM. On Sat 17 Oct at 4:00 PM, Maya Chen got 'Air: sensitive groups, AQI 118' during her son's game and found it too eager. She taps 'Turn these off' on that row in Mail to raise her level, and wants to be sure the pickup reminder stays on. Thresholds are per person; Maya's change does not affect Sam.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Give every notification Pantopus sends exactly one honest switch, on one page, and show when the phone is holding or blocking it.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: First, the master switch 'Push notifications from Pantopus' (or the pinned banner when the OS blocks delivery). Second, the five group headers. Third, the delivery helper under each group, which says how that group arrives. There is no page-level primary action, because each switch saves on its own.\n\nCONTENT (fixtures apply; the deltas are below)\nThe page reads top to bottom:\n- Pinned master: 'Push notifications from Pantopus', ON. Helper: 'Turning this off stops every notification. Everything still shows inside the app.' Device line, per platform: iOS 'Sends to this iPhone and one browser.' · Android 'Sends to this phone and one browser.' · web 'Sends to this browser and one iPhone.'\n- One-time migration line: 'We moved your home reminder settings here. Nothing you turned off was turned on.' It has a Dismiss button.\n- BRIEFINGS. Helper under the header: 'Sound and banner, at the times below.'\n  - 'Morning briefing', ON, 7:00 AM. Caption: 'Today's dates and weather in one message, only when something needs you. Nothing sent in the last day repeats.'\n  - 'Evening briefing', ON, 6:00 PM. Caption: 'Only when something needs you. No news means nothing's up.' Second line: 'Pickup comes with the evening briefing.' Status line: 'Last sent today, 6:00 PM · pickup'.\n  - Status row: 'Pickup day · Tuesday (confirmed by Sam)'.\n  - Caption: 'Briefings follow your home, 2418 NE Larkspur Loop.'\n  - Row: 'Pause briefings'.\n  - Native only: 'Home screen widget · Add', hidden once a widget has been placed.\n- AIR & WEATHER ALERTS\n  - Master 'Air & weather alerts', ON. Helper: 'Can come through Focus when the air quality index (AQI) is 151 or higher, or there's a weather warning.'\n  - Caption: 'One alert when air crosses your level. It updates if air gets worse. National Weather Service warnings always come while this is on.'\n  - Threshold as three radio rows, each with EPA's full health statement as its meaning line (let it wrap). Before Maya's change, the first one is selected, matching what the server sends today:\n    1. 'Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups · AQI 101 and up'. Meaning: 'Members of sensitive groups may experience health effects. The general public is less likely to be affected.'\n    2. 'Unhealthy · AQI 151 and up'. Meaning: 'Some members of the general public may experience health effects; members of sensitive groups may experience more serious health effects.'\n    3. 'Very Unhealthy · AQI 201 and up'. Meaning: 'Health alert: The risk of health effects is increased for everyone.'\n- DATES & BILLS (renamed from 'Home Reminders'). Helper under the header: 'Sound and banner.'\n  - 'Date reminders', ON. Helper: 'The reminders you set before a date — like 14 days before your lease notice is due.'\n  - 'Bill reminders', ON. Helper: 'Clark Public Utilities and any bill you add.'\n  - 'Task reminders', ON. Helper: 'Household tasks with a due date.'\n  - Group caption: 'Only for dates, bills and tasks where a reminder is set. To stop one date's reminders, open that date and set Remind me to never.'\n  - These are three switches, so muting dates never mutes bills or tasks.\n- HOUSEHOLD ACTIVITY\n  - Master 'Household activity', ON. Helper: 'Quiet — shows in your list, no sound. Always in your Mail notifications, even with this off.'\n  - 'Bills marked paid', ON. Caption: 'Louder only if a bill you still see as unpaid is due within 3 days.'\n  - 'Tasks completed', OFF. Caption: 'Only tasks you created or were assigned.'\n  - 'Calendar events added', ON.\n  - 'People joining or leaving', ON. Caption: 'When someone accepts an invitation or leaves this household.'\n  - When the master is off, these four rows show their saved values, disabled, with the caption 'Turn on Household activity to change these.'\n- ACCOUNT & SECURITY. Helper under the header: 'Sound and banner.'\n  - 'Sign-ins and invitations to you', ON. Helper: 'New sign-ins to your account and household invitations sent to you.'\n- OTHER NOTIFICATIONS: 'Gig Updates', 'Mail Summary', 'Beacon Notifications', drawn exactly as the screenshot shows, with the same row style as above.\n- Help link in the same slot as on the other settings pages.\nWorst case to fit: the pinned banner, the migration line and the paused-briefings row with its caption all at once, at 390 wide.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION: Five labelled groups in this fixed order, then Other notifications last. The order never changes, because each of the five groups is one permanent Android channel and one iOS category. Air & weather alerts and Household activity each start with a master switch row, with its delivery helper directly under that master in text.secondary. Briefings, Dates & bills and Account & security have no master row: their switches are the group's control, and the delivery helper sits directly under the group header. Never put helper text in the group footer: people check one switch at a time. The evening briefing's silence promise sits in its own row caption, because the people who open this page stopped getting notifications and want to know whether they are still on. Every row reads its own OS state. When the OS blocks a row, draw the switch off and disabled, with a leading warning glyph and a text.primary line 'Off in Android settings · Open'. The saved choice is kept and comes back when the OS allows it. A switch never reads ON when nothing can be delivered. When the whole app is blocked on this device and nothing else delivers, pin a full-width banner above the master: warning glyph, text.primary on the warning tint, 'Notifications are off for Pantopus. These rows still update inside the app.', then 'Open Settings'. The widget is offered once, inside that banner. Use amber only when a switch the person turned on cannot be delivered. The device line is per device: when push is on in a browser but this phone has not allowed it, it says so and offers Turn on.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS: Tapping a switch saves it right away. The row shows 'Saving…', then 'Saved', as a live status message and never a toast. If a save fails, the switch returns to its last saved value and an InlineErrorRow appears. Tapping a time row opens the platform time picker (iOS wheel in a sheet, Material 3 time picker, web native time input). 'Pause briefings' opens a short list: 'For 1 week' / 'For 2 weeks' / 'Until a date I pick' (opens the platform date picker). Once paused, the row reads 'Paused until Mon 26 Oct · Resume' with the caption 'Pickup reminders pause too.', and the evening status line is hidden. Every paused state names its end date. The radio rows are single choice, and selection is shown by a filled dot plus bold text, which looks different from focus. A deep-link landing (?group= or 'Turn these off') scrolls once and fades the highlight within 300ms. Under Reduce Motion, the highlight is a static outline. A switch that saves successfully plays one light haptic tick. Nothing on this page is gesture-only.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: NotificationAsk (state 'switch ON but OS blocked'). QuietDayReceipt (briefing settings row variant 'Skipped tonight — nothing needed you'). FactRow (pickup-day status row, known and missing variants; 'Notifications · Open' row). LockedActionRow (not-at-this-tier variant). InlineErrorRow (save failed). OfflineNotice. NotificationRow (the entry point). ScopeChip (the saved-place frame). WarmingSkeleton (row skeleton).\n\nACCESSIBILITY: Reading order: banner, master, device line, then each group header with its helper, master (if any) and rows, then Other notifications. Each switch's spoken label includes its helper and OS state. Example for a blocked row: 'Evening briefing, off in Android settings, dimmed. Your choice, on at 6:00 PM, is kept. Open.' Status messages use a polite live region and never move focus. On a ?group= or 'Turn these off' landing, accessibility focus moves to the highlighted group header. Targets are 44pt on iOS, 48dp with 8dp gaps on Android, and 44px on web. Focus never sits under the pinned banner, which reserves scroll padding. At AX5 and 200%, labels and meaning lines wrap and switches drop below the label.\n\nCOPY\n- Actions: 'Set it' · 'Open Settings' · 'Open' · 'Resume' · 'Retry' · 'Dismiss' · 'Add a place' · 'Turn on' · 'Add' · 'Show me how'.\n- Status: 'Saving…' · 'Saved' · 'Off in Android settings · Open' · 'Notifications are off for Pantopus. These rows still update inside the app. · Open Settings'.\n- Pause list: 'For 1 week' · 'For 2 weeks' · 'Until a date I pick'. Paused: 'Paused until Mon 26 Oct · Resume'. Caption: 'Pickup reminders pause too.'\n- Scheduled Summary (iOS): 'Your iPhone may hold pickup reminders for your summary. · Open Settings'.\n- Time Sensitive off (iOS): 'Time Sensitive is off in iOS Settings. Alerts may wait until Focus ends. · Open Settings'.\n- Blocked-but-kept caption: 'Your choice is kept'.\n- Device lines when this phone is not allowed: 'Sends to one browser. This iPhone isn't allowed yet · Turn on'. When this phone is blocked but a browser delivers: 'Sends to one browser. This iPhone is off in iOS Settings · Open Settings'. When nothing delivers: 'This iPhone: off in iOS Settings'.\n- Quiet night: 'Skipped tonight — nothing needed you'; dated form 'Skipped Sun 18 Oct — nothing needed you'.\n- Save error: 'Couldn't save Evening briefing. Check your connection and try again. · Retry'.\n- No location: 'Briefings need an address. Save one to turn these on.' and 'Air & weather alerts need an address too.'\n- Timezone (only when the phone is outside Pacific time): 'Your phone is on Mountain Time. Briefings use Pacific Time, your address's time zone.'\n- Web blocked: 'Notifications are blocked in this browser. These rows still update inside the app. · Show me how'.\n- Offline: 'You're offline. Your settings are shown as last saved. Switches work again when you're back online.'\n- Replacement row (home settings and Mail account area): 'Notifications · Open'.\n\nEDGE CASES\n- Saved place only (Jordan Lee at PLACE B, 1107 NE Birchfield Ct):\n  - The briefings caption reads 'Briefings follow your saved place, 1107 NE Birchfield Ct · Saved place · Only you'.\n  - The pickup row reads 'Pickup day · Not set · Set it', with the caption 'The city lists Thursday. Set your pickup day to get the night-before reminder.'\n  - Household activity is one grey LockedActionRow, 'Claim this address first', with no action.\n  - Bill reminders and Task reminders are hidden.\n- No location: the briefing switches and the Air & weather alerts master are off and disabled, each with its needs-an-address line and 'Add a place'.\n- Whole app blocked on this phone, nothing else delivers: every group switch off and disabled with 'Your choice is kept'; device line 'This iPhone: off in iOS Settings'.\n- Whole app blocked on this phone but a browser still delivers: no pinned banner; switches stay ON; device line 'Sends to one browser. This iPhone is off in iOS Settings · Open Settings'.\n- Loading: row skeletons, not a spinner.\n- Many devices: the device line wraps.\n- Web push on, this phone not allowed: the device line variant above; the Briefings switches stay ON (the browser still delivers).\n- Two blocked channels: each blocked row gets its own line.\n- Household master off: the four rows disabled with their saved values.\n- Paused: the evening status line is hidden; no 'Skipped' line shows while paused.\n- The per-home switches are gone from the home settings page. In their place is one row, 'Notifications · Open', that opens this page.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of per-home notification switches, draw this one page linked from the home settings — because those switches never saved anything.\n- Instead of 'Home Reminders', draw 'Dates & bills' with three switches — because people with no home get these too, and muting dates must not mute bills or tasks.\n- Instead of a segmented AQI control, draw three radio rows with EPA's meanings — because segments truncate at large text.\n- Instead of a 151 default, select 101 — because the server alerts at 101.\n- Instead of a switch that shows ON while the OS blocks it, draw it off and disabled with 'Off in Android settings · Open' — because a switch that pretends is worse than no switch.\n- Instead of a keeper group or a 'Tips and news' switch, draw the five groups plus the existing Other notifications — because Pantopus never sends marketing or keeper notifications, and every type that sends needs one home.\n- Instead of helper text in the group footer, put it under each master or group header — because people read one switch at a time.\n- Instead of a Device Location briefing option, draw the one 'Briefings follow' caption — because briefings follow an address, not the phone.\n- Instead of an open-ended pause, name the end date — because a paused state people forget becomes a silent failure.\n\nDONE WHEN: Every notification type this design introduces maps to exactly one switch, including joins and leaves and task reminders, and every type that still sends has a switch. Every group states how it is delivered. The air threshold matches what the server sends. No switch reads ON, or is spoken as on, while nothing can be delivered. The evening row states the silence promise and when it last sent, and never says 'Skipped' while paused or on a night something was sent. Every pause names its end date. The device line is honest per device. Flow check: from an air alert's 'Turn these off', Maya picks 'Very Unhealthy · AQI 201 and up' and the pickup reminder is untouched.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f4-notification-settings · web-1440 · 01-default · light: the full dense page with the master, the migration line, all five groups and Other notifications.\n2. f4-notification-settings · ios · 02-default · light: the same content as a grouped inset list.\n3. f4-notification-settings · android · 03-default · light: the same content as an M3 preference list; 'Calendar events added' shows 'Saving…' and 'Bills marked paid' shows 'Saved'.\n4. f4-notification-settings · ios · 04-os-denied · light: the pinned banner above the master. Every group switch is off and disabled, and each shows the caption 'Your choice is kept' under its label. The device line reads 'This iPhone: off in iOS Settings'. The widget is offered once inside the banner.\n5. f4-notification-settings · android · 05-channel-blocked · light: the Air group is off and disabled, reading 'Off in Android settings · Open'.\n6. f4-notification-settings · ios · 06-summary-and-time-sensitive · light: the Scheduled Summary caption with Open Settings on Evening briefing, and the Time Sensitive line on Air.\n7. f4-notification-settings · ios · 07-this-phone-off · light: device line 'Sends to one browser. This iPhone isn't allowed yet · Turn on', switches still ON.\n8. f4-notification-settings · web-1440 · 08-landing-air · light: arrived via ?group=air, with the Air group highlighted and 'Very Unhealthy · AQI 201 and up' selected.\n9. f4-notification-settings · web-390 · 09-saved-place · light: the PLACE B variant.\n10. f4-notification-settings · web-1440 · 10-no-location · light: briefing switches and the Air & weather master off and disabled, both needs-an-address lines, 'Add a place'.\n11. f4-notification-settings · web-1440 · 11-paused-timezone · light: the timezone caption; the Pause row reads 'Paused until Mon 26 Oct · Resume' with 'Pickup reminders pause too.'; the evening status line is hidden.\n12. f4-notification-settings · web-390 · 12-quiet-night · light: the evening status line reads 'Skipped Sun 18 Oct — nothing needed you'; the Household master is off with its four rows disabled and their caption.\n13. f4-notification-settings · web-1440 · 13-loading · light: row skeletons.\n14. f4-notification-settings · web-1440 · 14-save-error · light: Evening briefing reverted, with an InlineErrorRow.\n15. f4-notification-settings · web-1440 · 15-replacement-rows · light: panel 1, the home settings page with the switches gone and one row 'Notifications · Open'; panel 2, the Mail account area with the push switch gone and one row 'Notifications · Open'.\n16. f4-notification-settings · web-390 · 16-offline · light: an OfflineNotice, with switches disabled and the reason shown.\n17. f4-notification-settings · web-1440 · 17-browser-blocked · light: the web banner with 'Show me how' and the web device line.\n18. f4-notification-settings · ios · 18-ax5 · light: the Air group at AX5, with radio rows and EPA meaning lines wrapping and switches below labels.\n19. f4-notification-settings · web-390 · 19-greyscale · light: frame 9 in greyscale.\n20. f4-notification-settings · web-1440 · 20-default · dark: the dark twin of frame 1.\n21. f4-notification-settings · ios · 21-os-denied · dark: the dark twin of frame 4.\n22. Notes. List:\n  - assumptions: Maya's ON values are her own choices; the defaults after a grant are Household activity OFF and Morning briefing OFF unless chosen on the card; the evening default is ON at 6:00 PM; thresholds are per person; Task reminders default ON like Bill reminders;\n  - the rule for dates: Morning briefing lists the day's dates; Date reminders are the lead-time series. Muting one never mutes the other;\n  - every invented string: master helper, all device lines (iPhone, Android, web, not allowed, off in iOS Settings), 'Your choice is kept', group helpers, captions, 'Task reminders' and its helper, the Dates & bills group caption, 'People joining or leaving' caption, the Tasks completed caption, pause list and 'Pickup reminders pause too.', 'Skipped Sun 18 Oct — nothing needed you', Time Sensitive line, both needs-an-address lines, the timezone caption (changed from the earlier '7:00 AM Pacific' wording), web banner, offline line, 'Notifications · Open', the ?group= values, the alert title 'Air: sensitive groups, AQI 118' (category-true for 118), and the Scheduled Summary line (flow-02 quotes it as 'Pickup reminders may arrive with your summary');\n  - deviations: Account & security no longer says it can come through Focus, to keep the rule that only the air group mentions Focus; whether sign-ins should be Time Sensitive is an open call; Task reminders chosen as a third switch rather than widening Bill reminders;\n  - omitted states;\n  - open calls:\n    - the threshold control depends on the backend storing a per-user threshold;\n    - whether the master switch stays once each group has its own switch;\n    - whether Account & security can be switched off;\n    - whether Gig Updates, Mail Summary and Beacon Notifications still send; any that no longer sends is removed; any that moves (for example Mail Summary to Mail Day settings) must keep a working switch there before removal from this page ships;\n    - pickup day confirmer is Sam here and a fresh save in the primer; pick one fixture.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for 'continue'.\nTurn 2: artboards 7-12, then wait for 'continue'.\nTurn 3: artboards 13-18, then wait for 'continue'.\nTurn 4: artboards 19-22.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Added a 'Task reminders' switch to Dates & bills so task reminders keep a switch (design doc section 3, derive f5-reminder-settings-copy; review major)",
          "Replaced 'Until I turn them back on' with 'Until a date I pick'; every paused state names its end date (per-surface change, research; review major)",
          "Kept Gig Updates, Mail Summary and Beacon Notifications in an 'Other notifications' section; Notes asks whether each still sends and requires a working switch elsewhere before any removal; rewrote the INSTEAD OF line (review major)",
          "Artboard 4 redrawn: all group switches off and disabled with 'Your choice is kept', device line 'This iPhone: off in iOS Settings'; added browser-still-delivers edge case (review major)",
          "Split artboard 11 into 11-paused-timezone (status line hidden, 'Pickup reminders pause too.') and 12-quiet-night ('Skipped Sun 18 Oct — nothing needed you', household master off); renumbered to 22 artboards and rebatched (review major, invariant 4)",
          "No-location state also disables the Air & weather master with 'Air & weather alerts need an address too.' (derive f4-8)",
          "DONE WHEN qualified to types this design introduces plus every type that still sends",
          "Scheduled Summary caption gains '· Open Settings' (research)",
          "Tasks completed caption: 'Only tasks you created or were assigned.' (research)",
          "Deep-link landing moves accessibility focus to the highlighted group header (brief)",
          "Scenario alert title changed to category-true 'Air: sensitive groups, AQI 118' (30 characters), listed as invented",
          "Dropped the Focus clause from Account & security; recorded as a deliberate choice on Notes",
          "EPA full health statements used verbatim, allowed to wrap (brief P13)",
          "Artboard 15 adds the Mail account area panel with 'Notifications · Open'",
          "Device line variants for web and Android added",
          "Offline copy now says what still works (OfflineNotice rule)",
