      {
        "id": "f1-claim-receipt",
        "name": "Claimed — what came with you",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 21,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Claimed — what came with you · f1-claim-receipt\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen 'Verified success' (the post-claim and post-verify success screen). This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed.\nChanges to the host:\n- The verified headline 'Your address is verified.' is used only once a verification has finished. Directly under it, add the method line 'Address verified by postcard · Mon 19 Oct'. If any headline you keep is a bare 'Verified' or uses celebration wording, keep its position and style but set the line to 'Address verified by postcard · Mon 19 Oct', and list the change on Notes.\n- Claim-time version (before verification): the headline reads 'You claimed 2418 NE Larkspur Loop.' and the method line reads 'Postcard on its way · mailed Mon 28 Sep'. The verified-only 'Now available' rows are omitted in this version.\n- Replace the subline ('You're now an address-proven neighbor at …') with the summary sentence.\n- 'Now available' rows (verified version only) use the GrantLimitList unlocked strings, each with a tick: 'Message your neighbors' · 'Get a residency letter' · 'Show your Residency Pass' · 'Share what you pay in rent (Real Rent)' · 'Earn a Block Founder rank'. Remove any 'permanent 0% marketplace fee' line. Use 'Block Founder' for the permanent rank and 'Founding Neighbor' only for the scarce first-5 tier. Replace any 'verified neighbors' wording with these strings.\n- Order: headline → method line → summary → 'Came with you' manifest → consent block → FactCount line → closing line → 'Now available' rows (verified only) → 'Go to your place'.\n- Change 'Go to your place' from filled to an outlined button. It is how Maya leaves, and leaving keeps the dates Only you, so it must not compete with the two consent buttons.\n- The staged reveal becomes one 200ms fade (static under Reduce Motion). Keep the seal at its existing size, with no halo animation.\n\nATTACH:\n- The existing Verified success screen on web 1440, web 390, iOS and Android.\n- The place file (Place tab) on web 1440, showing its top banner slot and its fact rows.\n- Today with the 'Saved place · Only you' chip, for reference.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: Web 1440x900 with the left sidebar. Web 390x844. iOS 393x852. Android 412x915.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Place tab. The timing model: claiming created the home on Mon 28 Sep, when Maya requested the postcard. The server copied the saved place's pickup day, dates and keeper to the home in that same step and removed the duplicate saved-place entry. Every carried date has stayed Only you (pending) since then. Sam Ortega joined on Wed 7 Oct and has not seen them. This receipt appears when the claim finishes. It appears again when verification finishes if the dates question is still unanswered.\nPeople reach it in five ways:\n1. The claim flow ends here (claim-time version: claim headline, before any household member).\n2. The address-verification flow ends here (postcard code entered): verified version.\n3. The first time the place file opens after a claim, its banner slot shows the claim receipt banner once. The banner links here. It ranks after invite, reissue and compare arrival, and before mailbox arrival, setup and verify. If a higher banner is showing, it waits for the next place-file open. It counts as shown only once it has rendered.\n4. From then on, the place file row 'What moved when you claimed' opens this same manifest.\n5. The deep link /app/place?verified=1 shows the receipt later.\nWhat this screen receives: the list of carried items, any item that failed to move, and the people in the household (plus pending invitations). What it hands on: Today now uses the home (same sections, no chip). Each date keeps its own visibility control ('Only you' / 'Household') in the Date sheet and on its place-file row, so either choice can be reversed per date.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM. Six weeks ago Maya Chen saved HOME A; she set the pickup day, entered two dates and named Ollie. On Mon 28 Sep she claimed it and left the receipt without choosing. Sam joined on Wed 7 Oct. She has just typed her postcard code, and the question is asked again.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Name every fact that moved from the saved place to the home, and ask before the one privacy change the move causes.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS:\n1. The headline and method line, then the summary sentence.\n2. The manifest rows with their scope pairs.\n3. The consent question. Its two peer buttons are the only actions that matter here.\n\nCONTENT (fixtures apply; the deltas are below)\nDeltas: the claim date Mon 28 Sep, Sam's join date Wed 7 Oct. For frame 13 only, Maya's saved place is 1107 NE Birchfield Ct (a fixture deviation; see Notes).\nSummary line: 'Your pickup day, 2 dates and Ollie came with you.'\nHeader: the ScopeChip 'Saved place · Only you', struck through, followed by 'Your household'. Section label: 'Came with you'. Legend, printed once: '✓ You added this'.\nManifest, one row per carried item. The summary counts only the rows that carried. A failed item is drawn as a separate InlineErrorRow below them and is not counted.\nVerified version (Mon 19 Oct):\n- Pickup day · 'Tuesday · garbage every week, recycling every other week · next recycling tomorrow'. Caption: 'Everyone in this household will see this.' Scope pair: Only you → household.\n- Lease ends · 'in 163 days · Wed 31 Mar 2027'. Caption: 'Notice due Mon 1 Mar 2027 · reminder Mon 15 Feb'. Scope pair: Only you → household (pending).\n- Warranty ends · 'Water heater · in 54 days · Sat 12 Dec 2026'. Scope pair: Only you → household (pending).\n- Ollie (your keeper) · 'Otter'. Caption: 'Everyone in this household will see Ollie.' Scope pair: Only you → household.\nClaim-time version (Mon 28 Sep), same rows with these values:\n- Pickup day · 'Tuesday · garbage every week, recycling every other week · next recycling Tue 6 Oct' (Tue 29 Sep is garbage only).\n- Lease ends · 'in 184 days · Wed 31 Mar 2027'.\n- Warranty ends · 'Water heater · in 75 days · Sat 12 Dec 2026'.\nConsent block:\n- Question: 'Share the 2 dates you entered with Sam?'\n- Caption: 'Until you choose, only you will see them. If you share, anyone who joins later will see them too, including priya@example.com if she accepts. You can change this for each date later.'\n- Two peer buttons: 'Share with the household' and 'Keep them to myself'.\nBelow the manifest:\n- A FactCount line reading '14 on file', with category pips and the link 'See your place file'. It is not a manifest row. It shows the same integer as the place file header.\n- Closing line: 'Today now uses this home.'\nWorst case: a failed item, a long provider name, and a date title that wraps to two lines.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION: This is a short receipt, not a celebration.\n- Draw flat rows on surface.raised under the summary, with no card per item.\n- Each row is a DateRow (pickup variant for the pickup row, default variant for dates), with its optional ScopeChip in the scope-change pair variant: person glyph → small arrow → house glyph. Pending shows a dashed house glyph until the person chooses.\n- The keeper row is a DateRow-shaped row with the KeeperStrip species avatar scaled to the KindGlyph's 24pt slot, in place of the KindGlyph.\n- The pickup and date rows carry the ProvenanceMark 'You added this'. Do not add a second tick to mean 'moved'; the scope pair and the section label 'Came with you' show that the item moved.\n- The migration shows on each row, not once in prose, so each row can be checked against what Maya remembers typing.\n- Both consent buttons are filled primary.700, the same width and height, side by side; stacked at 390 wide and at AX5.\n- If there are no dates, there is no consent block.\n- If nothing moved, the screen shows only the plain success screen plus 'Today now uses this home.' Never draw an empty list or '0 items'.\n- When the claimed address differs from the saved place, nothing carries. The screen is the plain success screen plus 'Today now uses 2418 NE Larkspur Loop. 1107 NE Birchfield Ct is still saved. · Your places'. 'Your places' opens the Your places screen.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS: The two consent buttons are peers of equal size and weight.\n- Share. Each date's pair becomes a solid house glyph with a 200ms cross-fade. The buttons are replaced by the InlineUndo line 'Shared with Sam · Undo', which stays until Maya leaves the screen.\n- Keep. Each date's pair becomes person → person. The buttons are replaced by the line 'Only you will see these 2 dates. You can change this in each date.'\n- Leaving without choosing (including 'Go to your place') keeps the dates Only you. The pending pair stays pending on the revisited receipt, and the question is asked again there.\n- Either choice plays one light haptic tick.\n- Retry on a failed row retries that item only; on success it joins the rows above and the counts update.\n- Phase 2: Ollie's pose settles to calm once. Under Reduce Motion this is a static swap, and the glyph changes are instant.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: DateRow (pickup and default variants), ScopeChip (scope-change pair, pending, declined and struck variants), ProvenanceMark, KindGlyph, FactCount, GrantLimitList (unlocked strings for Now available), InlineErrorRow (carry failed variant), InlineUndo, LandingBannerSlot (one-time claim receipt banner), FactRow ('What moved when you claimed' receipt link), KeeperStrip species avatar (phase 2, at the 24pt slot), OfflineNotice, WarmingSkeleton (row skeleton).\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- The summary sentence is a status message (role=status). Reading order: headline, method line, summary, manifest, consent block, FactCount line, closing line, Now available rows, Go to your place.\n- The manifest is a list, announced as '4 items'.\n- Each row is one element. Example: 'Lease ends, in 163 days, Wednesday 31 March 2027, you added this. Was visible to only you, household pending your choice.'\n- After a choice, the buttons are replaced by the result line, and focus moves to it (and to Undo when present).\n- FactCount is spoken '14 things on file: place, dates, people.'\n- Targets are 44pt / 48dp / 44px. Scope is carried by glyph shape plus a spoken name, never by colour.\n\nCOPY\n- Verified headline: 'Your address is verified.' Method line: 'Address verified by postcard · Mon 19 Oct'.\n- Claim-time headline: 'You claimed 2418 NE Larkspur Loop.' Claim-time method line: 'Postcard on its way · mailed Mon 28 Sep'.\n- Failed item: 'We couldn't move your water-heater warranty · Retry'.\n- Summary when one item fails: 'Your pickup day, 1 date and Ollie came with you.' Question: 'Share the date you entered with Sam?' Keep result: 'Only you will see this date. You can change this in the date.'\n- Phase 1 summary: 'Your pickup day and 2 dates came with you.'\n- Only you in the household so far (claim time): 'Share the 2 dates you entered with people who join this household?' with the caption 'It's just you here for now. You can change this for each date later.'\n- A different address was claimed: 'Today now uses 2418 NE Larkspur Loop. 1107 NE Birchfield Ct is still saved. · Your places'.\n- Place file banner: 'Your pickup day, 2 dates and Ollie came with you · See what moved'.\n- Place file row: 'What moved when you claimed'.\n- Offline: 'You're offline. Only you will see your dates until you choose.'\n\nEDGE CASES\n- Phase 1 has no keeper row, and the summary drops 'and Ollie'.\n- Dates only.\n- Pickup day only (no consent block).\n- Claim time: no household members yet; the future-members question; the claim headline; no Now available rows.\n- A long address wraps in the different-address line.\n- Slow manifest (1 second or more): skeleton rows under the summary.\n- Offline: the buttons are disabled with a reason, and the dates stay Only you.\n- A member without calendar edit rights sees the rows but not the consent block. This must be confirmed in Notes.\n- Already claimed by someone else: no receipt; the flow goes to the household request path.\n- Household already has its own pickup day or keeper: not reachable in this flow (the carry runs at claim, when the household is new). Recorded on Notes with its copy for a future household-request receipt.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of 'are now visible to everyone', draw the conditional question with dates pending — because silence is not consent.\n- Instead of confetti, a badge, a halo or a progress bar, draw a plain manifest — because this is a receipt to check.\n- Instead of 'Ollie knows 11 things', draw a separate '14 on file' line — because a creature that 'knows' reads like surveillance.\n- Instead of a quietly missing row, draw the failed item as its own InlineErrorRow with Retry, and counts that match the carried rows — because loss must be visible.\n- Instead of a one-time banner as the only way back, draw the 'What moved when you claimed' row — because receipts are revisited.\n- Instead of naming Dana, name only real household members and pending invitations — because Dana is a friend who compared places and not a household member.\n- Instead of a filled 'Go to your place' beside the consent buttons, draw it outlined — because leaving is a quiet default, not a third choice.\n- Instead of 'Your address is verified.' on the claim-time receipt, draw 'You claimed 2418 NE Larkspur Loop.' — because unverified looks unverified.\n\nDONE WHEN: The summary counts equal the carried rows in every frame, including phase 1 and the failed state. Nothing is shared before a tap. Each choice is stated as a fact and can be reversed per date in the Date sheet and the place file. The verified version states the method and date; the claim-time version never says verified and shows no verified-only unlocks. No withdrawn fee promise or mixed founder naming appears. The same manifest opens again from the place file. Today shows the home without re-laying out.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f1-claim-receipt · web-1440 · 01-all-carried-pending · light: the verification receipt with headline, method line, the dense manifest, the consent block, FactCount, Now available rows and the outlined Go to your place.\n2. f1-claim-receipt · web-390 · 02-all-carried-pending · light: the same, at phone width, consent buttons stacked.\n3. f1-claim-receipt · ios · 03-all-carried-pending · light: the native equivalent.\n4. f1-claim-receipt · android · 04-all-carried-pending · light: the native equivalent.\n5. f1-claim-receipt · web-1440 · 05-shared · light: solid house glyphs, with 'Shared with Sam · Undo' in place of the buttons.\n6. f1-claim-receipt · web-1440 · 06-kept-to-myself · light: person → person, with the result line in place of the buttons.\n7. f1-claim-receipt · web-390 · 07-carry-failed · light: three carried rows, the warranty as a separate InlineErrorRow below them, the adjusted summary and the one-date question.\n8. f1-claim-receipt · web-390 · 08-phase-1 · light: pickup + 2 dates, 3 rows, summary 'Your pickup day and 2 dates came with you.'\n9. f1-claim-receipt · web-390 · 09-nothing-to-carry · light: the plain success screen plus the closing line.\n10. f1-claim-receipt · web-1440 · 10-dates-only · light: two date rows and the consent block.\n11. f1-claim-receipt · web-390 · 11-pickup-only · light: one row, no consent block.\n12. f1-claim-receipt · web-1440 · 12-claim-time-only-you · light: Mon 28 Sep receipt with 'You claimed 2418 NE Larkspur Loop.', 'Postcard on its way · mailed Mon 28 Sep', the claim-time row values, the future-members question, and no Now available rows.\n13. f1-claim-receipt · web-390 · 13-different-address · light: plain success plus the still-saved line for 1107 NE Birchfield Ct with '· Your places'.\n14. f1-claim-receipt · web-1440 · 14-place-file-banner-and-row · light: the place file with the one-time banner, the persistent row, and a date row showing its 'Only you' / 'Household' control.\n15. f1-claim-receipt · web-390 · 15-loading · light: skeleton rows.\n16. f1-claim-receipt · web-390 · 16-offline · light: disabled consent buttons with the reason.\n17. f1-claim-receipt · ios · 17-ax5 · light: rows stacked, the scope pair on its own line, consent buttons stacked.\n18. f1-claim-receipt · web-390 · 18-greyscale · light: frame 2 in greyscale.\n19. f1-claim-receipt · web-1440 · 19-all-carried-pending · dark: dark twin of frame 1.\n20. f1-claim-receipt · ios · 20-kept-to-myself · dark: frame 6 content on iOS, in dark mode.\n21. Notes:\n   - Assumptions: the Mon 28 Sep claim and Wed 7 Oct join timeline; the carry runs at claim, while flow-06 step 4 places it at code entry, so the flow needs updating.\n   - Fixture deviation: frame 13 gives Maya the saved place 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, which the house style assigns to Jordan Lee; the founder may swap in a Maya-only address.\n   - Every invented string: both headlines if changed, both method lines ('Address verified by postcard' replaces the contract's 'Address confirmed by postcard' example, because the glossary forbids 'confirm'), claim-time row values, 'Keep them to myself' (replaces 'Keep them private to me' quoted in flow-06), the consent caption, '· Your places', result lines, offline line, banner and row copy.\n   - Foundations items: the KeeperStrip species avatar at the 24pt KindGlyph slot is a new size for the Foundations board.\n   - Integer rule: the receipt FactCount, the place file header and the keeper strip must show the same integer (14 here; the keeper strip spec says 11).\n   - Host copy changes: Now available rows now use GrantLimitList strings; any 0% marketplace fee line removed; Block Founder / Founding Neighbor naming fixed.\n   - Omitted states: already claimed by someone else (no receipt). Household already has a pickup day or keeper: unreachable while the carry runs at claim on a new household; if a household-request receipt is added later, use 'Your pickup day (Wednesday) wasn't moved — the household uses Tuesday, confirmed by Sam · Change pickup day' (the summary count drops it) and 'Ollie stayed as your saved-place keeper — this household already has a keeper.'\n   - Open questions:\n     - keeper and pickup visibility change without a consent step;\n     - whether sharing notifies Sam, and if so whether it waits until Undo closes;\n     - the claim receipt banner's rank in the banner slot;\n     - whether to ask for the move-in date at claim;\n     - that the first-week ticks and the widget label move silently;\n     - confirm that members without calendar edit rights see no consent block.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for 'continue'.\nTurn 2: artboards 7-12, then wait for 'continue'.\nTurn 3: artboards 13-18, then wait for 'continue'.\nTurn 4: artboards 19-21.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Claim-time version gets its own headline 'You claimed 2418 NE Larkspur Loop.' and omits the verified-only Now available rows; the verified headline is used only after verification (invariant 1; review major x2)",
          "Claim-time frame 12 uses values correct for Mon 28 Sep: lease in 184 days, warranty in 75 days, next recycling Tue 6 Oct (review major)",
          "Now available rows use GrantLimitList strings, remove any 0% marketplace fee line, and fix Block Founder / Founding Neighbor naming (derive f9-founding-promise-copy; review major)",
          "Household-already-has-pickup-day and kept-keeper states marked unreachable under the timing model and moved to Notes with copy, including a new kept-keeper string; frame 11 annotation removed",
          "Pickup caption uses the canonical ScopeChip sentence 'Everyone in this household will see this.'",
          "Method line reads 'Address verified by postcard · Mon 19 Oct' (glossary forbids 'confirm'); contract example discrepancy noted",
          "Per-date visibility control lives in the Date sheet and on the place-file row (research); frame 14 shows it",
          "Different-address line gains '· Your places', opening Your places (critique)",
          "KeeperStrip species avatar scaled to the 24pt KindGlyph slot, flagged as a Foundations item on Notes",
          "PLACE B reuse in frame 13 flagged as a fixture deviation",
          "Retired scope wording replaced: 'only you will see them' and the offline line",
          "Decline renamed 'Keep them to myself'; both consent buttons filled primary.700, same size, stacked at 390 and AX5",
          "Count rule reworded: summary counts carried rows only; the failed item is a separate uncounted InlineErrorRow",
          "FactCount set to '14 on file' to match the place file header; Notes requires one integer across surfaces",
          "Focus moves to the result line (and Undo) after a choice",
          "Receipt timing reworded: appears when the claim finishes, again at verification if the question is unanswered",
          "Added an INSTEAD OF line against the verified headline at claim time"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f6-home-basics-rows",
        "name": "Home basics: move-in date + restore the moving checklist",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 20,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Home settings, Home Info section · f6-home-basics-rows\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Home settings\" (per-home settings). This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed. You add two rows to the Home Info group, under the existing Address and Home name rows. Add no new section header, card, illustration or setup banner.\n\nATTACH: (1) the current Home settings screen for HOME A on iOS, Android, web 1440 and web 390; (2) the Foundations boards 00a (ProvenanceMark, ScopeChip, OfflineNotice and FreshnessLine), 00c (FactRow, LockedActionRow, InlineErrorRow) and 00d (InlineUndo); (3) the accepted x-date-sheet artboards for view-mine and per-kind validation on iOS, Android and web. Draw the DateSheet from these and change only the Move-in date specifics listed below; (4) the place file's Moved in row and its dismissed moving-checklist line, for the arrival frame.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852 (native grouped list). Android 412x915 (Material 3 list). Web 1440x900 (left sidebar, settings in the content column) and 390x844 (bottom tab bar).\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Place tab → HOME A → Settings → Home Info. People arrive three ways.\n(1) Settings, through the existing per-home settings entry shown in the attached screenshot: on every platform, Place dashboard → Home tools → Settings; on iOS, the per-home settings index; on Android, the home's settings screen; on web, the settings page /app/homes/<HOME A>/settings. Draw the rows only on that web settings page and leave the separate /edit page unchanged.\n(2) The place file's \"Moved in\" row. Web: /app/homes/<HOME A>/settings?focus=move-in. Native: the home-settings deep link with the same focus. The page scrolls once to the Moved in row, fades a highlight on it and moves focus to it. When the value is \"Not set\", the DateSheet also opens after the highlight. This row and the place file row write the same date.\n(3) The place file's dismissed-checklist line \"Show again in home settings\". Web: ?focus=moving-checklist; native uses the same focus. The page lands with the Moving checklist row highlighted. The place file keeps its own InlineUndo for the moment of dismissal; this row is the lasting way back.\nWhat arrives: the home and which row to focus. Nothing is typed in advance. Homes claimed without a move-in date arrive with \"Not set\". The claim flow gap is recorded on Notes.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Maya Chen, owner of HOME A, on Mon 19 Oct 2026 at 6:10 PM. She claimed the address today, 20 days after moving in. At claim she ticked \"I just moved in\", so the app stamped today, Mon 19 Oct 2026, as her move-in date. The checklist showed with the wrong window and she hid it. She wants the real date, Tue 29 Sep 2026, and she wants the checklist back. Sam Ortega (member) opens the same screen on his Pixel. He accepted his invite earlier today and has hidden his own checklist.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Correct the move-in date that turns the 60-day moving checklist on, and bring back a hidden checklist.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: (1) The Moved in value. (2) The helper line under it, which says what the date controls. (3) The Moving checklist row with its \"Show again\" action. Primary action: tap the Moved in row to change the date.\n\nCONTENT (fixture deltas; everything else is HOME A as pasted):\n- Stamped value: Mon 19 Oct 2026, stamped at claim from Maya's \"I just moved in\" tick. Its checklist window would end Fri 18 Dec 2026 (in 60 days).\n- Corrected value: Tue 29 Sep 2026, set by Maya. The window ends Sat 28 Nov 2026 (in 40 days).\n- Future-date example: Sun 1 Nov 2026 (in 13 days; the window would run until Thu 31 Dec 2026).\n- Older than 60 days: Fri 14 Aug 2026 (the window ended Tue 13 Oct 2026).\n- Likely typo: Wed 29 Sep 2027 (the same day and month one year later, in 345 days).\n- Sam has hidden his own checklist (invented, for artboard 13).\n- Home name row: keep the screenshot's value. If there is none, use \"Larkspur Loop\".\n- Worst case: a 320pt column at AX5, showing Maya's view with both rows, the helper line, a status line, both scope sentences and an error row.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION: Draw two FactRows in the existing list pattern: the label above the value, then a trailing chevron or text action. There is no chart. The helper line is the key design decision. Without it, \"Moved in\" reads as trivia rather than as the switch for the moving checklist. Draw the helper in bodySmall text.secondary directly under the value. It shows in every state and wraps rather than truncating at 320pt.\nRow 1, \"Moved in\": the value is in body text.primary with a trailing ProvenanceMark S (you-added). Print the legend word \"You added this\" once, next to that mark. Under the helper, draw a status line in caption text.secondary. Its wording depends on the state for this viewer:\n- Checklist hidden: \"Checklist window ends Sat 28 Nov · in 40 days\" (artboards 1, 3, 4, 5, 13, 15, 16, 17, 18). With the stamped value it reads \"Checklist window ends Fri 18 Dec · in 60 days\" (artboards 2, 11, 19).\n- Checklist showing: \"Showing in your place file until Sat 28 Nov · in 40 days\" (artboard 14 only).\n- Saving (1s or longer): \"Saving Tue 29 Sep 2026…\" with a small inline progress indicator (artboard 10).\n- Just saved: \"Saved\" for 2 seconds, then the line returns to its checklist wording.\n- Not set: no status line. Future date: the start note replaces it. Older than 60 days: the older-than-60-days note replaces it.\nWhen row 1 has a date and the viewer can edit, give it a chevron and make the whole row the target. When there is no date, the value reads \"Not set\" in text.secondary (text.strong on a sunken row), with a text action \"Add\", and the helper still shows. Directly under row 1, draw the ScopeChip sentence \"Everyone in this household will see this.\"\nRow 2, \"Moving checklist\": value \"Hidden\" and a trailing text action \"Show again\" in primary.700. Draw this row only while the checklist is hidden for this viewer and its 60-day window has not ended. Hiding is saved on the server per person, so the row appears on every device. If the checklist was never hidden, or the window has ended, leave the row out (do not grey it out). Directly under row 2, draw the ScopeChip sentence \"Only you will see this.\"\nIn Sam's view (artboard 13): the Moved in value keeps the ProvenanceMark S tick shape, and the legend word reads \"Added by Maya Chen\" instead of \"You added this\". Leave out the household sentence under Moved in, because the LockedActionRow already names who can change it. Keep the status line, and keep \"Only you will see this.\" under his Moving checklist row.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS: Tapping the Moved in row opens the DateSheet with the Move-in date kind already chosen. Skip the kind grid. The sheet title is \"Move-in date\". The field opens holding the current value and accepts typing. iOS: the compact date picker (calendar with month/year jump) beside the typeable field. Android: the Material 3 modal date picker with its keyboard-input mode toggle visible. Web: a native typeable date input. Hide the \"Not sure of the day\" toggle, because the 60-day window needs an exact day. Hide the ReminderLeadControl for this kind, because a move-in date needs no reminder. The sheet footer carries the ScopeChip sentence \"Everyone in this household will see this.\", then Save and a visible Close. Validation suggests a fix and never blocks the save:\n- Today or any past date within 60 days: saves with no note.\n- Tomorrow up to 90 days ahead: saves with the start note, drawn as an info glyph with text.primary.\n- More than 90 days ahead: the suggested fix appears in the sheet before saving. \"Keep Wed 29 Sep 2027\" saves that date with the start note \"Your moving checklist will start Wed 29 Sep 2027 · in 345 days.\"\n- More than 60 days in the past: saves with the older-than-60-days note (info glyph, text.primary).\nOn Save, the sheet closes. If the save takes 1s or longer, the value keeps Mon 19 Oct 2026, the row is not tappable, and the status line reads \"Saving Tue 29 Sep 2026…\" with the inline progress indicator. Under 1s, show no progress. On success, the value changes to Tue 29 Sep 2026, the status line reads \"Saved\", and iOS and Android give one light haptic tick. Tapping \"Show again\" restores the checklist right away. The row collapses into an InlineUndo, \"Moving checklist is back in your place file · Undo\", which stays until Maya leaves the screen and has no timer. Deep-link arrivals scroll once, fade a highlight in 300ms or less, and move focus to the row. With Reduce Motion on, the screen jumps to the row, and the highlight and the Saved line cross-fade. No action depends on a gesture.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: FactRow (known, missing, permission-disabled variants) · DateSheet (view-mine, Move-in date kind, per-kind validation with a suggested fix, saving, offline; kind grid, \"Not sure of the day\" and ReminderLeadControl hidden) · ProvenanceMark (you-added, S) · ScopeChip (footer sentence form, used under each row and in the sheet footer) · InlineUndo (restored row) · InlineErrorRow (save failed, value preserved) · LockedActionRow (\"names who can act\" variant, no link) · OfflineNotice (read-only cached screen, with its FreshnessLine).\n\nACCESSIBILITY: Reading order is label → value → mark → helper → status → scope sentence. Spoken label for row 1 (Maya): \"Moved in, Tuesday 29 September 2026, you added this. Shows your moving checklist for 60 days. Checklist window ends Saturday 28 November, in 40 days. Button, change date.\" Sam: \"Moved in, Tuesday 29 September 2026, added by Maya Chen. Shows your moving checklist for 60 days. Checklist window ends Saturday 28 November, in 40 days. Only Maya Chen can change this.\" Row 2: \"Moving checklist, hidden. Only you will see this. Button, show again.\" Targets follow FactRow: the Moved in row with a chevron is one whole-row target; on the \"Not set\" row and the Moving checklist row, \"Add\" and \"Show again\" are separate text buttons, and those rows are not targets. Every target is 44pt on iOS, 48dp on Android (8dp gaps) and 44px on web. The mark is never a target on its own. Status changes (Saving Tue 29 Sep 2026, Saved, Retrying, Moving checklist is back) are polite live regions. Errors sit next to the row and Retry is spoken \"Retry saving move-in date\". Selection looks different from focus. At AX5 the value stacks under the label and every line wraps. The mark's shape carries meaning; colour carries none.\n\nCOPY:\n- Row labels: \"Moved in\" · \"Moving checklist\"\n- Helper: \"Shows your moving checklist for 60 days.\"\n- Status, hidden: \"Checklist window ends Sat 28 Nov · in 40 days\" (stamped: \"Checklist window ends Fri 18 Dec · in 60 days\")\n- Status, showing: \"Showing in your place file until Sat 28 Nov · in 40 days\"\n- Status, saving: \"Saving Tue 29 Sep 2026…\" · saved: \"Saved\"\n- Legend: \"You added this\"; Sam's view: \"Added by Maya Chen\"\n- Scope: \"Everyone in this household will see this.\" (under Moved in for editors, and in the sheet footer) · \"Only you will see this.\" (under Moving checklist)\n- Empty value: \"Not set\". Action: \"Add\"\n- Restore row: value \"Hidden\", action \"Show again\". Undo line: \"Moving checklist is back in your place file · Undo\"\n- Start note: \"Your moving checklist will start Sun 1 Nov · in 13 days.\"\n- Older-than-60-days note: \"Saved. Your moving checklist ran until Tue 13 Oct, so it won't show now.\"\n- Suggested fix: \"That's almost a year away. Did you mean Tue 29 Sep 2026?\" with buttons \"Use Tue 29 Sep 2026\" and \"Keep Wed 29 Sep 2027\" at equal weight\n- Save error: \"We couldn't save Tue 29 Sep 2026. Your move-in date is still Mon 19 Oct 2026.\" with the button \"Retry\"\n- Offline: FreshnessLine \"You're offline · as of 6:10 PM\"; under Moved in: \"You're offline. You can change the move-in date when you're back.\"; under Show again: \"Showing the checklist again needs a connection.\"\n- Member view: \"Only Maya Chen can change this.\"\n- Sheet: title \"Move-in date\", buttons \"Save\" and \"Close\"\n\nEDGE CASES: A long address in the existing Address row wraps to 2 lines. A date more than 90 days ahead gets the suggested fix. Keeping it saves it with the start note. A date years in the past saves with the older-than-60-days note. When the window has already ended, the Moving checklist row is absent, because there is nothing to show again. An empty value slot shows the words \"Not set\", never a blank. On a slow save, the value keeps the old date and the status line says which date is saving. When the save fails, draw the InlineErrorRow on an errorBg slot under row 1. The value keeps Mon 19 Oct 2026 and its status line. Retry resends Tue 29 Sep 2026. Tapping the row reopens the DateSheet with Tue 29 Sep 2026 already filled in. Offline, the cached value stays readable, the Moved in row and Show again are disabled but focusable, and each carries its stated reason. Sam (member) sees Moved in as plain read-only text with no chevron, plus the LockedActionRow line. Hiding is per person, so Sam still gets his own \"Show again\". On web, draw the rows only on the settings page and leave the /edit page unchanged.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of a \"Finish setting up your home\" card with a progress bar, draw two plain rows in the existing list, because this is a setting to correct, not an onboarding step.\n- Instead of \"Not set\" in faint grey, draw it in text.secondary with an Add action, because it is the switch for the whole moving checklist and has to be readable (text.muted is 2.54:1).\n- Instead of red or warning styling on the start and older-than-60-days notes, draw an info glyph with text.primary, because the date is valid and the note only explains when the checklist shows.\n- Instead of blocking unusual dates, draw a suggested fix with two equal buttons, because a real move-in date is usually in the past.\n- Instead of a greyed-out date control for Sam, draw the date as plain text plus \"Only Maya Chen can change this.\", because a control that looks dead reads as a broken app.\n- Instead of a timed \"Show again\" toast, draw InlineUndo that stays until the person leaves, because undo must not expire.\n- Instead of one household sentence for the whole group, draw one scope sentence under each row, because the date is shared and hiding the checklist is personal.\n- Instead of showing the newly picked date while the save is still running, keep the old date and write \"Saving Tue 29 Sep 2026…\", because the value slot must only show what is saved.\n\nDONE WHEN: A mover whose date was stamped at claim can set the real date on iOS, Android and web in two taps plus typing. The helper line says what the date does in every state. The status line never contradicts the Moving checklist row. While saving, Maya can see both the saved date and the date on its way. A hidden checklist can be brought back from any device, and the screen says that only the viewer sees that choice. The error frame names both the date that failed and the date still saved. No state looks like an error unless a save failed. Every frame reads correctly in greyscale and at AX5.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f6-home-basics-rows · ios · 01-set-dense · light — Maya, settled after saving: Moved in Tue 29 Sep 2026 with tick and \"You added this\", helper, status \"Checklist window ends Sat 28 Nov · in 40 days\", household sentence, Moving checklist Hidden with its separate Show again button, \"Only you will see this.\"\n2. f6-home-basics-rows · ios · 02-date-sheet-open · light — DateSheet over the list, opened from the stamped Mon 19 Oct 2026. The field now holds the typed Tue 29 Sep 2026. Compact picker; no kind grid, no \"Not sure\" toggle, no ReminderLeadControl; footer sentence, Save, Close.\n3. f6-home-basics-rows · android · 01-set-dense · light — the content of 1 in the M3 list; inset of the M3 modal date picker with its keyboard-input toggle.\n4. f6-home-basics-rows · web-1440 · 01-set-dense · light — the settings page in the sidebar layout, with the content of 1; inset of the typeable date input.\n5. f6-home-basics-rows · web-390 · 01-set-dense · light — mobile web with the bottom tab bar, content of 1.\n6. f6-home-basics-rows · ios · 03-not-set · light — \"Not set\" with a separate Add button, helper, household sentence, no status line; restore row absent (never hidden).\n7. f6-home-basics-rows · ios · 04-future-date · light — Sun 1 Nov 2026 saved; start note \"Your moving checklist will start Sun 1 Nov · in 13 days.\" in place of the status line; restore row absent.\n8. f6-home-basics-rows · ios · 05-past-60-days · light — Fri 14 Aug 2026 saved with the older-than-60-days note; restore row absent, because the window has ended and there is nothing to show again.\n9. f6-home-basics-rows · ios · 06-suggested-fix · light — the sheet holding Wed 29 Sep 2027 with the suggested fix and two equal buttons, \"Use Tue 29 Sep 2026\" and \"Keep Wed 29 Sep 2027\".\n10. f6-home-basics-rows · ios · 07-saving · light — value Mon 19 Oct 2026; status line \"Saving Tue 29 Sep 2026…\" with inline progress; row not tappable. Labelled crop: the same row a moment later with value Tue 29 Sep 2026 and status \"Saved\".\n11. f6-home-basics-rows · ios · 08-save-error · light — value Mon 19 Oct 2026 with its status line; InlineErrorRow \"We couldn't save Tue 29 Sep 2026. Your move-in date is still Mon 19 Oct 2026.\" with Retry.\n12. f6-home-basics-rows · android · 09-offline · light — \"You're offline · as of 6:10 PM\" at top; both rows disabled with their reason captions.\n13. f6-home-basics-rows · android · 10-member-read-only · light — Sam's view: plain Tue 29 Sep 2026 with tick and \"Added by Maya Chen\", helper, status \"Checklist window ends Sat 28 Nov · in 40 days\", LockedActionRow \"Only Maya Chen can change this.\" (no household sentence under Moved in), his own Moving checklist row with Show again and \"Only you will see this.\"\n14. f6-home-basics-rows · ios · 11-restored-undo · light — InlineUndo \"Moving checklist is back in your place file · Undo\"; status now \"Showing in your place file until Sat 28 Nov · in 40 days\".\n15. f6-home-basics-rows · ios · 12-deep-link-arrival · light — arrival from the place file's Moved in row: row highlighted, focus ring on it; labelled crop of the Moving checklist row highlighted for the \"Show again in home settings\" arrival.\n16. f6-home-basics-rows · ios · 13-ax5 · light — 320pt content at AX5: both rows, helper, status, both scope sentences and the error row, all stacked and wrapped.\n17. f6-home-basics-rows · ios · 14-greyscale · light — artboard 1 in greyscale.\n18. f6-home-basics-rows · ios · 01-set-dense · dark — dark twin of 1.\n19. f6-home-basics-rows · ios · 08-save-error · dark — dark twin of 11.\n20. f6-home-basics-rows · Notes — assumptions, every invented string, omitted states, open questions.\n\nNotes must record:\n- Every invented string: \"Checklist window ends …\", \"Showing in your place file until …\", \"Saving Tue 29 Sep 2026…\", \"Saved\", \"Added by Maya Chen\", \"Showing the checklist again needs a connection.\", the save-error sentence, the suggested-fix sentence and its buttons \"Use Tue 29 Sep 2026\" and \"Keep Wed 29 Sep 2027\", the start note for Wed 29 Sep 2027, and Sam's hidden checklist.\n- Date order: the status, saving, showing and start-note lines open with their own deadline wording, so the relative count follows the date, as in f6-place-section-details. Every other date uses the house order.\n- Assumption: the stamped date carries the you-added tick because Maya ticked \"I just moved in\" at claim. The claim checkbox is the source.\n- Assumption: Sam accepted his invite earlier today and hid his checklist on his Pixel. The dates are unchanged.\n- The validation rule as an assumption: more than 90 days ahead gets the suggested fix; tomorrow to 90 days gets the start note; more than 60 days past gets the older note.\n- DateSheet, Move-in date kind: the kind grid, \"Not sure of the day\" and ReminderLeadControl are hidden. This deviates from the contract anatomy.\n- The proposed focus parameters ?focus=move-in and ?focus=moving-checklist, and their native deep-link equivalents.\n- Editors are the owner, admins and members with home edit rights. Sam has none of these in the fixture.\n- Research recommends keying the checklist to each person's own move-in date, which would give Sam his own date, rather than the home's.\n- The claim flow should ask for, or carry over, the move-in date.\n- \"Added by Maya Chen\" is a contract gap, since the tick's legend word is only \"You added this\".\n- The helper says \"moving checklist\" rather than \"first-week steps\" so it does not collide with Today's 7-day first-week row.\n- Web has two settings surfaces. The rows go on /app/homes/[id]/settings, and /edit is unchanged.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for continue. Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue. Turn 3: 13-18, then wait for continue. Turn 4: 19-20.",
        "changeLog": [
          "ATTACH: replaced the single 'Foundations board' with boards 00a, 00c and 00d, added the x-date-sheet view-mine and validation artboards as the DateSheet source, and renumbered the place-file attachment to (4) (review, major).",
          "Saving is now one consistent behaviour: the value keeps the old date, the status line reads 'Saving Tue 29 Sep 2026…', then 'Saved' and a haptic tick. Artboard 10 was updated and COPY and Notes gained both strings (review, major).",
          "Entry points: named the per-platform settings routes from the derive proposal and the web page /app/homes/<HOME A>/settings (/edit unchanged), and added the ?focus=move-in and ?focus=moving-checklist URLs, recorded as proposed on Notes (review, minor).",
          "The target model now follows FactRow: the chevron row is a whole-row target, and 'Add' and 'Show again' are separate text buttons (review, minor).",
          "Suggested-fix buttons now include the weekday: 'Use Tue 29 Sep 2026' and 'Keep Wed 29 Sep 2027'. Added what 'Keep' saves: the start note, in 345 days (review, minor).",
          "Sam: his spoken label now includes the status line, artboard 13 shows the status line, the household sentence under Moved in is left out in his view, and 'Only you will see this.' stays (review, minor x2).",
          "The window-ended rule is defined: the restore row is absent on artboard 8 and in EDGE CASES (review, minor x2).",
          "Notes now records: the date-order exception, the stamped-date tick assumption (from the claim checkbox), the assumption about Sam's invite timing, the DateSheet anatomy deviation, and the focus parameters (review, minor).",
          "Added an INSTEAD OF line about showing the old date while saving; all v1 substance is kept."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f6-place-section-details",
        "name": "Place section details: risk instrument, free radon kits, registration deadline",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 29,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Place section details: Risk & readiness and Civic · f6-place-section-details\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screens \"Place > Risk & readiness\" and \"Place > Civic\". This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed. On Risk: replace the separate flood, wildfire and radon-zone chip rows with the four-row ScaleStrip instrument, and add one outbound kit action to the existing \"Lead & radon\" card. Keep the section header, the seismic entry, and the Lead & radon card's build-year lead line, county-zone phrase and grey screening disclaimer exactly as the screenshot shows them. The strip and the card state the same zone in their own words. On Civic: add a \"Your registration\" block above the existing election banner. Keep the election banner, polling card and ballot preview as they are. On both pages, keep the host's existing \"Your household\" ScopeChip in the page header. If the screenshot has none, add it under the page title.\n\nATTACH: (1) Risk & readiness and Civic for HOME A on iOS, Android, web 1440 and web 390; (2) Foundations boards 00a (ProvenanceMark, SourceCaption, ScopeChip, FreshnessLine and OfflineNotice), 00b (ScaleStrip, AqiBand), 00c (TextActionRow, InlineErrorRow) and 00d (WarmingSkeleton); (3) the detail-size artboard from the scale-strips prompt; (4) the accepted x-provenance-sheet specimen and the x-date-sheet view-seeded voter artboard; (5) the place file's Voter registration row for PLACE B, for the proposed saved-place frame.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852 · Android 412x915 · web 1440x900 (left sidebar plus the Place section rail) and 390x844.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Place tab → HOME A → Risk & readiness (web /app/place/risk), and Place tab → HOME A → Civic (web /app/place/civic). Entry points:\n- The two section rows in the Place tab.\n- The place file's \"Voter registration\" row. It opens Civic, scrolls once to the registration block and highlights it. Web: /app/place/civic?focus=registration. Native: the civic deep link with the same registration focus.\n- The seasonal headline for the registration deadline, which lands on the same focus.\n- From a compare view (flow 05): a row tap on a compare strip opens the ProvenanceSheet, not this page. Only when the viewer is signed in and the \"You\" address is their primary home does that sheet add a row \"See all readings for Larkspur Loop\". That row opens Risk with the layer highlighted (web /app/place/risk?focus=wildfire, a proposed focus parameter; native uses the risk deep link with the same focus). The page header then shows the named-home ScopeChip \"Larkspur Loop · Your household\", so no reading appears under another address's context. Dana's row and typed addresses never link here.\n- The mover's civic path (flow 13): the seasonal headline, then the place file's moving row \"Update your voter registration\", then here. The previous step hands over the state and the per-method dates, so the wording here must match exactly.\n- The place file's voter row at PLACE B, for a saved-place mover. PROPOSED: today this page needs a claimed primary home, so this arrival is drawn once as a proposal (artboard 18).\n- After sign-up from the January radon headline (web /app/place/risk?focus=radon). The signed-out outbound kit link is drawn in the seasonal-aha prompt. Here, the page scrolls so that both the radon row and the kit row are in view, and the radon row is highlighted.\nThese pages resolve the primary home only. Next step: \"Remind me\" opens the DateSheet in view-seeded voter mode. There the person picks a method (Online, Mail, In person), the reminder follows that method's deadline, \"I did this\" records a self-report for that person only, and the sheet carries its own line saying the app can't check registration status.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Maya Chen on Mon 19 Oct 2026, 6:10 PM. She moved to Washington this fall. She opens Civic from her place file to see which way to register is still open. Then she checks Risk, because Dana's compare card made her curious about radon. For the proposed saved-place frame: Jordan Lee at PLACE B, the same evening, arriving from his place file's voter row.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Read each public hazard on its own authority's scale, take the one free step (a radon test), and see which voter registration path is still open, with the official place to check it.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: Risk: (1) the four value lines, (2) the marker positions, (3) the Radon caption \"only a test tells you about this home\". The kit row is the first action below the instrument: one scroll down on phones, above the fold on web-1440. Civic: (1) \"Online/mail: must arrive by Mon 26 Oct · in 7 days\", (2) the in-person line, (3) \"Check or update at VoteWA ↗\". Primary action on Risk: \"Order a free radon kit from WA Dept of Health ↗\". Primary action on Civic: \"Check or update at VoteWA ↗\".\n\nCONTENT (HOME A readings as pasted; deltas only):\n- Air in the dense frames: \"AQI 42 · Good\", observed 6:00 PM today. The stale crop uses the fixture time 7:00 AM.\n- Lead line build year: keep the screenshot's wording. If a year is needed, use 1998 (invented).\n- In-person-only date: Tue 27 Oct 2026.\n- Self-report date: Sat 17 Oct 2026 (invented).\n- The Civic dense frame uses \"Official\" confidence (an assumption, recorded on Notes). The unverified frame uses the hollow mark.\n- Alert air reading: \"AQI 118 · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups\".\n- Worst case: AX5 at 320pt with all four rows and the kit action (artboard 23), and the Civic stack of registration block, election banner, polling card and ballot preview (artboard 24).\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION:\nRISK. Vertical order: page title → ScopeChip → summary line → instrument → Lead & radon card (with the kit row) → seismic entry. The summary line is one line in bodySmall: \"Four public readings for this address, each on its own scale.\" The instrument is one ScaleStrip at detail size, full width, with 48pt rows in this fixed order:\n- Flood zone: \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\". Three bands: Minimal (X) · 0.2% a year (shaded X) · 1% a year or more (A/V zones). The marker sits in band 1, labelled \"Zone X\". Caption: \"FEMA · area zone · effective Sep 2021\".\n- Wildfire hazard potential: \"Moderate · 3 of 5\". Bands: Very low · Low · Moderate · High · Very high. Caption: \"USFS · relative hazard, 30 m model · 2023\".\n- Air quality index (AQI): \"AQI 42 · Good\". AqiBand instrument row: six equal ColorVision Assist segments, the last labelled \"301+\", with 2px gaps, a keyline and a halo marker. The band name is printed beside the track, never on the fill. The pollutant is left out inside the instrument. Caption: \"AirNow air quality index (AQI) · nearest monitors · observed 6:00 PM today\".\n- Radon zone: \"Zone 1 — highest potential of EPA's 3 zones\". Bands run Zone 3 · Zone 2 · Zone 1, left to right; the marker is in Zone 1. Caption: \"EPA · county-wide estimate — only a test tells you about this home\".\nEvery row carries a FILLED mark. Print \"● Official\" once, beside the first mark. Flood, wildfire and radon tracks are neutral, with band dividers and a keyline in ink at 3:1 or better. The occupied band is shown by the marker, its printed name and an outline. Only Air is coloured. The tracks never share an axis and never add up to a total. Draw no icon array anywhere on this surface. The rule for adding one later goes on Notes.\nDegraded states:\n- No data: a greyed track, no marker, and \"Not on record\" at full row height.\n- \"FEMA hasn't mapped flood hazard here\" and \"Non-burnable land cover (USFS)\" are their own states. Neither looks like \"very low\".\n- Stale air: the caption appends its age, \"AirNow air quality index (AQI) · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM — 11 hours ago\". The Air mark stays at full ink, as on the ScaleStrip specimen; the age words carry the staleness.\n- Collapsed sources: when the instrument's content width is 360 or less (web-390, whose content is 358 after 16px gutters, and 320 at AX5), the four captions merge into \"Sources: FEMA, USFS, AirNow, EPA\". Air keeps \"observed 6:00 PM today\", and the Radon value keeps \"county-wide\". iOS 393, Android 412 and web-1440 keep full captions.\nIn the Lead & radon card, under the existing disclaimer, draw a 1px rule, leave 16pt, then a TextActionRow outbound row: \"Order a free radon kit from WA Dept of Health ↗\". Draw it as a bordered action row, not grey prose, because a second grey block under the first hides the only free action on the page. If the state has a program but no free kits, the row reads \"Visit the Washington Dept of Health radon program ↗\". If there is no program, draw no row at all and no generic EPA link. The kit row depends only on the state program. It stays when the card has partial coverage (no build year on file), and when the card shows its existing unavailable line \"No build year on file and no county radon coverage for this area yet.\"\n\nCIVIC. The \"Your registration\" block is a card above the election banner, because a dated action outranks information. Contents, top to bottom:\n- Title \"Your registration\".\n- Address line \"Larkspur Loop · Your household\" (the named-home ScopeChip). Show it only for people with more than one home, because this page always uses the primary home.\n- \"Washington · Tue 3 Nov 2026 general election\", then two method lines. In these two lines the relative count follows the date, because each line opens with its deadline wording. Every other date caption uses the house order.\n  - \"Online/mail: must arrive by Mon 26 Oct · in 7 days\"\n  - \"In person at Clark County Elections: until 8:00 PM Tue 3 Nov · in 15 days\"\n- \"Moved in? Registration is per address.\"\n- A SourceCaption with a FILLED mark and \"● Official\" printed once beside it: \"Washington Secretary of State · statewide · as of Mon 19 Oct ↗\".\n- Primary action: a TextActionRow outbound row, \"Check or update at VoteWA ↗\".\n- Directly under it, in caption text.secondary: \"Only VoteWA can tell you if you're registered.\"\n- Secondary action: a text button, \"Remind me\".\nAfter the online/mail deadline, that line reads \"Online/mail: closed Mon 26 Oct\" in text.secondary, and the in-person line leads. After 8:00 PM Tue 3 Nov the block is gone, and once the election has passed the existing \"No upcoming election\" state shows. If Maya reported registering, add one line under the method lines: \"You marked this done on Sat 17 Oct. Only you will see this.\", with a trailing chevron that opens the DateSheet, where she can clear it. Both method lines, VoteWA and its caption stay. Use no \"Registered\" wording anywhere. In the proposed saved-place frame, the page header chip reads \"Saved place · Only you\", the block has no address line, and the block content is otherwise identical. That frame never uses the words home, household or claim.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS: Each strip row is one target that opens the ProvenanceSheet. For flood, the sheet reads \"Only FEMA can change this\" with \"How to request a Letter of Map Amendment ↗\". For radon, the sheet states the county-wide scope and shows \"Get a free test kit\". Outbound links open an in-app browser on iOS and Android and a new tab on web, so the page survives the detour. \"Remind me\" opens the DateSheet in view-seeded voter mode. The self-report line opens the same sheet. Arrivals scroll once, fade a highlight in 300ms or less and move focus. With Reduce Motion on, arrivals jump and cross-fade, and skeletons are static. There are no haptics on this page. No action depends on a gesture or hover.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: ScaleStrip (detail size; no-data, not-studied and non-burnable variants; stale air row at full ink; AX5) · AqiBand (instrument row, stale) · SourceCaption (dated static, live, stale, county scope, collapsed sources line) · ProvenanceMark (official; unconfirmed on the civic seed) · ProvenanceSheet (hazard-owned-by-authority, radon) · ScopeChip (\"Your household\" in page headers; \"Larkspur Loop · Your household\" for multi-home and compare arrivals; \"Saved place · Only you\" in the proposed frame; sentence \"Only you will see this.\") · TextActionRow (outbound) · WarmingSkeleton (instrument) · InlineErrorRow (provider unreachable) · FreshnessLine and OfflineNotice · DateSheet (view-seeded voter, as the destination only).\n\nACCESSIBILITY: The summary line is read first. Then the instrument group, labelled (and given as the web text alternative) \"Flood Zone X, minimal flood hazard. Wildfire Moderate, 3 of 5. Air AQI 42, Good. Radon Zone 1, county-wide.\" Then each strip row as one element, then the card, then the seismic entry. Spoken labels: \"Flood zone: Zone X, minimal flood hazard, band 1 of 3, scale Minimal to 1% a year or more. FEMA, effective September 2021. Official.\" \"Wildfire hazard potential: Moderate, 3 of 5, scale Very low to Very high. USFS 2023. Official.\" \"Air quality index: 42, Good, category 1 of 6. AirNow, observed 6:00 PM. Official.\" \"Radon zone: Zone 1, highest potential of EPA's 3 zones, scale Zone 3 to Zone 1, county-wide estimate. EPA. Official.\" The rows are the text list for the instrument. Retry is spoken \"Retry air quality\". Links name their destination: \"Order a free radon kit, opens Washington State Department of Health website\" and \"Check or update at VoteWA, opens the state voter site\". Civic reading order: title → address line → state and election → method lines → self-report line → moved line → source → VoteWA → VoteWA caption → Remind me. Targets are 44pt / 48dp / 44px. Band position is always stated in words. Disabled links stay focusable with their reason read out.\n\nCOPY: all strings quoted above, plus:\n- \"Not on record\" · \"FEMA hasn't mapped flood hazard here\" · \"Non-burnable land cover (USFS)\"\n- 1%-a-year zone: \"Zone AE — 1% chance of flooding each year (about 1 in 4 over 30 years)\"\n- Legend words: \"● Official\" / \"○ On record, not confirmed\"\n- Unverified caption: \"Washington Secretary of State · statewide · as of Mon 19 Oct · not yet checked against the state site\"\n- Partial failure: \"We couldn't reach AirNow just now\" with \"Retry\"\n- Offline: \"You're offline · as of 6:10 PM\", with \"Opening this link needs a connection.\" under each disabled link\n- Compare sheet row: \"See all readings for Larkspur Loop\"\n- Existing section-unavailable fallback: unchanged\n\nEDGE CASES: A 1%-a-year zone uses the Zone AE string above, with the marker in band 3. The alert reading is \"AQI 118 · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups\". One layer missing keeps all four rows. No seeded voter rule: the block is absent, not an empty card. Unverified seed: hollow mark plus the unverified caption. On a slow load, show WarmingSkeleton after 1s. A member without edit rights sees everything; \"Remind me\" and the self-report are personal. A multi-home owner sees the address line. At content widths of 360 or less, the collapsed sources line applies.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of a letter grade, score, stars or radar, draw four separate strips, because four authorities share no scale and a single shape reads as a report card on a home.\n- Instead of \"Zone 1 of 3\", write \"Zone 1 — highest potential of EPA's 3 zones\", because \"N of M\" flips meaning next to wildfire's \"3 of 5\".\n- Instead of \"wildfire risk\" or \"this season\", write \"Wildfire hazard potential\", because USFS says its hazard potential is not a risk map or a seasonal outlook.\n- Instead of a hollow radon mark, draw it filled with the county-wide scope caption, because the zone is official and its limit is scope.\n- Instead of \"Check or update\" opening an internal sheet, send it to VoteWA and keep \"Remind me\" separate, because the app cannot know whether anyone is registered.\n- Instead of a \"Registered\" badge after a self-report, draw \"You marked this done on Sat 17 Oct. Only you will see this.\" with both deadlines still showing, because a self-report is never a fact for the household.\n- Instead of hiding the block after Mon 26 Oct, draw the in-person-only state, because in-person registration stays open until 8:00 PM Tue 3 Nov.\n- Instead of the kit as another grey caption, draw an outbound action row under a rule, because it is the only free step.\n\nDONE WHEN: The risk page matches the share card's instrument row for row. No frame implies a verdict about a home. Air always shows its time, and its age once stale. Radon offers the kit only where a program exists. Every source caption reads authority · scope · as-of. The civic block states both method deadlines with their weekdays, relative counts and source, and never states registration status, including after a self-report. Every page states its scope, and no compare arrival shows one address's readings under another's name. Flow moment: Maya (or Jordan, in the proposal) sees both paths, checks at VoteWA and sets a reminder separately.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f6-place-section-details · ios · 01-risk-dense · light — scope chip, summary line, four strips with \"● Official\", Lead & radon card with the kit row, seismic entry below.\n2. f6-place-section-details · ios · 02-civic-dense · light — scope chip, registration block with \"● Official\" and the VoteWA caption, then election banner, polling card and ballot preview.\n3. f6-place-section-details · web-1440 · 01-risk-dense · light — sidebar and section rail; full captions; kit row above the fold.\n4. f6-place-section-details · web-1440 · 02-civic-dense · light — the stack of 2 at desktop width.\n5. f6-place-section-details · android · 01-risk-dense · light — M3 version of 1.\n6. f6-place-section-details · android · 02-civic-dense · light — M3 version of 2.\n7. f6-place-section-details · web-390 · 01-risk-dense · light — collapsed sources line; Air keeps \"observed 6:00 PM today\"; Radon keeps \"county-wide\".\n8. f6-place-section-details · web-390 · 02-civic-dense · light — the civic stack on mobile web with the bottom tab bar.\n9. f6-place-section-details · ios · 03-risk-partial · light — wildfire \"Not on record\" with a greyed track; labelled crop of the stale Air row (\"observed 7:00 AM — 11 hours ago\", mark at full ink).\n10. f6-place-section-details · ios · 04-risk-special-states · light — four labelled single-row crops: (a) Flood \"FEMA hasn't mapped flood hazard here\"; (b) Wildfire \"Non-burnable land cover (USFS)\"; (c) Flood \"Zone AE — 1% chance of flooding each year (about 1 in 4 over 30 years)\" with the marker in band 3; (d) Air \"AQI 118 · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups\" with the marker in category 3.\n11. f6-place-section-details · ios · 05-provenance-sheets · light — the flood sheet over Risk: \"Only FEMA can change this\" with the LOMA link; labelled crop of the radon sheet with its county-wide scope and \"Get a free test kit\".\n12. f6-place-section-details · ios · 06-radon-program-variants · light — three labelled crops: free kits · program without kits (\"Visit the Washington Dept of Health radon program ↗\") · no program (no row).\n13. f6-place-section-details · ios · 07-lead-radon-coverage · light — two labelled card crops: no build year on file, with the zone phrase and kit row; the existing unavailable line with the kit row.\n14. f6-place-section-details · ios · 08-civic-unverified-multi-home · light — hollow mark, \"○ On record, not confirmed\", unverified caption, address line \"Larkspur Loop · Your household\".\n15. f6-place-section-details · ios · 09-civic-in-person-only · light — TODAY Tue 27 Oct; \"Online/mail: closed Mon 26 Oct\"; the in-person line leads with \"in 7 days\".\n16. f6-place-section-details · ios · 10-civic-self-reported · light — block with \"You marked this done on Sat 17 Oct. Only you will see this.\"; both method lines, VoteWA and its caption present; no \"Registered\" wording.\n17. f6-place-section-details · ios · 11-civic-absent-states · light — two crops: no seeded rule (block absent) and after Tue 3 Nov (\"No upcoming election\").\n18. f6-place-section-details · ios · 12-civic-saved-place · light — labelled PROPOSED: Jordan Lee at PLACE B, header chip \"Saved place · Only you\", the same registration block.\n19. f6-place-section-details · ios · 13-loading · light — WarmingSkeleton track outlines, static-capable.\n20. f6-place-section-details · ios · 14-error · light — the Air row's InlineErrorRow with the other rows live; crop of the section-unavailable fallback.\n21. f6-place-section-details · android · 15-offline · light — cached readings, \"You're offline · as of 6:10 PM\", links disabled with reasons.\n22. f6-place-section-details · ios · 16-arrivals · light — three labelled crops: (a) compare arrival: the ProvenanceSheet row \"See all readings for Larkspur Loop\", then Risk with header chip \"Larkspur Loop · Your household\" and the wildfire row highlighted and focused; (b) civic registration-focus arrival with the block highlighted; (c) radon arrival scrolled so the highlighted radon row and the kit row are both in view.\n23. f6-place-section-details · ios · 17-ax5-risk · light — text above full-width tracks at 320pt, collapsed sources line, all four rows and the kit row.\n24. f6-place-section-details · ios · 18-ax5-civic · light — the full civic stack at AX5, 320pt, everything wrapped.\n25. f6-place-section-details · ios · 19-greyscale-risk · light — frame 1 in greyscale; Air still readable by name and position.\n26. f6-place-section-details · ios · 01-risk-dense · dark — dark twin of 1.\n27. f6-place-section-details · ios · 02-civic-dense · dark — dark twin of 2.\n28. f6-place-section-details · ios · 09-civic-in-person-only · dark — dark twin of 15.\n29. f6-place-section-details · Notes — assumptions, invented strings, omitted states and open questions.\n\nNotes must list:\n- Invented strings: 1998; \"Four public readings for this address, each on its own scale.\"; \"Your registration\"; \"Washington · Tue 3 Nov 2026 general election\"; the Sat 17 Oct self-report line; \"Only VoteWA can tell you if you're registered.\"; \"Opening this link needs a connection.\"; \"See all readings for Larkspur Loop\"; \"observed 6:00 PM today\"; the stale Air caption; \"Visit the Washington Dept of Health radon program ↗\"; the what-if crops (Zone AE, AQI 118); the ?focus=wildfire and ?focus=radon parameters.\n- Assumptions: the Washington election_deadline row was checked against the state site before the pilot, so it is Official; until then, artboard 14's hollow treatment is the shipped default. The page reads the election_deadline rule directly, not the 14-day window that today's calendar read path expands, which would return nothing for a November deadline in October. The DateSheet voter mode carries the fuller \"we can't check registration status\" sentence; this block adds only the VoteWA caption.\n- Rules: the relative-count order used in the method lines. The icon-array rule: if one is ever added (detail or provenance sheet only), use a 4- or 100-cell array that shows the whole population, captioned \"about 1 in 4 over 30 years\"; never show a bare count without its base. The inventory's \"Check or update opens the Date sheet\" now lives on \"Remind me\". The compare-strip entry now goes through the ProvenanceSheet and reaches Risk only for the viewer's own primary home.\n- Omitted: none of the ProvenanceSheet variants beyond flood and radon.\n- Open questions: whether a saved place may open this page (flow 13 needs it; artboard 18 is a proposal); whether the compare sheet's \"See all readings\" row should exist at all; the contract's example kit label vs this verb-led label; the contract's short radon string vs \"of EPA's 3 zones\"; the contract's \"Zone AE — 1% chance each year\" vs this surface's \"of flooding\" wording; the wildfire caption \"relative hazard, 30 m model\" vs the 00b specimen's \"quarter-mile area\"; the layer labels, which now follow 00b (\"Wildfire hazard potential\", \"Air quality index (AQI)\") instead of v1's \"Wildfire hazard\" and \"Air today\"; the step copy follows the design doc's \"Moved in? Registration is per address.\" instead of v1's \"Moved recently?\".\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: 1-6, then wait for continue. Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue. Turn 3: 13-18, then wait for continue. Turn 4: 19-24, then wait for continue. Turn 5: 25-29.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Compare entry point rewritten per flow-05: a strip tap opens the ProvenanceSheet. Only for the viewer's own primary home does it offer 'See all readings for Larkspur Loop' into Risk, with the named-home ScopeChip in the header. Artboard 22 is updated, and the open question is on Notes (review, major).",
          "Risk vertical order is now stated: title, chip, summary, instrument, Lead & radon card with the kit row, then the seismic entry. FIRST FIVE SECONDS now ends on the radon caption, with the kit row placed one scroll down on phones. Radon arrivals scroll so the radon row and kit row are both in view (review, major).",
          "Civic SourceCaption now reads authority · scope · as-of: 'Washington Secretary of State · statewide · as of Mon 19 Oct ↗'. The election line moved into the block, and the unverified caption gained scope and as-of. The second review's 'checked Mon 5 Oct 2026' variant was not used because it conflicts with the house-style as-of form (review, major and minor).",
          "Notes records the assumption that the seeded voter rule is Official, and that the hollow mark is the shipped default until the rule is checked (review, minor).",
          "The collapsed-sources rule is rewritten as content width 360 or less (web-390 and AX5). Air keeps its time and Radon keeps 'county-wide'. iOS, Android and web-1440 keep full captions (review, minor x2).",
          "The stale Air mark stays at full ink, per the 00b specimen, and the age words carry the staleness (review, minor).",
          "Added an instrument text summary and group label, and added 'scale Zone 3 to Zone 1' to the radon spoken label (review, minor).",
          "The alert Air value drops PM2.5, and an AQI 118 crop was added to artboard 10 (review, minor).",
          "Layer labels changed to the contract strings 'Wildfire hazard potential' and 'Air quality index (AQI)'. The caption difference is listed as an open question (review, minor).",
          "Added the visible honesty caption 'Only VoteWA can tell you if you're registered.' and recorded that the DateSheet voter mode carries the fuller sentence (derive proposal f6-voter-step-sheet, review minor).",
          "Notes records the backend read-path dependency for the election_deadline rule (review, minor).",
          "Artboard 11 now includes a radon ProvenanceSheet crop (review, minor).",
          "The icon-array rule now allows a 4- or 100-cell array and bans bare counts (per-surface-changes, review minor).",
          "ATTACH now splits Foundations into 00a–00d and adds the x-provenance-sheet specimen and the x-date-sheet view-seeded voter artboard (review, minor).",
          "Step copy restored to the design doc's 'Moved in? Registration is per address.' Notes now lists every newly flagged invented string (review, minor)."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f3-members-roster",
        "name": "Members roster",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 24,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Who lives here (Members roster) · f3-members-roster\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Members\" (the home's Members & Security tab). This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed.\n- On web there must be exactly one members screen. The standalone members page and the dashboard's Members & Security tab become the same surface, so draw it once, as the tab. Keep the tab's existing security content below the roster, unchanged.\n- The old web \"Add guest\" page is deleted. It showed a success message without sending anything. Do not draw it anywhere.\n\nATTACH: the current Members screen on iOS, Android and web 1440 (the Members & Security tab, with the home header tabs Dashboard · Share · Members & Security · Settings); the place file's People section on iOS; the Foundations board from prompt 00.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852 (primary), Android 412x915, web 1440x900 (left sidebar) and 390x844 (bottom tab bar). Sheets: iOS sheets with detents; Android modal bottom sheets; web 1440 centred dialogs 480 wide; web 390 bottom sheets.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Place tab → place file for Larkspur Loop → People → Who lives here. On web the page is /app/homes/{id}/members, and it shows the same surface as the dashboard tab. Entry points:\n- the home dashboard Members card, quick action and Members & Security tab\n- the place file's People rows\n- the household block (\"Who lives here with you?\") once someone has joined\n- Today's member count\n- the Invite composer's Done, which returns here with the new Pending row highlighted once (\"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct · Resend\")\n- the Invite composer's Done after a Reissue, which returns here with that row highlighted once\n- the sender banner \"2 invitations need to be sent again · Fix\" and its in-app notification row, which land here scrolled to the Needs reissue rows, with a highlight that fades once\n- deep links /app/homes/{id}/members and their native equivalents.\nThe recipient banner \"You have 2 invitations\" does not come here. It opens the Invitations waiting for you list on Your places.\nWhat this screen hands on: Invite and \"Invite someone\" open the Invite composer with Email selected; Reissue opens it in its needs-reissue state; Resend on a pending or expired row works in place.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM. Maya Chen, owner of 2418 NE Larkspur Loop, has just sent an invitation to priya@example.com. She opens this screen to check it is really pending, and finds two older invitations that stopped working when the household's invite rules changed. Sam Ortega, a member, opens the same screen on his phone to see who lives there.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Let everyone in the household see who lives here, and let the people who manage the home fix invitations in one tap.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: (1) The role groups, each with its people. (2) The quieter Pending group underneath, where the two \"Needs reissue\" rows stand out by their glyph and their words. (3) The one primary action, \"Invite\", in the header. A member sees no Invite button; in its place is the line \"Maya Chen can invite people here.\"\n\nCONTENT: Use the FIXTURES. Deltas for this surface (list each on Notes):\n- Maya Chen (you) · Owner. Row: \"joined Thu 1 Oct 2026\". Person detail only: \"Address confirmed by postcard · Thu 8 Oct 2026\".\n- Sam Ortega · Member. Row: \"joined Sat 10 Oct 2026\". Person detail only: \"Joined by Maya Chen's invitation · Sat 10 Oct 2026\".\n- Lena Ortega · Guest. Row: \"access until Sun 1 Nov 2026\".\n- Pending, single-use link model: priya@example.com · \"Member · sent Mon 19 Oct · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · Resend. Invite link · \"Works once · Member · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · Turn off link.\n- Needs reissue: theo.park@example.com (\"Member · sent Mon 12 Oct\") and @rgarcia (\"Member · sent Tue 13 Oct\").\n- Expiring: noah.kim@example.com · \"Member · sent Tue 13 Oct · Expires tomorrow\".\n- Expired: ali.hassan@example.com · \"Member · sent Sun 11 Oct · Expired Sun 18 Oct\" · Resend. The expiry is words in text.secondary, with no red and no chip.\n- Declined: kai.brooks@example.com · StatusChip \"Declined · Thu 15 Oct\" · Remove.\n- Approval link model only: Invite link · \"Joiners wait for your OK · Member · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · Turn off link; Ana Ruiz, joined by link · \"Waiting for your OK\" · Approve / Remove.\n- Offline: FreshnessLine \"You're offline · as of 5:52 PM\".\n- Worst case (frame 18 only): 6 people — Maya Chen (Owner), Nora Patel (Admin), Sam Ortega, Ravi Shah, Elena Brooks (Members), Lena Ortega (Guest). 4 pending rows: margaret.oconnor-whitfield@example.com (38 characters; \"Member · sent Mon 19 Oct · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · Resend), theo.park@example.com and @rgarcia (Needs reissue), kai.brooks@example.com (Declined · Thu 15 Oct). Sam's member-view line in that household reads \"Maya Chen or Nora Patel can invite people here.\"\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION:\n- Header: title \"Who lives here\", the ScopeChip \"Your household\" beneath it, the primary \"Invite\", and a quiet secondary text action \"Visitor passes\". On web the tab label stays \"Members & Security\" as host chrome.\n- Role groups in this order, as overline labels: OWNER · ADMINS · MEMBERS · GUESTS. ADMINS, MEMBERS and GUESTS each carry a 44pt disclosure row: \"What can admins do?\", \"What can members do?\", \"What can guests do?\". Each expands in place into a GrantLimitList of verbs, not a permission matrix. OWNER carries \"What can owners do?\" as a proposed addition beyond MemberRow ⑦ (record it on Notes).\n- Under each label, one MemberRow per person: avatar, name, one caption (join date, or access-until for guests), overflow.\n- On every person row, including the viewer's own, draw no chip, badge, tick, caption or colour for how the person was verified. Verification appears in two places only: the person detail sheet (method and date), and a LockedActionRow on an action the viewer cannot use yet.\n- Pending group (owners and admins only), drawn last and quieter than the people, using InviteRow. Caption at its top: \"Only owners and admins see this.\"\n- A Needs reissue row: warning glyph, the text \"Needs reissue — your household's invite rules changed\" in text.primary, and an inline \"Reissue\".\n- An Expired row: the pending anatomy with its caption ending \"Expired Sun 18 Oct\" and an inline \"Resend\" (44pt). Record \"InviteRow expired variant\" on Notes as a proposed Foundations addition.\n- The two link models are alternatives, not a pair. Frames 1, 16, 17, 18, 19 and 21 draw the single-use model (the \"Works once\" link row). Frames 3, 4, 20 and 22 draw the approval model (the \"Joiners wait for your OK\" link row and Ana's \"Waiting for your OK\" row). Label each approval-model artboard, above the frame, \"approval variant, if links are not single-use\".\n- The roster is list-only; it has no chart. Missing data: a cold load over 1s shows WarmingSkeleton rows that keep the group structure; cached data shows FreshnessLine; a person with no join date shows only the role.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS:\n- A person row opens the person detail sheet with a visible \"Close\": name, role, join date and the verification line (method and date).\n- \"Confirm this person lives here\" appears only for a person who has not verified their address (they joined by invitation), in their detail and in their row overflow. For Maya viewing Sam, it opens the owner-attestation sheet in place of the detail (no stacked sheets). For anyone whose address is already confirmed, such as Maya, it is absent.\n- Row overflow on other people (owners and admins): Change role, Confirm this person lives here (only as above), Remove from Larkspur Loop. The viewer's own row holds only \"Leave Larkspur Loop\". Every overflow action is also a screen-reader custom action.\n- Change role opens a sheet titled \"Change Sam Ortega's role\": radio rows for Admin, Member and Guest, and two short columns, \"Member can\" and \"Admin can also\". When Guest is selected, an \"Access until\" row with a date control appears under the radio rows (platform date picker plus a typed alternative). Buttons \"Save role\" and \"Cancel\". On save, the sheet closes and \"Sam Ortega is now an admin\" is announced as a status message.\n- Remove and Leave use DestructiveConfirm.\n- Resend on a pending or expired row shows \"Sending…\" in place, then \"Sent again · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\". The row stays put. On an expired row, Resend issues a new 7-day expiry, and the row becomes a normal pending row.\n- Reissue opens the Invite composer in its needs-reissue state. After Done, this screen shows that row as a normal pending row: \"Sent again · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct · the old link no longer works\", highlighted once. Accessibility focus lands on that row.\n- Cancel invitation and Extend sit in the pending overflow. Extend appears only if the backend supports it (Notes); its result is \"Extended · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\". Cancel collapses the row to \"Cancelled invitation to priya@example.com · Undo\" (InlineUndo).\n- Turn off link collapses the link row to \"Link turned off · Undo\" (InlineUndo).\n- Approve moves Ana into MEMBERS and shows \"Ana Ruiz joined Larkspur Loop · Undo\" (InlineUndo). The \"Ana Ruiz joined\" notice to other members is sent only when Undo closes. Ana sees no household data until approved; only link joins need approval, and email and username invitations skip it.\n- Remove on a declined row uses InlineUndo. No InlineUndo has a timer.\n- \"Visitor passes\" opens the home's Share tab on web and the Share Center on iOS and Android, where visitor and service passes live. A household Guest is invited through Invite, by choosing Guest.\n- Motion: row insert and remove cross-fades of 300ms or less; the deep-link highlight fades once. Under Reduce Motion both are static.\n- Haptics: one light tick when Approve is confirmed, and nothing else on this screen.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED:\n- MemberRow: owner, admin, member, guest, you and empty variants. Draw the \"you\" variant without the ⑧ verification caption; method and date live only in the person detail sheet.\n- InviteRow: pending, expiring, needs reissue, declined, link active, awaiting approval, and the proposed expired variant; sending state; S3 offline reasons as published.\n- GrantLimitList: role disclosures; change-role columns.\n- LockedActionRow: names-who-can-act variant for members and legacy roles; verification variant in Sam's own detail.\n- ScopeChip (\"Your household\").\n- StatusChip: \"Declined · Thu 15 Oct\" and \"Waiting for your OK\", only on invitation rows, one per row.\n- DestructiveConfirm (Leave; Remove), InlineUndo, WarmingSkeleton (row skeleton), FreshnessLine, OfflineNotice, InlineErrorRow.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n- Reading order: title, scope chip, Invite, Visitor passes, each group label and its disclosure, the people, then Pending.\n- Each row is one element with a merged label, for example \"Sam Ortega, member, joined Saturday October 10 2026\" or \"Invitation to ali.hassan@example.com, member, expired Sunday 18 October. Resend.\" Row actions are custom actions.\n- Avatars are decorative.\n- Resend, Reissue, Approve, Remove, Undo and each overflow get 44pt / 48dp / 44px hit areas, even though they look like text.\n- Expiry, expired and reissue are stated in words, never by glyph or colour alone.\n- \"Sending\", \"Sent again\", \"Cancelled\", \"Link turned off\", \"Joined\", \"is now an admin\" and \"You're offline\" are polite status messages.\n- The Fix deep-link highlight moves accessibility focus to the first reissue row.\n- At AX5, captions wrap under names, group labels wrap, and the overflow stays reachable.\n\nCOPY:\n- Header \"Who lives here\" · ScopeChip \"Your household\" · button \"Invite\" · secondary \"Visitor passes\"\n- Member-view line \"Maya Chen can invite people here.\"\n- Pending caption \"Only owners and admins see this.\"\n- Disclosure rows \"What can owners do?\" · \"What can admins do?\" · \"What can members do?\" · \"What can guests do?\"\n- Members disclosure (exactly the shared GrantLimitList grants): \"Sees and edits the calendar\" · \"Sees bills and who paid\" · \"Sees who lives here\"\n- Guests disclosure: \"Same as Member until their access ends\"\n- Admins disclosure: \"Everything members can do\" · \"Invites people and resends invitations\" · \"Removes people and changes roles\" · \"Adds bills and marks them paid\"\n- Owners disclosure: \"Everything admins can do\" · \"Changes who can invite people here\"\n- Empty: \"Just you at Larkspur Loop\" · \"Invite someone\". In the empty state the header Invite is hidden; \"Invite someone\" is the single action.\n- Person detail: \"Close\" · \"Confirm this person lives here\"\n- Change role: \"Change Sam Ortega's role\" · \"Admin\" · \"Member\" · \"Guest\" · \"Member can\" · \"Admin can also\" · \"Access until\" · \"Save role\" / \"Cancel\" · status \"Sam Ortega is now an admin\"\n- Pending results: \"Sending…\" · \"Sent again · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · \"Cancelled invitation to priya@example.com · Undo\" · \"Link turned off · Undo\" · \"Extended · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · \"Ana Ruiz joined Larkspur Loop · Undo\"\n- LockedActionRow in Sam's own detail: \"Address verification needed to send neighbor messages · Verify address\"\n- Leave sheet: \"Leave Larkspur Loop?\" · \"You lose the household calendar, bills and tasks. Your saved places and private dates stay yours.\" · \"Leave Larkspur Loop\" / \"Stay\"\n- Remove sheet: \"Remove Sam Ortega from Larkspur Loop?\" · \"Sam loses the calendar, bills and tasks here. Bills Sam marked paid keep the note 'Sam (no longer here)'.\" · \"Remove Sam\" / \"Keep Sam\"\n- Sole owner, own row: \"You're the only owner. Make someone an admin and contact support to hand over ownership.\"\n- Access ended (revoked only): \"Your access to Larkspur Loop ended.\" · \"Your saved places and private dates are still yours.\" · \"Go to Your places\"\n- Legacy role without list access: \"Your role at Larkspur Loop doesn't include this list yet.\" · LockedActionRow \"Maya Chen can show you who lives here\"\n- Load error: \"We couldn't load who lives here. · Retry\"\n- Resend error: \"We couldn't resend to priya@example.com. · Retry\"\n- Offline: the Invite button shows the reason \"Inviting needs a connection.\" Pending rows use the published InviteRow S3 reasons (\"You're offline. You can resend when you're back.\" and the others). Person-row overflow uses the MemberRow S3 reason \"You're offline. You can change roles when you're back.\"\n\nEDGE CASES:\n- The 38-character email wraps to two lines and is never truncated before the @.\n- With 6 people and 4 pending rows, groups keep their labels and the page scrolls.\n- When an invitee accepts, their pending row is removed, and they appear in their role group for every member, with no status chip.\n- The sole owner's own row has no Leave; it shows the sole-owner line. Notes: product question on an owner-transfer control.\n- On Lena's end date her row leaves by itself; other members get the quiet row \"Lena's guest access ended\" (drawn in household notifications).\n- When someone joins, every member sees them; Pending stays owners-and-admins only.\n- Sam (member) sees no Pending group, no Invite, no role editing and no overflow on other people's rows. He sees Visitor passes only if his role allows Share; otherwise it is absent.\n- Revoked access gets the access-ended frame. A legacy role without list access gets the legacy frame: the household is still theirs, so it never says access ended.\n- Slow network: rows over 1s show skeletons; no full-page spinner.\n- Offline: the cached roster stays readable; actions are disabled with their reasons shown.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of \"Address-verified\" or \"Household member\" chips beside names, draw plain rows and put the method and date in the detail, because badging housemates reads as a ranking of the people you live with.\n- Instead of carrying over the green \"Household access\" chip that is being removed from iOS My Homes, draw nothing on roster rows, because that chip claims a verified status the member does not have.\n- Instead of an \"Add guest\" form that shows success, draw a secondary \"Visitor passes\" link that opens Share, because that page never sent anything and visitor passes already work there. A household Guest is chosen inside Invite.\n- Instead of a disabled Invite button for members, draw \"Maya Chen can invite people here.\", because a member can never invite, so name who can.\n- Instead of Resend on declined invitations, draw \"Declined · Thu 15 Oct\" with Remove only, so the sender is not prompted to nag. An expired invitation, which nobody answered, keeps Resend.\n- Instead of a red \"Expired\" chip, draw \"Expired Sun 18 Oct\" in the caption with Resend beside it, because the fix matters more than the alarm.\n- Instead of a per-person permission grid, draw coarse roles with a verb disclosure, because permission matrices lose non-expert members.\n- Instead of \"Your access ended\" for a legacy role, draw the reason and who can help, because that person still belongs to the household.\n\nDONE WHEN:\n- An invited member can list who lives here.\n- Maya can find a dead invitation (needs reissue or expired) and fix it in one tap per row, and afterwards she sees a pending row with \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct · Resend\".\n- An accepted invitation leaves Pending and the person appears in their role group.\n- No frame shows a verification chip or caption on a person, and no frame shows a control that does nothing.\n- The Members disclosure uses the same three grant strings the invitee reads.\n- Every frame reads correctly in greyscale.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f3-members-roster · ios · 01-owner-dense · light — Maya's view: header with scope chip, OWNER, MEMBERS, GUESTS, and Pending with theo.park@example.com and @rgarcia (Needs reissue · Reissue), priya@example.com (Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct · Resend) and the \"Works once\" link row.\n2. f3-members-roster · ios · 02-member-view · light — Sam's view: no Pending, no Invite, the names-who-can-act line.\n3. f3-members-roster · ios · 03-pending-states · light — labelled \"approval variant, if links are not single-use\": noah expiring, ali expired with Resend, kai declined, the \"Joiners wait for your OK\" link row, Ana waiting, priya's row mid \"Sending…\".\n4. f3-members-roster · ios · 04-after-reissue · light — labelled \"approval variant, if links are not single-use\": back from the composer, theo's row highlighted as \"Sent again … the old link no longer works\"; ali's row now \"Sent again · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\"; priya's row collapsed to the Cancelled Undo line; the link row collapsed to \"Link turned off · Undo\"; Ana's joined Undo line.\n5. f3-members-roster · ios · 05-person-detail-owner · light — Sam's detail as Maya sees it: method and date, Confirm this person lives here, Close.\n6. f3-members-roster · ios · 06-own-detail-locked · light — Sam's own detail with the verification LockedActionRow.\n7. f3-members-roster · ios · 07-change-role-sheet · light — Admin selected, the two capability columns, Save role / Cancel; inset below the sheet: the status \"Sam Ortega is now an admin\".\n8. f3-members-roster · ios · 08-leave-sheet · light — Sam leaving: what goes and what stays.\n9. f3-members-roster · ios · 09-remove-sheet · light — Maya removing Sam.\n10. f3-members-roster · ios · 10-empty-just-you · light — \"Just you at Larkspur Loop\" and Invite someone; header Invite hidden.\n11. f3-members-roster · ios · 11-loading · light — skeleton rows keeping the groups.\n12. f3-members-roster · ios · 12-error · light — load error row with Retry.\n13. f3-members-roster · ios · 13-offline · light — cached roster with FreshnessLine, Invite and row actions disabled with their reasons.\n14. f3-members-roster · ios · 14-access-ended · light — revoked access frame.\n15. f3-members-roster · ios · 15-legacy-no-list · light — legacy role: reason line and \"Maya Chen can show you who lives here\".\n16. f3-members-roster · android · 01-owner-dense · light — Material 3 version of frame 1.\n17. f3-members-roster · web-1440 · 01-owner-dense · light — the single Members & Security tab with frame 1's content, security content below.\n18. f3-members-roster · web-390 · 16-worst-case · light — Nora Patel, Ravi Shah, Elena Brooks and the others; 4 pending rows with the 38-character email wrapped.\n19. f3-members-roster · ios · 17-ax5 · light — frame 1 at AX5.\n20. f3-members-roster · android · 18-greyscale · light — frame 3 in greyscale, with the approval-variant label.\n21. f3-members-roster · ios · 01-owner-dense · dark — dark twin of frame 1.\n22. f3-members-roster · ios · 03-pending-states · dark — dark twin of frame 3, with the approval-variant label.\n23. f3-members-roster · web-1440 · 07-change-role-sheet · light — the change-role sheet as a centred 480-wide dialog with Guest selected and the \"Access until\" date row showing Sun 1 Nov 2026.\n24. f3-members-roster · ios · 99-Notes · light — every invented string (Nora Patel, Ravi Shah, Elena Brooks, margaret.oconnor-whitfield, noah, ali, kai, Ana, the approval link caption, all result lines, change-role strings, legacy and sole-owner copy); noah.kim replaces the earlier jordan.lee so no pending invitee shares a name with PLACE B's Jordan Lee; proposed Foundations additions: InviteRow expired variant, the owner disclosure (added beyond MemberRow ⑦), and the tasks grant (\"Proposed addition to the shared GrantLimitList set: 'Sees and edits tasks'. Add it to the composer caption, review and decision screen together, or not at all.\"); the \"you\" MemberRow is drawn without ⑧ here; the two link models (single-use vs approval is a backend choice; approval frames are labelled); Add guest page deleted, visitor passes live in Share; the recipient banner no longer lands here; product questions: Extend, owner transfer, owner-only powers, and whether admins as well as owners may use \"Confirm this person lives here\"; omitted states (Extend result drawn only as a string).\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 3: 13-18, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 4: 19-24.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Added an expired pending-invitation row (ali.hassan@example.com, 'Expired Sun 18 Oct', Resend issuing a new 7-day expiry) per flow-04 failure branch and research; drawn in frames 3 and 4; InviteRow expired variant recorded on Notes as a proposed addition (review majors).",
          "Artboard 1 (and dark twin 21) now show the two Needs reissue rows alongside priya and the link row so the hero frame shows the moment of truth (review major).",
          "Removed 'Sees and edits tasks' from the Members disclosure so it matches the three GrantLimitList contract strings; the tasks grant is recorded on Notes as a proposed shared addition (review major, doc confirms members have tasks.view/edit).",
          "Replaced the self-contradicting worst-case fixture with Nora Patel, Ravi Shah, Elena Brooks and four specified pending rows; member-view line 'Maya Chen or Nora Patel can invite people here.'; renamed jordan.lee to noah.kim to avoid clashing with PLACE B's Jordan Lee (review major).",
          "Added missing strings: change-role title, Save role / Cancel, Guest 'Access until' date row, 'Sam Ortega is now an admin', person detail 'Close', 'Link turned off · Undo', 'Extended · …' (review major + minor).",
          "Approval-model frames (3, 4, 20, 22) are explicitly labelled 'approval variant, if links are not single-use'; added the approval-model link row (derive proposal: active link is a pending row with Turn off link) (review minor).",
          "'Confirm this person lives here' now appears only for people who have not verified their address; Notes asks whether admins may confirm (review minor).",
          "Added edge case: an accepted invitation leaves Pending and the person appears in their role group, per flow-04 step 18 (review minor).",
          "Group labels changed to OWNER · ADMINS · MEMBERS · GUESTS per the published MemberRow board; owner disclosure kept as a proposed addition on Notes (review minor).",
          "MemberRow 'you' variant drawn without the ⑧ caption, stated explicitly (review minor).",
          "Offline copy aligned: Invite button reason plus published InviteRow S3 and MemberRow S3 reasons (review minor).",
          "Empty state: header Invite hidden so 'Invite someone' is the single action (review minor).",
          "Added the Fix notification row as an entry point and what this screen hands to the composer (flows-spec flow-12)."
        ]
