      {
        "id": "f3b-invitation-decision",
        "name": "Invitation decision (what you get now vs what needs verification)",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 25,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Invitation decision · f3b-invitation-decision\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Invitation decision\". This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed. The changes: (1) replace the ownership paragraph with a GrantLimitList of two lists, \"What you get now\" and \"What needs address verification\"; (2) before acceptance, show the household as a count only, and when signed out, show the home label and city instead of the street line; (3) on phones, pin the primary and Decline in a bottom bar; (4) when signed out, the primary reads \"Create account to accept\"; (5) give the accepted state two next steps; (6) give Decline an InlineUndo; (7) give each dead-invitation case its own frame with one next step.\n\nATTACH: the current invitation decision screen, signed in, at web 1440 and web 390; the current signed-out (public) invitation screen at web 390; the current iOS and Android invitation decision screens; the current accepted state on web (it shows \"Check current Home access\" and \"Open Home\"); the Foundations board.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: web 1440x900 (a centred content column up to 720px wide, the two lists side by side, buttons inline under the footnote); web 390x844; iOS 393x852 (a full-screen view with Close in the navigation bar); Android 412x915 (a top app bar with Up). Up on Android and Close on iOS go to the Place tab (Your places), including after a deep-link arrival. The screen sits outside the tab bar: draw no tab bar on any frame.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: no tab of its own. Entries: the deep link /invite/<token> from the invitation email, a text message, a shared link or a QR code; \"Review\" on the LandingBannerSlot on the Place tab (\"Maya Chen invited you to Larkspur Loop · Review\"); manual code entry on web at /app/homes/invite; the new-invitation push, which always opens this invitation, never a dashboard. The previous step hands over only the token. Signed out, the primary \"Create account to accept\" opens account creation on the web, with no app install and the token kept; a person who already has an account uses \"Already have an account? Sign in\". Either way she returns to this offer, signed in, and taps \"Accept\" here. Accept hands off to \"Open Home\" (the Place tab showing Larkspur Loop). Today then shows its own one-time notice that it now uses Larkspur Loop; that notice belongs to the Today prompt. \"Start address verification\" opens the \"Verify this address\" sheet with the invitation reason. The inviter's roster learns the answer (see Decline below).\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Priya Raman is moving into the spare room at HOME A. Maya Chen invited her as a Member an hour ago; the invitation went to priya@example.com and expires Mon 26 Oct. It is Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM. Priya made an account, priya@example.com, on her laptop yesterday. She opens the email on her Android phone in a mobile browser where she is signed out, and she has not installed the app. She taps \"Already have an account? Sign in\", signs in, and comes back to the offer.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Let someone accept household access knowing exactly what it gives and what it does not, then land them somewhere useful.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: first, who invited her and to where (\"Maya Chen invited you to Larkspur Loop\"); second, the \"What you get now\" list; third, the \"What needs address verification\" list. The one primary action is \"Accept\" (signed out: \"Create account to accept\"), visible without scrolling on every phone frame because it sits in the pinned bottom bar.\n\nCONTENT (fixture deltas only):\n- Manifest, as plain lines. Signed out: Home \"Larkspur Loop · Vancouver, WA\". Signed in: Home \"2418 NE Larkspur Loop, Vancouver, WA 98684\". Then From \"Maya Chen\" · Role \"Member\" · Access \"Starts when you accept · no end date\" · \"Expires Mon 26 Oct (in 7 days)\" · household line \"Maya Chen and 1 other live here\" (a count only, never names, before acceptance).\n- Lead line: \"This invitation gives you household access.\"\n- What you get now: \"Sees and edits the calendar\" · \"Sees bills and who paid\" · \"Sees who lives here\". These are exactly the rows Maya reviewed in the invite composer, from one shared string set.\n- What needs address verification: \"Message your neighbors\" · \"Get a residency letter\" · \"Show your Residency Pass\" · \"Share what you pay in rent (Real Rent)\" · \"Earn a Block Founder rank\". Under it, a disclosure \"See everything that needs it\" opens the shared caption: \"Also: residency claims, watching this home's records, postcard invites, fridge cards, letters to neighbors from Mail, the Founding Neighbor tier, and the address line on your profile.\"\n- Footnote, exact: \"This invitation does not grant ownership.\"\n- Worst case (frame 21): the street \"13410 NE Hazel Dell Avenue, Apartment 2207\" (42 characters), the inviter \"Maria-Fernanda Castellanos-Whitaker\", the role Guest with \"Access until Sun 1 Nov (in 13 days)\", and \"Maria-Fernanda Castellanos-Whitaker and 7 others live here\".\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION: order from top: title \"Maya Chen invited you to Larkspur Loop\", manifest, lead line, the two lists, footnote, then buttons. Web 1440: lists side by side, grant list on the left, buttons inline under the footnote. Phones (web-390, iOS, Android): lists stacked, grant list first; the primary and Decline sit side by side, equal width, in a pinned bottom bar on surface.base with a top hairline; the page reserves scroll padding equal to the bar's height. On the signed-out frame the caption and the sign-in link sit inside the bar, directly above the buttons, and the primary reads \"Create account to accept\". At AX5 the bar unpins, the buttons stack full width and follow the footnote. Both lists follow GrantLimitList exactly: 44pt rows, body type in text.primary, 16pt glyph (success-coloured tick for grants, lock in text.secondary for limits), both on surface.base. The limits get no tint, border, banner or alert icon. Each list has a heading, so words carry the meaning, not the glyph. Accepted state: both lists stay; the caption \"Verify your address to unlock these\" sits directly above the secondary button, and the caption \"Postcards take 5–10 days. Other ways can be faster.\" sits directly under it.\nDegradation: no expiry gives \"No expiry\". Unknown role gives the default Member lists plus the caption \"Standard member access\". Unknown city shows the label or street only. Unknown inviter gives \"Someone invited you to Larkspur Loop\". Unknown count drops the household line with no blank.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS: the primary (\"Accept\", or \"Create account to accept\" when signed out) is filled primary.700. \"Decline\" is an outlined button of equal width, with no confirm step. Declining shows the declined state using InlineUndo (declined-ask variant): the status line with a 44pt \"Undo\" beside it. Undo stays until Priya leaves the screen, with no countdown, and returns to the offer. Maya's notice is held and sent only after Priya leaves the declined screen. While accepting, Accept shows an inline spinner and \"Joining…\" is announced as a status; no full-page spinner. The accepted state cross-fades in within 300ms; under Reduce Motion it appears with no movement. One light haptic tick on the accepted state only. The disclosure expands in place. The verify sheet never opens by itself.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: GrantLimitList (invitation decision variant; accepted variant with its caption); MemberRow (collapsed roster line: count only before acceptance, names after); ScopeChip (\"Your household\", beside the home line in the accepted state only); InlineUndo (declined-ask variant: \"Declined. Maya Chen will see that this invitation was declined. · Undo\"; Maya's notice is held until Priya leaves the screen); WarmingSkeleton (row skeleton for manifest and lists); InlineErrorRow; OfflineNotice; LandingBannerSlot (the entry, on the Notes artboard only); PushCopy (the proposed new-invitation push, on the Notes artboard only). LockedActionRow is not used here: the limits are GrantLimitList lock rows, not locked controls.\n\nACCESSIBILITY: reading order: title, manifest, lead line, grant heading and rows, limit heading and rows, disclosure, footnote, caption and sign-in link, primary, Decline. Glyphs are decorative. Each list is a group named by its heading, e.g. \"What needs address verification, 5 items\". Buttons are at least 44pt iOS, 48dp Android with 8dp between, 44px web. Both lists are text.primary on base; never text.muted or text.secondary on sunken. \"Joining…\", \"You're in.\" and \"Declined.\" are announced without moving focus; Undo is focusable. At AX5 lists wrap, the bar unpins, and buttons stack.\n\nCOPY:\n- Signed out: caption \"You'll make an account next. You don't need the app.\" · primary \"Create account to accept\" (opens account creation on the web, token kept) · \"Decline\" · link \"Already have an account? Sign in\" (Priya's path; token kept).\n- Returned after sign-in: status line \"Signed in as priya@example.com\" · primary \"Accept\" · \"Decline\".\n- Accepted: title \"You're in.\"; household line \"Maya Chen, Sam Ortega and you live here\"; primary \"Open Home\"; caption \"Verify your address to unlock these\"; secondary \"Start address verification\"; caption \"Postcards take 5–10 days. Other ways can be faster.\"\n- Declined: \"Declined. Maya Chen will see that this invitation was declined.\" · \"Undo\" · button \"Go to Place\" (signed out: \"Look up your address\").\n- Expired: \"This invitation expired Mon 26 Oct. Ask Maya Chen to send a new one.\" · \"Go to Place\".\n- Revoked: \"Maya Chen cancelled this invitation. If that's a mistake, ask Maya to send a new one.\" · \"Go to Place\".\n- Already used: \"This invitation has already been used. If that wasn't you, tell Maya Chen.\" · \"Go to Place\".\n- Policy changed: \"This home changed who can invite people. We've told Maya Chen.\" · \"Go to Place\".\n- Already a member: \"You're already part of Larkspur Loop.\" · \"Open Home\".\n- Account mismatch: \"You're signed in as priya.raman@example.com. This invitation went to priya@example.com.\" · \"Accept as priya.raman@example.com\" · \"Switch account\".\n- Joined by link: \"Waiting for Maya's OK. You'll see the household once Maya approves.\" · \"Go to Place\".\n- Error: \"We couldn't load this invitation. Check your connection, then try again.\" · \"Retry\".\n- Offline: \"You're offline. Your invitation is saved. You can accept when you're back online.\" Accept and Decline stay visible and disabled, each with that reason.\n\"Go to Place\" opens the Place tab at Your places, or its empty state if the person has no place.\n\nEDGE CASES: the longest name and street wrap, never truncate. Guest adds the grant caption \"Same as Member until Sun 1 Nov (in 13 days)\". A large household reads \"… and 7 others live here\". Slow network: skeleton only after 1s. Several invitations: the list lives on Your places, not here. Opened after expiry (Tue 27 Oct): the expired frame. An already address-verified person accepting sees no verification button (assumption, see Notes). Account mismatch is a second account, not Priya's usual one.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of a paragraph about ownership, draw two short lists and the one-line footnote, because people skip the paragraph at the one moment consent matters.\n- Instead of product names as rows (\"Real Rent\"), draw verb rows, because a newcomer cannot tell what the names mean.\n- Instead of grey text on a sunken panel for the limits, draw the limit rows in text.primary on base, exactly like the grant rows, because these rows must be read (text.muted on sunken is 2.31:1).\n- Instead of \"Verify this address\" as the primary action after accepting, draw \"Open Home\" as primary and verification as a visible secondary, because people accepted in order to use household tools.\n- Instead of housemates' names or the house number on the signed-out page, draw \"Larkspur Loop · Vancouver, WA\" and \"Maya Chen and 1 other live here\", because a forwarded link must not reveal who lives where.\n- Instead of \"Accept\" on the signed-out page, draw \"Create account to accept\", because tapping it does not accept yet and she must tap Accept again after registering.\n- Instead of Accept scrolled below the lists on a phone, draw a pinned bottom bar, because the one action must be visible in five seconds.\n- Instead of a final Decline, draw Decline with an InlineUndo that lasts until she leaves, because a mis-tap notifies Maya.\n\nDONE WHEN: a first-time reader can say what she can do after joining and what still needs address verification, without opening anything. The grant rows match Maya's composer word for word. Nothing is styled as a warning. The primary is visible without scrolling on every phone frame, and its label says what it really does. The signed-out page shows no house number and no housemate names. Accepting lands on Larkspur Loop, not an empty Place tab. The verify sheet opens only on tap. Decline can be undone until she leaves, and Maya hears only after. Every dead invitation names the inviter and gives one next step. Signed-out acceptance works on mobile web.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f3b-invitation-decision · web-390 · 01-offer-signed-out · light — the dense default: label and city only, stacked lists, pinned bar with caption, sign-in link, \"Create account to accept\" and Decline.\n2. f3b-invitation-decision · ios · 02-offer · light — signed in, full street, stacked lists, pinned bar with Accept, Close in the navigation bar.\n3. f3b-invitation-decision · web-1440 · 03-offer · light — lists side by side, buttons inline under the footnote.\n4. f3b-invitation-decision · android · 04-offer · light — Material 3 top app bar with Up, stacked lists, pinned bar.\n5. f3b-invitation-decision · ios · 05-accepting · light — inline spinner and \"Joining…\".\n6. f3b-invitation-decision · ios · 06-accepted · light — \"You're in.\", named household, ScopeChip, Open Home, captions and the \"Start address verification\" secondary.\n7. f3b-invitation-decision · web-390 · 07-returned-after-sign-in · light — the first frame whose primary is \"Accept\" on mobile web: \"Signed in as priya@example.com\", full street.\n8. f3b-invitation-decision · web-390 · 08-accepted · light — Priya's accepted state on mobile web.\n9. f3b-invitation-decision · android · 09-accepted · light — the accepted state on Android.\n10. f3b-invitation-decision · web-390 · 10-declined-with-undo · light — InlineUndo with the sender-visibility sentence and Undo, then Go to Place.\n11. f3b-invitation-decision · web-1440 · 11-expired · light — expired Mon 26 Oct, ask Maya.\n12. f3b-invitation-decision · web-1440 · 12-revoked · light — Maya cancelled it.\n13. f3b-invitation-decision · web-1440 · 13-already-used · light — used by someone else.\n14. f3b-invitation-decision · web-1440 · 14-policy-changed · light — \"We've told Maya Chen.\"\n15. f3b-invitation-decision · web-1440 · 15-already-a-member · light — Open Home.\n16. f3b-invitation-decision · web-390 · 16-account-mismatch · light — two accounts, two choices.\n17. f3b-invitation-decision · web-390 · 17-waiting-for-approval · light — joined by link, waiting for Maya's OK.\n18. f3b-invitation-decision · web-1440 · 18-loading · light — skeleton in final slots.\n19. f3b-invitation-decision · web-1440 · 19-error · light — InlineErrorRow with Retry.\n20. f3b-invitation-decision · ios · 20-offline · light — cached offer, disabled buttons with reasons.\n21. f3b-invitation-decision · ios · 21-offer-worst-case-ax5 · light — AX5 text with the worst-case data, wrapped rows, bar unpinned, stacked buttons.\n22. f3b-invitation-decision · web-390 · 22-offer-greyscale · light — frame 1 in greyscale; grant and limit still distinct by glyph and heading.\n23. f3b-invitation-decision · web-390 · 23-offer-signed-out · dark — the dark twin of frame 1.\n24. f3b-invitation-decision · ios · 24-accepted · dark — the dark twin of frame 6.\n25. f3b-invitation-decision · web-1440 · 25-notes · light — Notes: the LandingBannerSlot entry; the proposed new-invitation push (invented, copy shared with the invite banner prompt): title \"Maya Chen invited you\" (21 characters), body \"Join Larkspur Loop on Pantopus\", hidden-preview \"Household invitation\", group Account & security, interruption level Time Sensitive on iOS / HIGH on Android per that group, landing this screen; Up and Close go to Your places; the doc's second sentence (\"To send neighbor messages or get a residency letter, verify the address yourself.\") is replaced by the two lists, and the footnote is kept as the doc's F3 section asks although F3b says to replace it; \"5–10 days\" deliberately replaces \"about a week\" to match the verify sheet; the accepted secondary is \"Start address verification\" with the caption \"Postcards take 5–10 days. Other ways can be faster.\", replacing the flow's \"Start address verification — postcards take 5–10 days\" because a member can also ask Maya (same day) or send a document (about 1 day); the signed-out primary is \"Create account to accept\" because it does not accept yet; the signed-out page shows label and city only, a change from the current public page; Maya is told of a decline only after Priya leaves (InlineUndo); \"Go to Place\" replaces the research string \"Back to your place\", because a declined invitee may have no place of their own; deliberately omitted from the grant list: tasks (members already have tasks.view/tasks.edit) and the pickup day, because the shared GrantLimitList string set has three rows — product decision: add them to the shared set so the composer and this screen both show them; assumption: accepting does not downgrade an existing address verification (the doc's writer sets household on accept); every invented string (priya.raman@example.com, Maria-Fernanda Castellanos-Whitaker, 13410 NE Hazel Dell Avenue, Apartment 2207, the \"Also:\" line, \"Look up your address\", \"Go to Place\", \"Create account to accept\", \"Access until Sun 1 Nov (in 13 days)\", \"Postcards take 5–10 days. Other ways can be faster.\", \"Signed in as priya@example.com\", the push strings); omitted states.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: 1-6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 3: 13-18, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 4: 19-24, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 5: 25.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Signed-out primary renamed 'Create account to accept' (opens web account creation, token kept); frame 1, FIRST FIVE SECONDS, LAYOUT and COPY updated; frame 7 is the first mobile-web frame whose primary is 'Accept' (major, flows-spec flow-04 step 7)",
          "Decline now uses the contract's InlineUndo (declined-ask variant) by name, with Maya's notice held until Priya leaves (major, component-contract InlineUndo)",
          "Added 'LockedActionRow is not used here' to FOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED (minor, contract)",
          "Accepted secondary shortened to 'Start address verification' with caption 'Postcards take 5–10 days. Other ways can be faster.'; change recorded on Notes (minor)",
          "Relative dates unified to 'Expires Mon 26 Oct (in 7 days)' / 'Access until Sun 1 Nov (in 13 days)', including the Guest caption (minor, house style)",
          "Up and iOS Close go to Your places, including deep-link arrivals (minor)",
          "Notes: push interruption level Time Sensitive / HIGH per Account & security (minor, brief §3)",
          "Notes: tasks and pickup day deliberately omitted from the grant list, with the product decision (minor, design doc §3)",
          "Notes: 'Go to Place' replaces 'Back to your place' and why (minor, per-surface changes)",
          "Notes: assumption that accepting does not downgrade an existing address verification (minor, design doc F3b)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f3b-verify-address-sheet",
        "name": "Verify this address (one sheet, many callers)",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": true,
        "frameCount": 28,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Verify this address · f3b-verify-address-sheet\n\nTYPE: NEW. One sheet with many callers; the caller sets its reason. Web has a \"What this unlocks\" prompt but no host that opens it; iOS and Android have only an inline verify banner. Design the sheet once and draw it identically on all three platforms.\n\nATTACH: the current web verify prompt (its \"What this unlocks\" list and method picker) as a starting point; the current Place dashboard verify banner on iOS and Android (a caller); the Foundations board.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852, a sheet with medium and large detents; Android 412x915, a Material 3 bottom sheet; web 1440x900, a centred modal 560px wide; web 390x844, a full-height sheet. Opening rule for every phone frame: at default text size, every method row must be visible on open. The unlock list shows two rows collapsed; with two or fewer methods the iOS sheet opens at medium, with more than two it opens at large. Every variant has a visible \"Close\" in the header, closes with Back or Escape, returns focus to the control that opened it, and never opens on top of another sheet.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: no tab and no route; it opens over its caller. Callers: \"Verify address\" on any LockedActionRow (Place: residency letter, Residency Pass, residency claims, fridge cards, Real Rent, watching this home's records; Nearby: neighbor messages, Block Founder rank, postcard invites, the Founding Neighbor tier; Mail: letters to neighbors; the address line on the profile); \"Enter code\" and \"See request\" on a pending LockedActionRow, which open this sheet in its postcard-pending or request-sent state; \"Start address verification\" on the accepted invitation; the Place dashboard verify banner; the place file's Proof row; the members roster's capability caption. Each caller passes a reason; the body stays the same. Choosing \"Ask Maya Chen to confirm\" sends Maya a push and an in-app row, which open \"Confirm this person lives here\" on her phone. Her answer returns to this sheet (confirmed, didn't confirm) and to the caller's LockedActionRow. Once confirmed, Done returns focus to the caller, whose control is now live.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Sam Ortega joined HOME A on Sat 10 Oct through Maya Chen's invitation: a household member, not yet address-verified. On Mon 19 Oct at 6:10 PM he taps \"Message a neighbor\" on Nearby, sees the LockedActionRow, and taps \"Verify address\". The postcard frames show the other path: Sam chose the postcard on Wed 14 Oct and is waiting for it. Maya's own address was confirmed by postcard, so she can confirm Sam.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Explain what address verification adds, then start one method, under a header that says why the sheet opened.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: first, the reason (\"To send neighbor messages, we need to confirm you live here.\"); second, the two unlocks people want most; third, the method rows with their time chips. No single primary button: each method row is the action, and no row is recommended.\n\nCONTENT (fixture deltas only):\n- Title \"Verify this address\". Address \"2418 NE Larkspur Loop, Vancouver, WA 98684\" with ScopeChip \"Your household\".\n- Reasons, one per caller, pattern \"To <action>, we need to confirm you live here.\": \"To send neighbor messages, we need to confirm you live here.\" · \"To get a residency letter, we need to confirm you live here.\" · after accepting an invitation (Priya Raman): \"You've joined Larkspur Loop. Confirming your address unlocks a few more things.\" · banner, Proof row and roster: \"Confirming you live here unlocks a few more things.\" The full per-caller list goes on Notes.\n- Unlock list: \"Message your neighbors\" · \"Get a residency letter\", then \"and 3 more\" expanding to \"Show your Residency Pass\" · \"Share what you pay in rent (Real Rent)\" · \"Earn a Block Founder rank\", plus the shared caption \"Also: residency claims, watching this home's records, postcard invites, fridge cards, letters to neighbors from Mail, the Founding Neighbor tier, and the address line on your profile.\"\n- Methods, in this fixed order (name · chip · requirement):\n  \"Postcard code\" · \"5–10 days\" · \"We mail a code to 2418 NE Larkspur Loop. Enter it when it arrives.\"\n  \"Document\" · \"About 1 day\" · \"A lease or utility bill from the last 90 days, in your name.\"\n  \"Landlord confirmation\" · \"1–3 days\" · \"We email the landlord on the lease. Needs a landlord contact on file.\"\n  \"Ask Maya Chen to confirm\" · \"Usually same day\" · \"Maya claimed this address, so Maya can confirm you live here. Maya will see your request.\"\n- Frame 1: Landlord confirmation shows \"No landlord contact is on file for Larkspur Loop.\" with a \"Not available\" chip in the time-chip column.\n- Worst case: the reason plus all unlocks expanded, four methods, one unavailable method with a two-line reason, iOS large detent.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION: order: header (title, Close, reason, address, ScopeChip), unlock list, hairline, method rows. Each method row is 64pt or taller and one target: 24pt leading glyph, method name (body, text.primary), requirement (bodySmall, text.secondary), and a right-aligned time chip. Time chip: StatusChip unchanged (surface.sunken fill, text.strong, 9.37:1). The chips align in one column, so \"how fast\" reads before any row is read in full. No server time: the chip reads \"Varies\", never dropped. An unavailable method stays in its place, its reason replacing the requirement (text.secondary, never text.muted), and the \"Not available\" chip replaces the time chip in the same column, so every row carries exactly one chip. The Ask row is always last.\nIn-flight rule, the same on every frame: while a postcard is on its way or a document is under review, the sheet shows only that pending block and the other method rows are not shown, because the check is already running and a second start would be refused. While the request to Maya is waiting, the other methods stay listed under \"Or verify another way\", because Maya may never answer; only the Ask row cannot be restarted.\nDegradation: no method available gives one line, \"No verification method is available for this address yet.\", plus the reason if confirming was turned off, and Close only; never a dead link.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS: tapping Postcard shows an inline confirm on the same sheet (\"We'll mail a code to 2418 NE Larkspur Loop\" · \"Send postcard\" · text button \"Choose another way\", 44pt, which returns to the method list), then the pending state. Tapping Document shows the accepted types (\"Accepted: a lease, rental agreement or utility bill from the last 90 days, with your name and this address. A Clark Public Utilities bill works.\"), then \"Choose a document\"; after upload, the under-review state. Tapping Ask sends the request; the row becomes the request-sent state in place, with \"Cancel request\" (text button, 44pt) available while Maya hasn't answered. The code field is one input with one-time-code autofill; paste is allowed. A correct code, an approved document, or Maya confirming while the sheet is open all replace the body with the confirmed state. The sheet grows to large when content needs it; Close, the grabber and scrolling all reach it, so drag is optional. Transitions are cross-fades of 300ms or less, static under Reduce Motion. One light haptic tick when a request or postcard is confirmed as sent, and one on the confirmed state.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: GrantLimitList (verify sheet unlock list: two rows plus \"and 3 more\"); StatusChip (the time chip and \"Not available\", unchanged, one per row); ScopeChip; LockedActionRow (the caller frame); WarmingSkeleton (row skeleton); InlineErrorRow; OfflineNotice.\n\nACCESSIBILITY: reading order: title, reason, address, scope, unlocks, methods top to bottom. Each method row reads as one element: \"Postcard code, 5 to 10 days, we mail a code to your address, button\". An unavailable row reads its reason and is announced as dimmed. The sheet traps focus; unique title \"Verify this address\". \"Request sent\", \"Postcard on its way\" and \"Your address is confirmed\" are announced politely. Targets at least 44pt, 48dp, 44px. At AX5 the chip moves under the method name and the sheet scrolls with padding under the last row.\n\nCOPY:\n- Postcard confirm: \"We'll mail a code to 2418 NE Larkspur Loop\" · \"Send postcard\" · \"Choose another way\".\n- Request sent: \"We asked Maya. You'll see Maya's answer here.\" · \"Asked today at 6:10 PM\" · \"Cancel request\" · heading \"Or verify another way\", then the other methods.\n- Maya hasn't answered (after Mon 26 Oct): \"Maya hasn't answered yet. You can verify another way.\" The other methods come first; the Ask row sits last with \"Asked Mon 19 Oct\".\n- Maya didn't confirm: \"Maya didn't confirm. You can still verify by postcard or with a document.\"\n- Confirmed: \"Your address is confirmed.\" · \"Address confirmed by Maya Chen · Mon 19 Oct 2026\" (or \"by postcard\", or \"by document\", with that day's date) · when Maya answered while the sheet was open, the line \"Maya confirmed you live at Larkspur Loop\" sits above · \"You can now send neighbor messages.\" (from the caller's reason) · \"Done\", which returns focus to the caller, whose control is now live. Never a bare \"Verified\".\n- Access ended: \"Your access to Larkspur Loop ended.\" · Close only.\n- Postcard pending: heading \"Your postcard is on its way.\" · \"Mailed Wed 14 Oct · expected by Sat 24 Oct (in 5 days) · code works until Fri 13 Nov (in 25 days)\" · field label \"Code from your postcard\" · \"Check code\" · \"Didn't arrive by Sat 24 Oct? Send a new code\", disabled, caption \"Available after Sat 24 Oct (in 5 days). Your first code will stop working.\" No second Start and no other method rows.\n- Wrong code: \"That code doesn't match. Check the postcard and try again.\"\n- Document under review: \"We're reviewing your document · answer by Tue 20 Oct (tomorrow)\". No other method rows.\n- Document rejected: \"We couldn't use your document: the name on it doesn't match your account.\" · \"Upload a different document\"; the other method rows return below.\n- Unavailable for this address type: \"Not available for this address: postcards can't be delivered here.\"\n- Unavailable to a non-owner: \"Not available for an address someone else has claimed.\"\n- Confirming turned off: \"Maya has turned off confirming housemates for Larkspur Loop. Ask Maya about it.\"\n- Error: \"We couldn't load the ways to verify. Try again.\" · \"Retry\".\n- Offline: \"You're offline. You can start verifying when you're back online.\" Rows stay visible and disabled, each with that reason.\n\nEDGE CASES: longest reason and street: the header wraps to three lines at most, then the sheet scrolls. No lease on file makes Landlord unavailable with its own reason. Slow network: row skeletons after 1s. Maya offline: the request still sends and waits. An already address-verified person never sees this sheet; the caller's control is live and the LockedActionRow is absent. An owner verifying their own claim sees no Ask row. The Ask row appears only when the owner is address-verified. A person with only a saved place never reaches this sheet; the caller says \"Claim this address first\". If Postcard and Document do not accept a non-owner on a claimed home, both show the non-owner reason and Ask is the only path (frame 12).\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of two sheets (after joining, and after a blocked tap), draw one sheet whose header changes with the reason, because the body must stay identical and the header honest.\n- Instead of a progress bar, step counter or percentage, draw method rows with time chips, because nothing here should read as \"40% verified\".\n- Instead of a highlighted \"Recommended\" method, draw equal rows, because the best method depends on the person.\n- Instead of opening at medium with the Ask row below the fold, open with every method row visible, because Sam's quickest finishable path must be seen.\n- Instead of hiding a method that doesn't apply, draw it with its reason and a single \"Not available\" chip, because unexplained absences read as broken.\n- Instead of \"5–7 days\", draw \"5–10 days\" and a late path that unlocks after the window, because postcards can be late.\n- Instead of info-blue text on an info tint (3.84:1), draw the neutral StatusChip, because the time must be read at caption size.\n- Instead of an endless \"pending\" after asking Maya, or a sheet that just closes on success, draw request sent, didn't confirm, hasn't answered and confirmed, each saying what happens next.\n\nDONE WHEN: Sam, a non-owner, sees on open, without scrolling, at least one method he can finish, with an honest time. The header names why the sheet opened. After asking, he sees a waiting state he can cancel. His pending state shows the mailed date, the window, the expiry and a late path locked until Sat 24 Oct. A rejected document says why. Success names the method and date and hands him back to a live control. No frame shows a percentage or a recommended method. No frame shows a dead link.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f3b-verify-address-sheet · ios · 01-non-owner-ask-offered · light — the dense default at large detent: neighbor-message reason, two unlocks, all four methods visible, Landlord not available (no contact on file), Ask Maya last.\n2. f3b-verify-address-sheet · ios · 02-picker-all-methods · light — four available methods, unlock list expanded with the Also caption.\n3. f3b-verify-address-sheet · ios · 03-postcard-confirm · light — the inline \"Send postcard\" confirm with \"Choose another way\".\n4. f3b-verify-address-sheet · ios · 04-request-sent · light — \"We asked Maya\", Cancel request, the other methods below.\n5. f3b-verify-address-sheet · ios · 05-owner-didnt-confirm · light — postcard and document offered.\n6. f3b-verify-address-sheet · ios · 06-owner-hasnt-answered · light — other methods first, Ask last with its date.\n7. f3b-verify-address-sheet · ios · 07-postcard-pending · light — dates with relative counts, code field, locked late path, no other method rows.\n8. f3b-verify-address-sheet · ios · 08-confirmed · light — Maya confirmed while the sheet was open: \"Your address is confirmed.\", \"Address confirmed by Maya Chen · Mon 19 Oct 2026\", the unlocked action, Done.\n9. f3b-verify-address-sheet · ios · 09-document-under-review · light — reviewing, answer by Tue 20 Oct, no other method rows.\n10. f3b-verify-address-sheet · ios · 10-document-rejected · light — the specific reason, a retry, the other methods below.\n11. f3b-verify-address-sheet · ios · 11-unavailable-address-type · light — Postcard not available here.\n12. f3b-verify-address-sheet · ios · 12-ask-only-path · light — Postcard and Document not available to a non-owner; Ask is the only path.\n13. f3b-verify-address-sheet · ios · 13-no-method-available · light — the single line, the confirming-turned-off reason, Close only.\n14. f3b-verify-address-sheet · ios · 14-access-ended · light — \"Your access to Larkspur Loop ended.\"\n15. f3b-verify-address-sheet · ios · 15-already-verified-caller · light — the Nearby caller with the control live and no row; label \"This sheet never opens in this state\".\n16. f3b-verify-address-sheet · ios · 16-loading · light — header plus row skeletons.\n17. f3b-verify-address-sheet · ios · 17-error · light — InlineErrorRow with Retry.\n18. f3b-verify-address-sheet · ios · 18-offline · light — rows disabled with reasons.\n19. f3b-verify-address-sheet · android · 19-non-owner-ask-offered · light — the Android twin of frame 1.\n20. f3b-verify-address-sheet · android · 20-postcard-pending · light — the Android twin of frame 7.\n21. f3b-verify-address-sheet · web-1440 · 21-picker-after-joining · light — Priya Raman just accepted: centred modal, invitation reason.\n22. f3b-verify-address-sheet · web-1440 · 22-postcard-pending · light — pending state in the modal.\n23. f3b-verify-address-sheet · web-390 · 23-picker-after-joining · light — the full-height sheet.\n24. f3b-verify-address-sheet · ios · 24-non-owner-ax5 · light — AX5, chips under names, scrolling.\n25. f3b-verify-address-sheet · ios · 25-postcard-pending-greyscale · light — frame 7 in greyscale.\n26. f3b-verify-address-sheet · ios · 26-non-owner-ask-offered · dark — the dark twin of frame 1.\n27. f3b-verify-address-sheet · ios · 27-postcard-pending · dark — the dark twin of frame 7.\n28. f3b-verify-address-sheet · web-1440 · 28-notes · light — Notes: the reason string for every caller (\"To show your Residency Pass…\", \"To make a residency claim…\", \"To print a fridge card…\", \"To share what you pay in rent…\", \"To watch this home's records…\", \"To earn a Block Founder rank…\", \"To send a postcard invite…\", \"To join as a Founding Neighbor…\", \"To send a letter to neighbors…\", \"To show your address on your profile…\", each ending \"we need to confirm you live here.\"); the unlock list is rewritten as the shared GrantLimitList verb rows (research: plain-language verbs), replacing the doc's \"unchanged\" list; the in-flight rule (postcard pending and document under review hide the other methods; the request to Maya keeps them because it depends on another person) and why; the Document row carries a short requirement and the full accepted-types sentence moved to the step after the tap; the admin override method is not user-facing; assumption: Postcard and Document accept a non-owner occupant, and if not they render as frame 12; product decision: \"Ask the owner\" is a proposed method outside the doc's list, counts as address verification, and is offered only when the owner is address-verified; assumption and product decision: an owner setting that turns off confirming; the time chip uses the neutral StatusChip (9.37:1), which meets the per-surface contrast change without the info tint; Sat 24 Oct replaces Mon 2 Nov because it is the mailed date plus 10 days; frame 6 is drawn as of Tue 27 Oct; every invented string (the dates Wed 14 Oct, Sat 24 Oct, Tue 20 Oct, Fri 13 Nov and Mon 26 Oct, the short Document requirement, wrong-code, under-review and rejected-document text, the confirmed lines, \"Choose another way\", the address-type reason, the landlord reason, the confirming-turned-off line, the access-ended line, \"Cancel request\", the Also line, the generic reason, Priya Raman as the just-joined caller); omitted states: Android picker with all methods (follows frame 2), web-390 postcard pending (follows frame 7), confirmed by postcard or document (follows frame 8 with the method swapped), wrong code (inline under the field).\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: 1-6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 3: 13-18, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 4: 19-24, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 5: 25-28.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Added the confirmed success state (method and date, unlocked action, Done returns to the live caller, light haptic) and artboard 08-confirmed; renumbered to 28 frames and updated batch plan and frame references (major, brief §6, flows-spec step 17)",
          "Covered Maya confirming while the sheet is open in the confirmed state (minor)",
          "Defined the in-flight rule: postcard pending and document under review hide other methods; the request to Maya keeps them; recorded on Notes (minor, inventory 'not a second start')",
          "Added 'Choose another way' text button to the inline postcard confirm (minor)",
          "'Not available' chip now replaces the time chip in the same column, one chip per row (minor, StatusChip contract)",
          "Shortened the Document row requirement; full accepted-types sentence moved to the post-tap step (minor)",
          "Added the relative count to 'Available after Sat 24 Oct (in 5 days)' (minor, house style)",
          "Notes: unlock list rewritten as shared GrantLimitList verb rows, replacing the doc's 'unchanged' list (minor, design doc F3b)",
          "Callers now include 'Enter code' and 'See request' from pending LockedActionRow variants, matching the locked-row prompt"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f3b-owner-attestation",
        "name": "Confirm this person lives here (owner attestation)",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": true,
        "frameCount": 25,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Confirm this person lives here · f3b-owner-attestation\n\nTYPE: NEW. This sheet does not exist on any platform yet.\n\nATTACH: the members roster for HOME A as the owner sees it (the host screen, with a member row's overflow menu open); the Foundations board.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852, a sheet that opens at the detent showing everything down to the buttons without scrolling at default text size (large if medium cannot hold it); Android 412x915, a Material 3 bottom sheet; web 1440x900, a centred modal 520px wide; web 390x844, a sheet. Header control: \"Not now\" in the request-pending, ticked, confirming, loading, error and offline states; \"Close\" in the confirmed, declined, request-withdrawn, access-ended, already-verified and permission-denied states. Every variant closes with Back or Escape, returns focus to the control that opened it, and never opens on top of another sheet.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Place tab → Larkspur Loop → Members roster. Three entries. (1) The pending group row \"Sam Ortega asked you to confirm they live here · Review\". (2) \"Confirm lives here\" in a member row's overflow menu, usable without a request. (3) The push: title \"Sam asked you to confirm\", body \"Does Sam live with you?\", hidden-preview placeholder \"Household request\". The push lands on this sheet over the roster, never on the dashboard, including from a cold start; its NotificationRow twin opens the same sheet. The request starts on Sam's phone, from \"Ask Maya Chen to confirm\" in the \"Verify this address\" sheet, and the push is sent at that moment. What goes back: Sam's sheet and LockedActionRow update to confirmed, didn't confirm, or access ended, and Sam gets the in-app row \"Maya confirmed you live at Larkspur Loop\".\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Maya Chen owns HOME A; her own address was confirmed by postcard on Tue 15 Sep 2026. Sam Ortega joined on Sat 10 Oct through Maya's invitation: a household member, not yet address-verified. At 6:10 PM on Mon 19 Oct he tried to message a neighbor and asked Maya to confirm. A minute later Maya taps the push on her iPhone.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Let the person who claimed this address confirm, in one act, that a housemate really lives here, so the housemate can finish address verification.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: first, the title question (\"Does Sam live here?\"); second, the person block (name, when he joined, who invited him); third, the checkbox and the consequence line beneath it. The one primary action is \"Confirm Sam lives here\", disabled until the box is ticked.\n\nCONTENT (fixture deltas only):\n- Title: \"Does Sam live here?\"\n- Person block: 40pt initials avatar \"SO\", \"Sam Ortega\", caption \"Joined Larkspur Loop on Sat 10 Oct 2026 · invited by you\". Below: \"2418 NE Larkspur Loop, Vancouver, WA 98684\" with ScopeChip \"Your household\".\n- Grants, heading \"Once you confirm, Sam can also\". Use the same items in the same order as the verify sheet Sam saw, in their third-person forms from the shared string set, so no row reads as being about Maya: \"Message neighbors\" · \"Get a residency letter\" · \"Show a Residency Pass\", then \"and 2 more\", expanding in place to \"Share what Sam pays in rent (Real Rent)\" · \"Earn a Block Founder rank\" and the shared caption \"Also: residency claims, watching this home's records, postcard invites, fridge cards, letters to neighbors from Mail, the Founding Neighbor tier, and the address line on Sam's profile.\"\n- Checkbox, unticked by default: \"I confirm Sam Ortega lives at 2418 NE Larkspur Loop.\"\n- Consequence line, directly beneath, body text: \"This tells Pantopus that Sam lives here. It does not give Sam ownership of this home and does not let Sam remove you. We'll record that you confirmed it, with today's date.\"\n- Buttons: \"Confirm Sam lives here\" and \"Don't confirm\".\n- Worst case: the name \"Maria-Fernanda Castellanos-Whitaker\", no avatar photo, an unknown join date.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION: a vouching act, not a permissions screen: one person, one statement, one checkbox, two buttons. Fixed vertical order: header (header control, title), person block, grant rows, hairline, checkbox with its consequence line, buttons. Grant rows use the same tick glyph, 44pt row height and body text.primary type as the \"What you get now\" list on the invitation decision, so Maya recognises the list. The consequence line is the only place that says what confirming does not do: plain body text in text.primary, no box, no warning colour. Buttons are full width and equal size, stacked on phones, side by side on web 1440: Confirm filled primary.700; Don't confirm outlined neutral, never red. At default size the buttons sit in view at the bottom of the sheet; at AX5 they unpin and follow the consequence line, matching the invitation decision.\nDegradation: unknown join date gives \"joined recently\". No photo gives the initials monogram. If Sam's unlock list can't be resolved, show the three default rows with the caption \"Standard unlocks after address verification\".\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS: the whole checkbox row (44pt or taller) toggles the box. Ticking enables Confirm with a 150ms fade. While confirming, Confirm shows an inline spinner and \"Confirming…\" is announced. The confirmed state replaces the body with a cross-fade of 300ms or less, static under Reduce Motion, with one light haptic tick. \"Not now\" closes the sheet and leaves the request in the roster's pending group, with no new push. \"Don't confirm\" needs no second dialog: its result shows in place as InlineUndo (declined-ask variant), with a 44pt \"Undo\" beside \"You didn't confirm.\" Undo stays until Maya closes the sheet, with no countdown, and returns to the ticked-or-unticked request as it was. Sam is told only after the sheet closes. \"Done\" and \"Close\" both close the result states. From a cold start, the row skeleton shows only after 1s.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: MemberRow (the person block uses its avatar, name and caption; no status chip); GrantLimitList (attestation grants variant: three rows plus \"and 2 more\" and the shared caption, in the third-person forms); ScopeChip; InlineUndo (declined-ask variant: \"You didn't confirm. … · Undo\"; Sam's notice is held until the sheet closes); WarmingSkeleton (row skeleton for the person block and grant rows; only after 1s); PushCopy (the push preview on artboard 13); NotificationRow (the in-app twin, artboard 13); InlineErrorRow; OfflineNotice.\n\nACCESSIBILITY: reading order: header control first (spoken \"Not now, closes this sheet\" or \"Close, closes this sheet\"), then title, person, address, scope, grants heading and rows, checkbox with the consequence line as its hint, Confirm, Don't confirm. Checkbox: \"I confirm Sam Ortega lives at 2418 NE Larkspur Loop, checkbox, not checked\". Disabled Confirm: \"Confirm Sam lives here, dimmed, tick the box first\". Targets at least 44pt, 48dp, 44px, with 8dp between buttons. The sheet traps focus; unique title \"Does Sam live here?\". Results are announced as status messages; Undo is focusable. At AX5 the sheet scrolls and the buttons unpin and follow the consequence line.\n\nCOPY:\n- Confirmed: \"Confirmed. Sam's address is verified.\" · \"Address confirmed by Maya Chen · Mon 19 Oct 2026\" · \"Sam can now message your neighbors and get a residency letter. We've let Sam know.\" · \"Done\".\n- Declined: \"You didn't confirm. Sam stays in your household and can still verify by postcard or with a document. We'll let Sam know when you close this.\" · \"Undo\" · \"Done\".\n- Request withdrawn (Sam cancelled his request while the sheet was open): \"Sam cancelled this request. You can still confirm from Sam's row in Members.\" · \"Done\".\n- Access ended (Sam left or was removed): \"Sam no longer has access to Larkspur Loop, so there's nothing to confirm.\" · \"Done\".\n- Already verified: \"Sam's address is already confirmed.\" · \"Address confirmed by document · Fri 16 Oct 2026\" · \"Done\". No checkbox.\n- Permission denied (Priya Raman, a member who opens the request link after joining): \"Only the owner or an admin of this home can confirm who lives here. Maya Chen can do this.\" · \"Done\".\n- Error: \"We couldn't save your confirmation. Nothing changed. Try again.\" · \"Retry\". The box stays ticked.\n- Offline: \"You're offline. You can confirm when you're back online.\" The checkbox and both buttons stay visible and disabled, each with that reason.\n\nEDGE CASES: the longest name wraps: title uses the first name only (\"Does Maria-Fernanda live here?\"), the checkbox sentence and the grant row use the full or first name as written above. Several requests give one sheet per person, opened from separate pending rows, never stacked. If Sam cancels his request while the sheet is open, it switches to request withdrawn; if Sam leaves or is removed, it switches to access ended. Slow network: the button spinner shows after 1s. An admin sees the same sheet as the owner. Only an address-verified owner or admin sees this sheet. \"Not now\" keeps the request pending until it lapses on Mon 26 Oct: the pending row disappears and Sam's sheet says Maya hasn't answered. The sheet never offers role changes.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of a permissions matrix, capability grid or role picker, draw one person, one sentence and one checkbox, because this is a vouch, not an admin screen.\n- Instead of a pre-ticked box, draw it unticked with Confirm disabled, because the owner must make the statement herself.\n- Instead of a quiet \"Not now\" as the only way out, draw \"Don't confirm\" as an equal button and \"Not now\" as the header control, because declining is an answer and deferring is a different one.\n- Instead of a final \"Don't confirm\" that tells Sam at once, draw InlineUndo that lasts until Maya closes the sheet, because a mis-tap on an equal-size neighbour button would notify Sam.\n- Instead of red for Don't confirm, draw an outlined neutral button, because declining removes no one.\n- Instead of a warning box for the limits, draw the consequence line as plain text under the checkbox, because it must be read, not skimmed past.\n- Instead of \"your\" rows copied from Sam's sheet, draw the same items in the same order in third-person forms (\"Share what Sam pays in rent\"), because Maya must not think she is sharing her own rent or profile.\n- Instead of a bare \"Verified\" on the result, draw \"Address confirmed by Maya Chen · Mon 19 Oct 2026\", because a badge without a method and date is misread.\n\nDONE WHEN: Maya can confirm in two taps (tick, then confirm) from the push. She approves the same items, in the same order, that Sam was shown, and every row plainly describes Sam. She can see that confirming grants no ownership. Declining is as easy as confirming and can be undone until she closes the sheet. Sam sees the result without asking again. A withdrawn request never claims Sam lost access. Every state that cannot be acted on says why, offers Done, and shows Close in the header.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f3b-owner-attestation · ios · 01-request-pending · light — the dense default: box unticked, Confirm disabled, Not now in the header.\n2. f3b-owner-attestation · ios · 02-ticked-grants-expanded · light — box ticked, Confirm enabled, \"and 2 more\" open with the Also caption.\n3. f3b-owner-attestation · ios · 03-confirming · light — the inline spinner.\n4. f3b-owner-attestation · ios · 04-confirmed · light — the attributed, dated result, Close in the header.\n5. f3b-owner-attestation · ios · 05-declined-with-undo · light — InlineUndo: \"You didn't confirm\", Sam stays, Undo, \"We'll let Sam know when you close this.\"\n6. f3b-owner-attestation · ios · 06-request-withdrawn · light — Sam cancelled; confirm from his row in Members.\n7. f3b-owner-attestation · ios · 07-access-ended · light — Sam left; nothing to confirm.\n8. f3b-owner-attestation · ios · 08-already-verified · light — method and date, no checkbox.\n9. f3b-owner-attestation · ios · 09-permission-denied · light — Priya Raman's view, naming Maya.\n10. f3b-owner-attestation · ios · 10-loading · light — cold start from the push: title, row skeleton for the person block and grant rows.\n11. f3b-owner-attestation · ios · 11-error · light — InlineErrorRow, box still ticked.\n12. f3b-owner-attestation · ios · 12-offline · light — disabled controls with reasons.\n13. f3b-owner-attestation · ios · 13-push-and-roster-entry · light — the PushCopy preview (title, body, hidden-preview version), the NotificationRow twin and the roster pending row that open the sheet.\n14. f3b-owner-attestation · web-1440 · 14-request-pending · light — centred modal, buttons side by side.\n15. f3b-owner-attestation · web-1440 · 15-confirmed · light — the result in the modal.\n16. f3b-owner-attestation · web-1440 · 16-permission-denied · light — Priya Raman's view as a member.\n17. f3b-owner-attestation · android · 17-request-pending · light — Material 3 bottom sheet.\n18. f3b-owner-attestation · android · 18-confirming · light — Android progress state.\n19. f3b-owner-attestation · android · 19-declined-with-undo · light — Android result with Undo.\n20. f3b-owner-attestation · web-390 · 20-request-pending · light — the mobile web sheet.\n21. f3b-owner-attestation · ios · 21-request-pending-ax5 · light — AX5 with the worst-case name, scrolling, buttons unpinned after the consequence line.\n22. f3b-owner-attestation · ios · 22-request-pending-greyscale · light — frame 1 in greyscale.\n23. f3b-owner-attestation · ios · 23-request-pending · dark — the dark twin of frame 1.\n24. f3b-owner-attestation · ios · 24-confirmed · dark — the dark twin of frame 4.\n25. f3b-owner-attestation · web-1440 · 25-notes · light — Notes: the push strings replace the inventory's \"Sam is verifying this address\" and the flow's \"Sam is verifying Maple St\", because the push names the ask; it is sent when Sam taps Ask, not when he starts any method; group: Account & security (on by default, so Maya receives it; household activity is off by default); the brief sets Time Sensitive (iOS) / HIGH (Android) for this group, and lowering this push to Active / DEFAULT is a product decision to confirm — because Android importance is set per channel, a lower level would need its own channel; product decision: owner attestation is a new address-verification method (it records the address as verified by the owner) that is not in the doc's decision-8 list (postcard code, reviewed document, landlord confirmation, admin override); whether it is needed depends on whether postcard and document accept a non-owner occupant; the grant rows use third-person forms of the shared strings, so the Foundations board needs a person-aware form of GrantLimitList for this variant; \"Not now\" keeps the request pending until it lapses on Mon 26 Oct, and Sam then sees \"Maya hasn't answered yet\" (not \"didn't confirm\"), a departure from the flow's \"didn't confirm\" outcome for Not now; \"Don't confirm\" holds Sam's notice until the sheet closes (InlineUndo); request withdrawn is separate from access ended; assumptions: Priya Raman has accepted her invitation; only an address-verified owner or admin sees this sheet; withdrawing a confirmation later is a product decision to confirm; timing: Sam asked at 6:10 PM, matching the verify sheet; every invented string (\"SO\", the pending-row text, \"Household request\", the push title and body, the heading \"Once you confirm, Sam can also\", the third-person grant rows and Also ending, the record sentence, the declined and request-withdrawn lines, Tue 15 Sep 2026, the lapse date Mon 26 Oct, the document date Fri 16 Oct, \"Standard unlocks after address verification\", Priya Raman as the member viewer); omitted states: Android and web-390 twins of the other results (they follow frames 4-12).\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: 1-6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 3: 13-18, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 4: 19-24, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 5: 25.",
        "changeLog": [
          "'Don't confirm' now uses InlineUndo: Undo stays until Maya closes the sheet and Sam is told only afterwards; copy, components, frames 5 and 19 updated (major x2, brief P19, contract InlineUndo)",
          "Added a separate request-withdrawn state and artboard; access ended now applies only when Sam leaves or is removed (major)",
          "Grant rows switched to third-person forms ('Message neighbors', 'Show a Residency Pass', 'Share what Sam pays in rent (Real Rent)', 'address line on Sam's profile'); person-aware GrantLimitList flagged on Notes; DONE WHEN now 'same items, in the same order' (major)",
          "Added WarmingSkeleton and a loading artboard for cold starts from the push (minor)",
          "Notes: push placed in Account & security, level Time Sensitive / HIGH per the brief, with lowering it flagged as a product decision and the per-channel Android note (minor x2, brief §3)",
          "Notes: owner attestation recorded as a new address-verification method outside decision 8 (minor, design doc F3b, critique)",
          "Notes: 'Not now' lapse on Mon 26 Oct leads to 'hasn't answered', a departure from the flow (minor, flows-spec flow-04)",
          "Degradation caption changed to 'Standard unlocks after address verification' (minor, glossary bans 'resident')",
          "At AX5 the buttons unpin and follow the consequence line; header control is first in reading order and spoken with its effect (minor)",
          "Renumbered to 25 frames and updated batch plan"
        ]
