      {
        "id": "f3-bill-detail-web",
        "name": "Bill detail (new web route)",
        "platforms": [
          "web"
        ],
        "isNew": true,
        "frameCount": 23,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Bill detail · f3-bill-detail-web\n\nTYPE: NEW. Web only. Web has no page for a single bill today, so every money notification lands on a list. Match the attached Bills list and the native bill detail. Use no new card style.\n\nATTACH: the web Bills list at 1440 and 390; the web Place tab with the left sidebar at 1440; the web Notifications list at 1440; the iOS bill detail screen (for content order only).\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: web 1440x900 with the left sidebar (Place selected); web 390x844 with the four-tab bottom bar (Place selected). Draw no native frames in this project. The native bill detail changes (the same undo, lock row, removed state, Paid landing and amount field) are drawn in the f3-bills-list project.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Place tab › Larkspur Loop › Bills › one bill. URL /app/homes/{home}/bills/{bill}. Arrivals:\n1. A single \"Maya marked Clark PUD paid\" row in Notifications (/app/notifications). The page opens in the Paid state. A grouped \"Maya marked 3 bills paid\" row lands on the Bills list instead.\n2. A bill reminder row in Notifications (sent the day before and the day of the due date).\n3. A Bills list row (the whole row is the link). Back returns to the list with that row highlighted.\n4. The Today 14-day strip money row (phase 2).\n5. \"Added to bills\" on a Mail piece (phase 2).\nWeb gets no push. A phone push opens the native bill detail; the in-app row is the web twin. The back link always names where the person came from: \"Back to notifications\" after arrivals 1 and 2, \"Back to bills\" after arrival 3, \"Back to Today\" after arrival 4, \"Back to Mail\" after arrival 5. What happens next: Mark paid → Undo stays open → Maya leaves the page → Sam gets one paid notice → Sam taps it and lands here in the Paid state.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Maya Chen, owner of HOME A, at her laptop on Mon 19 Oct at 6:10 PM. She just paid Clark Public Utilities on the utility's website and opened the bill from its row in Bills to record it, so Sam doesn't pay it too. Second viewer: Sam Ortega, a member who can see bills but cannot mark them paid. He opens the same bill from \"Maya marked Clark PUD paid\". The reminder-row arrival is drawn only in frame 06 (due today, viewed Fri 23 Oct).\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Give every bill notification, reminder and calendar row one exact page that shows the amount, the due date and who marked it paid.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: first the amount \"$142.18\" (h1, tabular figures); second \"Due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\" (h3, text.secondary) with one StatusChip \"Upcoming\"; third the single primary button \"Mark paid\". Everything else sits below these as evidence.\n\nCONTENT (fixture deltas)\n- Bill: Clark Public Utilities · Electric · account ending 4417 · $142.18 · due Fri 23 Oct · repeats monthly · Visible to: Your household · Added by Maya · Sat 3 Oct · Reminders: Thu 22 Oct and Fri 23 Oct (day before and day of). After marking: \"Next due Mon 23 Nov\".\n- Overdue example: NW Natural · Gas · $41.18 · due line \"Was due Tue 13 Oct · 6 days ago\". The StatusChip alone carries the word \"Overdue\".\n- Only-you example: State Farm renters insurance · $22.50 · due Sat 7 Nov · Visible to: Only you · added by hand.\n- Phase-2 evidence, drawn in frames 01, 04 and 09 and owned by the f10-bill-provenance and f10-bill-trend projects. Maya's view (she took the photo): \"From a photo you took · Sat 3 Oct\" with a 56px thumbnail, \"We read this from your photo. You confirmed the amount on Sat 3 Oct.\", \"View the photo\", \"Fix what we read\". Any other viewer (Sam): \"From a photo Maya took · Sat 3 Oct\" and \"We read this from Maya's photo. Maya confirmed the amount on Sat 3 Oct.\" Trend: the 12 monthly amounts Maya added, Nov 2025 to Oct 2026: 118, 164, 178, 171, 146, 121, 104, 98, 112, 119, 128.64, 142.18. One reference line at $131, from 14 homes nearby.\n- Worst case: provider \"City of Vancouver Water, Sewer and Stormwater Utility\"; amount $3,412.56 on \"Clark County Treasurer · Property tax, 2nd half\", due Mon 2 Nov, with the Details line \"moved from Sat 31 Oct\".\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\n- 1440: back link, then breadcrumb \"Place › Larkspur Loop › Bills › Clark Public Utilities\", then a 2/3 + 1/3 split. Left column, top to bottom: provider (h2) with ScopeChip \"Your household\"; amount h1 with the StatusChip beside it; due line; attribution line (Paid only); action row with the primary \"Mark paid\" (primary.700 fill) and the text buttons \"Paid a different amount\" and \"Skip this month\"; an overflow menu button holding \"Edit\" and \"Remove\"; the provenance block; the trend card. Right column: a \"Details\" card with label/value rows: Type, Account, Repeats, Visible to, Added by, Reminders.\n- On an Only-you bill, drop the ScopeChip. Under the provider, print the ScopeChip sentence \"Only you will see this.\" and the Details row reads \"Visible to: Only you\".\n- Until phase 2 ships, the provenance block and the trend are absent, not placeholders: the left column ends after the action row with no empty slots. A bill added by hand never has a provenance block or a slot for one.\n- 390: one column: back link, provider, amount, due line, chip, a full-width \"Mark paid\", the secondary actions stacked, then Details, provenance and trend.\n- Trend: zero-based columns filled primary.600. The X axis shows months; the Y axis shows dollars from $0 ($0, $50, $100, $150, $200). The Oct column is labelled \"Oct · $142.18\" and carries a ProvenanceMark S tick with the words \"You added this\" printed once beside the label. All 12 columns are amounts Maya added; draw the tick only on the labelled Oct column, and say so in the Show amounts table. The nearby average is ONE dashed horizontal line in text.strong ink, labelled \"Nearby average $131 · 14 homes\". Above the chart, the summary sentence: \"October: $142.18. Nearby average: $131, from 14 homes.\" Under the chart, the SourceCaption \"Pantopus · 14 homes nearby · as of Mon 19 Oct\". Below that, a \"Show amounts\" disclosure lists all 12 values. Fallbacks: with too few homes, draw the bars, no line, and the caption \"Not enough homes nearby to compare yet\". With 4 months of history, draw 4 columns and leave the other months empty, never $0. On a cold load, use the WarmingSkeleton instrument variant. If the trend fails, show InlineErrorRow \"We couldn't load the 12-month trend · Retry\" and keep the bill above it live.\n- Sam's Paid frame (04) shows the provenance block with Maya's wording and ends before the trend; the trend's wording for a viewer who did not add the amounts is an open question for Notes.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- Mark paid: the button row becomes the InlineUndo line \"Marked paid · Undo\" (role=status). The chip changes to \"Paid\". The attribution reads \"Paid by you · Mon 19 Oct\". \"Next due Mon 23 Nov\" appears. The Reminders row reads \"No more reminders for Fri 23 Oct, for anyone. Next reminders: Sun 22 Nov and Mon 23 Nov.\" A caption reads \"We'll let Sam know when you leave this page.\" Undo stays until Maya leaves the page (navigates away or closes the tab), restores everything and sends nothing. Leaving sends exactly one paid notice to each other person who can see bills, cancels this month's scheduled reminders for everyone, and replaces any reminder already delivered with the paid notice. November's reminders stay scheduled.\n- Overdue bills use the same \"Mark paid\" primary, with the same InlineUndo and the same delayed notice; the overdue fact stays in the due line and chip.\n- Paid a different amount: an inline amount field pre-filled with $142.18, and a button that restates the value (\"Mark $120.00 paid\"), then the same InlineUndo. Afterwards the attribution reads \"Paid by you · $120.00 · Mon 19 Oct\", the h1 keeps $142.18, and the Details card adds the row \"Paid: $120.00 of $142.18\".\n- Skip this month: InlineUndo \"Skipped this month · Undo\" plus \"Next due Mon 23 Nov\". It cancels this month's reminders for everyone and sends no household notice.\n- Remove: no dialog. On the phase-1 bill, the page collapses to \"Removed Clark Public Utilities · Undo\" with \"Sam won't see it anymore.\" and \"Back to bills\". On a bill that came from a photo, the line reads \"Removed Clark Public Utilities and its photo · Undo\", with the same second line; the photo delete itself is owned by f10-bill-provenance. A removed bill also leaves the Bills list's Upcoming segment.\n- Only-you bill: Mark paid shows the InlineUndo with no notice caption, and Remove shows \"Removed State Farm renters insurance · Undo\" with no second line. Draw both as callouts on frame 10.\n- A link to a bill that no longer exists opens this route's removed state: \"That bill was removed.\" plus the back link that names where the person came from (\"Back to notifications\" from a notification, \"Back to bills\" from the list).\n- On a link arrival, focus moves to the h1 and the headline block fades a highlight once (300ms). With Reduce Motion, show the highlight without the fade. Escape closes the overflow menu. Web has no haptics.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: StatusChip (Upcoming · Due today · Overdue with the error glyph · Paid); ScopeChip (\"Your household\" chip; \"Only you will see this.\" sentence); InlineUndo (marked paid, skipped, removed, and the \"bill + photo deleted\" variant for a photo-backed bill); LockedActionRow (\"names who can act\" variant); ProvenanceMark and SourceCaption (inside the trend and provenance block); WarmingSkeleton; InlineErrorRow; FreshnessLine; OfflineNotice (a reason caption under each disabled control). BillRow is not used on this page. The headline is the h1 amount block described above, which replaces the Foundations in-context crop that shows BillRow as this page's header; record this on Notes.\n\nACCESSIBILITY: Reading order: back link, breadcrumb, provider, amount, due, status, attribution, primary action, Details, evidence, trend. Document title \"Clark Public Utilities bill, $142.18\". The chart is role=img labelled with its summary sentence, followed by the Show amounts table. Marks are spoken (\"you added this\"). Targets are 44px. \"Overdue\" is a word plus a glyph, never colour alone. The reference line is dashed and labelled, so it reads in greyscale. Undo announces politely and is focusable. A disabled control keeps focus and reads its reason. At 1440 with 200% zoom (720px effective), the Details card drops below the main column.\n\nCOPY: \"Mark paid\" · \"Paid a different amount\" · \"Mark $120.00 paid\" · \"Skip this month\" · \"Edit\" · \"Remove\" · \"Marked paid · Undo\" · \"Skipped this month · Undo\" · \"Removed Clark Public Utilities · Undo\" · \"Removed Clark Public Utilities and its photo · Undo\" · \"Removed State Farm renters insurance · Undo\" · \"Sam won't see it anymore.\" · \"Paid by you · Mon 19 Oct\" · \"Paid by Maya · Mon 19 Oct\" · \"Paid by you · $120.00 · Mon 19 Oct\" · \"Paid: $120.00 of $142.18\" · \"Next due Mon 23 Nov\" · \"We'll let Sam know when you leave this page.\" · \"No more reminders for Fri 23 Oct, for anyone. Next reminders: Sun 22 Nov and Mon 23 Nov.\" · \"Maya can mark this paid.\" · \"Already marked paid by you on your phone · 6:02 PM\" · \"Already marked paid by Maya · 6:02 PM\" · \"Due today\" · \"Due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\" · \"Was due Tue 13 Oct · 6 days ago\" · \"Visible to: Your household\" / \"Visible to: Only you\" · \"Only you will see this.\" · \"That bill was removed.\" + \"Back to notifications\" / \"Back to bills\" · \"You can't see this bill\" / \"Bills at Larkspur Loop are shared with your household. Maya can change your access.\" + \"Back to Larkspur Loop\" · \"We couldn't load this bill. Check your connection, then try again.\" + \"Retry\" · \"You're offline · as of 5:40 PM\" · \"Marking paid needs a connection.\" (under Mark paid) · \"Changes to this bill need a connection.\" (under Paid a different amount, Skip this month, Edit and Remove) · \"Pantopus · 14 homes nearby · as of Mon 19 Oct\" · \"Not enough homes nearby to compare yet\" · \"We couldn't load the 12-month trend · Retry\".\n\nEDGE CASES: The longest provider wraps to two lines; the amount never truncates. $3,412.56 fits the h1 at 390. The attribution line wraps and never truncates before the person's name. A Paid landing is reassurance, not an error: neutral chip, no error or success slab. It appears after a paid notice, in a race, and when a Paid row is opened from Bills. When one person marks the same bill on two devices, the second sees \"Already marked paid by you on your phone · 6:02 PM\"; when two people who can manage bills act at once, the second sees \"Already marked paid by Maya · 6:02 PM\". Nothing is sent twice. A member (Sam) sees no Mark paid, Edit or Remove, only LockedActionRow \"Maya can mark this paid.\" An Only-you bill never sends a paid notice. A guest without bill access sees the denied page with no provider or amount. Offline keeps the cached values and disables each action with its own reason caption.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of putting the provenance block or trend above the amount, draw them beneath it, because they are evidence for the number the reader came to see.\n- Instead of paired bars or a second peer series, draw one reference line labelled with its home count, because paired bars suggest one household competing with another.\n- Instead of a confidence percentage on the read, draw \"You confirmed the amount on Sat 3 Oct\", because a percentage makes people distrust a value they already checked.\n- Instead of a confirm dialog for Mark paid, draw the InlineUndo line and hold the notice until Maya leaves, because undo prevents mis-taps without adding a step.\n- Instead of a greyed Mark paid for a member, draw LockedActionRow naming Maya, because Sam needs to know who can record it.\n- Instead of a 404 or blank page for a removed bill, draw \"That bill was removed.\" with a back link to where the person came from, because a stale notification must never dead-end.\n- Instead of \"From a photo you took\" on Sam's view, write \"From a photo Maya took\", because the line must be true for the person reading it.\n- Instead of a zero baseline when data is short, omit the line, because the missing line is the honest signal.\n\nDONE WHEN: Within five seconds Maya can say what she owes, when it is due and what to press. After Mark paid, the page says Sam will be told, and he is told once, when she leaves. Sam lands on a calm Paid page naming Maya. No reminder for this month reaches Sam after the bill is paid, and the page says November's are still coming. Every arrival resolves to this bill or to a designed fallback, never a list or a blank page.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 01-upcoming-dense · light — Maya from Bills: Clark $142.18, Details, provenance block, full trend with SourceCaption.\n2. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 02-upcoming-phase1 · light — the same bill with no provenance block and no trend; the left column ends after the action row.\n3. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 03-marked-paid-undo · light — \"Marked paid · Undo\", Paid chip, \"Paid by you · Mon 19 Oct\", Next due, new reminders line, notice caption.\n4. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 04-paid-landing-member · light — Sam from the notification, \"Paid by Maya · Mon 19 Oct\", provenance in Maya's wording, Back to notifications.\n5. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 05-member-unpaid · light — Sam, phase-1 page, Upcoming, LockedActionRow \"Maya can mark this paid.\"\n6. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 06-due-today · light — Maya on Fri 23 Oct from the reminder row, chip \"Due today\", Back to notifications.\n7. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 07-overdue · light — NW Natural $41.18, Overdue chip with glyph, \"Was due Tue 13 Oct · 6 days ago\", primary \"Mark paid\".\n8. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 08-paid-different-amount · light — left panel: inline amount field and \"Mark $120.00 paid\"; right panel: the result with \"Paid by you · $120.00 · Mon 19 Oct\", h1 $142.18, Details \"Paid: $120.00 of $142.18\".\n9. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 09-removed · light — left panel: the photo-backed bill from frame 01 collapsed to \"Removed Clark Public Utilities and its photo · Undo\" with \"Sam won't see it anymore.\" and a callout giving the phase-1 wording \"Removed Clark Public Utilities · Undo\"; right panel: the link-arrival state \"That bill was removed.\" + \"Back to notifications\".\n10. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 10-only-you-manual · light — State Farm $22.50, no ScopeChip, \"Only you will see this.\", no provenance, bars only with \"Not enough homes nearby to compare yet\"; callouts: Mark paid with no notice caption, and \"Removed State Farm renters insurance · Undo\" with no second line.\n11. f3-bill-detail-web · web-390 · 11-upcoming · light — one-column version of 01.\n12. f3-bill-detail-web · web-390 · 12-marked-paid-undo · light — one-column version of 03.\n13. f3-bill-detail-web · web-390 · 13-race · light — Paid state with \"Already marked paid by you on your phone · 6:02 PM\".\n14. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 14-permission-denied · light — guest view, no amount or provider.\n15. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 15-loading · light — WarmingSkeleton in final geometry.\n16. f3-bill-detail-web · web-390 · 16-error · light — load failed with Retry.\n17. f3-bill-detail-web · web-390 · 17-offline · light — cached values; each disabled action with its reason caption.\n18. f3-bill-detail-web · web-390 · 18-worst-case · light — longest provider, $3,412.56, \"moved from Sat 31 Oct\".\n19. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 19-200-percent · light — 720px effective width, Details card below the main column, nothing truncated.\n20. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 20-greyscale · light — frame 01 in greyscale.\n21. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 01-upcoming-dense · dark — dark twin of 1.\n22. f3-bill-detail-web · web-1440 · 04-paid-landing-member · dark — dark twin of 4.\n23. f3-bill-detail-web · Notes — (a) Assumptions: Skip behaviour; Only-you default; due today viewed Fri 23 Oct; \"Already paid\" from the brief is the same write, labelled \"Mark paid\"; attribution wording is \"Paid by <name> · <date>\" on this page and on the Bills list, while notifications say \"marked … paid\"; the h1 amount block replaces the Foundations BillRow header crop for this page. (b) Every invented string, listed verbatim: every COPY string above that is not in the design doc or the contract, plus account 4417, NW Natural, State Farm renters insurance and $22.50, the trend values, 6:02 PM, City of Vancouver Water, Sewer and Stormwater Utility, Clark County Treasurer · Property tax, 2nd half $3,412.56 as a bill, the Sat 3 Oct photo date, the nearby average $131 from 14 homes, the SourceCaption, and the reminders Thu 22 / Fri 23 Oct and Sun 22 / Mon 23 Nov. (c) States described but not drawn: the second-manager race line, the 4-month partial trend, the trend failure row. (d) Open decisions: letting members record \"I paid this\"; what ends the undo window (leaving the page, closing the tab); the trend wording for a viewer who did not add the amounts. (e) Engineering notes: ship the Android link-router branches for /bills and /calendar in the same release; fix the removed-bill status spelling so a removed bill leaves Upcoming; change the bill_paid and bill-reminder link from /app/homes/{home}/bills to /app/homes/{home}/bills/{bill}, and add both types to the web notification routing; the native bill detail on iOS and Android must adopt the same Mark paid InlineUndo with the delayed notice, the LockedActionRow \"Maya can mark this paid.\", \"That bill was removed.\", the calm Paid landing and the \"Paid a different amount\" field; those native frames are drawn in the f3-bills-list project.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: 1-6, then wait for continue. Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue. Turn 3: 13-18, then wait for continue. Turn 4: 19-23.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Added Notes engineering note that native bill detail must adopt the same undo, lock row, removed state, Paid landing and amount field, drawn in f3-bills-list (review minor, derive f3-bills-member-and-paid-landing)",
          "Remove on a photo-backed bill now reads 'Removed Clark Public Utilities and its photo · Undo' using the InlineUndo bill + photo variant; frame 09 is the photo-backed bill with a phase-1 callout (review minor, f10-bill-provenance)",
          "Added Notes engineering note to change bill_paid/bill-reminder links to /bills/{bill} and add them to web routing (review minor, derive f10-7)",
          "Expanded Notes invented-strings list to every COPY string plus the named deltas (review minors x2, house style)",
          "Added per-control offline reasons: 'Changes to this bill need a connection.' (review minor, OfflineNotice contract)",
          "Aligned attribution to 'Paid by <name> · <date>' with Bills list and Foundations; due line now 'Was due Tue 13 Oct · 6 days ago' with the chip carrying 'Overdue' (review minors)",
          "Replaced the BillRow entry: not used; h1 block replaces the Foundations header crop, recorded on Notes (review minor, 00c)",
          "Added Only-you variants: no notice caption, 'Removed State Farm renters insurance · Undo' with no second line, drawn as callouts on frame 10 (review minor)",
          "Added SourceCaption 'Pantopus · 14 homes nearby · as of Mon 19 Oct' under the trend (review minor)",
          "Defined the different-amount Paid state: attribution with $120.00, h1 keeps $142.18, Details 'Paid: $120.00 of $142.18'; frame 08 gains a result panel (review minor)",
          "Skip now explicitly cancels this month's reminders for everyone, matching f3-bills-list",
          "Mark ProvenanceMark word changed to the plain 'You added this' next to the tick glyph (no literal tick character in text)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f3-bills-list",
        "name": "Bills list (member read-only + payer attribution)",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 28,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Bills list (plus the native bill detail changes) · f3-bills-list\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screens \"Bills list\" and \"Bill detail\" (iOS and Android). These screens already exist in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshots are exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed.\n\nATTACH: the Bills list on web 1440, web 390, iOS and Android; the native bill detail on iOS and Android (frames 22-25 extend them). For context only (do not redraw): the home dashboard Bills card.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: web 1440x900 (left sidebar) and 390x844 (bottom tab bar); iOS 393x852 (large title \"Bills\", back \"Larkspur Loop\"); Android 412x915 (Material 3 top app bar). Place is the selected tab everywhere. The web bill detail is a separate project (f3-bill-detail-web); the native bill detail is drawn here.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Place tab › place file Money section › Larkspur Loop › Bills. Other ways in:\n- the home dashboard Bills card \"View\";\n- the home header Bills tab;\n- a grouped paid notice (\"Maya marked 3 bills paid\"), from the phone tray or from the Notifications row body, which opens the Paid segment with those three rows highlighted;\n- Back from bill detail, which highlights the row you came from.\nA single paid notice or a bill reminder opens bill detail, not this list; on native, that bill detail opens in the Paid state (frame 22). Every row hands off to bill detail (web /app/homes/{home}/bills/{bill}; native pantopus://homes/{home}/bills/{bill}). List links: /app/homes/{home}/bills?linkedType=bill&linkedId={bill} for one row; /app/homes/{home}/bills?segment=paid&linkedIds={bill},{bill},{bill} for a grouped notice.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: The dense default is Sam Ortega's phone on Mon 19 Oct at 6:10 PM. Sam is a member at HOME A. He can see bills, but only Maya can mark them paid. He checks whether the power bill is handled before paying it himself. Frames that say \"Maya's view\" are Maya Chen's (owner, can manage bills). Every artboard line below names its viewer.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Let everyone in the household see the bills and who marked each one paid, so two people do not pay the same bill.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: first the header: ScopeChip \"Your household\", then \"1 overdue · $41.18\", then \"3 upcoming · $306.17 through Mon 2 Nov · You and Maya can see these\"; second the column of amounts; third each row's second line, \"Not marked paid yet\" or \"Paid by Maya · Thu 15 Oct\". The primary action is opening a row. There is no mark-paid button on any row face.\n\nCONTENT (fixture deltas)\n- Upcoming (fixtures): Clark Public Utilities $142.18 · Due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct; City of Vancouver water $84.00 · Due in 9 days · Wed 28 Oct; Comcast $79.99 · Due in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov. HOA dues is a date on this home, not a bill, so it is not listed here.\n- Overdue (delta): NW Natural $41.18 · Was due Tue 13 Oct · 6 days ago · Overdue.\n- Paid (delta): Waste Connections $38.75 · Paid by Maya · Thu 15 Oct; Comcast $79.99 · Paid by Maya · Thu 15 Oct; Clark Public Utilities $128.64 · Paid by Maya · Thu 15 Oct; City of Vancouver water $81.60 · Paid by Theo (no longer here) · Fri 28 Aug. List any due dates you give these Paid rows on Notes.\n- Only-you (delta, Maya's view only): State Farm renters insurance $22.50 · Due in 19 days · Sat 7 Nov.\n- Worst case: provider \"City of Vancouver Water, Sewer and Stormwater Utility\"; \"Clark County Treasurer · Property tax, 2nd half\" $3,412.56 due Mon 2 Nov; the total line then reads \"4 upcoming · $3,718.73 through Mon 2 Nov · You and Sam can see these\".\n- Who can see: the total line always names the people who can see bills, never \"Everyone\", because finance access can differ (a guest may have none). Sam's view ends \"· You and Maya can see these\"; Maya's view ends \"· You and Sam can see these\". With four or more people, name two and count the rest: \"· You, Sam and 2 others can see these\".\n- Window rule: Upcoming lists every unpaid bill. The header total covers household bills only, through the due date of the last household bill listed. Overdue bills get their own header line, \"1 overdue · $41.18\", above the total line, and are not in it. Only-you rows are listed for their owner but never counted, and Maya's header adds \"1 bill only you can see\" under the total line.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\n- List header, in this order: ScopeChip \"Your household\"; \"1 overdue · $41.18\" (when present); the total line with the named people; \"1 bill only you can see\" (owner only, when present); a FreshnessLine with a 44pt / 48dp / 44px \"Refresh\" text button; the ChoiceChip segment Upcoming / Paid / All (iOS segmented control, Android M3 filter chips, web ChoiceChip segment row); on Sam's view, LockedActionRow \"Maya can mark bills paid.\" last.\n- Rows use BillRow, identical on all three platforms. Line 1: provider (bodyMedium, truncates first), one StatusChip, and the amount right-aligned in tabular figures, so the amounts form one column. Line 2: the due date (bodySmall, text.secondary) and, right-aligned, the attribution: \"Paid by Maya · Thu 15 Oct\" on paid rows, \"Not marked paid yet\" (bodySmall, text.secondary) on unpaid rows. The name never truncates. Paid rows use the Paid chip. Overdue rows use the Overdue chip with its glyph.\n- Only-you rows print a 12pt person glyph plus \"Only you\" at the start of line 2, before the due date. It is not a chip; the row keeps its one StatusChip.\n- Upcoming shows the overdue group first, under the overline \"OVERDUE\", then the upcoming rows. The All segment adds month overlines once there are more than 20 rows.\n- Manage (Maya's view): each row has an overflow button (44pt / 48dp / 44px) with \"Mark paid\", \"Paid a different amount\" and \"Skip this month\". Sam's rows have no overflow; the whole row opens detail.\n- Highlight from a notification: BillRow S2 highlighted (Foundations 1.8: infoBg wash plus the 4pt border.focus leading bar, with the focus ring 2px outside the row on arrival). The target row scrolls into view once and receives accessibility focus. With three rows, focus goes to the first. The wash and bar fade over 300ms once the person scrolls; the focus ring remains. The highlight opens nothing by itself.\n- Draw no budget bar, spend meter or ring.\n- Native bill detail (frames 22-25), iOS and Android, in this order: provider with ScopeChip; amount (large, tabular); due line with one StatusChip; attribution (Paid only); the primary \"Mark paid\" (manage) or LockedActionRow \"Maya can mark this paid.\" (member); the text buttons \"Paid a different amount\" and \"Skip this month\"; an overflow with \"Edit\" and \"Remove\"; then a Details list (Type, Account, Repeats, Visible to, Added by, Reminders). A Paid landing is calm: neutral Paid chip, no success or error slab.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- Mark paid (row overflow or native detail): the row changes in place to InlineUndo \"Clark Public Utilities marked paid · Undo\" with the caption \"We'll let Sam know when you leave this screen.\" (iOS and Android) or \"We'll let Sam know when you leave this page.\" (web). On native detail the button row becomes \"Marked paid · Undo\" with the same caption. On Android it is echoed by a Snackbar with Undo that stays open while TalkBack is on. On iOS the inline line is also announced. Undo lasts until Maya leaves the screen and sends nothing. The household paid notice is sent only after that, this month's reminders stop for everyone, any delivered reminder is replaced by the paid notice, and the repeating bill reappears in Upcoming as \"Next due Mon 23 Nov\". These are the same rules as the web bill detail. On an Only-you bill there is no caption and no notice.\n- Paid a different amount (row overflow): opens native bill detail with the amount field open and focused, pre-filled with $142.18, and the button \"Mark $120.00 paid\" (frame 24). After marking, the attribution reads \"Paid by you · $120.00 · Mon 19 Oct\" and Details adds \"Paid: $120.00 of $142.18\".\n- Skip this month (overflow): the row changes to InlineUndo \"Comcast skipped this month · Undo\" plus \"Next due Wed 2 Dec\". It cancels this month's reminders for everyone and sends no household notice.\n- Remove (native detail overflow): no dialog; the screen collapses to \"Removed Clark Public Utilities · Undo\" with \"Sam won't see it anymore.\" A link to a removed bill opens \"That bill was removed.\" plus \"Back to notifications\" (or \"Back to bills\").\n- The overflow menu is also exposed as custom accessibility actions. There are no swipe-only actions.\n- Refresh: every platform has the \"Refresh\" text button in the FreshnessLine; native also supports pull to refresh. Both refresh in place with FreshnessLine \"Updating…\" and no full-screen spinner.\n- Haptics: one light tick when Mark paid is tapped (iOS light impact; Android CONFIRM). No haptic on Undo or Skip.\n- Reduce Motion: the highlight appears and clears with no fade or scroll animation.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: BillRow (V1 manage; V3 only-me; V4 former-member; S2 highlighted; S3 marked-paid; S5 offline) and BillRow V2b (member, no overflow) with one surface change: line 2 right reads \"Not marked paid yet\" on unpaid rows, and the \"who can act\" reason moves once to the header LockedActionRow \"Maya can mark bills paid.\" Record this on Notes as a deviation from V2b. Deviation from BillRow V3: the short form \"Only you\" keeps line 2 on one line; record on Notes. StatusChip; ChoiceChip (segment); ScopeChip (\"Your household\"); LockedActionRow (\"names who can act\" variant); InlineUndo (marked paid, skipped, removed); FreshnessLine; OfflineNotice; WarmingSkeleton (row skeleton); InlineErrorRow.\n\nACCESSIBILITY: Reading order: ScopeChip, overdue line, total line, only-you line, FreshnessLine, segment, lock row, rows. Each row is one merged element, for example \"Clark Public Utilities, 142 dollars 18 cents, due Friday October 23, in 4 days, upcoming, not marked paid yet\" or \"…, paid by Maya on Thursday October 15\". Overflow items are custom actions. A highlighted row gets focus and the announcement \"From your notification\". Overdue and Only you are words, not colour. The segment shows selection with a check plus fill, which differs from the focus ring. Targets are 44pt, 48dp and 44px. At AX5 and 200%, line 2 stacks under line 1, the amount moves under the provider, and the segment becomes radio rows. Undo announces as a status. On native detail, the disabled or locked action reads its reason.\n\nCOPY: \"3 upcoming · $306.17 through Mon 2 Nov · You and Maya can see these\" (Sam) · \"3 upcoming · $306.17 through Mon 2 Nov · You and Sam can see these\" (Maya) · \"You, Sam and 2 others can see these\" · \"1 overdue · $41.18\" · \"OVERDUE\" · \"Maya can mark bills paid.\" · \"Maya can mark this paid.\" · \"Upcoming\" / \"Paid\" / \"All\" · \"Mark paid\" · \"Paid a different amount\" · \"Mark $120.00 paid\" · \"Skip this month\" · \"Edit\" · \"Remove\" · \"Clark Public Utilities marked paid · Undo\" · \"Marked paid · Undo\" · \"We'll let Sam know when you leave this screen.\" · \"We'll let Sam know when you leave this page.\" · \"Comcast skipped this month · Undo\" · \"Removed Clark Public Utilities · Undo\" · \"Sam won't see it anymore.\" · \"That bill was removed.\" + \"Back to notifications\" / \"Back to bills\" · \"Next due Mon 23 Nov\" · \"Next due Wed 2 Dec\" · \"Not marked paid yet\" · \"Paid by Maya · Thu 15 Oct\" · \"Paid by Maya · Mon 19 Oct\" · \"Paid by you · Thu 15 Oct\" · \"Paid by you · $120.00 · Mon 19 Oct\" · \"Paid: $120.00 of $142.18\" · \"Paid by Theo (no longer here) · Fri 28 Aug\" · \"Only you\" · \"1 bill only you can see\" · \"From your notification\" · \"Checked — no household bills on file\" + \"Add a bill\" (Maya) / \"Maya can add bills here.\" (Sam) · \"Checked — nothing due. Paid bills are under Paid.\" · \"We couldn't load your bills. Check your connection, then try again.\" + \"Retry\" · \"You're offline · as of 5:40 PM\" · \"Amounts and paid status as of 5:40 PM. Changes since then aren't shown.\" · \"Marking paid needs a connection.\" · \"Changes to this bill need a connection.\" · \"Refresh\" · \"Updated 2h ago\" · \"Updating…\" · \"You can't see these bills\" / \"Bills at Larkspur Loop are shared with your household. Maya can change your access.\" + \"Back to Larkspur Loop\".\n\nEDGE CASES: The longest provider truncates before the amount or the attribution. $3,412.56 keeps the amount column aligned. With more than 20 bills, use month overlines. Zero bills is drawn for Maya and for Sam. An empty Upcoming with a populated Paid segment shows \"Checked — nothing due. Paid bills are under Paid.\" On a slow network, a cold load uses the row skeleton; a warm load keeps the rows. Offline and stale states say what is stale. A guest without bill access gets the denied state with no providers or amounts, and the people line for everyone else names only those who can see bills. A saved place never reaches this list: its place file shows the Money section as not available for a saved place. Only-you bills appear only for their owner, never count toward the household total and never notify. The same bill marked on two devices shows \"Already marked paid by you on your phone · 6:02 PM\" on native detail, and nothing is sent twice.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a one-tap Mark paid on the row face, keep it in the overflow with InlineUndo, because a mis-tap would tell the whole household.\n- Instead of an empty attribution slot on unpaid rows, print \"Not marked paid yet\", because Sam's question is whether anyone has handled it.\n- Instead of an avatar without a name, print \"Paid by Maya\", because the name is the point.\n- Instead of a greyed Mark paid for Sam, draw LockedActionRow \"Maya can mark bills paid.\", because he needs to know who can record it.\n- Instead of \"Everyone at Larkspur Loop can see these bills\", name the people in the total line, because a guest may not have bill access and \"everyone\" would be false.\n- Instead of a budget bar, spend meter or percentage ring, show the count and window total as text, because this list is about who paid, not a score.\n- Instead of a highlight that only changes colour, draw the 4pt leading bar and move focus, because the wash is invisible in greyscale and to screen readers.\n- Instead of an \"Only you\" chip next to the status, print the glyph and words on line 2, because one object has one status chip.\n\nDONE WHEN: Sam can tell in five seconds that Clark Public Utilities is not yet marked paid and that only Maya can mark it. Maya can mark a bill paid, from the list or native detail, and undo it without anyone being told, and the screen tells her Sam will hear when she leaves. The grouped notice lands on the right three rows with focus on the first. The header always names who can see the bills and states what is overdue and the window total. Sam's paid notice opens a calm native Paid page naming Maya.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f3-bills-list · ios · 01-upcoming-member-dense · light — Sam's view: header with named people, lock row, overdue group, three upcoming rows with \"Not marked paid yet\".\n2. f3-bills-list · web-1440 · 02-upcoming-manage · light — Maya's view with overflow buttons and \"You and Sam can see these\".\n3. f3-bills-list · android · 03-upcoming-manage · light — Maya's view.\n4. f3-bills-list · ios · 04-paid-segment · light — Sam's view: attribution on every row, including Theo.\n5. f3-bills-list · ios · 05-all-segment · light — Sam's view: mixed statuses.\n6. f3-bills-list · android · 06-overflow-open · light — Maya's view: the menu with the three actions.\n7. f3-bills-list · ios · 07-marked-paid-undo · light — Maya's view: \"Clark Public Utilities marked paid · Undo\" with the \"screen\" caption, plus Next due Mon 23 Nov.\n8. f3-bills-list · android · 08-marked-paid-snackbar · light — Maya's view: the Snackbar held open with TalkBack on.\n9. f3-bills-list · web-390 · 09-highlighted-grouped · light — Sam's view: Paid segment, three rows in BillRow S2 with the leading bar, focus ring on the first.\n10. f3-bills-list · ios · 10-highlighted-return · light — Sam's view: back from bill detail with one row highlighted and focused.\n11. f3-bills-list · ios · 11-only-you-and-skip · light — Maya's view: the State Farm row with \"Only you\", the \"1 bill only you can see\" header line, and \"Comcast skipped this month · Undo\".\n12. f3-bills-list · web-1440 · 12-empty · light — three panels: Maya zero bills, Sam zero bills, empty Upcoming with populated Paid.\n13. f3-bills-list · ios · 13-loading · light — Sam's view: row skeleton.\n14. f3-bills-list · android · 14-error · light — Sam's view: InlineErrorRow with Retry.\n15. f3-bills-list · ios · 15-offline-stale · light — Maya's view: cached rows, stale line, overflow open with each action disabled and its reason.\n16. f3-bills-list · web-390 · 16-permission-denied · light — guest view.\n17. f3-bills-list · ios · 17-worst-case · light — Maya's view: All segment, 22 rows with month overlines, longest provider, $3,412.56, \"You, Sam and 2 others can see these\".\n18. f3-bills-list · web-1440 · 18-member · light — Sam's view on desktop, \"You and Maya can see these\", web Refresh button.\n19. f3-bills-list · ios · 19-ax5 · light — Sam's view at AX5, stacked.\n20. f3-bills-list · android · 20-200-percent · light — Sam's view at 200% font.\n21. f3-bills-list · ios · 21-greyscale · light — frame 1 in greyscale.\n22. f3-bills-list · ios · 22-detail-member-paid-landing · light — native bill detail, Sam from the paid notice: Paid chip, \"Paid by Maya · Mon 19 Oct\", LockedActionRow \"Maya can mark this paid.\", calm, Back to notifications.\n23. f3-bills-list · android · 23-detail-marked-paid-undo · light — native bill detail, Maya: \"Marked paid · Undo\", \"We'll let Sam know when you leave this screen.\", Next due Mon 23 Nov.\n24. f3-bills-list · ios · 24-detail-different-amount · light — native bill detail, Maya: amount field open and focused at $142.18, button \"Mark $120.00 paid\".\n25. f3-bills-list · android · 25-detail-removed · light — left: \"Removed Clark Public Utilities · Undo\" with \"Sam won't see it anymore.\"; right: link arrival \"That bill was removed.\" + \"Back to notifications\".\n26. f3-bills-list · ios · 01-upcoming-member-dense · dark — dark twin of 1.\n27. f3-bills-list · ios · 07-marked-paid-undo · dark — dark twin of 7.\n28. f3-bills-list · Notes — (a) Assumptions: the window rule; \"Already paid\" from the brief is the same write, labelled \"Mark paid\"; HOA dues is a date, not a bill, on this surface, so the total is 3 upcoming · $306.17, which differs from the Foundations fixture (4 upcoming · $591.17); the research header sentence \"Everyone at Larkspur Loop can see these bills\" is replaced by the Foundations named-people form. (b) Deviations: BillRow V2b line 2 reads \"Not marked paid yet\" and the reason moves to the header LockedActionRow; BillRow V3 uses the short \"Only you\". (c) Every invented string, listed verbatim: every COPY string above not in the design doc or the contract, including \"Not marked paid yet\", \"From your notification\", \"1 bill only you can see\", \"Maya can mark bills paid.\", \"Checked — nothing due. Paid bills are under Paid.\", both \"leave this screen/page\" captions and \"You, Sam and 2 others can see these\"; plus Theo, NW Natural, State Farm, the Thu 15 Oct payments, Paid-row due dates, Comcast's Wed 2 Dec, the 18 extra rows in frame 17, City of Vancouver Water, Sewer and Stormwater Utility, and Clark County Treasurer · Property tax, 2nd half $3,412.56. (d) Open decision: letting members record \"I paid this\". Until decided, member rows have no overflow and the header LockedActionRow names Maya (the contract's member variant allows \"I paid this\" in the overflow). (e) Cross-prompt requirement: f3-member-home-dashboard must remove the one-tap Mark paid from the owner's Bills card (move it into an overflow with InlineUndo), and that card is drawn there. The web bill detail is drawn in f3-bill-detail-web with the same rules. (f) Engineering notes: the grouped link format above; the Android link-router branch for /homes/{home}/bills, without which frames 08-10 and the paid landing fall back to the dashboard; native BillDetailView and BillDetailScreen adopt the delayed notice, lock row, removed state, Paid landing and amount field drawn in frames 22-25.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: 1-6, then wait for continue. Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue. Turn 3: 13-18, then wait for continue. Turn 4: 19-24, then wait for continue. Turn 5: 25-28.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Replaced 'Everyone at Larkspur Loop can see these bills' with the Foundations named-people form merged into the total line ('· You and Maya can see these'); header order now ScopeChip, overdue, total, FreshnessLine, segment, lock row; FIRST FIVE SECONDS and COPY updated (review majors x2, contract ScopeChip doNot, 00c BillRow ⑧)",
          "Added native bill detail frames 22-25 (member Paid landing, Android marked paid undo, iOS different-amount field, removed state) and layout/interaction rules for them, since f3-bill-detail-web is web-only (review major, derive f3-bills-member-and-paid-landing)",
          "Highlight now uses BillRow S2 per Foundations 1.8 (4pt border.focus bar, focus ring on arrival); removed 2pt primary.700 wording (review major)",
          "Declared BillRow V2b deviation ('Not marked paid yet' on line 2, reason in header lock row) and V3 short-form 'Only you' deviation, both recorded on Notes (review major and minor)",
          "InlineUndo strings aligned to 00c: 'Clark Public Utilities marked paid · Undo', 'Comcast skipped this month · Undo' (review minor)",
          "Skip this month now cancels this month's reminders for everyone (review minor)",
