      {
        "id": "f3-household-notifications",
        "name": "Household activity notifications (rows, channel, routing)",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 26,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Household activity notifications · f3-household-notifications\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screens \"Notifications\" (the in-app list) and \"Notification settings\". These screens already exist in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshots are exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed.\n\nATTACH: the Notifications list on web 1440, web 390, iOS and Android; the header bell with its badge; Notification settings on iOS and Android; the native bill detail; the web Bills list; the household calendar; Today on iOS.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: web 1440x900 and 390x844; iOS 393x852; Android 412x915. Frames 06-09 are specification frames of the real OS tray for engineering, not in-app UI: draw them on the iOS lock screen and Notification Center and the Android notification shade, and label each \"OS tray (spec)\".\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: This is not a fifth tab. The list is a stack pushed over whichever of the four tabs is open, reached from the header bell (web: Notifications in the sidebar). The phone tray is the other way in. Settings are reached from Notification settings › Household activity, from \"Turn these off\" in a household row's menu, and from the household block's switch (an explicit opt-in, so it goes straight to the phone's own prompt). Each row hands off to its exact object:\n- Bill marked paid → that bill's detail, in the Paid state.\n- Grouped bills marked paid → Bills list, Paid segment, those rows highlighted.\n- Task finished → the task.\n- Event added → the household calendar, with the event highlighted.\n- Date reminder → the date's row on Today's 14-day strip, highlighted, or the place file Dates row when the date is outside the strip. A saved-place reminder opens Today for Cedar Ave; a home reminder opens Today for Larkspur Loop.\n- Bill reminder → that bill's detail.\n- Joined or left → the Larkspur Loop members list.\nPickup is not sent from here: it arrives only through the evening briefing.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Sam Ortega, a member at HOME A, on Mon 19 Oct at 6:10 PM. He also has a saved place, Cedar Ave (2207 SE Cedar Ave, Vancouver, WA 98664, \"Saved place · Only you\"), so rows carry a place label. He turned Household activity on last week. Maya just marked Clark Public Utilities paid, so Sam won't pay it too.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Make \"Maya marked Clark PUD paid\" arrive quietly, read clearly, and open the exact bill.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: first the unread dots and the actor's name at the start of each row; second the caption with the amount, date and place; third the grouped row's count. The primary action is tapping a row.\n\nCONTENT (fixture deltas). The actor is Maya because only she can mark bills paid; the canonical \"Sam marked Clark PUD paid\" is the same string with the names swapped. In-app captions add the relative count for dates beyond tomorrow. Rows, newest first:\n1. Unread · MC · \"Maya marked Clark PUD paid\" / \"$142.18 · due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct · Larkspur Loop · Today\"\n2. Unread · MC · \"Maya added Chimney sweep\" / \"in 19 days · Sat 7 Nov, 9:00 AM · Larkspur Loop · Today\"\n3. Unread · no avatar · \"Property tax due in 14 days\" / \"Clark County Treasurer · Mon 2 Nov · Larkspur Loop · ● Official\"\n4. Unread · MC · \"Maya finished HVAC filter\" / \"Your task · Larkspur Loop · Sun 18 Oct\"\n5. Read · no avatar · \"Theo left Larkspur Loop\" / \"Sun 18 Oct\"\n6. Read · MC · \"Maya marked 3 bills paid\" / \"Waste Connections, Comcast, Clark Public Utilities · $247.38 · Larkspur Loop · Thu 15 Oct\"\n7. Read · no avatar · \"NW Natural due tomorrow\" / \"$41.18 · Tue 13 Oct · Larkspur Loop · Mon 12 Oct\"\n8. Routing frame only: \"Insurance renews in 7 days\" / \"Mon 26 Oct · Cedar Ave · ✓ You added this\"\n9. Later frame (Wed 21 Oct), read, no avatar: \"Priya joined Larkspur Loop\" / \"Can see the calendar and bills · Wed 21 Oct\"\n10. Later frame (Wed 21 Oct), read, no avatar: \"Jenna's guest access ended\" / \"Larkspur Loop · Tue 20 Oct\"\n11. Unconfirmed example (frame 09): \"Unconfirmed: HOA due in 7 days\" / \"$285 · Sun 1 Nov · Larkspur Loop · ○ On record, not confirmed\"\n12. Lease example (frame 08's in-app twin): \"Lease notice due in 14 days\" / \"Tell your landlord · Mon 1 Mar 2027 · Larkspur Loop · ✓ You added this\"\nRows whose title already names the home (5 and 9) carry no place label.\n\nPUSH strings (title 30 characters or fewer, body 40 or fewer including the place label, no amounts, no house number). If the home has a nickname, use it in place of \"Larkspur Loop\". Task names in push bodies are shortened to fit 40 characters including the place label.\n- \"Maya marked Clark PUD paid\" / \"Due Fri 23 Oct · Larkspur Loop\"\n- Grouped, updated in place on Thu 15 Oct: \"Maya marked 3 bills paid\" / \"3 household bills · Larkspur Loop\"\n- \"Maya added Chimney sweep\" / \"Sat 7 Nov, 9:00 AM · Larkspur Loop\"\n- Long task title: \"Maya finished a task\" / \"Upstairs bathroom fan · Larkspur Loop\" (37)\n- Bill reminder: \"NW Natural due tomorrow\" / \"Larkspur Loop\"\n- Date reminder, Mon 15 Feb 2027 at 7:00 AM: \"Lease notice due in 14 days\" / \"Tell your landlord by Mon 1 Mar\" (31, no place label), action \"Done\"\n- Unconfirmed date reminder, Sun 25 Oct: \"Unconfirmed: HOA due in 7 days\" / \"By Sun 1 Nov · Larkspur Loop\", action \"Done\"\n- Hidden-preview placeholder: \"Household update\". Android public version: \"Pantopus · Household update\".\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\n- List: NotificationRow, two lines.\n  - A fixed 12pt leading column holds a 6pt unread dot. Read rows keep the empty column. Do not bold or tint unread rows.\n  - A 28pt initials avatar sits before the sentence. System rows (reminders, joins, leaves, guest access ended) keep the 28pt avatar slot empty, so the text stays aligned; draw no glyph in it.\n  - Line 1 starts with the actor.\n  - Line 2 is a middot caption: amount (in-app only) · relative count and date · place label (only for readers with more than one place) · time.\n  - Date reminders end with the ProvenanceMark S of the calendar row they came from, with its word the first time each mark appears: filled = official, hollow = on record, not confirmed, tick = you added this. A reminder for a hollow-mark date starts its title with \"Unconfirmed:\", in the list and in the tray. Bill reminders carry no mark.\n  - Web rows (390 and 1440) have a visible 44px menu button at the trailing edge holding \"Mark as read\" and \"Turn these off\". Native rows expose the same two as custom actions and a long-press menu.\n- Grouped row: ONE row, never three top-level rows. The row body opens Bills › Paid with the three rows highlighted. A trailing 44pt text button \"Show 3\" (\"Show {n}\" for any count) expands the three child rows in place and becomes \"Hide\". Each child row opens its own bill detail.\n- Gone target: when the object has been removed, the row redraws in its gone-target variant with the caption \"That bill was removed.\" Tapping it opens the bill's removed state (web and native alike): \"That bill was removed.\" plus \"Back to notifications\". A removed date row reads \"That date was removed.\"; tapping it opens Today for Larkspur Loop with the inline line \"That date was removed.\" at the top of the 14-day strip and a \"Back to notifications\" link (frame 12).\n- Delivery:\n  - Household activity is quiet. On iOS it is Passive: Notification Center only, no banner, no sound, one thread per home (\"Larkspur Loop\"). On Android it posts on the Household activity channel (LOW): shade only, no heads-up, one group per home with a summary; each child still makes sense alone.\n  - A bill-marked-paid notice is louder only when the bill was due within 3 days at the moment it was marked paid, and only for people who can see bills (they may be about to pay it): on iOS Active in the same thread; on Android on the Dates & bills channel (DEFAULT). Clark was due in 4 days, so this one arrives quietly.\n  - Task finished goes only to the task's creator or assignee. Event added stays quiet.\n  - Push avatars are circular initials. Date and bill reminders are Active / DEFAULT. Pickup goes out only as the evening briefing.\n- Settings (frames 15 Android, 16 iOS): the Household activity group card, matching f4-notification-settings exactly. First row: the master switch \"Household activity\" with the helper \"Quiet — shows in your list, no sound\" directly under it. Then three switches, each with an example line as helper: \"Bills marked paid\" (\"Maya marked Clark PUD paid\"), \"Tasks finished\" (\"Maya finished HVAC filter\"), \"Events added\" (\"Maya added Chimney sweep\"). Group captions: \"Paid notices for bills due within 3 days use your Dates & bills sound.\" and \"With notifications off, these still appear in Notifications.\" One set of switches covers every home; draw no per-home switches. The other four groups appear collapsed by name: Briefings · Air & weather alerts · Dates & bills · Account & security. Muting household activity never mutes security.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- Tapping a row marks it read and opens its object. The destination scrolls once and fades a highlight (300ms). Reduce Motion shows the highlight without the fade. \"Mark as read\" and \"Turn these off\" live in the row menu (web button, native custom actions and long-press). There are no swipe-only actions.\n- Tapping the grouped tray notice opens Bills › Paid with the three rows highlighted, the same as the in-app row body.\n- Resolving an item withdraws its notices. When Maya marks Clark paid, Sam's scheduled reminders for that bill this month are cancelled, and any delivered reminder is replaced by the paid notice in the same thread or group. Marking a date Done stops its later reminders.\n- If the app is open when a notice arrives, show no banner: the bell badge counts up (unread only), and the matching card or row highlights if it is on screen.\n- No tray action on household activity. Date reminders have one action, \"Done\". There is no \"Mark paid\" in the tray, because it would notify the household with no chance to undo.\n- No haptics on arrival.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: NotificationRow (bill_paid, task_completed, home_event_created, date reminder, bill reminder, joined / left, gone target; unread, read, push-off, offline). Deviations from NotificationRow, each recorded on Notes: (1) bill reminders carry no mark, because \"You added this\" is false for a member who didn't add the bill; (2) system rows keep the empty 28pt avatar slot, as Foundations draws it; (3) the grouped row's chevron is replaced by a \"Show 3\" / \"Hide\" text button, because the row body navigates; (4) web rows get a visible 44px menu button for \"Mark as read\" and \"Turn these off\"; (5) titles use the short provider name \"Clark PUD\" and keep the amount on line 2, to meet the 30-character title rule. PushCopy (household and date reminder variants, hidden-preview placeholder, collapsed and expanded tray, lock screen public version); ProvenanceMark; ScopeChip (\"Saved place · Only you\", \"Larkspur Loop · Your household\"); NotificationAsk (household switch → phone prompt; iOS denied → Open Settings); WarmingSkeleton; InlineErrorRow; OfflineNotice; FreshnessLine.\n\nACCESSIBILITY: Each row is one element, read \"Unread. Maya marked Clark PUD paid. 142 dollars 18 cents, due in 4 days, Friday October 23, Larkspur Loop, today.\" The dot's label is \"Unread\". Marks use their spoken names. The avatar is decorative. The grouped row reads its count and whether it is expanded; \"Show 3\" is its own button. Menu items are also custom actions. Targets are 44pt, 48dp and 44px. At AX5 and 200%, captions wrap to three lines and nothing truncates the actor. Unread uses position plus a dot, so it reads in greyscale. Landing highlights also move focus.\n\nCOPY: all row and push strings above, plus: \"Notifications\" · \"Notifications are off for Pantopus. You'll still see these here.\" + \"Turn on\" (iOS denied → \"Open Settings\") · \"That bill was removed.\" + \"Back to notifications\" · \"That date was removed.\" · \"Jenna's guest access ended\" · \"Mark as read\" · \"Turn these off\" · \"Show 3\" / \"Hide\" · \"Checked — nothing new. Household updates and reminders show here.\" · \"We couldn't load notifications. Check your connection, then try again.\" + \"Retry\" · \"You're offline · as of 5:40 PM\" · \"Household activity\" · \"Quiet — shows in your list, no sound\" · \"Bills marked paid\" · \"Tasks finished\" · \"Events added\" · \"Paid notices for bills due within 3 days use your Dates & bills sound.\" · \"With notifications off, these still appear in Notifications.\" · \"Saved place · Only you\" · \"Larkspur Loop · Your household\".\n\nEDGE CASES:\n- Fourteen or more unread rows stay readable because unread is only a dot.\n- A reader with a single place sees no place labels.\n- Long task title: \"Maya finished Replace the upstairs bathroom fan\" wraps in-app and never cuts \"Maya\"; the tray uses the short form above.\n- A 12-bill burst is one row, \"Maya marked 12 bills paid\", with \"Show 12\".\n- A removed bill or date uses the gone-target row and removed state above, never a blank screen.\n- A saved-place reminder opens Today for that saved place, never a home.\n- A member or guest who can't see bills never receives paid notices or bill reminders. Only-you bills never notify.\n- Exactly one paid notice goes to each other person, even after a retry.\n- Hidden previews show \"Household update\".\n- iOS Scheduled Summary may hold Active notices; the in-app row is the guarantee.\n- Offline keeps cached rows. A slow network refreshes in place.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a long title with the caveat at the end, write a title of 30 characters or fewer with the caveat first (\"Unconfirmed: HOA due in 7 days\"), because the tray cuts the end.\n- Instead of a pickup reminder here, rely on the evening briefing, because two notices for one pickup make people switch everything off.\n- Instead of amounts or street numbers in the tray, show them only in-app, because lock screens are visible to others.\n- Instead of a bold or tinted unread row, use the 6pt dot in its fixed column, because a long unread list must stay readable.\n- Instead of stacking three paid notices, update one grouped notice in place, because bursts overwhelm.\n- Instead of nagging wording like \"Sam still hasn't paid\", state only what someone did, with no keeper name or voice, because notices report actions, not blame.\n- Instead of filing household rows under security or system, use the Household activity group, because muting chatter must not mute security.\n- Instead of landing on a generic list when the object exists, open the object, because the notification promised it.\n\nDONE WHEN: Sam's phone stays quiet, yet his list shows Maya's action with her name first and opens the paid bill. No reminder for a paid bill ever reaches him. Every title fits in 30 characters and every body in 40 on both platforms, an unconfirmed date says so first, and every row, including a removed bill or date, lands on its object or on a designed fallback.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f3-household-notifications · ios · 01-unread-list-dense · light — rows 1-7, place labels, marks and legend words.\n2. f3-household-notifications · android · 02-unread-list · light — same content in Material 3.\n3. f3-household-notifications · web-1440 · 03-unread-list · light — list pane beside the sidebar, 44px row menu buttons.\n4. f3-household-notifications · ios · 04-read-later · light — Wed 21 Oct, all read, plus the Priya joined row and the \"Jenna's guest access ended\" row.\n5. f3-household-notifications · ios · 05-grouped-expanded · light — the grouped row collapsed, then expanded to \"Hide\", with callouts: row body → Bills › Paid highlighted; child row → bill detail.\n6. f3-household-notifications · ios · 06-tray-household-passive · light — OS tray (spec): Thu 15 Oct, Notification Center thread with the updated grouped notice, plus the hidden-preview version.\n7. f3-household-notifications · android · 07-tray-household-low · light — OS tray (spec): silent grouped shade entry and the public version \"Pantopus · Household update\".\n8. f3-household-notifications · ios · 08-tray-date-reminder · light — OS tray (spec): lease notice on Mon 15 Feb 2027, \"Tell your landlord by Mon 1 Mar\", expanded with Done, beside its in-app row 12.\n9. f3-household-notifications · android · 09-tray-unconfirmed-reminder · light — OS tray (spec): \"Unconfirmed: HOA due in 7 days\" in the shade on Sun 25 Oct, beside its in-app row with the hollow mark.\n10. f3-household-notifications · ios · 10-landing-resolves · light — row tapped, then the native bill detail Paid state (as drawn in f3-bills-list) with the highlight.\n11. f3-household-notifications · web-390 · 11-landing-bill-gone · light — gone-target row, then the bill's removed state with \"Back to notifications\".\n12. f3-household-notifications · ios · 12-landing-date-gone · light — the gone-target date row (\"That date was removed.\"), then Today for Larkspur Loop with \"That date was removed.\" above the 14-day strip and \"Back to notifications\".\n13. f3-household-notifications · ios · 13-routing-saved-place-vs-home · light — the Cedar Ave row and the Larkspur Loop row with their ScopeChips and their Today destinations.\n14. f3-household-notifications · ios · 14-notifications-off-banner · light — banner above the in-app rows.\n15. f3-household-notifications · android · 15-household-settings-group · light — group card matching f4: master, helper, three switches, both captions, the other four groups.\n16. f3-household-notifications · ios · 16-household-settings-group · light — same group on iOS.\n17. f3-household-notifications · web-1440 · 17-empty · light — \"Checked — nothing new…\".\n18. f3-household-notifications · ios · 18-loading · light — row skeleton.\n19. f3-household-notifications · android · 19-error · light — InlineErrorRow with Retry.\n20. f3-household-notifications · ios · 20-offline · light — cached rows.\n21. f3-household-notifications · ios · 21-ax5 · light — AX5 wrapping.\n22. f3-household-notifications · android · 22-200-percent · light — 200% font.\n23. f3-household-notifications · ios · 23-greyscale · light — frame 1 in greyscale.\n24. f3-household-notifications · ios · 01-unread-list-dense · dark — dark twin of 1.\n25. f3-household-notifications · ios · 06-tray-household-passive · dark — dark twin of 6.\n26. f3-household-notifications · Notes — (a) Name swap from the canonical string (Sam → Maya). (b) Every invented string, listed verbatim: Theo, Jenna and her Tue 20 Oct row, Priya's join, Cedar Ave, the Chimney sweep time, NW Natural, HOA as an on-record unconfirmed date, the tray date Thu 15 Oct, \"Upstairs bathroom fan\", \"Maya finished a task\", the settings example helpers, and every COPY string not in the design doc or contract. (c) Deviations: the five NotificationRow deviations above; the lease push body \"Tell your landlord by Mon 1 Mar\" drops the place label to keep the action within 40 characters (the place stays on the in-app row); the contract's roll-up \"Sam paid 3 bills\" should become \"{actor} marked {n} bills paid\"; the contract's \"Push is off\" string should change to the wording used here; the settings labels \"Bills marked paid\" and \"Tasks finished\" and the helper \"Quiet — shows in your list, no sound\" must be used in f4-notification-settings too. (d) Supersedes design doc F3: bill_paid title \"{actor} marked {provider short} paid\" (30 characters or fewer), push body \"Due {date} · {place}\" with no amount, in-app caption keeps the amount; link /app/homes/{home}/bills/{bill} (grouped: ?segment=paid&linkedIds=); home_event_created title \"{actor} added {title}\". (e) Assumptions: property_tax rules get reminders (not in design doc F5); otherwise swap row 3 for a new-kind date. (f) States described but not drawn: 12-bill burst, long in-app task title, single-place reader without labels, iOS Scheduled Summary holding an Active notice, retry deduplication. (g) Deferred to f4-notification-settings: the double-gate line (push master plus the home reminders switch), save and save-error states, and the per-group OS-state mirror. (h) Product decisions: burst window length; the optional iOS provisional test for this group only; the Android channel choice for due-soon paid notices. Settled: per-home switches are not offered; the \"Link from the first paid notice\" settings entry is cut, because \"Turn these off\" covers it. (i) Engineering notes: add bill_paid, bill reminder, home_event_created and calendar_date to the web notification routing and to the iOS deep-link router; links /app/today?rule={rule} (saved place) and /app/place/today?rule={rule} (home, route may be renamed by the merged Today plan); Android must ship the link-router branches for /bills, /calendar, /place/today?rule= and /today?rule= plus a household channel mapping with this feature, so nothing falls into the system channel or the dashboard; delete the local-state per-home toggles on the web home settings page.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: 1-6, then wait for continue. Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue. Turn 3: 13-18, then wait for continue. Turn 4: 19-24, then wait for continue. Turn 5: 25-26.",
