      {
        "id": "f8-scale-strips",
        "name": "The four-layer reading instrument (scale strips)",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 29,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: The four-layer reading instrument (scale strips) · f8-scale-strips\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Place > Risk & readiness\". This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed. The one change: replace its four separate inline chip rows (flood, wildfire, air, radon) with one ScaleStrip instrument. The same instrument is also used at two other sizes: compare size (390), in the compare arrival header and the compare reveal; and share-card size, in the unfurled share card and in the compare sheet's card preview. On this project, draw it once at all three sizes and in every state below.\n\nATTACH: screenshots of Place > Risk & readiness on iOS, Android and web 1440 (light), and of the /start preview step on web 390 showing the Band-A sections.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852 · Android 412x915 · web 390x844 and 1440x900 (left sidebar). Instrument sizes: detail (full content width; on web 1440 a 640 card in ScaleStrip's two-column layout; rows at least 48pt), compare (390 wide), share-card column (720 of the 1200x630 image; see LAYOUT).\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Place tab > Risk & readiness (web /app/place/risk). Ways in:\n(1) The \"Risk & readiness\" section row on the Place tab. The in-app Risk & readiness detail is reached only this way, once signed in.\n(2) The radon follow-up under the aha card on the signed-out /start preview. It scrolls to the Radon row of the Band-A instrument on /start itself, not to the in-app Risk & readiness screen.\n(3) The /start preview itself, signed out, where the detail size sits in the Band-A sections. The person has just read the seasonal aha and scrolls down; next comes the \"Keep this address handy\" wall.\n(4) The compare arrival header and compare reveal (compare size), and the share card plus the compare sheet's card preview (share-card size).\nNo push or widget opens this screen. On the detail and compare sizes, a row tap opens ProvenanceSheet (\"Where this fact comes from\"). On compare surfaces this is the flow's step 10 (flood row, \"Only FEMA can change this\"). This settles the inventory's \"compare strip tap\" and \"compare Air today row\" entries and v1's \"tap on any scale strip on a shared card\": they open ProvenanceSheet, not Risk & readiness or the Today air band. The share-card size (the unfurled image and the compare sheet's preview) has no taps.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Maya Chen, owner at HOME A, 2418 NE Larkspur Loop, on Mon 19 Oct 2026 at 6:10 PM. Dana's compare card arrived earlier, and Maya wants to know what the four readings mean for her own address. Signed-out and compare frames: Jordan Lee, new at PLACE B, 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas, reading Dana's card (Camas, WA, as of Sat 12 Sep 2026). PLACE B reads the same as the fixture: Zone X, Moderate 3 of 5, AQI 42, Zone 1. The compare sheet minted from his address shows the same values.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Make four readings from four different authorities comparable without inventing a grade or judging a home.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: The eye lands first on the four row names in fixed order (Flood zone · Wildfire hazard potential · Air quality index (AQI) · Radon zone), then on each value line (a word plus a number) with its capsule marker in a named band, then on the source caption under each row. The one action is tapping a row, which opens ProvenanceSheet. The instrument has no buttons.\n\nCONTENT (FIXTURES; deltas below)\nRows, always in this order. Each row is: row name → value line → track → band names → SourceCaption, with a ProvenanceMark S inside the caption. Use these row names at every size except the share card's short forms.\n- Flood zone · \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\" · bands \"Minimal (X)\" · \"0.2% a year (shaded X)\" · \"1% a year or more (A/V zones)\" · caption \"FEMA · area zone · effective Sep 2021\" · Official (filled).\n- Wildfire hazard potential · \"Moderate · 3 of 5\" · bands Very low · Low · Moderate · High · Very high · caption \"USFS · quarter-mile area · 2023\" · Official (filled).\n- Air quality index (AQI) · \"AQI 42 · Good\" · AqiBand with six segments (Good · Moderate · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups · Unhealthy · Very Unhealthy · Hazardous) · caption \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 5:00 PM today\" · Official (filled).\n- Radon zone · \"Zone 1 — highest potential (county)\" · bands \"Zone 3 · low potential\" · \"Zone 2 · moderate potential\" · \"Zone 1 · highest potential\" · caption \"EPA · county-wide estimate — only a test tells you about this home\" · Official (filled).\nLegend, once per surface: \"● Official\" · \"○ On record, not confirmed\" · \"✓ You added this\".\nDeltas:\n- Live air in the default frames is observed 5:00 PM (not the fixture's 7:00 AM). An air row is stale once its observation is more than 3 hours old.\n- Stale caption: \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM — 11 hours ago\", with the ProvenanceMark at full ink.\n- Alert air: \"AQI 118 · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups\", observed 4:00 PM (still fresh).\n- Flood in a 1% zone: \"Zone AE — 1% chance each year (about 1 in 4 over 30 years)\", at 6207 NE 42nd Ave, Vancouver, WA (the flow's second viewer address). A V zone adds the words \"plus coastal wave hazard\" and never gets a fourth band.\n- Street-only address match: the flood row stays FILLED, with the caption \"FEMA · matched to your street, not your parcel · effective Sep 2021\".\n- Frozen sender rows: every caption ends \"as of Sat 12 Sep 2026\"; the frozen air caption reads \"AirNow · on Sat 12 Sep 2026\".\n- Compare header, named: \"Dana · Camas, WA — what's on record for this area\". Anonymous: \"A place in Camas, WA — what's on record for this area\".\n- Share-card sender line (short form, one line): \"Dana · Camas, WA\", or \"A place in Camas, WA\" when anonymous.\n- Collapsed line adds \"on Sat 12 Sep\" to the air item, because frozen readings carry their date. The Foundations collapsed line should be updated to match.\n- Worst case: \"AQI 512 · Hazardous\", with the marker in the \"301+\" segment.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\n- Draw every track exactly as ScaleStrip on the Foundations board: the vertical capsule marker (never a disc), a 2px text.primary outline on the occupied band, and band names under the track. Wildfire prints only the two end names plus the occupied name. Every row has its own track, from least to most hazard, left to right, using only that authority's bands. There is no shared gridline, tick or axis across rows.\n- Flood, wildfire and radon tracks are neutral: surface.raised bands, 1.5px dividers and a keyline in text.secondary ink (3:1 or better). The occupied band is shown by the capsule, the outline and its name printed under the marker in text.primary. Do not give it a raised fill.\n- The Air row is AqiBand's instrument-row variant, the only coloured track: ColorVision Assist hues, equal-width segments with the marker placed by value within its segment, 2px surface gaps and a keyline. Range labels (\"0–50\" … \"301+\") sit under the segments. The category is printed in the value line (\"AQI 42 · Good\"), never on a fill. The row leaves out the EPA health statement; ProvenanceSheet for the air row shows it verbatim.\n- Wildfire keeps \"3 of 5\" because a higher number means more hazard there. Radon is described in words only and never uses \"N of M\".\n- Detail size: 12pt track in a 24pt track zone; row at least 48pt. Web 1440 uses the two-column layout (names, value and caption left 40%; track right 60%).\n- Compare size (390): all four rows stay. Captions shorten to \"FEMA · area zone · Sep 2021\", \"USFS · quarter-mile · 2023\", \"EPA · county-wide estimate\"; air uses two dated captions (below).\n- Compare variant: draw it exactly as ScaleStrip V5. Two same-form triangle pointers on one track: a line \"Dana\" (or \"Their place\" when anonymous) above, and \"You\" below. If both readings share a band, show the \"Same band\" chip and one value line starting \"Both:\". If not, show the \"Different band\" chip and two value lines, \"Dana: …\" and \"You: …\". Air follows V5 too: each pointer is placed by value inside its segment. If both fall in the same segment, show \"Same band\" and \"Both: AQI 42 · Good\", then two caption lines: \"Dana: AirNow · on Sat 12 Sep 2026\" and \"You: AirNow · observed 5:00 PM today\". If two readings share a band but not a provenance, print two value lines, each with its own ProvenanceMark and word, and keep the \"Same band\" chip. The mark always sits beside a value's text, never on a pointer.\n- Share-card size. This deliberately overrides the Foundations ScaleStrip 05-og-column recipe (520 column, one \"Official · …\" footer). Research requires 40px cap height, a dated air row, the full radon wording and a printed word next to every mark, and at 40px cap the rows measure about 530–700px. Where the two differ, draw this recipe, and label the specimen \"Proposed OG column v2 (supersedes 00b 05-og-column)\".\n  - Canvas 1200x630, always the light palette. Padding: 24 top and bottom, 32 left and right. Left column 720 wide, 32 gutter, right \"Yours?\" card 384 wide.\n  - Left column, top to bottom: sender line (40px cap on a 60px line, one line only), 8px gap, then four rows. A row is a 60px text line (40px cap), then a 40px track zone.\n  - Track zone, left to right: a 30px track with the capsule scaled to 8x40, then 8px, then an optional short qualifier at 28px cap, then 8px, then a 28px ProvenanceMark, 8px, and the mark's word at 28px cap (\"Official\", about 160px). The track takes whatever width is left, never less than 200px.\n  - Rows: \"Flood · Minimal (X)\" (no qualifier). \"Wildfire · Moderate\" with qualifier \"3 of 5\". \"Air · Good · AQI 42\" with qualifier \"on Sat 12 Sep\"; the track is AqiBand, and no text sits on a fill. Radon is the one two-line row: \"Radon · Zone 1\" over \"highest potential\", with qualifier \"county-wide\".\n  - Right card: \"Yours?\", \"pantopus.com\", and the sources line \"FEMA · USFS · AirNow · EPA\" at 28px cap, which may wrap to two lines inside the card.\n  - No headline, band names or per-row captions appear in the image. The full approved value strings go in the image's text alternative.\n  - Height budget, printed in the gutter: 24 + 60 + 8 + 3×100 + 160 + 24 = 576, leaving 54px spare.\n  - Unconfirmed token layer (hypothetical; see Notes): the ring mark replaces the disc, and \"On record, not confirmed\" prints at 28px cap on its own 40px line under that row's track. This uses 40 of the 54 spare pixels. If two or more rows are unconfirmed, they show the ring only, and one legend line \"○ On record, not confirmed\" (28px cap, 40px line) sits under the last row.\n  - A long sender name is cut with an ellipsis after the name, and the city is always kept (\"Marie-Marguerite-Sol… · Camas, WA\").\n- Collapsed text line (arrival header under 640px): \"Dana · Camas, WA · Flood X · Wildfire Moderate · Air 42 on Sat 12 Sep · Radon Zone 1 ›\", with no marker glyphs.\n- Missing data never blanks a row, because both compare columns must stay the same length. Draw a greyed track with no marker and \"Not on record\", or one of these distinct states: \"FEMA hasn't mapped flood hazard here\", \"Non-burnable land cover (USFS)\", \"No reading for this address right now\" (air). None of them may look like \"Very low\".\n- Narrow widths (320–360): merge the captions into \"Sources: FEMA, USFS, AirNow, EPA\". The air row still keeps \"today · 5:00 PM\" on its own line.\n- Below the instrument, the host keeps its screening disclaimer and the radon free-kit line unchanged (they belong to the Place section details).\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS: At detail and compare sizes, the whole row is the target; the marker, mark and track are never targets on their own. A tap opens ProvenanceSheet: an iOS medium detent, an Android ModalBottomSheet, a bottom sheet on mobile web, or a centred 560 modal on desktop, always with a visible Close. The sheet's report control depends on the layer: flood \"Only FEMA can change this\" with the LOMA link; wildfire \"Only USFS can change this\" with the link \"USFS Wildfire Hazard Potential ↗\"; radon \"Get a free test kit\"; air \"This reading looks wrong\"; a wrong parcel goes to Pantopus. Arriving from the radon follow-up scrolls once, fades a highlight on the Radon row, and moves accessibility focus there. With Reduce Motion, the highlight appears without animation. If a load takes 1s or more, show the WarmingSkeleton instrument skeleton (keyline and separators only), then cross-fade to values in 300ms or less. Under 1s, show no skeleton. With Reduce Motion, the skeleton is static with no shimmer. There are no haptics, because nothing here is a confirm.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: ScaleStrip (detail, compare, share-card column; no-data, not-studied, non-burnable, frozen, collapsed variants; differs tag; stale air row; AX5) · AqiBand (instrument-row variant) · ProvenanceMark (S on this surface; 28px with its printed word at share-card size) · SourceCaption (dated static, live, frozen token, county scope, street-match scope, collapsed sources) · ProvenanceSheet · FreshnessLine (per-fact stale) · WarmingSkeleton (instrument skeleton) · InlineErrorRow · OfflineNotice · ScopeChip (host header only).\n\nACCESSIBILITY: Reading order: legend, then Flood, Wildfire, Air, Radon. Each row is one element with a spoken label, for example:\n- \"Flood zone X, minimal flood hazard, scale Minimal to 1% a year or more. FEMA, area zone, effective September 2021. Official.\"\n- \"Wildfire hazard potential: Moderate, 3 of 5, scale Very low to Very high. USFS, quarter-mile area, 2023. Official.\"\n- \"Air quality index 42, Good, category 1 of 6. AirNow, observed 5 PM today. Official.\"\n- Street-matched row: \"Flood zone X, minimal flood hazard, scale Minimal to 1% a year or more. FEMA, matched to your street, not your parcel, effective September 2021. Official.\"\nEvery row has the custom action \"Where this fact comes from\". Summary sentence (web text alternative and native group label): \"Flood Zone X, minimal flood hazard. Wildfire Moderate, 3 of 5. Air AQI 42, Good, today. Radon Zone 1, county-wide.\" The rows are the text list. Targets: 44pt iOS, 48dp Android, 44px web. Meaning comes from position, the outline and the printed name, so every frame must read in greyscale. At AX5, text sits above a full-width track and values wrap, never truncate. The share card's text alternative lists all four full values, marks and sources, with no address.\n\nCOPY: The strings in CONTENT, plus: \"What's on record here\" (instrument heading), \"Retry air quality\", \"We couldn't reach AirNow just now\", \"You're offline · as of 5:40 PM\", \"Only USFS can change this\", \"USFS Wildfire Hazard Potential ↗\". Use \"hazard\" or \"potential\" as the authority does. Always write \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\", never \"minimal risk\" or \"100-year\".\n\nEDGE CASES\n- The longest host header is \"2418 NE Larkspur Loop, Vancouver, WA 98684\" plus ScopeChip \"Your household\", and it wraps.\n- A saved place (PLACE B) shows the same instrument; only the host chip changes, to \"Saved place · Only you\". Signed out on /start, it is the same with no chip. For a viewer with several homes, the block header names the address.\n- At AQI 512 the marker sits in \"301+\". The AE value is the longest and wraps to two lines.\n- If one provider fails, only that row shows InlineErrorRow; the other rows stay live.\n- Offline: rows stay cached with their age in words.\n- Slow network: the skeleton holds the final height.\n- Street-only match: the flood row stays filled; the scope words in the caption carry the limit.\n- A frozen token layer that was unconfirmed when minted (hypothetical) stays hollow with its words on every compare surface.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of letter grades, a score or stars, draw four separate authority tracks — because four unlike labels on one invented scale turn a public record into a report card on someone's home.\n- Instead of a radar chart, draw stacked rows — because a radar normalises unlike axes and its area reads as \"worse home\".\n- Instead of a green-to-red ramp on every track, colour only the air row, in EPA hues — because a shared ramp is a grade by another name, and EPA requires consistent AQI colours.\n- Instead of four flood bands (X · shaded X · AE · VE), draw three by annual chance — because AE and VE share the same 1% chance and are not successive steps.\n- Instead of a hollow mark on a FEMA, USFS or EPA row, draw it filled with a scope caption — because the dataset is official and its limit is scope, not doubt.\n- Instead of a raised fill on the occupied band, draw a 2px outline plus the printed name — because raised on base is 1.05:1 and invisible to low-vision readers.\n- Instead of \"Air today\" on a frozen card, write the date in the caption (\"Dana: AirNow · on Sat 12 Sep 2026\") — because a frozen reading is not today's.\n- Instead of sorting rows by difference, keep the fixed order — because a label works when facts sit in the same place every time.\n\nDONE WHEN: No grade, score or verdict appears anywhere. Radon reads as a county-wide estimate, not a claim about the home. All four rows appear in the same order at all three sizes, each with a word, a number and an \"authority · scope · as-of\" caption (or the sources line at share-card size). The tracks match the Foundations ScaleStrip anatomy. Every greyscale frame still reads. Frozen and live air carry different dates. A missing layer keeps its row. Official layers are always filled. The share-card column fits the printed 630 budget, with no row text under 40px cap and no word or qualifier under 28px cap.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f8-scale-strips · ios · 01-detail-all-four · light — Risk & readiness at HOME A: all four rows, the legend, air observed 5:00 PM, and the host disclaimer.\n2. f8-scale-strips · web-1440 · 02-three-sizes · light — specimens of the detail, compare (390) and full 1200x630 share-card sizes (labelled \"Proposed OG column v2 (supersedes 00b 05-og-column)\", with the height budget in the gutter), plus the collapsed text line. Under the detail and compare sizes, one extra street-matched flood row, filled, with the scope caption.\n3. f8-scale-strips · ios · 03-no-data-states · light — \"FEMA hasn't mapped flood hazard here\", \"Non-burnable land cover (USFS)\", \"No reading for this address right now\", radon \"Not on record\", and a Wildfire Very low row for contrast.\n4. f8-scale-strips · ios · 04-air-alert-and-stale · light — three air rows: AQI 118 at 4:00 PM, the stale 7:00 AM row (\"— 11 hours ago\"), and AQI 512 in \"301+\".\n5. f8-scale-strips · web-390 · 05-compare-same-band · light — Jordan (PLACE B) vs Dana, all filled. Every row shows \"Same band\" and a \"Both:\" value line; the air row has the two dated captions.\n6. f8-scale-strips · web-390 · 06-compare-different-band · light — an anonymous card (\"Their place\") vs a viewer at 6207 NE 42nd Ave. The viewer has Zone AE, wildfire Moderate 3 of 5, air AQI 42 observed 5:00 PM and radon Zone 1 (specimen values), so only Flood reads \"Different band\", with two value lines.\n7. f8-scale-strips · ios · 07-flood-scope-and-unconfirmed-specimen · light — the AE value wrapping; the HOME A street-matched flood row, filled, with its scope caption; then, gutter-labelled \"Hypothetical token confidence specimen — not a FEMA state; contract decision pending\": a compare row that shares a band but not a provenance (\"Dana: Zone X — minimal flood hazard\" with the ring and \"On record, not confirmed\"; \"You: Zone X — minimal flood hazard\" filled; \"Same band\" chip), and the same layer at share-card size with its word line.\n8. f8-scale-strips · ios · 08-row-tap-provenance-sheet · light — the radon row tapped, ProvenanceSheet at a medium detent, \"Get a free test kit\".\n9. f8-scale-strips · web-390 · 09-loading-and-partial-error · light — the instrument skeleton, then the air row showing \"We couldn't reach AirNow just now\" with \"Retry air quality\".\n10. f8-scale-strips · web-390 · 10-offline · light — cached rows under \"You're offline · as of 5:40 PM\".\n11. f8-scale-strips · web-390 · 11-narrow-320 · light — drawn 320 wide, with \"Sources: FEMA, USFS, AirNow, EPA\" and air keeping \"today · 5:00 PM\".\n12. f8-scale-strips · android · 12-detail-all-four · light — the Material 3 host with 48dp rows.\n13. f8-scale-strips · web-1440 · 13-risk-detail-desktop · light — /app/place/risk with the sidebar, the instrument in a 640 two-column card.\n14. f8-scale-strips · ios · 14-ax5 · light — text above full-width tracks, everything wrapping.\n15. f8-scale-strips · ios · 15-greyscale · light — frame 1 in greyscale, with a caption naming the non-colour cue per row.\n16. f8-scale-strips · ios · 16-detail-all-four · dark — dark twin of 1, keyline visible on the dark base.\n17. f8-scale-strips · web-1440 · 17-three-sizes · dark — dark twin of 2; the share-card specimen stays in the light palette on the dark board.\n18. f8-scale-strips · ios · 18-no-data-states · dark — dark twin of 3.\n19. f8-scale-strips · ios · 19-air-alert-and-stale · dark — dark twin of 4; maroon and purple segments keep 3:1 through the keyline.\n20. f8-scale-strips · web-390 · 20-compare-same-band · dark — dark twin of 5.\n21. f8-scale-strips · web-390 · 21-compare-different-band · dark — dark twin of 6.\n22. f8-scale-strips · ios · 22-flood-scope-and-unconfirmed-specimen · dark — dark twin of 7; the ring holds 3:1 on the dark base; the share-card specimen stays light.\n23. f8-scale-strips · ios · 23-row-tap-provenance-sheet · dark — dark twin of 8.\n24. f8-scale-strips · web-390 · 24-loading-and-partial-error · dark — dark twin of 9.\n25. f8-scale-strips · web-390 · 25-offline · dark — dark twin of 10.\n26. f8-scale-strips · ios · 26-ax5 · dark — dark twin of 14.\n27. f8-scale-strips · android · 27-detail-all-four · dark — dark twin of 12.\n28. f8-scale-strips · web-1440 · 28-risk-detail-desktop · dark — dark twin of 13.\n29. f8-scale-strips · Notes — The Notes artboard lists:\n- Blocking dependency (founder task): update 00b 05-og-column and the component contract's OG column to the 720 recipe before f8-og-compare-card and f8-compare-sheet are drawn. Until then, this project's \"Proposed OG column v2\" wins.\n- Measured share-card budget: 24 + 60 + 8 + 3×100 + 160 + 24 = 576 of 630; 54px spare for one unconfirmed word line (40px). Row text lines measure about 530–700px at 40px cap; words and qualifiers are 28px cap; track never under 200px.\n- Contract and Foundations deviations:\n  - The sources line moved from a full-width footer to the right card, and each row prints its own mark and \"Official\".\n  - Collapsed line \"Air 42 on Sat 12 Sep\" is proposed to replace the contract's \"Air 42\" and the flow's \"Air on Sep 12 · 42\"; 00b V10 should be updated.\n  - Row names follow 00b (\"Wildfire hazard potential\", \"Air quality index (AQI)\") instead of the research note's \"Wildfire hazard\" and \"Air today\"; \"today\" moves into the live caption.\n  - Hypothetical unconfirmed token layer (frames 7 and 22): the contract says official datasets are never hollow. The token's confidence field is shown only as a labelled specimen and needs a product decision.\n  - The two-or-more unconfirmed rows legend line uses 00b's C14 in-block legend instead of a word per glyph.\n- Assumptions: stale threshold for air is 3 hours; live air is observed 5:00 PM; Jordan's live air equals Dana's 42, so the compare sheet (Zone X, AQI 42 from PLACE B) agrees; Zone AE belongs to the flow's 6207 NE 42nd Ave viewer, not PLACE B; detail- and compare-size row taps open ProvenanceSheet, which resolves the inventory's compare entries; the share-card size has no taps; the air row leaves out the EPA statement and ProvenanceSheet carries it.\n- Invented strings: heading \"What's on record here\", the street-match caption, \"Their place\", the anonymous header and sender lines, the compare captions, the share-card short forms and qualifiers (\"Flood · Minimal (X)\", \"Wildfire · Moderate\", \"Air · Good · AQI 42\", \"on Sat 12 Sep\", \"Radon · Zone 1\", \"highest potential\", \"county-wide\"), \"Only USFS can change this\", \"USFS Wildfire Hazard Potential ↗\", the collapsed air item, the AQI 512 and Zone AE deltas, frame 6's specimen values, \"Retry air quality\", and the offline time.\n- Dark frames left out: narrow-320 (same tokens as 24–25) and greyscale (not meaningful in dark).\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: 1-6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 3: 13-18, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 4: 19-24, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 5: 25-29.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Street-matched FEMA flood row is now FILLED with the scope caption 'FEMA · matched to your street, not your parcel · effective Sep 2021'; hollow survives only as a labelled hypothetical token-confidence specimen in frames 7/22, logged as a contract decision (review major; component-contract ProvenanceMark doNot; per-surface change).",
          "Frame 5 is all filled; the unconfirmed compare row moved to frame 7 and frame 6 now lists the viewer's full specimen values (review minor).",
          "Rebuilt the share-card recipe with a measured budget: 24/32 padding, 60px sender line (short form 'Dana · Camas, WA' / 'A place in Camas, WA'), 100px rows (radon 160), 28px-cap qualifiers ('3 of 5', 'on Sat 12 Sep', 'county-wide') and mark words, a track never under 200px, the sources line in the right card, an unconfirmed word on its own line using the 54px spare, a legend line for two or more, and ellipsis for a long name (review majors on geometry).",
          "Share-card recipe is explicitly labelled 'Proposed OG column v2 (supersedes 00b 05-og-column)', and the Notes now carry a blocking founder task to update 00b and the contract (review majors).",
          "Track anatomy now defers to Foundations ScaleStrip: capsule marker, 2px outline, band names under the track, Air as AqiBand instrument row with range labels and the category in the value line; removed 'beside the marker/track' (review major vs 00b).",
          "Compare variant now follows ScaleStrip V5: 'Dana'/'You' pointer lines, 'Both:' value line, Air same-band merge with two dated captions, and a rule for a shared band with different provenance; INSTEAD OF line updated (review major).",
          "Sizes and interaction fixed: compare size = arrival header and reveal; share-card size = share card and the compare sheet preview, with no taps; ProvenanceSheet only at detail and compare sizes (review major).",
          "Row names unified to the 00b labels ('Wildfire hazard potential', 'Air quality index (AQI)'); 'today' moved into the live caption; removed the false Notes claim and the 'spell out AQI once' line (review major/minor).",
          "Radon band labels now read '… potential'; the stale caption uses the 00b wording with the mark at full ink; both removed from invented strings (review minor).",
          "The summary sentence now uses the 00b form plus 'today'; flood spoken labels add the scale endpoints and 'minimal flood hazard' (review minors).",
          "Added the wildfire ProvenanceSheet control 'Only USFS can change this' with a USFS link, listed as an invented string (review minor).",
          "Clarified that the radon follow-up scrolls to the Band-A instrument on /start, not to the in-app screen (review minor).",
          "The loading step now follows WarmingSkeleton: a skeleton only for loads of 1s or more, and none under 1s (review minor).",
          "The Notes now list the deviations: the collapsed dated air item (proposed replacement for the contract and flow variants), the row-name source, the Air same-band handling, and the sources-line move (review minors).",
          "Kept all v1 substance: fixed order, three flood bands, V-zone words, frozen captions, missing-data states, narrow-width sources, AX5, greyscale, dark twins, 29 artboards and the batch plan."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f8-compare-sheet",
        "name": "Compare with a friend (mint + consent)",
        "platforms": [
          "web"
        ],
        "isNew": true,
        "frameCount": 18,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Compare with a friend · f8-compare-sheet\n\nTYPE: NEW sheet over the existing, already-designed /start preview step. Keep that host screen exactly as it is, with one change: a TextActionRow under the aha card holding \"Share this address\" · \"Compare with a friend\", with the caption \"Compare cards show readings and your city, never your address.\" The caption speaks only about compare, because \"Share this address\" shares a link that contains the address. \"Share this address\" moves out of the WallBar footer into this row, so it appears once. The footer keeps only its app-download link.\n\nATTACH: screenshots of the /start preview step at web 390 and 1440 (light), and of the compare reveal step if one exists.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: Web only. Mobile web 390x844 is the primary case, drawn as a bottom sheet. Desktop 1440x900 is a centred modal 480 wide. Native apps have no sheet; their anonymous compare card belongs to the native share-and-compare surface.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: /start is the signed-out door before Place · Today · Nearby · Mail. The sheet is the same for signed-in viewers. It is reachable only from the preview step, never from the hero, because a card needs a finished preview.\nWays in:\n1. \"Compare with a friend\" in the TextActionRow under the aha card, with or without a ?vs= link.\n2. \"Send yours back\" on the compare reveal at /start?vs=<token>. The sheet receives the address the person typed on /start in this browser and makes the card from it.\nThe WallBar footer has no compare link; this settles the inventory's \"WallBar footer (demoted)\" entry. The sheet has no URL of its own. It hands off to the system share sheet or the clipboard, and from there to the messenger unfurl (the compare share card): the image, the title line and the description line.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Jordan Lee, 36, moved from Portland to PLACE B (1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas) on Fri 9 Oct and saved it on Sat 10 Oct from his laptop. On Mon 19 Oct at 6:10 PM he is on his iPhone, signed out. He opened Dana's compare link (Camas, WA, card as of Sat 12 Sep 2026), typed his address and saw both readings. Frames 1–4 show the sheet opened from \"Compare with a friend\" under his own preview. Frame 5 is the reciprocal moment, from \"Send yours back\". He wants to send his card without giving away his street.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Mint and send a compare link in one tap, showing exactly what the card will and will not reveal before anything is sent.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: The eye lands first on the card preview at true share proportions, then on the privacy line directly beneath it, then on the name toggle. The single primary action comes last: \"Share\" on mobile, \"Copy link\" on desktop.\n\nCONTENT (FIXTURES; deltas below). Draw these top to bottom:\n1. Title \"Compare with a friend\" and a visible Close.\n2. A line for the sender only, outside the card: \"Made from 1107 NE Birchfield Ct. The address stays off the card.\"\n3. The card preview, drawn as it will unfurl: the 1.91:1 image (1200x630 scaled to full sheet width), then the title line, then the description line with \"pantopus.com\". This preview uses the proposed OG column v2 (720 wide, 40px cap height, a printed word next to each mark), which supersedes the Foundations 05-og-column recipe. If the two differ, draw this one. If that layout crops or drops text, the preview shows the same.\n   - Image, light palette always. Padding 24 top and bottom, 32 left and right. Left column 720 wide, from the top:\n     - the sender line \"A place in Camas, WA\" (40px cap, one line)\n     - four ScaleStrip share-card rows, each a 60px text line at 40px cap over a 40px track zone: \"Flood · Minimal (X)\"; \"Wildfire · Moderate\"; \"Air · Good · AQI 42\" as a text line above its track, where the track uses the AqiBand hues and the text is never on a fill; and radon on two lines, \"Radon · Zone 1\" over \"highest potential\"\n     - in each track zone: a 30px track with the scaled capsule marker, then a short qualifier at 28px cap where the row has one (\"3 of 5\", \"on Mon 19 Oct\", \"county-wide\"), then a 28px filled ProvenanceMark and the word \"Official\" at 28px cap\n   - Image, right column (384 wide): a filled prompt card reading \"Yours?\" and \"pantopus.com\", then the sources line \"FEMA · USFS · AirNow · EPA\" at 28px cap, which may wrap to two lines. The image holds no headline.\n   - Title line (anonymous): \"What's on record at a place in Camas, WA. Yours?\"\n   - Description line, clamped to two lines with an ellipsis at a word boundary, as messengers do: \"Online or mail voter registration for Tue 3 Nov must arrive by Mon 26 Oct in Washington. FEMA, USFS, AirNow and EPA. Nextdoor is what your neighbors say. Pantopus is what's on record about your address.\"\n4. Privacy line: \"This card shows readings and your city, never your address. Anyone with the link can see this card until Sat 19 Dec.\"\n5. Toggle, off by default: \"Show my first name on the card\". When it is on, a \"First name\" field appears, empty, with focus. In frame 2 \"Jordan\" is typed with the caret, and the preview changes to \"Jordan · Camas, WA\" with the title \"What's on record at Jordan's place. Yours?\"\n6. URL row: \"pantopus.com/start?vs=eyJ2IjoxLCJjIjoiQ2FtYXM…\" with the caption \"Link works for 61 days · until Sat 19 Dec\". On mobile, the row also has a \"Copy link\" text button.\n7. Primary button: \"Share\" (mobile) or \"Copy link\" (desktop).\nReciprocal variant:\n- Title: \"Send yours back\".\n- Made-from line: \"Made from 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, the address you just typed. The address stays off the card.\"\n- Mobile button: \"Send my card\".\n- Everything else stays unchanged and visible, including the privacy line and the toggle.\nWorst case: the 24-character first name \"Marie-Marguerite-Solange\", the 81-character headline \"Property tax 2nd half is due Mon 2 Nov in Clark County. It moved from Sat 31 Oct.\", and an inline mint error.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION: The preview is the top of the sheet, at the size and proportions it will unfurl in a messenger. Never shrink it to a thumbnail or an icon. It renders exactly the token's contents and nothing more: no street, map, pin, coordinates or house image, even blurred. State precision in words (\"your city\"); a map centred on a home gives the home away. A first name plus a small city plus a rare reading can narrow a location. That is why the name toggle is off by default and the preview is the exact token. The card image inside the preview always uses the light palette, in dark frames too; only the sheet chrome and the unfurl text lines follow the theme. The preview has no taps. The privacy line sits directly under the preview. The toggle sits between the privacy line and the button, because it is the only control that changes what the card reveals. The button is last. At 390x844 (large detent), in the idle state, everything from the title to the button fits without scrolling. If the sheet must scroll (name field shown, 200% text, errors), the privacy line stays above the button.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- The link is minted as soon as the sheet opens, and minted again (debounced) when the toggle or name changes. The preview updates at once with a cross-fade of 150ms or less.\n- If minting takes 1 second or more, a small spinner shows on the URL row and Share is disabled, with \"Making your link…\" under it. Under 1 second, no indicator appears.\n- Share is enabled only once the link exists, so a tap opens the system share sheet with no network wait.\n- After a mint error, Share stays disabled with \"Share needs a link first.\" under it, and \"Try again\" sits in the InlineErrorRow.\n- Desktop \"Copy link\": the button reads \"Link copied\" for 18 seconds, with no visible countdown. The URL row keeps a tick and the word \"Copied\" until the link changes.\n- Mobile browsers without system sharing make \"Copy link\" the primary, and the URL row then drops its own Copy link button.\n- Cancelling the share sheet, or having no share targets, returns to ready with the neutral status \"Link ready. Share it again or copy it.\" and Copy link visible. No error glyph appears.\n- The toggle is a web switch (role=switch, 44px row) with the word On or Off printed beside it.\n- Escape, Close and the browser Back action close the sheet. The sheet slides in within 300ms, or fades with Reduce Motion. The web has no haptics.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: TextActionRow (host entry and compare-scoped caption; minting, copied, cancelled and offline states) · ScaleStrip (share-card size, proposed OG column v2, inside the preview) · AqiBand · ProvenanceMark (28px with printed words) · SourceCaption (collapsed sources line) · InlineErrorRow · OfflineNotice.\n\nACCESSIBILITY: Reading order: title (the dialog is labelled by it and focus lands on it), made-from line, preview image, unfurl title and description, privacy line, toggle, name field, URL row, button, Close. The preview image's text alternative (also the card's image description) is \"Card preview: A place in Camas, WA. Flood zone X, minimal flood hazard, official. Wildfire hazard potential moderate, 3 of 5, official. Air on Monday 19 October, AQI 42, Good, official. Radon zone 1, highest potential, county-wide, official. Sources: FEMA, USFS, AirNow, EPA. Yours?\" The sheet traps focus. On close, focus returns to the control that opened it (\"Compare with a friend\" or \"Send yours back\"). \"Link copied\", \"Making your link…\", errors and the cancelled status are polite status messages. Targets are 44px with 8px gaps. The toggle shows its state by position and the words On and Off, not colour alone. At 200% text the sheet scrolls, text wraps, and the preview stays full width. Selection looks different from focus.\n\nCOPY: The strings in CONTENT, plus:\n- \"We couldn't make your link. Check your connection, then try again.\" with \"Try again\"\n- \"Lots of links from this network in the last minute. Try again in a minute.\"\n- \"You're offline. Compare needs a connection.\"\n- \"Share needs a link first.\"\n- \"Making your link…\"\n- \"Link copied\"\n- \"Copied\"\n- \"Link ready. Share it again or copy it.\"\n\nEDGE CASES\n- Worst case: the long name is cut with an ellipsis after the name so the image's sender line stays on one line (\"Marie-Marguerite-Sol… · Camas, WA\"); the city is always kept. The sources line stays in the image, and no row, qualifier or mark word is dropped. The unfurl title line wraps in full. The 81-character headline sits in the description line (clamped to two lines, never cut mid-word) and never enters the image.\n- With the worst case plus an inline error, the sheet may scroll on mobile, but the privacy line stays above the button.\n- Signed-in and signed-out viewers see the same sheet.\n- Slow network: the spinner stays on the URL row, and the preview is never blanked.\n- Rate limit: a neutral clock glyph, not error styling.\n- Offline: the preview still renders from the loaded preview. Share and Copy are disabled, with the reason shown.\n- A layer with no data shows \"Not on record\" in its row.\n- A token layer minted as unconfirmed (hypothetical) shows the ring mark, with \"On record, not confirmed\" at 28px cap on its own line under that row's track, never a filled \"Official\". Official public layers are always filled.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of putting the privacy line after the button, place it directly under the preview — because consent read after the link exists is retroactive.\n- Instead of minting on the Share tap, pre-mint when the sheet opens — because the browser only allows sharing straight from a tap.\n- Instead of a red \"Share failed\" after a cancel, return to ready with Copy link visible — because a cancel and \"no targets\" look the same to the browser.\n- Instead of turning the name toggle on by default, leave it off — because a name plus a small city plus a rare reading can narrow a location.\n- Instead of \"Air today\" on the card, write \"on Mon 19 Oct\" in the air row — because the friend opens it days later.\n- Instead of a third link in the WallBar footer, keep compare in the TextActionRow under the aha — because a third footer link becomes a cramped 3-up row on a phone.\n- Instead of packing the headline and captions into the image, keep the image to layer names, band words, short qualifiers, marks with words, the sender line, the sources line and \"Yours?\" — because image text is unreadable at bubble size.\n- Instead of a generic error for rate limiting, give it its own wording with a time — because the person did nothing wrong.\n\nDONE WHEN: The person reads what the card shows before anything is sent. The preview shows exactly the token and nothing more, in the light palette, matching the share card. Share opens with no wait. A cancel reads as neutral. The reciprocal variant makes clear which address the card comes from, while that address never appears on the card. The compare caption makes no claim about \"Share this address\". Official layers are filled, and a hypothetical unconfirmed layer looks unconfirmed and fits its row. Every frame reads in greyscale.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f8-compare-sheet · web-390 · 01-idle · light — pre-minted, anonymous card, toggle off, Share enabled.\n2. f8-compare-sheet · web-390 · 02-name-shown · light — toggle On, \"Jordan\" typed with the caret, preview \"Jordan · Camas, WA\", title line updated.\n3. f8-compare-sheet · web-390 · 03-minting · light — spinner on the URL row; Share disabled with \"Making your link…\".\n4. f8-compare-sheet · web-390 · 04-share-sheet-open · light — the system share sheet over the dimmed sheet.\n5. f8-compare-sheet · web-390 · 05-reciprocal-send-yours-back · light — title \"Send yours back\", \"Send my card\", the typed-address made-from line; the privacy line and toggle are visible and unchanged.\n6. f8-compare-sheet · web-1440 · 06-desktop-idle · light — the centred 480 modal over /start, with \"Copy link\"; the host's TextActionRow with the compare caption is visible behind the scrim.\n7. f8-compare-sheet · web-1440 · 07-copied · light — \"Link copied\", and the URL row showing \"Copied\".\n8. f8-compare-sheet · web-390 · 08-share-cancelled · light — the neutral ready status, with Copy link visible.\n9. f8-compare-sheet · web-390 · 09-mint-error · light — InlineErrorRow with Try again; Share disabled with \"Share needs a link first.\"; preview kept.\n10. f8-compare-sheet · web-390 · 10-rate-limited · light — the clock glyph and its own copy.\n11. f8-compare-sheet · web-390 · 11-offline · light — preview shown; actions disabled with the reason.\n12. f8-compare-sheet · web-390 · 12-worst-case · light — the 24-character name cut with an ellipsis in the image's sender line, the sources line still in the image, the 81-character headline clamped in the description, and an inline error; the privacy line stays above the button.\n13. f8-compare-sheet · web-390 · 13-unconfirmed-token-specimen · light — gutter label \"Hypothetical: a token layer minted with confidence 'unconfirmed' — shown on the flood row only to test the fit; not a FEMA state\". That row shows the ring and \"On record, not confirmed\" on its own line under its track; the other rows stay filled.\n14. f8-compare-sheet · web-390 · 14-200pct · light — frame 1 at 200% text, scrolling, privacy line above the button.\n15. f8-compare-sheet · web-390 · 15-greyscale · light — frame 2 in greyscale.\n16. f8-compare-sheet · web-390 · 16-idle · dark — dark twin of 1; the card image stays light.\n17. f8-compare-sheet · web-390 · 17-mint-error · dark — dark twin of 9; the card image stays light.\n18. f8-compare-sheet · Notes — The Notes artboard lists:\n- Dependencies: depends on 00b 05-og-column (and the contract's OG column) being updated to the 720 recipe; until then this prompt wins. The move of \"Share this address\" from the WallBar footer into the TextActionRow conflicts with the derive proposal that kept it in the footer; the f8-seasonal-aha and WallBar prompts need the same change before build.\n- Flow-05 state map: 1 idle → 01, 2 name shown → 02, 7 share sheet opened → 04, 9 reciprocal → 05.\n- Sender recast to Jordan at PLACE B to match the house-style fixtures; flow-05 steps 2–4 (Maya, \"Maya · Camas, WA\") and 11–12 (Jordan, Vancouver) are represented by frames 01–05 with names and cities swapped.\n- Assumptions: Sat 19 Dec is an example expiry (61 days); the token lifetime is a product decision. The WallBar compare entry is resolved as absent. The anonymous title \"What's on record at a place in Camas, WA. Yours?\" matches the share card's anonymous state and is proposed to replace the flow's \"A place in Vancouver, WA · Yours?\". The design doc's footer contrast line now lives in the description line, per the image-text research. The headline moved out of the image. The sources line sits in the right card. Frame 13 is a hypothetical token and a contract deviation pending decision.\n- Engineering note: Share and Copy link taps fire t0_share_clicked with meta.method 'compare'.\n- Invented strings: the made-from lines, the TextActionRow caption \"Compare cards show readings and your city, never your address.\", the unfurl title and description lines, the status and error copy, \"Link ready. Share it again or copy it.\", \"Link works for 61 days · until Sat 19 Dec\", the worst-case name and headline, the short row forms and qualifiers, and the ellipsised sender line.\n- Omitted states: none.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: 1-6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 3: 13-18.",
        "changeLog": [
          "TextActionRow caption is scoped to compare ('Compare cards show readings and your city, never your address.') because 'Share this address' shares the address (review major; design doc §3).",
          "Frame 13 is now a labelled generic unconfirmed-token specimen, not a FEMA state; official layers are always filled; the unconfirmed word goes on its own line so it fits (review major).",
          "Preview image now uses the explicit 'proposed OG column v2' recipe from f8-scale-strips, which supersedes 00b 05-og-column; the Notes record the dependency (review major).",
          "Air row reworded: a text line above its track, with AqiBand hues on the track and no text on a fill; the date moved to the 28px qualifier 'on Mon 19 Oct' (review major and minor).",
          "Image rows updated to the measured short forms and qualifiers ('Wildfire · Moderate' + '3 of 5', 'Air · Good · AQI 42' + 'on Mon 19 Oct', 'Radon · Zone 1' / 'highest potential' + 'county-wide'); the text alternative updated to 'wildfire hazard potential'.",
          "Worst case keeps the sources line in the image by cutting the sender name with an ellipsis and keeping the city (review minor; research-findings).",
          "Named the analytics event: t0_share_clicked with meta.method 'compare' (review minor; inventory).",
          "Worst-case headline now ends with a full stop: 'Property tax 2nd half is due Mon 2 Nov in Clark County. It moved from Sat 31 Oct.' (81 characters, counted), and is listed on Notes (review minors).",
          "The description line in the preview clamps to two lines, and the privacy line stays above the button whenever the sheet scrolls (review minor).",
          "URL caption now reads 'Link works for 61 days · until Sat 19 Dec' (review minor; house-style relative-date rule).",
          "Reading order now starts with the title and ends with Close (review minor).",
          "Notes add: the flow-05 state map, the persona recast explanation, the WallBar/seasonal-aha change needed before build, and the derive-proposal conflict (review minors).",
          "Kept all v1 substance: pre-mint, debounced re-mint, spinner timing, synchronous share, neutral cancel, 18s Link copied, rate-limit and offline states, reciprocal variant, light-only card image, 18 artboards and the batch plan."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f8-compare-arrival-header",
        "name": "Compare arrival header on /start",
        "platforms": [
          "web"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 17,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Compare arrival header on /start · f8-compare-arrival-header\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"/start funnel — hero step\". This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed.\n- Keep: the page header, the H1 \"See what's true about your address.\", the lede, the page footer with its app-download link, and the sticky WallBar (signed out).\n- Move: the hero's address field, \"See your place\" button and privacy proof line move into the \"Your place\" column (at 640px and wider) or sit directly under the \"Your place\" heading (below 640px). There is exactly one address field on the page, in every frame.\n- Add: a compare header for visitors who arrive from a friend's link.\n\nATTACH: (1) /start hero step, signed out, at 390 and at 1440. (2) The same hero showing the \"from the card in your mailbox\" pill, whose position this header takes. (3) The /start page header in its signed-in form, if one exists. (4) The Foundations board frames for ScaleStrip (03-compare, including V9 and V10), SourceCaption and LandingBannerSlot (V5).\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: Web only. The main case is 390x844, because nearly every compare link is opened on a phone from a chat app. Also draw 1440x900, and one 360-wide frame for the merged sources line. The layout changes at 640px: below 640 the sender's card collapses to one line; at 640 and wider the page shows two equal columns.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Outside the four tabs. /start is the signed-out entry page in front of Place · Today · Nearby · Mail. Entry points: (a) tapping the unfurled compare share card in iMessage, WhatsApp, Slack or SMS; (b) a link in an email or DM; (c) a pasted or typed link. All three open https://pantopus.com/start?vs=<token>. (d) https://pantopus.com/start?vs=<token>&address=<address> submits on its own, skips this header and lands on the compare reveal. The previous step, the compare share card, hands over only what the token holds: an optional first name, a city, four readings frozen on the day the card was made, a headline of 90 characters or fewer, and an expiry date. No address, no coordinates. The next step is the compare reveal, which receives the typed address and keeps Dana's rows in the same order. A submit whose address can't be placed also goes to the compare reveal, which owns that failure (its no-match state keeps Dana's card and lets the visitor fix the address in place); this page draws no no-match state. If the viewer has the Pantopus app installed, the link still opens this web page, so the footer's app-download link stays.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Jordan Lee, 36, moved from Portland to PLACE B (1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas) on Fri 9 Oct. It is Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM, and he is on the bus home. Dana (FRIEND C) texts him her compare card. He saved PLACE B on his laptop, where he is signed in; on his phone's browser he is signed out.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Show a stranger what is on record where their friend lives, and leave their own address field as the only obvious next move.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS (390): first, the one-line summary of Dana's card at the top of the page; second, the focused, empty address field under \"Your place\"; third, the \"See your place\" button, the single primary action.\n\nCONTENT: Use the FIXTURES for Dana's card. Deltas for this surface:\n- Sender line: \"Dana · Camas, WA\". Subline: \"What's on record for this area\". Freshness line (one for the whole card): \"Dana's card · as of Sat 12 Sep\".\n- Rows, always in this order, each with a filled ProvenanceMark (all four are official); the legend \"● Official\" appears once. Layer labels are the Foundations labels:\n  - \"Flood zone\" — \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\" · caption \"FEMA · area zone · effective Sep 2021\"\n  - \"Wildfire hazard potential\" — \"Moderate · 3 of 5\" · caption \"USFS · quarter-mile area · 2023\"\n  - \"Air quality index (AQI) on Sat 12 Sep\" — \"AQI 42 · Good\" · caption \"AirNow · on Sat 12 Sep\"\n  - \"Radon zone\" — \"Zone 1 — highest potential (county)\" · caption \"EPA · county-wide estimate — only a test tells you about this home\"\n- Headline: \"Online or mail voter registration for Nov 3 must arrive by Mon 26 Oct in Washington.\" Caption: \"○ Washington Secretary of State · statewide · as of Sat 12 Sep\", with the legend word printed once beside it: \"○ On record, not confirmed\". The deadline is a seeded row nobody has checked, so its mark is hollow.\n- Collapsed line (below 640): \"Dana · Camas, WA · Flood X · Wildfire Moderate · Air 42 on Sat 12 Sep · Radon Zone 1 ›\". Short form: \"Dana · Camas, WA · 4 readings ›\".\n- \"Your place\" block: heading \"Your place\", placeholder \"Enter your address\", button \"See your place\", privacy proof line \"We don't post this anywhere. Nobody sees what you look up.\" Use the funnel's privacy proof line here, not the ScopeChip sentence: nothing is saved yet.\n- Contrast line: \"Nextdoor is what your neighbors say. Pantopus is what's on record about your address.\" On this page it sits below the address field.\n- Worst realistic case: sender \"Maximiliana-Josephine · Battle Ground, WA\"; Wildfire \"Very high · 5 of 5\"; Air \"AQI 312 · Hazardous\" in the 301+ segment; Flood not studied: \"FEMA hasn't mapped flood hazard here\"; Radon no data: \"Not on record\"; 90-character headline \"Online or mail voter registration for Nov 3 must arrive by Mon 26 Oct in Washington State.\"\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION:\n- Below 640px, top to bottom: page header; the collapsed sender line in the LandingBannerSlot position (a full-width 44px button, may wrap to two lines); H1; lede; \"Your place\"; field; button; privacy line; contrast line. The field, button and privacy line sit in the first viewport at 390x844 with no keyboard.\n- The collapsed line is plain text with no mark glyphs: four dots in a row would read as a rating, and a mark only means something on its own track.\n- Expanded, 361–639px wide (the 390 frames): the line opens in place into the freshness line, the four ScaleStrip rows, each with its own SourceCaption directly under its track (authority · scope · as-of, never merged), then the headline block with its hollow-mark caption (hidden when the deadline has passed). The field moves down and stays reachable.\n- Expanded, 320–360px wide only: the four rows drop their per-row captions and one merged sources line \"Sources: FEMA, USFS, AirNow, EPA\" follows the rows. The radon row keeps its value \"(county)\" so the scope still shows. Never draw \"Sources:\" on any frame wider than 360.\n- At 640px and wider, top to bottom: page header; two equal-height columns in the LandingBannerSlot position; then the H1, the lede and the contrast line.\n  - Left column: sender line, subline, freshness line, four ScaleStrip rows at compare size each with its own SourceCaption, then the headline block.\n  - Right column: a framed \"Your place\" column on surface.base with a strong ink keyline, holding only the heading, the field, the button and the privacy line. Leave the rest empty: the emptiness is the invitation.\n- In every ScaleStrip row: the track shows only that authority's own bands; the capsule marker shows Dana's band; the band name and number are printed as text; only the Air row uses AqiBand hues; the no-data row shows a greyed track, no marker and \"Not on record\"; the not-studied flood row shows a greyed track, no marker and \"FEMA hasn't mapped flood hazard here\".\n- The compare header occupies the LandingBannerSlot position under its precedence rule (invite > reissue > claim receipt > compare arrival > mailbox arrival), so the mailbox pill never renders with it. Only the expired-link banner uses the slot's pill anatomy (V5); the header itself is not pill-shaped.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS:\n- The field is focused on load. On a phone, load shows the focus ring and caret with no keyboard; the keyboard opens on the first tap. Frame 01 has no keyboard.\n- Keyboard open (frame 04): the collapsed line stays pinned under the page header and the H1 and lede scroll behind it; the privacy proof line sits directly under the field as one caption line, above the suggestion list, so it stays visible above the keyboard; the sticky WallBar is hidden and returns when the keyboard closes.\n- Typing is never blocked while the token is checked, and focus never moves when Dana's card arrives.\n- Suggestions open under the privacy line. Enter or \"See your place\" submits. On submit the page cross-fades to the compare reveal in 300ms or less, and Dana's rows keep their order.\n- The collapsed line opens and closes with a tap, Enter or Space; the chevron turns in 150ms. With Reduce Motion, rows appear with no rotation or slide.\n- Rows and captions here are flat text, not tap targets: the job is typing.\n- The expired banner's \"Close\" dismisses it; the ordinary hero stays.\n- No haptics (web).\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED:\n- LandingBannerSlot: position and precedence for the compare header; V5 expired compare link, with its trailing \"Close\" action, for frame 07.\n- AddressChip: sender label variant.\n- ScaleStrip: compare size, frozen, collapsed text line, no-data variant (V6), not-studied variant (V7). This surface overrides two published ScaleStrip specimens: (1) V10 adds the air date: \"Air 42 on Sat 12 Sep\"; (2) V9: the single freshness line \"Dana's card · as of Sat 12 Sep\" replaces the per-caption \"as of\" suffix, and the frozen air date sits in the layer label, not in the value line. Draw these overrides as written here.\n- AqiBand: instrument row.\n- SourceCaption: frozen-token variant, dated static variant, county-scope variant; collapsed sources line only on the 360 frame.\n- ProvenanceMark: filled on the four rows, hollow on the headline, each word printed once.\n- WarmingSkeleton: instrument skeleton.\n- FreshnessLine and OfflineNotice: form offline variant.\n- InlineErrorRow: not drawn on this surface (the compare reveal owns address no-match).\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n- Headings: the H1 is the page's only h1. \"Your place\" is an h2. Dana's card is a region labelled \"Dana's card from Camas, WA\" with no heading. Visual order and DOM order match.\n- Reading order below 640: header, Dana's card region, H1, lede, \"Your place\", field, privacy line, button, contrast line. At 640 and wider: header, Dana's card region, \"Your place\" column (field, privacy line, button), H1, lede, contrast line.\n- The field's description reads \"Compare with Dana's card from Camas, WA\", so a screen reader landing on the autofocused field hears the context.\n- The collapsed button is named \"Dana's card, Camas, Washington, as of Saturday 12 September: flood zone X, minimal flood hazard; wildfire hazard potential moderate, 3 of 5; air quality index 42, good, on 12 September; radon zone 1, highest potential, county-wide. Show readings.\" It has aria-expanded.\n- Each expanded row is one element, spoken as layer, value, position, scale ends, authority, date, provenance.\n- Targets at least 44px, including \"Close\"; the field is 48px tall. Text 4.5:1; field keyline and separators 3:1.\n- Every band is named in text, so greyscale loses nothing.\n- At 200% text, use the short collapsed form; rows stack text above a full-width track; nothing truncates.\n- The expired banner is role=status.\n\nCOPY (sentence case):\n- \"Your place\" · \"Enter your address\" · \"See your place\"\n- \"We don't post this anywhere. Nobody sees what you look up.\"\n- \"Show readings\" / \"Hide readings\"\n- \"A place in Camas, WA\" (card with no name)\n- \"That comparison link has expired. Type an address to see your own place. · Close\"\n- Online, check failed: \"We couldn't check this link just now. Showing the card as it was sent. · Retry\" (Retry spoken \"Retry checking this link\")\n- Offline, check failed: \"We couldn't check this link just now. Showing the card as it was sent.\" (no Retry; the OfflineNotice covers it)\n- \"You're offline. We can't look up an address right now.\" · disabled-button reason \"Looking up an address needs a connection.\"\n- Signed in with a saved place: \"Open Today\" in the page header; after the reveal it becomes \"Save this address\".\n\nEDGE CASES:\n- Worst case above: long name and city, AQI 312, one not-studied layer (flood) and one no-data layer (radon). The collapsed line switches to its short form.\n- Typing with 5 suggestions open, 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas, WA 98607 first; the collapsed line and privacy line stay visible above the keyboard.\n- Address can't be placed on submit: the page goes to the compare reveal's no-match state; nothing is drawn here.\n- Expired or tampered link: the V5 banner with \"Close\" in the slot above the ordinary hero; no sender column. Not an error page, not a modal.\n- Token check can't complete (network drops or server fails): draw the card from the token but keep it unchecked. Unchecked means: the collapsed line is text only; if expanded, the \"couldn't check\" line sits above the rows and the rows show values and captions with no ProvenanceMarks, so an unchecked card never looks official. If the token can't be read at all, show the expired banner. A spinner never hangs.\n- Offline: the OfflineNotice form line under the field; \"See your place\" is disabled with its reason shown.\n- Slow token check (1 second or more): at 390 a one-line skeleton; at 640+ Dana's column shows track outlines. The field is already live. Under 1 second, show nothing.\n- No first name: \"A place in Camas, WA\" everywhere the name would appear.\n- The headline deadline has passed on the viewing day: hide the headline block.\n- A compare link and the mailbox pill both apply: show only the compare header.\n- Signed in with a saved place (Jordan on his laptop): the page header swaps \"Sign in\" for \"Open Today\", and the sticky WallBar's account ask is hidden. Everything else stays the same.\n- Signed in with no saved place: the header shows the account menu only, with no \"Open Today\" (there is nothing to open yet); the WallBar account ask is hidden.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of stacking Dana's full card above the hero on a phone, draw the one-line text summary above the H1 and a focused field — because a stacked card pushes the field below the fold and kills the spread loop.\n- Instead of four tiny markers in the collapsed line, draw words and numbers — because a row of dots reads as a rating and fails the non-colour rule.\n- Instead of \"Air today\" on Dana's row, draw \"Air quality index (AQI) on Sat 12 Sep\" — because her reading is frozen.\n- Instead of a hollow radon mark, draw it filled with its county-wide caption under the row — because the EPA zone is official and its limit is its scope.\n- Instead of one \"Sources:\" line on the 390 and 1440 frames, give every row its own caption — because the merged line exists only for 320–360 widths.\n- Instead of a second address field in the hero, draw exactly one field inside \"Your place\" — because two fields split the one job.\n- Instead of a spinner while the link is checked, draw a live field with track outlines — because nothing should block typing.\n- Instead of an error page for an expired link, draw the quiet banner with \"Close\" over the normal hero — because the visitor can still do the job.\n- Instead of a map, street, photo or letter grade, draw the city and readings only — because the card promises never to reveal an address.\n\nDONE WHEN:\n- At 390x844 with no keyboard, the collapsed line, field, button and privacy line are in the first viewport.\n- The rows match the reveal in order and layer names, and the share card in order and values; Dana's air row carries its date.\n- A stranger can tell in five seconds whose card it is, where it is, and what to type.\n- Every row on the 390 and 1440 frames shows authority · scope · as-of.\n- The expired, offline and signed-in states each keep the page usable; a signed-in visitor is never asked to sign up.\n- An unchecked card never shows filled marks.\n- There is one address field on every frame.\n- Nothing states or implies anything about Dana's house.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f8-compare-arrival-header · web-390 · 01-collapsed-named · light — dense default: collapsed line at top, focused empty field, no keyboard.\n2. f8-compare-arrival-header · web-390 · 02-expanded · light — freshness line, four rows each with its own caption, headline block, field still reachable.\n3. f8-compare-arrival-header · web-1440 · 03-two-columns-named · light — Dana's column beside the empty \"Your place\" column, H1, lede and contrast line below.\n4. f8-compare-arrival-header · web-390 · 04-typing-suggestions · light — keyboard open, pinned collapsed line, field, privacy line under it, 5 suggestions, WallBar hidden.\n5. f8-compare-arrival-header · web-390 · 05-anonymous · light — \"A place in Camas, WA\".\n6. f8-compare-arrival-header · web-390 · 06-verifying · light — one-line skeleton, field live.\n7. f8-compare-arrival-header · web-390 · 07-expired · light — V5 banner with a 44px \"Close\" above the ordinary hero.\n8. f8-compare-arrival-header · web-390 · 08-offline · light — unchecked collapsed line (text only), \"couldn't check\" line without Retry, OfflineNotice form line under the field, \"See your place\" disabled with its reason.\n9. f8-compare-arrival-header · web-390 · 09-unchecked-expanded · light — online check failed, expanded: \"couldn't check\" line with Retry above rows that show values and captions with no marks.\n10. f8-compare-arrival-header · web-1440 · 10-signed-in · light — header shows \"Open Today\"; no sign-up wall.\n11. f8-compare-arrival-header · web-390 · 11-expanded-360 · light — drawn 360 wide: rows without per-row captions, one \"Sources: FEMA, USFS, AirNow, EPA\" line.\n12. f8-compare-arrival-header · web-390 · 12-worst-case · light — worst case, expanded, per-row captions, with the 90-character headline.\n13. f8-compare-arrival-header · web-390 · 13-text-200 · light — 200% text, short collapsed form.\n14. f8-compare-arrival-header · web-390 · 14-greyscale · light — frame 2 in greyscale.\n15. f8-compare-arrival-header · web-390 · 01-collapsed-named · dark — dark twin of frame 1.\n16. f8-compare-arrival-header · web-390 · 07-expired · dark — dark twin of frame 7.\n17. f8-compare-arrival-header · Notes — list every invented string (worst-case name, city and headline; the four other suggestions; the \"couldn't check\" lines and \"Retry checking this link\"; the offline reason line; \"Open Today\"; the field description; the region label). Also record:\n- \"Open Today\" replaces the inventory's \"Save this address\" on the hero because no address exists yet; a signed-in viewer with no saved place sees only the account menu; \"Save this address\" appears after the reveal, and its destination is an open product question.\n- Address no-match belongs to the compare reveal (its frame 06); this page's former no-match frame was removed; both surfaces use one string: We couldn't find \"<typed text>\". Check the spelling, or enter it line by line.\n- Contract updates: ScaleStrip V10 gains the frozen air date (\"Air 42 on Sat 12 Sep\"), per the research on frozen air readings; V9 uses one freshness line instead of a per-caption \"as of\", with the air date in the layer label.\n- The Foundations in-context crop for this surface shows \"Only you will see this.\" under the field; it should be corrected to the funnel privacy line used here.\n- Radon caption uses the contract string \"only a test tells you about this home\".\n- Load fires t0_compare_viewed (no UI).\n- The token needs a confidence field; a native app never intercepts this link; the voter headline now carries the weekday and the seasonal headline surface should match.\n- Flow spec: its persona and address (Maya, 6207 NE 42nd Ave) are replaced by the FRIEND C and PLACE B fixtures; frame map: collapsed = 01, typing = 04, expired = 07 (was 4).\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: artboards 7-12, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 3: artboards 13-17.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Expanded state at 390 now gives every ScaleStrip row its own SourceCaption; merged 'Sources:' line limited to 320–360 and drawn in a new 360 frame (review major, contract SourceCaption)",
          "Removed the no-match frame; a submit that can't be placed lands on the compare reveal's frame 06, with one shared no-match string recorded on Notes (review major, flows-spec failure branch, derive f8-2)",
