      {
        "id": "f7-today-widget",
        "name": "Today at your address (home-screen widget, three sizes)",
        "platforms": [
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": true,
        "frameCount": 27,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Today at your address (home-screen widget, three sizes) · f7-today-widget\n\nTYPE: NEW. This is a home-screen widget, drawn as artwork on a phone home screen. It is not an in-app screen.\n\nATTACH: the existing Pantopus \"Tasks near me\" widget on iOS and on Android (for widget chrome and radius only), and the Foundations board frames for ProvenanceMark, KindGlyph, FourteenDayStrip, AqiBand, YearBand, FreshnessLine and QuietDayReceipt.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS\niOS: draw on a 393x852 home screen. Small is 158x158pt, medium 338x158pt and large 338x354pt, with 16pt inner margins, so the content areas are 126x126, 306x126 and 306x322. Use the system widget corner radius.\nAndroid: one responsive widget. It is one entry in the picker, and people resize it. Assume the Pixel Launcher 5-column portrait grid, where a block of cells is (73 × columns − 16) by (118 × rows − 16) dp: 2x2 = 130x220dp, 4x2 = 276x220dp, 4x4 = 276x456dp. Also draw the declared minimums: 2x2 at 109x115dp and 4x2 at 245x115dp. Use the system corner radius (28dp at most). Write this assumed grid on Notes.\nAndroid is built with classic RemoteViews, not Glance. On every Android artboard, draw each size as a fixed set of rows, each either visible or gone. Strip cells, band segments and year lanes are fixed views or a single image, with their text beside them as separate live text. Text is never baked into an image. On the Android artboards, put a small \"image\" tag on every piece that is an image.\nThere is no web version.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE\nThe widget lives on the phone's home screen, outside the four tabs. People add it from the OS widget gallery (\"Today at your address\"), from the \"Put today on your home screen\" row in Place → Your place file, or from the how-to sheet (on Android, its \"Add to home screen\" button places the widget directly). The widget reads only the snapshot the app wrote on its last Today load; it never fetches anything itself.\nEach tap opens Today with pantopus://today?src=widget&section=…, except section=year, which opens Place → Your place file at its year band.\n- Small: the whole widget is one target, opening the hero's own section: section=pickup for a pickup hero, section=air for an air hero, section=strip for a date hero.\n- Medium: two regions, each at least 44pt / 48dp tall (a region may extend into the margins to reach that). The top region (label, hero, caption) opens the hero's section. The bottom region (next-date line, strip, air row) opens section=strip.\n- Large: four regions, each at least 44pt / 48dp. The year band → section=year. The hero line → its own section. The air line → section=air. The next-date line → section=strip. When air is the hero, the lower lines are pickup → section=pickup and next date → section=strip.\n- Android at the 115dp minimum height: one region, the hero.\n- No place: pantopus://today?src=widget, which opens the Add a place sheet.\nWhen someone confirms pickup, on Today or from the notification action, the confirm action rewrites the snapshot at once, so the hero's hollow ring becomes a tick with no Today load. When someone claims the address, the street label stays the same, the scope words change from \"Saved place · Only you\" to \"Your household\", and the marks update.\n\nWHO AND WHEN\nMaya Chen at HOME A, Mon 19 Oct, 7:40 AM. Today has just refreshed while she makes coffee. Tomorrow is a recycling week, and she hasn't confirmed the pickup schedule yet. At 6:10 PM she glances at her phone again without opening the app.\n\nTHE ONE JOB\nShow what's due at this address, what the air is like and what's next, right on the home screen, with no notification and no permission.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS\nThe eye lands first on the hero line (\"Recycling and garbage tomorrow\"), then on its mark and word (\"Unconfirmed\"), then on the size's instrument: the 14-day strip on medium, the year band on large. The only action is a tap, which opens that fact.\n\nCONTENT\nThe snapshot was written Mon 19 Oct at 7:40 AM for HOME A. Place label: \"Larkspur Loop\". Scope: \"Your household\".\nOne urgency ladder picks the hero at every size on both platforms: pickup today or tomorrow > AQI 101 or higher (fresh readings only) > nearest date > any pickup > any AQI. Day words are worked out at render time from the stored dates. They are never stored as text.\nDay-word timeline for HOME A (list both sequences on Notes):\n- Midnight entry, Mon 19 Oct: hero \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow\", caption \"Curbside by 6:30 AM\".\n- Evening-before entry, Mon 19 Oct 5:00 PM: the caption changes to \"Bins out tonight\"; the hero is unchanged. (This is the flow's \"Tomorrow has become Tonight\" moment.)\n- Midnight entry, Tue 20 Oct: hero \"Recycling and garbage today\", caption \"Curbside by 6:30 AM\".\n- Midnight entry, Wed 21 Oct: the ladder moves on to the date hero.\nThe facts:\n- Pickup hero: \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow\" · \"Curbside by 6:30 AM\" · [ProvenanceMark XS, unconfirmed] \"Unconfirmed\" · Waste Connections.\n- Air: \"AQI 42 · Good\" · AirNow · observed 7:00 AM · [ProvenanceMark XS, official] \"Official\".\n- Next date: \"Clark Public Utilities bill due\" · \"in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\" · [ProvenanceMark XS, you added] \"You added this\". Show no amounts anywhere on the widget.\n- Next 14 days, Mon 19 Oct to Sun 1 Nov (6 items): Tue 20 Oct recycling and garbage (hollow) · Fri 23 Oct Clark Public Utilities bill (tick) · Mon 26 Oct voter registration must arrive by (Washington rule, drawn as a full-height bar) · Tue 27 Oct garbage only (hollow) · Wed 28 Oct City of Vancouver water bill (tick) · Sun 1 Nov HOA dues (tick).\n- Year, Oct 2026 to Sep 2027. Lanes: You · Vancouver · Clark County · Washington. 9 dates.\n  - You: HOA dues 1 Nov · water-heater warranty ends 12 Dec · lease notice deadline 1 Mar · lease ends 31 Mar (the two March dates form a cluster marked \"2\").\n  - Vancouver: pickup service weeks, drawn as a light rhythm.\n  - Clark County: property tax 2nd half due Mon 2 Nov (moved from Sat 31 Oct) · property tax 1st half 30 Apr · tax appeal deadline 1 Jul (or 60 days after your notice).\n  - Washington: voter registration must arrive by 26 Oct · general election 3 Nov.\nDeltas (list each one on Notes):\n- Pickup today, Tue 20 Oct 6:00 AM: \"Recycling and garbage today\".\n- Date hero, Wed 21 Oct 8:00 AM: \"Clark Public Utilities bill due\" · \"in 2 days · Fri 23 Oct\".\n- Air hero, Thu 22 Oct 4:10 PM (the house style alert variant): \"Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups · AQI 118\", observed 4:00 PM, \"Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM\". The small widget uses the short form \"AQI 118 · Sensitive groups\". The lower lines read \"Garbage only · in 5 days · Tue 27 Oct\" and \"Clark Public Utilities bill due · Tomorrow\".\n- Confirmed: [ProvenanceMark XS, you added] + \"You · Tuesday\".\n- Saved place, PLACE B, Mon 19 Oct: label \"Birchfield Ct · Saved place · Only you\". Pickup is Thursday per the City of Camas (frequency Not set), so the strip shows hollow marks on Thu 22 and Thu 29 Oct plus the Mon 26 Oct Washington bar. The ladder picks the nearest date as hero: \"Online or mail registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\" · \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · [ProvenanceMark XS, official] \"Official\" · Washington. On small, use the short form \"Online or mail registration · Mon 26 Oct\". When the next date is the hero, the medium's next-date line shows the next pickup instead: \"Pickup · in 3 days · Thu 22 Oct\" with a hollow mark, \"Unconfirmed\" and City of Camas.\n- No pickup rule (invented saved place): \"Juniper Ct · Saved place · Only you\", Mon 19 Oct. Its strip shows only the Mon 26 voter bar. The hero is the same voter date, and the demoted line reads \"Set your pickup day\".\n- Nothing due (the same invented place, Mon 16 Nov 2026; there are no civic dates from 16 to 29 Nov): drawn cells with no marks, the QuietDayReceipt strip empty caption \"Checked — nothing in the next two weeks\", the demoted \"Set your pickup day\", and the air as hero, \"AQI 42 · Good\" (an invented reading for that date).\n- Holiday move, PLACE B, Mon 23 Nov 2026 (invented): hero \"Pickup moved to Fri 27 Nov\" · \"in 4 days · Thanksgiving · City of Camas\" · [ProvenanceMark XS, unconfirmed] \"Unconfirmed\". The strip draws the mark on Fri 27 Nov and a struck-through ghost mark on Thu 26 Nov, plus a hollow mark on Thu 3 Dec.\n- Stale air: the 7:40 AM snapshot seen at 6:10 PM.\n- Past the horizon: the same snapshot seen on Tue 3 Nov.\nWorst case: the medium air hero at the 245dp Android minimum.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\nEach size earns its space with a different form, not with more lines: small shows today, medium the next 14 days, large the year. Marks are always the ProvenanceMark component at 12pt, never a text character.\nSMALL (126pt content). Exactly four pieces: KindGlyph at widget size (16pt), the hero line, ProvenanceMark XS with its word, and the place label. There is no air chip, no date line, no logo and no keeper line. Vertical budget: a top row with the 16pt KindGlyph and the street label in caption, one line, with no scope words on small (16) + the hero in h3, at most 2 lines (56) + the mark and its word in caption (16) + three 8pt gaps (24) = 112. If the hero needs a third line, set it in body (16/24) and use 4pt gaps: 16 + 4 + 72 + 4 + 16 = 112. The small widget leaves out the authority for space; the spoken label carries it (note this on Notes).\nMEDIUM (126pt content), top to bottom:\n1. The label and scope in caption (16): \"Larkspur Loop · Your household\".\n2. KindGlyph and the hero, in body (16/24) at weight 600 (the weight h3 uses), one line (24).\n3. Caption (16): \"Curbside by 6:30 AM · [ProvenanceMark XS, unconfirmed] Unconfirmed · Waste Connections\" (after 5:00 PM, \"Bins out tonight · …\").\n4. Next-date line in caption (16): \"Next: Clark Public Utilities bill · in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\". This line has no mark: its tick sits on its strip cell and in the spoken label (flag this on Notes). If it doesn't fit on one line, shorten the title to the payee (\"Clark Public Utilities\"). Never use an ellipsis.\n5. FourteenDayStrip, widget medium variant, across the full 306pt (about 21.9pt per cell), one row (16): one 12pt mark per cell. On a day with several items, draw one mark plus an 11pt count numeral (\"2\"). Draw weekend cells with a lower-opacity fill, mark today with a 1.5px rule at the left edge of cell 1, and leave a 2pt extra gap before Mon 26 to show the week start. On iOS medium there is no anchor-label row. On the Android 4x2 at 220dp there is room, so print \"Today\" under cell 1 and \"Mon 26\" under cell 8 in 11pt.\n6. AqiBand, widget micro variant (16): six ColorVision Assist segments with 2px gaps, a keyline and a two-tone marker low in Good. Print \"AQI 42 · Good · AirNow 7:00 AM\" beside the bar, never on the fill.\nBudget: 16 + 4 + 24 + 16 + 4 + 16 + 4 + 16 + 4 + 16 = 120.\nWhen air is the hero, the micro band moves directly under the hero as its caption row (\"Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM · AirNow\"), followed by the next-date line and the strip. If the hero wraps to 2 lines, this still fits: 124.\nMedium drop order: the hero wraps first, then the next-date line drops (the date stays in the strip and in the spoken label), then the scope words drop, then the air row drops (never when air is the hero). The caption wraps to 2 lines before its authority is removed; if it wraps, the next-date line pays for the extra line.\nANDROID MINIMUM HEIGHT (115dp, about 83dp of content): one tap region. The label (16) + the hero in body, up to 2 lines (48) + its source caption (16) = 80. The strip, the air row and the lower lines are gone. Show this on artboard 17 using the air-hero data.\nLARGE (322pt content), top to bottom:\n1. Label and scope (16). This is the only size where the label may wrap to 2 lines.\n2. YearBand, widget large variant (about 150): 12 full-width month columns with three-letter month labels, and each lane label placed above its lane. Group markers per month per lane, with a count when there are 2 or more. Draw statewide rules as full-lane-height bars. Add a 1.5px today rule and a shaded 14-day window.\n3. Three lines, each a 44pt region: KindGlyph + the fact on the first row (the hero in body at weight 600, the others in bodySmall), and on the second row, in caption, the mark with its word, the authority and the date words. Hero: \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow\" / \"[unconfirmed] Unconfirmed · Waste Connections · Curbside by 6:30 AM\". Air: \"AQI 42 · Good\" / \"[official] Official · AirNow · observed 7:00 AM\". Next date: \"Clark Public Utilities bill due\" / \"[you added] You added this · in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\".\nThere is no keeper line. Budget: 16 + 150 + 132 + three 8pt gaps = 322. If the year band isn't legible at 338x354, ship small and medium only rather than filling large with extra text rows (record this go/no-go on Notes).\nMarks: filled = official, hollow = on record but not confirmed, tick = you added it. Strip and lane marks have no room for words, so the spoken label carries them (flag this on Notes).\nDegraded states. Each one must look different:\n- Air missing: the row goes and the layout rebalances. There is no hole and no failed widget.\n- Pickup missing: the next rung of the ladder takes the hero.\n- No pickup rule: \"Set your pickup day\" appears as a demoted caption line with no mark, in the next-date slot. It is never the hero.\n- Nothing due: cells drawn with no marks, plus \"Checked — nothing in the next two weeks\".\n- Stale, judged per fact: pickup and dates keep rendering until the 14-day snapshot horizon. Only the air row dims to 50% once its reading is more than 6 hours old, and the FreshnessLine per-fact variant \"Observed 7:00 AM · AirNow — 11 hours ago\" takes the next-date line's slot on medium, or the air line's second row on large. After a day, show the weekday: \"Observed Mon 7:00 AM · AirNow — 2 days ago\". A stale AQI of 101 or higher never takes the hero; the next rung does.\n- Past the horizon: every mark dims, the geometry stays, and the FreshnessLine reads \"As of Mon 19 Oct, 7:40 AM · Open to refresh\" (in the next-date slot on medium, under the label on large, replacing the mark row on small). This dated form is a deliberate variant of the contract's \"As of Mon 7:40 AM\", because on Tue 3 Nov a weekday alone is ambiguous. List it on Notes.\n- No snapshot: the glyph plus \"Open Pantopus to see today at your address\", with no cells drawn.\n- No place: the glyph plus \"Save an address to see today here\", with no cells drawn.\nThe street label never truncates.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\nWidgets respond to taps only; there are no gestures. The regions are listed above. There is no motion inside the widget and no haptics.\n- iOS: timeline entries at each local midnight for 14 days, plus the evening-before-pickup entry at 5:00 PM, so the day words change without the app being opened.\n- Android: the widget re-renders from the stored dates on its 30-minute update period, so day words change within 30 minutes of midnight or 5:00 PM with no network call.\n- Android opens the app with the system launch transition from the widget background.\nPut this Smart Stack note on Notes: relevance is high from 5:00 PM on the evening before pickup until pickup morning, and whenever a fresh AQI is 101 or higher; medium for a date within 3 days; zero on quiet days. Today donates an intent each time it opens.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED\n- ProvenanceMark: XS (12pt) only. On iOS it is widgetAccentable, and the tick stays knocked out when tinted. On Android it uses fixed ink.\n- KindGlyph: widget 16pt.\n- FourteenDayStrip: widget medium variant (single mark plus count numeral, no per-cell labels on iOS).\n- AqiBand: widget micro variant, with EPA hues fixed on Android.\n- YearBand: widget large variant, with place-name lanes.\n- FreshnessLine: per-fact stale and widget past-horizon variants (dated form).\n- QuietDayReceipt: strip empty variant.\n- PickupCard: widget small hero variant, including its holiday moved and no rule variants.\n- DateRow: its grammar for the large widget's lines.\n- ScopeChip: its exact wording in the label line.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Text is 11pt or larger and is never rasterised.\n- Each widget is one element with one combined spoken label. Medium: \"Larkspur Loop, your household. Recycling and garbage tomorrow, curbside by 6:30 AM, Waste Connections, on record, not confirmed. Next: Clark Public Utilities bill due in 4 days, Friday 23 October, you added this. Next 14 days, 6 items: Tuesday recycling and garbage, not confirmed; Friday 23 bill, you added; Monday 26 voter registration deadline, official; Tuesday 27 garbage, not confirmed; Wednesday 28 water bill, you added; Sunday 1 November HOA dues, you added. Air quality index 42, Good, category 1 of 6, AirNow, observed 7 AM.\" Large adds: \"Next 12 months: 9 dates. Next: voter registration must arrive by Monday 26 October.\" Small: \"Larkspur Loop, your household. Recycling and garbage tomorrow, Waste Connections, on record, not confirmed.\"\n- At AX5 (iOS) and 200% (Android), the strip, band and lanes drop out. The hero, the place label, the next date and the air reading remain as wrapping text.\n- In tinted, StandBy and greyscale renderings, meaning survives through shape, gaps, opacity and words.\n- Tap regions are at least 44pt / 48dp. Marks are never targets on their own.\n\nCOPY\nToday at your address · Larkspur Loop · Your household · Birchfield Ct · Saved place · Only you · Juniper Ct · Recycling and garbage tomorrow · Recycling and garbage today · Garbage only · in 5 days · Tue 27 Oct · Curbside by 6:30 AM · Bins out tonight · Unconfirmed · Official · You added this · You · Tuesday · AQI 42 · Good · AirNow 7:00 AM · AQI 118 · Sensitive groups · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups · Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM · Observed 7:00 AM · AirNow — 11 hours ago · Observed Mon 7:00 AM · AirNow — 2 days ago · Clark Public Utilities bill due · in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct · Next: Clark Public Utilities bill · Tomorrow · Online or mail registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct · Online or mail registration · Mon 26 Oct · Pickup · in 3 days · Thu 22 Oct · City of Camas · Pickup moved to Fri 27 Nov · Thanksgiving · Today · Mon 26 · You · Vancouver · Clark County · Washington · Set your pickup day · Checked — nothing in the next two weeks · As of Mon 19 Oct, 7:40 AM · Open to refresh · Open Pantopus to see today at your address · Save an address to see today here.\n\nEDGE CASES\n- Longest label: \"Birchfield Ct · Saved place · Only you\". It never truncates: on large it may wrap to 2 lines; on medium and small the scope words drop first (the drop order), and the spoken label keeps them.\n- Highest AQI: 301 or more puts the marker in the last segment with the label \"Hazardous\".\n- A day with several items: one mark plus a count numeral (\"3\"); the full list is in the spoken label.\n- A holiday move: drawn on artboard 12.\n- Widget added before any Today load: the no-snapshot state.\n- Saved place vs claimed home: only the scope words change.\n- More than one place: the widget mirrors the last place Today showed, so the label is the only clue (the pilot has one address per person). Record on Notes that multiple addresses would later need a per-widget place choice.\n- \"Save an address to see today here\" appears only where the Add a place sheet exists on that platform (Notes).\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of three equal text lines, draw one hero picked by the ladder above the size's instrument, because a lease notice months away must not weigh the same as tomorrow's recycling.\n- Instead of a 120pt strip with 6pt dots and an initial under every cell, draw a full-width strip with one 12pt mark per cell and a count numeral, because 11pt text and a readable tick need about 21pt per cell.\n- Instead of a \"○\" typed into a caption, place the 12pt ProvenanceMark component, because a text glyph renders below the 12pt minimum.\n- Instead of greying the whole widget after 6 hours, dim only the air row with its age, because pickup rules and dates stay true for weeks.\n- Instead of the string \"AQI 42 Good\" or text on a coloured fill, draw the micro band with the name beside it, because the category must survive tinting.\n- Instead of every tap opening the top of Today, give each region its own section, because the tapped fact can be below the fold.\n- Instead of blanking a missing section, rebalance the layout, because a hole reads as broken.\n- Instead of a percentage, progress bar, ring or grade, draw marks in cells and lanes, because the widget states facts and does not score them.\n- Instead of Pantopus blue chrome on Android 12 and later, use Material dynamic roles (surface, primary, primaryContainer) with Pantopus tokens as the fallback, because Android's widget quality bar requires device theming. Marks and EPA hues stay fixed.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- After one Today load, all three facts are visible as text on every size that has room: small shows the hero only (its other facts are in the spoken label); medium shows the hero, the next-date line and the air reading, plus the strip; large shows the hero, air and next-date lines, plus the year band.\n- With the app closed, the caption becomes \"Bins out tonight\" at 5:00 PM and \"tomorrow\" becomes \"today\" after midnight.\n- Someone with no place sees \"Save an address to see today here\".\n- \"Nothing due\", \"stale\", \"past the horizon\" and \"no snapshot\" are four different pictures.\n- A confirmed pickup shows a tick without a Today load.\n- PLACE B never shows a quiet fortnight: its Thursday marks and the Mon 26 bar are always drawn.\n- On the AQI 118 day, the widget and Today agree on the hero.\n- Every size reads as text at AX5 and 200%, and every piece fits its stated height budget.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f7-today-widget · ios · 01-dense-set · light — home screen at Mon 19 Oct 7:40 AM with the small, medium and large widgets, pickup hero, hollow mark, next-date line.\n2. f7-today-widget · ios · 02-tap-regions · light — the medium and large from 01, with each tap region outlined in dashes and labelled with its section (large shows four regions, including section=air and section=year).\n3. f7-today-widget · ios · 03-small-ladder · light — four small widgets: pickup tomorrow, pickup today, date hero, air hero, each with its height budget annotated.\n4. f7-today-widget · ios · 04-air-hero · light — medium and large on Thu 22 Oct 4:10 PM, AQI 118, the band under the hero and \"Garbage only · in 5 days · Tue 27 Oct\".\n5. f7-today-widget · ios · 05-confirmed · light — small and medium after confirming, with the tick and \"You · Tuesday\".\n6. f7-today-widget · ios · 06-partial · light — two mediums: air missing (rebalanced) and pickup missing (the date wins the hero).\n7. f7-today-widget · ios · 07-no-rule · light — Juniper Ct small and medium on Mon 19 Oct: voter hero, only the Mon 26 bar, \"Set your pickup day\" demoted.\n8. f7-today-widget · ios · 08-nothing-due · light — Juniper Ct medium on Mon 16 Nov: drawn empty cells, \"Checked — nothing in the next two weeks\", air hero.\n9. f7-today-widget · ios · 09-stale-air · light — medium and large at 6:10 PM: \"Bins out tonight\", only the air row dimmed, \"Observed 7:00 AM · AirNow — 11 hours ago\".\n10. f7-today-widget · ios · 10-past-horizon · light — medium and large on Tue 3 Nov: every mark dimmed, geometry kept, \"As of Mon 19 Oct, 7:40 AM · Open to refresh\".\n11. f7-today-widget · ios · 11-no-snapshot-no-place · light — the two placeholders at small and medium, with no cells drawn.\n12. f7-today-widget · ios · 12-holiday-move · light — PLACE B small and medium on Mon 23 Nov: \"Pickup moved to Fri 27 Nov\", the moved mark and the struck ghost on Thu 26.\n13. f7-today-widget · ios · 13-saved-place · light — PLACE B small, medium and large on Mon 19 Oct: voter hero, hollow Thursday marks on Thu 22 and Thu 29, the Mon 26 bar, \"Birchfield Ct · Saved place · Only you\".\n14. f7-today-widget · ios · 14-tinted · dark — accented rendering of the three sizes, with the strip, band and marks still readable.\n15. f7-today-widget · ios · 15-standby · dark — StandBy: two small widgets scaled up on black, with no background, greyscale shapes and larger type, plus a red low-light copy.\n16. f7-today-widget · android · 16-dense-set · light — 2x2, 4x2 and 4x4 at the grid sizes in dynamic colour, with \"Today\" and \"Mon 26\" anchors on the 4x2 and image tags.\n17. f7-today-widget · android · 17-minimum-size · light — 2x2 at 109x115dp and 4x2 at 245x115dp with the air-hero data: one tap region, what dropped labelled.\n18. f7-today-widget · android · 18-dynamic-nonblue · light — 4x2 and 4x4 on a green wallpaper palette, with marks and EPA hues unchanged.\n19. f7-today-widget · ios · 19-ax5 · light — all three sizes at AX5, text only.\n20. f7-today-widget · android · 20-200-percent · light — 4x2 and 4x4 at 200%, text only.\n21. f7-today-widget · ios · 21-greyscale · light — artboard 01 in greyscale.\n22. f7-today-widget · ios · 22-dense-set · dark — the dark twin of 01.\n23. f7-today-widget · ios · 23-air-hero · dark — the dark twin of 04.\n24. f7-today-widget · ios · 24-stale-air · dark — the dark twin of 09, checking the dimmed row's contrast.\n25. f7-today-widget · ios · 25-past-horizon · dark — the dark twin of 10, checking the dimmed marks' contrast.\n26. f7-today-widget · android · 26-dense-set · dark — the dark twin of 16.\n27. f7-today-widget · ios · 27-notes · light — Notes: the Android grid assumption; RemoteViews rules and which pieces are images; the Android 30-minute re-render; the day-word sequences; Smart Stack rules; the strip-words and next-date-mark flags; small omitting the authority; the \"Unconfirmed\" short form (the scope always uses its full string); the dated past-horizon variant; the no-amounts choice; the large go/no-go; the add-a-place dependency; multi-address later; an optional Lock Screen rectangular version (not drawn); every invented string (Juniper Ct, the 16 Nov and 23 Nov dates, Thanksgiving move, \"Curbside by 6:30 AM\", \"Next:\"); omitted states.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: 7-12, then wait. Turn 3: 13-18, then wait. Turn 4: 19-24, then wait. Turn 5: 25-27.",
        "changeLog": [
          "PLACE B made truthful (review major): it now always shows hollow Thursday marks on Thu 22 and Thu 29 plus the Mon 26 Washington bar, with the voter date as hero, on a new 13-saved-place artboard. The no-rule and nothing-due states moved to an invented saved place, Juniper Ct (Mon 19 Oct and Mon 16 Nov 2026). Artboard 07 was split into 07-no-rule and 08-nothing-due.",
          "Added a next-date text line to the medium, so all three facts show as text (design doc Goal and acceptance). DONE WHEN now spells out each size's version of 'all three facts'.",
          "Added a vertical height budget for small, medium, large and the Android 115dp minimum (review major). Medium strip is one 12pt mark plus a count numeral. iOS medium drops the anchor-label row (today rule and week gap instead); the Android 4x2 keeps the 'Today' and 'Mon 26' anchors.",
          "Added the Android RemoteViews (no Glance) constraint: fixed rows toggled visible or gone, images tagged, text always live (design doc and derive proposal).",
          "Large widget now has four tap regions: year → section=year, hero → own section, air → section=air, next date → section=strip, with the air-hero variant. Every tap opens Today except year, which opens the place file.",
          "Scope string fixed to 'Birchfield Ct · Saved place · Only you' (invariant 2 and the ScopeChip contract). Small shows only the street. Removed the 'Only you' short form.",
          "Replaced the literal '○' with the ProvenanceMark XS component, and added the rule that marks are always the 12pt component.",
          "The medium caption now carries the authority (Waste Connections) and wraps before anything is removed. Notes records that small omits the authority.",
          "Added a holiday-move delta and artboard 12 (PLACE B, Thanksgiving, Fri 27 Nov with a struck ghost on Thu 26), per research principle P17.",
          "Stale air now uses the contract string 'Observed 7:00 AM · AirNow — 11 hours ago', with a weekday form after a day. A stale AQI of 101 or higher never takes the hero.",
          "Past-horizon line kept in the dated form, listed on Notes as a deliberate variant of the contract.",
          "Defined the day-word timeline: 5:00 PM evening entry switches the caption to 'Bins out tonight'; midnight switches tomorrow to today. Android re-renders every 30 minutes (updatePeriodMillis 1800000 per the design doc).",
          "On claim, the street label stays and only the scope words and marks change (flow-06). The confirm action rewrites the snapshot at once (flow-01).",
          "Air-hero lower line fixed to 'Garbage only · in 5 days · Tue 27 Oct' (date rule).",
          "Type fixed to 'body (16/24) at weight 600' instead of an off-scale name.",
          "Added 'no keeper line', the large-size go/no-go check, the add-a-place dependency, multi-address later and the optional Lock Screen rectangular version (Notes).",
          "Added dark twins of stale-air and past-horizon (24, 25). Frames 22 → 27; batch plan is now 5 turns."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f7-widget-tap-landing",
        "name": "Widget tap landing (attribution + forced refresh)",
        "platforms": [
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 19,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Widget tap landing (attribution + forced refresh) · f7-widget-tap-landing\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Today (one composition, both payloads)\". This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed.\n\nATTACH: Today for HOME A (loaded) on iOS and on Android; Today for PLACE B (saved place); Today's air band in its alert state; the medium widget artboard from f7-today-widget (01) and its air-hero artboard (04), so the tapped hero matches.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS\niOS 393x852 and Android 412x915. There is no web version, because the widget is native only.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE\nThis is the Today tab, opened by a tap on any size of the \"Today at your address\" widget. The link is pantopus://today?src=widget&section=pickup, strip or air.\n- section=year routes to Place → Your place file at its year band. It still starts the same forced Today refresh in the background, writes the snapshot and records the widget open, while it routes. So a past-horizon widget tapped on its year band still stops saying \"Open to refresh\".\n- With no section, Today opens at the top.\n- With no place, the Add a place sheet opens.\nWhat arrives: the section, the source (widget) and a snapshot that may be hours old.\nWhat this screen hands on (Notes, as behaviour; not drawn): a forced refresh (a real reload even when the app is already open), a new widget snapshot on success, and two separate events: session_open with trigger widget, and a snapshot-written event.\nAndroid must land on this same Today composition, never on the separate briefing screen. That screen shows different data and errors for a saved place.\nPush arrivals use their own link, pantopus://hub-today?deliveryId=…, and the two must not collide. The same route will later be reused by ?src=email (Notes).\n\nWHO AND WHEN\nMaya Chen at HOME A, Mon 19 Oct, 7:41 AM. A minute ago her widget said \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow\", and she tapped it. On Thu 22 Oct at 4:10 PM she taps the widget's air hero.\n\nTHE ONE JOB\nOpen the exact fact the widget showed, refresh it in place, and show that the refresh happened.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS\nThe eye lands first on the tapped section, already in view with a one-time highlight, then on the header freshness line (\"Updated just now\"), then on the rest of Today, unchanged. The next step is the section's own choice. On the pickup card, that is the two equal outlined buttons \"Yes, Tuesday is right\" and \"Change pickup day\".\n\nCONTENT\n- Header: \"2418 NE Larkspur Loop\" · ScopeChip \"Your household\" · FreshnessLine \"Updated just now\".\n- PickupCard: KindGlyph · \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow\" · \"Bins out tonight — curbside by 6:30 AM (Waste Connections)\" · hollow mark with \"City schedule, not yet confirmed\" · two equal outlined buttons, \"Yes, Tuesday is right\" and \"Change pickup day\".\n- FourteenDayStrip, Mon 19 Oct to Sun 1 Nov, 6 items: Tue 20 recycling and garbage (hollow) · Fri 23 Clark Public Utilities bill (tick) · Mon 26 voter registration must arrive by (full-height bar) · Tue 27 garbage only (hollow) · Wed 28 City of Vancouver water bill (tick) · Sun 1 Nov HOA dues (tick).\n- AqiBand: \"AQI 42 · Good\" · \"Air quality is satisfactory, and air pollution poses little or no risk.\" · \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM\".\n- Weather, alerts and signals: keep them exactly as the attached screenshot shows, and list their values on Notes.\nDeltas (list each one on Notes):\n- Arrival time 7:41 AM (the house fixture time is 6:10 PM).\n- Air arrival, Thu 22 Oct 4:10 PM, with an active crossing. The pinned slot at the top holds a compact crossing card: AqiBand alert variant, \"AQI 118 · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups\", \"Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM\", ScopeChip \"Your household\", SourceCaption \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 4:00 PM\". The full air band stays in its own position and reads \"AQI 118 · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups · PM2.5\", \"Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM\", \"Members of sensitive groups may experience health effects. The general public is less likely to be affected.\", \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 4:00 PM\". On that day, the PickupCard shows the next pickup: \"Garbage only · in 5 days · Tue 27 Oct\" (hollow). The strip covers Thu 22 Oct to Wed 4 Nov: Fri 23 Clark Public Utilities bill (tick) · Mon 26 voter registration bar · Tue 27 garbage only (hollow) · Wed 28 City of Vancouver water bill (tick) · Sun 1 Nov HOA dues (tick) · Mon 2 Nov property tax 2nd half (filled, Clark County) and Comcast bill (tick), drawn as one mark plus \"2\" · Tue 3 Nov general election (bar) and recycling and garbage (hollow). If a section below the fold is not in frame, don't draw it.\n- Failed refresh, the same Monday at 6:10 PM: \"Couldn't refresh · Retry\" above \"Updated 10h ago\". The air caption goes stale: \"Observed 7:00 AM · AirNow — 11 hours ago\".\n- Offline: \"You're offline · as of 7:41 AM\". Both pickup buttons are disabled, with the caption \"Confirming needs a connection.\"\n- PLACE B: \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\" · \"Saved place · Only you\", arriving with section=strip. Its strip shows hollow Thursday pickups on Thu 22 and Thu 29 Oct and the Mon 26 Oct voter bar. If its PickupCard is visible, it carries the T1 footer \"Only you will see this.\"\nWorst case: AX5 text with the pickup card highlighted.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\nChange only these:\n0. Scope chip. If the attached Today has no chip for a claimed home, add ScopeChip \"Your household\" next to the address (house style invariant 2). The inventory said \"claimed home (no chip)\", but the contract requires the chip. Follow the contract and note the conflict on Notes.\n1. Section landing. Read section:\n   - section=pickup or section=strip: scroll that section into view once, just below the header.\n   - section=air with an active crossing: do not scroll. The crossing card in the pinned slot gets the highlight and focus.\n   - section=air with no crossing: scroll the air band to just below the header and highlight it.\n   The highlight is an info-tint wash plus a 2px outline. It appears within 300ms, holds for about 2s, then fades out over 300ms. Accessibility focus moves to the section. Keep the section order exactly as it is.\n2. FreshnessLine, directly under the location row. It reads \"Updating…\", then \"Updated just now\", then ages as \"Updated 12m ago\" and \"Updated 2h ago\" using system relative time. The line is where state is shown; there is no toast.\n3. A 2pt indeterminate hairline under the header. It appears only if the refresh takes 1s or more. If the refresh finishes sooner, only the line changes. Cards do not dim, collapse or reflow.\n4. Failed refresh: \"Couldn't refresh · Retry\" (Retry is 44pt). All earlier content stays, and each stale fact shows its own age.\n5. A cold start is the only case that gets the full WarmingSkeleton, with the address already resolved.\n6. Android: the landing is this composition.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- Scrolling happens once. It is never repeated, including when content is added.\n- With Reduce Motion on, the screen jumps straight to the section, the highlight appears without animation and cross-fades out, and the hairline is a static 2pt line rather than an animated one.\n- Retry is a button. Nothing depends on pull-to-refresh.\n- Android opens with the system launch transition from the widget.\n- The only haptic is the existing light tick when \"Yes, Tuesday is right\" is confirmed.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED\nFreshnessLine (fresh, refreshing, failed, offline and per-fact stale variants) · WarmingSkeleton (section skeleton, cold start only) · OfflineNotice (read-only cached screen) · ScopeChip · PickupCard (highlighted on arrival; offline; T1 footer) · FourteenDayStrip (highlighted on arrival) · AqiBand (alert variant, in the pinned crossing card and the air band) · ProvenanceMark · SourceCaption · InlineErrorRow (only if a single provider fails).\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Focus moves to the highlighted section, whose label is read first, then the header.\n- The FreshnessLine is a polite live region and announces a change once.\n- The highlight is readable without colour, because it has an outline.\n- Selection looks different from focus.\n- Retry reads \"Retry refreshing Today\".\n- Pickup buttons are labelled \"Confirm Tuesday pickup\" and \"Change pickup day, opens date sheet\", and are 44pt / 48dp.\n- The crossing card reads \"Air quality index 118, Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups, crossed 101 at 4 PM, your household, AirNow.\"\n- At AX5 or 200%, the freshness line wraps and the buttons stack.\n- Disabled offline buttons stay focusable and read their reason.\n\nCOPY\nUpdated just now · Updated 12m ago · Updated 2h ago · Updated 10h ago · Updating… · Couldn't refresh · Retry · You're offline · as of 7:41 AM · Confirming needs a connection. · Your household · Saved place · Only you · Only you will see this. · AQI 118 · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups · Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM · Garbage only · in 5 days · Tue 27 Oct · Observed 7:00 AM · AirNow — 11 hours ago · Add a place.\n\nEDGE CASES\n- Longest address: \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\" with its chip. It wraps and never truncates.\n- The section is missing from the data (for example, no pickup rule): land at the top with no highlight.\n- An unknown section value: land at the top.\n- A slow refresh over 10s: keep the hairline and the content.\n- The refresh fails twice: the line stays, and no dialog opens.\n- No place: Today's \"Today starts with a place\", with the Add a place sheet over it.\n- A saved place never errors on Android.\n- A year-band tap: no Today frame is drawn; the refresh and events still run (Notes).\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a skeleton, dimmed cards or a spinner on a warm screen, keep the content and add only the hairline and the freshness line, because blanking the fact someone tapped to see is the one thing this landing must never do.\n- Instead of a toast saying \"Refreshed\", change the persistent header line, because the proof has to stay visible.\n- Instead of landing at the top of Today, scroll to the tapped section and highlight it once, because the air band sits below the fold.\n- Instead of scrolling the air band up and pushing the crossing off screen, keep the top in place and highlight the pinned crossing card, because the crossing is the fact the widget showed.\n- Instead of a manual Refresh button, a pull-to-refresh overlay or a \"came from widget\" badge, use the freshness line with Retry only on failure, because the refresh already runs on arrival.\n- Instead of reordering sections for the widget, use the pinned slot for an active crossing, because moving sections confuses people.\n- Instead of a filled primary button on the pickup card, keep its two equal outlined buttons, because the contract makes confirm and change peers.\n- Instead of the briefing screen on Android, use this composition, because the widget mirrors this data.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- A tap on the pickup hero lands on the pickup card, highlighted, showing \"Updated just now\".\n- A tap on the air hero shows the pinned crossing card at the top, highlighted, with no scrolling.\n- Content never blanks.\n- The widget stops showing \"Open to refresh\" after any tap, including a tap on the year band.\n- A saved-place user on Android sees Today, not an error.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f7-widget-tap-landing · ios · 01-arrived-pickup · light — Mon 7:41 AM, section=pickup, pickup card highlighted, \"Updated just now\".\n2. f7-widget-tap-landing · ios · 02-refreshing · light — the refresh runs past 1s: \"Updating…\" and the hairline, content unchanged.\n3. f7-widget-tap-landing · ios · 03-arrived-air · light — Thu 4:10 PM, section=air, no scroll, the pinned crossing card highlighted and focused, the Thu 22 Oct pickup card below it.\n4. f7-widget-tap-landing · ios · 04-arrived-strip · light — section=strip, strip highlighted.\n5. f7-widget-tap-landing · ios · 05-refresh-failed · light — 6:10 PM, \"Couldn't refresh · Retry\", \"Updated 10h ago\", stale air caption.\n6. f7-widget-tap-landing · ios · 06-cold-start · light — skeleton with the address resolved.\n7. f7-widget-tap-landing · ios · 07-offline · light — cached content with disabled pickup buttons and their reason.\n8. f7-widget-tap-landing · ios · 08-no-place · light — the Add a place sheet over the empty Today.\n9. f7-widget-tap-landing · ios · 09-saved-place · light — PLACE B, \"Saved place · Only you\", strip highlighted, T1 footer if the pickup card is visible.\n10. f7-widget-tap-landing · android · 10-arrived-pickup · light — the Android version of 01, on the root Today.\n11. f7-widget-tap-landing · android · 11-arrived-air · light — the Android version of 03.\n12. f7-widget-tap-landing · android · 12-saved-place · light — PLACE B renders, with no briefing-screen error.\n13. f7-widget-tap-landing · android · 13-refresh-failed · light — the Android version of 05.\n14. f7-widget-tap-landing · ios · 14-ax5 · light — 01 at AX5: the line wraps and the buttons stack.\n15. f7-widget-tap-landing · android · 15-200-percent · light — 10 at 200%.\n16. f7-widget-tap-landing · ios · 16-greyscale · light — 03 in greyscale; the highlight reads as an outline.\n17. f7-widget-tap-landing · ios · 17-arrived-pickup · dark — the dark twin of 01.\n18. f7-widget-tap-landing · android · 18-arrived-air · dark — the dark twin of 11.\n19. f7-widget-tap-landing · ios · 19-notes · light — Notes: the forced refresh, the snapshot write and the two separate events (session_open with trigger widget; snapshot written); section=year behaviour; the link formats, the push link and the later ?src=email reuse; highlight timing and Reduce Motion; the scope-chip conflict; weather values; the 7:41 AM delta; invented strings; omitted states.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: 7-12, then wait. Turn 3: 13-18, then wait. Turn 4: 19.",
        "changeLog": [
          "The air arrival no longer contradicts itself (review major). With an active crossing there is no scroll, and the pinned slot holds a compact crossing card with full copy, which gets the highlight and focus. With no crossing, the air band scrolls and is highlighted. Artboards 03 and 11 updated.",
          "section=year now also triggers the forced refresh, the snapshot write and session_open while it routes to the place file, so any tap clears 'Open to refresh' (inventory: 'any tap').",
          "Notes now lists session_open{trigger:widget} and a snapshot-written event as two separate events (per-surface and design doc §5).",
          "The highlight now appears within 300ms, holds about 2s and fades out over 300ms. With Reduce Motion, the hairline is static.",
          "Added Thu 22 Oct content for the air arrival: the strip window Thu 22 to Wed 4 Nov and the next-pickup card 'Garbage only · in 5 days · Tue 27 Oct'. Sections out of frame are left undrawn.",
          "Added layout change 0 (ScopeChip on a claimed home) and a Notes line on the conflict with the inventory's 'claimed home (no chip)'. Added the T1 footer 'Only you will see this.' to the PLACE B pickup card.",
          "FIRST FIVE SECONDS now describes two equal outlined peer buttons instead of 'the primary action' (PickupCard contract).",
          "Notes now covers the ?src=email reuse (derive proposal) and the 7:41 AM delta from the fixture time.",
          "Attached the f7-today-widget air-hero artboard (04) as well."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f7-widget-gallery",
        "name": "Widget gallery entry (name, description, preview)",
        "platforms": [
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": true,
        "frameCount": 14,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Widget gallery entry (name, description, preview) · f7-widget-gallery\n\nTYPE: NEW. This is preview artwork plus the OS picker screens that show it. It is not a running widget.\n\nATTACH: the f7-today-widget artboards 01 (iOS set), 13 (PLACE B saved place) and 16 (Android set), so the previews match the real widget exactly.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS\n- iOS: the widget gallery on 393x852. Draw the Pantopus detail page with its size carousel and the system \"Add Widget\" button. Previews are 158x158, 338x158 and 338x354pt.\n- Android: the widget picker on 412x915, with the Pantopus section expanded, and the long-press drag preview. The widget is one responsive widget, so the Pantopus section shows one entry, \"Today at your address\", with one preview at the default 4x2 target size (276x220dp, scaled to the picker), the system size label \"4 × 2\" and the description. People choose a size by resizing the widget after placing it.\n- Draw OS chrome in neutral system styling. Pantopus tokens apply only inside the previews.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE\nThis lives outside the four tabs, in the OS widget gallery.\n- iOS: touch and hold the home screen → Edit → Add Widget → search for or pick Pantopus.\n- Android: touch and hold the home screen → Widgets → Pantopus, or touch and hold the Pantopus icon → Widgets.\nThe how-to sheet (\"Put today on your home screen\") walks people here on iOS and on Android launchers that can't pin. This is the whole top of the widget funnel. Next step: the widget is placed and shows the person's snapshot, or the no-snapshot state if Today was never loaded.\n\nWHO AND WHEN\nMaya Chen, Mon 19 Oct, browsing her iPhone's widget gallery on the evening she moved her bins. A second person, Jordan Lee (PLACE B), has loaded Today once. Jordan is drawn on both platforms (iOS artboard 04, Android artboard 07) so the own-data rule can be compared side by side.\n\nTHE ONE JOB\nMake someone browsing the widget gallery understand what this widget shows and want to add it.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS\nThe eye lands first on the preview (a real-looking pickup day, strip and air band), then on the name \"Today at your address\", then on the verb-led description. The single primary action is the system Add Widget button, or on Android, dragging or tapping the entry.\n\nCONTENT\nName: \"Today at your address\".\nDescription: \"See pickup day, air quality and your next date at your address.\"\nThe baked sample is identical on both platforms and is also the preview for anyone with no place or no snapshot. It uses HOME A in its evening state. Its dates are offsets from the date it is rendered, so it always reads \"tomorrow\" and \"in 4 days\" and never goes past its horizon (Notes). As drawn, the dates are Mon 19 Oct. Every mark in a preview is the 12pt ProvenanceMark component, never a text character.\n- Small: KindGlyph · \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow\" · [ProvenanceMark XS, unconfirmed] \"Unconfirmed\" · \"Larkspur Loop\".\n- Medium (the densest): label \"Larkspur Loop · Your household\" · the same hero · \"Bins out tonight · [ProvenanceMark XS, unconfirmed] Unconfirmed · Waste Connections\" · the next-date line \"Next: Clark Public Utilities bill · in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\" · the 14-day strip with 6 items (Tue 20 hollow, Fri 23 tick, Mon 26 Washington bar, Tue 27 hollow, Wed 28 tick, Sun 1 Nov tick), one mark per cell · the AqiBand micro variant with the marker low in Good and \"AQI 42 · Good · AirNow 7:00 AM\" beside it.\n- Large: the year band (You · Vancouver · Clark County · Washington) with 9 dates spread across the lanes: HOA dues 1 Nov; water-heater warranty 12 Dec; lease notice 1 Mar and lease end 31 Mar as a March cluster \"2\"; property tax Mon 2 Nov and 30 Apr; appeal deadline 1 Jul; voter registration 26 Oct; election 3 Nov. Below it are three lines: the pickup hero with \"Unconfirmed · Waste Connections\"; \"AQI 42 · Good\" with a filled mark, \"Official · AirNow\"; and \"Clark Public Utilities bill due\" with a tick, \"You added this · in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\".\n- Android 4x2 preview: the medium composition at 220dp tall, with the \"Today\" and \"Mon 26\" anchor labels under the strip.\nAll three mark shapes appear, so the provenance marks (filled, hollow, tick) are visible before install.\nOwn-data delta (Jordan Lee's snapshot, used once one exists): label \"Birchfield Ct · Saved place · Only you\" on medium and large, and \"Birchfield Ct\" alone on small. The hero is \"Online or mail registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\" with the line \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" and a filled mark, \"Official · Washington\" (small uses the short form \"Online or mail registration · Mon 26 Oct\"). The next-date slot shows \"Pickup · in 3 days · Thu 22 Oct\" with a hollow mark, \"Unconfirmed · City of Camas\". The strip has hollow pickup marks on Thu 22 and Thu 29 Oct and the Mon 26 bar. AQI 42 · Good.\nList every invented string on Notes.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\n- Each preview uses the widget's own composition: small shows one fact, medium the strip, large the year, so the larger size visibly earns its space. No size may look emptier than the size below it.\n- The strip is about half full, the AQI marker sits clearly inside a named band, and the year lanes are spread across the months.\n- iOS gallery previews use the baked sample until a snapshot exists. After that they use the person's own data from a local read.\n- The Android picker entry uses Material dynamic colour. On Android 15 and later, a generated preview with the person's own data is pushed after their first Today load. Below Android 15, it stays the baked sample in dynamic colour.\n- The iOS redacted placeholder keeps the geometry: strip cells, band segments and lane rules stay drawn, and only the text becomes rounded bars.\n- The preview never shows an empty state.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\nThe OS owns every interaction: swiping the size carousel on iOS (which also has page dots), tapping Add Widget, and on Android touching and holding to drag, or tapping the entry to add it. The previews have no motion of their own. Haptics are the system's.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED\nProvenanceMark (XS, 12pt, with its word) · KindGlyph (widget 16pt) · FourteenDayStrip (widget medium) · AqiBand (widget micro) · YearBand (gallery sample variant) · PickupCard (widget small hero variant) · ScopeChip wording in the label line.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- The description reads in full and wraps at AX5 and 200%.\n- In the AX frames, previews use the widget's text-only form: hero, label, next date and air reading.\n- The preview's spoken label matches the widget's combined label.\n- Greyscale previews still separate the three mark shapes and the band segments.\n- Text in previews is 11pt or larger.\n\nCOPY\nToday at your address · See pickup day, air quality and your next date at your address. · Recycling and garbage tomorrow · Bins out tonight · Unconfirmed · Official · You added this · Waste Connections · Next: Clark Public Utilities bill · in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct · Larkspur Loop · Your household · Birchfield Ct · Saved place · Only you · AQI 42 · Good · AirNow 7:00 AM · Online or mail registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct · in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct · Pickup · in 3 days · Thu 22 Oct · City of Camas. Keep system button text and size labels as the OS writes them.\n\nEDGE CASES\n- No place, or no snapshot: the baked sample. Never \"Save an address to see today here\" and never a sign-in prompt.\n- Snapshot present on Android below 15: the baked sample in dynamic colour.\n- Long description at AX5: wraps to 3 lines.\n- Dark mode and a non-blue wallpaper: previews follow the theme, while marks and EPA hues stay fixed.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of reusing the live layout bound to real state, draw a dedicated populated sample, and switch to the person's own snapshot when one exists, because the live layout with no data sells the empty state.\n- Instead of a feature-style description (\"Pickup, air and your next date — no notification needed.\"), write a verb-led sentence, because the platform guidelines ask descriptions to start with a verb. The no-notification point lives in the how-to sheet.\n- Instead of a filled mark on the sample pickup, draw the hollow one with \"Unconfirmed\", because the sample must match what the widget really shows.\n- Instead of a \"○\" typed into a caption, place the 12pt ProvenanceMark component, because the preview exists to show the marks clearly before install.\n- Instead of three size tiles in the Android picker, draw one entry with one 4x2 preview and its size label, because it is a single resizable widget.\n- Instead of redaction that collapses into grey rectangles, keep cells, segments and lanes drawn, because the shape is the pitch.\n- Instead of a device frame, marketing headline, logo lockup, gloss or gradient, show the OS picker as it is, because this is system chrome.\n- Instead of Pantopus blue Android previews, use dynamic colour, because Android previews must match the device theme.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- Someone browsing the gallery sees a populated preview at the correct size for each iOS option, and one correct 4x2 preview on Android.\n- A brand-new user never sees an empty state.\n- A user with a snapshot sees their own address, with the full scope words.\n- The medium preview shows pickup, next date and air as text, matching the description.\n- The description starts with \"See\".\n- Larger sizes show more form, not more text.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f7-widget-gallery · ios · 01-gallery-medium · light — gallery detail page with the medium preview selected (the densest), name, description and Add Widget.\n2. f7-widget-gallery · ios · 02-gallery-small · light — small preview selected.\n3. f7-widget-gallery · ios · 03-gallery-large · light — large preview selected.\n4. f7-widget-gallery · ios · 04-own-snapshot · light — the medium preview showing Jordan Lee's own data, \"Birchfield Ct · Saved place · Only you\".\n5. f7-widget-gallery · android · 05-picker-entry · light — Pantopus section expanded: one entry, one dynamic-colour 4x2 preview, \"4 × 2\", name and description.\n6. f7-widget-gallery · android · 06-drag-preview · light — the long-press drag preview at 4x2 over a home screen.\n7. f7-widget-gallery · android · 07-generated-preview · light — the Android 15 picker entry showing Jordan's own data in its single 4x2 preview.\n8. f7-widget-gallery · ios · 08-redacted · light — the redacted placeholder with its geometry kept.\n9. f7-widget-gallery · ios · 09-ax5 · light — 01 at AX5: wrapped description, text-only preview.\n10. f7-widget-gallery · android · 10-200-percent · light — 05 at 200%: the single entry with a wrapped description.\n11. f7-widget-gallery · ios · 11-greyscale · light — 01 in greyscale.\n12. f7-widget-gallery · ios · 12-gallery-medium · dark — the dark twin of 01.\n13. f7-widget-gallery · android · 13-picker-entry · dark — the dark twin of 05.\n14. f7-widget-gallery · ios · 14-notes · light — Notes: when previews switch from the sample to the person's data on each platform; the sample's dates as offsets from the render date; Jordan drawn on both platforms; the method-specific voter wording; the next-date line without its own mark; invented strings; omitted states.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: 7-12, then wait. Turn 3: 13-14.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Android picker now shows one entry with one 4x2 preview, the size label '4 × 2' and the description (a single responsive widget), not three tiles. Artboards 05, 07, 10 and 13 updated and renamed to picker-entry where relevant.",
          "Own-data label now uses 'Birchfield Ct · Saved place · Only you' on medium and large, and 'Birchfield Ct' on small (invariant 2).",
          "Replaced the literal '○' with the 12pt ProvenanceMark component, and added the rule for all preview marks.",
          "The medium sample now includes the next-date line, matching the corrected f7-today-widget and the description's promise.",
          "Notes now says the baked sample's dates are offsets from the render date, so the preview never reads past its horizon.",
          "Jordan is drawn on both platforms, which resolves the persona and platform mismatch. Reordered artboards so 01 is the dense medium preview, then small, then large.",
          "Voter hero uses the method-specific wording 'Online or mail registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct' with 'in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct'. Added the PLACE B pickup line and the City of Camas authority.",
          "Attach references updated to the renumbered f7-today-widget artboards (16 for Android, 13 for PLACE B)."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f7-widget-howto-sheet",
        "name": "Add the widget (how-to, with a live preview)",
        "platforms": [
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": true,
        "frameCount": 14,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Put today on your home screen (how-to sheet) · f7-widget-howto-sheet\n\nTYPE: NEW sheet.\n\nATTACH: Your place file (Place tab) on iOS and on Android with the \"Put today on your home screen\" row visible; the Notifications settings page; the f7-today-widget medium artboard (01) and Android 4x2 (16), which are the preview this sheet shows.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS\n- iOS: a sheet over the Place tab on 393x852, using a custom detent sized to its content (about 520pt). At accessibility sizes it may grow to the large detent and scroll.\n- Android: a Material 3 ModalBottomSheet on 412x915, sized to its content, scrolling when needed.\n- There is no web version.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE\nThe Place tab → Your place file. Entry points:\n1. The \"Put today on your home screen\" row (subline \"Pickup, air and your next date. No notifications needed.\"). This is the durable entry. It replaces the old Today nudge row, which now lives only in the place file, not as a promo on Today. The row can be dismissed (the dismissal is saved on this device only). It is hidden while the person has no place, and hidden once a widget is placed.\n2. Settings → Notifications → the \"Home screen widget\" row, so the sheet is still reachable after a dismissal.\n3. A one-line inline hint shown once, right after the person confirms their pickup day on Today.\n4. After push is declined, the Today line \"Pickup still shows here on Today · Or put it on your home screen\".\nThe hints appear at most once every 24 hours and never as a blocking modal. For someone who declined push, the widget is ranked above the briefing ask, because it is the only return trigger that needs no permission.\nWhat this sheet receives: the person's latest snapshot, if one exists.\nWhat it hands on: on Android, the system pin dialog and then the placed widget; on iOS, the OS widget gallery.\nHow the app learns a widget is placed (Notes, as behaviour):\n- Android: the pin success callback, plus a check of placed widget IDs (AppWidgetManager.getAppWidgetIds) each time the app comes to the foreground.\n- iOS: a check of current widget configurations (WidgetCenter.getCurrentConfigurations) each time the app comes to the foreground. iOS has no callback, so there is no success line, and the place file row disappears the next time the app opens after the widget is added from the gallery.\n\nWHO AND WHEN\nMaya Chen at HOME A, Mon 19 Oct, 7:45 AM. She has just seen her pickup on Today and taps the place file row. On Android she has the same data, and her launcher supports pinning. Jordan Lee (PLACE B) has no snapshot yet. Someone new has no place at all.\n\nTHE ONE JOB\nShow people their own widget first, then get it onto the home screen, with one button on Android or three pictured steps on iOS.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS\nThe eye lands first on the preview of her own widget, then on the \"Your widget\" caption, then on the action. On Android the single primary action is \"Add to home screen\". On iOS it is the three steps followed by \"Done\".\n\nCONTENT\n- Title: \"Put today on your home screen\".\n- Line: \"Pickup, air and your next date, right on your home screen. No notifications needed.\"\n- Preview: Maya's own medium widget from her 7:45 AM snapshot, at true size (338x158pt on iOS, 276x220dp on Android). It shows \"Larkspur Loop · Your household\", \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow\", \"Curbside by 6:30 AM · [ProvenanceMark XS, unconfirmed] Unconfirmed · Waste Connections\", \"Next: Clark Public Utilities bill · in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\", the 14-day strip with 6 items, and \"AQI 42 · Good · AirNow 7:00 AM\" beside the micro band. Every mark is the 12pt ProvenanceMark component, never a text character. Caption: \"Your widget\".\n- iOS steps: \"1 Touch and hold an empty spot on your home screen.\" · \"2 Tap Edit, then Add Widget, and search for Pantopus.\" · \"3 Pick a size and add it.\" · button \"Done\".\n- Android, when the launcher supports pinning: primary \"Add to home screen\" and secondary \"Done\". The steps are hidden.\n- Android fallback, when pinning is unsupported: \"1 Touch and hold the Pantopus app icon.\" · \"2 Tap Widgets.\" · \"3 Touch and hold the widget, then drag it into place.\" · \"Done\".\n- Android after the pin succeeds: \"Added to your home screen.\" · \"Done\".\n- No snapshot (Jordan): the baked gallery sample with the label \"Larkspur Loop\" and no scope words (the scope would be false for this viewer). The caption \"Sample\" sits above the preview in label 13/18, text.strong.\n- No place, both platforms: the sample at reduced emphasis with the \"Sample\" caption. The steps and the \"Add to home screen\" button are hidden. The footer has a primary \"Save an address first\" (closes this sheet, then opens Add a place; sheets never stack) and a secondary \"Done\" of equal size.\nList every invented string on Notes.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\n- The preview is the top of the sheet, above any instructions. It is clearly an illustration: it cannot be tapped, it sits on a small home-screen ground patch (surface.sunken with the widget radius), and it carries its caption. Never reuse this widget look anywhere else in the app.\n- iOS vertical budget at default text size: grabber 12 + title 28 + intro in bodySmall, 2 lines, 40 + gap 12 + preview on its patch 182 + gap 12 + three step rows at 44pt each, each with a 32pt leading line illustration, 132 + pinned \"Done\" 50 + safe area 34 = 502, within the about-520pt content detent. No scrolling at default size.\n- Step illustrations are small line drawings of the gesture, each next to its text: a finger holding an empty home-screen grid; generic labelled pills reading \"Edit\" and \"Add Widget\" (not the exact button shapes); a size being picked. Never use OS screenshots.\n- On Android with pinning supported, the primary button sits directly under the preview.\n- Degraded states keep the same layout: no snapshot uses the sample with \"Sample\"; no place follows the rule in CONTENT.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- \"Add to home screen\" opens the Android system pin dialog, which shows a preview with the system's own Add and Cancel. The app hears back only if the person adds it.\n- \"Done\", the drag handle, Back (Android) and swipe-down all close the sheet. A visible \"Done\" is always present.\n- Step illustrations may play one short loop of 300ms or less that stops within 5s. With Reduce Motion on, they are static.\n- No app haptic on pin success; the system dialog provides its own feedback. The only app haptic stays the confirm tick elsewhere.\n- No sheet opens on top of this one.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED\nProvenanceMark (XS, 12pt) · KindGlyph · FourteenDayStrip (widget medium) · AqiBand (widget micro) · PickupCard (widget small hero variant, inside the preview) · ScopeChip wording in the preview label.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- The sheet's unique title is read first, then the preview, then the steps or button.\n- The preview is one image labelled \"Your widget preview: Larkspur Loop, recycling and garbage tomorrow, on record, not confirmed; next, Clark Public Utilities bill in 4 days; next 14 days, 6 items; air quality index 42, Good.\" The sample reads \"Sample widget preview\" first.\n- Step illustrations are decorative because their text sits beside them.\n- At AX5 or 200%, the sheet reaches the large detent and scrolls. The steps may move above the preview. \"Done\" stays pinned, with scroll padding so it never covers focus.\n- Buttons are 44pt / 48dp; paired footer buttons stack at large text.\n- The Android success line is a polite status message.\n\nCOPY\nPut today on your home screen · Pickup, air and your next date. No notifications needed. · Pickup, air and your next date, right on your home screen. No notifications needed. · Your widget · Sample · Touch and hold an empty spot on your home screen. · Tap Edit, then Add Widget, and search for Pantopus. · Pick a size and add it. · Touch and hold the Pantopus app icon. · Tap Widgets. · Touch and hold the widget, then drag it into place. · Add to home screen · Added to your home screen. · Save an address first · Home screen widget · Done.\n\nEDGE CASES\n- Longest label in the preview: \"Birchfield Ct · Saved place · Only you\" (it fits one line at 338pt; it never truncates).\n- The person cancels the pin dialog: return to the sheet unchanged, with no error.\n- The launcher can't pin: show the fallback steps.\n- A widget is already placed: the entry rows are hidden. If the sheet is reached anyway, it shows the Android success line or the iOS steps unchanged. (Not drawn; listed on Notes.)\n- Offline: everything still works, because the preview is local. (Not drawn; listed on Notes.)\n- A saved place vs a home: the preview label shows the matching scope.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of an \"Add it for me\" or \"Install widget\" button on iOS, draw the three pictured steps, because iOS has no way for an app to place a widget.\n- Instead of gesture steps on an Android launcher that supports pinning, draw \"Add to home screen\", because the system pin dialog does the placing.\n- Instead of \"Tap the plus in the corner\", write \"Tap Edit, then Add Widget\", because that is Apple's current wording.\n- Instead of \"scroll to Pantopus\" in the full picker, teach the app-icon route, because it opens straight to Pantopus's widgets.\n- Instead of a preview that looks like a live, tappable widget, draw a captioned illustration on a ground patch, because a fake widget that doesn't behave like one confuses people.\n- Instead of a generic mock-up when a snapshot exists, show her own data, because seeing her own recycling day is the reason to act.\n- Instead of showing another household's scope words in the sample, show the street name only under a \"Sample\" caption, because \"Your household\" would be false for this viewer.\n- Instead of forcing everything into the default detent at AX sizes, let the sheet grow and scroll, because large text must wrap, not truncate.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- At default text sizes, the first thing on the sheet is the person's own widget.\n- On Android one tap places it.\n- On iOS the steps match the current OS wording, and the sheet fits its content detent with no scrolling.\n- \"Save an address first\" leads to the same Add a place sheet as the widget's no-place tap, and \"Done\" is always visible.\n- After placement, the place file row is gone (Android at once; iOS on the next app open).\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f7-widget-howto-sheet · ios · 01-default · light — Maya's preview, \"Your widget\", three iOS steps, \"Done\", over the place file, fitting its content detent.\n2. f7-widget-howto-sheet · android · 02-pin-button · light — the preview with \"Add to home screen\" and \"Done\".\n3. f7-widget-howto-sheet · android · 03-pin-dialog · light — the system pin dialog over the sheet.\n4. f7-widget-howto-sheet · android · 04-pin-added · light — \"Added to your home screen.\"\n5. f7-widget-howto-sheet · android · 05-steps-fallback · light — pinning unsupported, app-icon steps ending \"Touch and hold the widget, then drag it into place.\"\n6. f7-widget-howto-sheet · ios · 06-no-snapshot · light — Jordan sees the sample under \"Sample\", labelled \"Larkspur Loop\" with no scope words.\n7. f7-widget-howto-sheet · ios · 07-no-place · light — the sample de-emphasised, steps hidden, equal \"Save an address first\" and \"Done\".\n8. f7-widget-howto-sheet · android · 08-no-place · light — the Android version of 07: no \"Add to home screen\", equal \"Save an address first\" and \"Done\".\n9. f7-widget-howto-sheet · ios · 09-ax5 · light — the large detent, scrolling, \"Done\" pinned.\n10. f7-widget-howto-sheet · android · 10-200-percent · light — 02 at 200%.\n11. f7-widget-howto-sheet · ios · 11-greyscale · light — 01 in greyscale.\n12. f7-widget-howto-sheet · ios · 12-default · dark — the dark twin of 01.\n13. f7-widget-howto-sheet · android · 13-pin-button · dark — the dark twin of 02.\n14. f7-widget-howto-sheet · ios · 14-notes · light — Notes: trigger rules (at most once per 24h, never modal); the nudge row merged into the place file with its dismissed, no-place and placed states; how the app learns a widget is placed on each platform and the iOS return-from-gallery case; the widget placement event from this sheet as the funnel measure; no app haptic on pin; the height budget; the sample label rule; the rule to check step wording at each OS release; omitted states (offline, already placed); invented strings.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: 7-12, then wait. Turn 3: 13-14.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Now states how the app learns a widget is placed: Android pin callback plus a placed-widget check on each foreground; iOS a widget-configuration check on each foreground, with no success line, and the row disappears on the next open. From flow-07 step 12, the derive proposal and the critique handoff gap.",
          "Replaced the medium detent with a content-sized detent (about 520pt) and an explicit height budget totalling 502 (review major). DONE WHEN and artboard 01 updated.",
          "No-place state defined for both platforms: steps and 'Add to home screen' hidden, with equal 'Save an address first' and 'Done'. Artboards 07 and 08 updated.",
          "Preview scope string fixed ('Birchfield Ct · Saved place · Only you'). The literal '○' replaced with the ProvenanceMark component. The preview now carries the next-date line and the 7:45 AM caption, matching the corrected widget.",
          "The no-snapshot sample shows 'Larkspur Loop' with no scope words, with 'Sample' above the preview in label 13/18, text.strong.",
          "Android fallback step 3 now reads 'Touch and hold the widget, then drag it into place.' (one responsive widget).",
          "Acknowledged the merge of the Today nudge row into the place-file row, with its subline and its dismissed, no-place and placed states. Settings row kept for re-entry.",
          "Dropped the pin-success haptic (the house rule allows a tick on confirm only; the system dialog gives its own feedback). Recorded on Notes.",
          "Offline, already-placed and the widget-placement funnel event are listed on Notes as omitted states and behaviour.",
          "DONE WHEN now says 'At default text sizes' so the AX exception doesn't contradict it. Inline hint trigger reworded to 'after the person confirms their pickup day'.",
          "Attach reference updated to the renumbered f7-today-widget Android artboard (16)."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f9-nearby-cells-map",
        "name": "Cells map detail (3-join unlock, split counts)",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 20,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Cells map detail · f9-nearby-cells-map\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Nearby — cells map\". This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed:\n(1) Print the activity level inside every block.\n(2) Add a detail panel for each block, with a locked and an unlocked version.\n(3) Show homes and posts as two separate counts.\n(4) Add zoom, pan and \"Show as a list\" controls.\n(5) On web 1440, fit the map into the single 720-wide Nearby column, with the panel as an inline card under it.\n(6) The fill now means neighbor posts in the last 30 days, not verified households. Replace the old legend and the old caption \"Cells, not rooftops… shaded by how many households have verified\" with the new legend below.\n(7) Replace the dashed edges on every block with the solid ink edges below. Dotted edges now mean only \"No data\".\n(8) Rename the viewer's square from \"Your cell\" to \"Your block\", in the same word Block Founders uses directly above.\n\nATTACH: the current Nearby cells map on web 1440, web 390, iOS and Android, and the Foundations board. If Invite rewards and Block Founders are already designed, also attach the top of Nearby showing them. If not, draw only a 24pt stub of the Block Founders card above the map, and nothing more of it.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: Web 1440x900 with the left sidebar. The Nearby column is 720 wide. The map spans the column at 720x514, which keeps the true block shape. The block panel opens as an inline card directly under the map, with a visible \"Done\"; choosing another block replaces its content. Web 390x844 with the bottom tab bar: the panel is a bottom sheet. iOS 393x852: a sheet at the medium detent, with the map visible above it. Android 412x915: a Material 3 bottom sheet, with the map visible above it.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: The Nearby tab, third block, below Invite rewards and Block Founders. Entry points:\n(a) The Nearby tab: tap a block or a list row.\n(b) The \"3 neighbors join\" row on Invite rewards, whose action reads \"See the map\". It scrolls to the map, opens the panel for the viewer's own block, fades a highlight once, and moves VoiceOver, TalkBack or keyboard focus to the panel title \"Fircrest · Your block\".\n(c) \"See Fircrest on the map\" in Block Founders, with the same landing.\n(d) The deep link /app/nearby?section=map on web, and the same path in the apps. It scrolls to the map and opens the viewer's own block panel, exactly like (b).\nThe only thing handed over is which block to open. No push and no widget ever lead here, and no journey in the flows passes through this screen.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Maya Chen, owner at HOME A, Mon 19 Oct 2026 at 6:10 PM. Three neighbors have joined with her link, so her numbers are unlocked. She taps her own block, Fircrest, to see whether anyone around her posts. The locked frames show the same Maya at 6:10 PM on earlier Mondays: frame 04 on Mon 21 Sep (0 joined), frames 05 and 13 on Mon 28 Sep (1 joined), frames 06 and 08 on Mon 5 Oct (2 joined). Draw the same map levels as frame 01 in those frames.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Tap a block and either read its real numbers or see exactly what would unlock them, without the map ever feeling held back.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: The eye lands first on the grid of blocks, each with its level printed inside and her own block ringed. Second is the panel title \"Fircrest · Your block\". Third are the two separate counts: homes, then posts. The unlocked panel is for reading and has no primary button. In the locked panel, the one primary action is \"Copy link\".\n\nCONTENT: Use the house style FIXTURES. The deltas for this screen follow. List every one of them on the Notes artboard.\n- Base map: a muted street grid from east Vancouver to west Camas, showing I-205, SR-14, NE 164th Ave, NE 192nd Ave, the Camas paper mill, and Lacamas Lake at the east edge. Add a scale bar in tenths of a mile. Draw no home marker.\n- Blocks: a 5x5 grid of rectangles centred on Fircrest, each about 0.86 km east–west by 0.61 km north–south (about 1.4:1). Fircrest contains HOME A.\n- Values, as homes with a verified address / neighbor posts in 30 days:\n  - Fircrest: fewer than 10 / 14 (level 6–15), plus 3 posts from Pantopus that are not counted.\n  - Fisher's Landing: 11 / 31 (level 16+). This is the busiest block and the only one whose homes count prints as a numeral.\n  - Grass Valley: fewer than 10 / 9 (6–15). Sifton: fewer than 10 / 6 (6–15). Dawson's Ridge: fewer than 10 / 3 (1–5). Lacamas Shores: fewer than 10 / 0 (0).\n  - Forest Home: no data.\n  - The other 18 blocks show a level only, mostly \"0\" or \"1–5\".\n- Homes counts under 10 always print as \"Fewer than 10 homes with a verified address\", with no numeral and no house glyphs. Numerals appear only at 10 or more.\n- Daily neighbor posts in Fircrest, Sun 20 Sep → Mon 19 Oct (30 bars): 0,1,0,0,2,0,1,0,0,1,0,0,2,1,0,0,1,0,0,1,0,2,0,0,1,1,0,0,0,0. Total 14. The non-zero days are Mon 21 Sep (1), Thu 24 Sep (2), Sat 26 Sep (1), Tue 29 Sep (1), Fri 2 Oct (2), Sat 3 Oct (1), Tue 6 Oct (1), Fri 9 Oct (1), Sun 11 Oct (2), Wed 14 Oct (1) and Thu 15 Oct (1). Thu 15 Oct is the last non-zero bar; Fri 16 to Mon 19 Oct are zero.\n- Posts from Pantopus: short dashes below the baseline on Tue 29 Sep, Wed 7 Oct and Mon 12 Oct.\n- Fircrest's Founding window: 2 of 5 open, closes Sun 25 Oct. It opened Sun 4 Oct, so 15 of its 21 days have passed. These values must match Block Founders exactly. Fisher's Landing's window is closed.\n- Joins: Dana joined Tue 22 Sep and Luis M. joined Thu 1 Oct. Hannah K. joined Tue 13 Oct, and her join unlocked the numbers.\n- Link: pantopus.com/join/maya-4k2p.\n- Worst case: Fisher's Landing, with 11 homes and 31 posts, as numerals only.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION:\n- Block levels: fill each block by neighbor posts in the last 30 days. Light mode uses primary.100 / 200 / 300 / 500 for 0 / 1–5 / 6–15 / 16+. Dark mode uses primary.900 / 800 / 700 / 600.\n- Print the level (\"0\", \"1–5\", \"6–15\" or \"16+\") inside every block, in text.primary at label 13/18. Place it on a small label plate: surface.base, radius xs, with a 1px text.secondary edge. The plate must pass 4.5:1 on every fill in both themes. The printed label carries the meaning; the fill only supports it.\n- Block edges: in light mode, 1.5px solid text.primary ink lines. In dark mode, 1.5px solid text.primary (#E5E7EB) lines. Both clear 3:1 on every fill step.\n- The viewer's block: a two-tone ring, with an outer 2px text.primary ring and an inner 2px surface.base halo, plus the printed tag \"Your block\". In both themes, the printed tag carries the meaning; never rely on the ring alone.\n- A no-data block has a surface.base fill and a dotted text.secondary edge, and prints \"No data\" on its plate instead of a level.\n- Block size by viewport:\n  - On iOS, Android and web 390, the map opens zoomed to about 3 columns centred on Fircrest, with each block at least 96x68pt. The pan buttons reach the rest.\n  - Web 1440 shows all 25 blocks at 720x514.\n  - At AX5, the screen opens in the list view. The map prints levels only on blocks at least 48pt tall.\n- Legend under the map: \"Neighbor posts in the last 30 days: 0 · 1–5 · 6–15 · 16+ · No data\" and \"Posts from Pantopus aren't counted.\"\n- The free layer is the grid plus the levels, and it shows at every tier. Only the numbers are locked, in the panel and in the list.\n- Unlocked panel, top to bottom:\n  1. The title \"Fircrest · Your block\" and its level plate.\n  2. \"Homes with a verified address\": \"Fewer than 10 homes with a verified address\", with the caption \"Counts cover the whole block, never a single home.\"\n  3. The SlotMeter row.\n  4. \"Neighbor posts, last 30 days\": the numeral 14 and a 30-day bar strip drawn from the series in CONTENT, bars above a baseline in primary.600. Never draw a decorative or invented trend line. Draw the posts from Pantopus as short dashes below the baseline, outside the total, with the caption \"3 posts from Pantopus not counted\". Add a \"Show days as a list\" disclosure, which prints only the 11 non-zero days.\n  5. \"Last neighbor post · 4 days ago · Thu 15 Oct\".\n  6. A FreshnessLine.\n- Locked panel: the same title and level plate. Under them, in order:\n  - the sentence \"Numbers unlock when 3 neighbors join with your link.\"\n  - one row for each neighbor who has joined\n  - the remaining count\n  - \"Copy link\" as a filled primary.700 button\n  - the \"Share link\" row with its caption\n  - \"Activity levels stay visible for everyone.\"\n- Zero-join locked panel: replace the sentence and the remaining count with the single line \"No one has joined with your link yet. Numbers unlock when 3 neighbors join.\"\n- No-data panel (Forest Home): the block's name and \"No homes with a verified address here yet\", and nothing else.\n- Window-closed panel (Fisher's Landing): the numerals 11 and 31, no glyphs, and no SlotMeter row.\n- Map controls, bottom right: + and − buttons, four pan arrows and \"Center on your block\", each 44pt. Above the map is a \"Show as a list\" / \"Show map\" toggle.\n- List rows:\n  - Unlocked: name · level · homes, for example \"Fircrest · 6–15 posts · Fewer than 10 homes\" and \"Fisher's Landing · 16+ posts · 11 homes\".\n  - Locked: name · level · \"Numbers locked\" in the homes slot. A locked list never shows homes or post counts.\n- If tiles are slow or missing, draw the vector fallback. The map extent never widens by itself.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS:\n- Tapping a block or a list row opens its panel; the whole block is the tap target.\n- Pinch and drag also work, but the buttons can do everything they do.\n- The sheet opens in 250ms. On web 1440, the inline card cross-fades its content.\n- Zoom animates in 200ms.\n- With Reduce Motion on, use cross-fades and instant zoom steps, with no shimmer.\n- \"Copy link\" shows \"Link copied\" as a status message and gives no haptic.\n- \"Share link\" opens the system share sheet.\n- The sheet or card has a visible \"Done\" and also closes with Back or Escape. Opening another block replaces the content; sheets never stack.\n- On deep-link landings, focus moves to the panel title.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED:\n- PublicPointMap, cells map variant: rectangles, a printed level in each, zoom buttons and the list view. \"Show as a list\" is the user-facing label for its \"List cells\" view. On this surface it keeps the true 1.4:1 block shape instead of a 16:9 thumb, and uses the two-tone ring described above.\n- SlotMeter, Block Founders panel variant, meter row only, with no RankBadge. Omit it entirely when the window is closed or the lookup failed.\n- WarmingSkeleton, panel variant: rows for homes and posts only, with no meter-shaped placeholder.\n- FreshnessLine, OfflineNotice and InlineErrorRow.\n- TextActionRow for \"Share link\". \"Link copied\" follows its copied state (role=status).\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n- Reading order: map summary, list toggle, blocks, panel title, homes, Founding slots, posts, last post, freshness.\n- Map summary: \"Map of 25 blocks around your address. Your block, Fircrest, has 6 to 15 neighbor posts in 30 days. Busiest: Fisher's Landing, 16 or more.\"\n- Spoken labels for blocks:\n  - Unlocked: \"Fircrest, your block, 6 to 15 posts in 30 days, numbers unlocked, button.\"\n  - Locked: \"Fircrest, your block, 6 to 15 posts in 30 days, numbers locked, button.\"\n  - No data: \"Forest Home, no data yet, button.\"\n- Homes row: \"Fewer than 10 homes with a verified address in Fircrest.\"\n- Bar strip: \"14 neighbor posts in 30 days. 3 posts from Pantopus not counted.\" On iOS, the strip exposes an audio graph (AXChartDescriptor). On Android and web, the day list is the accessible equivalent.\n- SlotMeter: \"Founding Neighbor slots: 2 of 5 open, closes Sunday October 25.\"\n- Tap targets: at least 44pt on iOS, 48dp on Android and 44px on web. Blocks on phones are at least 96x68pt.\n- Meaning never depends on colour. It is carried by the printed levels, the labelled ring, bars versus dashes, and the dotted no-data edge.\n\nCOPY: \"Your block\" · \"Show as a list\" · \"Show map\" · \"Center on your block\" · \"Zoom in\" · \"Zoom out\" · \"No data\" · \"Neighbor posts in the last 30 days: 0 · 1–5 · 6–15 · 16+ · No data\" · \"Posts from Pantopus aren't counted.\" · \"Homes with a verified address\" · \"Fewer than 10 homes with a verified address\" · \"Counts cover the whole block, never a single home.\" · \"Neighbor posts, last 30 days\" · \"3 posts from Pantopus not counted\" · \"Show days as a list\" · \"Last neighbor post · 4 days ago · Thu 15 Oct\" · \"No homes with a verified address here yet\" · \"Numbers locked\" · \"Numbers unlock when 3 neighbors join with your link.\" · \"Activity levels stay visible for everyone.\" · \"Dana · joined Tue 22 Sep\" · \"Luis M. · joined Thu 1 Oct\" · \"2 more neighbors need to join\" · \"1 more neighbor needs to join\" · \"No one has joined with your link yet. Numbers unlock when 3 neighbors join.\" · \"Copy link\" · \"Link copied\" · \"Share link\" · \"People who use your link see that it helps you.\" · \"We couldn't load the numbers for Fircrest.\" with the button \"Retry\" (spoken \"Retry Fircrest numbers\") · \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\" · \"Sharing needs a connection.\" · \"Updated 2m ago\" · \"Done\"\n\nEDGE CASES:\n- Blocks with 10 or more homes show the numeral only. Under 10, the floored phrase.\n- A two-line block name, such as \"Fisher's Landing\" at AX5, wraps.\n- Zero, one and two joins each get their own frame.\n- A block whose window is closed has no SlotMeter row.\n- On a slow network, the map draws first and the panel shows the homes and posts skeleton. The SlotMeter appears only after the lookup succeeds.\n- Offline:\n  - Cached counts show their age.\n  - \"Copy link\" still works.\n  - Only \"Share link\" is disabled, with the caption \"Sharing needs a connection.\"\n- The unlock needs 3 neighbors to join with your link.\n- A viewer with no address gets no \"Your block\" ring. Put this assumption on Notes.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of a blurred, fogged or padlocked map for locked viewers, draw the full map with printed levels and lock only the numbers — because a sparse pilot map already looks empty, a blur makes sparse look withheld, and someone would spend 3 joins to find nothing behind it.\n- Instead of one blended activity score, draw homes and posts as two rows — because a blended number would shrink overnight, with no visible reason, once Pantopus posts stop counting.\n- Instead of exact small homes counts or countable house glyphs, draw \"Fewer than 10 homes with a verified address\" — because a count of 1 or 2 next to a named roster singles out a household.\n- Instead of dropping Pantopus posts silently, draw them as dashes below the baseline with their count — because the exclusion must be visible.\n- Instead of a lightness-only ramp, print each level on a label plate in every block — because adjacent ramp steps differ by only 1.16 to 1.66:1.\n- Instead of hexagons, a 6-column grid or squashed squares on a phone, draw true 1.4:1 rectangles zoomed to about 3 columns — because each target must be at least 96x68pt.\n- Instead of \"1 of 3\" or a progress bar, draw the people who joined plus \"2 more neighbors need to join\" — because completion fractions are banned.\n- Instead of zero glyphs or an empty five-segment meter for a no-data block, draw a dotted \"No data\" block and one sentence — because an empty meter reads as five open slots, and \"0\" must look different from \"no data\".\n\nDONE WHEN:\n- Within five seconds, a locked viewer sees where the activity is, knows that 3 joins unlock the numbers, and knows that \"Copy link\" is how.\n- A locked viewer never sees a homes or posts count, on the map, in the panel or in the list.\n- Homes and posts are never merged, and the Pantopus exclusion is visible.\n- No homes count under 10 appears anywhere.\n- The bar strip adds up to 14 and ends on Thu 15 Oct.\n- The SlotMeter matches Block Founders (2 of 5 open, closes Sun 25 Oct), and is absent when the window is closed or the lookup failed.\n- \"See the map\" on Invite rewards lands on an open Fircrest panel with focus on \"Fircrest · Your block\".\n- Every block on a phone is at least 96x68pt, every edge and ring clears 3:1, and every level reads in dark mode.\n- Every frame reads correctly in greyscale and works with buttons alone.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f9-nearby-cells-map · web-1440 · 01-unlocked-your-block · light — the dense default: the 720x514 map with all 25 blocks and printed levels, Fircrest ringed, and the unlocked inline card under the map.\n2. f9-nearby-cells-map · ios · 02-unlocked-sheet · light — the map zoomed to about 3 columns, with the medium-detent sheet.\n3. f9-nearby-cells-map · ios · 03-landing-from-rewards · light — scrolled to the map, the Fircrest panel open, the highlight fading, and the VoiceOver focus ring on \"Fircrest · Your block\".\n4. f9-nearby-cells-map · web-1440 · 04-locked-none-joined · light — Mon 21 Sep: the full map and a locked inline card with the zero-join line and \"Copy link\".\n5. f9-nearby-cells-map · ios · 05-locked-one-joined · light — Mon 28 Sep: Dana's row, \"2 more neighbors need to join\", and the link rows.\n6. f9-nearby-cells-map · android · 06-locked-two-joined · light — Mon 5 Oct: two rows and \"1 more neighbor needs to join\".\n7. f9-nearby-cells-map · ios · 07-list-view-unlocked · light — \"Show as a list\", unlocked rows with name, level and homes.\n8. f9-nearby-cells-map · web-390 · 08-list-view-locked · light — Mon 5 Oct: locked rows reading \"Numbers locked\" in the homes slot.\n9. f9-nearby-cells-map · web-390 · 09-busiest-block-window-closed · light — the Fisher's Landing panel: 11 and 31 as numerals, no SlotMeter row.\n10. f9-nearby-cells-map · web-390 · 10-no-data-block · light — Forest Home as a dotted \"No data\" block, with its one-sentence panel.\n11. f9-nearby-cells-map · web-390 · 11-loading · light — the map drawn, and a panel skeleton with rows for homes and posts only.\n12. f9-nearby-cells-map · android · 12-error · light — the map kept, with an InlineErrorRow in the panel.\n13. f9-nearby-cells-map · ios · 13-offline-locked · light — Mon 28 Sep: a locked panel with \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\", \"Copy link\" enabled, and \"Share link\" disabled with \"Sharing needs a connection.\"\n14. f9-nearby-cells-map · android · 14-unlocked-sheet · light — a Material bottom sheet over the zoomed map.\n15. f9-nearby-cells-map · web-390 · 15-unlocked-sheet · light — the mobile web sheet.\n16. f9-nearby-cells-map · ios · 16-ax5-list-first · light — the screen opened in the list view, with the Fircrest sheet scrolling and its rows stacked.\n17. f9-nearby-cells-map · web-1440 · 17-greyscale · light — frame 01 in greyscale.\n18. f9-nearby-cells-map · web-1440 · 01-unlocked-your-block · dark — the dark twin of 01: the dark ramp (900/800/700/600), text.primary edges, label plates and the two-tone ring.\n19. f9-nearby-cells-map · ios · 05-locked-one-joined · dark — the dark twin of 05.\n20. Notes — assumptions, invented strings (block names, values, the daily series and dash days, the link, join dates, the base-map landmarks), omitted states, and open questions. Include these items:\n- \"Blocking product question: the server hides verified-home counts under 10. Showing exact small counts, as the inventory asks, needs a privacy decision. If approved, add frame 01b showing '3' with glyphs.\"\n- \"Block names are invented. The server sends only a grid reference per block. Where do names come from, and what does an unnamed block show?\"\n- \"Block = one map square on Nearby; Block Founders uses the same word.\"\n- \"Assumes Pantopus-made posts are already excluded from neighbor counts (F9 seeder item) before this panel ships.\"\n- \"The PublicPointMap '2px primary ring' in Foundations fails 3:1 on the top ramp steps and should adopt this two-tone ring.\"\n- \"The one invitee with a verified address, Dana, lives outside Fircrest.\"\n- \"Open question: the locked Fircrest panel hides numbers that Block Founders shows directly above it.\"\n- \"The bar strip is drawn from 30 real daily counts; there is no decorative trend line.\"\n- \"A viewer with no address gets no ring.\"\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: artboards 7-12, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 3: artboards 13-18, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 4: artboards 19-20.",
        "changeLog": [
          "TYPE adds (6) fill now means posts, old verified-household caption and legend replaced, (7) dashed edges replaced by solid ink edges, (8) 'Your cell' becomes 'Your block' (review major: host contradiction; naming major)",
          "Grid corrected to 5x5 blocks of about 0.86 x 0.61 km (1.4:1); web map 720x514; phones about 3 columns at 96x68pt minimum; 24 changed to 25 everywhere (review major)",
          "Homes counts under 10 now print as 'Fewer than 10 homes with a verified address' with no glyphs; only Fisher's Landing shows a numeral; exact-small-counts is now a blocking privacy question on Notes (review major, server k-anon floor)",
          "Edge and ring contrast fixed: text.primary edges in both themes, dark ramp 900/800/700/600, two-tone 2px ring plus printed tag; Foundations ring note added (review major and minor)",
          "'area' renamed 'block' throughout to match Block Founders (review major)",
          "Added the 30-day daily series (corrected so it sums to 14 and ends Thu 15 Oct, since the reviewer's suggested series summed to 13 and ended Wed 14 Oct) plus Pantopus dash days; the day list shows non-zero days only (review major)",
          "List rows hide homes for locked viewers ('Numbers locked'); frame 07 marked unlocked; new frame 08 locked list (review major)",
          "Loading skeleton has no meter placeholder; SlotMeter appears only after the lookup (review minor, contract)",
          "Notes adds the de-curation dependency (review minor, research)",
          "Added iOS AXChartDescriptor audio graph (review minor, research)",
          "Locked frames dated (Mon 21 Sep, Mon 28 Sep, Mon 5 Oct, 6:10 PM); zero-join copy merged into one line (review minor)",
          "Deep link now opens the own-block panel; locked spoken label added (review minor)",
          "SlotMeter scoped to meter row only, no RankBadge (review minor)",
          "Retry label split into visible 'Retry' and spoken 'Retry Fircrest numbers' (review minor, contract)",
          "Artboard manifest renumbered to 20 frames; batch plan updated"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f9-block-founders-panel",
        "name": "Block Founders (rank vs tier, slot meter, postcard allowance)",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 22,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Block Founders · f9-block-founders-panel\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Block Founders\", which today is the section under Place › Your block. This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed:\n(1) The section moves to the Nearby tab.\n(2) Rank and tier become two different shapes in two different rows.\n(3) The postcard allowance becomes a counter above the address field.\n(4) A postcard front/back preview sits above the send button.\n(5) Place › Your block shrinks to one pointer row.\n(6) The slot meter and countdown pill are replaced by the Foundations SlotMeter: solid segments for taken slots, hatched segments for open ones, the label \"2 of 5 open\", and a neutral \"Closes Sun 25 Oct\" pill with no countdown.\n(7) The rank becomes a separate RankBadge.\n(8) Remove the existing \"permanent\" caption from the rank.\nKeep every other existing element unchanged.\n\nATTACH: the current Block Founders section on web 1440, web 390, iOS and Android; the current Place › Your block screen; the Foundations board. If Invite rewards is already designed, also attach the top of Nearby showing it. If it is not, draw only a 24pt stub of that card above this section.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: Web 1440x900 with the left sidebar, as a single content column at most 720 wide. This is the same Nearby column as Invite rewards and the cells map. Web 390x844 with the bottom tab bar. iOS 393x852. Android 412x915, Material 3.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: The Nearby tab, directly under Invite rewards and above the cells map. Entry points:\n(a) The Nearby tab.\n(b) The Place › Your block pointer row, which switches to Nearby and scrolls here.\n(c) Invite rewards: \"Send postcard invite\", on its hero and on Row A, scrolls to the counter.\n(d) \"See your block\" on the address-verified success screen. The rank is already assigned when the person arrives. The panel heading gets a one-time highlight fade and accessibility focus.\n(e) The deep link /app/nearby?section=block.\nThere is no push or widget entry, because Founding and referral content is never pushed. No journey in the flows passes through here. Locked controls use the pattern \"Address verification needed to <action> · Verify address\". This section hands off in two ways: \"See Fircrest on the map\" opens the cells map with the Fircrest panel open, and \"See how you earn more\" scrolls to Invite rewards.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Maya Chen, owner at HOME A, on Mon 19 Oct 2026 at 6:10 PM. Her address was confirmed by postcard on Thu 8 Oct. That made her Block Founder #3 and one of the first 5 homes in the Founding window. Three neighbors have joined with her link, so she gets 6 postcards a week. She has already sent 2 and wants to send one to the house two doors down.\nOther viewers:\n- The teaser frame shows Sam Ortega, a household member at HOME A whose address is not yet verified, on Mon 19 Oct.\n- The saved-place frame shows Jordan Lee at PLACE B, on Mon 19 Oct.\n- The later-verifier frame shows an unnamed neighbor on Fircrest who became Block Founder #7 on Tue 3 Nov.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Give each thing its own name (the rank is a place in order; the tier is the first 5, with a dated window), and show this week's earned postcard allowance before any of it is spent.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: The eye lands first on the rank badge with its large numeral 3. Second, the separate Founding Neighbor block with its five-segment meter and date. Third, the counter \"4 of 6 postcard invites left this week\". The primary action is \"Send postcard invite\".\n\nCONTENT: Use the house style FIXTURES. The deltas for this screen are below; list every one of them on the Notes artboard.\n- Header: \"Your block · Fircrest\", the caption \"Around NE Larkspur Loop\", the ScopeChip \"Your household\", and \"Address confirmed by postcard · Thu 8 Oct\".\n- Rank (RankBadge): overline \"BLOCK FOUNDER\", numeral \"3\", caption \"The 3rd home verified on this block.\" Do not print \"Permanent\". Spoken label: \"Block Founder number 3. The 3rd home verified on this block.\"\n- Tier, in its own row:\n  - Title \"Founding Neighbor\" and the line \"You're one of the first 5 homes verified on this block.\"\n  - SlotMeter reading \"2 of 5 open\": 3 segments taken, 2 open, and the neutral pill \"Closes Sun 25 Oct\". The window opened Sun 4 Oct, so 15 of its 21 days have passed. Only the roster says which slot is Maya's; the meter carries no \"You\" label.\n  - A disclosure titled \"What Founding Neighbor means\": \"A badge for the first 5 homes verified here within 21 days of the first. It's a badge only: no money and no fee change. Anyone who verifies later still gets a Block Founder rank.\"\n- Roster, headed \"Block Founders here\":\n  - \"#1 Marisol T. · verified Sun 4 Oct\"\n  - \"#2 Ken A. · verified Tue 6 Oct\"\n  - \"#3 You · verified Thu 8 Oct\"\n  - Then the text button \"See Fircrest on the map\".\n- Composer, headed \"Postcard invites\":\n  - Counter above the field: \"4 of 6 postcard invites left this week\" · \"3 base + 3 earned from neighbors who joined\" · \"Resets in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · the link \"See how you earn more\", which opens Invite rewards.\n  - Field labelled \"Neighbor's mailing address\", filled with \"2430 NE Larkspur Loop, Vancouver, WA 98684\".\n  - Postcard preview:\n    - Front: \"A neighbor on NE Larkspur Loop invited you\" / \"See what's on public record for your address.\"\n    - Back: \"From a neighbor on NE Larkspur Loop\" · \"To: Resident, 2430 NE Larkspur Loop, Vancouver, WA 98684\" · \"pantopus.com/join · code 4K2P 7M\".\n    - Caption: \"We print your street, never your name or house number.\"\n  - Button \"Send postcard invite\", with the caption \"One postcard per address. We never send reminders.\"\n- Long address (frame 18): \"17804 NE Fishers Landing Ridge Dr, Unit 214B, Vancouver, WA 98684\".\n- After the window closes (frame 06, Maya on Mon 26 Oct): #4 \"Ana R. · verified Fri 23 Oct\" and #5 \"Tom B. · verified Sat 24 Oct\" filled the last two slots. The composer reads \"6 of 6 postcard invites left this week\" · \"3 base + 3 earned from neighbors who joined\" · \"Resets in 7 days · Mon 2 Nov\".\n- Later verifier (frame 07, Tue 3 Nov): roster rows #1 to #5 as above, then the pinned row \"#7 You · verified Tue 3 Nov\", then \"Show all 7\". The hidden #6 is \"Joy L. · verified Wed 28 Oct\". The composer reads \"3 of 3 postcard invites left this week\" · \"3 base\" · \"Resets in 6 days · Mon 9 Nov\".\n- Sam's roster: \"#1 Marisol T. · verified Sun 4 Oct\", \"#2 Ken A. · verified Tue 6 Oct\", \"#3 Maya C. · verified Thu 8 Oct\". No row says \"You\".\n- Saved place (Jordan): the header reads \"Your saved place's block · Birchfield\" with the ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\". Roster: \"#1 Priya S. · verified Wed 30 Sep\".\n- Worst case: a roster of 12 founders shows the first 5, then \"Show all 12\". The rank numeral can have 2 digits (#12).\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION:\n- Rank and tier are two shapes in two rows, and they never share a sentence.\n  - RankBadge: a squared badge (radius md) on surface.sunken, with the numeral in h1.\n  - Tier block: a card row with the SlotMeter spanning its width.\n    - Five bounded capsule segments. Taken segments are solid primary.600. Open segments have a diagonal hatch in text.secondary ink.\n    - The numeral label, and a 2px elapsed bar in neutral tokens.\n    - The date pill, in surface.sunken with text.strong.\n- The five abstract segments must look nothing like the four round density dots in the address preview.\n- Allowance glyph row, directly above the field: six postcard glyphs in two labelled groups.\n  - \"Base\": 3 plain glyphs.\n  - \"Earned\": 3 glyphs, each with a small \"+\" corner badge.\n  - The 2 used glyphs (both base) carry a diagonal strike on a sunken fill, with the caption \"Used 2\".\n  - Draw glyph outlines in text.secondary ink. Mark used glyphs with a strike, never with filled versus hollow.\n- Dark twins: surface.sunken is the same colour as surface.base, so give the RankBadge a 1px text.secondary edge, and let used glyphs rely on the strike and the caption, not on the fill.\n- The preview is two side-by-side thumbnails at 3:2. Tapping one enlarges it in place, with a visible \"Show smaller\" text button (44pt).\n- Degrade:\n  - When the window is closed or full, drop the SlotMeter, the elapsed bar and the date pill, with no message.\n  - A viewer who is one of the first 5 keeps a static row with the title \"Founding Neighbor\" and the line \"You're one of the first 5 homes verified on this block.\", with no meter, pill or date.\n  - A viewer who is not one of the first 5 gets no tier row and shows the rank only.\n  - When the slot lookup fails, leave the whole tier block out and draw no skeleton for it.\n- Unverified teaser (Sam): the roster, no RankBadge, no SlotMeter, and two LockedActionRows, one in the rank slot and one in the composer slot.\n- Saved place (Jordan): show the Birchfield roster, no RankBadge, no SlotMeter, no composer and no LockedActionRow. A plain row replaces the meter and the composer, with the sentence \"Block Founder ranks are for verified homes. Start by claiming this address.\" and a separate text button \"Claim this address\".\n- Place pointer row: \"Your block · Fircrest\", the caption \"Block Founders and postcard invites are in Nearby\", and a chevron.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS:\n- \"Send postcard invite\" places the order. On success:\n  - The counter updates to \"3 of 6\".\n  - The status line reads \"Postcard invite on its way to 2430 NE Larkspur Loop\".\n  - The phone gives one light haptic tick.\n- The preview updates as the address changes.\n- An enlarged thumbnail shrinks back with \"Show smaller\", Escape or Back.\n- Disclosures expand in place in 200ms. Under Reduce Motion they cross-fade.\n- Disabled controls stay focusable and read out their reason. Tapping one shows the same reason.\n- A typed address is never cleared on error.\n- From the pointer row, the transition is a tab switch plus one scroll.\n- The landing from \"See your block\" scrolls once, fades a highlight on \"Your block · Fircrest\", and moves focus to that heading.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED:\n- SlotMeter, Block Founders panel variant, including its separate RankBadge. Use the anatomy exactly as the contract gives it.\n- ScopeChip: \"Your household\" for Maya and Sam; \"Saved place · Only you\" for Jordan.\n- LockedActionRow, list-row variant, for Sam only. Jordan gets no LockedActionRow.\n- StatusChip is not used; the date appears only in the SlotMeter pill.\n- InlineErrorRow, on errorBg only for a failed send.\n- WarmingSkeleton (row skeleton), FreshnessLine and OfflineNotice.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n- Reading order: header, rank, tier, roster, counter, field, preview, button.\n- SlotMeter: \"Founding Neighbor slots: 2 of 5 open, closes Sunday October 25.\"\n- Glyph row: \"6 postcard invites this week: 3 base, 3 earned, 2 used, 4 left.\"\n- Preview images have alt text that repeats their printed words.\n- The status line and errors are polite live regions.\n- The send error's Retry is spoken \"Retry postcard to 2430 NE Larkspur Loop\".\n- Tap targets are 44pt on iOS, 48dp on Android with 8dp gaps, and 44px on web.\n- Rank versus tier is carried by shape plus words. Used glyphs are carried by the strike plus the caption.\n\nCOPY: \"Postcard invites\" · \"Send postcard invite\" · \"See how you earn more\" · \"What Founding Neighbor means\" · \"See Fircrest on the map\" · \"Show smaller\" · \"Show all 12\" · \"Show all 7\" · \"Postcard invite on its way to 2430 NE Larkspur Loop\"\n- Exhausted: \"0 of 6 postcard invites left this week\" · \"Resets in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · \"You've used this week's postcards.\"\n- Send error: \"We couldn't send a postcard to 2430 NE Larkspur Loop. This didn't use one of your postcards. Check the address and try again.\" · \"Retry\"\n- Refused address: \"We can't send a postcard invite to this address. This didn't use one of your postcards. Try a different address.\"\n- Rate-limited: \"You can send your next postcard at 6:22 PM. A short wait between postcards keeps any one block from getting a pile of them.\"\n- Teaser: \"Address verification needed to claim a Block Founder rank · Verify address\" · \"Address verification needed to send postcard invites · Verify address\"\n- No founders yet: \"No Block Founders here yet. The first home verified here becomes Block Founder #1.\"\n- Saved place: \"Block Founder ranks are for verified homes. Start by claiming this address.\" · \"Claim this address\"\n- Errors and offline: \"We couldn't load Block Founders just now.\" with \"Retry\" (spoken \"Retry Block Founders\") · \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\" · \"Sending a postcard needs a connection.\"\n\nEDGE CASES:\n- The long address wraps to two lines in the field and on the back of the preview.\n- A 2-digit rank and a 12-row roster (listed on Notes; not drawn).\n- After the window closes: Maya keeps the static tier row. A later verifier (#7) shows the rank without a tier.\n- No founders on the block.\n- The allowance at 6 of 6 (frame 06), at 1 of 6, and at 0 of 6 with the reset day.\n- Refused addresses: an address that got a postcard in the last 90 days, one that opted out, or one already on Pantopus. All three get the same neutral message and never say why, because saying why is a claim about a neighbor's home. The send error also gives no reason.\n- On a slow network, skeletons show everywhere except the tier block.\n- Offline, the composer is disabled and states its reason.\n- Tiers: T4 (Maya), T3 (Sam, teaser), T1 (Jordan, claim first).\n- No keeper, creature or leaderboard appears anywhere in this section.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of rank and tier as matching chips in one sentence, draw a squared numeral badge and a separate meter row — because if they share a shape, the rename changes nothing a reader can see.\n- Instead of a warning-tinted \"closes in 6 days\" countdown, draw the neutral pill \"Closes Sun 25 Oct\" — because a real deadline for a badge must not borrow the alarm styling kept for civic and bill dates.\n- Instead of filled versus hollow segments, draw solid versus hatched segments with \"2 of 5 open\" — because filled versus hollow means provenance only.\n- Instead of an empty or skeleton meter when the lookup fails, draw no tier block at all — because an empty meter reads as five open slots, which is a false promise.\n- Instead of removing Maya's title when the window closes, keep a static \"Founding Neighbor\" row with no meter — because she earned it, and only the meter and the date end.\n- Instead of an allowance under the button or in a toast, draw the counter above the field — because today people learn they earned a postcard only after spending one.\n- Instead of sending blind, draw the front and back preview above the button, showing the street-only sender line — because people should consent to what goes out in their name.\n- Instead of a live \"12 minutes\" countdown, draw the fixed time \"6:22 PM\" — because a ticking timer adds pressure without adding information.\n\nDONE WHEN:\n- A first-time reader can say which title every verified home gets (Block Founder rank) and which one is limited to the first 5 homes, with a join window that closes Sun 25 Oct (Founding Neighbor).\n- \"4 of 6 · 3 base + 3 earned · Resets in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" is readable before sending and matches Invite rewards.\n- The meter and the date disappear, with no message, when the window closes. The whole tier block disappears when the lookup failed. A first-5 member keeps the title.\n- Sam sees the roster and an explained path, with no slot promise. Jordan sees a plain claim path and no rank.\n- \"See your block\" on the verified success screen lands here with focus on the heading.\n- The word \"permanent\" appears nowhere.\n- Every frame reads correctly in greyscale.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f9-block-founders-panel · web-1440 · 01-verified-rank-and-tier · light — the dense default in the 720 column: header, RankBadge, tier with SlotMeter, roster, and composer with counter, preview and button.\n2. f9-block-founders-panel · ios · 02-verified-rank-and-tier · light — the same on iOS.\n3. f9-block-founders-panel · ios · 03-landing-from-verified · light — Nearby scrolled to \"Your block · Fircrest\", the highlight fading, a focus ring on the heading.\n4. f9-block-founders-panel · android · 04-verified-rank-and-tier · light — the same as 01 on Android.\n5. f9-block-founders-panel · web-390 · 05-postcard-preview-open · light — the front thumbnail enlarged in place, with \"Show smaller\".\n6. f9-block-founders-panel · ios · 06-window-closed · light — Maya on Mon 26 Oct: rank, the static \"Founding Neighbor\" title and line, the roster of 5, no meter or pill, and the composer at 6 of 6 resetting Mon 2 Nov.\n7. f9-block-founders-panel · web-390 · 07-later-verifier-rank-only · light — Block Founder #7 on Tue 3 Nov with no tier row, a roster with \"#7 You\" pinned and \"Show all 7\", and the composer at 3 of 3 resetting Mon 9 Nov.\n8. f9-block-founders-panel · ios · 08-unverified-teaser · light — Sam: the roster with \"#3 Maya C.\", two LockedActionRows, no meter.\n9. f9-block-founders-panel · web-390 · 09-saved-place-only · light — Jordan at PLACE B: the Birchfield header and roster, the plain claim sentence, and the \"Claim this address\" text button; no meter and no composer.\n10. f9-block-founders-panel · web-390 · 10-no-founders-yet · light — the empty roster sentence.\n11. f9-block-founders-panel · ios · 11-allowance-exhausted · light — 0 of 6, the reset day, and send disabled with its reason.\n12. f9-block-founders-panel · android · 12-send-error · light — the address kept and the neutral error with \"Retry\" on errorBg. Below the frame, a small labelled inset shows the refused-address message.\n13. f9-block-founders-panel · web-390 · 13-rate-limited · light — \"at 6:22 PM\".\n14. f9-block-founders-panel · ios · 14-loading · light — row skeletons, and no tier skeleton.\n15. f9-block-founders-panel · android · 15-error · light — the panel InlineErrorRow.\n16. f9-block-founders-panel · ios · 16-offline · light — composer disabled, with the age shown.\n17. f9-block-founders-panel · web-1440 · 17-place-pointer-row · light — Place › Your block reduced to one row.\n18. f9-block-founders-panel · ios · 18-ax5 · light — the badge above the tier, glyphs wrapping, the preview stacked, and the long address wrapping in the field and on the preview back.\n19. f9-block-founders-panel · web-1440 · 19-greyscale · light — frame 01 in greyscale.\n20. f9-block-founders-panel · web-1440 · 01-verified-rank-and-tier · dark — the dark twin of 01, with the RankBadge edge.\n21. f9-block-founders-panel · ios · 11-allowance-exhausted · dark — the dark twin of 11, with used glyphs shown by strike and caption.\n22. Notes — assumptions, invented strings, omitted states and open questions.\n- Invented strings: Fircrest, Birchfield, the neighbor addresses (including the long one), the code, and the roster names and dates.\n- Omitted states: allowance at 1 of 6; a 2-digit rank and a 12-row roster with \"Show all 12\".\n- Assumptions:\n  - After the window closes, a first-5 member keeps a static title.\n  - The window is never extended or reopened silently; a reopened window would carry a stated reason.\n  - Frame 03 shows the landing with today's data for comparability; a real landing happens on the verification day.\n  - Block = one map square on Nearby; the cells map uses the same word.\n- Open questions:\n  - Does the rank survive staleness, move-out and re-verification? A \"Permanent\" caption is allowed only if the data model guarantees it.\n  - When the lookup fails, should a first-5 member's own title still show?\n  - Does the allowance reset on a fixed Monday, or 7 days after each send?\n  - Can a postcard be cancelled before the print cut-off? If yes, the status line gains \"Cancel this postcard\" until then.\n  - Should a clearer name than \"Founding Neighbor\" be tested?\n  - The 10-join referral reward is labelled \"Founding Neighbor badge\" on the server, which collides with the first-5 tier. It needs a new name before launch.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: artboards 7-12, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 3: artboards 13-18, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 4: artboards 19-22.",
        "changeLog": [
          "DONE WHEN rewritten so the Founding Neighbor title is not described as expiring (review major)",
          "THE ONE JOB no longer calls the rank permanent; change list adds (8) remove the 'permanent' caption; Permanent question kept on Notes (review minor, contract SlotMeter copy rule)",
          "Added: no keeper, creature or leaderboard in this section (review minor, research)",
          "Jordan's frame now shows the Birchfield roster (invented row listed on Notes), with no SlotMeter or composer; the claim row replaces both (review minor)",
          "Dark twins: RankBadge gets a 1px text.secondary edge; used glyphs rely on strike and caption (review minor, tokens)",
          "Notes: frame 03 uses today's data for comparability (review minor)",
          "Notes: the window is never silently extended or reopened (review minor, research)",
          "Notes: block = one map square; cells map aligned to 'block' (review minor)",
          "Frame 06 composer set to 6 of 6 resetting Mon 2 Nov; frame 07 composer set to 3 of 3 resetting Mon 9 Nov (review minor)",
          "Sam's roster reads '#3 Maya C.' with no 'You'; Sam's layout spelled out (review minor)",
          "2-digit rank and 12-row roster added to Notes' omitted states (review minor)",
          "Disclosure renamed 'What Founding Neighbor means'; enlarged preview gets 'Show smaller', Escape and Back (review minor)",
          "Send error action is now 'Retry' with a spoken target; panel error Retry also names its target; concrete long address added and used in frame 18 (review minor, contract)",
          "Notes: open question on cancelling a postcard before the print cut-off (review minor, brief P19)",
          "Added the hand-offs (map and Invite rewards) to the arrival section, per flows"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f9-invite-rewards-card",
        "name": "Invite rewards (what a join actually pays)",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": true,
        "frameCount": 21,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Invite rewards · f9-invite-rewards-card\n\nTYPE: NEW card, placed inside the existing designed screen \"Nearby\". That host screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed: add this card as the first card on the tab.\n- On web the card is entirely new.\n- On iOS and Android it replaces the referral block that currently sits in the profile insight cards. Match that block's frame, padding and type, and treat the contents below as new. Do not draw the profile without the block; list its removal on Notes.\n\nATTACH: the current Nearby tab on web 1440, web 390, iOS and Android; the current iOS and Android profile referral block; the Foundations board. Generate this card before Block Founders and the cells map. Below this card, draw only a 24pt stub of the next card.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: Web 1440x900 with the left sidebar. Content sits in a single Nearby column, at most 720 wide, shared with Block Founders and the cells map. Web 390x844 with the bottom tab bar. iOS 393x852. Android 412x915, Material 3.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: The top of the Nearby tab, above Block Founders and the cells map. People arrive by:\n(a) Opening the Nearby tab.\n(b) Tapping \"See what this earns\" on the post-share confirmation, the status line shown after a completed share of the neighbor link on another surface. That confirmation belongs to the sharing surface and is not drawn here.\n(c) Tapping \"See how you earn more\" under the Block Founders counter. This scrolls here with a one-time highlight fade and moves focus to the card title.\n(d) The deep link /app/nearby?section=rewards. A signed-out visitor is sent to sign-in, then returned here.\nThe card hands off in two ways:\n- \"Send postcard invite\" scrolls to the Block Founders counter.\n- \"See the map\" goes to the cells map with the viewer's block open.\nThe card is never pushed, and no widget shows it. No journey in the flows passes through it.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Maya Chen, owner at HOME A, Mon 19 Oct 2026, 6:10 PM. Her address was verified on Thu 8 Oct. She shared her link in September. Three neighbors have joined, she has sent 2 postcards this week, and she opens Nearby to see what that got her. The zero-, one- and two-join frames are counterfactual fixtures, also dated Mon 19 Oct: Maya, verified, with 2 postcards sent, as if 0, 1 or 2 neighbors had joined. Other frames show different viewers on the same day: Sam Ortega, a household member whose address is not verified, and Jordan Lee at PLACE B.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Say honestly what each neighbor who joins earns the person, right where the link is copied.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: The eye lands first on the link row with \"Copy link\", then on the hero \"6 postcard invites this week\", then on the two unlocked reward rows. The primary action is \"Copy link\".\n\nCONTENT: Use the house style FIXTURES. The deltas for this screen follow. List every one of them on the Notes artboard.\n- Title: \"Invite rewards\".\n- Link row:\n  - Label \"Your link for neighbors\" · \"pantopus.com/join/maya-4k2p\" · \"Copy link\" · \"Share link\".\n  - Below: \"People who open your link see that you can earn postcard invites when neighbors join, and they get their own address reading.\" · \"Preview what they see\".\n- Hero (h2): \"6 postcard invites this week\". Under it: \"3 base + 3 earned · 4 left\" · \"Resets in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · the text button \"Send postcard invite\". These numbers match the Block Founders counter \"4 of 6 postcard invites left this week\".\n- Stage ledger:\n  - Steps: \"Invited 11\" → \"Joined 3\" → \"Address verified 1\", with the caption \"Rewards count neighbors who join.\"\n  - A \"See who joined\" disclosure opens three rows: \"Dana · joined Tue 22 Sep · address verified\" · \"Luis M. · joined Thu 1 Oct · address not verified yet\" · \"Hannah K. · joined Tue 13 Oct · address not verified yet\".\n  - Dana lives in Camas, outside Fircrest.\n- Reward rows. They come from the server, one row each:\n  - Row A, unlocked: \"Each neighbor who joins: +1 postcard invite every week, up to +3\" · \"Earning +3 · the most you can earn\" · trailing label \"Send postcard invite\".\n  - Row B, unlocked: \"3 neighbors join: see homes, open founder slots and posts for each block on the map\" · \"Unlocked\" · trailing label \"See the map\".\n  - Row C, the next locked row: \"10 neighbors join: a badge for bringing 10 neighbors\" · \"7 more neighbors need to join\". The server labels this reward \"Founding Neighbor badge\". Do not print that label, because it is the name of the first-5 tier shown in Block Founders directly below.\n  - \"More rewards (1)\". Expanded, it shows Row D: \"25 neighbors join: Block Builder badge\" · \"22 more neighbors need to join\".\n- Locked-row expansions (one sentence each):\n  - Row A: \"An extra postcard invite every week for each neighbor who joins, up to 3 more.\"\n  - Row B: \"See homes and posts for every block on the Nearby map.\"\n  - Row C: \"A badge next to your name on posts once 10 neighbors join with your link.\"\n  - Row D: \"The Block Builder badge next to your name once 25 neighbors join.\"\n- The \"Preview what they see\" sheet, titled \"What your neighbors see\": \"Maya invited you to Pantopus\" · \"See what's on public record for your address: flood, wildfire, air and radon.\" · \"Maya can earn extra postcard invites when neighbors join with this link.\" · \"Type your address\". It has a visible \"Done\".\n- Card footer, the last lines of the card: the FreshnessLine \"Updated 4m ago\", the caption \"New joins can take up to 5 minutes to show.\", then the ScopeChip sentence \"Only you will see this.\"\n- Sam's frame (T3, address not verified): link \"pantopus.com/join/sam-7h3d\", and no one has joined yet.\n- Jordan's frame (T1, saved place): link \"pantopus.com/join/jordan-9q4r\", and no one has joined yet.\n- Worst case: a 14-word reward label and a 4-word label both fit in two lines without reflow. A fifth row sent by the server fits the same rhythm.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION:\n- Order: the link and the payoff share one card. The link row comes first, then the hero, then the ledger, then the reward rows, then the footer. The card never opens on something the person has not earned.\n- \"Copy link\" is the only filled button. The hero's \"Send postcard invite\" is a text button (primary.700, 44pt, no fill).\n- The ledger is three labelled steps joined by arrows, each with its count next to its words. Draw no bar, ring or percentage. In the \"See who joined\" rows, each person's stage is printed in words at the end of the row.\n- Unlocked rows:\n  - Unlocked rows sit on surface.base with a 3px primary.600 left rail.\n  - An unlocked row with a verb (Rows A and B) shows the trailing verb label and a chevron, never filled, and the whole row is the tap target.\n  - An unlocked badge row (Rows C and D) shows \"Unlocked · shown next to your name on posts\". It has no verb and no chevron, and it is not a tap target.\n- Locked rows sit on surface.sunken with a 3px left rail in text.secondary ink. Their requirement is printed in text.strong where the chevron would be.\n- Dark twins: surface.sunken equals surface.base, so the rail colour and the printed requirement or \"Unlocked\" word carry the difference, and locked rows get a 1px text.secondary edge.\n- Show only the unlocked rows plus the next locked row. Collapse everything else into \"More rewards (N)\".\n- The disclosure line in the preview sheet is the same at every join count, including at the +3 cap.\n- Zero joins (counterfactual):\n  - Hero: \"3 postcard invites this week\" · \"3 base · 1 left\" · \"Resets in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\".\n  - Ledger: \"No one has used your link yet.\"\n  - Row A is the next locked row, with \"1 more neighbor needs to join\". Then \"More rewards (3)\".\n- One join (counterfactual):\n  - Hero: \"4 postcard invites this week\" · \"3 base + 1 earned · 2 left\" · \"Resets in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\".\n  - Row A reads \"Earning +1 so far\".\n  - Row B is next, with \"2 more neighbors need to join\". Then \"More rewards (2)\".\n- Two joins (counterfactual, also the stale frame):\n  - Hero: \"5 postcard invites this week\" · \"3 base + 2 earned · 3 left\" · \"Resets in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\".\n  - Row A reads \"Earning +2 so far\".\n  - Row B is next, with \"1 more neighbor needs to join\". Then \"More rewards (2)\".\n- Address not verified (Sam):\n  - A LockedActionRow in the hero slot: \"Address verification needed to send postcard invites · Verify address\".\n  - Row A is the next locked row: \"Each neighbor who joins: +1 postcard invite every week, up to +3, once your address is verified\" · \"1 more neighbor needs to join\". Then \"More rewards (3)\".\n  - The link row works as normal.\n- Saved place (Jordan):\n  - No LockedActionRow. A plain row in the hero slot: \"Postcard invites are for verified homes. Start by claiming this address.\" with a separate text button \"Claim this address\".\n  - Row A is the next locked row with the same \"once your address is verified\" ending and \"1 more neighbor needs to join\". Then \"More rewards (3)\". The link row works.\n- Degrade: if the rewards data fails, show the link row with \"Copy link\" and an InlineErrorRow under it. The link works in every state.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS:\n- \"Copy link\" copies the link and shows \"Link copied\" as a status message. It gives no haptic.\n- \"Share link\" opens the system share sheet, titled \"See what's on public record for your address\". Never draw a custom chooser. Cancelling is neutral.\n- An unlocked row with a verb is one tap target and goes to its destination. Tapping a locked row expands it in place to its one sentence; it never navigates.\n- Disclosures open and close in 200ms. Under Reduce Motion they cross-fade.\n- The preview sheet has \"Done\" and also closes with Back or Escape.\n- When a tier unlocks, the row simply switches to unlocked. Draw no confetti and no count-up.\n- Arriving from Block Founders: one scroll, a one-time highlight fade on the card, and focus on \"Invite rewards\".\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED:\n- ScopeChip, footer sentence form: \"Only you will see this.\", as the card's last line.\n- \"Copy link\" is a filled primary.700 button. Its \"Link copied\" status follows the TextActionRow copied state (role=status).\n- TextActionRow for \"Share link\" and \"Preview what they see\".\n- FreshnessLine \"Updated 4m ago\", followed by the plain caption \"New joins can take up to 5 minutes to show.\" There is no Refresh control.\n- LockedActionRow, list-row variant, in the hero slot, for Sam only.\n- WarmingSkeleton (row skeleton), InlineErrorRow and OfflineNotice.\n- SlotMeter is not drawn here. Founding details live in Block Founders.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n- Reading order: title, link, copy, share, disclosure, hero, ledger, rows, more, footer.\n- Ledger spoken label: \"11 invited, 3 joined, 1 with a verified address.\"\n- Joined rows spoken labels match the visible words: \"Dana, joined September 22, address verified.\" · \"Luis M., joined October 1, address not verified yet.\" · \"Hannah K., joined October 13, address not verified yet.\"\n- Each reward row is one element, for example \"10 neighbors join: a badge for bringing 10 neighbors. Locked. 7 more neighbors need to join.\"\n- The error Retry is spoken \"Retry invite rewards\".\n- The link can be spoken letter by letter on request.\n- \"Link copied\" and the FreshnessLine are polite live regions.\n- Targets are 44pt on iOS, 48dp on Android with 8dp gaps, and 44px on web.\n- Locked versus unlocked is shown by surface, rail and words, never by opacity alone.\n\nCOPY: \"Invite rewards\" · \"Your link for neighbors\" · \"Only you will see this.\" · \"Copy link\" · \"Link copied\" · \"Share link\" · \"Preview what they see\" · \"What your neighbors see\" · \"Done\" · \"Send postcard invite\" · \"See the map\" · \"See who joined\" · \"Rewards count neighbors who join.\" · \"No one has used your link yet.\" · \"More rewards (1)\" · \"Show fewer\" · \"Unlocked\" · \"Unlocked · shown next to your name on posts\" · \"Updated 4m ago\" · \"New joins can take up to 5 minutes to show.\" · \"We couldn't load your rewards just now.\" with \"Retry\" · \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\" · \"Sharing needs a connection.\" · \"Address verification needed to send postcard invites · Verify address\" · \"Postcard invites are for verified homes. Start by claiming this address.\" · \"Claim this address\"\n- Entry string owned by the post-share confirmation, not drawn here: \"See what this earns\".\n- All rewards unlocked (Maya with 26 joined): Rows A and B read \"Unlocked\" with their verbs, and Row A also reads \"Earning +3 · the most you can earn\". Rows C and D read \"Unlocked · shown next to your name on posts\".\n\nEDGE CASES:\n- A long link wraps rather than truncating.\n- Large counts, such as \"Invited 140 · Joined 26 · Address verified 9\".\n- Zero, one, two and all-unlocked each get their own frame.\n- Right after a join the counts can be stale. They still read 2, with \"Updated 4m ago\" and the 5-minute caption.\n- On a slow network the link row shows first, and everything else shows skeletons.\n- Offline, the link can still be copied. \"Share link\" is disabled with \"Sharing needs a connection.\"\n- The card never shows cash, Earn, priority matching or gig matching.\n- The card offers no contact import, no bulk invite and no \"remind them\" control.\n- Tier variants: T4 (Maya), T3 (Sam, locked allowance) and T1 (Jordan, claim first).\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of listing every locked tier with distant counts, draw the unlocked rows, the next locked row and \"More rewards (N)\" — because far-off goals mostly record a shortfall.\n- Instead of \"An extra postcard invite this week\", write the real rule, \"+1 every week, up to +3\" — because the reward repeats and has a cap, and people should see both.\n- Instead of \"Maya gets an extra postcard invite each week when you join\", write \"Maya can earn extra postcard invites when neighbors join with this link.\" — because at the cap another join earns her nothing, and a misstated reward is deceptive.\n- Instead of \"Block Builder, and 6 postcard invites a week permanently\", write only \"Block Builder badge\" — because at 3 joins the person already has 6 a week.\n- Instead of \"3 joined · 11 invited\", draw the stages Invited → Joined → Address verified, and print each person's stage — because progress should match what counts.\n- Instead of a percentage, ring, progress bar or \"+1 of up to +3\", draw counts and \"7 more neighbors need to join\" — because nothing here should read as a completion fraction.\n- Instead of dimming locked rows, draw a sunken row with its requirement in words — because a locked row should state a requirement, not show a faded promise.\n- Instead of a leaderboard, lottery, mystery reward, keeper or confetti on this card, show only the viewer's own counts and fixed rewards — because social comparison and chance rewards lower motivation and pressure people.\n- Instead of printing \"Founding Neighbor badge\" on the 10-join row, draw \"a badge for bringing 10 neighbors\" — because that name belongs to the first-5 tier directly below.\n\nDONE WHEN:\n- In five seconds a reader can copy the link and say what they have already earned: 6 a week, 3 of them earned.\n- The allowance numbers and the reset line match Block Founders exactly.\n- Every statement about the reward, including the recipient preview, stays true at the +3 cap.\n- Every unlocked row with a verb lands on a real screen: the counter or the map. Badge rows are clearly not buttons.\n- The words \"Founding Neighbor\" appear nowhere on this card.\n- Sam and Jordan never see an allowance they cannot use.\n- The zero state feels usable, not like a failure.\n- The card still works when the rewards data fails.\n- Every frame reads correctly in greyscale.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f9-invite-rewards-card · web-1440 · 01-three-joined · light — the dense default at the top of the 720 Nearby column, with a 24pt stub below.\n2. f9-invite-rewards-card · ios · 02-three-joined · light — the same on iOS.\n3. f9-invite-rewards-card · android · 03-three-joined · light — the same on Android.\n4. f9-invite-rewards-card · web-390 · 04-none-joined · light — the realistic pilot state (counterfactual Maya, 0 joins), Row A as next locked row.\n5. f9-invite-rewards-card · ios · 05-one-joined · light — \"Earning +1 so far\", \"2 left\" and \"More rewards (2)\".\n6. f9-invite-rewards-card · web-390 · 06-all-unlocked · light — four unlocked rows; badge rows have no chevron.\n7. f9-invite-rewards-card · ios · 07-address-not-verified · light — Sam: the LockedActionRow in the hero slot, and Row A as the next locked row with the conditional wording.\n8. f9-invite-rewards-card · android · 08-saved-place-only · light — Jordan: the plain claim row in the hero slot.\n9. f9-invite-rewards-card · ios · 09-who-joined-and-more-expanded · light — both disclosures open, with a printed stage on each person.\n10. f9-invite-rewards-card · web-390 · 10-join-preview-sheet · light — \"What your neighbors see\", with the cap-safe disclosure line.\n11. f9-invite-rewards-card · ios · 11-loading · light — the link row plus row skeletons.\n12. f9-invite-rewards-card · android · 12-error · light — the link row plus the InlineErrorRow.\n13. f9-invite-rewards-card · web-390 · 13-stale-after-join · light — the two-join content, \"Updated 4m ago\", and the 5-minute caption.\n14. f9-invite-rewards-card · ios · 14-link-copied · light — the copied state.\n15. f9-invite-rewards-card · android · 15-offline · light — copy enabled, share disabled with its reason.\n16. f9-invite-rewards-card · ios · 16-ax5 · light — rows stacked, ledger vertical.\n17. f9-invite-rewards-card · web-1440 · 17-greyscale · light — frame 01 in greyscale.\n18. f9-invite-rewards-card · web-1440 · 18-landing-from-block-founders · light — the highlight fading and a focus ring on \"Invite rewards\".\n19. f9-invite-rewards-card · web-1440 · 01-three-joined · dark — the dark twin of 01, with rails, words and locked-row edges carrying the difference.\n20. f9-invite-rewards-card · web-390 · 04-none-joined · dark — the dark twin of 04.\n21. Notes — assumptions, invented strings, omitted states and open questions.\n- Invented strings: the links, names, join dates and stages; the share title; the preview copy; the badge-row wording; the locked-row expansion sentences; \"See what this earns\", owned by the post-share confirmation.\n- Omitted states: signed-out, where /app/nearby?section=rewards redirects to sign-in and then returns here. The post-share confirmation that carries \"See what this earns\". The profile insight cards on iOS and Android lose the referral block; no frame is drawn for that.\n- Assumptions: the zero-, one- and two-join frames are counterfactual fixtures of a verified Maya on Mon 19 Oct with 2 postcards sent. Dana, the one invitee with a verified address, lives outside Fircrest. Unlocked badges show next to the person's name on posts. The FreshnessLine has no Refresh control because the server caches for 5 minutes.\n- Disclosure rule: the recipient disclosure must stay true at the cap. Variants considered: below the cap, \"Maya gets an extra postcard invite each week when you join\"; at the cap, \"Maya earns a badge when enough neighbors join.\" The drawn line, \"Maya can earn extra postcard invites when neighbors join with this link.\", is used at every count.\n- Blocking product question: the server label \"Founding Neighbor badge\" collides with the first-5 tier, so the reward needs a new name before launch.\n- Other open questions:\n  - Do earned invites accrue before address verification?\n  - Which stage counts as a join?\n  - Does the join page name the sender?\n  - The title \"Invite rewards\" overlaps the household term \"Invite\".\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: artboards 7-12, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 3: artboards 13-18, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 4: artboards 19-21.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Recipient disclosure rewritten to stay true at the +3 cap ('Maya can earn extra postcard invites when neighbors join with this link.'), fixed at every count; link-row caption softened to match; both variants and the rule are on Notes (two review majors, FTC research)",
          "Zero, one and two-join frames reframed as counterfactual fixtures of a verified Maya on Mon 19 Oct; 'her first week' removed (review major)",
          "Added bans on leaderboard, lottery, mystery reward and keeper, and on contact import, bulk invite and 'remind them' (review major, per-surface change and research)",
          "Sam uses the LockedActionRow list-row variant in the hero slot (two review minors, contract)",
          "Entry (b) host named as the post-share confirmation; 'See what this earns' added to COPY and Notes as an omitted, invented string (two review minors)",
          "Row B now mentions open founder slots without printing 'Founding Neighbor'; uses 'block' (review minor)",
          "Every joined row prints its stage, matching the spoken labels; Hannah's spoken label added (two review minors)",
          "Every hero variant carries 'N left' (1, 2, 3 and 4 left, with 2 sent) and a separate 'Resets in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct' line matching Block Founders (review minor)",
          "Dark twins: rail and words carry locked vs unlocked, and locked rows get a 1px edge (review minor, tokens)",
          "Sam and Jordan show Row A as the next locked row with '1 more neighbor needs to join' and 'More rewards (3)'; the Row B mention is removed (review minor)",
          "All-unlocked copy aligned with the badge-row layout rule (review minor)",
          "Hero 'Send postcard invite' is a text button; Row A's is a trailing label with a chevron, never filled (review minor)",
          "Locked-row expansion sentences written for Rows A to D; the ScopeChip sentence placed as the card's last line under the FreshnessLine (review minor)",
          "New frame 18, the landing from Block Founders; manifest renumbered to 21 frames and the batch plan updated (review minor)",
          "Retry spoken target added (contract InlineErrorRow)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f10-mail-day-triage",
        "name": "Mail Day triage (snap-aware)",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": true,
        "frameCount": 26,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Mail Day · f10-mail-day-triage\n\nTYPE: On web this is a NEW screen, a new page at /app/mailbox/mail-day. Web has no triage page today, and the Mail Day nav item currently opens the Mail Day settings page. On iOS and Android this is an EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Mail Day\". This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed:\n- The streak chip is removed. The last-scan caption \"Last scan today, 6:04 PM\" takes its place.\n- The top app bar holds the title \"Mail Day · Mon 19 Oct\" only, with no actions. The address, ScopeChip, last-scan caption and a new \"Mail Day settings\" link sit in the header block beneath it.\n- A sticky footer that holds \"Scan today's stack\" and \"Finish day\" on every state, directly above the bottom tab bar. The empty hero's own button moves into this footer.\n- ScanMoreCard is removed. The footer button replaces it and opens the same scanner.\n- The photographed row.\n- The decision buttons, including \"Add a due date\" on dated digital rows.\n- Swipe shortcuts on digital rows only.\n- The decided row that collapses in place, and the Reviewed today undo.\n- The footer scroll padding.\n- The recap line.\n- The states below.\n\nATTACH: iOS Mail Day, populated (with ScanMoreCard and the streak chip) and the empty hero with \"Scan today's stack\". Android Mail Day, the same two. The web Mail tab with the mailbox nav and the Mail Day banner.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: Web 1440x900 and 390x844 (bottom tab bar). iOS 393x852. Android 412x915. Web gets the full state set because it is new. The native frames show the extension changes.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Mail tab → Mail Day. This is the tab's working page. Settings become a \"Mail Day settings\" link inside it.\nEntry points:\n- The Mail Day item in the web mailbox nav. It must point to this page, or the feature is invisible on web.\n- The Mail Day banner in the mailbox layout.\n- The 6:30 PM Mail Day push.\n- The Money section of the Place file.\n- The \"Scan mail\" action chip on Today (iOS). It lands here and opens the scanner.\n- Deep links /app/mailbox/mail-day and pantopus://mailbox/mailday.\nPeople also come back here from two places:\n- The capture tray. After \"Done (4)\", one photographed row appears per piece, uploading or being read.\n- Confirm what we read. The row then says \"Added to bills\" or \"Filed\" and stays in Needs a call until the paper is decided.\nConfirm what we read opens by itself only once, right after Done, when a piece is already read. If Maya closes it, or nothing is read yet, she starts it from \"Check what we read\" on the row. That is the state drawn here.\nThis screen hands off to:\n- \"Scan today's stack\": the system document scanner, then the capture tray.\n- \"Check what we read\": Confirm what we read.\n- \"Add a due date\": the Date sheet in create mode.\n- \"See the piece\": the mail piece.\n- The Date sheet, from the no-claimed-address notice. This screen owns that notice.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Maya Chen at HOME A, Mon 19 Oct 2026, 6:10 PM. At 6:04 PM she scanned tonight's stack: 4 letters. Confirm what we read opened, and she closed it to look at the list. Now:\n- The Clark Public Utilities and Larkspur Loop HOA bills have been read but not checked. The machine misread Clark's due date as Fri 13 Nov.\n- The Chase statement is still uploading.\n- The water bill's second page failed to upload.\n- Five digital pieces are waiting for a decision.\n- Six pieces are already decided, including two she scanned at lunch.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Turn tonight's paper and digital mail into decisions Maya can finish in one sitting.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS:\n1) The header text \"Mail Day · Mon 19 Oct\".\n2) The first Needs a call row: the Clark Public Utilities photo, \"$142.18 · due in 25 days · Fri 13 Nov\" (the value as read, not yet checked), and its ring mark.\n3) The footer pair, \"Scan today's stack\" and \"Finish day\".\nPrimary action: \"Check what we read\" on the first unconfirmed row. It is the only filled button on the screen.\n\nCONTENT (the house style fixtures, plus these additions)\nHeader: \"Mail Day · Mon 19 Oct\" · \"2418 NE Larkspur Loop\" · ScopeChip \"Your household\" · caption \"Last scan today, 6:04 PM\" · link \"Mail Day settings\". No streak chip anywhere.\nNeeds a call (9). The legend sits once under the heading: \"○ Read from your photo · not confirmed   ✓ You added this\". Rows keep their arrival order (tonight's scan first, then digital mail) and never re-sort while Maya works:\n1. Photo. Clark Public Utilities · Bill · \"$142.18 · due in 25 days · Fri 13 Nov\" · ring mark · filled \"Check what we read\"\n2. Photo, ring. Title \"Photo of your mail\" · line 2 \"1 of 2 uploaded · page 2 at 60%\"\n3. Photo, retry glyph. Title \"Photo of your mail\" · line 2 \"Upload failed · Retry\"\n4. Photo. Larkspur Loop HOA · Bill · \"$285.00 · due in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov\" · ring mark · outlined \"Check what we read\"\n5. Clark County Treasurer · Statement · \"Property tax 2nd half · due in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov\" · \"Decide\"\n6. State Farm · Renewal · \"Auto policy renews in 16 days · Wed 4 Nov\" · \"Decide\"\n7. Clark County Elections · Notice · \"Voters' pamphlet for Tue 3 Nov\" · \"Decide\"\n8. Capital One · Statement · \"Account ending 2290\" · \"Decide\"\n9. Waste Connections · Service notice · \"Holiday pickup schedule\" · \"Decide\"\nThe \"Decide\" buttons are outlined.\nReviewed today (6). Collapsed, it is one line: \"Reviewed today · 6\" with \"Show\". Expanded, the rows are:\n- \"Comcast · Added to bills · Paper recycled · Photo kept · Undo\"\n- \"Coupon mailer · Paper recycled · Photo deleted · Undo\"\n- \"Sam Ortega · Letter · Passed to Sam · Undo\"\n- \"Previous resident · Returned to sender · Undo\"\n- \"Fred Meyer · Ad · Recycled · Undo\"\n- \"USPS · Change of address confirmed · Filed · Undo\"\nThen \"Undo all 6\" after the last row. It appears only in the expanded section.\nBelow the list: \"Last Mail Day, Sat 17 Oct: 7 pieces\". No minutes, no time taken.\nSetup nudges: below the recap, keep the existing native setup nudge rows exactly as in the attached screenshot, at most one visible at a time. On web draw one: \"Choose which days are Mail Days\" · \"Mail Day settings\". The reminder nudge is replaced by the NotificationAsk card row on the finished state.\nSticky footer: the caption \"9 still need a call. They'll be here tomorrow.\" sits above two equal buttons, tonal \"Scan today's stack\" and outlined \"Finish day\".\nWorst case:\n- 40 pieces in Needs a call. Show 20, then \"Show 20 more\".\n- The sender \"Washington State Department of Labor & Industries\" wraps to two lines.\n- The amount is \"$12,480.00\".\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\nOne row layout for every piece, digital or photographed:\n- ThumbnailRail, 56pt, triage row variant. On digital rows it collapses completely. Never draw an empty square.\n- Title line: the sender, in bodyMedium.\n- Line 2: the kind plus exactly one fact, in bodySmall text.secondary. The fact is the short summary of the read, exactly as read until Maya checks it (row 1 shows the misread Fri 13 Nov). It is never an editor.\n- Optional ProvenanceMark S.\n- The row's action button.\nAt web-390, iOS and Android, the action button sits on its own line under the text, left-aligned with the text column, 44pt/48dp tall. Put the button in the trailing position only at web-1440.\nNot confirmed rows:\n- ProvenanceMark S in its read-from-your-photo variant (ring).\n- Row fill warningBg with a 2px warning left border. All words on it are text.primary.\n- Never red, because a read waiting for a check is not a failure.\n- No per-row \"not confirmed\" words: the legend says it once, and the button \"Check what we read\" names the next step.\nRows not read yet: the title reads \"Photo of your mail\", and line 2 shows only the ThumbnailRail upload status (\"1 of 2 uploaded · page 2 at 60%\", \"Upload failed · Retry\") or nothing. Never a blank title, a spinner or $0.00.\nUploading rows: a determinate ring inside the rail, with the ThumbnailRail text value. The percentage always describes one page. The row body keeps its spacing.\nFailed rows: the InlineErrorRow upload failed variant inside the row, and a retry glyph in the rail.\nAfter Check: line 2 shows the checked value (row 1 becomes \"$142.18 · due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\"), the mark becomes you-added (tick), and the row reads \"Added to bills · Undo\" or \"Filed · Undo\". The outlined \"Decide\" appears. A row leaves Needs a call only when it is decided.\nThe filled button: once row 1 is checked, the filled \"Check what we read\" moves to the next unconfirmed row (row 4, HOA). While a Decide panel is open, no decision button is filled; all are outlined at equal weight.\nDecide expands the row in place into a vertical list of 48pt full-width outlined action buttons with verb-led labels:\n- Photographed rows: \"Recycle paper, keep photo\" · \"Recycle paper, delete photo\" · \"Keep paper and photo\".\n- Digital rows whose line 2 has a date (rows 5, 6, 7): \"Add a due date\" first. It opens the Date sheet in create mode pre-filled with the kind (Property tax for the Treasurer row, with the amount if one is known). Then \"File\" · \"Recycle\" · \"Pass to Sam\" · \"Return to sender\".\n- A digital bill with an amount (none tonight): \"Add to bills\" first, which opens Confirm what we read without a photo.\n- Other digital rows: \"File\" · \"Recycle\" · \"Pass to Sam\" · \"Return to sender\".\nAfter a date is added, the row shows \"Date added · Undo\" and still needs a paper decision (File or Recycle).\nUnder the buttons, a separate text link \"See the piece\".\nEach decision button commits. The row then collapses in place, still inside Needs a call, to its InlineUndo triage decision line (for example \"Clark Public Utilities · Paper recycled · Photo kept · Undo\"). It stays there until Maya leaves the screen, and the Reviewed today count goes up by one. On the next visit it appears only inside Reviewed today.\nWeb 1440 widths: app sidebar 240 and mailbox nav 200 (with \"Mail Day\" selected) sit flush; then a 24 gutter, list column 648, 24 gutter, right column 280, 24 right margin, totalling 1440. The right column holds the recap, the setup nudge and the link \"Mail snaps: privacy and storage\". The footer sticks to the bottom of the list column.\nWeb 390 and native: one column. The footer sits directly above the bottom tab bar and stays visible on every state and scroll position, with scroll padding equal to its height. There is no floating button.\nWhen data is missing:\n- No photos: no rail.\n- No fact: the kind only.\n- First Mail Day: no recap.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n\"Scan today's stack\" checks for a claimed address and bill access first, then opens the system scanner. The tray opens over this screen when the scanner returns.\nSwipe: digital rows only. A trailing swipe reveals File and Recycle as shortcuts. Photographed rows have no swipe; Decide and the accessibility custom actions are the path, because every photographed piece needs a photo decision too.\nUndo:\n- A decided row keeps its Undo in place until Maya leaves the screen, then inside Reviewed today until Finish day. No countdown.\n- On a reviewed row, Undo reverses the paper and photo decision only. The row goes back to Needs a call, where \"Added to bills · Undo\" removes the bill.\n- A snackbar may echo \"Recycled · Undo\", but never replaces the row.\n- \"Pass to Sam\" notifies Sam only when the day closes. A new bill notifies the household only when the day closes.\nFinish day closes the day: every undo closes, held notifications go out, and the page collapses to the finished state.\nThe NotificationAsk card row (\"Get a Mail Day reminder at 6:30 PM?\") appears only on the finished state, directly under the finished line. It appears only when the reminder is off, and never after a push landing. \"Yes\" opens the OS permission dialog directly. \"Not now\" never asks again on its own. \"No thanks\" turns it off for good.\nMotion:\n- A decided row collapses in place over 200ms. Under Reduce Motion it cross-fades.\n- Upload rings fill without looping.\nHaptics: one light tick on Finish day only.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: ThumbnailRail (triage row) · ProvenanceMark (read-from-your-photo, you-added) · ScopeChip · InlineUndo (triage decision, collapsed in place, \"Undo all 6\") · InlineErrorRow (upload failed, provider unreachable for the load error) · OfflineNotice (queued writes) · FreshnessLine · WarmingSkeleton (row skeleton) · LockedActionRow (names who can act) · NotificationAsk (card row) · DateSheet (create mode: pre-filled kind from a dated digital row, Bill kind from the no-claimed-address notice).\n\nACCESSIBILITY\nReading order: header, legend, Needs a call rows top to bottom, Reviewed today, recap, setup nudge, footer.\nEach row is one element. Example: \"Clark Public Utilities, bill, 142 dollars 18 cents, due in 25 days, Friday 13 November, read from your photo, not confirmed. Actions: Check what we read, See the piece.\" \"Read from your photo, not confirmed\" is a new spoken name. List it on Notes.\nRings announce \"1 of 2 uploaded, page 2 at 60 percent\". Status changes are polite live regions.\nTargets are 44pt, 48dp and 44px.\n\"Not confirmed\" is carried by the ring shape, the legend and the button label, never by amber alone.\nThe footer's scroll padding keeps a focused row out from under it.\nEach decision is a button. The committed row states its outcome in words, and its Undo is focusable.\nSwipe shortcuts are also custom actions on digital rows.\nAt AX5 and 200%: the rail stays 56pt, text wraps, and the footer buttons stack.\n\nCOPY\nButtons and links: \"Scan today's stack\" · \"Check what we read\" · \"Decide\" · \"Add a due date\" · \"Add to bills\" · \"Recycle paper, keep photo\" · \"Recycle paper, delete photo\" · \"Keep paper and photo\" · \"File\" · \"Recycle\" · \"Pass to Sam\" · \"Return to sender\" · \"See the piece\" · \"Retry\" · \"Undo\" · \"Undo all 6\" · \"Show\" · \"Show 20 more\" · \"Finish day\" · \"Mail Day settings\" · \"Mail snaps: privacy and storage\".\nRow outcomes: \"Added to bills · Undo\" · \"Filed · Undo\" · \"Date added · Undo\" · \"Clark Public Utilities · Paper recycled · Photo kept · Undo\".\nRecap: \"Last Mail Day, Sat 17 Oct: 7 pieces\". Nudge: \"Choose which days are Mail Days\".\nFinished, when Needs a call is empty: \"Day finished. Every piece you added today has a decision.\"\nFinished, when pieces remain: \"Day finished. 9 pieces still need a call. They'll be here tomorrow.\"\nNever write \"all caught up\" or \"all your mail\".\nReminder ask: \"Get a Mail Day reminder at 6:30 PM?\" · \"Yes\" · \"Not now\" · \"No thanks\".\nEmpty (web and native): \"No mail added today\" / \"When the mail comes, scan the stack and decide each piece here.\" The footer shows \"Scan today's stack\" as the filled button. Finish day is hidden.\nError: \"We couldn't load today's mail. Check your connection, then retry.\" · \"Retry\".\nOffline: \"You're offline · as of 6:02 PM\". Queued photos: \"Will upload when you're back online\". Queued decisions: \"Will save when you're back online\".\nReading unavailable: \"We can't read photos right now. Your photos are saved. Add the amount and due date yourself.\"\nNo claimed address, the same strings on all three F10 surfaces: \"Mail snap needs a claimed address\" / \"Bills need a claimed address. You can still add a due date for yourself. Only you will see this.\" · \"Add a due date\" · \"Claim this address\".\nLimited access, the same string on all three F10 surfaces: \"Only Maya and Sam can see bill senders, amounts and photos.\"\nMail Day push: \"Mail Day tonight\" / \"Scan and sort today's mail\".\n\nEDGE CASES\n- The longest sender wraps to two lines. \"$12,480.00\" fits beside a two-line sender.\n- 40 pieces show 20 at a time.\n- Zero pieces show the empty state, with the footer scan button.\n- A load over 1s shows row skeletons. Under 1s, show nothing.\n- A load failure keeps the header and footer live.\n- Offline: cached rows stay readable, and decisions queue.\n- Reading unavailable: every photo row's title reads \"Photo of your mail\" with no kind and no fact, and \"Check what we read\" still opens Confirm what we read with blank fields for manual entry.\n- No claimed address (Jordan Lee at PLACE B, ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\"): the scan button opens the notice instead of a camera. \"Add a due date\" replaces the notice with the Date sheet. The sheets never stack.\n- Guest without bill access (Alex Kim): photographed and money rows read \"Bill · photographed today\". A document glyph replaces the thumbnail, and no sender or amount shows. A LockedActionRow names who can act.\n- Multi-home: the header reads \"Larkspur Loop · Your household\".\n\nINSTEAD OF\nInstead of the scan button only in the empty hero, draw it in the sticky footer on every state — because anyone with one piece queued otherwise has no way to scan.\nInstead of \"Comcast · Recycled · Undo (4s)\" with a countdown, draw a static \"Undo\" on a row that collapses in place and lasts until Finish day — because a timed or hidden undo fails people who need more time.\nInstead of a progress bar or a \"6 of 15 done\" meter for the day, draw the plain count in the footer caption — because a completion bar turns the mail into a score. Upload rings with a percentage are allowed, because they describe one page, not the day.\nInstead of a streak chip or \"7 pieces, 3 minutes\", draw \"Last scan today, 6:04 PM\" and \"Last Mail Day, Sat 17 Oct: 7 pieces\" — because streaks and timings punish missed or slow days.\nInstead of amber text or a red error for a read waiting for a check, draw the ring mark, the legend and text.primary on warningBg — because not confirmed is not a failure.\nInstead of the corrected date on an unchecked row, draw the value exactly as read — because a right-looking read removes the reason to check it.\nInstead of radio rows that commit on a tap, or a swipe that recycles a photographed bill, draw full-width verb-led buttons that pair paper and photo — because accidental or half decisions keep document photos silently.\nInstead of a floating button or a labelled top-bar action, draw the footer pair above the tab bar — because the product has no floating button, and a long label truncates beside the title.\n\nDONE WHEN:\n- A person with digital mail already queued can scan from any scroll position.\n- Every photographed read looks unconfirmed, and shows what was read, until it is checked.\n- No piece leaves Needs a call without a decision on both the paper and the photo.\n- A dated digital piece can become a Date from its row.\n- Every decided row shows its Undo where it was decided, and can be undone until Finish day, with no countdown.\n- The finished line never claims completeness when pieces remain.\n- The screen has exactly one filled button.\n- A guest never sees a sender, amount or photo they cannot access.\n- Web reaches this page from the Mail nav.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f10-mail-day-triage · web-390 · 01-populated-dense · light — the 9 + 6 case above, row 1 showing \"$142.18 · due in 25 days · Fri 13 Nov\". Draw it as a tall frame with the viewport marked. The footer sits above the tab bar, with scroll padding so the last row clears it.\n2. f10-mail-day-triage · web-1440 · 01-populated-dense · light — the web page with the stated widths adding to 1440.\n3. f10-mail-day-triage · ios · 01-populated-dense · light — extension of the attached screen: no streak chip, last-scan caption, footer pair above the tab bar, no ScanMoreCard.\n4. f10-mail-day-triage · android · 01-populated-dense · light — the same, in Material 3, with no floating button.\n5. f10-mail-day-triage · web-390 · 02-decide-open · light — after the check: row 1 line 2 reads \"$142.18 · due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\" with the tick and \"Added to bills · Undo\", Decide expanded into three outlined buttons and the \"See the piece\" link; row 4's \"Check what we read\" is now filled.\n6. f10-mail-day-triage · web-390 · 03-decide-digital-date · light — row 5 (Clark County Treasurer) expanded: \"Add a due date\" first, then File · Recycle · Pass to Sam · Return to sender, and \"See the piece\".\n7. f10-mail-day-triage · web-390 · 04-decided-in-place · light — row 8 collapsed in place inside Needs a call as \"Capital One · Filed · Undo\"; header \"Needs a call (8)\", \"Reviewed today · 7\", footer caption \"8 still need a call. They'll be here tomorrow.\"\n8. f10-mail-day-triage · web-390 · 05-just-scanned · light — back from the tray, nothing read yet: four photo rows titled \"Photo of your mail\", uploading or with no line 2.\n9. f10-mail-day-triage · web-390 · 06-reviewed-expanded · light — scrolled to the bottom: six Undo rows, \"Undo all 6\", recap, setup nudge, footer padding visible.\n10. f10-mail-day-triage · web-390 · 07-day-finished · light — \"Day finished. 9 pieces still need a call. They'll be here tomorrow.\" with the NotificationAsk card row under it.\n11. f10-mail-day-triage · web-390 · 08-empty · light — the empty state, with the footer scan button filled.\n12. f10-mail-day-triage · ios · 08-empty · light — the native empty hero, its button now in the footer.\n13. f10-mail-day-triage · web-390 · 09-loading · light — row skeletons in their final positions.\n14. f10-mail-day-triage · web-390 · 10-error · light — InlineErrorRow, with the header and footer live.\n15. f10-mail-day-triage · web-390 · 11-offline · light — queued rows reading \"Will upload when you're back online\" and \"Will save when you're back online\".\n16. f10-mail-day-triage · web-390 · 12-reading-unavailable · light — the notice; photo rows titled \"Photo of your mail\" with no kind, each with \"Check what we read\" (opens blank fields).\n17. f10-mail-day-triage · web-390 · 13-no-claimed-home · light — Jordan Lee sees the notice, which leads to the Date sheet.\n18. f10-mail-day-triage · web-390 · 14-limited-access · light — Alex Kim's guest view with a LockedActionRow.\n19. f10-mail-day-triage · ios · 13-no-claimed-home · light — the native notice. The capture tray relies on this frame.\n20. f10-mail-day-triage · android · 13-no-claimed-home · light — the native notice.\n21. f10-mail-day-triage · ios · 15-ax5 · light — the dense case at AX5, with wrapped rows and stacked footer buttons.\n22. f10-mail-day-triage · android · 16-font-200 · light — the dense case at 200%.\n23. f10-mail-day-triage · web-390 · 17-greyscale · light — frame 1 in greyscale. The ring, the legend and the button still say \"not confirmed\".\n24. f10-mail-day-triage · ios · 01-populated-dense · dark — dark twin of frame 3.\n25. f10-mail-day-triage · web-390 · 02-decide-open · dark — dark twin of frame 5.\n26. f10-mail-day-triage · web-1440 · 99-notes · light — Notes. List:\n- Every invented string: Larkspur Loop HOA, Capital One 2290, Alex Kim as a guest, the reviewed senders, Comcast and the coupon coming from a 12:40 PM scan, the 6:30 PM push time, the Mail Day push copy, the reminder ask \"Get a Mail Day reminder at 6:30 PM?\", the recap \"Last Mail Day, Sat 17 Oct: 7 pieces\", the nudge \"Choose which days are Mail Days\", \"Will save when you're back online\", \"Date added · Undo\", the unified limited-access string.\n- Row 1 shows the misread date (Fri 13 Nov) until Maya checks it; it is corrected to Fri 23 Oct on Confirm what we read.\n- Frame 1 is the state after Maya closed Confirm what we read. Chase is uploading, and the water bill's page 2 failed. The rows' senders are the ground truth from the tray.\n- The house fixture bills (Clark Public Utilities, City of Vancouver water, Comcast) are the state after tonight's confirmations. Clark and water are not on the bills list yet. Comcast was added at lunch.\n- The HOA row: the HOA dues Date already exists. The duplicate check covers Dates of kind HOA dues, so confirming offers Keep both or Replace.\n- After a date is added to a digital row, the row still needs a paper decision (File or Recycle).\n- The per-row \"not confirmed\" words are dropped in favour of the legend (a ProvenanceMark rule).\n- \"Read from your photo · not confirmed\" and its spoken name are pending additions to the ProvenanceMark contract.\n- NotificationAsk (card row) on this screen is a pending addition to the contract's Used in list. It replaces the reminder setup nudge; other setup nudges stay below the recap.\n- The reading-unavailable notice here differs on purpose from Confirm what we read's (\"We couldn't read this one automatically…\"): this one covers every photo, that one covers one piece. Both end \"Add the amount and due date yourself.\"\n- \"No mail added today\" is a deliberate exception to the glossary's \"Checked — nothing …\" pattern, because Mail Day checks nothing.\n- The Mail Day push stays triage-only. It never names a bill or an amount, and never repeats a bill reminder.\n- Open decision: if Finish day is never tapped, the day closes by itself at the next Mail Day time (or after 20 hours); undo closes and held notifications go out then. Draw nothing for it.\n- Open decision: which notification group the Mail Day push belongs to.\n- Any omitted state.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: 1-6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: 7-12, then wait. Turn 3: 13-18, then wait. Turn 4: 19-24, then wait. Turn 5: 25-26.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Row 1 now shows the misread value \"$142.18 · due in 25 days · Fri 13 Nov\" in FIRST FIVE SECONDS, CONTENT, the spoken example and frames 1-4, 21-24; only the post-check frame 5 shows Fri 23 Oct; Notes records the correction (review major, storyline with f10-extraction-confirm).",
          "Native change list now names the streak chip removal (replaced by the last-scan caption), the title-only top app bar, the Mail Day settings link, dated-row actions, digital-only swipes, the in-place decided row and the recap (review major; derive f10-1 streak chip; per-surface 'No streak').",
          "Reading-unavailable frame redrawn: rows titled 'Photo of your mail' with no kind, and 'Check what we read' opens blank fields; added as an edge case (review major, honesty rule).",
          "Swipe shortcuts limited to digital rows; photographed rows use Decide and custom actions (review major, research triage pitfall on silently kept photos).",
          "Decisions now collapse in place inside Needs a call as InlineUndo lines until Maya leaves the screen, then live in Reviewed today; motion changed to collapse/cross-fade; new artboard 04-decided-in-place (review major, InlineUndo contract, brief P19).",
          "Dated digital rows get 'Add a due date' opening DateSheet create mode pre-filled; digital bills with an amount get 'Add to bills'; new artboard 03-decide-digital-date; Notes records the remaining paper decision (review major, design doc F10 pay/remind actions).",
          "Unread rows: title 'Photo of your mail', line 2 carries only the upload status or nothing; LAYOUT and CONTENT now agree (review minor, raised twice).",
          "Ring text changed to '1 of 2 uploaded · page 2 at 60%', matching the tray's per-page pattern (tray review minor).",
          "Filled-button rule now moves to row 4 after row 1 is checked, and no decision button is filled while Decide is open; drawn in frame 5 (review minor).",
          "Recap changed to 'Last Mail Day, Sat 17 Oct: 7 pieces' with no minutes, since Sunday has no USPS mail and timings read as a score; INSTEAD OF updated (review minor).",
          "Setup nudges kept below the recap (one at a time, native as in screenshot, one web example); NotificationAsk replaces only the reminder nudge; recorded on Notes (review minor, inventory contents, derive f10-1).",
          "Web-1440 widths now add to 1440 (240+200 flush, 24, 648, 24, 280, 24); footer placed directly above the bottom tab bar on web-390 and native (review minor).",
          "One limited-access string used on all F10 screens; NotificationAsk addition to the contract noted on Notes (review minor).",
          "Notes: 6:30 PM push time, reminder-ask copy, recap and nudge added to invented strings; open decision added for an untapped Finish day (auto-close, held notifications); note on the deliberately different reading-unavailable strings and the 'No mail added today' glossary exception (review minors).",
          "Artboards grew from 24 to 26 and were renumbered; batch plan now has five turns."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f10-snap-capture-tray",
        "name": "Snap capture tray (batch session)",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": true,
        "frameCount": 26,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Today's stack (capture tray) · f10-snap-capture-tray\n\nTYPE: NEW. A sheet on iOS, Android and mobile web, and a modal on web desktop. It opens over Mail Day, which stays visible behind the scrim.\n\nATTACH: Mail Day populated on iOS, Android and web 390 (the host behind the scrim). The shipped web \"Snap and sell\" listing modal, for the drop-target pattern to copy. The Foundations board.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852, sheet at the large detent, plus one landscape frame at 852x393. Android 412x915, a full-height Material 3 bottom sheet. Web 1440x900, a centred modal. Web 390x844, a bottom sheet.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Mail tab → Mail Day → this tray.\nEntry points:\n- \"Scan today's stack\" in the Mail Day sticky footer, on every state including the empty one. It replaces the native ScanMoreCard.\n- The \"Scan mail\" action chip on Today (iOS). It lands on Mail Day and opens the scanner.\nBefore anything opens, the app checks for a claimed address and for bill permissions.\nOn iOS and Android, the system document scanner then shoots the pages, and this tray opens when the scanner returns them. Pantopus draws nothing inside the scanner.\nOn web, \"Scan today's stack\" opens this tray directly, with a file picker.\nHand-off: \"Done (4)\" closes the tray. Mail Day then shows one row per piece, titled \"Photo of your mail\" while pages upload and are read in the background. If a piece is already read at that moment, Confirm what we read opens by itself, once. Otherwise Maya starts it from \"Check what we read\" on the row.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Maya Chen at HOME A, Mon 19 Oct 2026, 6:08 PM. At 6:04 PM she scanned 8 pages from tonight's stack in one scanner session. Each page starts as its own piece. She has already tapped \"Same letter as previous\" on pages 2, 7 and 8. Page 4 is still separate. She is checking the pages before she closes the tray.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Turn a scanned stack into grouped, uploading pieces in one sitting, with no stop between pages.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS:\n1) The row of page thumbnails with upload rings.\n2) The count \"8 pages · 5 pieces\" and the audience line.\n3) \"Done (5)\".\nPrimary action: \"Done (5)\".\n\nCONTENT (the house style fixtures, plus these additions)\nTitle: \"Today's stack\". Count: \"8 pages · 5 pieces\". Live status: \"5 of 8 pages uploaded\".\nThumbnails, in scan order. The captions show page numbers only. Senders are not shown, because reading happens after upload.\n- \"Pages 1–2\": a stacked thumbnail labelled \"2 pages\", uploaded.\n- \"Page 3\": \"Uploading, 60%\".\n- \"Page 4\": \"Upload failed · Retry\".\n- \"Page 5\": uploaded.\n- \"Pages 6–8\": a stacked thumbnail labelled \"3 pages\", with the status \"2 of 3 uploaded · page 7 at 40%\".\nA percentage always describes one page, never the stack.\nThe ground truth, which is listed on Notes only and never drawn:\n- Pages 1–2: the Clark Public Utilities bill.\n- Pages 3–4: the City of Vancouver water bill.\n- Page 5: the Larkspur Loop HOA dues notice.\n- Pages 6–8: the Chase statement. Page 8 is a blank back page.\nAudience line, always visible, with ScopeChip \"Your household\" beside it: \"Only your household can see these photos: you and Sam.\"\nActions: outlined \"Scan more\" and filled \"Done (5)\", equal size, side by side.\nWorst case: 30 pages. A 12-page letter joined into one piece (\"12 pages\"). Every upload failing at once.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\nThe thumbnail row is the fixed centre of the sheet: ThumbnailRail, capture queue variant, 96x128pt thumbnails, radius md.\n- It scrolls sideways. The newest page enters at the right and stays in view. It never collapses.\n- Each thumbnail carries its own ring with a text value.\n- A joined piece is a stacked thumbnail with a page-count label. The count counts pieces, not photos.\nBelow the row sits the selection action row, hidden until something is selected.\nBelow that: the audience line, then the count and both buttons. They sit in the bottom third on native and at the bottom right on web desktop, within one-handed reach. The count and buttons stay pinned while the row scrolls.\nSelection: a 2px ink outline plus a check badge, drawn differently from the focus ring. It reveals an action row of 44pt/48dp buttons:\n- A single page: \"Retake\" (reopens the scanner for that page) · \"Delete\" · \"Same letter as previous\" (hidden on page 1). A failed page adds \"Retry\".\n- A joined letter: \"Show 3 pages\" · \"Delete letter\" · \"Split into separate pages\".\n- \"Show 3 pages\" fans the stack out in place into its page thumbnails. Each page can then be selected, with Retake · Delete · Retry · \"Separate from previous page\" (hidden on the letter's first page). \"Group again\" folds them back.\nWeb 1440: a drop target fills the left of the modal, with \"Drag photos of your mail here\", \"Choose files\" and the caption \"JPEG, PNG or HEIC, up to 25 MB each.\" The queue sits beside it.\nWeb 390: \"Take a photo\" and \"Choose from photos\", then the same queue. \"Take a photo\" opens the phone's own camera, which has a manual shutter.\nNo viewfinder chrome on web.\nWhen things are missing:\n- Zero pages (web only; native always returns with pages): one empty slot captioned \"Pages you add show up here\".\n- Scanner unavailable: the photo fallback frame.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\nSelecting:\n- Tap selects.\n- Long-press (native) and hover (web) are shortcuts that show the same action row. They are never the only way.\nDeleting:\n- Delete is instant. An InlineUndo appears in the page's slot (\"Page 8 removed · Undo\") and lasts until the tray closes. No dialog.\n- Delete is the only way to drop pages.\nScanning and uploading:\n- \"Scan more\" reopens the scanner and adds the new pages at the end.\n- Failed pages retry one by one, or all together with the bulk retry.\n- Done works with failures and keeps the failed pages queued.\n- Drag to reorder is not offered.\nClosing:\n- The sheet has no separate Close.\n- The pinned \"Done (N)\" is the visible way out.\n- Back, Escape and swipe-down all act exactly like Done. They keep every page and continue uploading. Nothing is discarded.\nChecks before the scanner: the guest check and the member check each appear once, before that person's first scan. \"Cancel\" returns to Mail Day with no camera.\nNotice sheets: \"Add a due date\" on a notice replaces the notice with the Date sheet (create mode, Bill kind). Sheets never stack.\nMotion:\n- New thumbnails slide in from the right over 200ms. Under Reduce Motion they fade in.\n- Fan-out and fold take 200ms, or a cross-fade under Reduce Motion.\n- Rings fill without looping.\nHaptics: one light tick when Done commits.\nThe tray works in portrait and landscape. In landscape, the queue is on the left and the buttons are on the right.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: ThumbnailRail (capture queue: uploading, failed, joined) · ScopeChip (chip \"Your household\" beside the audience line) · InlineUndo (removed row) · InlineErrorRow (upload failed) · OfflineNotice (queued writes) · LockedActionRow (names who can act) · DateSheet (create mode, Bill kind, from the PDF rejection).\n\nACCESSIBILITY\nReading order: title, count, thumbnails left to right, action row, audience line, buttons.\nEach thumbnail is one element. Examples:\n- \"Page 3 of 8, uploading, 60 percent. Actions: Retake, Delete, Same letter as previous.\"\n- \"Pages 1 and 2, one letter, uploaded. Actions: Show 2 pages, Delete letter, Split into separate pages.\"\n- \"Pages 6 to 8, one letter, 2 of 3 uploaded, page 7 at 40 percent.\"\nUpload status is a polite live region (\"5 of 8 pages uploaded\").\nTargets are 44pt, 48dp and 44px, with 8dp gaps. No ring sits under a delete target.\nDone (N) is always visible and always reachable.\nAt AX5 and 200%, the row becomes a vertical list with the actions inline under each page, and the sheet scrolls.\nStatus is shown by a ring plus words, never by colour alone.\n\nCOPY\nTray: \"Today's stack\" · \"8 pages · 5 pieces\" · \"5 of 8 pages uploaded\" · \"Uploading, 60%\" · \"2 of 3 uploaded · page 7 at 40%\" · \"1 of 2 uploaded · Upload failed · Retry\" · \"Upload failed · Retry\" · \"Retry 3 pages\" · \"Retry 8 pages\".\nSelection: \"Retake\" · \"Delete\" · \"Retry\" · \"Same letter as previous\" · \"Split into separate pages\" · \"Separate from previous page\" · \"Show 3 pages\" · \"Delete letter\" · \"Group again\" · \"Page 8 removed · Undo\".\nButtons: \"Scan more\" · \"Done (5)\".\nAudience (Maya's and Sam's view): \"Only your household can see these photos: you and Sam.\"\nAudience with a guest in the home (Maya's view): \"Only your household can see these photos: you and Sam. Alex can't see photos or amounts.\"\nAudience in Alex's own tray: \"You can see these photos until you tap Done. After that, only Maya and Sam can.\"\nOffline: \"You're offline. Your pages are saved on this phone and will upload when you're back online.\" Each queued page reads \"Will upload when you're back online\". The ring label may shorten to \"Waiting\" only if space forces it; list this on Notes.\nScanner unavailable: \"This phone can't run the page scanner. Take a photo of each page, or choose photos you already took.\" · \"Take a photo\" · \"Choose from photos\". On Android, add the caption \"Choose up to 100 photos at a time\".\nCamera off (iOS and web): \"Pantopus can't use the camera. Turn on Camera in Settings, or choose photos you already took.\" · \"Open Settings\" · \"Choose from photos instead\".\niOS camera purpose string: \"Pantopus uses the camera to photograph bills and letters you choose to add to your home.\"\nRejected files (web):\n- \"scan_0412.png is 38.6 MB. Mail snaps must be under 25 MB. Save it smaller and try again.\"\n- \"IMG_2231.DNG isn't a JPEG, PNG or HEIC file. Export it as a JPEG and try again.\"\n- \"statement.pdf: PDF bills aren't supported yet. Add the due date by hand instead.\" · \"Add a due date\"\n- \"notes.docx isn't a photo. Choose a JPEG, PNG or HEIC file.\"\nDrop target: \"Drag photos of your mail here\" · \"Choose files\" · \"JPEG, PNG or HEIC, up to 25 MB each.\"\nNo claimed address, before any camera, using Mail Day's strings exactly: \"Mail snap needs a claimed address\" / \"Bills need a claimed address. You can still add a due date for yourself. Only you will see this.\" · \"Add a due date\" · \"Claim this address\".\nGuest check (Alex), once, before his first scan: \"You can scan and file mail here\" / \"Only Maya can add bills here. Only Maya and Sam can see bill senders, amounts and photos.\" · \"Scan and file\" · \"Cancel\".\nMember check (Sam), once, before his first scan: \"You can scan and file mail here\" / \"Only Maya can add bills here. You can see amounts and bill photos.\" · \"Scan and file\" · \"Cancel\".\n\nEDGE CASES\n- 30 pages: the row scrolls, and the count and buttons stay pinned.\n- A 12-page letter shows one stack labelled \"12 pages\".\n- All 8 uploads fail: each page shows Retry, one \"Retry 8 pages\" appears above the buttons, and Done stays enabled.\n- Slow network: rings sit at their true value. No batch spinner.\n- Offline: pages read \"Will upload when you're back online\", and Done works.\n- HEIC files are converted before web thumbnails show, so there are no broken images.\n- The scanner is unsupported on some iOS devices and on low-memory Android phones: show the fallback frame. \"Take a photo\" uses the system camera with a manual shutter and never fires on its own.\n- Android never shows a camera-permission frame, because its scanner needs no permission.\n- \"Choose from photos\" opens the system picker with multi-select and never asks for photo-library access.\n- No claimed address (Jordan Lee at PLACE B, ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\"): checked before the scanner opens. The notice is Mail Day's and is drawn there, not here.\n- Guest (Alex Kim) and member without add rights (Sam Ortega): checked before the scanner opens. Both may scan and file.\n\nINSTEAD OF\nInstead of a Pantopus viewfinder with a strip inside it, draw a queue that opens after the system scanner returns — because the system scanners can't be customised and already handle edges and batches.\nInstead of a small delete glyph on each thumbnail and retake only on long-press or hover, draw a visible action row for the selection — because small and hidden controls get mis-tapped or missed.\nInstead of \"Photos are stored privately to your home and never shown to neighbors\", draw \"Only your household can see these photos: you and Sam.\" — because the real audience is inside the home.\nInstead of one batch spinner, or a stack reading \"2 of 3 uploaded, 40%\", draw a ring on each page with its own Retry and a percentage for one named page — because people need to see which page failed, and two disagreeing numbers read as an error.\nInstead of a one-shot picker that closes after each page, draw one tray that holds the whole stack — because a stack of mail is a batch.\nInstead of a camera-permission frame on Android, draw \"This phone can't run the page scanner\" — because that is the real Android failure.\nInstead of a camera that opens and then refuses to save, draw the address and permission checks before the scanner — because a photographed bill that can't be saved wastes the effort.\nInstead of a Close button beside Done, draw one pinned \"Done (N)\" and let Back and Escape act like it — because Close next to uploading pages reads as \"discard\".\n\nDONE WHEN:\n- Maya can scan the whole stack (4 letters, 8 pages).\n- She can join two-page letters, split them again, open a stack to remove a blank page with Undo, and see who can see the photos.\n- She can press Done with a failed page still queued.\n- Nobody reaches a camera they cannot save from.\n- Sam and Alex are told once, before scanning, that only Maya can add bills.\n- Every action has a visible 44pt/48dp control.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f10-snap-capture-tray · ios · 01-queue-uploading · light — the dense 8-page, 5-piece case over Mail Day.\n2. f10-snap-capture-tray · ios · 02-page-selected · light — page 4 selected (2px ink outline and check badge), with the action row Retake · Delete · Same letter as previous · Retry; count still \"8 pages · 5 pieces\", \"Done (5)\".\n3. f10-snap-capture-tray · ios · 03-pages-joined · light — the moment after \"Same letter as previous\"; page 3 has finished uploading by now. Pages 3–4 are a \"2 pages\" stack reading \"1 of 2 uploaded · Upload failed · Retry\"; count \"8 pages · 4 pieces\"; \"Done (4)\".\n4. f10-snap-capture-tray · ios · 04-letter-fanned-page-removed · light — the pages 6–8 stack fanned out. Page 8 (a blank back page) has been deleted, and its slot reads \"Page 8 removed · Undo\". Page 7 is selected with Retake · Delete · Separate from previous page. \"Group again\" is shown. The count reads \"7 pages · 4 pieces\" and the button reads \"Done (4)\".\n5. f10-snap-capture-tray · android · 01-queue-uploading · light — the Material 3 full-height sheet.\n6. f10-snap-capture-tray · web-1440 · 01-drop-target-with-files · light — the modal with the drop target and the queue.\n7. f10-snap-capture-tray · web-390 · 01-take-photo · light — \"Take a photo\" and \"Choose from photos\" above the queue.\n8. f10-snap-capture-tray · ios · 05-all-uploaded · light — every ring complete, \"Done (4)\" ready.\n9. f10-snap-capture-tray · ios · 06-upload-failed · light — three pages failed, \"Retry 3 pages\", Done enabled.\n10. f10-snap-capture-tray · web-1440 · 07-rejected-files · light — the four rejection rows under the queue.\n11. f10-snap-capture-tray · ios · 08-offline · light — the pages read \"Will upload when you're back online\".\n12. f10-snap-capture-tray · ios · 09-scanner-unavailable · light — the photo fallback.\n13. f10-snap-capture-tray · android · 09-scanner-unavailable · light — the photo fallback, with the picker cap caption.\n14. f10-snap-capture-tray · ios · 10-camera-off · light — \"Open Settings\" and \"Choose from photos instead\".\n15. f10-snap-capture-tray · web-390 · 10-camera-off · light — the browser has blocked the camera.\n16. f10-snap-capture-tray · web-1440 · 11-no-camera-empty · light — the drop target only, with the empty slot caption.\n17. f10-snap-capture-tray · web-390 · 08-offline · light — the mobile web bottom sheet offline, pages reading \"Will upload when you're back online\", Done enabled.\n18. f10-snap-capture-tray · ios · 12-guest-check · light — Alex Kim sees the one-time check before his first scan, with \"Scan and file\" and \"Cancel\".\n19. f10-snap-capture-tray · ios · 13-member-check · light — Sam Ortega sees the one-time check before his first scan.\n20. f10-snap-capture-tray · ios · 14-landscape · light — 852x393, queue on the left, buttons on the right.\n21. f10-snap-capture-tray · ios · 15-ax5 · light — the vertical list at AX5.\n22. f10-snap-capture-tray · android · 16-font-200 · light — the vertical list at 200%.\n23. f10-snap-capture-tray · ios · 17-greyscale · light — frame 1 in greyscale.\n24. f10-snap-capture-tray · ios · 01-queue-uploading · dark — dark twin of frame 1.\n25. f10-snap-capture-tray · ios · 06-upload-failed · dark — dark twin of frame 9.\n26. f10-snap-capture-tray · web-1440 · 99-notes · light — Notes. Include:\n- A three-step strip: \"Scan today's stack\" (or the \"Scan mail\" chip on Today, iOS) → system scanner (not drawn by Pantopus) → \"Today's stack\".\n- The sender ground truth per page.\n- Departs from the design doc: the iOS system document scanner and the Android ML Kit document scanner (JPEG output requested) instead of the system camera picker and a CameraX shutter. Needs founder sign-off.\n- The no-claimed-address notice is owned by Mail Day and drawn on \"f10-mail-day-triage · ios · 13-no-claimed-home · light\".\n- Every invented string: Larkspur Loop HOA, the file names and sizes, Alex Kim, \"Split into separate pages\", \"Separate from previous page\", \"Show 3 pages\", \"Group again\", \"Delete letter\", the member-check and guest-check copy, Alex's own audience line, the \"Waiting\" short label, and the 100-photo picker cap (the real cap comes from the device).\n- \"Choose from photos\" is a deliberate wording choice over the research's \"Choose from library\", so one term is used on native and web.\n- The guest and member checks use \"Cancel\", not \"Not now\", because they are gates, not asks.\n- The named-people audience sentence is a pending ScopeChip contract variant (the contract's name-the-people exception, because photo permissions differ).\n- Upload counts and percentages describe files moving, not a person's progress. They are the ThumbnailRail contract's upload state and are not a house-style score. A percentage always names one page.\n- Permission assumptions: Maya holds bill management. Sam, as a member, can see amounts but cannot add bills. Alex, as a guest, can do neither. All three may scan and file.\n- \"Upload failed · Retry\" is used exactly as the contract states it.\n- Open decisions: single-page PDF support on web; what a guest's filed photos show to the guest, including whether Alex's own tray line holds (it depends on this); how long photos are kept.\n- Any omitted state.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: 1-6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: 7-12, then wait. Turn 3: 13-18, then wait. Turn 4: 19-24, then wait. Turn 5: 25-26.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Frame 2 split into 02-page-selected (before) and 03-pages-joined (after, with page 3 finished uploading); later frames renumbered; 26 frames; batch plan updated (review major and minor).",
          "Artboard 16 (no-claimed-home) replaced by a web-390 offline frame; Notes name the Mail Day artboard that owns the notice; 'Draw it active' removed from the Today chip entry, and the chip added to the Notes strip (review minors).",
          "Stack ring text changed to '2 of 3 uploaded · page 7 at 40%' so two numbers never disagree; Notes say a percentage always names one page (review minor).",
          "Joined stack action renamed 'Split into separate pages'; single pages inside a fanned letter get 'Separate from previous page'; COPY, accessibility and Notes updated (review minor).",
          "Guest path clarified: the guest audience string is Maya's view; Alex's own tray line added and tied to the open decision; guest and member checks use 'Scan and file' · 'Cancel' and appear once each (review minor, glossary 'Not now' rule).",
          "Notes: design-doc departure (system document scanners instead of SystemCameraPicker/CameraX) flagged for sign-off (review minor).",
          "Notes: 'Choose from photos' recorded as a deliberate wording choice over 'Choose from library' (review minor, per-surface changes).",
          "Notes: named-people audience sentence listed as a pending ScopeChip variant; ScopeChip chip placed beside the line (review minor, contract copy rules).",
          "Notes: upload counts and percentages declared the ThumbnailRail upload state, not a house-style score (review minor).",
          "Guest-check body uses the unified F10 limited-access string (cross-surface consistency with f10-mail-day-triage).",
          "DateSheet usage narrowed to the PDF rejection, since the no-claimed-address notice is drawn on Mail Day."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f10-extraction-confirm",
        "name": "Confirm what we read (extraction review)",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": true,
        "frameCount": 29,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Confirm what we read · f10-extraction-confirm\n\nTYPE: NEW. A full screen on all platforms, not a sheet. It is one step in a scan → confirm → next piece loop over Mail Day.\nPresentation per platform:\n- iOS: a full-screen cover.\n- Android: a full-screen destination where Back equals Close.\n- web-1440: it replaces the content area, and the app sidebar stays visible.\n- web-390: it fills the screen.\nClose keeps typed values and leaves the piece not confirmed.\n\nATTACH: Mail Day populated (iOS, Android, web 1440). The Date sheet, because its kind grid and Remind me control are reused here. The Foundations board.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852, plus one landscape frame at 852x393. Android 412x915. Web 1440x900 and 390x844.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Mail tab → Mail Day → Confirm what we read.\nEntry points:\n- Automatically, once, right after \"Done (4)\" in the capture tray, if a piece has already been read.\n- \"Check what we read\" on any not-confirmed Mail Day row (Mail Day shows the value as read, here \"due in 25 days · Fri 13 Nov\").\n- \"Add to bills\" on a digital Mail Day bill with an amount: this screen opens without a photo pane.\n- \"Fix what we read\" on a bill's \"From a photo you took\" block. It opens with the saved values and tick marks, and the commit reads \"Save changes to this bill\".\nIt receives the photo and its pages, the piece number, the kind, and the values read. Where available, it also receives the photo area and the printed label each value came from.\nIt hands off:\n- \"Add to bills\" creates the bill, puts it on the household calendar, sets the reminders, and offers \"Next piece\".\n- \"Just file it\" files the piece with no bill.\n- After the last piece, it returns to Mail Day. There the rows read \"Added to bills · Undo\" or \"Filed · Undo\" with the checked value, and wait for a paper decision.\n- \"Where does this photo go?\" opens \"Mail snaps: privacy and storage\".\n- Mark paid happens later on the bill, never here.\nThe no-claimed-address notice belongs to Mail Day, which checks before any scan, so this screen never shows it.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Maya Chen at HOME A, Mon 19 Oct 2026, 6:12 PM. She is on the sofa with the paper stack beside her. She closed the auto-opened review to look at the list, and has now tapped \"Check what we read\" on the Clark Public Utilities row. The machine picked the wrong date.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Turn what we read from the photo into facts Maya has checked before anything reaches bills, the calendar or a reminder.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS:\n1) The photo, pinned, with the Due date area outlined.\n2) The Due date \"Fri 13 Nov 2026\", flagged \"We weren't sure — check this\", with the alternative \"Fri 23 Oct (Payment due date)\" right under it.\n3) The button \"Add $142.18 due Fri 13 Nov to bills\" in the pinned commit bar.\nPrimary action: that button. It is filled, but it never receives focus automatically while any field is flagged.\n\nCONTENT (the house style fixtures, plus these additions)\nCommit label rule: \"Add <amount> due <weekday day month> to bills\". If a value is blank, it reads \"Add to bills\".\nTop bar: \"Close\" · \"Piece 1 of 4\" · \"Skip for now\".\nKind line, in every frame: KindGlyph bill + \"Looks like a bill · Electric\" + the button \"Change kind\".\nLegend, shown once: \"○ Read from your photo · not confirmed\". After commit, it swaps to \"✓ You added this\".\nPhoto pane: page 1 of 2, with \"Page 1 of 2\" and the buttons \"Previous page\" and \"Next page\".\nMain fields, each with its hollow mark:\n- Payee: \"Clark Public Utilities\".\n- Amount: a crop of the printed \"$142.18\", the caption \"Read beside \"Amount due\"\", and an editable \"$142.18\" at h3 size.\n- Due date: a crop, the caption \"Read beside \"Next bill date\"\", an editable \"Fri 13 Nov 2026\", and the flag \"We weren't sure — check this\". Alternatives: \"Fri 23 Oct (Payment due date)\" · \"Thu 8 Oct (Statement date)\".\nSecondary row, normally collapsed: \"Account ending ····4471\" with \"Edit\". In this frame it is expanded, because Account ending carries the flag \"We weren't sure — check this\".\nRemind me (ReminderLeadControl, extraction confirm variant, 7 days by default):\n- 7 days is selected. The timeline reads Fri 6 Nov · Thu 12 Nov · Fri 13 Nov.\n- The caption under it: \"We'll also remind you the day before and on the day.\"\n- 60 and 30 are drawn disabled, each with its reason (\"Mon 14 Sep has passed\", \"Wed 14 Oct has passed\").\nAudience line at the foot of the fields, directly above the commit bar, with ScopeChip \"Your household\" beside it: \"Only your household can see this photo: you and Sam.\" · link \"Where does this photo go?\"\nCommit bar, equal size: filled \"Add $142.18 due Fri 13 Nov to bills\" and outlined \"Just file it\".\nFrame 02, date corrected:\n- \"Fri 23 Oct 2026\" is selected and the field shows \"You changed this\".\n- The reminder switches. 60, 30 and 7 are disabled with their reasons (\"Mon 24 Aug has passed\", \"Wed 23 Sep has passed\", \"Fri 16 Oct has passed\"). 1 day is pre-selected as the suggested alternative, with the caption \"7 days before has passed, so we'll remind you 1 day before.\"\n- The timeline reads Thu 22 Oct · Fri 23 Oct.\n- The commit reads \"Add $142.18 due Fri 23 Oct to bills\".\nSuccess: \"Added to bills and your calendar: $142.18, due Fri 23 Oct. We'll remind you 1 day before (Thu 22 Oct) and on the day.\" · \"Undo\" · \"Next piece\".\nHigh-confidence frame (Piece 2 of 4), drawn after Maya retried the water upload on Mail Day:\n- City of Vancouver · water · \"$84.00\" · \"Wed 28 Oct 2026\". No flags, but still hollow marks.\n- 7 days is selected. The timeline reads Wed 21 Oct · Tue 27 Oct · Wed 28 Oct.\n- Success: \"Added to bills and your calendar: $84.00, due Wed 28 Oct. We'll remind you 7 days before (Wed 21 Oct), the day before and on the day.\"\nStatement frame (Piece 4 of 4):\n- Chase · \"Looks like a statement\" · \"Change kind\" · \"Account ending ····8830\".\n- Filled \"Just file it\" and outlined \"Add as a bill\". \"Add as a bill\" reveals the Payee, Amount and Due date fields in place.\n- Changing the kind to Bill also brings back \"Add to bills\".\nPayee suggestions come only from bills already added: \"Comcast · last added today\".\nDuplicate frame: a second photo of the same Clark bill at 6:20 PM, Piece 1 of 1. The banner reads \"You already added Clark Public Utilities · $142.18 · due Fri 23 Oct to bills.\" · \"Keep both\" · \"Replace\".\nMember frame (Sam Ortega):\n- The values are read and visible.\n- \"Just file it\" is filled.\n- \"Add to bills\" is disabled, with a LockedActionRow: \"Only Maya can add bills here.\"\n- Remind me is hidden.\nGuest frame (Alex Kim):\n- The photo pane is replaced by a document glyph and the line \"Photo of your mail · only Maya and Sam can open it\".\n- A LockedActionRow: \"Only Maya and Sam can see bill senders, amounts and photos.\"\n- The kind line is shown. No values are shown.\n- \"Just file it\" is filled. \"Add to bills\" is disabled with \"Only Maya can add bills here.\"\nWorst case: the payee \"Washington State Department of Labor & Industries\", the amount \"$12,480.00\", a due date on Mon 2 Nov 2026 and another 2 years out, and three date alternatives.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\nPhoto beside fields, never photo then fields.\n- Phone: the photo is a pinned pane in the top 42%, and the fields scroll beneath it. It never scrolls away. It shrinks to 25%, showing the zoomed area, when the keyboard is up or text is at AX sizes.\n- Landscape: the photo moves to the left half.\n- Desktop: the photo pane takes 55% on the left and the fields 45% on the right. Each scrolls on its own.\n- The pane has \"Zoom in\", \"Zoom out\", \"Fit\", the page buttons and \"See the piece\".\nCommit bar:\n- Phone and web-390: the two commits sit in a bottom bar pinned above the home indicator, with scroll padding equal to its height, so the last field, Remind me and the audience line clear it.\n- The bar hides while the keyboard is up.\n- At AX5 and 200% the buttons stack and the commit label wraps to two lines.\n- Landscape and web-1440: the bar is pinned to the bottom of the fields column.\nFocusing a field zooms the pane to the area it was read from and outlines that area in two tones: a 2px dark ink line inside a 1px white line. With no area, the pane stays at fit width with no outline, and the field shows \"We can't point to where we read this.\"\nCertainty is shown per field, only in words and shape:\n- Every read field carries the hollow read-from-your-photo mark before commit, confident or not.\n- Uncertain fields add the text flag and up to 3 alternatives as ChoiceChips.\n- Editing a field or tapping an alternative clears its flag and shows \"You changed this\".\n- After commit, every field turns to the you-added tick.\n- Amount and Due date always get the crop and the label caption, whatever the certainty.\nThe commit button restates the values, so the last thing Maya reads is the value.\nWhen data is missing:\n- No read: blank fields with the placeholders \"Payee\", \"Amount\" and \"Due date\". Never $0.00 or today's date.\n- No area: the caption instead of an outline.\n- No photo (a digital bill from Mail Day): no pane; the fields fill the width.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\nTapping a field opens the right control in place, with the value selected:\n- Payee: text, with payee suggestions.\n- Amount: a decimal pad with a \"$\" prefix.\n- Due date: the native date control, which accepts dates 2 years out. iOS uses the compact control with month and year jump, Android uses text-input mode, and web uses a typed input.\n- Account ending: a 4-digit number pad.\n\"Change kind\" opens the KindGlyph tile grid plus bill-type ChoiceChips in place.\nThere is no \"What's wrong?\" step. Tapping an alternative sets it in one tap.\nCommits:\n- \"Just file it\" needs no fields.\n- If Amount or Due date is blank, \"Add to bills\" shows \"Needed to add a bill\" under those fields, and only then.\n- Duplicate: until Maya picks Keep both or Replace, \"Add to bills\" is disabled and reads \"Choose Keep both or Replace first\". \"Just file it\" stays live. Neither choice is pre-selected.\nUndo:\n- After commit, Undo stays on this screen until Next piece or leaving.\n- After that, each piece's Undo stays on its Mail Day row (\"Added to bills · Undo\") until Finish day.\n- Adding a bill notifies the household only when the Mail Day closes.\n- \"Save changes to this bill\" (from a saved bill) holds household notifications until its Undo closes, when Maya leaves this screen.\n\"Skip for now\" moves to the next piece and leaves the row not confirmed.\nThis screen has no report control. A photo read is corrected in place.\nMotion: the pane zoom animates over 250ms. Under Reduce Motion it cuts with a fade.\nHaptics: one light tick on a successful commit.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: ProvenanceMark (read-from-your-photo, you-added) · KindGlyph (row and tile) · ReminderLeadControl (extraction confirm variant, lead already passed, with its caption) · ChoiceChip (alternatives, bill type) · ScopeChip (chip \"Your household\" beside the audience line; the line itself uses the contract's name-the-people exception because photo permissions differ) · InlineUndo · InlineErrorRow (save failed, values kept) · OfflineNotice (queued writes) · LockedActionRow (names who can act) · WarmingSkeleton (field rows while reading).\n\nACCESSIBILITY\nReading order: piece count, kind line with Change kind, legend, photo summary, fields top to bottom, Remind me, audience line, commits.\nEach field is one element. Example: \"Due date, Friday 13 November 2026, read beside Next bill date, read from your photo, not confirmed. We weren't sure, check this. 2 other dates found.\" \"Read from your photo, not confirmed\" is a new spoken name; list it on Notes.\n\"Change kind\" is spoken \"Change kind, currently bill\".\nThe photo has a label: \"Photo of a Clark Public Utilities bill, page 1 of 2.\"\nThe pane controls are buttons, not only pinch.\nTargets are 44pt, 48dp and 44px.\nThe focused field is never hidden behind the keyboard, the pane or the commit bar.\nThe outline and the marks reach at least 3:1 on any photo.\nFlags are words, not colour.\nStatus messages (\"Adding…\", \"Added\", \"Couldn't add\") are live regions.\nDisabled reminder segments and the disabled \"Add to bills\" stay focusable and read their reasons.\nAt AX5 and 200%, the pane is 25%, fields stack label over value, the reminder control becomes radio rows, and the commit buttons stack.\n\nCOPY\nTop bar: \"Close\" · \"Piece 1 of 4\" · \"Skip for now\".\nPhoto pane: \"Zoom in\" · \"Zoom out\" · \"Fit\" · \"Previous page\" · \"Next page\" · \"See the piece\" · \"Where does this photo go?\"\nReminder caption: \"We'll also remind you the day before and on the day.\"\nReading: \"Reading your mail…\"\nUnreadable: \"We couldn't read this photo. It may be blurry or cut off.\" · \"Retake\" · \"Enter it yourself\".\nReading unavailable: \"We couldn't read this one automatically. Add the amount and due date yourself.\"\nSaving: \"Adding…\".\nError: \"We couldn't add this bill. Your changes are kept. Try again.\" · \"Try again\".\nOffline: \"You're offline. Your changes are kept, and this piece stays not confirmed until you're back online.\" The commit becomes \"Add when back online\".\nAccess removed: \"You no longer have access to bills at 2418 NE Larkspur Loop. Your photo is kept.\" · \"Just file it\".\nMember and guest reasons: \"Only Maya can add bills here.\" · \"Only Maya and Sam can see bill senders, amounts and photos.\"\nDuplicate: \"You already added Clark Public Utilities · $142.18 · due Fri 23 Oct to bills.\" · \"Keep both\" · \"Replace\" · \"Choose Keep both or Replace first\".\nOther buttons: \"Next piece\" · \"Undo\" · \"Add as a bill\" · \"Change kind\" · \"Edit\" · \"Save changes to this bill\".\nNever use the word \"Paid\" anywhere on this screen, and never \"AI\" or \"OCR\".\n\nEDGE CASES\n- The long payee wraps to two lines, and the commit button wraps to two lines rather than cutting off the values.\n- \"$12,480.00\" fits at h3.\n- A date 2 years out can be typed.\n- Three alternatives at most.\n- A 12-page piece shows \"Page 1 of 12\" on the pane, with page buttons.\n- Slow reading keeps skeleton rows, with \"Just file it\" live.\n- Offline, error and saving states keep every typed value.\n- A bill read as a statement can still become a bill: \"Add as a bill\", or \"Change kind\".\n- Sam loses bill access while this screen is open: show the access-removed state.\n\nINSTEAD OF\nInstead of editable chips (\"Due Oct 12 · $142 · Clark PUD · Confirm\"), draw one field per value with its own control — because money, dates and names need different keyboards, and chips hide which value was uncertain.\nInstead of filled marks on the confident fields, draw every read field hollow until commit, then all ticked — because a confident read can still be wrong, and filled means official or confirmed.\nInstead of a percentage, meter or \"87% sure\" badge, draw the words \"We weren't sure — check this\" and the alternatives — because people can act on words and choices.\nInstead of a photo you tap to expand, draw a pinned pane that shrinks with the keyboard or large text — because Maya is proofreading against the source.\nInstead of commit buttons at the end of a long scroll, draw them in a pinned bar with scroll padding — because the value-restating button must be reachable without losing the photo.\nInstead of a single-colour focus-blue outline, draw a two-tone outline — because it must show on any photo.\nInstead of \"$0.00\" or today's date when reading fails, draw empty fields with placeholders — because a believable default gets approved.\nInstead of hiding the bill path for statements, draw \"Add as a bill\" beside \"Just file it\" and \"Change kind\" on every kind line — because the kind is itself an unconfirmed read.\n\nDONE WHEN:\n- The misread due date (Fri 13 Nov) is corrected to Fri 23 Oct in one tap on an alternative, and the reminder and the commit update to match.\n- Nothing is marked as confirmed before \"Add to bills\".\n- The commit and success lines state the amount, the due date and the real reminder dates.\n- The commit is visible without scrolling on a phone.\n- The manual path works when reading is unavailable.\n- Sam can file but not add, and says why. Alex sees no photo, payee or amount.\n- The word \"Paid\" never appears.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f10-extraction-confirm · ios · 01-low-confidence · light — the dense Clark case, Piece 1 of 4, with the misread Fri 13 Nov, the reminder caption, the audience line above the pinned commit bar.\n2. f10-extraction-confirm · ios · 02-date-corrected · light — Fri 23 Oct chosen, \"You changed this\", the reminder at 1 day with disabled segments, and the updated commit.\n3. f10-extraction-confirm · ios · 03-amount-editing · light — keyboard up, pane at 25%, two-tone outline on the amount, commit bar hidden.\n4. f10-extraction-confirm · web-1440 · 01-low-confidence · light — 55/45 panes, sidebar visible, commit bar at the bottom of the fields column.\n5. f10-extraction-confirm · android · 01-low-confidence · light — Material 3 controls.\n6. f10-extraction-confirm · ios · 04-added · light — the success line, ticks, the \"✓ You added this\" legend, Undo and Next piece.\n7. f10-extraction-confirm · ios · 05-high-confidence · light — Piece 2 of 4, City of Vancouver, 7-day reminders.\n8. f10-extraction-confirm · ios · 06-statement · light — Piece 4 of 4, Chase, \"Change kind\" on the kind line, \"Just file it\" filled, \"Add as a bill\" outlined.\n9. f10-extraction-confirm · ios · 07-reading · light — skeleton fields and \"Reading your mail…\".\n10. f10-extraction-confirm · ios · 08-reading-unavailable · light — blank fields after pressing Add, with \"Needed to add a bill\".\n11. f10-extraction-confirm · ios · 09-unreadable-photo · light — \"Retake\" or \"Enter it yourself\".\n12. f10-extraction-confirm · ios · 10-duplicate · light — the banner with Keep both and Replace, and the commit disabled.\n13. f10-extraction-confirm · ios · 11-member · light — Sam: values visible, file only.\n14. f10-extraction-confirm · ios · 12-guest · light — Alex: document glyph, file only.\n15. f10-extraction-confirm · web-1440 · 12-guest · light — the desktop guest view.\n16. f10-extraction-confirm · android · 12-guest · light — the Android guest view.\n17. f10-extraction-confirm · ios · 13-access-removed · light — Sam's access removed while the screen was open. The photo pane is replaced by the document glyph, and \"Just file it\" is shown.\n18. f10-extraction-confirm · ios · 14-saving · light — \"Adding…\".\n19. f10-extraction-confirm · ios · 15-save-error · light — values kept, \"Try again\".\n20. f10-extraction-confirm · ios · 16-offline · light — \"Add when back online\".\n21. f10-extraction-confirm · ios · 17-landscape · light — photo on the left, fields on the right, commit bar at the foot of the fields.\n22. f10-extraction-confirm · web-390 · 01-low-confidence · light — mobile web, commit bar pinned.\n23. f10-extraction-confirm · ios · 18-fix-what-we-read · light — opened from a saved bill, with ticks and \"Save changes to this bill\".\n24. f10-extraction-confirm · ios · 19-ax5 · light — pane at 25%, stacked fields, reminder as radio rows, commit buttons stacked with the label on two lines.\n25. f10-extraction-confirm · android · 20-font-200 · light — 200% text.\n26. f10-extraction-confirm · ios · 21-greyscale · light — frame 1 in greyscale.\n27. f10-extraction-confirm · ios · 01-low-confidence · dark — dark twin of frame 1.\n28. f10-extraction-confirm · ios · 10-duplicate · dark — dark twin of frame 12.\n29. f10-extraction-confirm · web-1440 · 99-notes · light — Notes. List:\n- Invented strings: the label captions, \"Next bill date\" and the Fri 13 Nov misread, the Thu 8 Oct statement date, account endings 4471 and 8830, bill types, Alex Kim, \"Skip for now\", \"Change kind\", \"Comcast · last added today\", the 6:20 PM duplicate scan, the duplicate banner, the access-removed copy, the disabled-segment reasons, the unified limited-access string.\n- \"○ Read from your photo · not confirmed\" and its spoken name must be added to the ProvenanceMark contract (prompt 00) before build, so all F10 surfaces use the same words.\n- The audience line names the people under the ScopeChip contract's name-the-people exception; it is a pending ScopeChip variant.\n- Success copy extends the doc string (\"Added to your calendar. We'll remind you {lead} before.\") to restate the values and the real reminder dates.\n- Auto-selecting 1 day when the default lead has passed is a deliberate suggested alternative.\n- The reminder reconciliation: the lead from Remind me, plus the day before and the day of. Today's reminder job sends only the day before and the day of, so the chosen lead needs a new lead-time setting stored on each bill.\n- The explanation of photo reads lives in the one provenance sheet (authority \"We read this from your photo\"), reached from the bill. This screen corrects in place and has no \"This isn't right\" report control, which is reserved for public-record facts.\n- Mark paid happens on the bill (bill detail and its \"From a photo you took\" block), never here.\n- Held notifications go out when the Mail Day closes: on Finish day, or automatically at the next Mail Day time (open decision shared with Mail Day).\n- This screen's reading-unavailable string differs on purpose from Mail Day's notice: this one covers one piece.\n- The house fixture bills are the state after commit, so frame 1 has no duplicate. The duplicate frame is a second scan of the same bill.\n- Confirming the HOA piece matches the existing HOA dues Date in the duplicate check.\n- The storyline: Mail Day shows the Fri 13 Nov misread until this screen corrects it. Chase uploaded after a delay and is read as Piece 4. Water is read after Maya retried its failed page.\n- Permission assumptions: only Maya can add bills. Sam can see amounts. Alex can see neither.\n- Open decision: whether a guest who took the photo may see it (drawn hidden).\n- Any omitted state.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: 1-6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: 7-12, then wait. Turn 3: 13-18, then wait. Turn 4: 19-24, then wait. Turn 5: 25-29.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Commit buttons now sit in a bottom bar pinned above the home indicator with scroll padding, hidden with the keyboard, stacked at AX5/200%, pinned to the fields column in landscape and web-1440; drawn in frames 1, 3, 4, 21, 22 and 24; DONE WHEN and INSTEAD OF updated (review major).",
          "Audience line moved to the foot of the fields, directly above the commit bar; reading order now matches (review minor).",
          "ScopeChip usage restated as the chip beside the line plus the contract's name-the-people exception; Notes list it as a pending variant (review minors, raised twice).",
          "'Change kind' now sits on the kind line in every frame (spoken 'Change kind, currently bill'); Kind removed from the secondary row, which reads 'Account ending ····4471' with 'Edit' (review minor).",
          "Duplicate banner changed to 'You already added Clark Public Utilities · $142.18 · due Fri 23 Oct to bills.' (review minor).",
          "ReminderLeadControl contract caption shown under the control in frame 1; Notes explain that the chosen lead needs a lead-time setting on each bill because today's reminder job only sends day-before and day-of (review minor; code identifiers kept out of the prompt).",
          "Notes: success copy recorded as an extension of the doc string (research P20) (review minor).",
          "Notes: photo-read explanation merged into the one provenance sheet; this screen has no 'This isn't right' control (review minor, FINAL MERGES, research-findings).",
          "Notes and hand-off: Mark paid happens on the bill, never here; 'Save changes to this bill' holds household notifications until its Undo closes (review minor, doc acceptance criterion).",
          "Notes: held notifications go out when the Mail Day closes, including the auto-close open decision shared with Mail Day (review minor).",
          "New entry point: 'Add to bills' from a digital Mail Day bill opens this screen without a photo pane (cross-surface change from the f10-mail-day-triage review).",
          "Guest limited-access string unified with the other F10 surfaces; Notes record why this screen's reading-unavailable string differs from Mail Day's.",
          "Entry point and storyline notes now state that Mail Day shows the Fri 13 Nov misread until this screen corrects it (cross-surface storyline fix)."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f10-mail-piece-photo",
        "name": "Photographed mail piece (the record, and the photo viewer)",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 27,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Photographed mail piece (the record, and the photo viewer) · f10-mail-piece-photo\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of two existing designed screens, \"Mailbox drawer list\" and \"Mail piece detail\". This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed. There is no separate photo viewer screen: the mail piece detail is the viewer.\n\nATTACH: the current mailbox drawer list and mail piece detail on web 1440, iOS and Android; the Mail Day screen with a \"Needs a call\" row and a \"Reviewed today\" row; the Confirm what we read screen; the Foundations board (ThumbnailRail, DestructiveConfirm, ChoiceChip, ScopeChip, StatusChip, ProvenanceMark, LockedActionRow, WarmingSkeleton, OfflineNotice).\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: web 1440x900 (left sidebar) and 390x844; iOS 393x852; Android 412x915. Portrait and landscape both work.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Mail tab → mailbox drawer → mail piece. The piece is pushed onto the Mail stack, not presented. Every entry opens the same piece:\n- \"See the piece\" on a Mail Day row in \"Reviewed today\". The row's thumbnail is part of the same row target and opens the same piece. It hands over the piece; Back returns to Mail Day.\n- \"See the piece\" (or the thumbnail) on a Mail Day row in \"Needs a call\". It opens the not-confirmed-yet state (below); Back returns to Mail Day, and the row stays in \"Needs a call\".\n- A mailbox drawer row, including a payee or amount search. The mailbox banner opens the drawer, not a piece.\n- \"View the photo\" in the bill provenance block on Bill detail. It hands over the bill's source piece; Back returns to the bill.\n- \"See the piece\" on the Confirm what we read photo pane. Back returns there.\n- A row in the \"Photos of your mail\" card in Mail Day settings. Back returns to the card.\n- Direct link (not drawn): pantopus.app/app/mailbox/<drawer>/<piece> on web, and the same path in the native Mail stack.\nThe piece hands off to Bill detail (\"Added to bills\"), to Confirm what we read (\"Confirm what we read\") and to the Photos of your mail card (\"Manage mail snaps\").\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Maya Chen, owner of HOME A. The scene is Tue 20 Oct 2026 at 7:30 AM, the morning after Mail Day (a fixture delta). Last night at 6:04 PM she scanned the 2-page Clark Public Utilities bill, confirmed what we read and added it to bills. This morning she wants to check the account number printed on page 1.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Answer \"where did the thing I photographed go?\" after triage ends, and be the one place where the photo can be seen and permanently deleted.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: (1) The letter itself, readable at fit-to-width, letterhead and account line above the sheet. (2) The facts: payee, amount, due date. (3) The link \"Added to bills · $142.18 due Fri 23 Oct\". Primary action: that link. \"Delete this photo\" is present but quieter.\n\nCONTENT (house style fixtures; list every delta on Notes)\nFixture deltas: guest Alex Kim has no bill access. Sam Ortega has bill access. Account ending 4471; only the last 4 digits ever appear as text.\nPhotographed pieces, newest first. These are the newest of the same 17 stored photos listed on the Photos of your mail card; older pieces continue further down the drawer.\n- Clark Public Utilities · 2 pages · $142.18 · due Fri 23 Oct · Added to bills · photographed Mon 19 Oct 6:04 PM by Maya · Paper recycled · photo kept until Sun 17 Jan 2027\n- Comcast · $79.99 · due Mon 2 Nov · Added to bills · photographed Mon 19 Oct\n- Larkspur Loop HOA · read as $285.00 · due Sun 1 Nov · Not confirmed yet (still in Needs a call) · photographed Mon 19 Oct\n- Chase statement · 2 pages · Filed, no bill · photographed Mon 19 Oct\n- NW Natural · $61.08 · was due Fri 16 Oct · Added to bills · Overdue · photographed Mon 5 Oct\n- Riverview Bank statement · Filed, no bill · photographed Wed 30 Sep · photo kept until Tue 29 Dec (photographed by mistake)\n- Waste Connections · Filed, no bill · photographed Mon 21 Sep\n- Not classified · no facts · reads \"Photographed Sat 12 Sep\"\n- Clark Public Utilities · $109.60 · Paid · photographed Mon 21 Sep · photo deleted Sat 17 Oct · text record kept (not one of the 17 stored photos)\nDigital row, no photo: State Farm · renews Wed 4 Nov · $612.40.\nWorst case: \"Washington State Department of Labor & Industries\" · $12,480.00 · 12 pages.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\nDraw this as a document viewer, not a photo gallery: small print must be legible and zoomable. Draw no carousel and no paging dots. Pages of the same piece show \"Page 1 of 2\" with Previous page and Next page buttons, bottom-left.\n\nImage stage. The page sits full-bleed, top-aligned, fit-to-width, on the dark app surface token in both themes (the one scrim exception; state it on Notes). Chrome on the stage uses dark-theme tokens in both themes.\n- Top bar, on all three platforms: the platform back control (iOS back chevron, Android top app bar back arrow, web Back link) and the payee as title. Draw no overflow menu; Download and Delete live only in the facts panel.\n- Bottom-right: a zoom cluster of Zoom out · Fit · Zoom in (44pt iOS / 48dp Android with 8dp gaps / 44px web) and a \"1x\" readout. Bottom-left: Previous page and Next page, opposite the zoom cluster.\n\nFacts panel. It follows the app theme. Facts are read-only here; corrections happen through \"Fix what we read\" on the bill. On native it is a bottom sheet with three detents:\n- peek: payee, amount and due date, plus the link row (or \"Confirm what we read\" on a not-confirmed piece);\n- medium: stops at 45% of the height, so the letterhead and account line stay visible above it; shows everything;\n- large: AX sizes only.\nOn web 1440 it is a 360px right rail, so it never sits on the letterhead. On web 390 it is a bottom panel. In order:\n1. Payee (h3).\n2. \"$142.18 · due in 3 days · Fri 23 Oct\" with ProvenanceMark S (you-added) beside the amount, and the legend \"✓ You added this\" printed once in this panel.\n3. \"Account ending 4471\".\n4. The link row \"Added to bills · $142.18 due Fri 23 Oct\".\n5. \"Photographed Mon 19 Oct 2026 at 6:04 PM by you\".\n6. \"Paper recycled · photo kept until Sun 17 Jan 2027\".\n7. The audience line with ScopeChip \"Your household\": \"You and Sam can see this photo. Nobody nearby can.\"\n8. The row \"Manage mail snaps\", captioned \"Where these photos are kept\".\n9. Web only: \"Download\". It goes through the signed-in download, never a public link.\n10. \"Delete this photo\", in text.error on base with a border.\n\nAt 2x on a portrait letter, the top third of the page stays clear: the top bar shrinks to a 44pt compact bar and the sheet drops to its peek.\n\nPiece states (each changes the facts panel only as listed):\n- Photographed, not confirmed yet (Larkspur Loop HOA). Payee, amount and due date carry ProvenanceMark S read-from-your-photo (the unconfirmed ring), with the legend \"○ On record, not confirmed\" once, and the line \"Not confirmed yet\" under them. The link row is replaced by the primary link \"Confirm what we read\". Line 6 reads \"Photo kept until Sun 17 Jan 2027\".\n- Filed without a bill (Riverview Bank statement). Show only what Maya confirmed when filing: the payee with the you-added mark, and the line \"Filed, no bill\". No amount, no account digits, no link row and no empty slot.\n- Not classified: no facts, only \"Photographed Sat 12 Sep\".\n- Photo deleted (September Clark Public Utilities). The stage shows the quiet document glyph and \"The photo was deleted on Sat 17 Oct. The amount you confirmed stays.\" The facts (with the you-added mark), \"Paid\" and the bill link remain; Delete this photo is gone. A piece with no bill uses \"The photo was deleted on <date>. The mail record stays.\" (list on Notes; not drawn).\n\nDrawer list.\n- Add a ChoiceChip filter \"Photographed\" and a search field \"Search payee or amount\".\n- Print the legend once, under the filter row: \"✓ You added this · ○ On record, not confirmed\".\n- Photographed rows get a ThumbnailRail (drawer variant, 40x52) and key facts on line 2, e.g. \"$142.18 · due Fri 23 Oct · Added to bills\". Committed rows (added to bills or filed) draw ProvenanceMark S (you-added) after the amount, or after \"Filed, no bill\". The Clark Public Utilities thumbnail is stacked, labelled \"2 pages\"; Chase is stacked, \"2 pages\".\n- Larkspur Loop HOA line 2: \"$285.00 · due Sun 1 Nov · Not confirmed yet\" with the read-from-your-photo ring.\n- NW Natural carries StatusChip \"Overdue\".\n- Riverview, Chase and Waste Connections read \"Filed, no bill\". Not classified reads \"Photographed Sat 12 Sep\" with no mark.\n- The September Clark Public Utilities row uses the ThumbnailRail deleted variant: a quiet document glyph plus \"photo deleted Sat 17 Oct\".\n- On State Farm, the rail collapses.\n- Mix these with at least six digital rows from the attached screenshot, and use this one thumbnail treatment everywhere.\n\nGuest (Alex). The top bar shows only Back and the title \"Bill\" (\"Mail\" when no bill is linked), never the payee. The stage shows the document glyph, no image. The facts panel shows the reason line and LockedActionRow, with no Download and no Delete. Drawer rows show a document glyph instead of a thumbnail and no sender or amount: \"Bill · photographed Mon 19 Oct\" when a bill is linked, otherwise \"Mail · photographed Mon 19 Oct\".\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- Zoom in steps 1x → 2x → 4x; Fit returns to 1x. Double-tap cycles 1x → 2x → 4x → 1x. Pinch is a shortcut only.\n- Panning at 2x and 4x: drag is a shortcut. On web, arrow keys pan the page and scrollbars show. On native, VoiceOver and TalkBack scroll actions pan.\n- Chrome may auto-hide on the first zoom, and a single tap brings it back, but only when no assistive technology is running. While VoiceOver, TalkBack, Switch Control or Full Keyboard Access is on, chrome never hides and stays in the accessibility tree with a \"Show controls\" action.\n- \"Delete this photo\" opens DestructiveConfirm as drawn on the Foundations board: the custom in-app dialog with stacked buttons on iOS (not the system alert), the M3 basic dialog on Android, a centred dialog on web. It is never a second sheet over the facts sheet. The body depends on the piece (see COPY). After confirming, the piece switches to its photo-deleted state and a live region reads the matching result line. Deletion is permanent, so there is no Undo.\n- Deleting the photo of a not-confirmed piece leaves it in Needs a call; Confirm what we read then opens without a photo pane.\n- On web, Escape resets zoom to Fit. Browser Back returns to the row that opened the piece and restores focus to it.\n- The stage cross-fades in within 200ms. Reduce Motion: zoom jumps without animation and skeletons are static.\n- Haptics: one light tick when the delete is confirmed.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED\nThumbnailRail (drawer variant; stacked \"2 pages\"; deleted and offline states) · ProvenanceMark (S; you-added on committed facts, read-from-your-photo ring on the not-confirmed-yet state) · DestructiveConfirm (one photo variant for pieces with a bill; plus two new body variants requested from the Foundations board: no bill, and not confirmed yet) · ChoiceChip (filter \"Photographed\") · ScopeChip (\"Your household\") · StatusChip (Overdue) · LockedActionRow (names who can act) · OfflineNotice · InlineErrorRow · WarmingSkeleton (row variant bars in the facts panel).\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Reading order: title, facts, bill link, date taken, audience, actions, then the page image.\n- The image is labelled \"Photo of Clark Public Utilities bill, page 1 of 2, zoom 1x\". Buttons read \"Zoom in\", \"Zoom out\", \"Fit to screen\", \"Previous page\", \"Next page\".\n- A drawer row is one element: \"Clark Public Utilities, 142 dollars 18 cents, due Friday 23 October, you added this, added to bills, photographed, 2 pages.\" The HOA row: \"Larkspur Loop HOA, 285 dollars, due Sunday 1 November, on record, not confirmed, still in Needs a call.\" Riverview: \"Riverview Bank statement, filed, no bill, you added this, photographed.\"\n- Every mark a sighted user sees is spoken, and nothing is spoken that is not drawn.\n- Targets are 44pt / 48dp with 8dp gaps / 44px, and a thumbnail or mark is never a target on its own.\n- Overdue and \"Not confirmed yet\" are carried by words and the mark's shape, never colour.\n- The confirm puts keyboard focus on Keep, never on Delete.\n- At AX5 the facts panel opens at its large detent and scrolls, fact pairs stack, and the zoom cluster and page buttons stay visible.\n\nCOPY (sentence case)\n\"Photographed\" · \"Search payee or amount\" · \"✓ You added this · ○ On record, not confirmed\" · \"No photographed mail matches \"999.00\"\" · \"Clear search\"\n\"$142.18 · due in 3 days · Fri 23 Oct\" · \"✓ You added this\" · \"Added to bills · $142.18 due Fri 23 Oct\" · \"Photographed Mon 19 Oct 2026 at 6:04 PM by you\" · \"Paper recycled · photo kept until Sun 17 Jan 2027\" · \"Page 1 of 2\" · \"Previous page\" · \"Next page\" · \"Show controls\"\n\"You and Sam can see this photo. Nobody nearby can.\" · \"Manage mail snaps\" · \"Where these photos are kept\" · \"Download\" · \"Delete this photo\"\nNot confirmed yet: \"○ On record, not confirmed\" · \"Not confirmed yet\" · \"Confirm what we read\" · \"Photo kept until Sun 17 Jan 2027\"\nFiled: \"Filed, no bill\"\nConfirm (title and buttons on every variant): \"Delete this photo?\" · \"Delete photo\" / \"Keep it\"\n- Piece with a bill: body \"The bill and its amount stay; only the photo is removed.\" · result \"Photo deleted. The bill stays.\" · deleted line \"The photo was deleted on Sat 17 Oct. The amount you confirmed stays.\"\n- Filed or not classified: body \"The mail record stays in Mail; only the photo is removed.\" · result \"Photo deleted. The mail record stays.\" · deleted line \"The photo was deleted on Tue 20 Oct. The mail record stays.\"\n- Not confirmed yet: body \"What we read stays unconfirmed in Needs a call; only the photo is removed.\" · result \"Photo deleted. What we read is still in Needs a call.\"\nGuest (Alex): title \"Bill\" · \"A bill arrived Mon 19 Oct. Only Maya and Sam can see its photo, sender and amount.\" with LockedActionRow \"Maya or Sam can open this photo.\" · rows \"Bill · photographed Mon 19 Oct\" / \"Mail · photographed Mon 19 Oct\"\nExpired link: \"This photo's secure link expired.\" · \"Retry\"\nError: \"We couldn't load this piece of mail.\" · \"Retry\"\nOffline: stage \"This photo isn't saved on this device.\" · panel top line \"You're offline · as of Mon 19 Oct, 9:40 PM\" · under Delete and Download: \"Needs a connection.\"\nEmpty filter: \"No photographed mail yet. Pieces you photograph on Mail Day appear here.\"\n\nEDGE CASES\n- The longest payee wraps to two lines and never truncates. \"$12,480.00\" fits. A 12-page piece shows \"Page 1 of 12\".\n- 60 photographed pieces paginate the way the existing drawer does.\n- Zero matches: \"No photographed mail matches \"999.00\"\" and \"Clear search\". No photographed mail at all: the empty-filter line.\n- Slow network: no indicator under 1s, then WarmingSkeleton (row variant bars in the facts panel; shimmer, static under Reduce Motion). The key facts arrive before the page image.\n- Expired link: a quiet static re-fetch first; only if that fails, the expired message.\n- Offline: the stage shows the ThumbnailRail offline glyph with \"This photo isn't saved on this device.\"; the panel shows cached facts under \"You're offline · as of Mon 19 Oct, 9:40 PM\"; Delete and Download are disabled with their reason.\n- Guest Alex: a direct link opens the guest state, never a missing-page error.\n- A saved place (PLACE B) has no photographed mail.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a swipeable gallery with paging dots, draw one document with zoom buttons and page buttons — because people come here to read small print.\n- Instead of chrome that hides on every tap, draw chrome that stays while assistive technology runs, plus a \"Show controls\" action — because under VoiceOver a single tap only moves focus.\n- Instead of an unconfirmed read shown as plain settled facts, draw the ring mark, \"Not confirmed yet\" and \"Confirm what we read\" — because a machine read stays unconfirmed until a person commits it.\n- Instead of editable amount fields on the piece, draw read-only facts and send fixes to the bill — because the piece is the record and the bill is the obligation.\n- Instead of one confirm sentence for every piece, draw the body that matches the piece (bill stays / mail record stays / still in Needs a call) — because the confirm must say truthfully what survives, and a bank statement has no bill.\n- Instead of the iOS system alert, draw the Foundations custom dialog — because the system alert cannot show the outlined destructive button.\n- Instead of a broken-image icon, draw the quiet document glyph with the deletion date — because the record still exists.\n- Instead of a blurred photo, the payee as title or \"Only your household can see this photo\", draw no photo, the title \"Bill\", and named people (\"Only Maya and Sam\", \"You and Sam\") — because bill access differs inside a household and a bill photo is finance data.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- Typing \"142.18\" finds the piece; typing \"999.00\" shows the no-match line with Clear search.\n- Page 1 reads at 2x with its top third clear, and at medium detent the letterhead and account line are visible.\n- The bill is one tap away, and an unconfirmed read is one tap from Confirm what we read.\n- Maya can delete the Riverview statement photo knowing the mail record stays, delete a bill photo knowing the bill stays, and knows until when each photo is kept.\n- Every mark on the drawer has its word on the drawer, and every spoken mark is drawn.\n- Every control is reachable with VoiceOver on.\n- Alex sees that a bill arrived, and nothing more.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f10-mail-piece-photo · ios · 01-piece-with-bill · light — Clark Public Utilities page 1 top-aligned at fit, sheet at medium (45%), tick mark and legend beside the amount.\n2. f10-mail-piece-photo · ios · 02-zoomed-2x · light — 2x on the letterhead, compact bar, sheet at peek with the link row, \"2x\" readout, page buttons bottom-left.\n3. f10-mail-piece-photo · web-1440 · 03-drawer-filter-off · light — six digital rows mixed with the nine photographed rows, legend under the filter row, marks on committed rows and the HOA ring.\n4. f10-mail-piece-photo · web-1440 · 04-drawer-filter-on-search · light — \"Photographed\" selected, \"142.18\" typed, one match.\n5. f10-mail-piece-photo · web-1440 · 05-drawer-no-matches · light — \"Photographed\" selected, \"999.00\" typed, the no-match line with \"Clear search\".\n6. f10-mail-piece-photo · ios · 06-not-confirmed-yet · light — Larkspur Loop HOA from Needs a call: ring marks, legend, \"Not confirmed yet\", \"Confirm what we read\".\n7. f10-mail-piece-photo · ios · 07-filed-no-bill · light — Riverview Bank statement: payee with tick, \"Filed, no bill\", no link row.\n8. f10-mail-piece-photo · ios · 08-delete-confirm · light — Clark Public Utilities: the Foundations custom dialog with the bill body, stacked buttons, focus on Keep it.\n9. f10-mail-piece-photo · ios · 08b-delete-confirm-filed · light — Riverview: the same dialog with \"The mail record stays in Mail; only the photo is removed.\"\n10. f10-mail-piece-photo · ios · 09-photo-deleted · light — September Clark Public Utilities, glyph, deleted line, facts and bill link kept.\n11. f10-mail-piece-photo · ios · 10-guest · light — Alex: Back and title \"Bill\" only, date, reason, LockedActionRow, no image, no Download or Delete; inset shows the guest drawer rows \"Bill · …\" and \"Mail · …\".\n12. f10-mail-piece-photo · ios · 11-link-expired · light — the expired message with Retry.\n13. f10-mail-piece-photo · ios · 12-loading · light — dark stage, WarmingSkeleton row bars in the panel.\n14. f10-mail-piece-photo · ios · 13-error · light — InlineErrorRow in the panel, nothing cached.\n15. f10-mail-piece-photo · ios · 14-offline · light — offline glyph on the stage, \"You're offline · as of Mon 19 Oct, 9:40 PM\", cached facts, Delete disabled with its reason.\n16. f10-mail-piece-photo · android · 15-piece-with-bill · light — Material top app bar back arrow, bottom sheet at medium.\n17. f10-mail-piece-photo · android · 16-drawer-filter-on · light — M3 filter chip, search and legend.\n18. f10-mail-piece-photo · web-1440 · 17-piece-right-rail · light — Back link, stage plus 360px rail with Download.\n19. f10-mail-piece-photo · web-390 · 18-piece-with-bill · light — bottom panel.\n20. f10-mail-piece-photo · ios · 19-worst-case · light — Labor & Industries, $12,480.00, \"Page 1 of 12\".\n21. f10-mail-piece-photo · ios · 20-drawer-filter-on · light — iOS drawer with \"Photographed\" selected, legend, ring on HOA, deleted-rail row.\n22. f10-mail-piece-photo · ios · 20b-landscape · light — landscape phone, sheet at peek.\n23. f10-mail-piece-photo · ios · 21-ax5 · light — AX5, large detent, stacked facts.\n24. f10-mail-piece-photo · ios · 22-greyscale · light — frame 1 in greyscale.\n25. f10-mail-piece-photo · ios · 01-piece-with-bill · dark — dark twin of frame 1.\n26. f10-mail-piece-photo · web-1440 · 04-drawer-filter-on-search · dark — dark twin of frame 4.\n27. Notes — the scrim exception; the Tue 20 Oct scene date; fixture delta \"Alex Kim (guest, no bill access)\"; \"kept until Sun 17 Jan 2027\" and \"Tue 29 Dec\" assume the same undecided 90-day retention stand-in as the Photos of your mail card; which Riverview values were read but never confirmed (amount, account digits) and are therefore not shown; request to the Foundations board: two new DestructiveConfirm one-photo body variants (no bill; not confirmed yet) and their result lines; the no-bill deleted line (not drawn); engineering notes (web converts HEIC to JPEG before drawing any thumbnail or page; web uses the existing mail piece route under /app/mailbox/); every invented string; assumptions; omitted states (the empty-filter frame \"No photographed mail yet…\", Android 200%, the not-classified piece).\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: 1-6, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 2: 7-12, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 3: 13-18, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 4: 19-24, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 5: 25-27.",
        "changeLog": [
          "DestructiveConfirm now has three bodies matching what truly survives: bill (V1 unchanged), filed/unclassified ('The mail record stays in Mail…'), and not confirmed yet ('What we read stays unconfirmed in Needs a call…'), each with its own result line; added frame 08b (Riverview) and a Notes request to the Foundations board (review major, contract DestructiveConfirm, flow-08).",
          "DestructiveConfirm is drawn as on the Foundations board (custom iOS dialog, M3 basic dialog, web centred dialog), not the iOS system alert; frame 8 updated (review major, 00d).",
          "Drawer legend printed once under the filter row; committed rows draw the you-added mark, HOA draws the ring; spoken labels now match what is drawn and the HOA label no longer repeats 'not confirmed' (review major).",
          "Sheet has three detents (peek incl. link row, medium at 45% with top-aligned page, large for AX) (review minor).",
          "Removed the top-bar overflow menu; Download and Delete live only in the facts panel; guest top bar is Back + title (review minor).",
          "Guest drawer rows use 'Bill · …' only when a bill is linked, otherwise 'Mail · …' (review minor).",
          "Added Mail Day row thumbnail and mailbox banner entry points, and the direct-link path (review minor, derive f10-4, f10-9).",
          "Skeleton is WarmingSkeleton row variant, shimmer with static under Reduce Motion (review minor, contract).",
          "Offline state now shows the ThumbnailRail offline glyph and 'You're offline · as of Mon 19 Oct, 9:40 PM' (review minor, OfflineNotice).",
          "Added iOS drawer frame (20) and moved landscape to 20b; guest drawer rows shown in frame 10's inset; Notes names Alex Kim as a fixture delta and lists the empty-filter frame as omitted (review minor).",
          "Keyboard focus on Keep in the confirm, per 00d anatomy."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f10-bill-provenance",
        "name": "Bill provenance block (from a photo you took)",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 24,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Bill provenance block (from a photo you took) · f10-bill-provenance\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Bill detail\". On iOS and Android: this screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed. On web, the bill detail route is a new screen designed in the \"Bill detail (new web route)\" project; attach that design output as the host and keep it exactly. On every platform you add one block beneath the bill's facts, and nothing else.\n\nATTACH: Bill detail on iOS and Android; the \"Bill detail (new web route)\" design output at web 1440 and 390; the Bills list with a few rows; the Foundations board (ProvenanceMark, ProvenanceSheet, ThumbnailRail, DestructiveConfirm, InlineUndo, StatusChip, LockedActionRow, WarmingSkeleton).\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: web 1440x900 (left sidebar) and 390x844; iOS 393x852; Android 412x915.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Place tab → place file → Money → Bills → Bill detail. Every arrival lands on this bill, never on a list:\n- a Bills list row;\n- the Today 14-day strip's money row, \"Clark Public Utilities · $142.18 · in 3 days · Fri 23 Oct\";\n- the bill reminder push on Thu 22 Oct, \"Clark PUD due tomorrow\" / \"Larkspur Loop\", which carries no amount;\n- the household notification \"Sam marked Clark PUD paid\", which opens the paid state (sent only to members with bill access);\n- \"Added to bills\" on the photographed mail piece in the Mail tab;\n- direct links (not drawn): web /app/homes/<home>/bills/<bill>; native pantopus://homes/<home>/bills/<bill>.\nGuest Alex arrives only by a direct link; members without bill access receive no bill notifications.\nEach arrival hands over one bill. The block hands off to the mail piece (\"View the photo\") and to Confirm what we read, reopened with this bill's values (\"Fix what we read\").\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Maya Chen, owner of HOME A, at 7:30 AM on Tue 20 Oct 2026 (a fixture delta). She opened the bill from Today. At 6:04 PM the evening before, she scanned it on Mail Day and confirmed what we read.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Show honestly where this bill came from: a machine read a photo and a person confirmed it. Give one place to fix it, view the photo, or delete both.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS:\n1. The amount \"$142.18\" and \"due in 3 days · Fri 23 Oct\". This is the host headline.\n2. StatusChip \"Upcoming\".\n3. Below them, the quiet block \"From a photo you took · Mon 19 Oct\".\nThe host's Mark paid stays the screen's primary action. Inside the block, \"View the photo\" leads.\n\nCONTENT (house style fixtures; list every delta on Notes)\nFixture deltas: Sam Ortega has bill access: he can add bills and mark them paid. Alex Kim is a guest without bill access.\nHost: Clark Public Utilities · $142.18 · due Fri 23 Oct · account ending 4471 · service address 2418 NE Larkspur Loop, Vancouver, WA 98684 · \"Added by you · Mon 19 Oct\". This existing host line is the plain-words label for the block's mark on the main screen.\nBlock (Maya took the photo):\n- a 56pt stacked thumbnail labelled \"2 pages\";\n- header \"From a photo you took · Mon 19 Oct\";\n- line \"We read this from your photo. You confirmed the amount on Mon 19 Oct.\"\nVariants:\n- Corrected date (Maya): \"We read Thu 8 Oct, the statement date. You changed it to Fri 23 Oct on Mon 19 Oct.\"\n- Sam took and confirmed it: header \"From a photo Sam took · Mon 19 Oct\"; line \"We read this from Sam's photo. Sam confirmed the amount on Mon 19 Oct.\"; corrected line \"We read Thu 8 Oct, the statement date. Sam changed it to Fri 23 Oct on Mon 19 Oct.\"; host line \"Added by Sam · Mon 19 Oct\". The header always names the person who took the photo.\n- Paid (frame dated Fri 23 Oct): \"Paid by Sam · Thu 22 Oct\".\n- Overdue (frame dated Mon 26 Oct): \"Overdue · was due Fri 23 Oct\".\n- Photo deleted: the September bill, Clark Public Utilities · $109.60 · Paid, \"From a photo you took · Mon 21 Sep\", and \"The photo was deleted on Sat 17 Oct. The amount you confirmed stays.\"\n- Guest (Alex): host headline \"A household bill · due Fri 23 Oct\" with no payee or amount; block header \"From a photo Maya took · Mon 19 Oct\"; line \"We read this from Maya's photo. Maya confirmed it on Mon 19 Oct.\"\nWorst case: \"Washington State Department of Labor & Industries\" · $12,480.00 · due Mon 2 Nov · 12 pages, frame dated Fri 23 Oct, all in Sam's wording: header \"From a photo Sam took · Mon 19 Oct\", line \"We read Thu 15 Oct, the statement date. Sam changed it to Mon 2 Nov on Mon 19 Oct.\", and \"Paid by Sam · Thu 22 Oct\".\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\nPlacement:\n- The block is evidence placed beneath the bill's facts, never a banner. It sits below the amount, due date, status and account facts, and above the bill trend card.\n- It uses surface.raised, one step quieter than the bill facts. Light mode: a border.default hairline plus shadow sm. Dark mode: an edge of at least 3:1 ink.\n\nRow 1 is the whole-row target (44pt min):\n- ThumbnailRail (56pt, radius md) on the left.\n- To its right: ProvenanceMark S (you-added), then the header in bodySmall and the line in caption, both text.secondary. The row prints no legend word; the header names the person.\nActions:\n- Under row 1, two text buttons: \"View the photo\" and \"Fix what we read\".\n- At the block's foot, set apart by 16pt: \"Delete the bill and the photo\" in text.error on base with a border.\n- On a snapped bill, both the host's remove action and \"Delete the bill and the photo\" open this same DestructiveConfirm; they share one confirm and one outcome.\n\nMarks:\n- Every committed bill shows the filled mark with the knocked-out tick, whoever added it. A corrected value keeps that mark; only the plain-text history line tells the story.\n- Draw no hollow mark in this block, no confidence number, and no \"AI\" label.\n\nTapping row 1 opens ProvenanceSheet, titled \"Where this fact comes from\" (iOS medium detent; Android ModalBottomSheet; web 1440 a 560px centred modal; web 390 a bottom sheet), with a visible Close and, in order:\n- mark L plus the contract legend line (\"● Official · ○ On record, not confirmed · ✓ You added this\") with \"✓ You added this\" emphasised as the current shape; the legend is the same in every variant;\n- Authority: \"Your photo · read Mon 19 Oct 6:04 PM\" (Sam's variant: \"Sam's photo · read Mon 19 Oct 6:04 PM\");\n- the confidence sentence \"Read from your photo on Mon 19 Oct. You confirmed the payee, amount and due date.\" In the corrected variant: \"Read from your photo on Mon 19 Oct. You confirmed the payee and amount, and changed the due date to Fri 23 Oct.\" In Sam's variant: \"Read from Sam's photo on Mon 19 Oct. Sam confirmed the payee, amount and due date.\";\n- Covers: \"Your household\";\n- Source: the no-URL state, a flat caption \"Your photo\" with no link glyph, not tappable;\n- a foot control \"Fix what we read\". Corrections happen in place; this sheet does not offer the public-record \"This isn't right\" reason list.\n\nDegradation:\n- A hand-entered bill has no block at all: no empty slot, no \"No photo\" row.\n- Photo deleted: the rail uses its deleted variant (quiet document glyph plus words). \"View the photo\" is removed. \"Fix what we read\" stays and opens the confirm screen without a photo pane. The delete reads \"Delete the bill\" and opens the bill-only confirm.\n- Loading: the host renders first; the block slot is held at its final height by WarmingSkeleton (row variant: a 56pt square plus two bars; shimmer, static under Reduce Motion), with no text.\n- Offline: the rail uses its offline variant.\n- Guest (Alex): the thumbnail is replaced by a document glyph, because a photo of a bill shows the amount. The block shows its header and line, and in place of the three actions one LockedActionRow \"Maya or Sam can view, fix or delete this bill.\" The host's Mark paid is replaced by LockedActionRow \"Maya or Sam can mark this paid.\"\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\nNavigation:\n- \"View the photo\" opens the mail piece; Back returns here.\n- \"Fix what we read\" reopens Confirm what we read with the bill's values. Committing there returns here with the history line updated.\nDelete:\n- Delete opens DestructiveConfirm as drawn on the Foundations board: the custom in-app dialog with stacked buttons on iOS (not the system alert, so the outlined destructive button shows), the M3 basic dialog on Android, a centred dialog on web. Keyboard focus lands on the Keep button. On confirm, Maya returns to Bills.\n- The row collapses in place to InlineUndo \"Bill and photo deleted · Undo\" (bill-only: \"Bill deleted · Undo\"), which stays until she leaves the screen. A snackbar may echo it, and it stays while a screen reader runs.\n- Nothing is removed and no reminder is cancelled until the undo closes. The deleted bill never lingers under Upcoming.\nArrival, motion and haptics:\n- A push arrival moves focus to the amount with no highlight animation.\n- Reduce Motion: cross-fades only; the skeleton is static.\n- One light haptic tick when the delete is confirmed.\n- Android Back and web Escape close the sheet and the confirm; focus returns to row 1.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: ProvenanceMark (you-added; S in the block, L in the sheet) · ProvenanceSheet (photo-read fact type, no-URL source, foot control \"Fix what we read\") · ThumbnailRail (56pt, stacked; deleted and offline states) · DestructiveConfirm (new variants requested from the Foundations board: bill plus photo, and bill only) · InlineUndo (bill plus photo deleted; bill deleted) · StatusChip (Upcoming, Overdue, Paid) · BillRow (on the Bills list after delete) · LockedActionRow (names who can act) · WarmingSkeleton (row variant) · InlineErrorRow · OfflineNotice.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\nReading order: host facts, then the block's header, line and mark name, then its actions.\nRow 1 is read as one element: \"From a photo you took, Monday 19 October. We read this from your photo. You confirmed the amount on Monday 19 October. You added this. Opens where this fact comes from.\" In Sam's variant: \"From a photo Sam took, Monday 19 October. We read this from Sam's photo. Sam confirmed the amount on Monday 19 October. Added by your household. Opens where this fact comes from.\"\nElements:\n- The thumbnail is labelled \"Photo of the bill, 2 pages\" and is never a target by itself.\n- Disabled actions stay focusable and read their reason.\n- Overdue is stated in words; the error hue appears on the glyph only.\n- The confirm puts keyboard focus on Keep, never on Delete.\n- The skeleton reads \"Loading\" once.\nAX5: the thumbnail moves above the text, and the two text buttons stack full width.\n\nCOPY (sentence case)\n\"From a photo you took · Mon 19 Oct\" · \"From a photo Sam took · Mon 19 Oct\" · \"From a photo Maya took · Mon 19 Oct\"\n\"We read this from your photo. You confirmed the amount on Mon 19 Oct.\"\n\"We read this from Sam's photo. Sam confirmed the amount on Mon 19 Oct.\"\n\"We read this from Maya's photo. Maya confirmed it on Mon 19 Oct.\"\n\"We read Thu 8 Oct, the statement date. You changed it to Fri 23 Oct on Mon 19 Oct.\"\n\"We read Thu 8 Oct, the statement date. Sam changed it to Fri 23 Oct on Mon 19 Oct.\"\n\"due in 3 days · Fri 23 Oct\" · \"Added by you · Mon 19 Oct\" · \"Added by Sam · Mon 19 Oct\"\n\"View the photo\" · \"Fix what we read\" · \"Delete the bill and the photo\" · \"Delete the bill\"\nSheet: \"Where this fact comes from\" · \"✓ You added this\" · \"Your photo · read Mon 19 Oct 6:04 PM\" · \"Sam's photo · read Mon 19 Oct 6:04 PM\" · the three confidence sentences above · \"Covers: Your household\" · \"Source: Your photo\" · \"Close\"\nConfirm, bill plus photo:\n- title \"Delete this bill and its photo?\"\n- body \"This removes the $142.18 Clark Public Utilities bill, its reminders and both photo pages. The mail record stays in Mail. Nothing else changes.\" The page words follow the page count: \"the photo\" for 1 page, \"both photo pages\" for 2, \"all 12 photo pages\" for 12.\n- buttons \"Delete bill and photo\" / \"Keep them\"\nConfirm, bill only (photo already deleted):\n- title \"Delete this bill?\"\n- body \"This removes the $109.60 Clark Public Utilities bill. The mail record stays in Mail. Nothing else changes.\"\n- buttons \"Delete bill\" / \"Keep it\"\n\"Bill and photo deleted · Undo\" · \"Bill deleted · Undo\"\n\"The photo was deleted on Sat 17 Oct. The amount you confirmed stays.\"\n\"Paid by Sam · Thu 22 Oct\" · \"Overdue · was due Fri 23 Oct\"\nGuest (Alex): \"A household bill · due Fri 23 Oct\" · \"Only Maya and Sam can see this bill's sender, amount and photo.\" · LockedActionRow \"Maya or Sam can view, fix or delete this bill.\" · LockedActionRow \"Maya or Sam can mark this paid.\"\nError: \"We couldn't load where this bill came from.\" · \"Retry\"\nOffline: \"You're offline. The photo isn't saved on this device.\" · under each action: \"Needs a connection.\"\n\nEDGE CASES\n- The longest payee wraps and never truncates. \"$12,480.00\" fits the host headline.\n- A 12-page piece shows the stacked thumbnail labelled \"12 pages\", and its confirm body says \"all 12 photo pages\".\n- Slow network: the host renders first, the block slot shows WarmingSkeleton row variant at full height (shimmer; static under Reduce Motion), then the error row if loading fails.\n- A member with view-only bill access (not drawn; list on Notes) sees Fix and Delete replaced by LockedActionRow \"Maya or Sam can fix or delete this bill.\"\n- The paid arrival reads as reassurance, and the block is unchanged.\n- Overdue: the chip changes and the block stays quiet.\n- A saved place (PLACE B) has no bills, so this block never appears there.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a banner above the amount, draw a quiet block beneath the facts — because the amount is what people came for.\n- Instead of a hollow mark on a corrected bill, draw the tick mark plus a plain history line — because the person confirmed it, and a hollow mark would say they had not.\n- Instead of \"You added this\" printed beside \"From a photo Sam took\", print only the header that names the person and keep the unchanged legend in the sheet — because the row must say who added the bill.\n- Instead of a confidence percentage or an \"AI\" badge, draw \"You confirmed the amount on Mon 19 Oct\" — because a score invites doubt about a value already checked.\n- Instead of a \"No photo\" placeholder on a hand-entered bill, draw nothing — because an empty slot reads as missing data.\n- Instead of \"Paid\" for confirming a read, say \"confirmed\" — because Paid only ever means Mark paid.\n- Instead of a confirm that only warns the delete is permanent, or the iOS system alert, draw the Foundations custom dialog that names the bill and pages that go and the mail record that stays — because people need to know what survives.\n- Instead of three greyed-out actions for a guest, draw one LockedActionRow naming who can act — because present-but-inert controls are not allowed.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- On every arrival, the amount is read first and the photo origin second.\n- Anyone reading the block can say who took the photo and who confirmed it.\n- The photo is one tap away, and fixes happen in place.\n- Delete removes bill and photo together, from either delete control, with an undo that has no timer; after the photo is gone, the bill-only confirm says exactly what goes.\n- A corrected date never looks unconfirmed.\n- A hand-entered bill looks exactly as it does today.\n- Alex sees that a household bill is due, and no payee, amount or photo.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f10-bill-provenance · ios · 01-snapped-confirmed · light — Clark Public Utilities, block beneath the facts, Mark paid in the host.\n2. f10-bill-provenance · ios · 02-manual-no-block · light — the same bill entered by hand, no block.\n3. f10-bill-provenance · ios · 03-corrected-date · light — tick mark plus Maya's history line.\n4. f10-bill-provenance · ios · 04-provenance-sheet · light — \"Where this fact comes from\" at medium detent with legend, Authority, sentence, Covers, flat Source caption, Fix what we read, Close.\n5. f10-bill-provenance · ios · 05-delete-confirm · light — the Foundations custom dialog, bill plus photo, stacked buttons, focus on Keep them.\n6. f10-bill-provenance · ios · 06-deleted-undo · light — Bills list row collapsed to \"Bill and photo deleted · Undo\".\n7. f10-bill-provenance · ios · 07-photo-deleted · light — September bill, deleted rail, \"Delete the bill\".\n8. f10-bill-provenance · ios · 07b-delete-bill-confirm · light — the bill-only dialog \"Delete this bill?\" over the September bill.\n9. f10-bill-provenance · ios · 08-paid-by-sam · light — landing from Sam's notification on Fri 23 Oct, reassurance.\n10. f10-bill-provenance · ios · 09-sam-took-photo · light — Sam's header, Sam's corrected line, \"Added by Sam · Mon 19 Oct\" in the host.\n11. f10-bill-provenance · ios · 10-overdue · light — Mon 26 Oct, Overdue chip, quiet block.\n12. f10-bill-provenance · ios · 11-guest · light — Alex: \"A household bill · due Fri 23 Oct\", \"From a photo Maya took\", Maya's line, document glyph, both LockedActionRows.\n13. f10-bill-provenance · ios · 12-loading · light — host facts rendered, block slot held by WarmingSkeleton (56pt square plus two bars), no text.\n14. f10-bill-provenance · ios · 13-error · light — InlineErrorRow in the block slot, bill intact.\n15. f10-bill-provenance · ios · 14-offline · light — offline rail, disabled actions with reasons.\n16. f10-bill-provenance · android · 15-snapped-confirmed · light — Material version of frame 1.\n17. f10-bill-provenance · web-1440 · 16-snapped-confirmed · light — the new bill detail route with the left sidebar.\n18. f10-bill-provenance · web-1440 · 17-provenance-sheet · light — 560px centred modal with Close.\n19. f10-bill-provenance · web-390 · 18-worst-case · light — Labor & Industries in Sam's wording: header, corrected line, paid line, \"12 pages\".\n20. f10-bill-provenance · ios · 19-ax5 · light — AX5 stacking.\n21. f10-bill-provenance · ios · 20-greyscale · light — frame 1 in greyscale.\n22. f10-bill-provenance · ios · 01-snapped-confirmed · dark — dark twin of frame 1.\n23. f10-bill-provenance · ios · 10-overdue · dark — dark twin of frame 10.\n24. Notes — the scene dates; Sam has bill access (adds bills, marks paid); Alex Kim is a guest without bill access and gets no bill notifications; the view-only member variant (not drawn); open items for the Foundations board: new DestructiveConfirm variants \"bill plus photo\" and \"bill only\" (titles, bodies, buttons), new InlineUndo string \"Bill deleted · Undo\", the photo-read ProvenanceSheet fact-type variant with foot control \"Fix what we read\", and the question of the tick mark's spoken name when another household member added the fact (proposed: \"Added by your household\"; fallback: the fixed name \"you added this\"); engineering: fix the web bill delete status cancelled → canceled so a deleted snapped bill leaves Upcoming; every invented string (Thu 15 Oct statement date, Authority lines, the page-count wording, Maya's guest line); assumptions; omitted states (Android 200%, web-390 sheet).\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: 1-6, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 2: 7-12, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 3: 13-18, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 4: 19-24.",
        "changeLog": [
          "DestructiveConfirm drawn as on the Foundations board (custom iOS dialog, M3 basic dialog, web centred dialog), not the system alert; bill-plus-photo listed on Notes as a new Foundations variant (review major, 00d).",
          "Added the bill-only confirm ('Delete this bill?', no reminders on a paid bill), 'Bill deleted · Undo', and frame 07b; page words in the confirm body follow the page count (review minor x2).",
          "Guests arrive only by direct link; members without bill access get no bill notifications, so no payee leaks (review minor x2, design doc F10).",
          "ProvenanceSheet gains the no-URL Source flat caption 'Your photo'; legend unchanged in every variant; Sam's Authority line 'Sam's photo · read …' (review minor/major).",
          "Sam's spoken label rewritten per review major; 'Added by your household' listed on Notes as a proposed spoken name with the contract's fixed name as fallback.",
          "Guest block now has Maya's line and one LockedActionRow replacing three disabled actions (review minor, contract LockedActionRow).",
          "Skeleton shimmer by default, static under Reduce Motion; deep-link URLs added (review minor).",
          "Notes engineering line: web delete status cancelled → canceled (review minor, inventory uxNote).",
          "Keyboard focus on Keep per 00d; INSTEAD OF gains the guest locked-row line (8 lines)."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f10-bill-trend",
        "name": "Bill trend vs the going rate",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 19,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Bill trend vs the going rate (internal name; no user-facing string says \"going rate\") · f10-bill-trend\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Bill detail\". This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed. You are adding one card, directly beneath the bill provenance block. On a hand-entered bill, which has no block, it goes directly beneath the bill facts. On web, the host is the \"Bill detail (new web route)\" design output.\n\nATTACH: Bill detail on iOS and Android; the \"Bill detail (new web route)\" design output at web 1440 and 390; the same screen with the bill provenance block; the place file Money section; the Foundations board (SourceCaption, FreshnessLine, WarmingSkeleton, InlineErrorRow, ProvenanceMark, OfflineNotice).\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: web 1440x900 (left sidebar) and 390x844; iOS 393x852; Android 412x915.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Place tab → place file → Money → Bills → Bill detail. There is one card per bill type. People arrive by:\n- Any arrival at Bill detail: a Bills list row, the Today strip money row, the bill reminder push, the household notification row, or \"Added to bills\" on a mail piece. They scroll to the card.\n- The place file Money section, whose bill row opens Bill detail and scrolls once to this card. A highlight fades in 300ms and focus moves to the card title.\nIn the mail-snap journey this card is the last step: after Mark paid, the person scrolls down to see this month's column against the nearby average.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Maya Chen, owner of HOME A, on Tue 20 Oct 2026 at 7:30 AM (fixture delta: the morning after Mail Day). She has had the Clark Public Utilities account for a year. Last night she confirmed October's $142.18 bill from a photo, and now she wonders whether that is normal for around here.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Answer \"is this bill normal for around here?\" at a glance, so the monthly visit has a payoff.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: (1) the summary sentence; (2) October's column with \"$142\" printed above it; (3) the nearby average line and its key. There is no primary action; \"Show amounts\" is the only control.\n\nCONTENT (fixture deltas only; list each on Notes):\n- Card title: \"Clark Public Utilities · last 12 months\".\n- Amounts, Nov 2025 → Oct 2026: 118.22, 167.05, 198.73, 186.41, 151.60, 112.88, 94.15, 88.02, 103.77, 121.34, 109.60, 142.18. October is the bill open on this screen; it came from a photo Maya confirmed on Mon 19 Oct. September ($109.60) also came from a photo she confirmed.\n- Nearby average: $127.40 across 14 homes, from Pantopus. It updated Thu 1 Oct.\n- Partial history: Jun–Oct 2026 only (88.02, 103.77, 121.34, 109.60, 142.18).\n- Worst case: the same 12 amounts with January replaced by $412.90, standing in for an electric-heat winter; the axis top moves to $450.\n- Offline: cached as of Mon 19 Oct, 9:40 PM.\n- Guest without bill access: Alex Kim. Sam Ortega has bill access.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION:\n- Chart form: a zero-based column chart of your own amounts, with the nearby average as one horizontal reference line. It is never a second series of paired bars, because paired bars read as one household against another, while a baseline reads as the typical amount.\n- Summary sentence (body): \"October $142. Your last 12 months ranged from $88 in June to $199 in January. The average of 14 homes nearby is $127.\"\n- Key line, directly above the plot, left-aligned, caption size, wrapping on narrow widths: a small column swatch with \"Your amounts\", a 16pt sample of the reference line with \"Nearby average $127\", and the tick mark with \"✓ You added this\" (the mark's legend word, once on this card). The line itself carries no in-plot label.\n- Plot, 160pt tall:\n  - 12 equal columns with 4px gaps.\n  - A month initial under each (N D J F M A M J J A S O). A hairline and a \"2026\" caption sit under January, where the year turns.\n  - The y-axis starts at $0 and has only two labels: $0 at the baseline and $200 at the top. The top rounds up to the next $50 above the largest amount. There are no interior gridlines.\n- Columns:\n  - Light mode, past months: filled primary.600.\n  - Light mode, current month: primary.800 with a 2px text.primary outline, \"$142\" printed above it with a 2px base halo, and ProvenanceMark XS (you-added) centred under its initial. Only the current column carries the mark. The provenance block above and this chart agree.\n  - Dark mode: past columns primary.500; current month primary.300 with a 2px dark text.primary outline; the reference line in dark text.secondary with a dark raised halo. State the computed contrast ratios on Notes.\n  - All columns use one ink family; high months get no success or error colour, because a high winter bill is not a failure.\n- Reference line (light): 1.5px in text.strong with a 2px surface halo where it crosses columns, spanning the plot at $127.40.\n- Below the plot, one SourceCaption in the contract order authority · scope · as-of: \"Pantopus · your confirmed bills and the average of 14 homes nearby (confirmed amounts only) · updated Thu 1 Oct\".\n- Then the \"Show amounts\" disclosure. It opens 12 rows with full month names, newest first: \"October 2026 · $142.18 · from a photo you confirmed\", \"September 2026 · $109.60 · from a photo you confirmed\", \"August 2026 · $121.34\" … \"November 2025 · $118.22\". A month with no bill reads \"no bill\". On a hand-entered bill the October row reads \"October 2026 · $142.18 · you added this\".\n- Degradation:\n  - Not enough homes: draw the columns and no line at all. The key line drops the line sample. The caption \"Not enough homes nearby to compare yet\" sits under the plot, and the SourceCaption reads \"Pantopus · your household's confirmed bills · updated Mon 19 Oct\", with no nearby-average clause. The summary drops its last sentence. The missing line is the honest signal. Never draw a line at zero, a dashed baseline, or a county or state figure in its place.\n  - Partial history: keep all 12 month slots and their initials. Months with no bill hold no column. A caption adds \"You've had this bill since June.\" The summary reads \"October $142. Since June your bill ranged from $88 in June to $142 in October. The average of 14 homes nearby is $127.\" The line is still drawn.\n  - Stale average (a cached average exists): the line stays at $127.40 and a FreshnessLine under the SourceCaption reads \"Nearby average from Pantopus, Thu 1 Oct · Couldn't refresh · Retry\".\n  - Failed average (nothing cached): columns drawn, no line, no line sample, and FreshnessLine failed variant \"Couldn't load the nearby average from Pantopus · Retry\". The summary drops its last sentence.\n  - Offline: the cached chart stays at full contrast (never greyed), with the FreshnessLine offline line under the card header.\n  - Guest without bill access (Alex): the title becomes \"Household bill · last 12 months\" (no payee). The plot, key and SourceCaption are replaced by one reason line only, with no shapes, no blurred numbers and no locked-action row (the card has no action to lock).\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS:\n- Columns are not individual tap targets on phones. Values are read through \"Show amounts\".\n- On web 1440, each column is keyboard-focusable, and focus shows its value in a label. The same value is in the list, so nothing depends on hover.\n- \"Show amounts\" expands in place in 200ms and becomes \"Hide amounts\".\n- Retry on the stale or failed line refreshes only the average; the columns stay.\n- Columns do not animate in. Reduce Motion: expand is a cross-fade; the skeleton is static. No haptics.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: ProvenanceMark (you-added, XS, current column only; legend in the key line) · SourceCaption · FreshnessLine (offline, stale and failed) · WarmingSkeleton (instrument variant, 12 varied columns; shimmer, static under Reduce Motion) · InlineErrorRow · OfflineNotice.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n- iOS: the chart exposes audio-graph navigation; its label is the summary sentence.\n- Android and web: the chart is an image whose label is the summary sentence, and the \"Show amounts\" list is the equivalent table.\n- Month initials are never spoken alone.\n- Reading order: title, summary, key line, chart, caption, source, freshness, Show amounts.\n- Columns reach at least 3:1 against the card in both themes. The current month differs by its printed value, outline and mark, not by hue alone.\n- The disclosure has a 44pt/48dp/44px target and announces expanded or collapsed. Retry has a 44pt target.\n- At AX5: the summary and key line wrap, the plot keeps its height and goes full width, and list rows stack month over amount.\n- The frame must read correctly in greyscale.\n\nCOPY (sentence case):\n- \"Clark Public Utilities · last 12 months\"\n- \"October $142. Your last 12 months ranged from $88 in June to $199 in January. The average of 14 homes nearby is $127.\"\n- Key: \"Your amounts\" · \"Nearby average $127\" · \"✓ You added this\"\n- \"Pantopus · your confirmed bills and the average of 14 homes nearby (confirmed amounts only) · updated Thu 1 Oct\"\n- \"Show amounts\" / \"Hide amounts\" · \"October 2026 · $142.18 · from a photo you confirmed\" · \"September 2026 · $109.60 · from a photo you confirmed\" · hand-entered: \"October 2026 · $142.18 · you added this\" · partial history: \"May 2026 · no bill\"\n- \"Not enough homes nearby to compare yet\" · \"Pantopus · your household's confirmed bills · updated Mon 19 Oct\" · \"You've had this bill since June.\"\n- Guest (Alex): \"Household bill · last 12 months\" · \"Only Maya and Sam can see bill amounts.\"\n- Error: \"We couldn't load the last 12 months.\" · \"Retry\"\n- Offline: \"You're offline · as of Mon 19 Oct, 9:40 PM\"\n- Stale average: \"Nearby average from Pantopus, Thu 1 Oct · Couldn't refresh · Retry\"\n- Failed average: \"Couldn't load the nearby average from Pantopus · Retry\"\n- Worst-case summary: \"October $142. Your last 12 months ranged from $88 in June to $413 in January. The average of 14 homes nearby is $127.\"\n\nEDGE CASES:\n- Largest amount $412.90: the axis top becomes $450; the key line stays above the plot and \"$142\" stays above October.\n- One month of history: one column and eleven empty slots, with \"You've had this bill since October.\"\n- Zero confirmed amounts: the card is absent.\n- An unconfirmed read is never a column and never counts toward any average.\n- Slow network: the bill renders first, and the card shows WarmingSkeleton instrument variant, 12 varied columns (shimmer; static under Reduce Motion), with no line and no caption claim.\n- A saved place has no bills, so there is no card.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of paired bars for you and the neighbourhood, draw one reference line — because the average is a typical amount, not another household.\n- Instead of a label sitting on the line inside the plot, draw a key line above the plot — because an in-plot label covers the July to October columns.\n- Instead of \"12% above average\" or an up arrow, draw the plain summary sentence — because a verdict judges the household and the house rules ban percentages.\n- Instead of pale primary.200 columns, or success and error colours on high months, draw primary.600 columns in one ink plus a list of amounts — because column height is the information, needs 3:1, and a high winter bill is not a failure.\n- Instead of a zero line or a county figure when homes are too few, draw no line, drop the average from the source caption and say why — because the missing line is the honest signal.\n- Instead of \"your neighbours\" on the line, write \"Nearby average\" and \"14 homes nearby\" — because it describes an average, not anyone's home.\n- Instead of a line or area chart of your amounts, draw columns — because months are separate bills.\n- Instead of greying the offline chart, keep full contrast and add the \"as of\" line — because stale values stay readable with their age.\n\nDONE WHEN: Maya reads \"is this normal?\" from the sentence alone. A screen-reader user gets all 12 amounts, including \"no bill\" months. With too few homes, the line is simply absent, the source caption makes no average claim, and the caption says why. A stale or failed average names Pantopus and offers Retry. Nothing on the card compares households or grades the bill. Alex sees only that amounts are limited to Maya and Sam.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f10-bill-trend · ios · 01-twelve-months · light — full year, key line, line, \"$142\" and tick on October, beneath the provenance block.\n2. f10-bill-trend · ios · 02-show-amounts-open · light — 12-row list expanded, October and September with \"from a photo you confirmed\".\n3. f10-bill-trend · ios · 03-partial-history · light — Jun–Oct columns, seven empty labelled slots, line drawn.\n4. f10-bill-trend · ios · 04-not-enough-homes · light — columns, no line, new caption, SourceCaption without the average clause.\n5. f10-bill-trend · ios · 05-guest · light — Alex: \"Household bill\" title, reason line only, no shapes.\n6. f10-bill-trend · ios · 06-loading · light — WarmingSkeleton instrument variant, 12 varied columns (shimmer frame).\n7. f10-bill-trend · ios · 07-error · light — InlineErrorRow, bill above intact.\n8. f10-bill-trend · ios · 08-offline · light — cached chart at full contrast, \"You're offline · as of Mon 19 Oct, 9:40 PM\".\n9. f10-bill-trend · ios · 09-average-failed · light — columns, no line, FreshnessLine failed variant naming Pantopus.\n10. f10-bill-trend · ios · 10-average-stale · light — line kept, \"Nearby average from Pantopus, Thu 1 Oct · Couldn't refresh · Retry\".\n11. f10-bill-trend · android · 11-twelve-months · light — Material version of frame 1.\n12. f10-bill-trend · web-1440 · 12-twelve-months · light — bill detail route, October column focused, arrival from the place file highlight.\n13. f10-bill-trend · web-390 · 13-hand-entered · light — hand-entered bill, card directly under the facts, list open with \"October 2026 · $142.18 · you added this\".\n14. f10-bill-trend · ios · 14-worst-case · light — $412.90 January, axis $450, key line above the plot.\n15. f10-bill-trend · ios · 15-ax5 · light — AX5 layout.\n16. f10-bill-trend · ios · 16-greyscale · light — frame 1 in greyscale.\n17. f10-bill-trend · ios · 01-twelve-months · dark — dark twin of frame 1, with the named dark steps.\n18. f10-bill-trend · ios · 04-not-enough-homes · dark — dark twin of frame 4.\n19. Notes — the Tue 20 Oct scene date; the dark column steps and their computed ratios; departure from the inventory for the founder to decide: the inventory says a snapped bill marks its column, but the tick sits on the current column only, even though September was also from a photo (alternative: an XS tick under every column whose bill came from a confirmed photo); do not build this from the decorative Sparkline primitive, every column comes from confirmed amounts; engineering note: iOS uses Swift Charts so audio graphs work; every invented string (all 12 amounts, $127.40, 14 homes, Thu 1 Oct, $412.90, the hand-entered, not-enough-homes and failed-average strings); assumptions; omitted states (Android 200%, static skeleton frame).\n\nBATCH PLAN:\nTurn 1: 1-6, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 2: 7-12, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 3: 13-18, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 4: 19.",
        "changeLog": [
          "SourceCaption reordered to the contract's authority · scope · as-of, including the not-enough-homes variant (review minor x2).",
          "Kept the current-column-only tick and recorded it on Notes as a departure from the inventory for the founder, with the every-photo-column alternative (review minor).",
          "Skeleton is WarmingSkeleton instrument variant, shimmer with static under Reduce Motion (review minor).",
          "Guest state keeps only the reason line; LockedActionRow dropped because the card has no action (review minor).",
          "INSTEAD OF merged to 8 lines (colour rule folded into the pale-columns line and also stated in LAYOUT); worst case now 'an electric-heat winter' (review minor).",
          "Offline full-contrast rule added to Degradation; OfflineNotice replaces LockedActionRow in ATTACH."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "f10-mail-snap-privacy",
        "name": "Mail snaps: privacy and storage",
        "platforms": [
          "web",
          "ios",
          "android"
        ],
        "isNew": false,
        "frameCount": 21,
        "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Mail snaps: privacy and storage · f10-mail-snap-privacy\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Mail Day settings\". This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed. You are adding one card, \"Photos of your mail\". On web it goes in the settings column. On iOS and Android it goes in the Mail Day settings stack, not in notification settings.\n\nATTACH: Mail Day settings on web 1440 (settings column), iOS and Android; the Mail Day screen with its settings row; the household member roster; the Foundations board (ThumbnailRail, DestructiveConfirm, ScopeChip, LockedActionRow, InlineErrorRow, WarmingSkeleton, OfflineNotice, FreshnessLine).\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: web 1440x900 (left sidebar; card measure 720px max) and 390x844; iOS 393x852; Android 412x915.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Mail tab → Mail Day → settings. Entry points:\n- Web: the \"Mail snap settings\" link on the Mail Day page.\n- Native: the settings row on the Mail Day screen.\n- \"Manage mail snaps\" on a photographed mail piece.\n- \"Where does this photo go?\" on the \"Confirm what we read\" screen.\n- The privacy mirror's \"What we store\" row.\nArrivals from a link scroll once to this card, fade a highlight within 300ms, and move focus to the card title. Each list row opens that mail piece, where one photo can be deleted; Back returns here.\nJourney: someone who photographed a bank statement by mistake comes here, finds it in the list, opens it and deletes that photo, or deletes all of them. Their bills survive either way.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Maya Chen, owner of HOME A, on Tue 20 Oct 2026 at 7:30 AM (a fixture delta: the morning after last night's Mail Day). On Wed 30 Sep she photographed a Riverview Bank statement by mistake. Now she wants to see which photos exist and who can see them.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: One place to understand where photos of your mail are kept, who can see them, and to delete them.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: (1) the title \"Photos of your mail\" with ScopeChip \"Your household\"; (2) the three-row \"What we keep / Who can see them / How to delete\" grid; (3) the list of photos. There is no single primary button. The toggle is the main control, and the destructive action comes last.\n\nCONTENT (fixture deltas only; list each on Notes):\n- Sam Ortega has bill access. Alex Kim is a guest without bill access.\n- 17 photos, 41.3 MB. A piece with several pages is one row. List, newest first (the same pieces the mailbox drawer shows under \"Photographed\"):\n  - Clark Public Utilities · Mon 19 Oct · 2 pages · 4.8 MB\n  - Comcast · Mon 19 Oct · 1.9 MB\n  - Larkspur Loop HOA · Mon 19 Oct · 1.9 MB (its read is not confirmed yet; still in Needs a call)\n  - Chase statement · Mon 19 Oct · 2 pages · 4.4 MB · Filed, no bill\n  - NW Natural · Mon 5 Oct · 2.1 MB\n  - Riverview Bank statement · Wed 30 Sep · 4.2 MB · Filed, no bill\n  - Waste Connections · Mon 21 Sep · 2.2 MB · Filed, no bill\n  - Not classified · Sat 12 Sep · 3.6 MB\n  - then \"Show all 17 photos\"\n- Retention is an open product decision. Draw the retention period as 90 days on every frame. Option A (frames 01-03 and the rest): keeping photos is on and each photo is deleted 90 days after it was taken. Option B (frame 04 only): keeping photos is off by default.\n- Worst case: 240 photos · 1.2 GB, and the payee \"Washington State Department of Labor & Industries\" · 12 pages.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION: A trust surface, not a preferences grid. One column in this fixed order:\n1. Title and ScopeChip \"Your household\".\n2. The explainer (body, two sentences).\n3. The grid. Three label/value rows (label in label style, value in body). Each value ends with a link to the control that changes it; write \"None\" as the word, never as a dash.\n   - \"What we keep\": \"The photo, which shows everything printed on the page, including your full account number. From it we save the payee, amount, due date and last 4 account digits as text. Full account numbers saved as text: None.\" Link: \"Change what we keep\" (scrolls to the toggle).\n   - \"Who can see them\": \"You and Sam. Alex sees that a piece arrived, not the photo or the amount. People nearby: None.\" Link: \"Manage who can see bills\" (opens the household member roster with its bill-access roles).\n   - \"How to delete\": \"One photo: open it in the list below. All photos: use Delete all mail snaps at the end of this card.\" Links: \"Go to the list\" and \"Go to Delete all mail snaps\" (each scrolls to its target).\n4. The single toggle \"Keep the photo after we read it\". Its consequence line sits directly beneath it and changes with the toggle; it is never a static helper.\n5. The count line.\n6. The list. Each row: ThumbnailRail (privacy variant, 32pt), payee, date and size, with a \"Filed, no bill\" or \"2 pages\" tag where it applies. The whole row is the target and opens the piece. The first 8 rows always show on the card and are never hidden behind a disclosure; \"Show all 17 photos\" expands the remaining rows in place and moves focus to the first new row. Rows have no checkboxes and no per-row delete.\n7. \"Delete all mail snaps\" in text.error on base with a border. It is never a filled red slab and never above the list.\n- Show no reminder or notification preferences on this card.\n\nState-specific layouts:\n- Maya turned it off (frame 03): toggle off, the off consequence line, then the line \"These 17 were taken while the setting was on. Each is still deleted 90 days after it was taken.\", then the count line and list unchanged.\n- Option B, off by default (frame 04): toggle off, the off consequence line, no retention clause anywhere, the zero-state grid rows, no count line, no list and no delete button, and the option B zero line in the list slot: \"No mail snaps stored. With this setting off, we delete each photo after we read it.\"\n- Zero photos (frames 07-08): the list, count line and delete button are absent (not disabled). The grid's first row reads \"Photos: None right now. The payee, amount, due date and last 4 account digits you confirmed stay with your bills. Full account numbers saved as text: None.\" The How to delete value reads \"Nothing to delete right now.\" with no links. The list slot shows \"No mail snaps stored. Photos you take on Mail Day will be listed here.\"\n- Reading off (frame 09): the notice \"Reading photos is turned off on this deployment. You can still photograph a piece of mail and type the payee, amount and due date yourself.\" replaces the explainer's first sentence. The What we keep value reads \"The photo, which shows everything printed on the page, including your full account number. From it we save the payee, amount, due date and last 4 account digits you type. Full account numbers saved as text: None.\" The toggle still works; its on line is unchanged and its off line becomes \"We delete each photo once you've typed what it says.\"\n- Loading (frame 10): the explainer, grid and toggle render at once; the list slot is held by WarmingSkeleton (row variant, 8 rows with 32pt squares; shimmer, static under Reduce Motion), no text.\n- Error (frame 11): the explainer, grid and toggle still render, and InlineErrorRow sits in the list slot.\n- Member without bill access, seen by Maya (frame 12): a hypothetical where Sam has no bill access. The who value reads \"You can see these photos. Sam and Alex see that a piece arrived, not the photo or the amount. People nearby: None.\"\n- Guest view (Alex, frame 13): explainer and grid only; no count line, no list, no delete button. The toggle is disabled with LockedActionRow. Grid values from Alex's point of view, none with a link:\n  - What we keep: \"The photo, which shows everything printed on the page, including the full account number. From it we save the payee, amount, due date and last 4 account digits as text. Full account numbers saved as text: None.\"\n  - Who can see them: \"Maya and Sam. You see that a piece arrived, not the photo or the amount. People nearby: None.\"\n  - How to delete: \"Maya or Sam can delete these photos.\"\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS:\n- The toggle changes the consequence line at once, and the change is announced. Turning it off never deletes existing photos; the \"These 17 were taken…\" line appears.\n- \"Delete all mail snaps\" opens DestructiveConfirm V2 (all photos) exactly as drawn on the Foundations board: the custom in-app dialog with stacked buttons on iOS (not the system alert), the M3 basic dialog on Android, a centred dialog on web. Keyboard focus lands on Keep them.\n- Deleting uses the component's own deleting state inside the dialog: the title stays, the body becomes \"Deleting 5 of 17…\" with a 4pt bar, updated at most every 5 items (5, 10, 15, then done), both buttons are hidden, and Back, Escape and swipe do nothing. The card behind does not show a second progress line.\n- When done, the dialog closes and the card shows the result line \"17 photos deleted. The bills and their amounts stay.\" above its zero state.\n- Pieces still in Needs a call (Larkspur Loop HOA) stay there after Delete all; Confirm what we read then opens without a photo pane.\n- Deletion is permanent, so there is no Undo.\n- Grid links scroll once and move focus to their target.\n- Reduce Motion: no row collapse animation; states cross-fade; the skeleton is static. One light haptic tick on confirming the delete.\n- In the open state, Back or Escape closes the confirm.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: ScopeChip (\"Your household\") · ThumbnailRail (privacy list, 32pt; offline state) · DestructiveConfirm (V2 all photos; open, deleting and done states) · LockedActionRow (names who can act) · WarmingSkeleton (row variant) · InlineErrorRow · OfflineNotice · FreshnessLine.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n- Reading order follows the fixed order above.\n- Each grid row reads as one element, label then value; its links follow as separate focusable elements.\n- Each list row reads as one element: \"Riverview Bank statement, photographed Wednesday 30 September, 4.2 megabytes, filed, no bill. Opens the photo.\"\n- The toggle speaks its label, its state and the consequence line.\n- Targets are 44pt / 48dp with 8dp gaps / 44px, and thumbnails are never separate targets.\n- Progress (\"Deleting 5 of 17\") and the result are polite live regions. The skeleton reads \"Loading\" once.\n- At AX5 the grid stacks label above value, list rows stack payee above date and size, and the toggle label wraps above the switch.\n- No meaning depends on colour; the delete button reads by its words.\n\nCOPY (sentence case):\n- \"Photos of your mail\"\n- \"We read the photo to suggest a payee, amount and due date. You confirm before anything is saved.\"\n- \"What we keep\" · \"Who can see them\" · \"How to delete\" · \"Change what we keep\" · \"Manage who can see bills\" · \"Go to the list\" · \"Go to Delete all mail snaps\"\n- \"You and Sam. Alex sees that a piece arrived, not the photo or the amount. People nearby: None.\"\n- \"Keep the photo after we read it\"\n- On: \"We keep each photo for 90 days so you can check it, then delete it. The payee, amount and due date stay.\"\n- Off: \"We read the photo, then delete it. Only the payee, amount and due date stay.\"\n- \"These 17 were taken while the setting was on. Each is still deleted 90 days after it was taken.\"\n- \"17 photos · 41.3 MB · each kept 90 days, then deleted\" · \"Show all 17 photos\" · \"Filed, no bill\" · \"2 pages\"\n- \"Delete all mail snaps\"\n- Confirm: title \"Delete all 17 photos?\" · body \"The bills and their amounts stay; only the photos are removed.\" · buttons \"Delete 17 photos\" / \"Keep them\" · deleting \"Deleting 5 of 17…\"\n- Result: \"17 photos deleted. The bills and their amounts stay.\"\n- Zero: \"No mail snaps stored. Photos you take on Mail Day will be listed here.\" · option B: \"No mail snaps stored. With this setting off, we delete each photo after we read it.\" · grid row \"Photos: None right now. The payee, amount, due date and last 4 account digits you confirmed stay with your bills. Full account numbers saved as text: None.\" · \"Nothing to delete right now.\"\n- Reading off: \"Reading photos is turned off on this deployment. You can still photograph a piece of mail and type the payee, amount and due date yourself.\" · \"We delete each photo once you've typed what it says.\"\n- Member without bill access: \"You can see these photos. Sam and Alex see that a piece arrived, not the photo or the amount. People nearby: None.\"\n- Guest view (Alex): \"Maya and Sam. You see that a piece arrived, not the photo or the amount. People nearby: None.\" · \"Maya or Sam can delete these photos.\" · \"Only Maya and Sam can see these photos.\" with LockedActionRow \"Maya or Sam can change this setting or delete these photos.\"\n- Error: \"We couldn't load your mail snaps.\" · \"Retry\"\n- Offline: \"You're offline · list as of Mon 19 Oct, 9:40 PM\" · on the toggle and delete: \"Needs a connection.\"\n\nEDGE CASES:\n- 240 photos: the card shows 8 rows and \"Show all 240 photos\". The count line reads \"240 photos · 1.2 GB · each kept 90 days, then deleted\". The confirm reads \"Delete all 240 photos?\" and progress counts in steps of 5.\n- Long payee: wraps and never truncates.\n- A 2-page piece counts as 2 photos and 1 row, tagged \"2 pages\". A 12-page piece is one row tagged \"12 pages\".\n- Unconfirmed pieces: after Delete all, they stay in Needs a call and Confirm what we read opens without a photo pane.\n- Slow network: see frame 10. Error: see frame 11.\n- Offline: cached list at full contrast; toggle and delete disabled with \"Needs a connection.\"; rows without a cached thumbnail use the ThumbnailRail offline state.\n- A saved place has no mail snaps, so the card is absent.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of stacked settings toggles, draw paragraph → grid → one toggle with its consequence → count → list → delete — because this card exists to build trust, not to hold settings.\n- Instead of a \"View snaps\" disclosure or a count chip, show the first 8 rows on the card — because people must see a mistaken bank statement before they can remove it.\n- Instead of \"Everyone in this household can see them\" or \"People without bill access\", name who sees what (\"You and Sam. Alex sees…\") — because bill access differs within a household.\n- Instead of \"Full account numbers: None\" alone, say the photo itself shows the full number — because the stored image carries it even when the text does not.\n- Instead of keeping photos with no stated end, state the 90 days in the consequence and count lines — because the photos show full account numbers.\n- Instead of \"What we keep: None\" after deleting photos, say the confirmed bill facts stay — because the bills still hold payee, amount, due date and last 4 digits.\n- Instead of a disabled delete button when nothing is stored, or a confirm that only says it cannot be undone, draw no button at zero and a confirm that says the bills and their amounts stay — because a destructive control with nothing to act on only alarms people, and losing bills is the fear.\n- Instead of reminder settings on this card, leave them out — because per-home notification toggles do not save today.\n\nDONE WHEN: Maya can find the Riverview Bank statement without leaving the card. She can tell exactly who can see it (Sam yes, Alex no), how long it is kept, and that the photo shows her full account number, and she can delete it, or all 17, knowing her bills stay. A card with zero photos has no destructive control and still says what bill facts remain. The founder can compare option A (frame 02) with option B (frame 04), and each frame states only what is true for that option. Alex, a guest, is told what they can and cannot see, in words that are true for Alex.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f10-mail-snap-privacy · web-1440 · 01-photos-kept · light — settings column, full card at 720px, who-row naming Sam and Alex, 8 rows plus \"Show all 17 photos\".\n2. f10-mail-snap-privacy · ios · 02-photos-kept · light — option A in the Mail Day settings stack.\n3. f10-mail-snap-privacy · ios · 03-maya-turned-off · light — toggle off, off consequence, \"These 17 were taken…\" line, list unchanged.\n4. f10-mail-snap-privacy · ios · 04-option-off-by-default · light — option B: toggle off by default, off consequence, no retention clause, zero-state grid rows, the option B zero line.\n5. f10-mail-snap-privacy · ios · 05-delete-all-confirm · light — DestructiveConfirm V2 as the Foundations custom dialog, stacked buttons, focus on Keep them.\n6. f10-mail-snap-privacy · ios · 06-deleting · light — the same dialog in its deleting state, \"Deleting 5 of 17…\" with the bar, buttons hidden.\n7. f10-mail-snap-privacy · ios · 07-deleted · light — result line above the zero state.\n8. f10-mail-snap-privacy · ios · 08-zero-snaps · light — zero grid rows, \"Nothing to delete right now.\", no list, no delete button.\n9. f10-mail-snap-privacy · ios · 09-reading-off · light — notice replacing the first explainer sentence, \"…digits you type\", toggle working with the reading-off off line.\n10. f10-mail-snap-privacy · ios · 10-loading · light — explainer, grid and toggle rendered; list slot held by WarmingSkeleton (8 rows, 32pt squares).\n11. f10-mail-snap-privacy · ios · 11-error · light — InlineErrorRow in the list slot.\n12. f10-mail-snap-privacy · ios · 12-member-without-bill-access · light — Maya's view where Sam has no bill access, who-row naming Sam and Alex.\n13. f10-mail-snap-privacy · ios · 13-guest-view · light — Alex's view: explainer, Alex's grid values without links, disabled toggle, LockedActionRow.\n14. f10-mail-snap-privacy · ios · 14-offline · light — cached list, disabled controls with reasons.\n15. f10-mail-snap-privacy · android · 15-photos-kept · light — Material switch and list.\n16. f10-mail-snap-privacy · web-390 · 16-worst-case · light — 240 photos, \"Show all 240 photos\", \"Washington State Department of Labor & Industries\".\n17. f10-mail-snap-privacy · ios · 17-ax5 · light — AX5 stacking.\n18. f10-mail-snap-privacy · ios · 18-greyscale · light — frame 2 in greyscale.\n19. f10-mail-snap-privacy · web-1440 · 01-photos-kept · dark — dark twin of frame 1.\n20. f10-mail-snap-privacy · ios · 06-deleting · dark — dark twin of frame 6.\n21. Notes — \"90 days is a stand-in; the retention period and default (option A bounded retention vs option B off by default) are undecided product calls\"; under option B the \"These 17…\" line and the list appear only if photos were kept; the inventory's third explainer sentence \"Photos stay private to this home.\" is dropped because access differs within the household, and the Who can see them row replaces it; alternative who-row wording for households without a named guest: \"People in your household without bill access see that a piece arrived, not the photo or the amount.\"; this card uses the Foundations DestructiveConfirm V2 strings and in-dialog progress, so the earlier count-line progress, per-row \"Deleting\" tags and \"Wait until deleting finishes.\" are dropped; ScopeChip uses \"Your household\" because Maya has one home; unconfirmed pieces stay in Needs a call after Delete all; the Tue 20 Oct scene date; Alex Kim as a fixture delta; every invented string; assumptions; omitted states (Android 200%, the done state for 240 photos).\n\nBATCH PLAN:\nTurn 1: 1-6, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 2: 7-12, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 3: 13-18, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 4: 19-21.",
        "changeLog": [
          "Replaced every '[N]' with 90; Notes keeps one line saying 90 is a stand-in for undecided product calls (review major).",
          "DestructiveConfirm uses Foundations V2 exactly: custom iOS dialog (not system alert), V2 body, in-dialog deleting state 'Deleting 5 of 17…' in steps of 5, done line '17 photos deleted. The bills and their amounts stay.'; count-line progress, row 'Deleting' tags and the toggle reason were dropped and recorded on Notes (review major, 00d).",
          "Option B frame gets its own true zero line ('With this setting off, we delete each photo after we read it.') (review major).",
          "Restored 'on this deployment' in the reading-off notice; reading-off What we keep says 'digits you type' and the off line becomes 'We delete each photo once you've typed what it says.' (review minor x2).",
          "Who-row names Sam and Alex by default; category wording moved to Notes as an alternative; ScopeChip is 'Your household' for a single-home owner (review minor x2, contract ScopeChip).",
          "Zero states: How to delete reads 'Nothing to delete right now.' with no links; link renamed 'Go to Delete all mail snaps' (review minor).",
          "Frame 12 premise is now 'Sam has no bill access', and its who-row also names Alex (review minor).",
          "'Show all 17 photos' expands in place and moves focus; first 8 rows never hidden (review minor).",
          "Added edge case: unconfirmed pieces stay in Needs a call after Delete all, and Confirm what we read opens without a photo pane (review minor).",
