      {
        "ids": [
          "f9-verification-promise-copy",
          "f9-founding-meter-preview",
          "f8-positioning-copy"
        ],
        "prompts": [
          {
            "id": "f9-verification-promise-copy",
            "name": "Verification promise lists (one name per thing, no withdrawn fee promise)",
            "platforms": [
              "web",
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": false,
            "frameCount": 20,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Verification promise lists · f9-verification-promise-copy\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of four existing designed surfaces: the \"Verify this address\" sheet (web sheet; the iOS and Android sheet drawn by f3b-verify-address-sheet), \"Verified success\" (web page; the last step of the iOS and Android verify flow), the Place file \"Proof\" row, and the \"Meet the block\" mover row. This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed.\n\nATTACH: (1) The web Verify this address sheet at 1440 and 390, with the unlock list open. (2) The web Verified success page. (3) The iOS verify flow: the unlock-list step and the final step. (4) The Android verify sheet and final step, if already drawn by f3b; otherwise the Android inline verify banner. (5) The Place file Proof row on web 390 and iOS. (6) The \"Meet the block\" mover row on web, iOS and Android. (7) The Block Founders panel on Nearby, for the rank badge and date pill shapes.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: web 1440x900 and 390x844 · iOS 393x852 · Android 412x915. On Android, the unlock list inside the f3b Verify this address sheet uses exactly the same GrantLimitList strings as web and iOS. Android also changes the mover row, the Place file Proof row and the success step. f3b draws the sheet itself; this prompt fixes its strings.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE\n- The verify sheet opens from: Place tab → Place file → Proof row → \"Verify\"; the Place dashboard verify banner; the \"Verify address\" link on any LockedActionRow; the invitation-accepted screen; and the members roster capability caption. The caller supplies the reason line in the header. Keep that line exactly as the host draws it (for Sam's household case: \"To send neighbor messages, we need to confirm you live here.\").\n- Verified success is reached three ways. On web, a correct postcard code redirects to pantopus.com/app/place?verified=1. On iOS and Android, it is the flow's last step. When a document or landlord check finishes later, a notification lands here.\n- f1-claim-receipt adds a receipt list under the success headline after a claim. When both appear, the receipt comes after the method line and before the rank. On the success frames, mark that position with a thin labelled bracket in the margin, \"Claim receipt (drawn by f1-claim-receipt)\". Draw no receipt rows.\n- The mover row sits in the Place file's mover section while the move-in date is within 60 days. The old Just Moved card on Today was merged into these Place file rows, so draw the row in the Place file, not on Today.\n- Hand-off: success leads to Nearby → Block Founders panel, where the rank, the tier and the invite allowance also live. After that, the Proof row shows how and when the address was confirmed.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Maya Chen owns HOME A, 2418 NE Larkspur Loop. She moved in Mon 28 Sep 2026 (assumed). On Mon 19 Oct 2026 at 6:10 PM, her postcard has arrived. She opens Place file → Proof, reads what verifying adds, enters the code and lands on success. Two homes on her block verified before her. Her block's Founding window opened Mon 5 Oct, had 3 of 5 slots open and closes Sun 25 Oct, so she takes slot 3. Sam Ortega is a household member who joined by invite; his address is not verified. On Mon 12 Oct he opened the sheet from the household reason header and chose the postcard, so on Mon 19 Oct his check is pending.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Wherever verification is offered, say plainly what it adds and what it doesn't. Use one name per thing (Block Founder is the rank, Founding Neighbor is the first-5 badge), and never show the withdrawn fee promise.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: On the sheet, the eye lands first on the heading \"What needs address verification\", then on the two visible rows, then on the host's existing primary action (unchanged). The first method card, Postcard code, stays fully visible above the fold at 390x844. On success, the eye lands first on \"Address verified\" and its method-and-date line, then on the rank badge, then on the existing primary action.\n\nCONTENT (fixture deltas only)\n- Maya's rank after verifying: Block Founder #3. Her tier: Founding Neighbor, slot 3 of 5.\n- Invite allowance for a new verifier with 0 converted referrals: 3 postcard invites this week. Rule: the weekly cap is 3 plus 1 for each neighbor who joins through your invite, up to 6 in total.\n- Pending example (Sam): postcard mailed Mon 12 Oct, expected Thu 22 Oct (in 3 days from Mon 19 Oct).\n- Worst case: Block Founder #148, 6 invites (3 base + 3 earned), address wrapping to two lines at 390.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\n- Unlock list on the sheet (web, iOS, Android): GrantLimitList, V4 verify-unlock variant, drawn exactly as the Foundations board defines it. Heading \"What needs address verification\". It has the five lock rows from the shared string set, no sub lines, 44pt rows, a 16pt lock glyph in text.secondary and a verb phrase in body text.primary. Two rows are visible, then the 44pt disclosure row \"and 3 more\" with a chevron. The labels are now shorter, so each row is one or two lines at default text size, never three. Every host (f3b-verify-address-sheet, f3b-invitation-decision, attestation) shows this same list.\n- Collapsed sheet: directly under the list, draw one plain text.secondary line: \"Verifying confirms you live here. It doesn't change fees or anything that's free.\" Then the host's method cards.\n- Expanded sheet, and success: below the list (on success, below the allowance row), draw an overline \"WHAT STAYS THE SAME\" and three plain text rows with no glyphs.\n- Success, top to bottom: title, address, method line, [claim receipt position], rank row, tier row (conditional), allowance row, what stays the same, actions. The rank condition, the invite formula and the Founding tier appear here, where they are granted, and never on the sheet.\n- Rank row: the SlotMeter RankBadge (squared, radius md, surface.sunken, overline \"BLOCK FOUNDER\", numeral \"#3\"), with the label \"Your rank on this block\" beside it and, under the label, the caption \"Your number is set when your address is confirmed.\" in text.secondary.\n- Tier row: a neutral pill (surface.sunken, text.strong) with no warning tint, and its caption under it. Rank and tier are never the same shape, never side by side in one sentence, and each has its own row, at least 24pt apart.\n- Founding tier rule: the tier row appears on success only when this viewer's home holds the slot. It never appears as an offer. When the window is closed or the lookup failed, draw no Founding offer anywhere. A tier the home already holds still shows on success.\n- If the rank lookup fails on success, put an InlineErrorRow in the rank slot.\n- Before/after frame: the same row at its old three-line height beside its new two-line height, with the rhythm measurements labelled. The list gets shorter, so draw it shorter.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS: \"and 3 more\" expands in place with a 200ms height change; under Reduce Motion it appears instantly. The whole Proof row is the tap target and opens the sheet. The mover row keeps its existing tap. On iOS, success plays one light haptic tick; on Android, one light confirm haptic. There are no other haptics, no confetti and no badge animation. Success announces \"Address verified\" as a status message.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED\n- GrantLimitList: V4 verify-unlock, contract strings unchanged.\n- SlotMeter: RankBadge shape and its neutral pill only; no meter is drawn on this surface.\n- FactRow for the Proof row: missing (unverified), not-at-this-tier (saved place) and known. The pending Proof row uses the FactRow known layout with the LockedActionRow pending sentence as its value and no ProvenanceMark. The verified rows use FactRow known with a FILLED ProvenanceMark (confirmed) beside the method-and-date value, and no check badge.\n- LockedActionRow: pending variant, for Sam.\n- InlineErrorRow · WarmingSkeleton (row skeleton, rank and allowance rows only) · OfflineNotice (read-only cached screen variant, with per-control reason captions).\n\nACCESSIBILITY: Reading order on success: title, address, method line, claim receipt (when present), rank, rank caption, tier, allowance, what stays the same, actions. Spoken labels: the badge reads \"Block Founder number 3 on this block\"; the pill reads \"Founding Neighbor, slot 3 of 5\"; Retry reads \"Retry block details\". The lock glyph is decorative; the list heading carries the meaning. The disclosure is a button that announces its expanded state. Disabled method cards offline stay focusable and read their reason. Targets are 44pt / 48dp / 44px. In greyscale, rank and tier differ by shape alone. At iOS AX5 and Android 200%, rows wrap past two lines, the badge stacks above its caption, and the sheet scrolls.\n\nCOPY (sentence case, identical on web, iOS and Android)\nSheet list heading (from GrantLimitList V4): \"What needs address verification\"\nSheet list, visible: \"Message your neighbors\" · \"Get a residency letter\" · disclosure \"and 3 more\"\nExpanded: \"Show your Residency Pass\" · \"Share what you pay in rent (Real Rent)\" · \"Earn a Block Founder rank\"\nCollapsed sheet line: \"Verifying confirms you live here. It doesn't change fees or anything that's free.\"\nWhat stays the same (expanded sheet and success): overline \"WHAT STAYS THE SAME\" · \"Readings, reminders and dates work the same whether or not you verify.\" · \"Verifying doesn't change any fees.\" · \"It confirms you live here. It isn't a background check.\"\nSuccess: title \"Address verified\" · \"2418 NE Larkspur Loop, Vancouver, WA 98684\" · \"Address confirmed by postcard · Mon 19 Oct 2026\" · badge + \"Your rank on this block\" / \"Your number is set when your address is confirmed.\" · pill \"Founding Neighbor · slot 3 of 5\" / \"One of the first 5 verified homes on this block.\" · \"3 postcard invites this week\" / \"Each neighbor who joins through your invite adds 1 more a week, up to 6.\" · text link \"See your block on Nearby\"\nRank failed: \"We couldn't load your block details\" + \"Retry\"\nProof row: unverified \"Verify this address to become a Block Founder here.\" + \"Verify\" · pending \"We're checking your postcard code — expected in 3 days · Thu 22 Oct\" with caption \"Postcard mailed Mon 12 Oct\" · verified \"Address confirmed by postcard · Mon 19 Oct 2026\" · confirmed by the owner \"Confirmed by Maya Chen · Mon 19 Oct 2026\" · saved place \"Claim this address first\" (grey, no action)\nSam's LockedActionRow, pending: \"We're checking your postcard code — expected in 3 days · Thu 22 Oct\" (no link)\nMover row payoff, before: \"Verify this address to become a Block Founder here.\" After: \"You're Block Founder #3 on this block.\"\nOffline: notice \"You're offline. You can still read what verifying adds.\" · reason caption under each disabled method card \"Verifying needs a connection.\"\nRemoved from every surface: \"Permanent 0% marketplace fee\", \"permanent\"/\"permanently\", \"The Nearby cells map in detail\", \"Post to your block\", \"6 postcard invites a week instead of 3\".\n\nEDGE CASES\n- Wrap the long address; never truncate it. A 3-digit rank widens the badge, and the numeral is never cut.\n- Maximum allowance: \"6 postcard invites this week\" / \"3 base + 3 from neighbors who joined\".\n- Window closed or lookup failed: no tier row on success and no Founding offer anywhere. A household member whose home already holds the slot sees no Founding offer.\n- Slow network: the title and method line render from the verify response; the rank and allowance rows show row skeletons; the tier row has no skeleton and appears only once loaded.\n- Offline: OfflineNotice \"You're offline. You can still read what verifying adds.\" above the list; the list stays readable; the method cards (Postcard code and the others) are disabled, each with the caption \"Verifying needs a connection.\" No silent dead buttons.\n- Pending (Sam): the Proof row and his LockedActionRow show the pending line and carry no Verify link, so the sheet does not reopen from them until the check resolves. If another host still opens the sheet, it shows the LockedActionRow pending line in place of the method cards.\n- Mover row: shown only while the move-in date is within 60 days (HOME A: until Fri 27 Nov with the assumed Mon 28 Sep move-in); after that the row is gone.\n- Document method: \"Address confirmed by document · Mon 19 Oct 2026\". Already verified: the sheet never opens.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of \"your permanent rank\", draw \"Your rank on this block\" plus its condition line — because a verification can lapse, and nothing yet guarantees the rank survives that.\n- Instead of showing \"#3\" before verifying, draw \"Earn a Block Founder rank\" — because the number can change before the code is entered, and the Block Founders panel shows no rank to people who haven't verified.\n- Instead of a warning-tinted countdown pill, draw a neutral pill — because the badge is a perk, not an obligation.\n- Instead of one chip shape for both names, draw the squared RankBadge and the round tier pill — because the rename only works if readers can see the difference.\n- Instead of a bare \"Verified\" or a check badge, draw the method and date with a filled ProvenanceMark — because a bare badge gets read as an endorsement.\n- Instead of sub lines, invite rows or a Founding row in the sheet list, draw the V4 five rows under \"What needs address verification\" and put those facts on success — because every host must show one identical unlock list.\n- Instead of the full what-stays-the-same block on the collapsed sheet, draw one line — because the method cards must stay above the fold.\n- Instead of padding rows back to three lines, draw the shorter two-line rows and let the list end sooner — because a shorter list is the point of the rename.\n\nDONE WHEN: No frame contains \"permanent\", \"0%\", the cells-map row or \"instead of 3\". \"Block Founder\" and \"Founding Neighbor\" never share a sentence. In greyscale, rank and tier differ by shape. Every verification mention names its method and date. Web, iOS and Android show exactly the same strings, and the sheet list matches GrantLimitList V4 exactly, heading included. No row goes past two lines at default size. The invite numbers follow 3 + 1 per converted referral, up to 6. The rank row states its condition. No viewer is offered a Founding slot their home already holds. At 390x844 the Postcard code card is fully visible on the collapsed sheet. The offline frame has no control disabled without a reason.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f9-verification-promise-copy · web-1440 · 01-verify-sheet-expanded · light: Maya, Mon 19 Oct; heading \"What needs address verification\", all five rows, the what-stays-the-same list, the method cards below.\n2. f9-verification-promise-copy · web-1440 · 02-verified-success · light: Maya's full success page with the rank row and its condition caption, tier and allowance rows, and the claim receipt bracket.\n3. f9-verification-promise-copy · web-390 · 03-verify-sheet-collapsed · light: Sam, Mon 12 Oct, before he chooses a method; reason header \"To send neighbor messages, we need to confirm you live here.\" as the host draws it, the heading, two rows plus \"and 3 more\", the one-line note, and the Postcard code card fully visible above the fold at 390x844.\n4. f9-verification-promise-copy · web-390 · 04-rhythm-before-after · light: one row at the old three-line height beside the new two-line height, measured.\n5. f9-verification-promise-copy · ios · 05-verify-sheet-expanded · light: iOS unlock-list step, expanded, same heading.\n6. f9-verification-promise-copy · ios · 06-verified-success · light: iOS final step with badge, condition caption and pill.\n7. f9-verification-promise-copy · android · 07-verify-sheet-expanded · light: Android f3b sheet with the identical expanded list.\n8. f9-verification-promise-copy · android · 08-verified-success · light: Android final step with badge, condition caption and pill.\n9. f9-verification-promise-copy · web-390 · 09-founding-closed-success · light: success with no tier row; rank and allowance unchanged.\n10. f9-verification-promise-copy · web-390 · 10-place-file-proof-rows · light: five stacked Proof rows: unverified with Verify; pending (known layout, no mark) with caption; verified by postcard with filled mark; confirmed by Maya Chen with filled mark; saved place.\n11. f9-verification-promise-copy · ios · 11-mover-row · light: \"Meet the block\" row before and after verifying, in the Place file mover section (move-in Mon 28 Sep, within 60 days).\n12. f9-verification-promise-copy · android · 12-mover-row-200pct · light: the mover row before and after, at 200% text.\n13. f9-verification-promise-copy · web-390 · 13-rank-failed · light: success with InlineErrorRow in the rank slot.\n14. f9-verification-promise-copy · web-390 · 14-slow-network · light: success with title and method line, row skeletons for rank and allowance, no tier skeleton.\n15. f9-verification-promise-copy · web-390 · 15-offline · light: sheet with OfflineNotice \"You're offline. You can still read what verifying adds.\", list readable, method cards disabled with \"Verifying needs a connection.\"\n16. f9-verification-promise-copy · ios · 16-ax5 · light: success at AX5, stacked and scrolling.\n17. f9-verification-promise-copy · web-390 · 17-greyscale · light: success in greyscale.\n18. f9-verification-promise-copy · web-1440 · 18-verify-sheet-expanded · dark: dark twin of 1.\n19. f9-verification-promise-copy · ios · 19-verified-success · dark: dark twin of 6.\n20. f9-verification-promise-copy · Notes:\n- Assumptions: HOME A move-in Mon 28 Sep 2026; Founding window Mon 5 Oct to Sun 25 Oct (21 days).\n- Every invented string: the collapsed-sheet line; the what-stays-the-same overline and rows; the pending lines \"expected in 3 days · Thu 22 Oct\" and \"Postcard mailed Mon 12 Oct\"; the rank caption \"Your number is set when your address is confirmed.\"; the allowance caption \"Each neighbor who joins through your invite adds 1 more a week, up to 6.\"; the rank-failed line; the success link; \"Confirmed by Maya Chen\"; the offline notice and \"Verifying needs a connection.\"; Sam's Mon 12 Oct timeline; plus any string you added.\n- Replaced v1 strings with reasons: \"Confirmed by postcard code\" became \"Address confirmed by postcard\"; \"stays free\" became \"work the same\"; \"and 4/5 more\" became \"and 3 more\"; the heading \"What this unlocks\" became \"What needs address verification\" to match GrantLimitList V4. Proposed change (not applied): if the founder prefers \"What this unlocks\", change prompt 00c V4 first.\n- Deviation: the pending date puts the relative count first (\"in 3 days · Thu 22 Oct\") per the house style; prompt 00c's LockedActionRow pending string uses the range \"expected Thu 22–Thu 29 Oct\". Proposed: align 00c and f3b-locked-action-row with one form.\n- \"Proposed change to the shared GrantLimitList lock set: add 'Send postcard invites' (6 rows, 'and 4 more') on every host (invitation decision, verify sheet, attestation); not applied until prompt 00 is updated.\"\n- The rank condition \"Your number is set when your address is confirmed.\" appears on success and on the Block Founders panel. The window close date \"Closes Sun 25 Oct\" moved off the sheet; it lives on the Block Founders panel and f9-founding-meter-preview.\n- Fixture conflict: prompt 00b's SlotMeter uses \"Closes Tue 27 Oct\", which is inconsistent with a 21-day window from Mon 5 Oct. Proposed change: 00b uses Sun 25 Oct.\n- Conflict: the saved-place Proof row follows the contract (\"Claim this address first\"), while x-place-file says \"Not here — this is a saved place\".\n- Build note: the copy check must cover the web, iOS and Android apps, or the native apps will keep the old names.\n- Flags for the founder: any \"free\" wording needs a pricing decision; is the Founding Neighbor tier per home or per person; which notification category carries a finished document or landlord check (one settings page has Security, the other doesn't); add \"kept even if you move\" to the rank caption only if the data model guarantees it; confirm whether posting to your block needs verification; run a confusion test on Founding Neighbor vs \"First 5 on this block\".\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for continue. Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue. Turn 3: 13-18, then wait for continue. Turn 4: 19-20.",
            "changeLog": [
              "List heading changed to GrantLimitList V4's \"What needs address verification\" in FIRST FIVE SECONDS, LAYOUT and COPY; \"What this unlocks\" is kept on Notes as a proposed 00c change (major, review).",
              "Added the rank condition caption \"Your number is set when your address is confirmed.\" under \"Your rank on this block\" on success. Notes now say it appears on both success and the Block Founders panel, and keep the \"kept even if you move\" flag (major, review).",
              "Pending strings now put the relative count first, \"expected in 3 days · Thu 22 Oct\", per house style and 00c ordering. Notes record the mismatch with 00c's range string (minor, review).",
              "Offline now reads \"You're offline. You can still read what verifying adds.\", and the method cards are disabled with the reason \"Verifying needs a connection.\" Updated in EDGE CASES, COPY, frame 15 and Notes (minor, contract OfflineNotice).",
              "The mover row now shows only while the move-in date is within 60 days, with an assumed HOME A move-in of Mon 28 Sep 2026 (minor, x-place-file).",
              "Frame 3 is now dated Sam, Mon 12 Oct, before he chooses a method, with the host reason header quoted. Added a pending edge case: no Verify link, the sheet does not reopen, and any other host shows the pending line in place of the method cards (minor, review ×2).",
              "Allowance caption now reads \"Each neighbor who joins through your invite adds 1 more a week, up to 6.\", matching the doc's cap of 3 + min(referrals, 3). Listed as invented (minor, doc §F9).",
              "Specified the FactRow treatment: the pending row uses the known layout with no ProvenanceMark, and the verified rows use the known layout with a filled ProvenanceMark and no check badge (minor, contract).",
              "Kept Sun 25 Oct as the close date and added a Notes item proposing that 00b's Tue 27 Oct fixture change to match (minor, 00b).",
              "Stated the Founding window start (Mon 5 Oct) and the 24pt rank/tier separation from 00b; all other substance unchanged."
            ]
