                    "evidence": "prompts-v2/00b.md C5: \"When a state renders nothing (fail-closed), draw the host context around the gap. In the gutter, add a dashed 1px text.secondary annotation box reading \\\"Nothing renders here. No space is reserved and no message is shown.\\\"\" Prompt artboard 5: \"no density card; the neighbouring cards close the gap.\"",
                    "fix": "Artboards 4, 5 and 9: add \"with the Foundations C5 gutter annotation at the removed slot (frame 4: at the removed slot block; frame 5 and 9: between the neighbouring cards)\"."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The state numbers inside artboard names drift from their manifest positions, and web offline is not covered.",
                    "evidence": "Artboard 10 is named \"09b-edge-meters\", artboard 11 \"10-open\" and so on through artboard 18 \"17-wall-same-block\". EDGE CASES cover only \"Offline on native\".",
                    "fix": "Renumber the NN-state slugs to match manifest positions (10-edge-meters, 11-open, 12-open, 13-offline, 14-ax5, 15-200pct, 16-greyscale, 17-open dark, 18-wall-same-block dark). Add to EDGE CASES: \"Web offline: the /start form's OfflineNotice form-offline variant; no preview, no card.\""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "f8-positioning-copy",
                "pass": true,
                "issues": [
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The chat unfurl frame could lead Claude Design to draw a real messaging app's UI (iMessage, WhatsApp), which counts as imitating another product.",
                    "evidence": "Artboard 8: \"two stacked 360px chat unfurls with the same description\"; LAYOUT: \"the link's description text under the image and title\".",
                    "fix": "Artboard 8: add \"drawn as a generic, unbranded link-preview bubble (image, title, description, domain 'pantopus.com') with no messaging-app chrome, logos or colours\"."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The 320 check is named with the web-390 platform token, so its size can't be read from the name.",
                    "evidence": "Artboard 3: \"f8-positioning-copy · web-390 · 03-narrow-320 · light: a 320x568 frame\".",
                    "fix": "Keep the token, which is allowed, but add \"artboard size 320x568, not 390x844\" to the line, and add \"03-narrow-320 is sized 320x568\" to Notes so the reviewer knows the size is intentional."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The native offline state is described but has no frame, and the claim that the field is the first interactive element ignores any existing header link on web /start.",
                    "evidence": "EDGE CASES: \"On native offline, the hero is unchanged and the existing offline handling applies below the field.\" WHERE IT LIVES: \"Apart from the sender strip and the landing banner, the field is the first interactive element.\" flows-spec flow-01 step 1: \"The field is the first interactive element.\"",
                    "fix": "Either add an artboard \"f8-positioning-copy · android · 12b-offline · light: hero unchanged, OfflineNotice below the field\" (and rebalance BATCH PLAN), or state in Notes that offline is omitted because the hero is static. Add to WHERE IT LIVES: \"Any existing header 'Sign in' link stays but comes after the field in focus order.\""
                  }
                ]
