                    "issue": "P1's detail says recycling is not set, but the HOME A fixture says recycling is every other Tuesday with the next one on Tue 20 Oct. The attached PickupCard names the bins. Nothing tells Claude Design which to trust.",
                    "evidence": "P1 Detail: \"Tomorrow, Tue 20 Oct · recycling schedule not set\". House fixture: \"recycling every other Tuesday (next Tue 20 Oct)\". After self-fix: \"Tomorrow, Tue 20 Oct · Recycling and garbage\".",
                    "fix": "Add to Notes: \"Before confirmation the city seed carries only the weekday (frequency Not set), so P1 omits recycling. The fixture's every-other-Tuesday recycling is what Maya enters in the DateSheet.\""
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "Several payloads are underspecified. P2 and P5 name no ScopeChip or place, and P6 names no ScopeChip. P5's SourceCaption has no as-of, which invariant 5 requires. Wildfire (USFS), a dataset that opens this sheet from ScaleStrip rows, has no confidence sentence or Covers line, although the per-surface change asks for one confidence sentence per dataset. The Fixed resolved sheet does not state its mark.",
                    "evidence": "P5: \"SourceCaption: 'EPA · county-wide'\". House invariant 5: \"authority · scope · as-of\". Per-surface: \"one confidence sentence per dataset\". COPY lists P1-P7 only. Resolved Fixed: no mark stated.",
                    "fix": "Add \"ScopeChip 'Your household' (HOME A)\" to P2, P5 and P6. Change P5's caption to \"EPA · county-wide · zone map as published\" and list it in Notes. Add a copy line, \"Wildfire: 'Official. USFS models hazard potential for a quarter-mile area, not for one building.' Covers: 'The quarter-mile area around this address'\", and list it in Notes. Add to the Fixed resolved sheet: \"Mark: hollow (the city schedule is still not confirmed by the household).\""
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The flood 'map is wrong' path is carried only by jargon. 'Letter of Map Amendment' is above grade 6-8, and nothing says in plain words that this row is for people who think the map is wrong.",
                    "evidence": "LAYOUT Flood: \"The outbound row 'How to request a Letter of Map Amendment · FEMA ↗'.\" Per-surface: \"Hazard: wrong place matched / map is wrong, which links to 'Only FEMA can change this…'\"",
                    "fix": "Change the body line to \"Only FEMA can change this. If you think the map is wrong for your building, you can ask FEMA to review it.\" Keep the outbound row as \"Ask FEMA to review the map (Letter of Map Amendment) ↗\"."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "Schedule facts have no confirm action in the sheet. Someone who arrives from a calendar or place-file DateRow (not the PickupCard) and sees that Tuesday is right can confirm only by opening the DateSheet. Research asks for a one-tap household confirm that turns the ring into a tick.",
                    "evidence": "research-findings: \"A household member confirms or corrects the pickup day with one tap: the hollow mark becomes a tick.\" PickupCard contract: \"'Yes, Tuesday is right' / 'Change pickup day'\". The prompt's schedule foot offers only \"Set my pickup day\" and \"This isn't right\".",
                    "fix": "In the schedule default foot, draw two outlined peer buttons, 'Yes, Tuesday is right' and 'Set my pickup day', then the quiet 'This isn't right'. Confirm writes the rule in place (ring becomes tick, SourceCaption 'You set this · Mon 19 Oct') with one light haptic and no dismissal. Update FIRST FIVE SECONDS to match."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "Date copy departs from the house format: absolute dates come before the relative count, and 'Tomorrow' is given a date, although the brief says it stands alone.",
                    "evidence": "\"by Mon 26 Oct (in 7 days)\", \"New date: Mon 2 Nov (in 14 days)\", \"Tomorrow, Tue 20 Oct\". House MICROCOPY: \"beyond tomorrow, add the relative count: 'in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct'\". Brief: \"Tonight, Today and Tomorrow stand alone.\"",
                    "fix": "Use \"checking by in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\". Better, reword to \"We'll check it against … and tell you here — in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct.\" Use \"New date: in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov\" and change the detail lines to \"Tomorrow · Recycling and garbage\"."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "Two artboards each put two sheets side by side inside a single 'ios' 393pt artboard, which breaks the artboard-name viewport contract. The greyscale proof uses the schedule frame, which carries no colour, rather than the AQI frame, the only coloured scale (P13).",
                    "evidence": "Artboard 3: \"two sheets side by side\". Artboard 13: \"two sheets: Fixed (Friday) and No change\". Artboard 27: \"frame 1 in greyscale\".",
                    "fix": "Split artboard 3 into '09-reported-checking' and '11-check-slipped', and artboard 13 into '10-resolved-fixed' and '10b-resolved-no-change'. Rebalance the BATCH PLAN (still at most 6 per turn). Change artboard 27 to \"x-provenance-sheet · ios · 16-greyscale · light — frame 7 (air, AqiBand) in greyscale; the separators and printed category name carry meaning.\""
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "Accessibility gaps. The L mark is 'visual only', but nothing says to hide it from assistive tech, so its name is announced twice. The ScaleStrip inside the sheet is not marked as non-interactive, although its contract row is a 48pt target. Retry has no target label. The self-fix has no offline reason string. Signed-out 'Sign in' does not say it returns to the sheet with the reason kept (P2).",
                    "evidence": "LAYOUT item 2: \"It is visual only and is not a target.\" ACCESSIBILITY: \"The value with its mark name…\". Contract InlineErrorRow: \"Retry names its target\". EDGE CASES: \"The report control, the source row and the self-fix are disabled, each with its reason.\" COPY Offline lists only two reasons.",
                    "fix": "Add: \"ProvenanceMark L is hidden from assistive tech; its name is read in the value label.\" Add: \"Inside this sheet the ScaleStrip and AqiBand are read-only: one accessibility element each, not tappable.\" Add: \"Retry is labelled 'Retry sending report'.\" Add the offline reason \"You can change your pickup day when you're back online.\" Add: \"After sign-in, the person returns to this sheet with 'We matched the wrong spot' still chosen.\""
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The stale mark is drawn at 50% opacity. Following the contract literally drops the text.secondary ink below the house invariant of 3:1 for marks.",
                    "evidence": "LAYOUT Degraded: \"Stale: the same mark at 50% opacity\". House INVARIANT 1: \"Marks are at least 12pt with a stroke of at least 1.5px and at least 3:1 contrast.\"",
                    "fix": "Change to: \"Stale: the same mark, dimmed only as far as 3:1 still holds (text.secondary ink stays ≥3:1). The age is carried by the FreshnessLine words 'Observed 7:00 AM · AirNow — 11 hours ago'.\" Record this in Notes as a contract clarification."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "clean": false
      },
      {
        "ids": [
          "x-date-sheet"
        ],
        "prompts": [
          {
            "id": "x-date-sheet",
            "name": "The Date sheet (one sheet, three modes, ten kinds)",
            "platforms": [
              "web",
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": true,
            "frameCount": 34,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: The Date sheet · x-date-sheet\n\nTYPE: NEW. This one sheet replaces seven: add a date, pickup quick-set, the pickup editor, the voter step sheet, the date detail sheet, the remove-date confirm, and the reminder picker. Draw ONE component, DateSheet. The mode (create / view-mine / view-seeded) and the kind change the body. Scope decides only whether the visibility choice appears.\n- At a saved place there is no choice, and the footer always reads 'Only you will see this.'\n- At a home, for kinds other than Bill and the seeded kinds, the footer sentence and the saved message follow the selected chip. With Only you selected, they read 'Only you will see this.' and 'Saved to your calendar. Only you.' With Household selected, they read 'Everyone in this household will see this.' and 'Saved to your household calendar.' A new date at a home starts on Only you.\n- Bill at a home shows no visibility chips. Its footer names the people who can see it: 'You and Sam can see this bill.' Never write 'Everyone in this household' on a bill.\n- Seeded kinds (voter registration, property-tax appeal, property-tax due) never show visibility chips. The mailing date, plan and reminders a person enters are Only you, so their footer reads 'Only you will see this.'\n\nATTACH: screenshots of the place file (Dates section), Today with the 14-day strip and the pickup card, the provenance sheet ('Where this fact comes from'), and the Foundations board from prompt 00. In every frame, draw the host dimmed behind the sheet exactly as it appears in its screenshot.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS\n- iOS 393x852: a .sheet at the large detent.\n  - Header control: in create mode, and in view-mine once something has been edited, the header shows a leading 'Cancel' and Save sits in the sticky footer. In view-seeded, and in view-mine with no edits, the header shows 'Done'.\n  - When a Back control is present, Back is leading and Cancel/Done moves to the trailing edge. Arriving from the provenance sheet, the sheet grows from the medium to the large detent with a cross-fade.\n  - The date field is the compact date pill. Tapping it opens the system calendar with its month/year jump. That is a system control, not a second sheet.\n- Android 412x915: a Material 3 ModalBottomSheet with a close (X) icon button labelled 'Close' at the top start.\n  - For Lease ends, Notice deadline, Insurance renews and Warranty ends, embed the M3 DatePicker inside the sheet in Input display mode. It is an outlined text field 'MM/DD/YYYY' with a trailing calendar-toggle icon button (48dp, labelled 'Switch to calendar').\n  - All other kinds, including Next recycling, use the inline calendar mode with the same input toggle. The calendar always expands inline inside the sheet and is never a dialog.\n- Web 1440x900: a right-side SlidePanel, 480 wide, over the place file. Web 390x844: a bottom sheet. Both use a typeable date input and put the same Cancel/Done text button at the top right.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE\nThe sheet opens over Place (the place file) or Today. It never has a route of its own. Entry points:\n- Place file: a missing-fact row such as 'When does your lease end?' opens create mode with that kind already picked. A known-fact row opens view-mine.\n- Place file: the mover row for voter registration leads to the civic registration block. The F8 seasonal headline goes there too: /app/place/civic?focus=registration or pantopus://place/{homeId}/civic.\n- Civic registration block: 'Remind me', or the deadline row, opens view-seeded voter registration. 'Check or update at VoteWA ↗' stays outbound, both in the block and in this sheet.\n- Today: the '+ Add a date' row at the foot of the 14-day strip opens create mode with no kind picked. A strip list row opens view-mine or view-seeded. Strip cells are not targets.\n- Today pickup card: 'Change pickup day' and the no-rule line 'Set your pickup day' open the Pickup day kind with the city weekday already selected, so one tap on Save confirms it. FirstWeekRow 'Next: set your pickup day →' does the same.\n- Settings > Notifications: the pickup status row opens the Pickup day kind the same way.\n- Provenance sheet: 'Not my schedule', then 'Set my pickup day', replaces the provenance sheet's content with this sheet and adds a header Back control, '‹ Where this fact comes from'. The two sheets never stack.\n- Household calendar: its rows are read-only there, so editing opens this sheet.\n- Mail: with no claimed home, 'Mail snap needs a claimed address' opens the Bill kind as plain manual entry.\n- Reminder push: the app lands on the date's row (the strip list row if the date is within 14 days, otherwise the place file Dates row). The row is highlighted and takes focus, then view-mine opens. A bill reminder lands on the bill's row. Web: /app/place/today?rule=cal_7f3a2 (home) or /app/today?rule=cal_7f3a2 (saved place). Native: pantopus://place/today?rule=cal_7f3a2.\n- Create links: web /app/place/today?add=date&kind=lease_end at a home and /app/today?add=date at a saved place. Native pantopus://place/today?add=date and pantopus://place/today?add=date&kind=lease_end.\nHanded over from the caller: the scope (home or saved place), any preselected kind, and the rule id.\nHanded on after saving:\n- The sheet returns the person to where they came from. The calling row updates in place with the ProvenanceMark you-added.\n- The pickup card shows 'You · Thursday' with no caveat. The FirstWeekRow advances, and the widget snapshot is rewritten.\n- 'I did this' on voter registration also ticks the place file mover row 'Update your voter registration' as you-added. That tick stays Only you. Undo un-ticks it.\n- On native only: if notification permission was never asked and this is the first pickup day saved, the sheet closes and then the notification primer opens. The two are never stacked, and the primer never opens after a failed save. If permission was already granted or denied, nothing opens.\n\nWHO AND WHEN\n- Mon 19 Oct 2026, 6:10 PM. Maya Chen at HOME A has her lease PDF open: it ends Wed 31 Mar 2027 and requires 30 days' notice. She taps 'When does your lease end?' in the place file.\n- Jordan Lee at PLACE B moved in ten days ago. The provenance sheet says Thursday per the City of Camas, but he wants to set it himself and say how often recycling comes. He taps 'Not my schedule', then 'Set my pickup day', and picks Weekly. He tapped 'Not now' on the first notification ask.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Tell the app a date once, see exactly when you'll be reminded, and see who else can see it.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS\n1. The date, spelled out: 'Wed 31 Mar 2027'.\n2. The action date it creates: 'Notice deadline · in 133 days · Mon 1 Mar 2027'.\n3. The reminder timeline, with real dates.\nThe single primary action is Save. The footer scope sentence sits directly above it.\n\nCONTENT (house style fixtures; deltas only)\n- Sheet title: 'Add a date' in create mode; otherwise the kind name.\n- Kind tiles (KindGlyph tile variant): Pickup day · Move-in date · Lease ends · Notice deadline · Insurance renews · Warranty ends · HOA dues · Property-tax appeal · Voter registration · Bill. Bill is phase 2: draw it, and label it phase 2 on Notes.\n- Default leads: 14 days for Lease ends; 30 for Warranty, Insurance and HOA; 7 for Bill. If the default has already passed, the segment shows the passed reason and the suggestion.\n- Lease ends (HOME A):\n  - Date Wed 31 Mar 2027.\n  - 'How much notice does your lease require?' with ChoiceChips 20 days (WA minimum) · 30 · 60 · Other, captioned 'Check your lease.' Maya picks 30.\n  - This creates the linked DateRow 'Notice deadline · in 133 days · Mon 1 Mar 2027', titled 'Tell your landlord in writing by Mon 1 Mar'. Reminders attach to that row.\n  - Other notice lengths: 20 days gives Thu 11 Mar 2027. 60 days gives Sat 30 Jan 2027, a Saturday, so the sheet suggests 'That's a Saturday. Plan to send it by Fri 29 Jan.'\n- Lease reminders: segments 60 / 30 / 14 / 7 / 1 days before the notice deadline, 14 selected. Ticks: Mon 15 Feb 2027 · Sun 28 Feb 2027 · Mon 1 Mar 2027.\n- Warranty ends: 'Water heater warranty — Rheem 40-gal', Sat 12 Dec 2026, reminder 30 days. Ticks: Thu 12 Nov · Fri 11 Dec · Sat 12 Dec.\n- HOA dues: $285, Sun 1 Nov 2026, in 13 days.\n- Insurance renews with 'Not sure of the day': 'Renters insurance — PEMCO · about Jan 2027', reminder Fri 1 Jan 2027.\n- Move-in date (PLACE B): Fri 9 Oct 2026. It is in the past, and that is valid.\n- Pickup day (PLACE B):\n  - Thursday arrives preselected with a hollow mark and the SourceCaption '○ City of Camas · city schedule · 2026 calendar'. The legend word 'On record, not confirmed' is printed once beside it.\n  - Recycling frequency: Not set / Weekly / Every other week. Jordan picks Weekly. 'Next recycling' appears only for Every other week.\n  - Read-only preview: 'Thu 22 Oct · Thu 29 Oct · Thu 5 Nov'. Under it: 'Next holiday move: Thanksgiving — Thu 26 Nov moves to Fri 27 Nov · City of Camas 2026 calendar', with a struck ghost 'Thu 26 Nov'.\n  - Preview dates after the last published City of Camas calendar (Dec 2026) carry the caption 'projected', never a confirmed look.\n- Pickup day (HOME A), already set: 'Set by Sam Ortega · Tuesday · confirmed Sat 3 Oct 2026'. The household rule wins and the row says who set it. Every other week, 'Next recycling' Tue 20 Oct, preview Tue 20 Oct · Tue 3 Nov · Tue 17 Nov, no holiday moves.\n- Voter registration (seeded, statewide, person-scoped):\n  - Checked caption: '● Washington Secretary of State · statewide · checked Oct 2026'. Unconfirmed caption: '○ Washington Secretary of State · statewide · added Sep 2026'.\n  - Headline 'General election · Tue 3 Nov 2026'.\n  - Method DateRows, titles exactly: 'Online or by mail — must arrive by Mon 26 Oct 2026' (line 2: 'in 7 days') and 'In person, Clark County Elections — until 8:00 PM Tue 3 Nov 2026' (line 2: 'in 15 days').\n  - Line: 'Registration is per address. We can't see whether you're registered.'\n  - Plan: 'How will you register?' Online / Mail / In person.\n  - Then the outlined 'I did this' button, TextActionRow 'Check or update at VoteWA ↗', and the footer 'Only you will see this.'\n- Property-tax appeal (seeded, county, phase 2 data; SourceCaption 'Clark County Board of Equalization · county · checked Oct 2026'):\n  - 'Your county lets you challenge the assessed value your tax is based on.'\n  - DateRow conditional rule: 'Closes July 1, or 60 days after your value notice was mailed.' Then 'Late appeals can't be accepted.'\n  - Input 'When was your notice mailed?' with the option 'I haven't gotten one yet'.\n  - After Mon 14 Sep 2026 is entered: 'Closes in 25 days · Fri 13 Nov 2026', with the you-added mark.\n- Property-tax due row opened from the strip: 'Property tax, 2nd half — due Mon 2 Nov', with 'moved from Sat 31 Oct' in the detail.\n- Bill (HOME A): Clark Public Utilities $142.18, due Fri 23 Oct (in 4 days, so the 7-day default has passed).\n- Worst case: a 68-character title, 'Water heater warranty — Rheem 40-gal, installed by Columbia Plumbing', wrapping to two lines.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\nTop to bottom:\n- Header: title and Cancel/Done (Close on Android), with Back leading when present.\n- Kind grid: 2 columns × 5 rows, with no step before it.\n  - Each tile is a whole-tile target at least 56pt tall (48dp minimum on Android), with 8pt gaps, holding the KindGlyph tile variant (42pt) and its label, which wraps to two lines.\n  - Selected tile: the KindGlyph contract's filled radio dot plus a bold label, with a focus ring that looks different from it.\n  - Before a kind is picked, only the grid and a disabled Save show.\n  - After a pick, the grid collapses in place to one row, '[glyph] Lease ends · Change kind'. That row re-expands the grid.\n- HOA dues and Bill: an Amount field above the date.\n- Date field, with the spelled-out weekday date under it, then the 'Not sure of the day' toggle, which swaps the field for month and year.\n- The kind-specific block.\n- Optional title.\n- The 'Remind me' switch row: iOS Toggle, M3 Switch or web switch, 44pt/48dp.\n- ReminderLeadControl, shown only while the switch is on. Under it, a mini timeline: three ticks back from the action date, each labelled with a real date, and a leader line to the event. Caption: 'We'll also remind you the day before and on the day.' Second line: 'Reminders arrive at 7:00 AM.' With the switch off, it collapses to 'No reminders. This date still shows on Today and in your place file.'\n- With 'Not sure of the day' on, the segments hide and one tick shows at the start of the month, captioned 'We'll remind you at the start of Jan 2027.'\n- At a home only, for non-bill, non-seeded kinds: ChoiceChips 'Visible to: Only you · Household'.\n- ScopeChip in sentence form, then the footer. The body keeps scroll padding for it.\nFOOTER BY MODE (sticky):\n- Create: ScopeChip sentence plus filled Save, disabled until a kind and a valid date are set.\n- View-mine with no edits: ScopeChip sentence only. 'Mark done' is an outlined button in the body; 'Remove this date' is a text button.\n- View-mine after an edit: filled Save appears, and the header switches to Cancel.\n- View-seeded: ScopeChip sentence only until Remind me, the plan or the mailing date changes; then filled Save appears. 'I did this' is an outlined body button, never filled.\nPer kind:\n(a) Lease ends, Notice deadline, Insurance renews, Warranty ends, HOA dues and Bill: date field, 'Not sure of the day', title, switch and ReminderLeadControl.\n  - Switch default: on for Lease ends, Notice deadline, HOA dues and Bill; off for Insurance and Warranty.\n  - Bill at HOME A is pre-filled from a mail snap. Fields read from the photo carry the read-from-your-photo mark and the flag 'We weren't sure — check this', and each becomes you-added on Save. No Visible to chips; footer 'You and Sam can see this bill.' A member without finance permission sees Save disabled and a LockedActionRow 'Maya or Sam can add bills here'. No bill string says Paid until Mark paid is tapped.\n  - Bill at a saved place is plain manual entry with no photo wording, saved as a you-added date, not a household bill.\n(b) Move-in date: the date field only. No 'Not sure of the day', no switch, no reminder block.\n(c) Pickup day has no single date field. It has:\n  - A weekday chooser of seven ChoiceChips, Mon to Sun, spoken as full day names; radio rows at AX5.\n  - Then frequency, then 'Next recycling' (inline calendar, Every other week only), then the preview.\n  - In place of the lead control, one line, chosen by state: 'We'll remind you the night before, with your evening briefing (6:00 PM).' (notifications and evening briefing on); 'Notifications are off. Pickup still shows on Today the night before.' (notifications or evening briefing off); 'After you save, we'll ask to remind you the night before (6:00 PM).' (native, permission never asked).\n(d) Voter registration: method rows, then the plan, then the switch and ReminderLeadControl, which appear only after a plan is picked.\n  - Online: 1 day selected; 60/30/7 disabled with 'Too close to set'. Ticks Sun 25 Oct · Mon 26 Oct, captioned 'We'll remind you the day before and on the day.'\n  - Mail: 'Mail takes a few days. Send it by Wed 21 Oct.' 1 day selected; 60/30/7 disabled with 'Too close to set'. Ticks Tue 20 Oct · Wed 21 Oct, captioned 'We'll remind you the day before and on the day.'\n  - In person: 7 days selected. Ticks Tue 27 Oct · Mon 2 Nov · Tue 3 Nov.\n(e) Property-tax appeal: the rule plus the mailing-date input.\n  - Before a mailing date is entered, the h2 date slot shows the rule, not a date: 'July 1, or later' with the caption 'may be later'.\n  - 'I haven't gotten one yet' keeps the rule and shows 'Closes Thu 1 Jul 2027 or later · we'll ask again when your notice comes'. It sets no computed date and fires no reminder.\n  - The switch and ReminderLeadControl appear only once a date is computed.\nView modes:\n- The date shows large (h2) with its SourceCaption and mark. One legend word is printed at first use.\n- View-seeded: fields are locked and drawn as plain text with no outlines. Remind me and 'This isn't right' stay live.\n- A seeded row uses the filled mark only when its source has been checked. Otherwise it uses the hollow mark, its 'added' caption, and a line such as 'Not yet checked against the Washington Secretary of State site'.\nCollision: the existing row is drawn inline with its mark. 'Replace it' is previewed: the old row struck through above the new values, which are labelled 'New'.\nTimeline rules: a reminder date that has already passed is disabled, with the reason. Two ticks on the same day draw as one tick.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- Tapping a tile collapses the grid in 200ms. Under Reduce Motion it cross-fades.\n- Date entry: web accepts 03/31/2027, 31 Mar 2027 and March 31 2027, and paste works. Android input mode takes MM/DD/YYYY. iOS uses the compact date pill; tapping it opens the system calendar with the month/year jump, which is a system control and not a second sheet.\n- Save shows a spinner inside the button, then the status message, then the sheet closes. A successful save gives one light haptic tick; nothing else does.\n- Unsaved edits block swipe-to-dismiss. Cancel, Android Back or web Escape opens a native action sheet (an M3 dialog on Android, a small panel dialog on web) with 'Discard this date' / 'Keep editing'.\n- 'Remove this date' closes the sheet and the calling row collapses to an InlineUndo that stays until the person leaves the screen. Every removal cancels that date's reminders. For an Only-you date it reads 'Removed \"Water heater warranty — Rheem 40-gal\" · Undo'. For a Household-visible date it reads 'Removed for everyone in this household: \"Renters insurance — PEMCO\" · Undo', and the household is not told until Undo is gone. At HOME A the pickup kind reads 'Clear household pickup day' and behaves the same way.\n- 'Mark done' ('I gave notice' on a notice deadline, 'I did this' on voter, 'Mark paid' on a Bill at a home) cancels the remaining reminders.\n  - The status line shows with an InlineUndo 'Undo' until the person leaves.\n  - Reopened later, view-mine reads 'You marked this done Mon 19 Oct · Undo', and Undo restores the remaining reminders.\n  - Offline, the voter tick is queued on the device and uses the same copy.\n- 'This isn't right' opens the ProvenanceSheet in place, with Back. It ends at the dated receipt 'Reported Mon 19 Oct. We'll check it against the Washington Secretary of State by Mon 26 Oct and tell you here.', and the row then shows 'You reported this · checking'.\n- 'Check or update at VoteWA ↗' opens an in-app browser on native and a new tab on web.\n- Reminder push tray action 'Done' marks the date done without opening the app and cancels the remaining reminders. In the foreground there is no banner; the matching row is highlighted instead.\n- Nothing works by swipe alone.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED\nDateSheet (create, view-mine, view-seeded, bill mode, conditional seeded) · KindGlyph (tile and row) · ReminderLeadControl (date sheet and lease variants; the lease variant here adds the 14 segment; the extraction confirm default is 7) · DateRow (deadline, conditional rule and holiday moved variants) · ProvenanceMark (S and M; official, unconfirmed, you-added, read-from-your-photo) · SourceCaption · ScopeChip (footer sentence form) · ChoiceChip (visibility, notice length, voter plan, frequency, weekday) · InlineUndo · InlineErrorRow (save failed, load failed) · OfflineNotice (form offline) · LockedActionRow (names-who-can-act variant, with no 'Verify address' link) · TextActionRow (outbound) · WarmingSkeleton (row skeleton) · ProvenanceSheet · PushCopy (date reminder).\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Reading order: title, kind, date, action date, reminders, visibility, footer, Save.\n- The sheet has a unique title and traps focus.\n- After a tile pick, focus stays on the collapsed row '[glyph] Lease ends · Change kind', in the same position, and 'Lease ends selected' is announced.\n- The timeline is spoken as one sentence: 'Reminders on Mon 15 Feb, Sun 28 Feb and Mon 1 Mar.'\n- Marks are spoken as 'official', 'on record, not confirmed' or 'you added this'.\n- Selection looks different from focus in every control. ChoiceChips use a check plus primary.50 fill.\n- Errors sit next to their field and are announced politely. Saved, Removed, Reported and Marked done are status messages.\n- Targets are 44pt on iOS and web and 48dp on Android.\n- At AX5, the kinds become a one-column list, the reminder control and the weekday chips become radio rows, pairs stack, and the sheet scrolls.\n\nCOPY\n- Buttons: 'Save' · 'Change kind' · 'Remove this date' · 'Clear household pickup day' · 'Mark done' · 'I gave notice' · 'I did this' · 'Mark paid' · 'Replace it' · 'Open it' · 'Add as a separate calendar event' · 'Cancel' · 'Try again' · 'Done' · 'Undo' · 'This isn't right' · 'Discard this date' · 'Keep editing' · 'Keep it on file' · 'Change the date' · 'Use Wed 31 Mar 2027' · 'Remind 7 days before' · 'Remind 1 day before'.\n- Switch: 'Remind me'. Visibility: 'Visible to: Only you · Household'.\n- Saved: 'Saved to your calendar. Only you.' / 'Saved to your household calendar.' / bill: 'Saved. You and Sam can see this bill.'\n- Done: 'You marked this done · Only you' (voter and Only-you dates) or 'You marked this done · Your household' (Household dates), then 'We won't remind you again about this.'\n- Removed: 'Removed \"Water heater warranty — Rheem 40-gal\" · Undo' / 'Removed for everyone in this household: \"Renters insurance — PEMCO\" · Undo'.\n- Report receipt: 'Reported Mon 19 Oct. We'll check it against the Washington Secretary of State by Mon 26 Oct and tell you here.' Row: 'You reported this · checking'.\n- Past date: 'That date has passed. Did you mean Wed 31 Mar 2027?'\n- Lead passed (HOA): 'That's already passed — remind 7 days before (Sun 25 Oct)?' Bill: 'That's already passed — remind 1 day before (Thu 22 Oct)?'\n- Warranty in the past: 'This warranty already ended. Keep it on file?' with 'Keep it on file' / 'Change the date' at equal weight.\n- Save failed: 'Couldn't save that date. Try again.' Typed values are kept.\n- Remove failed: 'Couldn't remove that date. Try again.'\n- Load failed: 'Couldn't load that date.' with 'Try again'.\n- Offline, viewing: 'You're offline. You can read this date; saving needs a connection.' Offline, creating: 'You're offline. Saving a new date needs a connection.' Remind me and 'This isn't right' are disabled.\n- Guest: 'Maya or Sam can change dates at this home.' Bill without finance permission: 'Maya or Sam can add bills here'.\n- Unreadable bill: 'We couldn't read this one automatically. Add the amount and due date yourself.'\n- Unconfirmed seed: 'Not yet checked against the Washington Secretary of State site'.\n- Reminder push (PushCopy date reminder, on Notes): 'Lease notice due in 14 days' / 'Tell your landlord by Mon 1 Mar', action 'Done'.\n\nEDGE CASES\n- Collision at a home: 'Warranty ends is already on file: Water heater warranty — Rheem 40-gal · Sat 12 Dec 2026.' Choices: Replace it (previewed) / Add as a separate calendar event / Cancel.\n- Collision at a saved place: before typing, the tile's subline reads 'One per kind for now · already set for Sat 12 Dec'. After the tap: 'You can keep one Warranty ends date per place for now. Water heater warranty — Rheem 40-gal · Sat 12 Dec 2026 is already on file.' Choices: 'Open it' / 'Replace it' (previewed) / 'Cancel'.\n- A reminder opened for a removed date lands on Today with 'That date was removed.' No error modal, no blank page.\n- Notifications off: the timeline caption reads 'Notifications are off. These show on Today and in your place file.' Pickup uses its own notifications-off line.\n- Slow open from a push: a row skeleton appears inside the sheet only if the open takes 1s or longer; static under Reduce Motion.\n- Bills never show $0.00 or today's date in place of a blank.\n- Voter deadline passed for online: 'You can still register in person until 8:00 PM Tue 3 Nov.' Both passed: 'The deadline for Tue 3 Nov has passed.'\n- No seeded voter rule for the state: 'We don't have this state's deadline yet.' The outbound link appears only if we hold the office URL, never with a guessed date.\n- Many items and the longest title: the 68-character title wraps. The largest amount is $285.\n- Tiers: a saved place shows no visibility chips and no household words. A guest sees every field and Remind me disabled, plus the LockedActionRow. A pickup already set by Sam shows who set it. A member without finance permission cannot save a bill.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a multi-step wizard, draw the kind as one tap that collapses in place — because the kind is a choice, not a stage.\n- Instead of a calendar you page through for 31 Mar 2027, draw a typeable field (web, Android) or the compact pill with the month/year jump (iOS) — because document dates are far away and copied, and sheets never stack.\n- Instead of one lead with one leader line, draw all three ticks with real dates — because three reminders fire.\n- Instead of anchoring the lease reminder to the lease end, anchor it to the Notice deadline — because that is the day she must act.\n- Instead of a date field and lead control on Pickup day, draw a weekday chooser and the night-before line — because pickup repeats and rides the evening briefing.\n- Instead of working out recycling from the garbage day, draw an explicit frequency, a Next recycling field and a preview — because Not set is a real value.\n- Instead of a single seeded tax date, draw the rule with 'may be later' until a mailing date exists — because the deadline is conditional.\n- Instead of a filled mark and a 'checked' caption on every seeded row, draw hollow with 'added Sep 2026' until checked — because unverified must look unverified.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- A saved-place user can set a pickup day and a lease date.\n- Every reminder that will fire is visible with its date, the lease reminder lands before Mon 1 Mar, and a date can be saved with no reminder.\n- 31 Mar 2027 is reachable in 2–3 taps on each platform.\n- Recycling is never inferred, and pickup never promises a push that cannot fire.\n- Scope and visibility are stated at the moment of input, the footer always matches the selected chip, and a bill names who can see it.\n- A guest cannot write.\n- Seeded and you-added dates can be told apart in greyscale.\n- Marking done stops the reminders, says so, and can be undone.\n- A report ends on a dated receipt.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. x-date-sheet · ios · 01-create-lease-dense · light — HOME A, Lease ends, 30-day notice, linked Notice deadline row, lease segments with 14 selected, three ticks, Only you selected, footer 'Only you will see this.' Inset: the iOS month/year wheel set to March 2027, with taps numbered 1 (pill), 2 (month/year), 3 (day 31).\n2. x-date-sheet · ios · 02-create-empty · light — full kind grid, nothing chosen, disabled Save, over the Today strip.\n3. x-date-sheet · ios · 03-pickup-weekly · light — PLACE B, arrived from the provenance sheet with Back '‹ Where this fact comes from' leading and Cancel trailing; Thursday hollow; Weekly; preview Thu 22 Oct · Thu 29 Oct · Thu 5 Nov; holiday line with struck ghost Thu 26 Nov; line 'After you save, we'll ask to remind you the night before (6:00 PM).'\n4. x-date-sheet · ios · 04-view-mine-warranty · light — Remind me on, 30 selected, 60 disabled, ticks, outlined Mark done, Remove this date, footer sentence only.\n5. x-date-sheet · ios · 05-view-seeded-voter · light — '● … checked Oct 2026', method rows with 'in 7 days' / 'in 15 days' line 2, plan Online, two ticks, outlined I did this, VoteWA link, filled Save (plan changed), 'Only you will see this.'\n6. x-date-sheet · ios · 06-view-seeded-voter-unconfirmed · light — hollow mark, '○ … added Sep 2026', 'Not yet checked against the Washington Secretary of State site', no plan yet, footer sentence only.\n7. x-date-sheet · ios · 07-view-seeded-tax-appeal · light — HOME A (Maya rents), footer 'Only you will see this.'; left: rule, 'July 1, or later' with 'may be later', question empty; right: after 'I haven't gotten one yet'.\n8. x-date-sheet · ios · 08-tax-appeal-computed · light — HOME A, filled Board of Equalization caption, you-added 'Closes in 25 days · Fri 13 Nov 2026', reminders, Save, 'Only you will see this.'\n9. x-date-sheet · ios · 09-collision-warranty-home · light — HOME A, existing row inline, Replace it previewed, three choices.\n10. x-date-sheet · ios · 10-collision-warranty-saved-place · light — PLACE B, tile subline, full message, Open it / Replace it / Cancel.\n11. x-date-sheet · ios · 11-lead-passed-hoa · light — HOA $285 Sun 1 Nov, default 30 selected but disabled with its reason, suggestion 'That's already passed — remind 7 days before (Sun 25 Oct)?' and button 'Remind 7 days before'.\n12. x-date-sheet · ios · 12-past-date-lease · light — 31 Mar 2026 typed, with 'Use Wed 31 Mar 2027'.\n13. x-date-sheet · ios · 13-lease-notice-weekend · light — 60 days gives Sat 30 Jan; suggests Fri 29 Jan.\n14. x-date-sheet · ios · 14-not-sure-of-day · light — PLACE B, 'about Jan 2027', switch on, segments hidden, one tick Fri 1 Jan with 'We'll remind you at the start of Jan 2027.', no chips, footer 'Only you will see this.'\n15. x-date-sheet · ios · 15-view-mine-insurance-visibility · light — HOME A, Renters insurance switched Only you → Household, household footer, Remind me off with its caption, Cancel in header.\n16. x-date-sheet · ios · 16-saved · light — inset: Save with its spinner (saving); then 'Saved to your calendar. Only you.'; then the place file row with the you-added mark.\n17. x-date-sheet · ios · 17-notice-marked-done · light — HOME A Household notice: 'I gave notice' done, 'You marked this done · Your household', reminders cancelled, InlineUndo; inset shows the later 'You marked this done Mon 19 Oct · Undo'.\n18. x-date-sheet · ios · 18-removed-undo · light — place file warranty row collapsed to InlineUndo; inset: 'Removed for everyone in this household: \"Renters insurance — PEMCO\" · Undo'.\n19. x-date-sheet · ios · 19-discard-unsaved · light — typed lease date, action sheet with Discard this date / Keep editing.\n20. x-date-sheet · ios · 20-loading-from-reminder · light — left: highlighted row and the sheet's row skeleton; right: 'Couldn't load that date. · Try again'.\n21. x-date-sheet · ios · 21-save-failed · light — typed values kept, InlineErrorRow.\n22. x-date-sheet · ios · 22-offline · light — view-mine read-only date; Save, Remind me and 'This isn't right' disabled, each with its reason; inset: create mode with 'You're offline. Saving a new date needs a connection.'\n23. x-date-sheet · ios · 23-permission-denied-guest · light — viewer Alex Rivera, guest at HOME A; fields and Remind me disabled; LockedActionRow 'Maya or Sam can change dates at this home.'\n24. x-date-sheet · ios · 24-bill-prefilled · light — HOME A, Clark Public Utilities $142.18 due Fri 23 Oct, read-from-your-photo marks, one 'We weren't sure — check this' flag, 7 default passed with the 'Remind 1 day before' suggestion, no chips, footer 'You and Sam can see this bill.'\n25. x-date-sheet · ios · 25-bill-unreadable · light — HOME A, snap of Clark Public Utilities, amount and due date blank (never $0.00), Save disabled until both are filled, footer 'You and Sam can see this bill.'\n26. x-date-sheet · ios · 26-pickup-home-set-by-sam · light — HOME A, 'Set by Sam Ortega', Tuesday, Every other week, Next recycling Tue 20 Oct, preview Tue 20 Oct · Tue 3 Nov · Tue 17 Nov, night-before line, Clear household pickup day.\n27. x-date-sheet · android · 27-create-lease-dense · light — embedded input picker with 03/31/2027 and the calendar toggle, Close (X).\n28. x-date-sheet · web-1440 · 28-create-lease-dense · light — right SlidePanel over the place file, typed '31 Mar 2027'.\n29. x-date-sheet · web-390 · 29-view-seeded-voter · light — bottom sheet, checked caption.\n30. x-date-sheet · ios · 30-ax5-create-lease · light — left: create-empty as a one-column kind list; right: lease chosen, scrolled to reminder radio rows and stacked visibility options.\n31. x-date-sheet · ios · 31-greyscale-marks · light — frames 3 (hollow Thursday) and 8 (filled caption plus you-added date) side by side in greyscale, legend words visible.\n32. x-date-sheet · ios · 32-create-lease-dense · dark — dark twin of frame 1.\n33. x-date-sheet · ios · 33-view-seeded-voter · dark — dark twin of frame 5, checked caption.\n34. x-date-sheet · Notes — the Notes board, with:\n  - The PushCopy date-reminder tray preview (7:00 AM): Done marks the date done without opening the app and cancels the remaining reminders. Active/DEFAULT. Also listed in the in-app notifications. In the foreground there is no banner; the row is highlighted instead. A bill reminder lands on the bill.\n  - Hand-offs: close, then the notification primer on native for a first pickup save; the FirstWeekRow advances; the widget is rewritten; 'I did this' on voter ticks the place file mover row 'Update your voter registration' as you-added, Only you, and Undo un-ticks it.\n  - Assumptions:\n    - Seeded rows are filled only when checked, and seeds launch hollow.\n    - Thu 12 Nov is unmoved: the City of Camas 2026 calendar moves only the Wednesday route, Veterans' Day Wed Nov 11 → Thu Nov 12.\n    - Camas collects recycling weekly, so every-other-week is shown at HOME A (Vancouver).\n    - The tax-appeal seed appears at any Clark County address, including a rental. Property-tax appeal seeds are F12 phase 2 data. Bill is phase 2.\n    - Backend blockers: saved-place scope must outrank the city rule, or a saved-place correction is dropped; reminder leads must allow 0–60 days; saved-place Bill and Move-in date need a kind or storage (not in the F5 kind list).\n    - Deep-link paths follow whatever Today route f1-today-tab settles on; the ?event= alias is folded into ?rule=.\n    - Done replaces the voter sheet's 'Not now'.\n    - 'Confirm Tuesday / Pick a different day' became the preselected chooser plus Save.\n    - InlineUndo, with a consequence prefix for household dates, replaces the household remove-confirm.\n    - 'Visible to' is the label.\n    - Alex Rivera is an invented guest; Priya's invite is still pending.\n  - For prompt 00:\n    - Add the 14 segment to the lease variant.\n    - Add the 'Remind me' switch and its off state to ReminderLeadControl/DateSheet.\n    - The contract sample Thu 24 Sep is replaced by Sun 25 Oct.\n    - PushCopy date-reminder body and DateRow sample Sun 31 Jan become Mon 1 Mar ('Tell your landlord by Mon 1 Mar'), the HOME A fixture.\n    - flow-03 step 4 (60 days, Sat 30 Jan) is superseded by the Mon 15 Feb fixture.\n    - Flow-02's Luis is shown as Jordan at PLACE B.\n  - Invented strings: PEMCO; the Rheem title; Columbia Plumbing; Mon 14 Sep 2026; Alex Rivera; 'Mail takes a few days. Send it by Wed 21 Oct.'; Tue 27 Oct; 'checked Oct 2026'; 'added Sep 2026'; cal_7f3a2; 'Too close to set'; 'Reminders arrive at 7:00 AM.'; 'Clear household pickup day'; 'You marked this done · Your household'; 'You and Sam can see this bill.'; 'Saved. You and Sam can see this bill.'; 'Maya or Sam can add bills here'; 'Remind 7 days before'; 'Remind 1 day before'; 'We'll remind you at the start of Jan 2027.'; the three pickup reminder lines; 'Next holiday move: …'; the report receipt; every error, suggestion, discard and collision string.\n  - Omitted states: notifications-off caption; pickup notifications-off line; 'That date was removed.'; remove failed; voter deadline passed; no seeded voter rule; offline voter tick queued; report submitted (dated receipt, then 'You reported this · checking'); saved-place manual Bill; saved-place Lease ends (same footer as frame 14); bill Save disabled for a member without finance permission; Mark paid on a bill; projected pickup dates after Dec 2026; property-tax due (view-seeded, moved from Sat 31 Oct); Mail voter plan.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for continue.\nTurn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue.\nTurn 3: 13-18, then wait for continue.\nTurn 4: 19-24, then wait for continue.\nTurn 5: 25-30, then wait for continue.\nTurn 6: 31-34.",
            "changeLog": [
              "Report path now ends on the dated receipt naming the Washington Secretary of State and Mon 26 Oct, and the row then shows 'You reported this · checking'. 'Report submitted (dated receipt)' is in Omitted states (review, major).",
              "Bill at a home: no visibility chips, footer 'You and Sam can see this bill.', and a LockedActionRow 'Maya or Sam can add bills here' with Save disabled for members without finance permission. That variant is listed under Omitted states (review, major).",
              "Removing a date always cancels its reminders. Household-visible removals get the consequence prefix 'Removed for everyone in this household: …', shown as an inset on frame 18 (review, major).",
              "New hand-off: 'I did this' on voter ticks the place file mover row as you-added and Only you, and Undo un-ticks it. Added to the Notes hand-offs (review, major).",
              "Pickup reminder line now has three variants: on, notifications or evening briefing off, and permission never asked. The never-asked variant is drawn in frame 3 (review, major).",
              "'Mark paid' added for a Bill at a home, with a no-Paid-until-marked rule, in COPY buttons (review, major).",
              "iOS date entry: the compact pill opens the system calendar with the month/year jump. Web and Android input formats are separated. INSTEAD OF is rewritten. Frame 1 gets a numbered 1–3 tap inset of the month/year wheel (review, major).",
              "Every-other-week demo moved from Camas to HOME A in frame 26. Jordan now picks Weekly, with preview Thu 22 Oct · Thu 29 Oct · Thu 5 Nov and a Thanksgiving next-holiday line. WHO AND WHEN is updated (review, major).",
              "Voter captions split: checked ('● … checked Oct 2026', frames 5, 29, 33) and unconfirmed ('○ … added Sep 2026', frame 6) (review, major).",
              "New FOOTER BY MODE list. Seeded kinds never show chips and their footer reads 'Only you will see this.' Frames 7 and 8 are set at HOME A with that footer (review, major).",
              "Mail voter plan: 1 day selected, 60/30/7 disabled, ticks Tue 20 Oct and Wed 21 Oct with the day-before caption (review, minor).",
              "Default leads stated per kind (lease 14; warranty, insurance, HOA 30; bill 7). 'Remind 7 days before' button added and shown in frame 11. The bill's passed-default suggestion is in frame 24 (review, minor).",
              "Back is leading and Cancel/Done is trailing when Back is present, with the medium-to-large detent cross-fade. Jordan's path now goes 'Not my schedule' → 'Set my pickup day' (review, minor).",
              "Guest frame uses the invented Alex Rivera, listed on Notes. Priya's pending invite is noted (review, minor, two findings reconciled).",
              "'You marked this done · Your household' for Household dates, used in frame 17 (review, minor).",
              "Added: the before-kind state (grid plus disabled Save), the Amount field for HOA and Bill, Android inline calendar for other kinds, the Not-sure-of-the-day tick rule, and the create-mode offline copy, shown as an inset in frame 22 (review, minor).",
              "Saving state drawn as an inset in frame 16 (review, minor).",
              "Projected caption for pickup dates after Dec 2026, listed under Omitted states (review, minor).",
              "Notes updated: property-tax appeal marked F12 phase 2; saved-place Bill and Move-in storage added as a backend blocker; the PushCopy/DateRow Sun 31 Jan → Mon 1 Mar change flagged for prompt 00; property-tax due and Mail voter plan added to Omitted states (review, minor).",
              "Notification details on Notes: Done works in the background and cancels the remaining reminders, Active/DEFAULT, listed in-app, highlight with no banner in the foreground, and a bill reminder lands on the bill (review, minor).",
              "Voter method row titles now match the contract strings exactly, with 'in 7 days' / 'in 15 days' on line 2 (review, minor).",
              "Added the Settings > Notifications pickup entry point and the full web create paths (/app/place/today?add=date&kind=lease_end, /app/today?add=date) (review, minor).",
              "All v1 substance kept: the ten kinds, lease notice math, collision handling, tax-appeal rule, voter person-scoping, AX5, greyscale and dark twins, deep links, and the Notes assumptions."
            ]
          }
