                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The saved-place collision copy is wrong, and the change makes the product claim false. The design doc caps it at one row per kind per place, but the prompt says one per place.",
                    "evidence": "Design doc F5: 'One row per kind per place in v1 (a second warranty goes into `HomeCalendarEvent` later); the UI says \"one per kind for now\".' Prompt EDGE CASES: 'At a saved place, say it before typing, under the tile: 'One per place for now · already set''.",
                    "fix": "Change the string to 'One per kind for now · already set for Sat 12 Dec' (the tile-level hint follows the f5-add-date-sheet pattern 'Warranty ends — already set for …'). At a saved place, also offer an explicit, previewed 'Replace it' (f5-add-date-sheet uxRisk: 'make Replace an explicit, previewed choice'). Add a saved-place collision artboard, or list it as omitted on Notes."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The prompt draws every seeded row with the filled Official mark and has no frame for the unconfirmed seed. Every source says seeds launch unverified with a hollow mark until someone checks them. Flagging the choice as an assumption on Notes does not draw the state that will actually ship, and invariant 1 requires it.",
                    "evidence": "Design doc F6: 'Seed state-scoped … election_deadline … `confidence 'unverified'` until each is checked.' F12: tax_appeal '`confidence 'unverified'` until checked'. Inventory visualization: 'Seeded mode shows the hollow provenance mark beside the date and the authority as a caption.' f6-voter-step-sheet states: 'ready, confidence unverified — badge + 'not yet checked against the state site''. flow-13 failure: 'Unverified seed. A hollow mark plus the source.' Prompt: 'Voter registration (seeded, statewide; filled mark …)', 'Property-tax appeal (seeded, county; filled mark …)', Notes: 'seeded rows drawn Official because they were checked against the authority'.",
                    "fix": "Add an artboard, e.g. 'view-seeded-voter-unconfirmed', that shows the hollow mark, the SourceCaption and the line 'Not yet checked against the Washington Secretary of State site'. State in LAYOUT that a seeded row uses the filled mark only when its confidence is official and otherwise uses the hollow mark."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The prompt gets the civic block entry point wrong. In both the flow and the design doc, the block's 'Check or update' is the outbound link to the state site, and a separate 'Remind me' is what leads to the Date sheet.",
                    "evidence": "flows-spec flow-13 step 3: 'He sees … an outbound 'Check or update at VoteWA', and a separate 'Remind me'. … The check goes to the official state site.' Design doc F6: 'Check or update at {state office}.' flows-spec contradictions: 'f6-place-section-details's civic 'Check or update' opens the Date sheet, while the design doc F6 sends the user to the state office.' Prompt: 'Civic registration block: 'Check or update' opens view-seeded voter registration.'",
                    "fix": "Replace the line with: 'Civic registration block: 'Remind me' (or the deadline row) opens view-seeded voter registration. 'Check or update at VoteWA ↗' there stays outbound.' Also note that the place-file mover row goes through the f6 civic block in flow-13."
                  },
