                    "evidence": "Research-findings: 'nothing becomes shared until the person makes an explicit choice … Every date later carries its own visibility control in the date sheet and the place file ('Only you' / 'Household').' flows-spec flow-06 step 11: 'x-date-sheet | view-mine at home scope with per-date visibility control | She opens Renters insurance and sees 'Visible to: Only you · Household'. She switches it to Household.' House style invariant 2: 'Scope changes need an explicit choice.' Prompt: 'Scope changes only three things: the footer sentence, whether a visibility choice is shown, and the saved message' and 'At a home only: the ChoiceChip pair 'Who can see this: Only you · Household'.'",
                    "fix": "State the default for a new date at a home, then make the footer and the saved message follow the selected chip: Only you → 'Only you will see this.' and 'Saved to your calendar. Only you.'; Household → 'Everyone in this household will see this.' and 'Saved to your household calendar.' Settle on one label ('Visible to:' as in flow-06, or record the change on Notes). Add an artboard: 'view-mine-insurance-visibility · HOME A · Renters insurance switched Only you → Household'."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The prompt never shows what the tax-appeal date slot holds before the mailing date is entered, or what 'I haven't got one yet' does. Because view modes show 'the date large (h2)', a designer is likely to put a single date there, and the research forbids that.",
                    "evidence": "Research-findings: 'Only once that is answered does the row show a single computed date … Until then the strip and year band show the July 1 marker with a 'may be later' caption.' flows-spec flow-11: 'A conditional deadline is never shown as a single seeded date.' Prompt: 'In view modes, the date is shown large (h2)…' and artboard 6 'the rule, and the mailing-date question still empty.'",
                    "fix": "Add: 'Before the mailing date is entered, the h2 slot shows the rule, not a date. The row reads 'July 1, or later' with the caption 'may be later'. Choosing 'I haven't got one yet' keeps the rule, sets no computed date and fires no reminder until a date is entered.' Name the July 1 year (1 Jul 2027) if it is shown."
