      {
        "ids": [
          "x-place-file"
        ],
        "prompts": [
          {
            "id": "x-place-file",
            "name": "Your place file",
            "platforms": [
              "web",
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": true,
            "frameCount": 24,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Your place file · x-place-file\n\nTYPE: NEW. Nothing like it exists yet. Build it only from the Foundations components and the existing row and card styles.\n\nATTACH: the current Place tab root on web 1440 (with the left sidebar), web 390, iOS and Android (including any section switcher it shows); the current Today tab on iOS (so the band's 14-day window matches the FourteenDayStrip geometry); the Foundations board from prompt 00. These Place tab screenshots are for the chrome only: the sidebar, the bottom tab bar, the navigation bar and any section switcher. Keep those exactly. Everything below them is replaced by this screen, so do not keep the old dashboard cards (including the old Just Moved card).\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: web 1440x900 (sidebar) and 390x844 (bottom tab bar); iOS 393x852 with the large title \"Your place file\" that collapses on scroll; Android 412x915 with the Material 3 large top app bar.\n\nWHY IT IS SHAPED THIS WAY (do not optimise this away)\nThis is one list replacing four: the first-week checklist, Just moved, Your dates and the keeper's list of facts. Draw them as sections of one file, with one tick and one dismissal per row. Never split \"Set up your place\", \"Just moved\" or Dates back into separate cards. Ticks and dismissals are stored on the server and sync across devices; the sync banner is the only visible sign of that. A date more than 14 days away is visible only on this screen. In the current app, a lease end 5 months out would be saved, confirmed and then hidden until 2 weeks before it fires. This screen also gives the Place tab a job before an address is claimed.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE\nThis screen is the index of the Place tab (Place · Today · Nearby · Mail) on every platform: web /app/place, and the Place tab root on iOS and Android. It needs a place; a person with no saved place sees the Your places empty state instead. Arrivals:\n1. Tapping Place in the tab bar or sidebar.\n2. Today's FirstWeekRow (\"Next: set your pickup day →\", shown for 7 days). It lands on \"Set up your place\" with that step highlighted. Both use the same step set and agree on what is done.\n3. The claim receipt's \"See your place file\" button (formerly \"See what we know\"). The receipt hands over the carried items, which appear here once as a banner and stay in the \"What moved when you claimed\" row.\n4. The keeper strip's count (phase 2). The number there equals the number here.\n5. A reminder push with no specific date lands at the top. A reminder for a date more than 14 days away lands on that date's row: highlighted, focus moved to it, then the DateSheet opens in view mode. Links: web /app/place?rule=notice-deadline · pantopus://place?rule=notice-deadline.\n6. The large widget's year strip lands on the year band: web /app/place?section=year · pantopus://place?section=year.\nExits: rows open the DateSheet, the ProvenanceSheet, Your places, the home dashboard (read-only variant for members), the members roster, the invite composer, the bills list, Mail Day triage, the bill trend, the home documents list, the verify sheet, the privacy mirror, the keeper naming sheet, the Civic registration block, the widget how-to sheet and the claim receipt. \"Next 14 days\" opens Today's 14-day strip. Risk & readiness and Civic stay reachable (see LAYOUT).\n\nWHO AND WHEN\nDense frames: Maya Chen, owner of HOME A, Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM. She moved in 23 days ago, claimed on Sat 17 Oct; Sam Ortega joined Sun 18 Oct. She wants to check nothing in the year ahead is missing, including the lease notice.\nPLACE B frames: the fixture's Jordan Lee, never named on screen. Delta: Jordan saved PLACE B on Sat 17 Oct (not Sat 10 Oct), so the first week runs until Sat 24 Oct.\n\nTHE ONE JOB\nSee every fact on file for this address in one list, including dates months away, and add the few that are missing.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS\nHOME A (every first-week step done): 1. address, ScopeChip \"Your household\", \"11 on file\". 2. Band summary \"Next: voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\". 3. The first Just moved row, \"Update your voter registration\", whose filled button \"See how to update\" is the one primary action. The two remaining asks (widget, insurance) are quiet rows in their own sections, below the fold.\nPLACE B (first week): 1. address, ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\", \"2 on file\". 2. The band. 3. \"Set up your place\", primary action \"Set your pickup day\".\nPromoted asks follow the activation order: pickup day, then a reminder or the widget, then one date or one person. Never more than 3. On native, ask 2 is \"Turn on a reminder or add the widget\"; on web (no widget) it is \"Turn on a reminder\".\n\nCONTENT (house style fixtures; deltas only)\nHOME A deltas: moved in Sat 26 Sep 2026, so Just moved shows until Wed 25 Nov. Maya set Tuesday pickup on Sat 10 Oct while it was a saved place; it carried at the claim (Sat 17 Oct) with the lease end, notice deadline, warranty and Ollie. Maya set the move-in date on the home on Sun 18 Oct, after the claim. The warranty is \"Only you\"; everything else is \"Your household\". Priya invite sent Mon 19 Oct. Bills came from mail snaps (tick). Address not verified.\nCount rule: \"on file\" counts what this household holds plus address-specific records such as the pickup weekday. County and state rules are shown, not counted. HOME A = 11: Place 3 (address, pickup day, moved in) · Dates 4 (HOA dues, warranty, notice deadline, lease ends) · Money 3 bills · People 1 (Sam). PLACE B = 2: address and the Thursday pickup weekday (on record, not confirmed; \"Set your pickup day\" stays undone because nobody confirmed it or set how often).\n\nHeader, in order: \"Your place file\"; \"2418 NE Larkspur Loop\" / \"Vancouver, WA 98684\"; ScopeChip \"Your household\"; FreshnessLine \"Updated 4m ago\"; FactCount \"11 on file\" with pips Place · Dates · Money · People; legend \"● Official · ○ On record, not confirmed · ✓ You added this\", printed once.\n\nYear band \"The year ahead\", Oct 2026–Sep 2027:\n- You (tick): Nov (HOA dues) · Dec (warranty) · Mar with count \"2\" (notice deadline, lease ends).\n- Your city: Tuesday service rhythm with tick for Oct–Dec, dashed with the word \"projected\" from Jan (last published hauler calendar is Dec 2026). No Tuesday holiday move is published for Oct–Dec.\n- Your county (filled): Nov (property tax 2nd half) · Apr (1st half) · Jul (appeal, caption \"may be later\").\n- Your state (filled, full-lane-height bars): Oct (Mon 26 Oct) · Nov (Tue 3 Nov).\n- Summary \"Next 12 months: 9 dates, plus pickup every Tuesday. Next: voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct.\" Caption \"Every date is listed below.\" Link row \"Next 14 days · See them on Today ›\".\n\nJUST MOVED, caption \"Shown until Wed 25 Nov, 60 days after you moved in\". Undone rows first, done last:\n- \"Update your voter registration\" · \"Registration is per address · in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · button \"See how to update\" opens the Civic registration block (per-method dates and \"Check or update at VoteWA ↗\"). Never state or imply whether Maya is registered.\n- \"Move your utilities\" · Clark Public Utilities, NW Natural, City of Vancouver.\n- \"Forward your mail\" · USPS · done and quiet: \"You marked this done Sat 3 Oct\".\n\nPLACE:\n- Your home · \"Larkspur Loop ›\" opens the home dashboard (absent on a saved place).\n- Address · full address · chevron to Your places · tick.\n- Pickup day · \"You · Tuesday\" · \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow · carts out by 6:30 AM\" · SourceCaption \"Waste Connections · recycling every other Tuesday · you confirmed Sat 10 Oct\". Opens the DateSheet pickup kind.\n- Moved in · \"Sat 26 Sep 2026\" · tick · helper \"Shows your moving list for 60 days\".\n- What neighbors see · \"Same spot every time, about 0.3 mi\" (opens the privacy mirror).\n- Keeper (phase 2): named: \"Keeper · Ollie\" with chevron to the keeper naming sheet. Unnamed or skipped: quiet FactRow \"Give your place a keeper\" with text \"Add\", no badge, never promoted.\n- Put today on your home screen · \"Pickup, air and your next date. No notifications needed.\" iOS and Android only, with a small thumbnail of Maya's own widget (live snapshot: Tuesday pickup, AQI 42, HOA dues) at the leading edge. Quiet for HOME A.\n- What moved when you claimed · \"Pickup day, 3 dates and Ollie · Sat 17 Oct\". A move-in date saved on a saved place also carries at claim and is listed here when present.\n- Your reports · \"1 checking\".\n\nDATES: DateRows in date order, relative count first:\n- Voter registration · \"Online or by mail — in 7 days · must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\" · second line \"In person, Clark County Elections — in 15 days · until 8:00 PM Tue 3 Nov\" · the DateRow's statewide tag \"Statewide — WA\" (its optional tag, not the visibility ScopeChip; no person or house glyph) · filled · Washington Secretary of State · \"Remind me\". Directly below, a separate TextActionRow (outbound) \"Check or update at VoteWA ↗\", not nested in the row target.\n- HOA dues · \"$285 · in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov\" · \"Every year\" · tick.\n- Property tax, 2nd half · \"Due in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov\" · \"Every year\" · filled · Clark County Treasurer. Detail one tap away: \"moved from Sat 31 Oct\".\n- Water-heater warranty ends · \"in 54 days · Sat 12 Dec\" · \"Reminders Thu 12 Nov, Fri 11 Dec and Sat 12 Dec\" · Only you.\n- \"Tell your landlord in writing by Mon 1 Mar 2027\" · \"in 4 months · Mon 1 Mar 2027\" · \"Reminders Mon 15 Feb, Sun 28 Feb and Mon 1 Mar\" · \"From your lease: 30 days' notice\".\n- Lease ends · \"in 5 months · Wed 31 Mar 2027\" · link line \"Notice deadline: Mon 1 Mar 2027\". No reminder on this row.\n- Property tax, 1st half · \"Due in 6 months · Fri 30 Apr 2027\" · \"Every year\" · filled.\n- Property-tax appeal · \"in 8 months · Thu 1 Jul 2027, or 60 days after your value notice was mailed\" · \"Every year\" · Clark County Board of Equalization · filled · text action \"Add the mailing date\".\n- Quiet ask \"When does your insurance renew?\" · \"Add a date\".\n- \"Open household calendar\".\nVisibility: on user-entered dates the glyph and word (person + \"Only you\", or house + \"Your household\") is a control that opens the DateSheet's visibility choice; scope changes only when someone picks. Seeded county and state rows show their source and carry no household scope.\n\nMONEY (phase 2): Bills · \"3 upcoming · $306.17 through Mon 2 Nov\" · \"Next: Clark Public Utilities $142.18 · in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\" · \"You and Sam can see these.\" Below, quiet rows \"Mail Day ›\" (Mail Day triage) and \"How your bills compare ›\" (bill trend).\n\nPEOPLE: hosts the household block (own prompt). With 2+ members it collapses to MemberRow \"Maya and Sam live here · View\". Below, InviteRow \"priya@example.com · Member · sent Mon 19 Oct · Expires Mon 26 Oct · Resend\".\n\nMORE YOU CAN ADD, collapsed \"More you can add (3)\": \"Verify this address\" (verify sheet), \"Your gas bill · NW Natural\" (bills), \"A home document, like your lease\" (home documents list). Proof has no section until something is known.\n\nWorst case: 9 dates, 3 mover rows, 3 bills and a pending invite in one phone scroll, with November marks in three lanes.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\n- Phones: one column, 16pt gutter. Order: header → LandingBannerSlot (only when it holds a banner) → year band card → Set up your place (PLACE B, first 7 days) → Just moved → Place → Risk & readiness and Civic → Dates → Money → People → Proof (only when known) → More you can add → footer.\n- Existing sections: if the attached host shows a section switcher (e.g. Risk & readiness · Civic), keep it unchanged above the title and make this file its first section. If not, add two navigation FactRows \"Risk & readiness\" and \"Civic\" directly after Place. Say on Notes which you drew.\n- Year band on phones and web-390: each lane label (You · Your city · Your county · Your state) is a caption line above its lane. 12 month columns share the card width (about 27pt each), three-letter labels, \"2027\" above Jan. Lanes on surface.raised with ink dividers. One XS ProvenanceMark per month cell per lane, plus a count numeral at 2+; never exact-day placement on a phone. Statewide rules are full-lane-height bars. Today rule 1.5px text.primary labelled \"Today\". The 14-day window is a primary.50 sliver at least 8pt wide with an ink edge, starting at the today rule, with a bracket above the month labels; its label sits outside the band as the link row. City lane: light service-week rhythm, dashed and \"projected\" after Dec 2026. A holiday move = mark plus a small \"moved\" glyph in its month cell; the moved date is written in the pickup row. Bills are not drawn on the band.\n- YearBand anatomy is fixed by prompt 00. If a phone cell cannot hold mark, count and \"moved\" glyph, draw 2 cluster options side by side on Notes and use the first in the frames.\n- Web 1440: band spans full content width with exact-day marks. A holiday move sits on its new day with a faint struck ghost on the usual day (web-1440 only). A leader line runs from the notice-deadline mark back to a reminder tick \"Reminder Mon 15 Feb\". Below: a 720 column (Just moved, Place, Risk & readiness and Civic, Dates, Money, People) and a 320 column (More you can add, open by default; Your reports; What moved when you claimed). No widget row.\n- Rows: FactRow 56pt, label above value. Annual and self-entered DateRows get the 2px home pillar token (home) left rule plus their recurrence caption.\n- Missing data: no rules → all 12 columns, 4 empty labelled lanes, QuietDayReceipt line \"Checked — nothing on file for the next year\". Whole-screen error → no band. County rules fail alone → county lane not drawn, InlineErrorRow in the band. Saved place → county lane reads \"County dates aren't available for a saved place\".\n- PLACE B header: ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\"; FactCount \"2 on file\", Place pip only (T1 can show only Place and Dates).\n- PLACE B \"Set up your place\" (caption \"For your first week · until Sat 24 Oct\", Dismiss): \"Save your address\" (ticked), \"Set your pickup day\" (primary), \"Turn on a reminder or add the widget\", \"Add one date that matters\". No fraction. Below, grey LockedActionRow (not at this tier) \"Add the people you live with · Claim this address first\", no button, not counted. These are the promoted asks, so the same facts show only a quiet \"Not set\" in sections below.\n- PLACE B Place: pickup \"Thursday · how often: Not set\", hollow mark, caption \"City of Camas · pickup Thursdays · 2026 calendar\", opens the DateSheet pickup kind. Below: \"Thanksgiving — moved to Fri 27 Nov · City of Camas 2026 calendar\"; the band's Nov city cell shows the \"moved\" glyph. \"Moved in · Not set · Add\" with helper \"Add it to see a moving list for 60 days\". Keeper row in skipped form.\n- Saved place with a move-in date: Just moved appears with the same rows; ticks and dismissals are stored against the saved place (frame 18).\n- PLACE B Dates: the voter row and VoteWA link, plus \"More you can add (4)\" (Lease ends, Insurance renews, Warranty ends, HOA dues).\n- PLACE B other sections: one grey row \"Money, people and proof · Not here — this is a saved place · Claim this address first\". While a claim is pending, the Proof block (below) replaces it; Money and People stay absent. Footer \"Only you will see this.\" and text link \"Claim this address\".\n- Proof pending (PLACE B): LockedActionRow (pending, no link) \"Postcard mailed Mon 19 Oct · expected Fri 23 Oct–Mon 2 Nov · code expires Wed 18 Nov\"; below it a separate FactRow \"Enter your code\" with chevron; below that a disabled, focusable button \"Send a new code\" with reason \"You can ask for a new code after Mon 2 Nov.\"\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- Targets: 44pt iOS, 48dp Android (8dp gaps), 44px web. Custom actions: Edit, Remind me, Where this comes from, Mark done.\n- One target per row: only the first promoted ask shows a filled button, and that button is the row's only target. Asks 2 and 3 show their verb as the row label with a chevron. \"Not now\" and \"Skip\" sit on one line of small text buttons under each promoted ask (44pt each, 8pt apart) and are also custom actions. On mover rows, dismiss and Mark done live in a 44pt overflow button and in custom actions; the row body is the single target. Quiet asks offer Skip through their overflow button and a custom action.\n- \"Not now\" turns a promoted ask into a quiet row that is never auto-promoted again. \"Skip\" collapses the row to InlineUndo, is stored on the server, and can be reopened from More you can add.\n- Year band: a tap anywhere scrolls to Dates. Native: one adjustable element; swipe up/down moves by month. Web: month columns are buttons in tab order; click or Enter highlights that month's rows, Escape clears. Link row opens Today.\n- Widget row: promoted at most once in any 24 hours, otherwise quiet. Android: opens the how-to sheet whose primary \"Add to home screen\" calls the system pin dialog. iOS: how-to sheet with the Edit → Add Widget steps. Disappears once a widget is placed.\n- Dismissed mover row collapses to InlineUndo until she leaves the screen. When all three are gone: \"You can show these again in home settings.\"\n- \"More you can add\" expands in place. Deep-link landing scrolls once, then fades the highlight; a deleted date lands at the top with a status line. Count updates silently, no count-up.\n- Motion 300ms or less; Reduce Motion uses cross-fades and a static skeleton.\n- Haptics: one light tick on \"Mark done\" only (iOS light impact; Android confirm haptic).\n- DateSheet: right SlidePanel web 1440, bottom SlidePanel web-390, large sheet iOS, ModalBottomSheet Android. ProvenanceSheet: centred modal 560 web 1440, bottom sheet web-390, medium detent iOS, ModalBottomSheet Android. Sheets never stack.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED\nYearBand (place file; empty checked), FourteenDayStrip (window geometry only), ProvenanceMark (XS band, S rows), SourceCaption, ScopeChip, FactCount (place file header; T1), FactRow (known, missing, not at this tier, done ask, declined, permission-disabled, \"What moved when you claimed\", \"Your reports\"). \"Set up your place\" is a group of FactRows (missing, done ask) using FirstWeekRow's step set and 7-day window; draw no FirstWeekRow here. DateRow (deadline, money, pickup, holiday moved, conditional rule, done; statewide tag), KindGlyph, LockedActionRow (names who can act; pending; not at this tier), InlineUndo (removed row; declined ask), LandingBannerSlot (sync merge; one-time claim receipt), FreshnessLine, OfflineNotice, InlineErrorRow (provider unreachable), QuietDayReceipt, WarmingSkeleton (instrument, row), MemberRow (collapsed), InviteRow, TextActionRow (outbound), DateSheet, ProvenanceSheet.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Reading order: title → address → scope → freshness → count → banner → band summary → band → link row → Set up your place → Just moved → Place → Risk & readiness → Civic → Dates → Money → People → Proof → More you can add → footer.\n- FactCount: \"11 things on file: place, dates, money, people.\"\n- Band: its summary plus \"The Dates list below has every date.\" A month reads: \"November: You, HOA dues Sunday 1 November, you added this. Your county, property tax second half due Monday 2 November, official. Your state, in-person voter registration until 8 PM Tuesday 3 November, official. Your city, pickup every Tuesday, you added this.\" A moved pickup is spoken with its new date.\n- Marks are never targets alone. Provenance = shape plus legend word; \"projected\" = word plus dash; statewide = bar shape. None rely on colour.\n- Visibility control: \"Visible to: Only you. Change who can see this.\"\n- Disabled Resend, Add and Send a new code stay focusable and read their reason. Banners, the deleted-date line and InlineUndo are status regions.\n- AX5: band keeps its lanes but scrolls sideways at readable scale, lane labels pinned, visible \"Earlier\" and \"Later\" buttons. FactRows stack label and value. Text wraps. \"Not now\" and \"Skip\" stack.\n\nCOPY (sentence case)\nEverything quoted above, plus:\n- Banners: \"Synced 3 items from your other device\" · \"Your pickup day, 3 dates and Ollie came with you. · See what moved\" · \"That date was removed.\"\n- Undo: “Hid “Move your utilities” · Undo” · “Skipped “When does your insurance renew?” · Undo”\n- All known: \"Everything we can hold about this place is on file\" (shown only when no asks remain).\n- Reports: \"Voter registration deadline · Checking · reported Sun 18 Oct · we'll check by Sun 25 Oct\" · \"Pickup day · Fixed Fri 16 Oct · recycling is every other Tuesday · Waste Connections\" · \"Property-tax appeal date · No change Wed 14 Oct · Clark County Board of Equalization lists Thu 1 Jul 2027, or 60 days after your notice\"\n- Member view: \"Maya can add bills here.\" · \"Maya can invite people here.\" · \"Maya can rename Ollie.\" · \"Maya can add and change dates here.\"\n- Voter done (Notes sample, Sat 24 Oct): \"You marked this done Sat 24 Oct · Only you\" · \"We can't check registration status.\"\n- Voter after online deadline (Notes sample, Tue 27 Oct): \"Voter registration · In person, Clark County Elections — in 7 days · until 8:00 PM Tue 3 Nov\", online line removed. After Tue 3 Nov the row leaves Dates and Civic reads \"No upcoming election\".\n- Appeal computed (Notes sample, Mon 10 May 2027, tick): \"Property-tax appeal · closes in 53 days · Fri 2 Jul 2027\" · \"60 days after your notice was mailed Mon 3 May\"\n- Offline: \"You're offline · as of 6:04 PM\" · \"Adding a date needs a connection.\" · \"Resending needs a connection.\" · after Mark done: \"Saved on this device. It'll sync.\"\n- Notifications off: \"Notifications are off. This date still shows here and on Today.\"\n- Errors: \"We couldn't load your place file just now · Retry\" · \"We couldn't reach Clark County's calendar just now · Retry\"\n- Done row: \"Done · You marked this done Tue 16 Feb · Reminders off\"\n\nEDGE CASES\n- Longest address \"Unit 1204, 10417 NE Hazel Dell Avenue, Vancouver, WA 98685\" wraps to two lines, never cut.\n- A month cell with 12 marks shows \"12\".\n- No dates: empty You lane; promoted ask \"Add one date that matters\".\n- Reminder link for a deleted date: top of screen, \"That date was removed.\", no modal, no blank.\n- Reminder dates show on rows whether notifications are on or off. If notifications are denied, ask 2 reads \"Add the widget\" (native) and the widget row ranks ahead of the reminder ask.\n- Slow network: skeleton only after 1 second; cached content never goes blank.\n- County rules fail to load: county lane not drawn, InlineErrorRow \"We couldn't reach Clark County's calendar just now · Retry\"; the rest of the file stays.\n- Approximate date: \"about Dec 2026\", counts as known, offers \"Add the exact day\".\n- A seeded rule not yet checked against its authority is hollow.\n- Widget placed: widget row gone (frame 17).\n- Member view (Sam): the Only-you warranty is hidden and not counted (\"10 on file\"); the Dec mark is gone from the You lane; summary \"Next 12 months: 8 dates, plus pickup every Tuesday. Next: voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct.\" Mover ticks are Sam's own, so \"Forward your mail\" is undone for him. Bills caption \"You and Maya can see these.\" Resend and the claim-receipt row are absent. \"Your home\" opens the read-only dashboard. Sam's Just moved runs Sun 18 Oct–Thu 17 Dec.\n- Guest: \"Bills · 3 on file\" with \"Maya can see and add bills here.\" A Guest without calendar.edit sees Dates rows with no Edit or Remind actions and one line \"Maya can add and change dates here.\"\n- Web: no widget row; ask 2 is \"Turn on a reminder\".\n- Phase-2 rows (Bills, Mail Day, bill compare, Keeper) are absent until shipped; the layout still works.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of keeping the old Place dashboard cards under the file, draw the file as the whole tab body — because this screen replaces them.\n- Instead of a five-segment ring or \"3 of 6\", draw \"11 on file\" with pips only for known categories — because any denominator reads as an unfinished task.\n- Instead of a button on every missing fact, draw one filled button, at most 3 promoted asks and the rest behind \"More you can add (3)\" — because about ten competing asks lowers completion.\n- Instead of day-accurate dots and an in-band \"Next 14 days\" label on phones, draw month clusters with counts, an 8pt sliver and the label as a link row — because about 0.8pt per day makes Mon 26 Oct, Mon 2 Nov and Tue 3 Nov overlap.\n- Instead of an even pickup rhythm all year, draw holiday moves and \"projected\" after Dec 2026 — because the hauler publishes one year at a time.\n- Instead of a dot or a visibility chip for a statewide deadline, draw a full-lane-height bar in \"Your state\" and the DateRow's statewide tag — because it is not a fact about this house.\n- Instead of the lease reminder on the lease-ends row, put the three reminders on the notice row — because a reminder tied to the lease end fires after the last day to act.\n- Instead of red X's, failure rows or an empty band on error, draw neutral invitations, one grey \"Not here\" row, and no band plus an InlineErrorRow — because missing is not broken and an empty band means \"checked, nothing found\".\n\nDONE WHEN\n- A lease end 5 months away is visible on the band and editable in Dates; the notice row holds the reminders.\n- Each frame has one obvious primary action above the fold, and each row has one target. Nothing reads as percent complete. A saved place looks smaller, not failing.\n- This count equals the keeper's count; Today's first-week row agrees about what is done.\n- Every statewide or county date shows its source and cannot be read as a claim about this house.\n- Scope is stated in the header, on each user-entered date and in the saved-place footer.\n- A reminder for a date beyond 14 days lands on that row; a deleted date lands with \"That date was removed.\"\n- Every ask can be declined and found again; the claim receipt, report outcomes and keeper re-entry can be found again.\n- A saved-place mover sees \"Update your voter registration\" once a move-in date is set.\n- The all-clear line appears only when no asks remain. The widget row disappears once placed.\n- Greyscale and AX5 frames still read correctly.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. x-place-file · ios · 01-dense-home · light — HOME A, Just moved open, all content above.\n2. x-place-file · ios · 02-saved-place-first-week · light — PLACE B: Set up your place, holiday move, skipped keeper row, grey \"Not here\" row.\n3. x-place-file · web-390 · 03-member-view · light — Sam's view: \"10 on file\", no Dec mark, 8-date summary, his own mover ticks, reasons naming Maya.\n4. x-place-file · ios · 04-dismissed-and-declined · light — \"Move your utilities\" collapsed to Undo; the insurance row's overflow open on Skip, then its collapsed InlineUndo.\n5. x-place-file · ios · 05-sync-merge · light — the sync banner, shown once.\n6. x-place-file · ios · 06-claim-receipt-banner · light — the one-time banner plus \"What moved when you claimed\".\n7. x-place-file · ios · 07-reminder-landing · light — Mon 15 Feb 2027, 7:00 AM. Band Feb 2027–Jan 2028; window Mon 15 Feb–Sun 28 Feb, so Mon 1 Mar sits just outside. No Just moved. Dates: \"Tell your landlord in writing by Mon 1 Mar 2027\" · \"in 14 days · Mon 1 Mar 2027\" (highlighted, focused) · \"Lease ends · in 44 days · Wed 31 Mar 2027\" · \"Property tax, 1st half · Due in 74 days · Fri 30 Apr 2027\" · \"Property-tax appeal · in 4 months · Thu 1 Jul 2027, or 60 days after your value notice was mailed\" · \"Property tax, 2nd half · Due in 8 months · Mon 1 Nov 2027\" · \"HOA dues · $285 · in 8 months · Mon 1 Nov 2027\".\n8. x-place-file · ios · 08-notice-done · light — Tue 16 Feb 2027: notice row quiet with tick and \"Reminders off\"; Lease ends stays.\n9. x-place-file · android · 09-postcard-pending · light — PLACE B, claim pending: the pending LockedActionRow, the \"Enter your code\" FactRow and the disabled \"Send a new code\" with its reason replace the \"Not here\" row.\n10. x-place-file · web-390 · 10-your-reports · light — the three reports expanded.\n11. x-place-file · ios · 11-all-known · light — Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM, variant where Maya's claim was completed by postcard: all three Just moved rows done and quiet (\"You marked this done …\"); \"Insurance renews · in 5 months · Sat 13 Mar 2027\" (Mar cell count 3, summary 10 dates); NW Natural $38.40 due Mon 9 Nov (Bills \"4 upcoming · $344.57 through Mon 9 Nov\"); Proof \"Address confirmed by postcard · Sat 17 Oct 2026\"; lease document; widget placed; appeal row shows its rule with no ask; More you can add absent. \"15 on file\", and \"Everything we can hold about this place is on file\" sits where More you can add was. No celebration.\n12. x-place-file · ios · 12-empty-year · light — layout premise: a claimed home with no seeded county or state rules, no pickup weekday on record and no dates; header \"Your household\" and \"1 on file\" (Place pip only); four empty labelled lanes plus \"Checked — nothing on file for the next year\"; promoted asks \"Set your pickup day\" and \"Add one date that matters\".\n13. x-place-file · ios · 13-loading · light — header plus instrument and row skeletons at full height.\n14. x-place-file · web-390 · 14-error · light — no band, InlineErrorRow \"We couldn't load your place file just now · Retry\".\n15. x-place-file · android · 15-offline · light — cached content, disabled actions with reasons, one offline Mark done with \"Saved on this device. It'll sync.\"\n16. x-place-file · web-1440 · 16-dense-home · light — exact days, leader line, two columns, no widget row.\n17. x-place-file · android · 17-dense-home-widget-placed · light — HOME A with no widget row.\n18. x-place-file · web-390 · 18-saved-place-mover · light — PLACE B after Jordan adds \"Moved in · Fri 9 Oct 2026\": \"3 on file\"; Just moved appears with caption \"Shown until Tue 8 Dec, 60 days after you moved in\" and its three rows, \"Update your voter registration\" first. Set up your place still shows, ask 2 reads \"Turn on a reminder\". Scope stays \"Saved place · Only you\".\n19. x-place-file · android · 19-deleted-date-landing · light — top of screen with \"That date was removed.\"\n20. x-place-file · ios · 20-ax5 · light — band scrolls sideways with pinned labels; rows stacked.\n21. x-place-file · ios · 21-greyscale · light — frame 1 in greyscale.\n22. x-place-file · ios · 01-dense-home · dark — dark twin of frame 1.\n23. x-place-file · ios · 02-saved-place-first-week · dark — dark twin of frame 2.\n24. Notes — Assumptions: Vancouver holiday calendar; seeded rules treated as checked; the count rule; frame 12's premise; frames 7–8 dated 2027; frame 11 as a postcard variant with all asks done; which Risk & readiness/Civic treatment you drew; Maya set the home move-in date on Sun 18 Oct after the claim, and a saved-place move-in date carries at claim; the 14-day notice lead is a custom lead set with ReminderLeadControl's \"other\" option; the helper \"Shows your moving list for 60 days\" must be used in home settings too; \"Open household calendar\" replaces \"Everyone here can see these\" to keep scope wording to the two ScopeChip strings. Row samples: voter done, voter after Mon 26 Oct and after Tue 3 Nov, appeal computed. Invented strings: PLACE B save date Sat 17 Oct; Tuesday set Sat 10 Oct; Sam's move-in = join date Sun 18 Oct; Fri 9 Oct move-in on PLACE B and Tue 8 Dec; postcard dates and \"Send a new code\"; longest address; deep-link URLs; frame 7, 11 and 12 rows; the Your reports dates; member-view lines; \"You can show these again in home settings.\"; \"Money, people and proof · Not here — this is a saved place\"; \"See how to update\"; \"Your home · Larkspur Loop\"; \"Mail Day\" and \"How your bills compare\"; offline, error and county-error lines; undo lines; notifications-off line; \"Open household calendar\"; widget thumbnail content; any cluster options. Omitted states: Guest bills and Guest dates rows (described in edge cases), all three mover rows dismissed.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: artboards 1–6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: 7–12, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 3: 13–18, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 4: 19–24.",
