      {
        "ids": [
          "f1-your-places",
          "f1-add-place-sheet",
          "f1-save-confirmation",
          "f1-email-verify-handoff"
        ],
        "prompts": [
          {
            "id": "f1-your-places",
            "name": "Your places (and which one Today uses)",
            "platforms": [
              "web",
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": false,
            "frameCount": 26,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Your places (and which one Today uses) · f1-your-places\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Saved places\". This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed.\n\nATTACH: (1) the current \"Saved places\" screen on iOS and on Android; (2) a web capture of the current web saved-places page (today it renders as a bare 760px page with no sidebar, no tab bar and no link to it anywhere); (3) the web Place tab shell at 1440 (left sidebar) and 390 (four-tab bar), which this list moves into; (4) Today's location row showing the \"Saved place · Only you\" chip; (5) the Foundations board.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852 · Android 412x915 · web 1440x900 with the left sidebar, Place selected · web 390x844 with the four-tab bar, Place selected. On every web frame, draw the list inside the normal Place shell at /app/place/saved.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Place tab. This one screen replaces both the old saved-places list and the planned \"Where Today gets this\" sheet; there is no second sheet. Entry points: (1) the Place tab itself for anyone with no claimed home, where this list is the tab's first screen; (2) tapping the \"Saved place · Only you\" chip in Today's location row; (3) the place file's Address row; (4) \"View saved places\" on the save confirmation; (5a) on iOS, the existing saved-places route from the feed context bar; (5b) on Android, the existing saved-places screen route; (6) proposed: the Notifications settings caption that names the place briefings follow; (7) the one-time notice on Today after a claim or a join (\"Today now uses 2418 NE Larkspur Loop. Mom's house is still saved.\" / \"Today now uses 2418 NE Larkspur Loop because you joined this household.\"), which Today owns and this screen does not draw; its \"Your places\" link opens this list. When the person arrives from the Today chip, scroll the row Today uses into view once, fade its highlight and move accessibility focus to it. When the person arrives from Today's claim or join notice, do the same for the home row. Where each action leads: Open goes to that place's place file. Claim this address opens the existing claim flow, which ends on the claim receipt. + Add a place opens the Add a place sheet, which returns here with the new row highlighted once. After Remove, Today stops using that address the next time it is viewed, with no delay; a removed address still showing on Today would read as a privacy failure.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Jordan Lee moved from Portland on Fri 9 Oct and saved 1107 NE Birchfield Ct on Sat 10 Oct, when he made his account. Over the next four days he saved four more addresses, and on Wed 14 Oct he chose Birchfield for Today. On Mon 19 Oct at 6:10 PM, Today shows Birchfield, and he taps the chip to check that Today isn't using Mom's house, his newest save.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: See every place you saved, see which one Today uses and why, and switch, claim or remove it.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: The eye lands first on the top row, which carries the only \"Used for Today\" badge, then on the sentence directly under it that says why, then on the other rows, which carry no badge. The one primary action is \"+ Add a place\" at the foot of the list. Row actions live in each row's menu.\n\nCONTENT (Jordan, Mon 19 Oct, except where marked):\nTitle \"Your places\". With no claimed home, the ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\" sits directly under the title. It replaces the retired line \"Only you can see these.\"\nEach row: label · city, state and ZIP · \"Saved <weekday date>\". The row Today uses always comes first, then the rest, newest first:\n- 1107 NE Birchfield Ct · Camas, WA 98607 · Saved Sat 10 Oct · badge \"Used for Today\". Directly under it: \"Today uses this place because you chose it.\"\n- Mom's house · Camas, WA 98607 · Saved Wed 14 Oct\n- Grandma and Grandpa's lake house on Lacamas Shores Drive · Camas, WA 98607 · Saved Tue 13 Oct (the worst-case label)\n- The Blairmont rental · Vancouver, WA 98683 · Saved Mon 12 Oct\n- Sister's apartment · Portland, OR 97214 · Saved Sun 11 Oct\nFoot row: \"+ Add a place\".\nRow menu, in this order: Open · Use for Today · Claim this address · Remove. The row Today already uses leaves out Use for Today.\nSingle place (Jordan on Sat 10 Oct): only the Birchfield row, with \"Today uses the address you saved most recently.\"\nSwitching: after Use for Today on Mom's house, the badge moves to that row, the row moves to the top, the sentence reads \"Today uses this place because you chose it.\" and the status line reads \"Today now uses Mom's house.\"\nRemoving the chosen place clears the choice, so Today falls back to the newest save: \"Removed \\\"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\\\" · Today now uses Mom's house · Undo\", and Mom's house takes the badge with \"Today uses the address you saved most recently.\" Undo puts the row back in place and, because it was the Today place, moves the badge back and restores the choice, announcing \"Today uses 1107 NE Birchfield Ct again.\"\nToday uses something not on this list (a recent viewing location, or a pin set in Notifications settings): no row carries a badge. One sentence under the header names the source: \"Today is using Downtown Camas, WA, a location you viewed recently. Choose Use for Today on a place to switch.\" or \"Today is using a location pinned in Notifications settings: Downtown Camas, WA.\"\nClaimed home (Maya, HOME A, Tue 1 Sep, arriving from Today's claim notice): the home row first: 2418 NE Larkspur Loop · Vancouver, WA 98684, with the home glyph, the ScopeChip \"Your household\" and the \"Used for Today\" badge. Its caption slot reads \"Claimed Tue 1 Sep\", and the sentence under the row reads \"Today uses your home because you claimed it.\" Then a section label \"Saved places\" carrying \"Saved place · Only you\", then Mom's house · Camas, WA 98607 · Saved Sat 29 Aug, and Sam's old apartment · Vancouver, WA 98661 · Saved Sat 15 Aug. In the menu on a saved row, Use for Today is disabled with the reason \"Today uses your claimed home.\"\nJust claimed (Jordan, hypothetical claim on Mon 19 Oct): one home row for 1107 NE Birchfield Ct (home glyph, \"Your household\", \"Used for Today\", caption \"Claimed Mon 19 Oct\", sentence \"Today uses your home because you claimed it.\"), then \"Saved places\" and his four saved rows. There is no Birchfield saved row.\nJust joined (Sam Ortega, HOME A member, Wed 2 Sep, arriving from Today's join notice): the home row with caption \"Joined Wed 2 Sep\" and the sentence \"Today uses your home because you joined this household.\" Under \"Saved places\": Old apartment · Vancouver, WA 98661 · Saved Sat 22 Aug.\nBanner slot on this screen shows only two lines, one at a time: the sync-merge line \"Synced 3 items from your other device · Review\" and the account-switch line \"You switched accounts. These places belong to this account. · Close\".\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION: Draw a plain vertical list. Exactly one row carries a filled \"Used for Today\" pill: primary.50 fill, primary.700 label, and a leading 12pt check glyph. Every other row carries nothing: one badge slot, one menu button, no chips, no status pills, no radio column. Put the precedence sentence (bodySmall, text.secondary) directly under the badged row, never in the page header, so the explanation sits beside the thing it explains. The one exception is the not-on-this-list state: its sentence sits under the header because no row is used. Scope placement: with no claimed home, the ScopeChip sits under the title. When the list contains a claimed home, the title carries no ScopeChip. The home row carries \"Your household\", and the section label \"Saved places\" above the saved rows carries \"Saved place · Only you\", with the same expand behaviour. Draw a claimed row as a home, not as a disabled saved place: the home glyph (the home pillar token, used only as an icon), the \"Your household\" ScopeChip, the badge, and the plain caption. The home row has no menu button; tapping it opens the place file. Arrival highlight: the target row gets a primary.50 fill that fades to surface.base once. When the service cannot say which place Today uses, draw no badge and put an InlineErrorRow in the sentence slot. The row menu is a popover on web-1440, a bottom sheet with Close on web-390, a pull-down menu from the row's More button on iOS (Remove in the destructive style), and the existing overflow menu sheet with Close on Android. Menus never stack on another sheet. Banner slot: the LandingBannerSlot sits above the title. These two lines rank below invite, reissue and claim receipt: if the V7 claim-receipt banner is pending, it wins and no other line shows. The account-switch line ranks between sync merge and setup. Never two banners.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS: Tapping a row opens it. The More button (44pt / 48dp / 44px) opens the menu. Use for Today: the row shows the inline line \"Changing the place Today uses…\" only if the change takes 1s or longer; on success the badge cross-fades to that row, the row moves to the top (max 300ms), and one light haptic tick plays. Nothing else has a haptic. Remove collapses the row in place to an InlineUndo (max 300ms height change), and the badge cross-fades to the next row in the same frame. Undo stays until the person leaves the screen; there is no timer and no confirm dialog. This replaces Android's current 4-second snackbar. Undo restores the row in place, and if it was the Today place it moves the badge back and restores the choice. If removal fails, the row comes back with an InlineErrorRow in its slot. Tapping a saved-place ScopeChip (hit area 44pt / 48dp / 44px, because it opens the control) expands one explanation in place: \"Only you will see saved places. To share this address with the people you live with, use Claim this address.\" plus a text button \"Claim this address\" for the place Today uses. Tapping the \"Your household\" chip on a home row expands \"Everyone in your household sees this home.\" with no button. Claiming an address clears any Use for Today choice, so the home is used and the home sentence stays true. Account-switch Close dismisses the line. Sync-merge Review opens the synced items. With Reduce Motion on, every change is a cross-fade and the arrival highlight is shown static. There are no swipe-only actions: every row action is also a menu item.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: ScopeChip (saved-place variant under the title or on the \"Saved places\" section label, expandable; \"Your household\" variant on home rows, expandable) · InlineUndo (removed-row variant, with the consequence in the same line) · WarmingSkeleton (row skeleton with the badge slot reserved) · OfflineNotice with FreshnessLine (offline variant) · InlineErrorRow (load failed; Use for Today failed; remove failed) · LandingBannerSlot (V6 sync merge exactly; proposed account-switch variant with trailing action Close, in the V5 pattern; V7 claim receipt when pending).\n\nACCESSIBILITY: Reading order: banner, title, scope chip, the Today row, the precedence sentence, the other rows, + Add a place. Each row is one element, for example: \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas, Washington 98607. Saved Saturday 10 October. Used for Today.\" The Today row's custom actions are Open, Claim this address and Remove; every other saved row's are Open, Use for Today, Claim this address and Remove. The More button reads \"More for 1107 NE Birchfield Ct\". The ScopeChip is spoken \"Visible to only you\" or \"Visible to your household\". The badge is a word, never only a colour, and the home glyph is carried by its shape. A disabled Use for Today stays focusable and reads its reason. Retry buttons are spoken \"Retry loading your places\", \"Retry removing Mom's house\" and \"Retry changing the place Today uses\". Removed rows, the saving line, the status line, the Undo announcement and every banner line are role=status. On arrival from Today, focus moves to the highlighted row. Targets are 44pt / 48dp / 44px with 8dp gaps. At AX5, label, city and saved date stack on separate lines, the badge moves under the label, and labels wrap and are never ellipsised.\n\nCOPY: \"Your places\" · \"Saved place · Only you\" · \"Your household\" · \"Saved places\" · \"Used for Today\" · \"Today uses the address you saved most recently.\" · \"Today uses this place because you chose it.\" · \"Today uses your home because you claimed it.\" · \"Today uses your home because you joined this household.\" · \"Claimed Tue 1 Sep\" · \"Claimed Mon 19 Oct\" · \"Joined Wed 2 Sep\" · \"Today uses your claimed home.\" (reason under a disabled Use for Today) · \"Today is using Downtown Camas, WA, a location you viewed recently. Choose Use for Today on a place to switch.\" · \"Today is using a location pinned in Notifications settings: Downtown Camas, WA.\" · \"Open\" · \"Use for Today\" · \"Claim this address\" · \"Remove\" · \"More for 1107 NE Birchfield Ct\" · \"Close\" · \"+ Add a place\" · \"Changing the place Today uses…\" · \"Today now uses Mom's house.\" · \"Only you will see saved places. To share this address with the people you live with, use Claim this address.\" · \"Everyone in your household sees this home.\" · \"Removed \\\"The Blairmont rental\\\" · Undo\" · \"Removed \\\"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\\\" · Today now uses Mom's house · Undo\" · \"Today uses 1107 NE Birchfield Ct again.\" · \"Removed \\\"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\\\" · Today will ask for a place · Undo\" · \"We couldn't remove Mom's house · Retry\" · \"We couldn't change the place Today uses · Retry\" · \"We couldn't load your places · Retry\" · Empty state: \"No places yet\" / \"Save an address and Today will show its weather, air, alerts and dates.\" / \"+ Add a place\" · \"You switched accounts. These places belong to this account. · Close\" · \"Synced 3 items from your other device · Review\" · \"You're offline · as of 6:04 PM\" · \"You're offline. You can open your places. Changes need a connection.\"\n\nEDGE CASES: The longest label wraps to three lines. With 12 places the list scrolls with no pagination, and the Today row stays first. With zero places, show the empty state. On a slow network, show skeletons only after 1s and keep the badge slot reserved. If Jordan removes his only place (Sat 10 Oct), the undo line says Today will ask for a place, and Today shows \"Today starts with a place\". A saved place outside Clark County, such as Sister's apartment, looks like any other row, with no warning. Claiming the saved address shows it once, as a home, and the saved row is gone. A claimed home plus a pin set in Notifications settings: no row is badged, and the header sentence reads \"Today is using a location pinned in Notifications settings: Downtown Camas, WA.\" When Today runs on a viewing location or a pin that is not a row, no row is badged and every saved row offers Use for Today. Offline, Open works from cache, and Use for Today, Claim and Remove are disabled with the reason. A different account on the same device resets the list and shows the account-switch line. If the claim-receipt banner is pending, the sync and account-switch lines wait.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of a chip or status on every row, draw one badge on one row — because one mark reads instantly and competing chips hide the answer.\n- Instead of a radio group, segmented control or settings picker, draw a list with a row menu — because this is a list of places, not a preference.\n- Instead of a greyed-out saved row for a claimed home, draw a home row with its glyph and \"Today uses your home because you claimed it.\" — because it is a fact, not a broken switch.\n- Instead of a separate \"Where Today gets this\" sheet, put the sentence under the badged row — because this list already answers that question.\n- Instead of \"Saved place · Only you\" over a list that holds a home, put each scope on its own section — because the home is visible to the household.\n- Instead of a \"Remove this place?\" dialog or a snackbar that times out, collapse the row to Removed · Undo — because undo that lasts is safer and faster.\n- Instead of a claim or join banner on this list, rely on Today's one-time notice and highlight the home row when its link lands here — because people with a home open Place on the place file and would never see a banner here.\n- Instead of \"home\" or \"household\" on saved rows, use \"Saved place\" — because a saved place is shared with nobody.\n\nDONE WHEN: A web person who saved a place can reach this list from the Place tab and from the Today chip. Anyone can say which place Today uses and why within five seconds, including when it is not on the list. Removing the Today place visibly moves the badge in the same frame, and Undo moves it back. After claiming, the address appears once, as a home, with no duplicate saved row (flow-06 step 9). No sentence claims more than the resolver guarantees. Every frame reads correctly in greyscale and at AX5. The recovery and error frames get the same polish as the default.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f1-your-places · ios · 01-multi-place · light — Jordan's five rows, Birchfield badged with \"because you chose it\", chip under the title, + Add a place.\n2. f1-your-places · web-1440 · 01-multi-place · light — same rows inside the Place shell with the sidebar; the menu popover is open on Mom's house.\n3. f1-your-places · android · 01-multi-place · light — same rows, Material 3 list.\n4. f1-your-places · web-390 · 01-multi-place · light — four-tab bar; the lake-house label wraps to three lines; the menu bottom sheet with Close is open on The Blairmont rental.\n5. f1-your-places · ios · 02-single-place-menu · light — Jordan on Sat 10 Oct: Birchfield only, \"saved most recently\"; pull-down menu shows Open, Claim this address and Remove (destructive).\n6. f1-your-places · android · 03-chip-expanded · light — single place; the saved-place chip expanded with its explanation and Claim this address.\n7. f1-your-places · ios · 04-home-outranks · light — Maya on Tue 1 Sep, arrived from Today's claim notice: no banner; the home row highlighted and focused, \"Claimed Tue 1 Sep\" and its sentence; \"Saved places\" label with its chip; the menu on Mom's house with Use for Today disabled and its reason.\n8. f1-your-places · android · 05-just-claimed · light — Jordan after claiming Birchfield: one home row, then his four saved rows; no Birchfield saved row.\n9. f1-your-places · web-1440 · 06-member-joined · light — Sam, arrived from Today's join notice: no banner; the home row highlighted with \"Joined Wed 2 Sep\" and its sentence; one saved row.\n10. f1-your-places · ios · 07-source-not-listed · light — Jordan's rows with no badge and the viewing-location sentence under the header.\n11. f1-your-places · ios · 08-removed-undo · light — the Birchfield undo line with its consequence; Mom's house now badged, \"saved most recently\".\n12. f1-your-places · web-390 · 09-chosen-for-today · light — Mom's house badged with \"because you chose it\" and the status line.\n13. f1-your-places · android · 10-saving-choice · light — \"Changing the place Today uses…\" on Mom's house; the badge still on Birchfield.\n14. f1-your-places · android · 11-remove-failed · light — Mom's house back in place with \"We couldn't remove Mom's house · Retry\".\n15. f1-your-places · android · 12-last-place-removed · light — \"Today will ask for a place\" undo line above the empty state.\n16. f1-your-places · ios · 13-empty · light — No places yet, + Add a place.\n17. f1-your-places · android · 14-loading · light — row skeletons with badge slots reserved.\n18. f1-your-places · ios · 15-offline · light — cached rows, FreshnessLine, disabled actions with the reason.\n19. f1-your-places · web-1440 · 16-error · light — InlineErrorRow with Retry, shell intact.\n20. f1-your-places · web-1440 · 17-account-switched · light — the account-switch line with Close above Maya's list.\n21. f1-your-places · android · 18-synced · light — the sync line with Review in the banner slot above Jordan's rows.\n22. f1-your-places · ios · 19-ax5 · light — artboard 1 content at AX5.\n23. f1-your-places · ios · 20-greyscale · light — artboard 7 in greyscale.\n24. f1-your-places · ios · 01-multi-place · dark — dark twin of artboard 1.\n25. f1-your-places · ios · 04-home-outranks · dark — dark twin of artboard 7, same section scopes.\n26. f1-your-places · web-1440 · 99-notes · light — see below.\nNotes must list: every invented string (Jordan's saves after Sat 10 Oct and his Wed 14 Oct choice; Mom's house, the lake-house label, The Blairmont rental and Sister's apartment; Maya's saved rows and their dates; Maya's Tue 1 Sep claim date; Sam's Wed 2 Sep join date and his Old apartment row; Jordan's hypothetical claim on Mon 19 Oct, since the fixture says not claimed yet; Downtown Camas, WA; the saving line; the chosen-for-today, not-on-list, claimed and joined sentences; the Undo announcement; the undo consequence lines; the remove-failed line; the household chip explanation; the account-switch line). Owned elsewhere: the one-time claim and join notices (\"Today now uses 2418 NE Larkspur Loop. Mom's house is still saved.\" and \"Today now uses 2418 NE Larkspur Loop because you joined this household.\") belong to Today, whose link opens this list. Proposed contract addition: a LandingBannerSlot account-switch variant with Close, ranked between sync merge and setup. The saved-place chip explanation is a deliberate exception to the rule that saved-place copy never says claim, because it names the action by its glossary term. Flow mapping: flow-06 step 1 = 02-single-place-menu; flow-06 step 9 = 05-just-claimed (its line \"Today always uses your home\" is replaced by \"Today uses your home because you claimed it.\"). Assumptions: claiming clears any Use for Today choice (a backend dependency); the home row has no menu. Backend dependency: Remove invalidates the Today cache at once; today both web Today mounts keep the address for 120s. Open questions: (1) Use for Today writes the same custom pin as a pin set in Notifications settings, and the resolver ranks that pin above a home; for a home owner with a pin, either the pin is cleared on claim or the home-row sentence must name the pin. Both home sentences and the disabled reason depend on this answer. (2) Which screen is the Place tab index for someone with no claimed home: Your places (the merge decision this prompt follows) or the place file, which the additions list also calls the Place tab index? (3) What user-facing name does a recent viewing location have? Omitted states: Use for Today failed uses the same InlineErrorRow as artboard 14.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for continue. Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue. Turn 3: 13-18, then wait for continue. Turn 4: 19-24, then wait for continue. Turn 5: 25-26.",
            "changeLog": [
              "Moved the one-time claimed and joined notices off this surface to Today (flows-spec flow-04 step 9); added entry point (7) from Today's notice with a once-only home-row highlight; redrew artboards 7 and 9 without a banner (review major).",
              "Removed 'always' claims: home caption now 'Claimed Tue 1 Sep', sentence 'Today uses your home because you claimed it.'; disabled reason 'Today uses your claimed home.'; added claimed home + Notifications pin edge case; open question (1) extended (review major + minor).",
              "LandingBannerSlot now uses V6 exactly with Review, account-switch line has Close and is one line, precedence stated (below invite/reissue/claim receipt; V7 wins; account-switch between sync merge and setup), proposed variant in Notes (review major + minor).",
              "Chip explanation rewritten to glossary term 'Only you will see saved places...'; household chip expansion sentence added (review minor).",
              "Added Android saved-places route (5b), Android overflow sheet with Close, Undo restore behaviour and announcement (review minor).",
              "Added named Retry spoken labels, flow-06 mapping note, backend cache-invalidation dependency (review minor)."
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "f1-add-place-sheet",
            "name": "Add a place (signed-in address search + save)",
            "platforms": [
              "web",
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": true,
            "frameCount": 20,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Add a place · f1-add-place-sheet\n\nTYPE: NEW. It is a sheet, and nothing like it exists for a signed-in person on web or Android.\n\nATTACH: (1) Today's no-place card and (2) the Your places list and its empty state, as backdrops; (3) the existing iOS save-place sheet, as a reference for sheet chrome only; (4) the Foundations board.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852: a sheet that opens at the large detent with a grabber and a visible Close, because the field is focused with the keyboard up; the dimmed host screen shows above it. Android 412x915: a Material 3 modal bottom sheet, fully expanded, with IME padding and a visible Close; it covers the tab bar. web 390x844: a full-height sheet with Close; it covers the tab bar. web 1440x900: a centred 560-wide modal with Close; the sidebar stays visible and dimmed behind it. On iOS, Android and web-390, Save and \"Only you will see this.\" are pinned directly above the keyboard, and the suggestion list scrolls between the field and the button.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: The sheet opens over Today and over the Place tab. Entry points: (1) Today's no-place card, whose button is now \"Add a place\" (it was \"Preview an address\"); (2) \"+ Add a place\" on Your places, both in the empty state and at the list foot; (3) a widget tap when there is no place (the widget reads \"Save an address to see today here\"), which opens Today with this sheet on top; (4) the place file's Address row when it is empty; (5) proposed: \"Save this address\" on the signed-in compare arrival header; (6) \"Save an address first\" in the widget how-to sheet footer: that sheet closes first and this sheet opens over Today; the two never stack. Deep link: web /app/today?add=place; iOS and Android open the Today route with an add-place parameter. All of these labels lead here. \"Preview an address\" stays only on buttons that really go to the /start preview. The sheet receives nothing pre-filled, except from the compare arrival header, where it opens on 03-selected with the address the person typed already confirmed as the AddressChip.\nOn success the sheet returns to where it was opened. From Today, the widget, or the Your places empty state (no place yet), it dismisses onto Today in its warming state, whose location row reads \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct · Saved place · Only you\". From the Your places list foot or the place file, it dismisses back to that screen with the new row highlighted once and the status line (role=status) at the top. From the compare arrival header, it dismisses back to the comparison with the status line.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Jordan Lee moved from Portland on Fri 9 Oct. On Sat 10 Oct at 6:10 PM, signed in on his iPhone with no place yet, he taps \"Add a place\" on Today and types his new address from memory, misspelled: \"1107 NE Birchfeild\". The duplicate, outside-area and chosen-place frames are Mon 19 Oct, when he already has five places, has chosen Birchfield for Today, and opens the sheet from the foot of Your places.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Type one address, save it privately, and see where it went.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: The eye lands first on the focused \"Street address\" field (caret in it, keyboard up on iOS and Android), then on the suggestion list directly beneath, then on the Save button pinned above the keyboard with \"Only you will see this.\" under it. Save is the single primary action.\n\nCONTENT:\nTitle \"Add a place\". Field label \"Street address\". Caption under the field: \"We use the address you type — no location access.\"\nTyped value: \"1107 NE Birchfeild\". Show five plain-text suggestions, ranked by distance from Camas and Vancouver, and forgiving the typo:\n- 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas, WA 98607\n- 1107 NE Birch St, Camas, WA 98607\n- 1170 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas, WA 98607\n- 1107 NW Birch Ave, Vancouver, WA 98685\n- 1107 SE Birchwood Dr, Portland, OR 97202\nAt the foot of every suggestion list: the quiet text button \"Can't find it? Enter it line by line\" (a 44pt row).\nSelected: the address appears as the AddressChip in its selected state (street, then city on the line below, with a check and a primary.700 edge) above the button. Button \"Save\". Directly under the button: \"Only you will see this.\"\nNot found: \"We couldn't find that address.\" plus the same \"Can't find it? Enter it line by line\" button. Tapping it opens four fields in the same sheet: \"Street address\" (keeps the typed text), \"City\", \"State\" (pre-filled \"WA\", editable) and \"ZIP code\".\nOutside Clark County (Mon 19 Oct): the typed and selected address is \"1402 NE 33rd Ave, Portland, OR 97232\", his old Portland address. Save stays enabled, and one line appears under the chip: \"Flood, wildfire, air and radon readings work here. Pickup days and local deadlines are on file only in Clark County, WA for now.\"\nDuplicate (Mon 19 Oct): typing \"408 NE Juniper St, Camas, WA 98607\" matches a saved place. That suggestion row reads \"Already saved as Mom's house · Wed 14 Oct\". Selecting it shows the AddressChip duplicate variant exactly: the chip, then You already saved this as “Mom’s house” · Use for Today, where Use for Today is the chip's own 44pt action. The Save button and \"Pick an address first\" are hidden. A text button \"Open it\" sits under the chip, followed by \"Only you will see this.\" If the duplicate is already the Today place, the chip action reads \"See Today\".\nSaved (from Today): the sheet dismisses onto Today, and the status line reads \"Saved privately. Today now uses 1107 NE Birchfield Ct.\"\nIf the save does not change what Today uses, the status line says which place Today still uses:\n- Chosen-place variant (Jordan on Mon 19 Oct saves 1402 NE 33rd Ave, Portland, from Your places): \"Saved privately. Today still uses 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, which you chose.\"\n- Home variant (Maya, HOME A, saves 1107 NE Birchfield Ct from Your places): \"Saved privately. Today still uses your home.\"\n- Viewing-location variant: \"Saved privately. Today still uses Downtown Camas, WA, a location you viewed recently.\"\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION: A deliberately compact sheet: one field, a plain list, one button and one scope sentence. It has no map, pin, thumbnail, reading, grade, \"what you'll get\" list, progress dots, step counter or second page, because the reading appears on Today a second later. Suggestion rows are text only, 48pt / 48dp / 44px tall, in body 16/24 text.primary; the part the person typed is in text.secondary. The not-found message, manual fields, outside-area line and duplicate chip all replace the suggestion list in place, and the sheet never changes height when a state replaces the list. While Save is disabled, the caption \"Pick an address first\" shows under it, above the scope sentence. At AX5 the sheet scrolls. On the Your places return frames, the new row sits in its newest-first position with a primary.50 highlight that fades once; the badge stays where it was.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS: Suggestions update as the person types. Show no indicator for lookups under 1s; after that, show \"Looking up addresses…\" in the list slot. Tapping a suggestion selects it and enables Save. Save shows its loading state, locks the field and clears the suggestions; the selected AddressChip stays. On success the sheet dismisses with the platform transition, and iOS and Android give one light haptic tick. Use for Today on the duplicate chip sets that place and dismisses to Today; Open it opens that place's file. Close, Android Back and web Escape discard the sheet and return focus to the button that opened it. After a save, focus moves to the status line's host (the new row, or Today's location row). With Reduce Motion on, list changes and dismissal are cross-fades and the row highlight is static.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: AddressChip (selected state; duplicate variant exactly, with its own Use for Today or See Today action) · ScopeChip (sentence form \"Only you will see this.\"; the saved-place chip on Today behind the sheet) · OfflineNotice (form-offline variant) · InlineErrorRow (save-failed variant, which keeps the value).\n\nACCESSIBILITY: The title \"Add a place\" is unique, and focus is trapped in the sheet. The field uses street-address autofill on every platform, and ZIP code uses a number keyboard. \"5 addresses found\" and each error are announced politely and tied to the field. Each suggestion row is one element that reads the full address; the duplicate row also reads \"Already saved as Mom's house\". Disabled Save stays focusable and reads \"Pick an address first\". Focus stays visible above the keyboard and the pinned button. The status line is role=status on whichever screen it lands. At AX5, the manual fields become one column and the addresses wrap. Nothing depends on colour.\n\nCOPY: \"Add a place\" · \"Close\" · \"Street address\" · \"We use the address you type — no location access.\" · \"Looking up addresses…\" · \"5 addresses found\" · \"Save\" · \"Only you will see this.\" · \"Pick an address first\" · \"We couldn't find that address.\" · \"Can't find it? Enter it line by line\" · \"City\" · \"State\" · \"ZIP code\" · \"Flood, wildfire, air and radon readings work here. Pickup days and local deadlines are on file only in Clark County, WA for now.\" · \"Already saved as Mom's house · Wed 14 Oct\" · You already saved this as “Mom’s house” · Use for Today · \"See Today\" · \"Open it\" · \"Saved privately. Today now uses 1107 NE Birchfield Ct.\" · \"Saved privately. Today still uses 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, which you chose.\" · \"Saved privately. Today still uses your home.\" · \"Saved privately. Today still uses Downtown Camas, WA, a location you viewed recently.\" · \"You're offline. We can't look up an address right now.\" · \"Saving needs a connection.\" · \"Address search isn't working right now. Enter it line by line instead.\" · \"We couldn't save that place. Your address is still here. Try again.\" · \"Try again\"\n\nEDGE CASES: For the longest address, \"12808 NE Lacamas Shores Rd, Unit 204, Camas, WA 98607\", wrap it to two lines in the list and let the chip's street line wrap. Show at most five suggestions. With zero suggestions, show the not-found frame. If the lookup service fails, show its message and open the manual fields. A line-by-line address that the map service cannot place still saves; Today then shows \"We couldn't place this address yet\". A slow save keeps the button loading and never shows a full-sheet spinner. Offline, the field and Save are disabled with reasons, and the typed text stays. If the duplicate is already the Today place, its chip action reads \"See Today\". A person who chose a place for Today keeps it, and so does anyone with a claimed home or a viewing location: the status line names what Today still uses. A place outside Clark County always saves. A Portland person entering line by line changes State from WA.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of a map, pin, preview card or reading, draw one field and a plain list — because this sheet only saves, and Today shows the reading.\n- Instead of \"Preview an address\" on buttons that open this sheet, or a link to /start inside it, write \"Add a place\" and keep the person here — because a label must predict where it goes and /start is the signed-out funnel.\n- Instead of a medium-detent sheet with the keyboard covering Save, open full height with Save pinned above the keyboard — because the person must see the button they need.\n- Instead of refusing an address outside Clark County, save it and name the layers that work there — because the preview works nationwide, and a false \"not served\" is the top complaint about address apps.\n- Instead of offering line-by-line entry only after a failure, keep the link at the foot of every list — because people reach for manual entry whenever autocomplete struggles.\n- Instead of asking someone to retype a saved or already-typed address, show the \"Already saved\" row or open pre-selected from the compare header — because we already hold it.\n- Instead of \"home\", \"claim\" or \"household\" anywhere inside the sheet, say \"place\" and \"Only you\" — because claiming is a much heavier promise than this button makes. Only the status line may name a claimed home.\n- Instead of sending every save to Today, return to the screen that opened the sheet and highlight the new row — because someone adding a sixth place is working in their list.\n\nDONE WHEN: A signed-in Android or iOS person with no place can go from Today's \"Add a place\" to Today running on the new address in one sheet, with no dead end. Someone adding from Your places sees the new row there. A typo still finds the address. A failed lookup still saves. A Portland address saves with its layer line. A duplicate or a compare-header address needs no retyping. Every status line is true for the person who sees it.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f1-add-place-sheet · ios · 01-suggestions · light — typo typed, five ranked rows, the line-by-line link, Save pinned above the keyboard, Today dimmed above.\n2. f1-add-place-sheet · web-1440 · 01-suggestions · light — centred modal over Today with the sidebar dimmed; same rows and link.\n3. f1-add-place-sheet · android · 01-suggestions · light — fully expanded sheet with IME padding; same rows and link.\n4. f1-add-place-sheet · web-390 · 01-suggestions · light — full-height sheet; same rows and link.\n5. f1-add-place-sheet · ios · 02-idle · light — empty focused field, caption, Save disabled with \"Pick an address first\" under it, scope sentence visible.\n6. f1-add-place-sheet · ios · 03-selected · light — Birchfield AddressChip selected (street, then city), Save enabled. The same frame is where the compare-header entry opens.\n7. f1-add-place-sheet · ios · 04-not-found-manual · light — the message and the four line-by-line fields open.\n8. f1-add-place-sheet · android · 05-outside-clark-county · light — Mon 19 Oct: the Portland address selected with its layer line.\n9. f1-add-place-sheet · ios · 06-duplicate · light — Mon 19 Oct: the Already saved row selected, the duplicate chip with its Use for Today action, Open it under it, scope sentence; no Save button.\n10. f1-add-place-sheet · android · 07-saving · light — button loading, field locked, suggestions cleared, the selected chip kept.\n11. f1-add-place-sheet · ios · 08-saved-onto-today · light — sheet mid-dismiss, Today behind with \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct · Saved place · Only you\" and the status line.\n12. f1-add-place-sheet · web-390 · 09-offline · light — form-offline line, field and Save disabled with reasons, typed text kept.\n13. f1-add-place-sheet · web-1440 · 10-save-error · light — InlineErrorRow, address kept.\n14. f1-add-place-sheet · android · 11-home-user-saved · light — Maya's Your places after the sheet closes: home row badged, new 1107 NE Birchfield Ct saved row highlighted, status \"Saved privately. Today still uses your home.\"\n15. f1-add-place-sheet · android · 12-chosen-place-user-saved · light — Jordan's Your places after the sheet closes: Birchfield still badged, new 1402 NE 33rd Ave row highlighted, status \"Saved privately. Today still uses 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, which you chose.\"\n16. f1-add-place-sheet · ios · 13-ax5 · light — artboard 6 at AX5, scrolling.\n17. f1-add-place-sheet · android · 14-greyscale · light — artboard 8 in greyscale.\n18. f1-add-place-sheet · ios · 01-suggestions · dark — dark twin of artboard 1.\n19. f1-add-place-sheet · ios · 04-not-found-manual · dark — dark twin of artboard 7.\n20. f1-add-place-sheet · web-1440 · 99-notes · light — see below.\nNotes must list: every invented string (the four other suggestions; the Portland address 1402 NE 33rd Ave, Portland, OR 97232; 408 NE Juniper St and Mom's house saved Wed 14 Oct; Maya's Birchfield save; the longest address; the layer line; every status line; Downtown Camas, WA; the State default \"WA\"; \"5 addresses found\"; \"We couldn't place this address yet\"). Date deltas: the default frames are Sat 10 Oct, not the fixture TODAY; this sheet draws the in-app path to the same Sat 10 Oct save that f1-email-verify-handoff draws through /start. Deliberate departures: the design doc's Today empty-state button \"Preview an address\" → /start becomes \"Add a place\" when it opens this sheet, so f1-today-tab frame 1 must say \"Add a place\"; the inventory's privacy line \"A private bookmark for your account. Nobody else can see it.\" is replaced by the contract sentence \"Only you will see this.\"; the inventory routed a successful save through f1-save-confirmation 03-saved, and this sheet instead reuses that screen's saved sentence as a status line on the screen it returns to; the date on a duplicate appears only in the suggestion row, not in the chip. Assumptions: State defaults to WA and stays editable; line-by-line entries save without a map match and Today shows \"We couldn't place this address yet\" (backend dependency); the native deep-link scheme for the add-place parameter; the compare-header entry returns to the comparison. Omitted states: slow lookup (\"Looking up addresses…\" in the list slot); lookup-service failure (uses the not-found layout with its own line); duplicate that is already the Today place (chip action See Today); the viewing-location status line; the compare-header pre-selected entry (same as artboard 6).\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for continue. Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue. Turn 3: 13-18, then wait for continue. Turn 4: 19-20.",
            "changeLog": [
              "Compare-header entry now opens on 03-selected with the typed address pre-confirmed (P2, house style AVOID retyping) (review major).",
              "Success returns to the opening screen: Today for no-place entries, Your places/place file with the new row highlighted otherwise; artboards 14 and 15 redrawn over Your places; ONE JOB updated (review major).",
              "AddressChip duplicate variant used exactly with its own Use for Today / See Today action; Save hidden; Open it under chip; date only on suggestion row; COPY and artboard 9 updated (review major).",
              "Widget how-to sheet closes before this opens; deep link /app/today?add=place added (review minor).",
              "Platform backdrop rules fixed per platform (sidebar dimmed on 1440, dimmed Today above iOS sheet, sheet covers tab bar on Android/web-390); selected chip is two lines (review minor).",
              "Added /start rule to INSTEAD OF (merged with the label line to stay at 8); State editable with WA default as assumption; unplaceable manual address edge case and 'We couldn't place this address yet'; slow lookup listed as omitted; save-confirmation routing departure listed (review minor)."
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "f1-save-confirmation",
            "name": "Saved — Today now uses this address",
            "platforms": [
              "web",
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": false,
            "frameCount": 21,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Saved — Today now uses this address · f1-save-confirmation\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Keep this address handy\", the pending-place confirmation. This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed. On web it becomes the success state of the save at /app/place?preview=<id>, inside the Place shell, not a separate page. On iOS and Android it stays the route it already is.\n\nATTACH: (1) the current \"Keep this address handy\" screen on iOS and Android; (2) a web capture of it at 1440 and 390; (3) the /start sticky save bar reading \"Keep this address handy\", for continuity; (4) Today's location row with the \"Saved place · Only you\" chip; (5) the Foundations board.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852 · Android 412x915 · web 1440x900 (Place shell with the sidebar, content column 560 wide) · web 390x844 (four-tab bar).\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Place tab, the save moment just before Today. Entry points: (1) /start → \"Keep this address handy\" → sign in → the save runs at once → 02-saving (only if it takes 1s or longer) → 03-saved. Register goes through f1-email-verify-handoff instead. The native launch funnel works the same way. (2) The email confirmation page (f1-email-verify-handoff): confirming by code or by link, on any device, goes straight to 03-saved while the address is held or saved, and 03-saved announces \"Email confirmed.\" once as a status line above its title. It never lands on the pre-save Save button or on a sign-in page. (3) 01-pre-save appears only when someone opens a preview link at /app/place?preview=<id> without having tapped \"Keep this address handy\". (4) The Add a place sheet does not open this screen: it reuses this screen's saved sentence as its status line. (5) 04a appears when the server still holds the address but the save did not run (for example /app/place opened without a working preview id). 04b appears when nothing is held, including a confirmation link opened after the hold ended in the held fallback. (6) 07 appears when the device is signed in to a different account from the one the address was started under. The previous step hands over the address the server holds, which is never only this device's storage, together with the account it was started under. Where each action leads: See Today goes to Today in its warming state, with the location row \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct · Saved place · Only you\". Claim this address opens the existing claim flow. View saved places opens Your places. Use for Today on a duplicate sets that place and goes to Today. Preview it on this account opens /start with the address already in the field. Switch account signs out and returns to this link. This screen never asks for notification permission.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Jordan Lee moved from Portland on Fri 9 Oct. At 12:20 PM on Sat 10 Oct he looked up 1107 NE Birchfield Ct on his laptop and registered. At 6:10 PM he taps the confirmation link in Mail on his iPhone and arrives here in the browser (the web-390 frame). The iOS and Android saved frames show the native launch-funnel path, where he signed in and the save ran at once, so they carry no \"Email confirmed.\" line. The outside-area and chosen-place frames are Mon 19 Oct, when he has chosen Birchfield for Today.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Say in one sentence what the save changed, then hand the person to Today.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: The eye lands first on the title \"Saved privately\" with its tick, then on the one sentence naming what changed, then on the filled \"See Today\" button, which is the single primary action.\n\nCONTENT:\nPre-save (01): title \"Keep this address handy\"; address line \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas, WA 98607\"; body \"Today and a night-before pickup reminder run on it.\"; primary \"Save\"; caption \"Only you will see this.\"\nPre-save outside Clark County (Mon 19 Oct, a preview link for 1402 NE 33rd Ave, Portland, OR 97232): the layer line under the address, \"Flood, wildfire, air and radon readings work here. Pickup days and local deadlines are on file only in Clark County, WA for now.\"; body \"Today runs on it.\"; the rest unchanged.\nSaved (03): when arriving from email confirmation, the status line \"Email confirmed.\" above the title; title \"Saved privately\" with a tick; the same address line; body \"Today now uses this address, and so will any reminders you turn on.\"; primary \"See Today\"; secondary \"Claim this address\" with the caption \"A separate step, only if you live here.\"; tertiary \"View saved places\"; caption under the stack \"Only you will see this.\" For an address outside Clark County, the layer line appears under the address here too.\nAnnounced on save: \"Saved privately. Today now uses 1107 NE Birchfield Ct.\"\nWhen the save does not change what Today uses:\n- Chosen-place variant (Jordan, Mon 19 Oct, saves the Portland address): body \"Today keeps using 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, the place you chose.\" Primary \"View saved places\"; secondary \"Claim this address\" with its caption; tertiary \"See Today\". Announced: \"Saved privately. Today still uses 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, which you chose.\"\n- Home variant (Maya, HOME A, saves 1107 NE Birchfield Ct): body \"Today keeps using your home, 2418 NE Larkspur Loop.\" Primary \"View saved places\"; secondary \"Claim this address\" with its caption (a person can hold more than one home); tertiary \"See Today\". Announced: \"Saved privately. Today still uses your home.\"\n- Viewing-location variant: body \"Today keeps using Downtown Camas, WA, a location you viewed recently.\" Actions as in the chosen-place variant.\nDuplicate: the AddressChip duplicate variant replaces the address line: You already saved this as “Mom’s house” · Use for Today. If it is already the Today place, the chip action reads \"See Today\".\nRecovery, address still held (04a): keep the pre-save title. Body \"Save the address you looked up?\" Below it, the AddressChip selectable recovery row \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas — Save it\", then a text button \"Different address\", then the caption \"Only you will see this.\"\nRecovery, nothing held (04b): keep the pre-save title. Body \"We stopped holding that address. Type it again to save it.\" Then a focused \"Street address\" field (pre-filled if this device still has the address, otherwise blank) that behaves like the Add a place field: suggestions under it and \"Can't find it? Enter it line by line\". Then the button \"Save it\" and the caption.\nStorage blocked (05, web, only when the address exists only on this device and the server holds nothing): \"We couldn't save that. Your browser blocked the storage we use to hold it. Allow site data for Pantopus, or open this link in another browser.\" with \"Try again\"; the address stays shown.\nSave failed (06, server error): an InlineErrorRow under the address, \"We couldn't save that. Try again.\" with \"Try again\"; the address stays shown and Save stays available.\nAccount switched, held fallback or preview link (07a): \"This preview was started on a different account, so we didn't save it.\" Primary \"Preview it on this account\"; text button \"Switch account\".\nAccount switched, saved at registration (07b): \"This address is saved to a different account. Switch account to see it.\" Primary \"Switch account\". The address line stays.\nOffline (08): the saved state from cache, with \"You're offline · as of 6:04 PM\". See Today and View saved places stay enabled (both open from cache). Claim is disabled, with the reason \"You're offline. Claiming needs a connection.\"\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION: A title that switches between two states, with one small still tick glyph in primary.700 at body size beside the saved title, and nothing more. Show the address once, as a single line under the title: not a card, and not repeated in the body. The layer line, when present, sits directly under the address in bodySmall text.secondary. The \"Email confirmed.\" line sits above the title in bodySmall text.secondary with no fill. Stack the actions full width in strict weight order: filled primary, outlined secondary, plain-text tertiary. \"Only you will see this.\" is a caption under the stack, never a second paragraph. The recovery and account-switched frames keep the pre-save title and swap only the body, so a lost address reads as \"pick it or type it\" rather than as an error page: no error red, no warning glyph, no illustration, and the same polish as the happy path. The held row comes first; the blank field appears only when nothing is held. When data is missing, the address line never goes blank: it falls back to a recovery frame.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS: Save swaps the title with a cross-fade of 200ms or less, and the tick appears still, with no animated check. iOS and Android give one light haptic tick on the saved state. Saving disables the actions and shows a quiet inline progress line, only if the save takes 1s or longer. \"Save it\" on the held row saves in one tap. \"Different address\" swaps the row for the field in place. With Reduce Motion on, every swap is instant.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: AddressChip (selectable recovery row; duplicate variant; always paired with the ScopeChip sentence) · ScopeChip (sentence form \"Only you will see this.\") · InlineErrorRow (save-failed variant, value kept) · OfflineNotice with FreshnessLine (offline variant).\n\nACCESSIBILITY: The saved confirmation, including \"Email confirmed.\", is role=status and is announced once without moving focus. On arrival from an email link, focus starts on the title. Reading order: status line, title, address, layer line, sentence, the actions with the Claim caption after Claim, scope caption. The tick is decorative, because the title carries the meaning. The held row is one 44pt element that reads \"Save 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas\". Buttons are 44pt / 48dp / 44px. Disabled actions stay focusable and read their reason. At AX5 the address and sentence wrap, and nothing truncates.\n\nCOPY: \"Keep this address handy\" · \"Today and a night-before pickup reminder run on it.\" · \"Today runs on it.\" · \"Save\" · \"Email confirmed.\" · \"Saved privately\" · \"Today now uses this address, and so will any reminders you turn on.\" · \"See Today\" · \"Claim this address\" · \"A separate step, only if you live here.\" · \"View saved places\" · \"Only you will see this.\" · \"Saved privately. Today now uses 1107 NE Birchfield Ct.\" · \"Today keeps using 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, the place you chose.\" · \"Saved privately. Today still uses 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, which you chose.\" · \"Today keeps using your home, 2418 NE Larkspur Loop.\" · \"Saved privately. Today still uses your home.\" · \"Today keeps using Downtown Camas, WA, a location you viewed recently.\" · You already saved this as “Mom’s house” · Use for Today · \"Save the address you looked up?\" · \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas — Save it\" · \"Different address\" · \"We stopped holding that address. Type it again to save it.\" · \"Street address\" · \"Can't find it? Enter it line by line\" · \"Save it\" · \"We couldn't save that. Your browser blocked the storage we use to hold it. Allow site data for Pantopus, or open this link in another browser.\" · \"We couldn't save that. Try again.\" · \"Try again\" · \"This preview was started on a different account, so we didn't save it.\" · \"Preview it on this account\" · \"This address is saved to a different account. Switch account to see it.\" · \"Switch account\" · \"You're offline · as of 6:04 PM\" · \"You're offline. Claiming needs a connection.\" · \"Flood, wildfire, air and radon readings work here. Pickup days and local deadlines are on file only in Clark County, WA for now.\"\n\nEDGE CASES: The longest address, \"12808 NE Lacamas Shores Rd, Unit 204, Camas, WA 98607\", wraps to two lines. An address outside Clark County gets the layer line in both 01 and 03, and its pre-save body promises no pickup reminder. An address that is already saved shows the AddressChip duplicate variant with Use for Today, or See Today when it is already the Today place. If a mail app's in-app browser has no cookies, it still lands on 03-saved and never on a sign-in page. A confirmation link opened after the hold ended lands on 04b. A slow save never shows a full-page spinner. A save failure keeps the address and offers Try again. Storage blocked appears only when the address lives only on this device. A claimed-home person gets the home variant; a person who chose a place or is on a viewing location gets the matching keeps-using variant. A different signed-in account gets 07a, which visibly refuses to save, or 07b, which says the address is already saved elsewhere.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of confetti, an animated check, a full-bleed illustration or \"Congratulations\", draw one still tick and one factual sentence — because a quiet acknowledgement is what people trust.\n- Instead of \"Set up a Home\" as primary, keep See Today primary and Claim this address secondary — because Today is where the value is, and claiming is optional.\n- Instead of a second Save tap after sign-in, run the save at once — because the person already asked to keep the address.\n- Instead of a blank field when the server holds the address, draw the one-tap held row — because nobody should retype what we hold.\n- Instead of promising a pickup reminder outside Clark County, say only \"Today runs on it.\" — because pickup days aren't on file there.\n- Instead of a notification ask or a \"Turn on reminders\" button here, say only what changed — because permission is asked later, after a pickup day is confirmed.\n- Instead of dead-end error pages for recovery or account switch, keep the title and give one clear next action — because the person is one tap from done.\n- Instead of \"we didn't save it\" when the address was saved at registration, say it is saved to a different account — because every status line must be true.\n\nDONE WHEN: Someone who registered on a laptop and confirmed on a phone sees \"Email confirmed.\", \"Saved privately\" and the address, and taps See Today, with nothing to retype (flow-01 step 9). A link opened after the hold ended lands on 04b with the field, never a sign-in page. Someone who signs in never taps Save twice. The one sentence names what changed and is true for that person. There is no celebration and no permission ask. The recovery frames look like the happy path, not like errors.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f1-save-confirmation · ios · 03-saved · light — native launch-funnel path: title, tick, address, sentence, three actions, captions; no Email confirmed line.\n2. f1-save-confirmation · web-1440 · 03-saved · light — inside the Place shell with the sidebar.\n3. f1-save-confirmation · android · 03-saved · light — native launch-funnel path.\n4. f1-save-confirmation · web-390 · 03-saved · light — four-tab bar; arrived from the email link, so \"Email confirmed.\" sits above the title.\n5. f1-save-confirmation · web-1440 · 01-pre-save · light — Keep this address handy, Save; shown only for a preview link opened without tapping Keep this address handy.\n6. f1-save-confirmation · ios · 02-saving · light — actions disabled, inline progress, address intact.\n7. f1-save-confirmation · ios · 04a-recovery-held · light — the held row plus Different address.\n8. f1-save-confirmation · android · 04b-recovery-nothing-held · light — the focused blank field with its line-by-line link, plus Save it.\n9. f1-save-confirmation · web-390 · 05-storage-error · light — address only on this device: storage-blocked message with what to do, Try again, address kept.\n10. f1-save-confirmation · android · 06-save-failed · light — InlineErrorRow under the address, Save still available.\n11. f1-save-confirmation · web-1440 · 07a-account-switched-held · light — refuses to save; Preview it on this account, Switch account.\n12. f1-save-confirmation · web-390 · 07b-account-switched-saved · light — \"This address is saved to a different account. Switch account to see it.\" with Switch account.\n13. f1-save-confirmation · ios · 08-offline · light — cached saved state; See Today and View saved places live; Claim disabled with its reason.\n14. f1-save-confirmation · android · 09-home-user-saved · light — Maya's variant.\n15. f1-save-confirmation · web-390 · 10-outside-area-pre-save · light — Portland address, layer line, \"Today runs on it.\"\n16. f1-save-confirmation · ios · 11-chosen-place-saved · light — Portland saved, layer line, \"Today keeps using 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, the place you chose.\", View saved places primary.\n17. f1-save-confirmation · ios · 12-ax5 · light — artboard 1 at AX5.\n18. f1-save-confirmation · android · 13-greyscale · light — artboard 3 in greyscale.\n19. f1-save-confirmation · ios · 03-saved · dark — dark twin of artboard 1.\n20. f1-save-confirmation · ios · 04a-recovery-held · dark — dark twin of artboard 7.\n21. f1-save-confirmation · web-1440 · 99-notes · light — see below.\nNotes must list: every invented string (the saved body sentence, \"Today runs on it.\", the Claim caption, the recovery lines, Switch account, the 07b line, the storage fix sentence, the offline reason, every keeps-using sentence, Downtown Camas, WA, the Portland address 1402 NE 33rd Ave, Maya saving 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, the longest address). Date deltas: the default frames are Sat 10 Oct, not the fixture TODAY; artboards 15 and 16 are Mon 19 Oct. Artboards 1, 3 and 19 depict the native launch-funnel path; artboard 4 depicts the email link. Artboard 5 is illustrative: Jordan's own path tapped Keep this address handy, so he skipped it. Assumptions: storage blocked applies only when the address exists only on this device and the server holds nothing; Switch account signs out and returns to this link; Preview it on this account pre-fills /start. Omitted states: the duplicate variant (AddressChip duplicate in place of the address line); the viewing-location variant; the in-area saved frame with no layer line is artboards 1-4.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for continue. Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue. Turn 3: 13-18, then wait for continue. Turn 4: 19-21.",
            "changeLog": [
              "Added entry (5) stating when 04a and 04b appear (including an expired-hold confirmation link, flows-spec flow-01 failure branch); entry (2) now 'while the address is held or saved' (review major).",
              "Split account-switched into 07a (held fallback / preview link, refuses to save) and 07b (saved at registration: 'This address is saved to a different account. Switch account to see it.'); new artboard 12; frame count 20→21 (review major).",
              "Offline: View saved places stays enabled from cache; only Claim disabled with 'You're offline. Claiming needs a connection.' (review minor).",
              "Duplicate uses the AddressChip duplicate variant with Use for Today / See Today; COPY updated (review minor).",
              "Home variant keeps Claim with reason (a person can hold more than one home); iOS/Android saved frames noted as native launch-funnel path; Maya's Birchfield save listed as invented (review minor).",
              "Storage-blocked frame limited to an address that exists only on this device; destinations for Preview it on this account and Switch account stated (review minor)."
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "f1-email-verify-handoff",
            "name": "Email verification handoff carrying the held address",
            "platforms": [
              "web"
            ],
            "isNew": false,
            "frameCount": 16,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Email verification handoff carrying the held address · f1-email-verify-handoff. In user-facing copy, \"verify\" becomes \"confirm\", because \"verify\" is reserved for address verification.\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screens \"Check your email\" (the page shown after registering) and the email confirmation landing. These screens already exist in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshots are exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed. Wherever the host says \"verify your email\", write \"confirm your email\" instead.\n\nATTACH: (1) a web capture of the current \"Check your email\" page at 1440 and 390; (2) the current confirmation landing; (3) the /start register form, for continuity; (4) the saved state (03-saved) from the f1-save-confirmation project, if it has been drawn; (5) the Foundations board.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: Web only: 1440x900 and 390x844. These are auth-shell pages, drawn with no tab bar and no sidebar on every frame.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: The auth shell, between register and the Place tab. Entry points: (1) submitting register from /start after looking up an address and tapping \"Keep this address handy\"; at that moment the server stores the address against the new account; (2) the link in the email, often opened on another device, or in a mail app's in-app browser with no cookies. Where it leads: confirming, by code or by link, on any device, goes straight to f1-save-confirmation 03-saved. That page announces \"Email confirmed.\" once as a status line above its title. There is no separate stop on this page and no timed redirect. It never lands on the pre-save Save button or on a sign-in page. A link tapped after the hold ended (held fallback) confirms the email and lands on f1-save-confirmation 04b, with the Street address field. If a different account is signed in on the device that opens the link, the link still confirms Jordan's email (confirmation follows the link, not the session), and then: in the held fallback it goes to f1-save-confirmation 07a, which refuses to save to the signed-in account and keeps the address held for Jordan; in the saved-at-registration variant it goes to f1-save-confirmation 07b, \"This address is saved to a different account. Switch account to see it.\"\n\nWHO AND WHEN: At 12:20 PM on Sat 10 Oct, the day after moving from Portland, Jordan Lee registers on his laptop after looking up 1107 NE Birchfield Ct and lands on \"Check your email\". At 6:10 PM he taps the link in Mail on his iPhone (web-390).\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Keep the looked-up address safe across the confirm-your-email gap, and let the person finish on whichever device they are using.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: The eye lands first on the headline \"Check your email\", then on the sentence saying the address is already saved, with the address chip beneath it, then on the code field. The single primary action is \"Confirm email\".\n\nCONTENT:\nThe headline stays \"Check your email\".\nSaved at registration (the default wherever the sign-in provider allows it): under the headline, \"Saved privately. Confirm your email to keep your account.\"\nHeld until confirmation (fallback): under the headline, \"We're holding 1107 NE Birchfield Ct for you. Confirm your email to save it.\" and, under the chip and scope sentence, \"We're holding it for 7 days, until Sat 17 Oct.\"\nChip: the AddressChip held variant, \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\" with \"Camas, WA 98607\" on the line below, followed by \"Only you will see this.\"\nKept host line: \"We sent a link to jordan.lee@example.com.\"\nCode: the field label \"Or enter the code from the email\", one 6-digit input, and the button \"Confirm email\".\nResend: \"Resend the link\", with the hint beside it: \"Can't find it? Check your spam or junk folder.\" After a resend, announce once: \"Sent. You can send another link in 1 minute.\" While that minute runs, the resend control is disabled with the reason \"You can send another link soon\". Show no ticking countdown. After one minute the control re-enables quietly; nothing is announced.\nWrong code: \"That code doesn't match. Check the newest email from Pantopus, or resend the link.\"\nConfirming: while it takes 1s or longer, Confirm email shows inline progress (\"Confirming…\"); then the page becomes f1-save-confirmation 03-saved with \"Email confirmed.\" above its title.\nNo address held: the untouched original copy, with no chip and no sentence, and the code field still present.\nHold expired (held fallback only; this page revisited on an alternative timeline, Mon 19 Oct): when the address label is still known, show the AddressChip expired state exactly: sunken fill, \"We're no longer holding this address.\" and the text button \"Search again\". \"Search again\" opens the \"Street address\" field pre-filled with \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas\", with suggestions and \"Can't find it? Enter it line by line\", then the button \"Hold it again\". Only when nothing is known does a blank \"Street address\" field appear, under the line \"We stopped holding that address.\", with the same suggestions, link and button. Tapping \"Hold it again\" starts a new 7-day hold and shows the held sentence again with \"We're holding it for 7 days, until Mon 26 Oct.\" The code field stays below.\nLink expired: \"This link has expired.\" with \"Send a new link\". The chip stays, with \"We're still holding 1107 NE Birchfield Ct.\" (held fallback) or \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct is still saved to your account.\" (saved at registration).\nSend failed: saved at registration, \"We couldn't send the email just now. Your address is still saved. Try again.\"; held fallback, \"We couldn't send the email just now. We're still holding 1107 NE Birchfield Ct. Try again.\" Both with \"Try again\".\nOffline: saved at registration, \"You're offline. Your address is still saved. Enter the code when you're back online.\"; held fallback, \"You're offline. We're still holding 1107 NE Birchfield Ct. Enter the code when you're back online.\"\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION: Keep the host layout. Add only these, in this order under the headline: the status sentence, the AddressChip, the scope sentence, then (held fallback only) the hold-length line. The existing \"We sent a link…\" line follows. Below it, add the code block: label, a single full-width input, and the Confirm email button. Then the resend row with the spam hint. The chip is a label only, never a map, a pin on a map, a street image or coordinates. The chip shows the street, then the city on the line below, at every width; at 390 each line may wrap further. With no address held, the chip slot collapses and leaves no gap. The hold-expired and link-expired frames use neutral styling, with no error red. Only the wrong-code and send-failed messages use the error glyph, and their text stays text.primary. Every caption is text.secondary, never text.muted.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS: Paste a full code into the one input or type it, then tap Confirm email. The link opens the same saved state on any device. Confirm email shows inline progress only if confirming takes 1s or longer; there is never a full-page spinner and never an automatic timed step. \"Search again\" swaps the expired chip for the pre-filled field in place. Page changes cross-fade in 200ms or less. With reduced motion on, changes are instant. Web has no haptics.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: AddressChip (held variant; expired state exactly, with Search again, for the hold-expired frame) · ScopeChip (sentence form \"Only you will see this.\") · InlineErrorRow (wrong code; send failed) · OfflineNotice (form-offline variant).\n\nACCESSIBILITY: On load, focus starts on the headline. Reading order: headline, status sentence, chip (read as the full address), scope sentence, hold line, mail line, code label and input, Confirm email, resend and hint. The code input is a single field with a numeric keypad and one-time-code autofill. Paste is allowed, and the field is never split into six boxes. Errors are tied to the input and announced politely. \"Confirming…\" and \"Sent. You can send another link in 1 minute.\" are announced once each; re-enabling is silent; \"Email confirmed.\" is announced once on the saved page. The disabled resend control stays focusable and reads its reason. After Search again, focus moves to the pre-filled field. The pin glyph is decorative. At 200% text and 320px reflow, the chip wraps, the code field and buttons go full width, and the email address breaks after the @. Every text passes 4.5:1 contrast. Targets are at least 44px.\n\nCOPY: \"Check your email\" · \"Saved privately. Confirm your email to keep your account.\" · \"We're holding 1107 NE Birchfield Ct for you. Confirm your email to save it.\" · \"We're holding it for 7 days, until Sat 17 Oct.\" · \"We're holding it for 7 days, until Mon 26 Oct.\" · \"Only you will see this.\" · \"We sent a link to jordan.lee@example.com.\" · \"Or enter the code from the email\" · \"Confirm email\" · \"Confirming…\" · \"Resend the link\" · \"Can't find it? Check your spam or junk folder.\" · \"Sent. You can send another link in 1 minute.\" · \"You can send another link soon\" · \"That code doesn't match. Check the newest email from Pantopus, or resend the link.\" · \"Email confirmed.\" · \"We're no longer holding this address.\" · \"Search again\" · \"We stopped holding that address.\" · \"Street address\" · \"Can't find it? Enter it line by line\" · \"Hold it again\" · \"This link has expired.\" · \"Send a new link\" · \"We're still holding 1107 NE Birchfield Ct.\" · \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct is still saved to your account.\" · \"We couldn't send the email just now. Your address is still saved. Try again.\" · \"We couldn't send the email just now. We're still holding 1107 NE Birchfield Ct. Try again.\" · \"Try again\" · \"You're offline. Your address is still saved. Enter the code when you're back online.\" · \"You're offline. We're still holding 1107 NE Birchfield Ct. Enter the code when you're back online.\"\n\nEDGE CASES: The longest email, \"jordan.lee-birchfield.household@example.com\", wraps after the @. The longest address, \"12808 NE Lacamas Shores Rd, Unit 204, Camas, WA 98607\", wraps inside the chip. After several resends, keep the same one-minute rule and the spam hint. A slow confirm shows only inline progress. An in-app browser with no cookies still lands on the saved state. A different account signed in on the phone goes to f1-save-confirmation 07a (held fallback) or 07b (saved at registration). A link tapped after the hold ended lands on f1-save-confirmation 04b. In the held fallback, the hold never lasts under 20 hours, and the page states its length and end date. When nothing was held, the frame shows no chip and no gap. Every \"still saved\" line appears only in the saved-at-registration variant; the held fallback always says \"still holding\".\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of \"Verify your email to save it\" as the default, write \"Saved privately. Confirm your email to keep your account.\" — because the save happens at registration and confirming protects only the account.\n- Instead of link-only confirmation or six separate digit boxes, add one pasteable 6-digit code input — because switching devices and spam folders stop people, and split boxes break paste and autofill.\n- Instead of a ticking \"0:47\" resend countdown, announce the wait once in words — because timers are hard to use and read aloud badly.\n- Instead of an \"Email confirmed\" stop that redirects on a timer, go straight to the saved page and announce it there — because timed changes are easy to miss with a screen reader.\n- Instead of a different message for the phone, draw one confirmed path for every device — because nothing went wrong on the phone and it must not look like recovery.\n- Instead of \"still saved\" while the address is only held, say \"still holding\" — because nothing is saved until confirmation in that variant.\n- Instead of the address buried in a paragraph, a map or a thumbnail, draw the AddressChip — because people should see what is held, as a label only.\n- Instead of a tab bar on these auth pages, keep the auth shell — because the person has not reached the app yet.\n\nDONE WHEN: Someone can register on a laptop and paste the code there, or tap the link on a phone, and either way land on \"Email confirmed.\" and \"Saved privately\" with the same address and nothing to retype (flow-01 steps 6-9). In the held fallback, the hold length and end date are stated, and an expired hold offers Search again with the address already filled. The phone path shows no hint of recovery. No line claims the address is saved while it is only held, and no line says it was not saved when it was.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f1-email-verify-handoff · web-1440 · 01-sent-saved · light — headline, saved sentence, chip, scope sentence, mail line, code field, Confirm email, resend with spam hint.\n2. f1-email-verify-handoff · web-390 · 01-sent-saved · light — chip street and city lines wrap at 390.\n3. f1-email-verify-handoff · web-1440 · 02-sent-held · light — held sentence plus \"We're holding it for 7 days, until Sat 17 Oct.\"\n4. f1-email-verify-handoff · web-390 · 03-confirmed-any-device · light — two frames side by side: this page with \"Confirming…\" on Confirm email, then f1-save-confirmation 03-saved with the \"Email confirmed.\" status line.\n5. f1-email-verify-handoff · web-1440 · 04-wrong-code · light — code kept, InlineErrorRow.\n6. f1-email-verify-handoff · web-390 · 05-resend-cooldown · light — Sent message and resend disabled with \"You can send another link soon\".\n7. f1-email-verify-handoff · web-1440 · 06-no-held-address · light — original copy, no chip, no gap.\n8. f1-email-verify-handoff · web-390 · 07-hold-expired · light — two frames side by side: the neutral expired AddressChip with Search again; then the pre-filled Street address field with suggestions, its line-by-line link and Hold it again.\n9. f1-email-verify-handoff · web-1440 · 08-link-expired · light — Send a new link, chip still present with \"We're still holding 1107 NE Birchfield Ct.\"\n10. f1-email-verify-handoff · web-390 · 09-send-error · light — held-fallback send-failed line with Try again.\n11. f1-email-verify-handoff · web-390 · 10-offline · light — saved-at-registration offline line.\n12. f1-email-verify-handoff · web-390 · 11-200pct-text · light — artboard 1 content at 200% text and 320px reflow.\n13. f1-email-verify-handoff · web-1440 · 12-greyscale · light — artboard 1 in greyscale.\n14. f1-email-verify-handoff · web-1440 · 01-sent-saved · dark — dark twin of artboard 1.\n15. f1-email-verify-handoff · web-390 · 03-confirmed-any-device · dark — dark twin of artboard 4.\n16. f1-email-verify-handoff · web-1440 · 99-notes · light — see below.\nNotes must list: every invented string (jordan.lee@example.com and the longest email; the code label and button; \"Confirming…\"; the spam hint; the cooldown lines; wrong-code, send-failed, offline, still-saved and still-holding lines; \"We stopped holding that address.\"; Hold it again; the longest address). Date deltas: Sat 10 Oct and the Sat 17 Oct hold end, not the fixture TODAY; the hold-expired frame is an alternative Mon 19 Oct timeline with a new end of Mon 26 Oct. Which frames depend on the provider allowing save at registration (1, 2, 11, 12, 13, 14) and which show the held fallback (3, 8, 9, 10). A link tapped after the hold ended lands on f1-save-confirmation 04b; the 07-hold-expired frame is the revisited Check your email page. Assumptions: a link confirms the email even when another account is signed in on that device; in the held fallback the address then stays held for Jordan. Backend dependency: the pending place must be stored on the server at register time; without it, confirming on another device loses the address. Refinements: the hold line \"We're holding it for 7 days, until Sat 17 Oct.\" extends the AddressChip held-variant string with the end date. The flow's step 8 sentence \"Saved … to your account.\" was dropped, because the saved page already says \"Saved privately\" and the flow requires the phone path to match every other device. Open question: do unconfirmed accounts expire? If they do, artboard 1 adds \"Confirm by Sat 17 Oct to keep your account and this place.\" Omitted states: saved-variant send-failed and held-variant offline (same layout as 10 and 11 with the other line); hold expired with nothing known (blank field under \"We stopped holding that address.\", same layout as the second half of artboard 8).\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for continue. Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue. Turn 3: 13-16.",
            "changeLog": [
              "Split different-account routing: held fallback → f1-save-confirmation 07a (refuses), saved at registration → 07b 'This address is saved to a different account. Switch account to see it.'; stated that the link still confirms the email (assumption in Notes) (review major).",
              "Hold-expired content now uses the AddressChip expired state exactly (sunken, 'We're no longer holding this address.', Search again) leading to the pre-filled field and Hold it again; blank field only when nothing is known; artboard 8 and COPY updated (review major).",
              "Notes frame mapping extended to (1, 2, 11, 12, 13, 14); expired-hold link lands on f1-save-confirmation 04b (review minor, flows-spec flow-01 failure).",
              "Chip shows street then city on its own line at every width (review minor, contract anatomy).",
              "Cooldown disabled reason now 'You can send another link soon'; control re-enables silently after one minute (review minor).",
              "INSTEAD OF restructured to one rule per line: merged digit boxes into the code line, split the chip and auth-shell lines (8 lines) (review minor)."
            ]
          }
        ],
