                    "evidence": "Design doc §3: \"resolveLocation ... reads UserNotificationPreferences (custom pin), UserViewingLocation, HomeOccupancy, then HomeOwner/Home\". Design doc F1: saved place is \"step 6b between recent viewing location and EMPTY_RESULT\". Inventory: \"'Use for Today' writes the existing UserNotificationPreferences custom pin, which already outranks everything in resolveLocation\". derive-proposals f1-location-source-sheet: source row \"Saved place · Only you\" / \"Your home\" / \"Pinned location\".",
                    "fix": "Add a state, with a frame or a Notes entry, where Today uses a location that is not one of these rows (a pinned or recent viewing location). In that state no row gets a badge, and a sentence under the header names the source. Also state what happens to an existing pin at claim time (it is cleared, or the precedence sentence changes) so that 'A home you've claimed always wins' stays true."
