        "prompts": [
          {
            "id": "f4-today-pickup-card",
            "name": "Tomorrow's pickup card (push landing + confirm/correct)",
            "platforms": [
              "web",
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": true,
            "frameCount": 29,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Tomorrow's pickup card · f4-today-pickup-card\n\nTYPE: NEW card placed inside the existing designed screen \"Today\". This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed: add this card, its states and its notification artwork.\n\nATTACH: Today on iOS 393, Android 412, web 390 and web 1440, showing the location row, the 14-day strip card and the briefing card below it, in both the \"Your household\" and the \"Saved place · Only you\" versions. Also attach the Foundations board from prompt 00.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852 (primary). Android 412x915. Web 390x844 and 1440x900. Draw the notification tray at true truncation on iOS 393 and Android 412. Frame 8 also shows the card at 320pt width.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE\nToday tab → Today. The card's slot is directly above the FourteenDayStrip card. It shows whenever tomorrow has a pickup, whether notifications are on or off. It is the in-app version of the push, so someone who never allowed notifications still gets the full job.\nEntry points:\n- Opening Today. This entry always works.\n- The night-before push, which comes inside the evening briefing at the person's chosen time (6:00 PM here). It opens pantopus://today?section=pickup (web: /app/today?section=pickup). Today pins the card under the location row and highlights it once. If Today is already open, no banner appears; the card just highlights.\n- The tray action \"That's My Day\". It confirms in the background without opening the app and rewrites the widget snapshot.\n- A tap on the widget hero. It opens pantopus://today?src=widget&section=pickup and lands the same way.\n- The place file's Pickup day row.\n- The 14-day strip's tonight cell. The strip is one adjustable element that scrolls to this card.\nHand-offs:\n- \"Change pickup day\" opens the DateSheet in pickup mode, with Tuesday pre-filled. Recycling is never inferred from the garbage day. Saving returns the person to this card. If the saved day is still tomorrow, the card shows confirmed-just-now. If it is not, the card shrinks to one status row (frame 13) with InlineUndo. That row stays until the person leaves Today; after that the card slot is empty until the night before the new day, and the FourteenDayStrip shows the tick on the new day.\n- When the saved day differs from the city's, the DateSheet offers one optional step, \"Also tell us the city's schedule looks wrong\". That report feeds the honesty count. The report status then rides on the card for the person's own day (frames 14 and 15).\n- Tapping the SourceCaption row opens the ProvenanceSheet in its schedule-fact variant. Its first action is \"Set my pickup day\", then the same optional report step.\n- The first confirm opens the reminder ask inside this card. \"Turn on reminders\" switches on the night-before row of the briefing card below, which then reads \"The night before pickup · 6:00 PM · Change\".\n- \"Show me how\" in the widget hint opens the widget how-to sheet (on Android, the pin action).\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Maya Chen at HOME A, Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM. The carts next door are already out. She opens Today to check whether tomorrow really is her day. Second person: Jordan Lee at PLACE B, his only place, in Thanksgiving week.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Say what goes out tonight and how sure we are, and let one tap turn the city's guess into this household's own pickup day.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: The eye should land on three things, in this order: (1) the headline \"Garbage tomorrow\" with its KindGlyph tile, (2) the instruction \"Bins out tonight — curbside by 6:30 AM (Waste Connections)\", (3) the hollow mark with \"City schedule, not yet confirmed\". The one decision is a pair of peer buttons, and neither is primary.\n\nCONTENT (deltas to FIXTURES)\nA city source gives only the weekday. Recycling frequency stays Not set until the household sets it.\n- Unconfirmed, HOME A: Headline \"Garbage tomorrow\". Instruction \"Bins out tonight — curbside by 6:30 AM (Waste Connections)\". SourceCaption \"○ City schedule, not yet confirmed · Waste Connections for the City of Vancouver · 2026 schedule\". Second caption \"Recycling: Not set\". Buttons \"Yes, Tuesday is right\" and \"Change pickup day\".\n- Confirmed by someone else (the full household rule): Headline \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow\". SourceCaption \"✓ Sam · Tuesday, confirmed 3 Oct 2026\". No caveat and no button pair. One text button reads \"Change pickup day\".\n- Confirmed just now: \"Yes, Tuesday is right\" confirms the weekday only. Headline stays \"Garbage tomorrow\". SourceCaption \"✓ You · Tuesday\", plus the status line \"Saved. Tuesday is your pickup day.\" At HOME A, add the scope sentence \"Everyone in this household will see this.\" One FactRow (missing variant), \"Add how often recycling goes out\", with the quiet text action \"Add\"; it opens the DateSheet in pickup mode at the frequency field. The reminder ask opens below: \"Remind you the night before? 6:00 PM\", caption \"Comes with the evening briefing\". It includes a PushCopy tray preview captioned \"This is the whole thing.\", showing \"Garbage tomorrow\" / \"Bins out tonight · Larkspur Loop\". Buttons: \"Turn on reminders\", \"Not now\" and \"No thanks\". On this frame the ask's three buttons are the only outlined button group.\n- Corrected to another day (frame 13, Mon 19 Oct): one status row, \"✓ Saved. Your pickup day is Wednesday · next pickup in 2 days · Wed 21 Oct\", then the scope sentence \"Everyone in this household will see this.\", then InlineUndo. The household is told only after Undo closes (when Maya leaves Today).\n- Reported (frame 14): On Mon 19 Oct Maya changed her pickup day to Wednesday and ticked the report step. Frame 14 is dated Tue 20 Oct, 6:10 PM. The card reads \"Garbage tomorrow\" with SourceCaption \"✓ You · Wednesday\" and \"Recycling: Not set\". Under it: the StatusLine \"You reported the city schedule · checking\" and the caption \"We'll check with Waste Connections by Mon 26 Oct\". One text button \"Change pickup day\".\n- Report resolved (frame 15): dated Tue 27 Oct, 6:10 PM, the same Wednesday card. The status slot reads either A \"Checked Mon 26 Oct · no change: Waste Connections lists Tuesday\" or B \"Corrected Mon 26 Oct: the city schedule now says Wednesday\". Draw both, stacked, labelled A and B.\n- Holiday move, PLACE B. Dated Thu 26 Nov 2026, 6:10 PM. Jordan earlier set Garbage only, weekly, Thursday.\n  - Headline \"Garbage only tomorrow — moved for Thanksgiving\".\n  - Instruction \"Bins out tonight — curbside by 6:30 AM (City of Camas)\".\n  - A struck ghost \"Thu 26 Nov\" next to \"Fri 27 Nov\".\n  - SourceCaption \"● Thanksgiving — moved to Fri 27 Nov · City of Camas 2026 calendar\", then \"✓ You · Thursday\".\n  - Footer \"Only you will see this.\"\n- Saved place, unconfirmed, PLACE B. Dated Wed 21 Oct, 6:10 PM.\n  - Headline \"Garbage tomorrow\". Instruction \"Bins out tonight — curbside by 6:30 AM (City of Camas)\".\n  - SourceCaption \"○ City schedule, not yet confirmed · City of Camas · 2026 calendar\". Second caption \"Recycling: Not set\".\n  - Buttons \"Yes, Thursday is right\" and \"Change pickup day\".\n  - Footer \"Only you will see this. No night-before pickup reminder until you set your pickup day.\"\n- No pickup rule: the card shrinks to a single FactRow, \"Set your pickup day\", with the action \"Add\".\n- Guest (frame 18): the viewer is Priya (priya@example.com), who joined HOME A as a Guest. The unconfirmed card shows no button pair. In its place is LockedActionRow (names who can act) \"Maya or Sam can change the pickup day\", with no link.\n- Worst case, HOME A, unconfirmed: Maya booked a bulk pickup for Tue 20 Oct.\n  - Headline \"Garbage and bulk pickup tomorrow\", with two KindGlyph tiles.\n  - Instruction \"Bins and bulk items out tonight — curbside by 6:30 AM (Waste Connections)\".\n  - The hollow city caption, \"Recycling: Not set\", plus \"✓ You · bulk pickup booked for Tue 20 Oct\".\n- Pushes (PushCopy). All pickup pushes, including the holiday move, are Active (iOS) / DEFAULT (Android), never Time Sensitive.\n  - Exactly one pickup push per night, sent inside the evening briefing at the person's chosen time (6:00 PM here), never as a separate reminder beside the briefing. It gets the highest relevance score. If the phone holds it for a Scheduled Summary, this card on Today is the guarantee.\n  - Unconfirmed, one place: \"Unconfirmed: pickup tomorrow\" / \"Garbage · Waste Connections schedule\" (36 characters), with the action \"That's My Day\".\n  - Unconfirmed, more than one place: \"Unconfirmed: pickup tomorrow\" / \"Garbage · city schedule · Larkspur Loop\" (39 characters), with \"That's My Day\".\n  - Confirmed, more than one place: \"Recycling + garbage tomorrow\" / \"Bins out tonight · Larkspur Loop\".\n  - Confirmed, one place: \"Recycling + garbage tomorrow\" / \"Bins out tonight · curbside by 6:30 AM\" (38 characters).\n  - Holiday move, sent Thu 26 Nov and never on Wed 25 Nov: \"Holiday move: pickup tomorrow\" / \"Moved from Thu · bins out tonight\".\n  - In the week before a holiday move (Thu 19 Nov for Jordan), the evening briefing's expanded body adds the line \"Next week: pickup moves to Fri 27 Nov for Thanksgiving\".\n  - Hidden-preview placeholder: \"Pickup reminder\". Android public version: \"Pantopus · Pickup reminder\".\n  - Show the street label only when the person has more than one place. For frames 3 and 20, assume Maya also has a second saved place.\nList every string you invent on the Notes artboard.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\nDraw one PickupCard as an emphasis card, in this order: KindGlyph tile at 42pt, then the h3 headline naming the bins, then the one-line instruction, then the SourceCaption with its ProvenanceMark at size S (plus \"Recycling: Not set\" when it applies), then any report status line, then the two peer outlined buttons side by side.\n- The mark carries provenance: hollow means the city's guess, tick means a person set it, filled means an official holiday notice. A report never changes the mark shape; the report shows only as the StatusLine.\n- The caveat words appear once, directly under the headline block. The caption may wrap, but it must never separate from the headline, because a screenshot of this card must not read as a confirmed claim.\n- For the holiday move, the new day carries the mark and the usual day is a struck ghost.\n- Frame 8 only: draw the bulk worst case at 393 and, beside it, at 320pt width. At 320 the headline, the caveat caption and both buttons still fit, and the caveat stays directly under the headline.\n- Degraded states: with no rule, the card becomes one FactRow line. With nothing tomorrow, the card is absent and the strip moves up. When stale, the content stays and the FreshnessLine states its age (\"Updated 2h ago\"). On a cold Today load, the card slot is a WarmingSkeleton (section) at its final height.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- \"Yes, Tuesday is right\" saves in place. The hollow ring changes to the tick and the caveat cross-fades to \"You · Tuesday\", in 300ms or less. Under Reduce Motion, use a plain cross-fade.\n- Play one light tick when the save succeeds (iOS light impact; Android confirm haptic). Nothing plays on the tap itself, and web has none.\n- The reminder ask appears only after the first successful confirm, and never after a failed save. Its three buttons are equal-weight outlined buttons.\n  - On iOS and Android 13+, \"Turn on reminders\" opens the system permission dialog directly. On Android 12 and below, it turns the row on with no dialog. On web, it opens the browser's dialog.\n  - If permission is already granted, \"Turn on reminders\" turns the night-before row on with no dialog.\n  - The inline ask here is the decision. The separate notification primer is not presented from this card.\n  - If the system dialog is declined, the ask is replaced by \"Pickup still shows here on Today\".\n  - On native only, a widget offer follows: \"Put today on your home screen\", with \"Show me how\". Show it at most once every 24 hours, and not at all if a widget is already placed.\n  - If reminders are already on, the confirm shows only that widget hint.\n- While the inline ask is open, the briefing card's night-before row is hidden. \"Not now\" here counts as \"Not now\" on that row, and \"No thanks\" counts as its lasting decline, so the row stays hidden. Undo brings back both. If the night-before row is already on or declined, the inline ask never opens.\n- \"Not now\" collapses the ask to InlineUndo \"No night-before briefing for now · Undo\". \"No thanks\" collapses it to InlineUndo \"No night-before briefing · You can turn it on in Notification settings under Briefings · Undo\" and is stored on the server. Date and bill reminders are not affected. Both undos stay until the person leaves Today.\n- A push arrival scrolls once, moves focus to the card, and fades a highlight. Under Reduce Motion, jump there, then fade.\n- No action is gesture-only.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: PickupCard (variants: unconfirmed, confirmed, holiday moved, no rule, bulk, T1, tray preview; states: saving, confirmed just now, error, offline, highlighted on arrival), KindGlyph (tile), ProvenanceMark (including reported), SourceCaption, ScopeChip (footer sentence form), PushCopy, NotificationAsk (card row form, inline), DateSheet (pickup mode), ProvenanceSheet (schedule fact), FactRow (missing), InlineUndo, InlineErrorRow (save failed), FreshnessLine, OfflineNotice, WarmingSkeleton (section), LockedActionRow (names who can act).\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Reading order: headline, instruction, source and mark, recycling line, report status, scope sentence, buttons.\n- The unconfirmed card reads as \"Garbage tomorrow. Bins out tonight, curbside by 6:30 AM. Waste Connections, on record, not confirmed. Recycling not set.\"\n- Spoken button labels: \"Confirm Tuesday pickup\" and \"Change pickup day, opens date sheet\". Retry is spoken as \"Retry saving pickup day\".\n- The caption row is a 44pt/48dp/44px target spoken as \"Where this fact comes from, opens sheet\". The mark alone is never a tap target.\n- All buttons are at least 44pt on iOS, 48dp on Android and 44px on web.\n- \"Saving\", \"Saved\", the report status and errors are polite live regions.\n- The struck day is also spoken: \"moved from Thursday 26 November\".\n\nCOPY: Use every string listed in CONTENT, plus the following.\n- Saving: \"Saving…\".\n- Error: \"We couldn't save your pickup day\" with \"Retry\".\n- Offline: \"You're offline · as of 6:02 PM\", with \"Confirming needs a connection.\" under the disabled buttons.\n- Stale: \"Updated 2h ago\".\n\nEDGE CASES\n- AX5: headline and captions wrap and the buttons stack full width.\n- On a night when the evening briefing is skipped (a low-signal day with no push), the card still shows exactly the same.\n- A saved place with no day set by the person never gets a push.\n- If a household member later confirms a different day, the household rule wins and the caption names who set it.\n- Pickup dates after the last published city calendar are marked \"projected\" and never confirmed.\n- On a slow network, keep the buttons live and show \"Saving…\". Show no skeleton on a warm screen.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a filled primary \"Yes\" beside a quiet text link, draw two identical outlined buttons, because confirming and correcting are both good outcomes, and favouring one skews the honesty count.\n- Instead of \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow\" from the city seed, draw \"Garbage tomorrow\" plus \"Recycling: Not set\", because the city gives only the weekday and a guessed recycling week is the exact wrong-night failure.\n- Instead of repeating \"not yet confirmed\" on every line, print it once beside the hollow mark, because repeated caveats turn into boilerplate.\n- Instead of a red or amber alert banner, draw a calm emphasis card on surface.base, because this is a weekly chore, not a warning.\n- Instead of a toast that fades while the city caveat stays, rewrite the caption in place, and keep a status row when the day moves off tomorrow, because the change must still be visible after a reload.\n- Instead of a report that disappears after sending, keep \"checking\" on the card for the person's own day until the outcome shows in place, because the loop must close where it started.\n- Instead of \"Bins out tonight.\" on the usual evening in a holiday week, move the headline and push to the moved day, because a reminder on the wrong night is false, whatever mark it carries.\n- Instead of a card that exists only behind a push, draw it on Today in every state, because notifications-off users depend on it.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- A notifications-off user can read, confirm and correct tomorrow's pickup on all three platforms.\n- After a confirm, the mark is a tick, the caveat is gone, and the widget and 14-day strip show the tick too. A correction to another day stays visible and says who will see it.\n- A filed report shows \"checking\" and later its outcome on the card for the person's own day.\n- Every push string fits within 30/40 characters, puts the caveat first, and carries no house number; there is one pickup push per night.\n- The same night-before question never shows twice on Today.\n- The holiday frame names its source and the moved day.\n- The 320pt worst case keeps the caveat under the headline.\n- All frames read correctly in greyscale.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 01-unconfirmed · light — dense default inside Today at HOME A, \"Recycling: Not set\"\n2. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 02-confirmed-by-sam · light — tick, \"Sam · Tuesday, confirmed 3 Oct 2026\"\n3. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 03-confirmed-just-now-reminder-ask · light — tick, scope sentence, recycling row, inline ask with caption and tray preview; the briefing card below shows only its morning row\n4. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 04-holiday-move · light — PLACE B, Thu 26 Nov, struck Thursday\n5. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 05-saved-place-unconfirmed · light — PLACE B, Only you, no reminder until the day is set\n6. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 06-no-pickup-day · light — single \"Set your pickup day\" row\n7. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 07-nothing-tomorrow · light — Today slice with the card absent\n8. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 08-bulk-worst-case · light — two tiles, long captions, at 393 and at 320pt side by side\n9. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 09-saving · light\n10. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 10-save-error · light — hollow mark kept, Retry\n11. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 11-offline-and-stale · light — \"Updated 2h ago\", disabled buttons\n12. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 12-notifications-denied-widget-offer · light — \"Pickup still shows here on Today\" and the widget hint\n13. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 13-corrected-to-another-day · light — one status row, household scope sentence, Undo\n14. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 14-reported-checking · light — Tue 20 Oct, Wednesday card with \"You reported the city schedule · checking\"\n15. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 15-report-resolved · light — Tue 27 Oct, outcomes A and B\n16. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 16-reminder-declined-undo · light — \"No thanks\" InlineUndo, briefing row hidden\n17. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 17-cold-load · light — WarmingSkeleton in the card slot\n18. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 18-guest-locked · light — Priya as Guest, LockedActionRow instead of the button pair\n19. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 19-arrived-from-push · light — pinned under the location row, highlight\n20. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 20-tray · light — lock screen collapsed, expanded with \"That's My Day\", unconfirmed one-place and multi-place, hidden preview, confirmed (multi-place and one-place) and holiday variants\n21. f4-today-pickup-card · android · 20-tray · light — collapsed, expanded with action, public version\n22. f4-today-pickup-card · android · 01-unconfirmed · light\n23. f4-today-pickup-card · web-390 · 01-unconfirmed · light\n24. f4-today-pickup-card · web-1440 · 01-unconfirmed · light\n25. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 21-ax5 · light — stacked buttons\n26. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 22-greyscale · light — frame 1 in greyscale\n27. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 01-unconfirmed · dark\n28. f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 04-holiday-move · dark\n29. f4-today-pickup-card · Notes — must list: every invented string; Maya's second saved place (frames 3 and 20); Priya as a Guest at HOME A (the fixture shows her invite still pending); that the one-place unconfirmed body names Waste Connections while the multi-place body uses the generic \"city schedule\" to stay within 40 characters with the street label; that \"Garbage\" replaces the brief's \"Recycling + garbage\" in unconfirmed pushes because a city seed gives only the weekday; that \"only\" is dropped from unconfirmed headlines because recycling is Not set; that \"Change pickup day\" replaces \"Not my schedule\" (verb-led label per the accessibility research), the honesty report is now the optional \"Also tell us the city's schedule looks wrong\" step, and flow-02 and the inventory entry need updating; that the DateSheet (pickup mode) needs that optional report step so the honesty count gets reports from Change pickup day; that household fan-out of a pickup-day change waits until Undo closes; that the inline ask replaces the notification primer from this card (brief onboarding #8, although flow-01 and the NotificationAsk contract show the primer); that report receipt copy (\"Reported Oct 19. We'll check it against … by Oct 26 and tell you here.\") belongs to the notification primer and provenance sheet surfaces; that web reminders assume a new web-push channel for briefings, which does not exist today, and without it web relies on this card and email; that the suppressed low-signal day is covered by the skipped-briefing edge case; that a saved-place confirm depends on a backend fix so the person's day outranks the city day, and without it the city day keeps rendering, so unconfirmed pickups must not be pushed to saved-place users until it ships\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: 1-6, then wait for continue.\nTurn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue.\nTurn 3: 13-18, then wait for continue.\nTurn 4: 19-24, then wait for continue.\nTurn 5: 25-29.",
            "changeLog": [
              "Rewrote Reported and Report-resolved as a concrete scenario: Maya moved to Wednesday on Mon 19 Oct; frame 14 dated Tue 20 Oct shows the Wednesday card with 'You reported the city schedule · checking'; frame 15 dated Tue 27 Oct shows outcomes A/B; hand-off and INSTEAD OF line updated; report never changes the mark shape (review major)",
              "Decline InlineUndo strings now say only the night-before briefing was declined and name the Briefings group; added caption 'Comes with the evening briefing' under the ask (review major; contract glossary Reminder vs Briefing)",
              "Unconfirmed one-place push body now names the authority: 'Garbage · Waste Connections schedule' (36); added multi-place body 'Garbage · city schedule · Larkspur Loop' (39); Notes explains the difference (review minor x2)",
              "Added push rules: one pickup push per night inside the evening briefing at the person's chosen time, highest relevance score, card is the guarantee under Scheduled Summary (component contract PushCopy doNot, flows-spec flow-02)",
              "Notes records the 'Not my schedule' → 'Change pickup day' rename, the report step's new home, and that flow-02 and the inventory need updating; also the DateSheet report-step dependency",
              "Guest frame now has a viewer (Priya, joined as Guest) and layout (LockedActionRow replaces the button pair); Priya listed as an assumption on Notes",
              "Added household scope sentence 'Everyone in this household will see this.' at HOME A for confirm and correction, and noted fan-out waits for Undo (research-findings, InlineUndo contract)",
              "Frame 8 now also draws the bulk worst case at 320pt (derive proposal f4-2)",
              "Added the already-granted path for 'Turn on reminders'",
              "Haptic spec corrected to one light tick (iOS light impact, Android confirm haptic), no code constants",
              "Source captions now carry as-of ('2026 schedule', '2026 calendar') per invariant 5",
              "'Set your recycling week' renamed 'Add how often recycling goes out' with quiet 'Add'; the ask stays the only outlined button group on frame 3",
              "Renumbered artboard states to follow manifest order (13-corrected … 22-greyscale)",
              "Holiday-week briefing line now given exactly: 'Next week: pickup moves to Fri 27 Nov for Thanksgiving'",
              "Saved-place footer aligned with the briefing card: 'No night-before pickup reminder until you set your pickup day.'",
              "Retry gets the spoken label 'Retry saving pickup day' (InlineErrorRow contract)",
              "Corrected-day hand-off now says the slot is empty until the night before the new day instead of 'the card is absent'"
