          {
            "id": "f1-today-air-band",
            "name": "Air quality band (and the alert landing)",
            "platforms": [
              "web",
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": false,
            "frameCount": 24,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Air quality band and alert landing · f1-today-air-band\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Today\" (its air section). This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed.\n\nATTACH: The current Today air section and the sections above and below it (weather, alerts) on iOS 393, Android 412, web 390 and web 1440. Also attach Today's location row in both the \"Your household\" and \"Saved place · Only you\" versions, and the Foundations board from prompt 00.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852 (primary). Android 412x915. Web 390x844 and 1440x900. Draw the tray at true truncation on iOS 393 and Android 412.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE\nToday tab → Today → the air section, between weather and alerts. It is always drawn, on clean-air days too.\nEntry points:\n- Scrolling Today.\n- An air alert push (iOS and Android). It opens pantopus://today?section=air, scrolls this section into view and highlights it once. The push is sent when AQI crosses the person's chosen threshold (101, 151 or 201; the default is 101), for claimed homes and saved places alike. Widening alerts to saved places never widens pickup pushes.\n- Web has no push today. The web URL /app/today?section=air exists for links and email; on web the crossing is seen in-app.\n- NOAA warning pushes land on the alerts section directly below. The same scope-chip rule applies there.\n- A tap on the widget's air hero, via ?src=widget&section=air.\n- The \"Air today\" row of the Nearby compare scale strip.\n- While a crossing is active, Today shows one row under the location row: \"Unhealthy air now · AQI 176 · See air quality\", which scrolls here (that row is drawn in the Today tab prompt).\nHand-offs:\n- Tapping the band row opens the ProvenanceSheet air variant, reading \"Preliminary reading from AirNow, observed 4:00 PM\" and \"Covers: nearest monitors\", with the report control \"This reading looks wrong\".\n- The overflow button in the air section header has one item, \"Change alert level\". It opens Notification settings at Air & weather alerts. Changing it there never touches the pickup reminder.\n\nWHO AND WHEN\n- Maya Chen at HOME A, Mon 19 Oct. She sees Good at 7:40 AM and gets a Gorge-smoke alert at 4:00 PM (AQI 118, her threshold 101). She also saved her mother's address, \"Mom's house\", 415 NE Dogwood St, Camas, WA 98607, which reads AQI 176 at the same time.\n- Jordan Lee at PLACE B, his only place, gets the first push Pantopus has ever sent him (AQI 176, his threshold 151), about an address he only saved.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Show where today's air sits on EPA's scale at a glance, and make an alert land on the crossing, and the address, that caused it.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: The eye should land on three things, in this order: (1) the value line \"AQI 118 · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups · Fine particles (PM2.5)\", (2) the band with its marker, plus the threshold rule \"Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM\", (3) EPA's health statement. The address label and ScopeChip sit above the band in alert frames. The only action is tapping the row for the source.\n\nCONTENT (deltas to FIXTURES)\nIn every frame, the first value line writes the pollutant as \"Fine particles (PM2.5)\". Any later mention in the same frame says \"PM2.5\" alone.\n- Good. Dated 7:40 AM.\n  - Value line \"AQI 42 · Good · Fine particles (PM2.5)\".\n  - Health statement \"Air quality is satisfactory, and air pollution poses little or no risk.\"\n  - SourceCaption \"● AirNow · nearest monitors · today · observed 7:00 AM\".\n- Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups alert, HOME A. Dated 4:10 PM.\n  - Address row \"2418 NE Larkspur Loop\" with ScopeChip \"Your household\".\n  - Value line \"AQI 118 · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups · Fine particles (PM2.5)\".\n  - Threshold rule at 101, labelled \"Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM\".\n  - EPA statement \"Members of sensitive groups may experience health effects. The general public is less likely to be affected.\"\n  - Sensitive groups for PM2.5: \"People with heart or lung disease, older adults, children, and people of lower socioeconomic status.\"\n  - A separate line labelled \"Pantopus note\": \"Smoke from the Gorge. Keep windows shut tonight.\" Under it, the caption \"NOAA smoke forecast · 3:00 PM\".\n  - Caption \"● AirNow · nearest monitors · today · observed 4:00 PM\".\n- Unhealthy alert, PLACE B. Jordan chose 151.\n  - Address row \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\" with \"Saved place · Only you\".\n  - Value line \"AQI 176 · Unhealthy · Fine particles (PM2.5)\", with the rule labelled \"Crossed 151 at 4:00 PM\".\n  - EPA statement \"Some members of the general public may experience health effects; members of sensitive groups may experience more serious health effects.\" Below it, the same sensitive-groups line and the Pantopus note with its caption.\n- Alert about another saved place (frame 4), Maya, dated 4:05 PM. Today opens on Mom's house instead of HOME A.\n  - Location row \"415 NE Dogwood St · Saved place · Only you\", with a 44pt text action \"Back to Larkspur Loop\".\n  - Value line \"AQI 176 · Unhealthy · Fine particles (PM2.5)\", with the rule at Maya's own level, labelled \"Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM\".\n  - The same EPA statement, sensitive-groups line, Pantopus note and caption as the PLACE B alert.\n- Still unhealthy, PLACE B. Dated 6:10 PM.\n  - Value line \"AQI 182 · Unhealthy · Fine particles (PM2.5)\", with the rule still labelled \"Crossed 151 at 4:00 PM\".\n  - Caption \"Still above your alert level. We won't send another alert until it drops below 151 and crosses again.\"\n  - Beside the frame, the delivered notification updated in place to \"Unhealthy air: AQI 182\" / \"AirNow 6:00 PM\".\n- Stale. Dated 6:10 PM: \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM today — 11 hours ago\".\n- Hazardous, worst case: \"AQI 612 · Hazardous · Fine particles (PM2.5)\". The marker is clamped at the right end of the 301+ segment and the number is printed. Statement: \"Health warning of emergency conditions: everyone is more likely to be affected.\"\n- Pushes (PushCopy, iOS and Android only). Use one separator style everywhere: \"AirNow 4:00 PM\", with no comma.\n  - Jordan, PLACE B, at 151 or above: \"Unhealthy air: AQI 176\" / \"AirNow 4:00 PM\". Time Sensitive (iOS) / HIGH (Android). He has one place, so there is no street label.\n  - Maya, HOME A, below 151: \"Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups\" / \"AQI 118 · AirNow 4:00 PM · Larkspur Loop\" (40 characters). Active / DEFAULT. She has more than one place, so her bodies carry the street label.\n  - Maya, Mom's house, at 151 or above: \"Unhealthy air: AQI 176\" / \"AirNow 4:00 PM · Dogwood St\". Time Sensitive / HIGH.\n  - NOAA warning pushes are Time Sensitive / HIGH. Only a real threshold crossing or a NOAA warning may use that level.\n  - A worsening reading updates the existing alert instead of stacking a new one.\n  - Placeholder \"Air quality alert\". Android public version \"Pantopus · Air quality alert\".\n  - Show the street label only when the person has more than one place.\nOn Notes, flag every EPA sentence (Good, Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups, Unhealthy, Hazardous) and the PM2.5 sensitive-groups line with \"verify verbatim against EPA's AQI technical document before build\", and list every string you invent.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\nDraw one AqiBand at detail size, in this order: address row with ScopeChip (alert frames only), then the value line, then the track, then the EPA statement, then the Pantopus note and its caption, then the SourceCaption. Spell out \"air quality index (AQI)\" once, in the section title. The overflow button sits in the section header, outside the row target, at 44pt/48dp/44px.\n- The track has six equal-width segments in EPA ColorVision Assist hues: Good, Moderate, Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups, Unhealthy, Very Unhealthy, Hazardous (end label 301+).\n- Put 2px surface gaps between segments and a keyline of at least 3:1 in both themes.\n- The marker is a two-tone halo marker. Its position inside its segment follows the value within that category's range.\n- The band name and number are printed in text.primary beside the marker, never on a fill. Label the segment ends 0, 51, 101, 151, 201 and 301+.\n- The threshold rule is a 1.5px text.primary line at the person's own chosen value, with its crossing time.\n- Degraded states:\n  - No reading: the same track greyed, with no marker, and \"No reading for this address right now\".\n  - Provider failed: the greyed track plus InlineErrorRow.\n  - Stale: values stay and only this row greys, with its age in words.\n  - Loading: WarmingSkeleton track outline at the final height.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- The band row (everything below the section header) is one target and opens the ProvenanceSheet.\n- An alert arrival scrolls once, moves accessibility focus to the band and fades a highlight within 300ms. Under Reduce Motion, jump there, then fade.\n- When an alert is about a saved place other than the one in view, Today opens on the alerted place; \"Back to Larkspur Loop\" returns to the usual place with a cross-fade.\n- The marker does not animate on refresh.\n- \"Change alert level\" lives in the header overflow and is also a custom accessibility action on the row.\n- No haptics.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: AqiBand (variants: detail, no reading, alert, still above threshold with no new push; states: ready, stale, offline), ScopeChip, SourceCaption (live variant), FreshnessLine (per-fact stale), InlineErrorRow (provider unreachable), OfflineNotice, WarmingSkeleton (section), ProvenanceSheet (air reading), PushCopy (air).\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Reading order: section header and overflow, address and scope, value line, band, statements, Pantopus note, source.\n- Spoken band label: \"Air quality index 118, Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups, category 3 of 6. Your alert level 101, crossed at 4 PM. AirNow, observed 4 PM.\"\n- Chart summary sentence (visible to screen readers): \"Air is in category 3 of 6 on EPA's scale.\" Follow it with a list of the six categories and their ranges.\n- The separators and printed names carry the meaning in greyscale.\n- Targets: row 44pt on iOS, 48dp on Android, 44px on web; overflow button and \"Back to Larkspur Loop\" the same, with 8dp spacing.\n\nCOPY: Use every string listed in CONTENT, plus the following.\n- Section title: \"Air quality index (AQI)\".\n- Provider failed: \"We couldn't reach AirNow just now\" with \"Retry air quality\".\n- Offline: \"You're offline · as of 6:02 PM\".\n- Alerts blocked by the phone: amber glyph, text.primary line \"Air alerts are on, but notifications are off for Pantopus\", button \"Open settings\". Draw it only when the person turned Air & weather alerts on, or changed the alert level, in Notification settings, and the phone now blocks Pantopus. A default-on setting after a decline at the phone's prompt draws nothing extra.\n- No place: \"Today starts with a place\" / \"Save an address and Today will show its weather, air, alerts and dates.\" / \"Preview an address\".\n\nEDGE CASES\n- AX5: the value line wraps above a full-width track and the category labels move into the list below.\n- Values over 500 are clamped, with the number printed.\n- A claimed home always shows \"Your household\", and a saved place always shows \"Saved place · Only you\".\n- An alert about one saved place while Today uses another: Today opens on the alerted address (frame 4) and offers the way back.\n- A long address such as \"12817 NE Fourth Plain Blvd Unit 204\" wraps above the ScopeChip; the chip moves to its own line and never truncates.\n- With no place, the section is not drawn and no alert is ever sent.\n- If notifications are denied at the phone's prompt, the band renders fully in-app, with no amber line.\n- On a slow network, keep the last reading and its age. Show a skeleton only on a cold load.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a proportional 0–500 track, draw six equal segments with a 301+ end, because proportional widths squeeze the everyday 0–100 range to about a fifth of the bar.\n- Instead of the standard EPA hues or a brand-blue ramp, draw ColorVision Assist hues with gaps and a keyline, because neighbouring standard hues fall below 3:1.\n- Instead of writing the band name on the fill, print it in text.primary beside the marker, because text on yellow or maroon fails contrast.\n- Instead of a paraphrased health line such as \"satisfactory for everyone\", print EPA's statement and put Pantopus context on its own \"Pantopus note\" line with a source, because EPA lists inaccurate cautionary statements as a reporting error.\n- Instead of a fixed 101 line, mark the threshold the person chose, because the landing must match the rule that actually fired.\n- Instead of hiding the band on a clean day or when a fetch fails, draw Good with its marker, and No reading as a greyed track, because silence and failure must look different.\n- Instead of landing an alert about Mom's house on Larkspur Loop's band, open Today on the alerted place with a way back, because the screen must agree with the push about the address.\n- Instead of a settings link for someone who declined notifications, draw nothing extra, because repeated pressure after a denial goes against platform guidance.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- The alert landing agrees with the push about the address, the threshold and the time: Jordan's 176 push has no label and lands on Birchfield Ct; Maya's 118 push says Larkspur Loop and lands on HOME A; Maya's Dogwood St push lands on Mom's house.\n- The push level matches the event: Time Sensitive only at 151 or above or for a NOAA warning.\n- Good, No reading, Stale and Offline are four visibly different pictures.\n- Every frame reads correctly in greyscale, and the marker reaches 3:1 on every segment, including maroon, in light and dark.\n- The still-unhealthy frame shows that no second push was sent and the first was updated in place.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f1-today-air-band · ios · 01-good · light — dense default at 7:40 AM inside Today\n2. f1-today-air-band · ios · 02-alert-usg-household · light — arrived from push, highlight, rule at 101\n3. f1-today-air-band · ios · 03-alert-unhealthy-saved-place · light — PLACE B, rule at 151\n4. f1-today-air-band · ios · 04-alert-other-saved-place · light — Maya lands on 415 NE Dogwood St, Saved place · Only you, \"Back to Larkspur Loop\", rule at 101\n5. f1-today-air-band · ios · 05-still-unhealthy-no-new-push · light — AQI 182, plus the same notification updated in place\n6. f1-today-air-band · ios · 06-stale · light\n7. f1-today-air-band · ios · 07-no-reading · light\n8. f1-today-air-band · ios · 08-provider-failed · light\n9. f1-today-air-band · ios · 09-offline · light\n10. f1-today-air-band · ios · 10-alerts-on-os-blocked · light — amber line with Open settings\n11. f1-today-air-band · ios · 11-no-place · light — Today starts with a place, no air section\n12. f1-today-air-band · ios · 12-hazardous-over-500 · light\n13. f1-today-air-band · ios · 13-loading · light\n14. f1-today-air-band · ios · 14-tray · light — Time Sensitive 176 (no label), Active 118 (Larkspur Loop), Time Sensitive 176 (Dogwood St), hidden preview\n15. f1-today-air-band · android · 14-tray · light — collapsed, expanded, public version\n16. f1-today-air-band · android · 02-alert-usg-household · light\n17. f1-today-air-band · web-390 · 02-alert-usg-household · light — opened from Today during an active crossing, no highlight\n18. f1-today-air-band · web-1440 · 01-good · light\n19. f1-today-air-band · ios · 15-ax5 · light — alert at AX5\n20. f1-today-air-band · ios · 16-greyscale · light — frame 2 in greyscale\n21. f1-today-air-band · ios · 01-good · dark\n22. f1-today-air-band · ios · 03-alert-unhealthy-saved-place · dark\n23. f1-today-air-band · ios · 12-hazardous-over-500 · dark — marker contrast on maroon\n24. f1-today-air-band · Notes — must list: assumptions (stale after 2 hours; PM2.5 is the dominant pollutant at 7:40 AM; Maya's saved place \"Mom's house\" at 415 NE Dogwood St, Camas, and its 176 reading; the Pantopus note source \"NOAA smoke forecast · 3:00 PM\"); every invented string; the EPA text to verify; that \"Pantopus note\" is used instead of \"From Pantopus\" because the glossary reserves \"From Pantopus\" for the curated-post chip (open naming decision); that the default threshold is 101 per the research brief and f4-notification-settings must select 101, not 151; that \"Change alert level\" is used where flow-10 says \"Turn these off\", so the flow needs updating; that the push body drops the comma in \"AirNow 4:00 PM\" to fit 40 characters; that air alert pushes on web assume a new web-push channel, which does not exist today, and without it web shows the crossing only in-app (and by email, if built); that frame 4 is the proposed answer to the open product decision of how Today switches to an alerted place other than the one in view; that the backend currently alerts only the newest saved place per user, so Mom's house is assumed to be Maya's newest, and the team must decide whether other saved places alert; that the review suggested marking 151 on frame 4 but the rule marks Maya's own level, 101; omitted states: \"OS permission denied — in-app only\" (renders identically to frames 1 and 2) and \"location source none\" (covered by frame 11)\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: 1-6, then wait for continue.\nTurn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue.\nTurn 3: 13-18, then wait for continue.\nTurn 4: 19-24.",
            "changeLog": [
              "Added frame 4 '04-alert-other-saved-place': Maya's alert about her saved place 'Mom's house' (415 NE Dogwood St, Camas) opens Today on that place with 'Back to Larkspur Loop'; push 'Unhealthy air: AQI 176' / 'AirNow 4:00 PM · Dogwood St'; Notes calls it the proposed answer to the open decision (review major, flow-10 moment of truth)",
              "Rule on frame 4 marks Maya's own level (101), not 151 as the review text suggested, to keep 'mark the threshold the person chose'; recorded on Notes",
              "Web push assumption made explicit: pushes are iOS/Android only; web-390 frame 17 is now 'opened from Today during an active crossing, no highlight'; Notes records the missing web-push channel (review major + minor)",
              "Notes records default threshold 101 and that f4-notification-settings must select 101, not 151 (flows-spec flow-10)",
              "Renamed the context line label to 'Pantopus note' because the glossary reserves 'From Pantopus'; logged as an open naming decision",
              "Pollutant gloss now plain meaning first: 'Fine particles (PM2.5)' on each frame's first value line; FIRST FIVE SECONDS updated; PM2.5-dominant-at-7:40 assumption on Notes",
              "Notes adds the backend newest-saved-place audience rule and the decision it needs",
              "Notes lists 'OS permission denied — in-app only' and 'location source none' as omitted states",
              "Amber line condition reworded so a default-on setting after an OS decline draws nothing",
              "Replaced 'Today's pinned slot' with the concrete active-crossing row 'Unhealthy air now · AQI 176 · See air quality' drawn in the Today tab prompt",
              "Still-unhealthy frame now shows the delivered notification updated in place to 'Unhealthy air: AQI 182'; long-address edge case added",
              "Renumbered artboards to follow manifest order (24 frames)"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "f4-briefing-optin-card",
            "name": "Briefing opt-in (morning + night-before, one card)",
            "platforms": [
              "web",
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": false,
            "frameCount": 29,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Briefing opt-in card · f4-briefing-optin-card\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Today\". You are adding one card. This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed. On iOS and Android this card is net-new; no briefing control exists outside Settings today. On web, this card replaces the old morning-only opt-in that sat in the home-only Place > Today detail. In that old location (frame 11 only), draw one FactRow (known variant, trailing chevron) with the label \"Briefings\" and the value \"Now on Today and in Notification settings\"; the row opens Notification settings, so home users who used the old opt-in are not stranded.\n\nATTACH:\n- Populated Today on web 390, iOS 393, Android 412 and web 1440, at HOME A and at PLACE B, with the pickup card and the first-week row visible.\n- The old web Place > Today detail with its morning opt-in.\n- The Today empty state \"Today starts with a place\".\n- The Foundations board from prompt 00.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: Web 390x844 (primary). iOS 393x852. Android 412x915. Web 1440x900.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE\nToday tab → Today, below the day's content and above the FirstWeekRow (\"Next: …\"). It shows for anyone with a place: a saved place or a claimed home. Neither owning nor verifying a home is required.\nEntry points:\n- Scrolling Today.\n- Coming back to Today after the pickup card's reminder ask.\n  - If the person said yes there, the night-before row is already collapsed to \"The night before pickup · 6:00 PM · Change\", showing the time they never chose so they can change it. The card does not re-ask or scroll.\n  - While that ask is open, the night-before row here is hidden.\n  - If the person chose \"Not now\" or \"No thanks\" there, the night-before row stays hidden, with the same meaning. The card shows only the morning row.\n- Its durable twin is Notification settings. The card's \"Notification settings\" link and each row's \"Change\" open it at Briefings.\nHand-offs: \"Yes\" on a row opens the system permission dialog directly (on web, the browser's). There is never a second primer. On grant, the row expands into time chips. A grant from either row also turns the evening briefing on (see INTERACTION).\n\nWHO AND WHEN\n- Maya Chen at HOME A, Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM, scrolling past tomorrow's pickup card. For this card, HOME A's pickup is the household rule Sam confirmed (Recycling and garbage, Tuesday).\n- Jordan Lee at PLACE B, who has only saved an address and has not set his pickup day (the City of Camas Thursday is shown hollow).\n- Maya again on her iPhone after turning briefings on in the web app (web-to-native move).\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Let anyone with a place turn on the night-before and morning briefings right here, show exactly what will arrive, and say honestly what won't.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: The eye should land on three things, in this order: (1) the top row question \"The night before pickup?\", (2) its caption \"Pickup comes with the evening briefing (6:00 PM)\" and the small tray preview under it, (3) the \"Yes\" / \"Not now\" / \"No thanks\" buttons under row 1. Each row has one decision, \"Yes\", with equal-weight declines beside it.\n\nCONTENT (deltas to FIXTURES)\nThe card has no title. It holds two list rows and one footer.\n- Row 1: \"The night before pickup?\" with the caption \"Pickup comes with the evening briefing (6:00 PM)\". In the never-asked state only, a compact PushCopy tray preview sits under the caption: \"Recycling + garbage tomorrow\" / \"Bins out tonight · curbside by 6:30 AM\", captioned \"This is the whole thing.\" Buttons: \"Yes\", \"Not now\", \"No thanks\". Chips after Yes: 5:00 PM · 6:00 PM (selected) · 7:00 PM · 8:00 PM.\n- Row 2: \"A morning heads-up?\" with the caption \"Date reminders at 7:00 AM\". Same three buttons. Chips after Yes: 6:30 AM · 7:00 AM (selected) · 7:30 AM · 8:00 AM.\n- Silence line, printed once for the whole card: \"Only when something needs you. No news means nothing's up.\"\n- Footer link: \"Notification settings\".\n- Collapsed on-rows: \"The night before pickup · 6:00 PM · Change\" and \"Morning briefing · 7:00 AM · Change\".\n- Quiet-night receipt, shown only when every check succeeded. Frame dated Wed 21 Oct, 6:10 PM: \"Checked 6:00 PM · nothing needs you tonight\". It is spoken as \"Checked at 6 PM: weather, air, alerts, your calendar. Nothing needs you tonight.\"\n- Saved place, PLACE B, no pickup day set by Jordan (city weekday only, hollow). Row 1 caption: \"Pickup is included once you set your pickup day. Until then, it only covers dates you've added.\" Trailing text action \"Set your pickup day\", which scrolls to the pickup card (or opens the DateSheet in pickup mode if the card is not on screen). The row 1 tray preview shows a date example instead: \"Tomorrow: truck rental return\" / \"Due by 10:00 AM · you added this\". Footer adds \"Briefings follow your saved place, 1107 NE Birchfield Ct.\" The caption and the text action disappear once Jordan sets his weekday, even if frequency is still Not set.\n- Declined in the card, per row: InlineUndo \"No night-before briefing · You can turn it on in Notification settings · Undo\" and \"No morning briefing · You can turn it on in Notification settings · Undo\". \"Not now\" shows \"No night-before briefing for now · Undo\" or \"No morning briefing for now · Undo\".\n- On in the app but blocked by the system: an amber glyph with the text.primary line \"Notifications are off for Pantopus\" and the button \"Open settings\". On web, the line is \"Notifications are off for Pantopus in this browser\" with \"How to turn them on\".\n- Declined at the system dialog (native): the card collapses to one text.secondary line, \"Pickup still shows here on Today · Or put it on your home screen\", with \"Show me how\". Shown once.\n- Declined at the browser dialog (web): the card collapses to one text.secondary line, \"Pickup still shows here on Today\", with no widget offer. Shown once.\n- On for web, not on this phone (iOS): \"The night before pickup · On in your browser\" and \"Turn on for this iPhone\".\n- Timezone caption \"Pacific Time\", placed beside the times. Show it only when the device is outside Pacific time.\n- FirstWeekRow on frames 3 and 4: \"Next: add one date or person →\".\nList every string you invent on the Notes artboard.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\nDraw one card on surface.base with two stacked list rows, each at least 56pt tall, night-before first.\n- Each row holds the question in body, the caption in bodySmall text.secondary, the tray preview (row 1, never-asked only) as a small inset on surface.raised, and a button row beneath.\n- Draw \"Yes\", \"Not now\" and \"No thanks\" as three equal outlined buttons, each at least 44pt/48dp/44px.\n- On grant, a row expands in place into one ChoiceChip row directly beneath it. The card grows and Today reflows below it. Do not use a modal or a separate time picker.\n- When both rows are on, each collapses to one value + Change line, night-before first. The card shrinks to about a third of its expanded height, so Today gets quieter as the person commits.\n- The amber line sits above both rows, full width, and only when a row is on and the system blocks delivery. A switch can never read on beneath an unread warning.\n- The silence line and the receipt sit at the foot of the card, above the settings link.\n- Loading: until the permission state is known, the card slot is a WarmingSkeleton (section) at the height of two rows. No row claims on or off.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- \"Yes\" opens the system dialog.\n  - If permission is already granted, \"Yes\" turns the row on and expands the chips with no dialog.\n  - On grant, the row expands its chips (under 300ms; cross-fade under Reduce Motion) and focus stays on the row.\n  - A grant from the morning row also turns the night-before row on, collapsed to \"The night before pickup · 6:00 PM · Change\", unless the night-before row was declined. A grant from the night-before row leaves the morning row asking.\n  - On Android, after a first denial the row stays with \"Yes\", which re-asks once. It collapses after the second denial, and only \"Open settings\" is offered if a row is on.\n  - On Android 12 and below, \"Yes\" turns the row on with no dialog.\n  - On iOS, \"Open settings\" opens the Pantopus notification page.\n  - On web, a browser decline collapses the card to its web line with no widget offer.\n- Tapping a chip saves at once. Show \"Saving…\", then \"Saved\" as polite live-region text on the row.\n- An expanded chip row collapses to its value + Change line when the person leaves Today.\n- \"Not now\" hides the row and never asks again on its own. \"No thanks\" records a lasting decline, stored on the server and reversible in settings. Both show the per-row InlineUndo until the person leaves Today. After that, the slot closes.\n- Once any briefing is on, the FirstWeekRow below moves on to its next step.\n- Play one light haptic tick only when a chip save succeeds (native).\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: NotificationAsk (card row form; time chips expansion; states: never asked, granted, declined, switch on but OS blocked, saving/Saved/Couldn't save; Android denied once), PushCopy (tray preview, compact), ChoiceChip (time), QuietDayReceipt (widget one-liner variant), InlineUndo (declined ask), InlineErrorRow (save failed), OfflineNotice, WarmingSkeleton (section), FactRow (known, old web location pointer), FirstWeekRow (neighbour; moves on to \"Next: add one date or person →\" once a briefing is on).\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Reading order: amber line (if present), row 1 (night before), its caption, its tray preview, its buttons or chips, row 2 (morning), its chips, silence line, receipt, settings link.\n- Each time chip has a hit target of at least 44pt / 48dp / 44px, with 8dp gaps. Chips show selection with a check and a fill, not colour alone. The focus ring must look different from selection.\n- At AX5, chips become radio rows and the three buttons stack.\n- Spoken row labels:\n  - \"Night-before briefing, off. Pickup comes with the evening briefing at 6 PM.\"\n  - \"Night-before briefing, on, 6 PM. Change.\"\n  - \"Morning briefing, off. Date reminders at 7 AM.\"\n- The tray preview is spoken as \"Example notification: Recycling and garbage tomorrow. Bins out tonight, curbside by 6:30 AM.\"\n- Spoken button labels: \"Turn on the night-before briefing\", \"Not now, night-before briefing\", \"No thanks, night-before briefing\"; \"Turn on the morning briefing\", \"Not now, morning briefing\", \"No thanks, morning briefing\". Retry is spoken as \"Retry saving briefing time\".\n- Status is announced without moving focus.\n\nCOPY: Use every string listed in CONTENT, plus the following.\n- Save error: \"We couldn't save your briefing time\" with \"Retry\". The row keeps its last saved value.\n- Offline: \"You're offline · as of 6:02 PM\", with \"Changing briefings needs a connection.\" under the disabled controls.\n- No place: the card is absent, and Today shows \"Today starts with a place\" / \"Save an address and Today will show its weather, air, alerts and dates.\" / \"Preview an address\".\n\nEDGE CASES\n- Both rows expanded at once at 390 wide: the chips wrap to two lines rather than scroll.\n- One row on and one off; both on; both declined (the card is absent).\n- A saved place without a set pickup day: the evening row still works for dates the person adds, and pickup is never promised. Air alerts are a separate setting and are not promised here.\n- The device is outside Pacific time.\n- The system permission is granted on web but not on this phone.\n- A decline in the pickup card's ask: only the morning row shows.\n- A slow save keeps the chip selected with \"Saving…\" and shows no spinner card.\n- The receipt is never shown while a check is pending or failed.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of two separate opt-in cards or a modal, draw one card with two rows that expand in place, because two competing asks create a ranking problem, and a modal trains dismissal.\n- Instead of the morning row on top, put the night-before row first, because it is the pickup trigger and the ask a person with a pickup rule needs most.\n- Instead of a primer with its own \"Yes\" or \"Allow\" before the system dialog, send \"Yes\" straight to the system dialog and show the exact notification inside the row, because a second yes is redundant and the preview is what makes the ask clear.\n- Instead of a permanent amber banner for someone who declined, collapse the card to one neutral line plus a one-time widget offer (native only), because repeated pressure after a denial goes against Android guidance.\n- Instead of a toggle that reads on while the system blocks delivery, show the amber line above the rows, because the card must match what the phone will actually deliver.\n- Instead of gating either row behind claiming or verifying a home, show both to anyone with a saved place, because turning on either briefing is how a saved-place user counts toward activation.\n- Instead of a caption promising bills, alerts or pickup to a saved place without a set day, name only what the evening briefing carries, because a saved place has no bills, air alerts are a separate setting, and pickup waits for the person's own day.\n- Instead of \"6:00pm\" and an always-on \"Pacific Time.\" caption, write \"6:00 PM\" and show the timezone only outside Pacific time, because the research brief's microcopy rules say so.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- A saved-place user can turn on either briefing from Today in two taps: \"Yes\", then the system prompt.\n- The person sees the exact notification before the system prompt.\n- What each row shows always matches the device's real permission, and nothing claims on or off before the permission is known.\n- Today never asks the night-before question twice, whether the answer came from this card or the pickup card.\n- A declined ask names the row that was declined, never reappears on its own, and can be turned on again from settings.\n- The silence line and receipt make a quiet night read as finished work.\n- Every frame reads correctly in greyscale and at AX5.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 01-never-asked · light — dense default under a populated Today at HOME A, night-before row first with its tray preview\n2. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 02-yes-time-chips · light — night-before row expanded, 6:00 PM selected\n3. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 03-one-on-one-off · light — night-before collapsed on top, morning row still asking, FirstWeekRow moved on\n4. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 04-both-on-collapsed · light — Wed 21 Oct quiet-night receipt, FirstWeekRow moved on\n5. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 05-granted-from-morning · light — morning chips expanded, night-before already collapsed to \"6:00 PM · Change\"\n6. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 06-saved-place · light — PLACE B, set-your-pickup-day caption and action, date tray preview, footer names Birchfield Ct\n7. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 07-saving · light\n8. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 08-save-error · light\n9. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 09-on-but-blocked · light — amber line above rows\n10. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 10-declined-undo · light — \"No night-before briefing · …\" InlineUndo, morning row still asking\n11. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 11-slot-closed · light — Today with the card absent, plus the old Place > Today location with its Briefings FactRow\n12. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 12-loading · light — WarmingSkeleton at two-row height\n13. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 13-no-place · light — Today starts with a place\n14. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 14-offline · light\n15. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 15-declined-at-browser · light — one neutral line, no widget offer\n16. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 16-after-pickup-decline · light — only the morning row\n17. f4-briefing-optin-card · ios · 01-never-asked · light\n18. f4-briefing-optin-card · ios · 17-declined-at-os-widget-offer · light\n19. f4-briefing-optin-card · ios · 09-on-but-blocked · light — Open settings\n20. f4-briefing-optin-card · ios · 18-this-phone-not-on · light — device set to Eastern Time; the times keep the caption \"Pacific Time\" because briefings follow the place's time zone\n21. f4-briefing-optin-card · android · 04-both-on-collapsed · light\n22. f4-briefing-optin-card · android · 09-on-but-blocked · light\n23. f4-briefing-optin-card · android · 19-denied-once-reask · light — row kept with Yes after the first denial\n24. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-1440 · 01-never-asked · light\n25. f4-briefing-optin-card · ios · 20-ax5 · light — chips as radio rows, stacked buttons\n26. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 21-greyscale · light — frame 2 in greyscale\n27. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 01-never-asked · dark\n28. f4-briefing-optin-card · web-390 · 09-on-but-blocked · dark\n29. f4-briefing-optin-card · Notes — must list: every invented string (including the saved-place caption, action and footer, the date tray preview, and the Briefings FactRow); that HOME A's pickup rule here is Sam's confirmed rule so the tray preview says \"Recycling + garbage\"; that the Briefings FactRow is drawn only if Place > Today still ships before the Today merge; that a grant from the morning row turns the evening briefing on, per the research brief's default-after-grant rule; that the quiet-night receipt is the one-line variant with a spoken check list, and the full per-provider receipt lives on Today's quiet-day state; that loading is also covered by the Today cold-load frame; that web rows assume a new web-push channel for briefings (backend plus service worker), which does not exist today, and that without it the web rows are not drawn and web relies on Today and an email trigger (flow-01 failure branch); that the \"Why didn't I get one?\" link is omitted because the receipt line here and the skipped-night row in Notification settings carry that answer; omitted states\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: 1-6, then wait for continue.\nTurn 2: 7-12, then wait for continue.\nTurn 3: 13-18, then wait for continue.\nTurn 4: 19-24, then wait for continue.\nTurn 5: 25-29.",
            "changeLog": [
              "Added the research brief's default-after-grant rule: a grant from the morning row also turns the night-before row on (collapsed, unless declined); new frame 5 '05-granted-from-morning' (review major; ux-research-brief §3)",
              "Saved-place condition now keyed to 'no pickup day set by Jordan' (not frequency); caption rewritten to 'Pickup is included once you set your pickup day. Until then, it only covers dates you've added.' with trailing 'Set your pickup day' action; caption disappears once the weekday is set (review major + minor; design doc F4/F5)",
              "Added a compact PushCopy tray preview under row 1 in the never-asked state ('Recycling + garbage tomorrow' / 'Bins out tonight · curbside by 6:30 AM', 'This is the whole thing.'), a date example for PLACE B, PushCopy in FOUNDATIONS, preview in reading order (review major; brief P6)",
              "Time chip hit targets stated as 44pt / 48dp / 44px with 8dp gaps",
              "Old-location pointer is now a FactRow (known, chevron) 'Briefings' / 'Now on Today and in Notification settings', drawn only if Place > Today survives the merge (two review findings conflicted: TextActionRow outbound vs FactRow; chose FactRow because the link is internal, not outbound)",
              "Timezone INSTEAD OF reason now cites the research brief's microcopy rules",
              "Quiet-night receipt keeps the one-liner but gets a spoken check list; Notes says the full receipt lives on Today's quiet-day state",
              "Timezone frame clarified: device on Eastern Time, times captioned 'Pacific Time'",
              "Decline InlineUndo strings are now per row (night-before / morning), for both Not now and No thanks",
              "FIRST FIVE SECONDS third item now the button row; FirstWeekRow moves on to 'Next: add one date or person →' on frames 3 and 4 and is listed as changed",
              "Added loading: WarmingSkeleton (section) at two-row height with no on/off claim; new frame 12 and a Notes entry",
              "Renumbered artboards to follow manifest order; frame count 27 → 29"
            ]
          }
