                    "evidence": "Hand-offs: 'When the saved day differs from the city's, the DateSheet offers one optional step, \"Also tell us the city's schedule looks wrong\"... this card then shows the reported state.' Also: 'If it is not, the card shrinks to one status row... after that the card is absent'. CONTENT: 'Reported: the card keeps its mark.' and 'Report resolved (frame dated Mon 26 Oct)... \"Corrected Mon 26 Oct: the city schedule now says Wednesday\"'. flows-spec flow-11 step 6: 'The pickup card updates to match.'",
                    "fix": "Rewrite the Reported and Report-resolved CONTENT bullets with a concrete scenario. (a) Reported: 'On Mon 19 Oct Maya changed her pickup day to Wednesday and ticked the report step. Frame 14 is dated Tue 20 Oct, 6:10 PM. The card reads \"Garbage tomorrow\" with \"✓ You · Wednesday\". Under it is the StatusLine \"You reported the city schedule · checking\" and the caption \"We'll check with Waste Connections by Mon 26 Oct\".' (b) Resolved: 'Frame 15 is dated Tue 27 Oct, 6:10 PM, the same Wednesday card. The slot reads A \"Checked Mon 26 Oct · no change: Waste Connections lists Tuesday\" or B \"Corrected Mon 26 Oct: the city schedule now says Wednesday\".' Then change the INSTEAD OF line to 'keep \"checking\" on the card for the person's own day until the outcome shows in place'."
