                    "issue": "The decline copy says more was turned off than really was. 'No thanks' only declines the night-before briefing row. The Undo line says 'No reminders', but date and bill reminders are a separate group that stays on. The component contract defines 'Reminder' as the notification before a date and 'Briefing' as the evening or morning push. So the person is told something false and gets sent to a Notification settings group with a different name.",
                    "evidence": "INTERACTION: '\"No thanks\" collapses it to InlineUndo \"No reminders · You can turn them on in Notification settings · Undo\"' and '\"Not now\" collapses the ask to InlineUndo \"No reminder for now · Undo\"'. Contract glossary: 'Reminder — the notification before a date', 'Briefing — the morning or evening summary push'. ux-research-brief §3 lists Briefings and 'Dates & bills' as separate groups.",
                    "fix": "Change the strings to: Not now → 'No night-before briefing for now · Undo'. No thanks → 'No night-before briefing · You can turn it on in Notification settings under Briefings · Undo'. Keep the ask 'Remind you the night before? 6:00 PM' and the 'Turn on reminders' button from the per-surface changes, but add the caption 'Comes with the evening briefing' under the ask so it matches the briefing card's row."
