      {
        "ids": [
          "f4-notification-primer",
          "f4-notification-settings",
          "f1-claim-receipt"
        ],
        "prompts": [
          {
            "id": "f4-notification-primer",
            "name": "Notification permission primer",
            "platforms": [
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": true,
            "frameCount": 17,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Notification permission primer · f4-notification-primer\n\nTYPE: NEW. Nothing like it exists in the Pantopus design system yet. Build it only from existing tokens, sheet styles and Foundations components.\n\nATTACH: The Mail tab notification list showing its push-off banner ('Push is off. You'll still see these here.'). Today on iOS and Android, showing the PickupCard (confirmed and confirmed-just-now states) and the briefing card (NotificationAsk in its card-row form). The place file (Place tab) showing its pickup row. The Date sheet on its pickup-day kind. Draw these hosts exactly as the screenshots show. Change them only where a state below says so. Where you draw the PickupCard, use the Foundations PickupCard button labels.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852: a sheet at medium detent with a grabber and a top bar with Close. It may scroll at large text sizes. Android 412x915: a Material 3 modal bottom sheet with a drag handle. Draw no web version: the web briefing card asks for browser permission itself.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: The sheet belongs to no tab. It opens over the screen where the person acted. It has no deep link, and it never opens at launch, sign-up or save. This sheet replaces the system prompt that iOS fires at cold launch today; that launch-time request is removed, so nothing asks on first launch. The primer never opens by itself. It opens only when the person taps an ask on an indirect entry.\nEntry points (the only two):\n1. Over Mail, when the person taps 'Turn on' in the push-off banner to get household updates on this phone. Never asked: the default Mail variant. iOS denied, Android denied once or Android blocked: the matching denied variant.\n2. Android only, denied once (the system says a reason should be shown): 'Turn on reminders' in the host's inline reminder ask opens the sheet in its denied-once pickup variant. The host is Today (the PickupCard) or the place file (the line under the pickup row).\nWhere it does not open:\n- After a pickup day saves in the Date sheet, the Date sheet closes first. The host then shows its own inline ask, 'Remind you the night before? 6:00 PM · Turn on reminders': on Today, the PickupCard's confirmed-just-now state; in the place file, the same line under the pickup row. On a phone never asked, tapping it opens the system dialog directly. The primer never stacks on the Date sheet and never follows the save. If the save failed, no ask appears; the card keeps its hollow mark and shows Retry.\n- iOS denied or Android blocked: the PickupCard and place file show no inline reminder ask. Only the Mail banner's 'Turn on' and the Notifications settings page lead to Open Settings.\n- Yes on the briefing card opens the system dialog directly, because the card already explains the request and a second screen would be a second 'Yes'.\nWhat it receives: the entry (Mail or pickup), the phone's permission state, and for pickup the confirmed weekday and the place's street label. What happens next: Continue opens the system dialog. After Allow, the person is back on the host. From Mail, Allow also switches Household activity on (it is off until switched on) and the banner reads 'Household updates are on · Change'. After any grant, Today's briefing card evening row reads '6:00 PM · Change', because evening is on by default after a grant; the morning row keeps asking. Focus returns to the control that opened the sheet: the Mail banner's Turn on, or the host's inline ask.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM. Maya Chen is at HOME A on her iPhone. She opens Mail and sees 'Sam marked Clark PUD paid' in the notification list under the banner 'Push is off. You'll still see these here.' She wants that kind of update on her phone and taps 'Turn on'. She has never been asked about notifications on this iPhone.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Show the exact notification the person is about to allow, then hand them to the system dialog without asking 'Yes' a second time.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: First, the title and the tray preview directly under it (the tray is the largest element). Second, the one-sentence body. Third, 'Continue' with 'Your phone will ask next.' under it. Continue is the only primary action.\n\nCONTENT (fixtures apply; these are the deltas)\nDelta: Maya also has a saved place, 'Grandma's', at 5200 SE Columbia River Dr, Vancouver. That second place is why each tray shows a street label.\nMail entry (default). Title: 'Household updates on this phone'. Body: 'Quiet updates from your household. Pickup the night before. Air alerts when it's unhealthy. Sign-in alerts for your account. Nothing else unless you turn it on.' Tray preview (PushCopy, bill paid): app name 'Pantopus', time '6:00 PM', title 'Sam marked Clark PUD paid', body 'Due Fri 23 Oct · Larkspur Loop'. Caption under the tray, line 1: 'This is the whole thing.' Line 2: 'Arrives quietly — no sound.' No amount appears on any tray.\nPickup entry (Android denied once only). Title: 'A reminder the night before pickup'. Body: 'Pickup the night before. Air alerts when it's unhealthy. Sign-in alerts for your account. Nothing else unless you turn it on.' Tray preview (PushCopy, confirmed pickup, the canonical string): title 'Recycling + garbage tomorrow' (28 characters), body 'Bins out tonight · Larkspur Loop'. Caption: 'This is the whole thing.'\nWorst case: the longest street labels, 'Due Fri 23 Oct · Columbia River Dr' and 'Bins out tonight · Columbia River Dr'. If a body does not fit, the preview truncates it at true width with a trailing ellipsis. Titles never truncate, because they stay within 30 characters.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION: Stack from top to bottom: grabber and top bar with Close (iOS) or drag handle (Android), title (h3), tray preview, caption (one or two lines), body (body 16/24), actions, caption under the button. The tray preview is the hero. Draw it at true tray proportions, inset on surface.raised over a surface.sunken well, with the platform's own notification anatomy. On iOS: rounded app icon, 'Pantopus', time, bold title, one body line. On Android: small monochrome icon, app name, a bullet, time. Frame it as an in-app illustration inside the sheet, with rounded corners and no system shadow. It must never look like a system alert or a live banner. The caveat-first rule protects honesty: an unconfirmed pickup's title is 'Unconfirmed: pickup tomorrow', so truncation can never cut the caveat. The specimen artboards prove this. If the street label is missing (one place only), drop it and keep 'Bins out tonight' or 'Due Fri 23 Oct'. Denied variants keep the same stack, replace the body with the two denied lines for that entry, and swap the actions.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\niOS default: one filled button, 'Continue', which opens the system dialog. The sheet has no 'Not now' button. Close sits in the top bar only, and swipe-down also closes. Closing does not fire the system dialog, and the sheet never reopens on its own.\niOS denied: one filled 'Open Settings' button, which opens Pantopus's notification page in iOS Settings. Close stays only in the top bar.\nAndroid default: 'Continue' and 'Not now' as peer buttons of the same height and weight. 'Not now' is this sheet's visible close: it closes the sheet and never fires the system dialog, so no denial is spent. It never re-presents the sheet on its own; the ask returns only when the person taps an ask again. Back behaves like 'Not now'. The permanent decline lives on the briefing card and in Settings.\nAndroid denied once: 'Continue' (fires the system dialog again) and 'Not now', as peers. Android blocked: 'Open Settings' (opens the Pantopus notification page) and 'Not now', as peers.\nThe sheet presents with the platform's standard sheet motion (300ms or less). Under Reduce Motion it cross-fades. The tray preview does not animate. Continue, Close, Open Settings and Not now have no haptic.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: NotificationAsk (variants primer iOS, primer Android, iOS denied, Android denied once, Android blocked; card-row form on the host). PushCopy (tray preview: bill paid, confirmed pickup, unconfirmed pickup, hidden-preview placeholders). PickupCard (host: confirmed, confirmed-just-now with the inline ask, error). NotificationRow (host: push-off banner and its granted line). OfflineNotice (queued writes). InlineErrorRow (save failed).\n\nACCESSIBILITY: Reading order: title, tray preview, caption, body, buttons, caption under the button. The tray is one element, spoken as 'Example notification: Sam marked Clark PUD paid. Due Friday 23 October, Larkspur Loop.' (pickup: 'Example notification: Recycling plus garbage tomorrow. Bins out tonight, Larkspur Loop.'). The sheet title is unique, focus stays inside the sheet, and focus returns to the control that opened it when the sheet closes. Buttons are 44pt on iOS and 48dp on Android, with 8dp between them. Button labels carry the meaning, never colour.\n\nCOPY\nButtons: 'Continue' · 'Not now' (Android only) · 'Open Settings' · 'Close' (iOS top bar only).\nCaption under Continue: 'Your phone will ask next.'\nDenied line 1 (both entries): 'Notifications are off for Pantopus on this phone.'\nDenied line 2, Mail entry: 'Household updates still show here in Mail.' Pickup entry: 'Pickup still shows on Today.'\nHost inline ask: 'Remind you the night before? 6:00 PM · Turn on reminders'.\nSave error, pickup entry: 'Couldn't save your reminder · Retry'. Save error, Mail entry: 'Couldn't turn on household updates · Retry'.\nOffline caption, Mail entry: 'You're offline. Household updates will turn on when you're back online.' Pickup entry: 'You're offline. Your reminder will save when you're back online.'\nMail banner after a grant: 'Household updates are on · Change'.\n\nEDGE CASES: Already granted: the sheet never appears. Mail 'Turn on' when the phone is already granted: no sheet; Household activity switches on in place, the banner reads 'Household updates are on · Change', and Change opens Notifications settings at /app/settings/notifications?group=household. A save that failed: no ask and no sheet. Offline: Continue still works, and the preference write is queued. Android denied once: Continue fires the system dialog again. A second denial blocks, and after that only Open Settings is offered. Android before version 13 needs no runtime prompt, so the sheet never appears. Large text: the tray preview grows with its own text and wraps its body to two lines. Hidden previews on the lock screen: the tray shows 'Pantopus · Household update' or 'Pantopus · Pickup reminder'.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a 'Yes' or 'Allow' button, draw 'Continue' with 'Your phone will ask next.' under it — because the system dialog is the decision and a lookalike Allow is manipulative.\n- Instead of a bell illustration, benefit bullets, or arrows toward the system dialog's Allow, draw the real tray preview — because people decide better when they see the actual notification.\n- Instead of styling the preview as a system alert, draw it as an inset illustration on raised-over-sunken — because the primer must never be mistaken for the system dialog.\n- Instead of a ghost 'Not now' beside a filled button on Android, draw two peer buttons — because a decline is a survivable outcome.\n- Instead of a long title with the caveat at the end, draw the canonical title of 30 characters or fewer — because tray truncation cuts the end of a title.\n- Instead of opening this sheet after a Date-sheet save or a PickupCard confirm, draw the host's own inline ask — because asks sit inline where they belong, and sheets never stack or open by themselves.\n- Instead of a persistent amber nag after a decline, draw the host with the widget offered once — because the widget is a return trigger that needs no permission.\n- Instead of a second Close button in the iOS denied sheet, keep Close in the top bar only — because one exit is enough.\n\nDONE WHEN: The primer never follows a card 'Yes', a Date-sheet save or an inline ask on a never-asked phone, and never opens by itself. Its only forward label is Continue (or Open Settings when denied). The trays match the canonical strings and fit at 393pt and 412dp with the caveat intact. Android 'Not now' spends no denial and never re-presents. Every denial frame names what still works for its entry, and every denial frame is reachable from a stated entry. Nothing asks at cold launch. The body names every default that sends, including sign-in alerts. A grant lands on '6:00 PM · Change' without Maya ever choosing a time, so she can change it.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f4-notification-primer · ios · 01-mail-entry · light: Maya's sheet over dimmed Mail after tapping Turn on in the push-off banner: 'Sam marked Clark PUD paid' tray, both caption lines, the body, Close in the top bar and Continue only.\n2. f4-notification-primer · android · 02-mail-entry · light: the same sheet on Android with Continue and Not now as peers.\n3. f4-notification-primer · android · 03-denied-once-pickup · light: over Today (PickupCard confirmed-just-now with its inline ask), the pickup title, 'Recycling + garbage tomorrow' tray, the pickup denied lines, Continue and Not now.\n4. f4-notification-primer · ios · 04-granted · light: back on Mail, banner reads 'Household updates are on · Change'; inset beside it shows Today's briefing card with the evening row '6:00 PM · Change' while the morning row still asks.\n5. f4-notification-primer · ios · 05-declined-at-os · light: left, Mail unchanged with its push-off banner; right, Today the next time it opens, with the briefing card slot closed and the PickupCard unchanged, its footer offering 'Put today on your home screen' once (at most once every 24 h). No amber, and no extra line.\n6. f4-notification-primer · android · 06-not-now · light: Mail unchanged after Not now. No system dialog fired. The banner still reads 'Push is off. You'll still see these here.'\n7. f4-notification-primer · ios · 07-denied-open-settings · light: over Mail, from Turn on: the Mail denied lines, one filled 'Open Settings' button, Close only in the top bar.\n8. f4-notification-primer · android · 08-denied-once-mail · light: over Mail, from Turn on: the Mail denied lines, Continue (asks again) and Not now.\n9. f4-notification-primer · android · 09-blocked · light: over Mail, from Turn on: the Mail denied lines, Open Settings and Not now.\n10. f4-notification-primer · ios · 10-never-shown · light: Today and Mail side by side with five annotations: 'Already granted: primer skipped'; 'Save failed: card shows Retry, no ask'; 'Mail Turn on while granted: banner reads Household updates are on · Change'; 'Date-sheet save: Date sheet closes, inline ask on the host, no primer'; 'iOS denied: no inline reminder ask on the PickupCard'.\n11. f4-notification-primer · ios · 11-offline-and-save-error · light: the Mail-entry sheet with the Mail offline caption, beside Mail with the InlineErrorRow 'Couldn't turn on household updates · Retry'.\n12. f4-notification-primer · ios · 12-tray-specimen · light: collapsed iOS trays at 393pt only: 'Recycling + garbage tomorrow' / 'Bins out tonight · Larkspur Loop'; worst case 'Bins out tonight · Columbia River Dr'; 'Unconfirmed: pickup tomorrow' / 'Recycling + garbage · city schedule'; 'Sam marked Clark PUD paid' / 'Due Fri 23 Oct · Columbia River Dr'; hidden previews 'Pantopus · Pickup reminder' and 'Pantopus · Household update'.\n13. f4-notification-primer · ios · 13-ax5 · light: frame 1 at AX5. The sheet scrolls, the tray wraps, and the button is full width.\n14. f4-notification-primer · android · 14-greyscale · light: frame 2 in greyscale, beside the same five tray strings drawn as collapsed Android trays at 412dp.\n15. f4-notification-primer · ios · 15-mail-entry · dark: dark twin of frame 1.\n16. f4-notification-primer · android · 16-denied-once-mail · dark: dark twin of frame 8.\n17. Notes:\n- Assumptions: Maya's second place 'Grandma's', 5200 SE Columbia River Dr; Maya skipped the inline reminder ask earlier, so her phone was never asked.\n- Annotation: 'Date-sheet save → Date sheet closes → inline ask on the host (Today PickupCard or place-file pickup row) → system dialog directly. No primer.'\n- Every invented string: both titles, both bodies, 'Arrives quietly — no sound.', all four denied lines, the inline ask, both save errors, both offline captions, 'Household updates are on · Change', 'Due Fri 23 Oct · Larkspur Loop', both Columbia River Dr worst cases, 'Pantopus · Household update' spoken form.\n- Changed from the contract: the primer body adds 'Sign-in alerts for your account.' because sign-in alerts are on by default; flag this for the NotificationAsk copy rule.\n- Omitted states: web (the card asks directly); Android before 13.\n- Decisions: provisional authorization is not used for pickup and is a possible test for the Mail (household) entry only. Android 'Not now' is the sheet's close; the permanent decline lives on the briefing card or in Settings. On Android the research says to show an educational screen only when the system says a reason should be shown, so the first-request Android frame (2) is a founder call.\n- Open questions: (a) flow-01 step 12 and flow-02 still place the primer after the first pickup confirm; this prompt follows the brief (inline ask, no primer), so the flows need updating. (b) The iOS visible Close conflicts with Apple's single-button pre-alert guidance. (c) PickupCard labels: the contract says 'Yes, Tuesday is right' / 'Change pickup day'; the brief and flows say 'That's my day' / 'Not my schedule'. The hosts are drawn with the Foundations PickupCard labels; the founder must reconcile them. (d) The Mail banner wording when the phone is allowed but Household activity is off still reads 'Push is off'; consider 'Household updates are off on this phone · Turn on'. (e) Pickup confirmer: settings shows 'confirmed by Sam'; pick one fixture across prompts.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for 'continue'.\nTurn 2: artboards 7-12, then wait for 'continue'.\nTurn 3: artboards 13-17.",
            "changeLog": [
              "Removed the auto-open after a Date-sheet save (brief P4, house-style AVOID asks in modals, no stacked sheets): the Date sheet closes and the host shows its inline ask 'Remind you the night before? 6:00 PM · Turn on reminders', which fires the system dialog directly; entries are now only Mail Turn on and the Android denied-once inline ask (review major)",
              "Rebuilt the manifest around the Mail entry: artboard 1 is the iOS Mail sheet, 2 its Android twin; granted (4) and dark (15) follow the Mail entry; the old pickup default frame became a Notes annotation and a frame-10 annotation (review major)",
              "WHO AND WHEN rewritten: Maya taps Turn on in the Mail push-off banner at 6:10 PM (review major)",
              "Stated that the host is Today or the place file, and that the Date sheet closes first; focus returns to the invoking control (review minor)",
              "Added iOS-denied and Android-blocked rule: no inline reminder ask on the PickupCard; only Mail Turn on and settings lead to Open Settings (review minor)",
              "Tray caption keeps 'This is the whole thing.' on both entries; 'Arrives quietly — no sound.' is a second line (PushCopy contract)",
              "Denied line 2 now depends on entry: Mail 'Household updates still show here in Mail.' / pickup 'Pickup still shows on Today.' (review minor)",
              "Frame 5 redrawn: briefing slot closed, PickupCard unchanged with the widget footer offered once, no extra line (NotificationAsk declined state)",
              "iOS denied: one filled Open Settings, Close only in the top bar (review minor)",
              "Bodies add 'Sign-in alerts for your account.' (brief section 3 defaults); flagged for the NotificationAsk contract on Notes",
              "Split the tray specimen: 393pt trays on iOS frame 12, 412dp trays moved into the Android greyscale frame 14; added bill-paid worst case and household hidden preview",
              "Added Mail-entry offline caption and save error; frame 4 shows the Mail banner after Allow",
              "Notes record: Android 'Not now' as the sheet's close with the permanent decline on the card or Settings (glossary), PickupCard label mismatch, banner wording when OS granted but group off, pickup confirmer fixture conflict, flows needing update",
              "Added an INSTEAD OF line against opening after a save or confirm, and one against a duplicate iOS Close"
            ]
