          {
            "id": "f4-notification-settings",
            "name": "Notifications settings (five groups)",
            "platforms": [
              "web",
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": false,
            "frameCount": 22,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Notifications settings · f4-notification-settings\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen 'Notification Preferences'. This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed.\nChanged, kept and merged on this page:\n- The page title becomes 'Notifications'.\n- 'Weather Alerts' and 'Air Quality Alerts' merge into one group, AIR & WEATHER ALERTS.\n- 'Home Reminders' becomes DATES & BILLS, with three switches.\n- Keep 'Gig Updates', 'Mail Summary' and 'Beacon Notifications' exactly as the screenshot shows, in one section below Account & security titled 'Other notifications'.\n- Replace 'Quiet Hours' with the 'Pause briefings' row.\n- Replace 'Briefing Location' and its three modes with one caption, 'Briefings follow <home or saved place>'. Draw no Device Location option.\n- Add the pinned master switch. It is the push switch that used to sit in the Mail account area; remove it there and put one row, 'Notifications · Open', in its place.\n\nATTACH: The existing Notification Preferences page on web 1440, iOS and Android. The Mail account area that holds today's push switch. The Today briefing card (for the 'More options' entry). A Mail notification row with its overflow menu open. The existing home settings page that still shows the per-home notification switches, which this change removes.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: Web 1440x900 uses the settings layout inside the left sidebar. Web 390x844. iOS 393x852 uses a grouped inset list. Android 412x915 uses a Material 3 preference list with group headers.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Settings > Notifications. On mobile, Settings opens from the account area in the Mail tab. On desktop, it opens from the sidebar. There is one page, and it has no tab of its own. Entry points:\n- Settings > Notifications, and the 'Notifications · Open' row in the Mail account area.\n- 'More options' on the Today briefing card.\n- 'Turn these off' in the overflow menu of any in-app notification row. The page scrolls once to that row's group and fades a highlight on it.\n- The first household 'marked paid' notification.\n- 'Change' on the Mail banner 'Household updates are on'.\n- The 'Manage reminders' link beside the Date sheet's 'Remind me' control.\n- The iOS Settings link 'Pantopus Notification Settings'.\n- Android's in-app settings link from the system notification page.\n- The 'Notifications · Open' row on the home settings page.\n- The deep link /app/settings/notifications, with ?group=briefings, ?group=air, ?group=dates, ?group=household or ?group=account for the group landing.\nWhat this page receives: from a notification row or ?group=, the group to highlight. What it hands on: 'Set it' opens the Date sheet on the pickup-day kind; 'Open Settings' opens the system notification page for Pantopus; 'Open' opens that Android channel; 'Turn on' on the device line asks this phone for permission; 'Add a place' opens place search; 'Show me how' opens the browser's own notification-permission help in a new tab.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM. On Sat 17 Oct at 4:00 PM, Maya Chen got 'Air: sensitive groups, AQI 118' during her son's game and found it too eager. She taps 'Turn these off' on that row in Mail to raise her level, and wants to be sure the pickup reminder stays on. Thresholds are per person; Maya's change does not affect Sam.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Give every notification Pantopus sends exactly one honest switch, on one page, and show when the phone is holding or blocking it.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: First, the master switch 'Push notifications from Pantopus' (or the pinned banner when the OS blocks delivery). Second, the five group headers. Third, the delivery helper under each group, which says how that group arrives. There is no page-level primary action, because each switch saves on its own.\n\nCONTENT (fixtures apply; the deltas are below)\nThe page reads top to bottom:\n- Pinned master: 'Push notifications from Pantopus', ON. Helper: 'Turning this off stops every notification. Everything still shows inside the app.' Device line, per platform: iOS 'Sends to this iPhone and one browser.' · Android 'Sends to this phone and one browser.' · web 'Sends to this browser and one iPhone.'\n- One-time migration line: 'We moved your home reminder settings here. Nothing you turned off was turned on.' It has a Dismiss button.\n- BRIEFINGS. Helper under the header: 'Sound and banner, at the times below.'\n  - 'Morning briefing', ON, 7:00 AM. Caption: 'Today's dates and weather in one message, only when something needs you. Nothing sent in the last day repeats.'\n  - 'Evening briefing', ON, 6:00 PM. Caption: 'Only when something needs you. No news means nothing's up.' Second line: 'Pickup comes with the evening briefing.' Status line: 'Last sent today, 6:00 PM · pickup'.\n  - Status row: 'Pickup day · Tuesday (confirmed by Sam)'.\n  - Caption: 'Briefings follow your home, 2418 NE Larkspur Loop.'\n  - Row: 'Pause briefings'.\n  - Native only: 'Home screen widget · Add', hidden once a widget has been placed.\n- AIR & WEATHER ALERTS\n  - Master 'Air & weather alerts', ON. Helper: 'Can come through Focus when the air quality index (AQI) is 151 or higher, or there's a weather warning.'\n  - Caption: 'One alert when air crosses your level. It updates if air gets worse. National Weather Service warnings always come while this is on.'\n  - Threshold as three radio rows, each with EPA's full health statement as its meaning line (let it wrap). Before Maya's change, the first one is selected, matching what the server sends today:\n    1. 'Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups · AQI 101 and up'. Meaning: 'Members of sensitive groups may experience health effects. The general public is less likely to be affected.'\n    2. 'Unhealthy · AQI 151 and up'. Meaning: 'Some members of the general public may experience health effects; members of sensitive groups may experience more serious health effects.'\n    3. 'Very Unhealthy · AQI 201 and up'. Meaning: 'Health alert: The risk of health effects is increased for everyone.'\n- DATES & BILLS (renamed from 'Home Reminders'). Helper under the header: 'Sound and banner.'\n  - 'Date reminders', ON. Helper: 'The reminders you set before a date — like 14 days before your lease notice is due.'\n  - 'Bill reminders', ON. Helper: 'Clark Public Utilities and any bill you add.'\n  - 'Task reminders', ON. Helper: 'Household tasks with a due date.'\n  - Group caption: 'Only for dates, bills and tasks where a reminder is set. To stop one date's reminders, open that date and set Remind me to never.'\n  - These are three switches, so muting dates never mutes bills or tasks.\n- HOUSEHOLD ACTIVITY\n  - Master 'Household activity', ON. Helper: 'Quiet — shows in your list, no sound. Always in your Mail notifications, even with this off.'\n  - 'Bills marked paid', ON. Caption: 'Louder only if a bill you still see as unpaid is due within 3 days.'\n  - 'Tasks completed', OFF. Caption: 'Only tasks you created or were assigned.'\n  - 'Calendar events added', ON.\n  - 'People joining or leaving', ON. Caption: 'When someone accepts an invitation or leaves this household.'\n  - When the master is off, these four rows show their saved values, disabled, with the caption 'Turn on Household activity to change these.'\n- ACCOUNT & SECURITY. Helper under the header: 'Sound and banner.'\n  - 'Sign-ins and invitations to you', ON. Helper: 'New sign-ins to your account and household invitations sent to you.'\n- OTHER NOTIFICATIONS: 'Gig Updates', 'Mail Summary', 'Beacon Notifications', drawn exactly as the screenshot shows, with the same row style as above.\n- Help link in the same slot as on the other settings pages.\nWorst case to fit: the pinned banner, the migration line and the paused-briefings row with its caption all at once, at 390 wide.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION: Five labelled groups in this fixed order, then Other notifications last. The order never changes, because each of the five groups is one permanent Android channel and one iOS category. Air & weather alerts and Household activity each start with a master switch row, with its delivery helper directly under that master in text.secondary. Briefings, Dates & bills and Account & security have no master row: their switches are the group's control, and the delivery helper sits directly under the group header. Never put helper text in the group footer: people check one switch at a time. The evening briefing's silence promise sits in its own row caption, because the people who open this page stopped getting notifications and want to know whether they are still on. Every row reads its own OS state. When the OS blocks a row, draw the switch off and disabled, with a leading warning glyph and a text.primary line 'Off in Android settings · Open'. The saved choice is kept and comes back when the OS allows it. A switch never reads ON when nothing can be delivered. When the whole app is blocked on this device and nothing else delivers, pin a full-width banner above the master: warning glyph, text.primary on the warning tint, 'Notifications are off for Pantopus. These rows still update inside the app.', then 'Open Settings'. The widget is offered once, inside that banner. Use amber only when a switch the person turned on cannot be delivered. The device line is per device: when push is on in a browser but this phone has not allowed it, it says so and offers Turn on.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS: Tapping a switch saves it right away. The row shows 'Saving…', then 'Saved', as a live status message and never a toast. If a save fails, the switch returns to its last saved value and an InlineErrorRow appears. Tapping a time row opens the platform time picker (iOS wheel in a sheet, Material 3 time picker, web native time input). 'Pause briefings' opens a short list: 'For 1 week' / 'For 2 weeks' / 'Until a date I pick' (opens the platform date picker). Once paused, the row reads 'Paused until Mon 26 Oct · Resume' with the caption 'Pickup reminders pause too.', and the evening status line is hidden. Every paused state names its end date. The radio rows are single choice, and selection is shown by a filled dot plus bold text, which looks different from focus. A deep-link landing (?group= or 'Turn these off') scrolls once and fades the highlight within 300ms. Under Reduce Motion, the highlight is a static outline. A switch that saves successfully plays one light haptic tick. Nothing on this page is gesture-only.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: NotificationAsk (state 'switch ON but OS blocked'). QuietDayReceipt (briefing settings row variant 'Skipped tonight — nothing needed you'). FactRow (pickup-day status row, known and missing variants; 'Notifications · Open' row). LockedActionRow (not-at-this-tier variant). InlineErrorRow (save failed). OfflineNotice. NotificationRow (the entry point). ScopeChip (the saved-place frame). WarmingSkeleton (row skeleton).\n\nACCESSIBILITY: Reading order: banner, master, device line, then each group header with its helper, master (if any) and rows, then Other notifications. Each switch's spoken label includes its helper and OS state. Example for a blocked row: 'Evening briefing, off in Android settings, dimmed. Your choice, on at 6:00 PM, is kept. Open.' Status messages use a polite live region and never move focus. On a ?group= or 'Turn these off' landing, accessibility focus moves to the highlighted group header. Targets are 44pt on iOS, 48dp with 8dp gaps on Android, and 44px on web. Focus never sits under the pinned banner, which reserves scroll padding. At AX5 and 200%, labels and meaning lines wrap and switches drop below the label.\n\nCOPY\n- Actions: 'Set it' · 'Open Settings' · 'Open' · 'Resume' · 'Retry' · 'Dismiss' · 'Add a place' · 'Turn on' · 'Add' · 'Show me how'.\n- Status: 'Saving…' · 'Saved' · 'Off in Android settings · Open' · 'Notifications are off for Pantopus. These rows still update inside the app. · Open Settings'.\n- Pause list: 'For 1 week' · 'For 2 weeks' · 'Until a date I pick'. Paused: 'Paused until Mon 26 Oct · Resume'. Caption: 'Pickup reminders pause too.'\n- Scheduled Summary (iOS): 'Your iPhone may hold pickup reminders for your summary. · Open Settings'.\n- Time Sensitive off (iOS): 'Time Sensitive is off in iOS Settings. Alerts may wait until Focus ends. · Open Settings'.\n- Blocked-but-kept caption: 'Your choice is kept'.\n- Device lines when this phone is not allowed: 'Sends to one browser. This iPhone isn't allowed yet · Turn on'. When this phone is blocked but a browser delivers: 'Sends to one browser. This iPhone is off in iOS Settings · Open Settings'. When nothing delivers: 'This iPhone: off in iOS Settings'.\n- Quiet night: 'Skipped tonight — nothing needed you'; dated form 'Skipped Sun 18 Oct — nothing needed you'.\n- Save error: 'Couldn't save Evening briefing. Check your connection and try again. · Retry'.\n- No location: 'Briefings need an address. Save one to turn these on.' and 'Air & weather alerts need an address too.'\n- Timezone (only when the phone is outside Pacific time): 'Your phone is on Mountain Time. Briefings use Pacific Time, your address's time zone.'\n- Web blocked: 'Notifications are blocked in this browser. These rows still update inside the app. · Show me how'.\n- Offline: 'You're offline. Your settings are shown as last saved. Switches work again when you're back online.'\n- Replacement row (home settings and Mail account area): 'Notifications · Open'.\n\nEDGE CASES\n- Saved place only (Jordan Lee at PLACE B, 1107 NE Birchfield Ct):\n  - The briefings caption reads 'Briefings follow your saved place, 1107 NE Birchfield Ct · Saved place · Only you'.\n  - The pickup row reads 'Pickup day · Not set · Set it', with the caption 'The city lists Thursday. Set your pickup day to get the night-before reminder.'\n  - Household activity is one grey LockedActionRow, 'Claim this address first', with no action.\n  - Bill reminders and Task reminders are hidden.\n- No location: the briefing switches and the Air & weather alerts master are off and disabled, each with its needs-an-address line and 'Add a place'.\n- Whole app blocked on this phone, nothing else delivers: every group switch off and disabled with 'Your choice is kept'; device line 'This iPhone: off in iOS Settings'.\n- Whole app blocked on this phone but a browser still delivers: no pinned banner; switches stay ON; device line 'Sends to one browser. This iPhone is off in iOS Settings · Open Settings'.\n- Loading: row skeletons, not a spinner.\n- Many devices: the device line wraps.\n- Web push on, this phone not allowed: the device line variant above; the Briefings switches stay ON (the browser still delivers).\n- Two blocked channels: each blocked row gets its own line.\n- Household master off: the four rows disabled with their saved values.\n- Paused: the evening status line is hidden; no 'Skipped' line shows while paused.\n- The per-home switches are gone from the home settings page. In their place is one row, 'Notifications · Open', that opens this page.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of per-home notification switches, draw this one page linked from the home settings — because those switches never saved anything.\n- Instead of 'Home Reminders', draw 'Dates & bills' with three switches — because people with no home get these too, and muting dates must not mute bills or tasks.\n- Instead of a segmented AQI control, draw three radio rows with EPA's meanings — because segments truncate at large text.\n- Instead of a 151 default, select 101 — because the server alerts at 101.\n- Instead of a switch that shows ON while the OS blocks it, draw it off and disabled with 'Off in Android settings · Open' — because a switch that pretends is worse than no switch.\n- Instead of a keeper group or a 'Tips and news' switch, draw the five groups plus the existing Other notifications — because Pantopus never sends marketing or keeper notifications, and every type that sends needs one home.\n- Instead of helper text in the group footer, put it under each master or group header — because people read one switch at a time.\n- Instead of a Device Location briefing option, draw the one 'Briefings follow' caption — because briefings follow an address, not the phone.\n- Instead of an open-ended pause, name the end date — because a paused state people forget becomes a silent failure.\n\nDONE WHEN: Every notification type this design introduces maps to exactly one switch, including joins and leaves and task reminders, and every type that still sends has a switch. Every group states how it is delivered. The air threshold matches what the server sends. No switch reads ON, or is spoken as on, while nothing can be delivered. The evening row states the silence promise and when it last sent, and never says 'Skipped' while paused or on a night something was sent. Every pause names its end date. The device line is honest per device. Flow check: from an air alert's 'Turn these off', Maya picks 'Very Unhealthy · AQI 201 and up' and the pickup reminder is untouched.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f4-notification-settings · web-1440 · 01-default · light: the full dense page with the master, the migration line, all five groups and Other notifications.\n2. f4-notification-settings · ios · 02-default · light: the same content as a grouped inset list.\n3. f4-notification-settings · android · 03-default · light: the same content as an M3 preference list; 'Calendar events added' shows 'Saving…' and 'Bills marked paid' shows 'Saved'.\n4. f4-notification-settings · ios · 04-os-denied · light: the pinned banner above the master. Every group switch is off and disabled, and each shows the caption 'Your choice is kept' under its label. The device line reads 'This iPhone: off in iOS Settings'. The widget is offered once inside the banner.\n5. f4-notification-settings · android · 05-channel-blocked · light: the Air group is off and disabled, reading 'Off in Android settings · Open'.\n6. f4-notification-settings · ios · 06-summary-and-time-sensitive · light: the Scheduled Summary caption with Open Settings on Evening briefing, and the Time Sensitive line on Air.\n7. f4-notification-settings · ios · 07-this-phone-off · light: device line 'Sends to one browser. This iPhone isn't allowed yet · Turn on', switches still ON.\n8. f4-notification-settings · web-1440 · 08-landing-air · light: arrived via ?group=air, with the Air group highlighted and 'Very Unhealthy · AQI 201 and up' selected.\n9. f4-notification-settings · web-390 · 09-saved-place · light: the PLACE B variant.\n10. f4-notification-settings · web-1440 · 10-no-location · light: briefing switches and the Air & weather master off and disabled, both needs-an-address lines, 'Add a place'.\n11. f4-notification-settings · web-1440 · 11-paused-timezone · light: the timezone caption; the Pause row reads 'Paused until Mon 26 Oct · Resume' with 'Pickup reminders pause too.'; the evening status line is hidden.\n12. f4-notification-settings · web-390 · 12-quiet-night · light: the evening status line reads 'Skipped Sun 18 Oct — nothing needed you'; the Household master is off with its four rows disabled and their caption.\n13. f4-notification-settings · web-1440 · 13-loading · light: row skeletons.\n14. f4-notification-settings · web-1440 · 14-save-error · light: Evening briefing reverted, with an InlineErrorRow.\n15. f4-notification-settings · web-1440 · 15-replacement-rows · light: panel 1, the home settings page with the switches gone and one row 'Notifications · Open'; panel 2, the Mail account area with the push switch gone and one row 'Notifications · Open'.\n16. f4-notification-settings · web-390 · 16-offline · light: an OfflineNotice, with switches disabled and the reason shown.\n17. f4-notification-settings · web-1440 · 17-browser-blocked · light: the web banner with 'Show me how' and the web device line.\n18. f4-notification-settings · ios · 18-ax5 · light: the Air group at AX5, with radio rows and EPA meaning lines wrapping and switches below labels.\n19. f4-notification-settings · web-390 · 19-greyscale · light: frame 9 in greyscale.\n20. f4-notification-settings · web-1440 · 20-default · dark: the dark twin of frame 1.\n21. f4-notification-settings · ios · 21-os-denied · dark: the dark twin of frame 4.\n22. Notes. List:\n  - assumptions: Maya's ON values are her own choices; the defaults after a grant are Household activity OFF and Morning briefing OFF unless chosen on the card; the evening default is ON at 6:00 PM; thresholds are per person; Task reminders default ON like Bill reminders;\n  - the rule for dates: Morning briefing lists the day's dates; Date reminders are the lead-time series. Muting one never mutes the other;\n  - every invented string: master helper, all device lines (iPhone, Android, web, not allowed, off in iOS Settings), 'Your choice is kept', group helpers, captions, 'Task reminders' and its helper, the Dates & bills group caption, 'People joining or leaving' caption, the Tasks completed caption, pause list and 'Pickup reminders pause too.', 'Skipped Sun 18 Oct — nothing needed you', Time Sensitive line, both needs-an-address lines, the timezone caption (changed from the earlier '7:00 AM Pacific' wording), web banner, offline line, 'Notifications · Open', the ?group= values, the alert title 'Air: sensitive groups, AQI 118' (category-true for 118), and the Scheduled Summary line (flow-02 quotes it as 'Pickup reminders may arrive with your summary');\n  - deviations: Account & security no longer says it can come through Focus, to keep the rule that only the air group mentions Focus; whether sign-ins should be Time Sensitive is an open call; Task reminders chosen as a third switch rather than widening Bill reminders;\n  - omitted states;\n  - open calls:\n    - the threshold control depends on the backend storing a per-user threshold;\n    - whether the master switch stays once each group has its own switch;\n    - whether Account & security can be switched off;\n    - whether Gig Updates, Mail Summary and Beacon Notifications still send; any that no longer sends is removed; any that moves (for example Mail Summary to Mail Day settings) must keep a working switch there before removal from this page ships;\n    - pickup day confirmer is Sam here and a fresh save in the primer; pick one fixture.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for 'continue'.\nTurn 2: artboards 7-12, then wait for 'continue'.\nTurn 3: artboards 13-18, then wait for 'continue'.\nTurn 4: artboards 19-22.",
