          {
            "id": "f1-claim-receipt",
            "name": "Claimed — what came with you",
            "platforms": [
              "web",
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": false,
            "frameCount": 21,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Claimed — what came with you · f1-claim-receipt\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen 'Verified success' (the post-claim and post-verify success screen). This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed.\nChanges to the host:\n- The verified headline 'Your address is verified.' is used only once a verification has finished. Directly under it, add the method line 'Address verified by postcard · Mon 19 Oct'. If any headline you keep is a bare 'Verified' or uses celebration wording, keep its position and style but set the line to 'Address verified by postcard · Mon 19 Oct', and list the change on Notes.\n- Claim-time version (before verification): the headline reads 'You claimed 2418 NE Larkspur Loop.' and the method line reads 'Postcard on its way · mailed Mon 28 Sep'. The verified-only 'Now available' rows are omitted in this version.\n- Replace the subline ('You're now an address-proven neighbor at …') with the summary sentence.\n- 'Now available' rows (verified version only) use the GrantLimitList unlocked strings, each with a tick: 'Message your neighbors' · 'Get a residency letter' · 'Show your Residency Pass' · 'Share what you pay in rent (Real Rent)' · 'Earn a Block Founder rank'. Remove any 'permanent 0% marketplace fee' line. Use 'Block Founder' for the permanent rank and 'Founding Neighbor' only for the scarce first-5 tier. Replace any 'verified neighbors' wording with these strings.\n- Order: headline → method line → summary → 'Came with you' manifest → consent block → FactCount line → closing line → 'Now available' rows (verified only) → 'Go to your place'.\n- Change 'Go to your place' from filled to an outlined button. It is how Maya leaves, and leaving keeps the dates Only you, so it must not compete with the two consent buttons.\n- The staged reveal becomes one 200ms fade (static under Reduce Motion). Keep the seal at its existing size, with no halo animation.\n\nATTACH:\n- The existing Verified success screen on web 1440, web 390, iOS and Android.\n- The place file (Place tab) on web 1440, showing its top banner slot and its fact rows.\n- Today with the 'Saved place · Only you' chip, for reference.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: Web 1440x900 with the left sidebar. Web 390x844. iOS 393x852. Android 412x915.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Place tab. The timing model: claiming created the home on Mon 28 Sep, when Maya requested the postcard. The server copied the saved place's pickup day, dates and keeper to the home in that same step and removed the duplicate saved-place entry. Every carried date has stayed Only you (pending) since then. Sam Ortega joined on Wed 7 Oct and has not seen them. This receipt appears when the claim finishes. It appears again when verification finishes if the dates question is still unanswered.\nPeople reach it in five ways:\n1. The claim flow ends here (claim-time version: claim headline, before any household member).\n2. The address-verification flow ends here (postcard code entered): verified version.\n3. The first time the place file opens after a claim, its banner slot shows the claim receipt banner once. The banner links here. It ranks after invite, reissue and compare arrival, and before mailbox arrival, setup and verify. If a higher banner is showing, it waits for the next place-file open. It counts as shown only once it has rendered.\n4. From then on, the place file row 'What moved when you claimed' opens this same manifest.\n5. The deep link /app/place?verified=1 shows the receipt later.\nWhat this screen receives: the list of carried items, any item that failed to move, and the people in the household (plus pending invitations). What it hands on: Today now uses the home (same sections, no chip). Each date keeps its own visibility control ('Only you' / 'Household') in the Date sheet and on its place-file row, so either choice can be reversed per date.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM. Six weeks ago Maya Chen saved HOME A; she set the pickup day, entered two dates and named Ollie. On Mon 28 Sep she claimed it and left the receipt without choosing. Sam joined on Wed 7 Oct. She has just typed her postcard code, and the question is asked again.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Name every fact that moved from the saved place to the home, and ask before the one privacy change the move causes.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS:\n1. The headline and method line, then the summary sentence.\n2. The manifest rows with their scope pairs.\n3. The consent question. Its two peer buttons are the only actions that matter here.\n\nCONTENT (fixtures apply; the deltas are below)\nDeltas: the claim date Mon 28 Sep, Sam's join date Wed 7 Oct. For frame 13 only, Maya's saved place is 1107 NE Birchfield Ct (a fixture deviation; see Notes).\nSummary line: 'Your pickup day, 2 dates and Ollie came with you.'\nHeader: the ScopeChip 'Saved place · Only you', struck through, followed by 'Your household'. Section label: 'Came with you'. Legend, printed once: '✓ You added this'.\nManifest, one row per carried item. The summary counts only the rows that carried. A failed item is drawn as a separate InlineErrorRow below them and is not counted.\nVerified version (Mon 19 Oct):\n- Pickup day · 'Tuesday · garbage every week, recycling every other week · next recycling tomorrow'. Caption: 'Everyone in this household will see this.' Scope pair: Only you → household.\n- Lease ends · 'in 163 days · Wed 31 Mar 2027'. Caption: 'Notice due Mon 1 Mar 2027 · reminder Mon 15 Feb'. Scope pair: Only you → household (pending).\n- Warranty ends · 'Water heater · in 54 days · Sat 12 Dec 2026'. Scope pair: Only you → household (pending).\n- Ollie (your keeper) · 'Otter'. Caption: 'Everyone in this household will see Ollie.' Scope pair: Only you → household.\nClaim-time version (Mon 28 Sep), same rows with these values:\n- Pickup day · 'Tuesday · garbage every week, recycling every other week · next recycling Tue 6 Oct' (Tue 29 Sep is garbage only).\n- Lease ends · 'in 184 days · Wed 31 Mar 2027'.\n- Warranty ends · 'Water heater · in 75 days · Sat 12 Dec 2026'.\nConsent block:\n- Question: 'Share the 2 dates you entered with Sam?'\n- Caption: 'Until you choose, only you will see them. If you share, anyone who joins later will see them too, including priya@example.com if she accepts. You can change this for each date later.'\n- Two peer buttons: 'Share with the household' and 'Keep them to myself'.\nBelow the manifest:\n- A FactCount line reading '14 on file', with category pips and the link 'See your place file'. It is not a manifest row. It shows the same integer as the place file header.\n- Closing line: 'Today now uses this home.'\nWorst case: a failed item, a long provider name, and a date title that wraps to two lines.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION: This is a short receipt, not a celebration.\n- Draw flat rows on surface.raised under the summary, with no card per item.\n- Each row is a DateRow (pickup variant for the pickup row, default variant for dates), with its optional ScopeChip in the scope-change pair variant: person glyph → small arrow → house glyph. Pending shows a dashed house glyph until the person chooses.\n- The keeper row is a DateRow-shaped row with the KeeperStrip species avatar scaled to the KindGlyph's 24pt slot, in place of the KindGlyph.\n- The pickup and date rows carry the ProvenanceMark 'You added this'. Do not add a second tick to mean 'moved'; the scope pair and the section label 'Came with you' show that the item moved.\n- The migration shows on each row, not once in prose, so each row can be checked against what Maya remembers typing.\n- Both consent buttons are filled primary.700, the same width and height, side by side; stacked at 390 wide and at AX5.\n- If there are no dates, there is no consent block.\n- If nothing moved, the screen shows only the plain success screen plus 'Today now uses this home.' Never draw an empty list or '0 items'.\n- When the claimed address differs from the saved place, nothing carries. The screen is the plain success screen plus 'Today now uses 2418 NE Larkspur Loop. 1107 NE Birchfield Ct is still saved. · Your places'. 'Your places' opens the Your places screen.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS: The two consent buttons are peers of equal size and weight.\n- Share. Each date's pair becomes a solid house glyph with a 200ms cross-fade. The buttons are replaced by the InlineUndo line 'Shared with Sam · Undo', which stays until Maya leaves the screen.\n- Keep. Each date's pair becomes person → person. The buttons are replaced by the line 'Only you will see these 2 dates. You can change this in each date.'\n- Leaving without choosing (including 'Go to your place') keeps the dates Only you. The pending pair stays pending on the revisited receipt, and the question is asked again there.\n- Either choice plays one light haptic tick.\n- Retry on a failed row retries that item only; on success it joins the rows above and the counts update.\n- Phase 2: Ollie's pose settles to calm once. Under Reduce Motion this is a static swap, and the glyph changes are instant.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: DateRow (pickup and default variants), ScopeChip (scope-change pair, pending, declined and struck variants), ProvenanceMark, KindGlyph, FactCount, GrantLimitList (unlocked strings for Now available), InlineErrorRow (carry failed variant), InlineUndo, LandingBannerSlot (one-time claim receipt banner), FactRow ('What moved when you claimed' receipt link), KeeperStrip species avatar (phase 2, at the 24pt slot), OfflineNotice, WarmingSkeleton (row skeleton).\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- The summary sentence is a status message (role=status). Reading order: headline, method line, summary, manifest, consent block, FactCount line, closing line, Now available rows, Go to your place.\n- The manifest is a list, announced as '4 items'.\n- Each row is one element. Example: 'Lease ends, in 163 days, Wednesday 31 March 2027, you added this. Was visible to only you, household pending your choice.'\n- After a choice, the buttons are replaced by the result line, and focus moves to it (and to Undo when present).\n- FactCount is spoken '14 things on file: place, dates, people.'\n- Targets are 44pt / 48dp / 44px. Scope is carried by glyph shape plus a spoken name, never by colour.\n\nCOPY\n- Verified headline: 'Your address is verified.' Method line: 'Address verified by postcard · Mon 19 Oct'.\n- Claim-time headline: 'You claimed 2418 NE Larkspur Loop.' Claim-time method line: 'Postcard on its way · mailed Mon 28 Sep'.\n- Failed item: 'We couldn't move your water-heater warranty · Retry'.\n- Summary when one item fails: 'Your pickup day, 1 date and Ollie came with you.' Question: 'Share the date you entered with Sam?' Keep result: 'Only you will see this date. You can change this in the date.'\n- Phase 1 summary: 'Your pickup day and 2 dates came with you.'\n- Only you in the household so far (claim time): 'Share the 2 dates you entered with people who join this household?' with the caption 'It's just you here for now. You can change this for each date later.'\n- A different address was claimed: 'Today now uses 2418 NE Larkspur Loop. 1107 NE Birchfield Ct is still saved. · Your places'.\n- Place file banner: 'Your pickup day, 2 dates and Ollie came with you · See what moved'.\n- Place file row: 'What moved when you claimed'.\n- Offline: 'You're offline. Only you will see your dates until you choose.'\n\nEDGE CASES\n- Phase 1 has no keeper row, and the summary drops 'and Ollie'.\n- Dates only.\n- Pickup day only (no consent block).\n- Claim time: no household members yet; the future-members question; the claim headline; no Now available rows.\n- A long address wraps in the different-address line.\n- Slow manifest (1 second or more): skeleton rows under the summary.\n- Offline: the buttons are disabled with a reason, and the dates stay Only you.\n- A member without calendar edit rights sees the rows but not the consent block. This must be confirmed in Notes.\n- Already claimed by someone else: no receipt; the flow goes to the household request path.\n- Household already has its own pickup day or keeper: not reachable in this flow (the carry runs at claim, when the household is new). Recorded on Notes with its copy for a future household-request receipt.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of 'are now visible to everyone', draw the conditional question with dates pending — because silence is not consent.\n- Instead of confetti, a badge, a halo or a progress bar, draw a plain manifest — because this is a receipt to check.\n- Instead of 'Ollie knows 11 things', draw a separate '14 on file' line — because a creature that 'knows' reads like surveillance.\n- Instead of a quietly missing row, draw the failed item as its own InlineErrorRow with Retry, and counts that match the carried rows — because loss must be visible.\n- Instead of a one-time banner as the only way back, draw the 'What moved when you claimed' row — because receipts are revisited.\n- Instead of naming Dana, name only real household members and pending invitations — because Dana is a friend who compared places and not a household member.\n- Instead of a filled 'Go to your place' beside the consent buttons, draw it outlined — because leaving is a quiet default, not a third choice.\n- Instead of 'Your address is verified.' on the claim-time receipt, draw 'You claimed 2418 NE Larkspur Loop.' — because unverified looks unverified.\n\nDONE WHEN: The summary counts equal the carried rows in every frame, including phase 1 and the failed state. Nothing is shared before a tap. Each choice is stated as a fact and can be reversed per date in the Date sheet and the place file. The verified version states the method and date; the claim-time version never says verified and shows no verified-only unlocks. No withdrawn fee promise or mixed founder naming appears. The same manifest opens again from the place file. Today shows the home without re-laying out.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f1-claim-receipt · web-1440 · 01-all-carried-pending · light: the verification receipt with headline, method line, the dense manifest, the consent block, FactCount, Now available rows and the outlined Go to your place.\n2. f1-claim-receipt · web-390 · 02-all-carried-pending · light: the same, at phone width, consent buttons stacked.\n3. f1-claim-receipt · ios · 03-all-carried-pending · light: the native equivalent.\n4. f1-claim-receipt · android · 04-all-carried-pending · light: the native equivalent.\n5. f1-claim-receipt · web-1440 · 05-shared · light: solid house glyphs, with 'Shared with Sam · Undo' in place of the buttons.\n6. f1-claim-receipt · web-1440 · 06-kept-to-myself · light: person → person, with the result line in place of the buttons.\n7. f1-claim-receipt · web-390 · 07-carry-failed · light: three carried rows, the warranty as a separate InlineErrorRow below them, the adjusted summary and the one-date question.\n8. f1-claim-receipt · web-390 · 08-phase-1 · light: pickup + 2 dates, 3 rows, summary 'Your pickup day and 2 dates came with you.'\n9. f1-claim-receipt · web-390 · 09-nothing-to-carry · light: the plain success screen plus the closing line.\n10. f1-claim-receipt · web-1440 · 10-dates-only · light: two date rows and the consent block.\n11. f1-claim-receipt · web-390 · 11-pickup-only · light: one row, no consent block.\n12. f1-claim-receipt · web-1440 · 12-claim-time-only-you · light: Mon 28 Sep receipt with 'You claimed 2418 NE Larkspur Loop.', 'Postcard on its way · mailed Mon 28 Sep', the claim-time row values, the future-members question, and no Now available rows.\n13. f1-claim-receipt · web-390 · 13-different-address · light: plain success plus the still-saved line for 1107 NE Birchfield Ct with '· Your places'.\n14. f1-claim-receipt · web-1440 · 14-place-file-banner-and-row · light: the place file with the one-time banner, the persistent row, and a date row showing its 'Only you' / 'Household' control.\n15. f1-claim-receipt · web-390 · 15-loading · light: skeleton rows.\n16. f1-claim-receipt · web-390 · 16-offline · light: disabled consent buttons with the reason.\n17. f1-claim-receipt · ios · 17-ax5 · light: rows stacked, the scope pair on its own line, consent buttons stacked.\n18. f1-claim-receipt · web-390 · 18-greyscale · light: frame 2 in greyscale.\n19. f1-claim-receipt · web-1440 · 19-all-carried-pending · dark: dark twin of frame 1.\n20. f1-claim-receipt · ios · 20-kept-to-myself · dark: frame 6 content on iOS, in dark mode.\n21. Notes:\n   - Assumptions: the Mon 28 Sep claim and Wed 7 Oct join timeline; the carry runs at claim, while flow-06 step 4 places it at code entry, so the flow needs updating.\n   - Fixture deviation: frame 13 gives Maya the saved place 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, which the house style assigns to Jordan Lee; the founder may swap in a Maya-only address.\n   - Every invented string: both headlines if changed, both method lines ('Address verified by postcard' replaces the contract's 'Address confirmed by postcard' example, because the glossary forbids 'confirm'), claim-time row values, 'Keep them to myself' (replaces 'Keep them private to me' quoted in flow-06), the consent caption, '· Your places', result lines, offline line, banner and row copy.\n   - Foundations items: the KeeperStrip species avatar at the 24pt KindGlyph slot is a new size for the Foundations board.\n   - Integer rule: the receipt FactCount, the place file header and the keeper strip must show the same integer (14 here; the keeper strip spec says 11).\n   - Host copy changes: Now available rows now use GrantLimitList strings; any 0% marketplace fee line removed; Block Founder / Founding Neighbor naming fixed.\n   - Omitted states: already claimed by someone else (no receipt). Household already has a pickup day or keeper: unreachable while the carry runs at claim on a new household; if a household-request receipt is added later, use 'Your pickup day (Wednesday) wasn't moved — the household uses Tuesday, confirmed by Sam · Change pickup day' (the summary count drops it) and 'Ollie stayed as your saved-place keeper — this household already has a keeper.'\n   - Open questions:\n     - keeper and pickup visibility change without a consent step;\n     - whether sharing notifies Sam, and if so whether it waits until Undo closes;\n     - the claim receipt banner's rank in the banner slot;\n     - whether to ask for the move-in date at claim;\n     - that the first-week ticks and the widget label move silently;\n     - confirm that members without calendar edit rights see no consent block.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for 'continue'.\nTurn 2: artboards 7-12, then wait for 'continue'.\nTurn 3: artboards 13-18, then wait for 'continue'.\nTurn 4: artboards 19-21.",
