                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The main frame contradicts itself. The status line says the checklist is showing, but the same frame shows the Moving checklist row as Hidden. A hidden checklist is not in the place file, so the status line is false in artboard 1, in its greyscale and dark twins (17, 18), and in the web and Android versions (3, 4, 5).",
                    "evidence": "Prompt LAYOUT: 'Under the helper, draw a status line in caption text.secondary: \"Showing in your place file until Sat 28 Nov\"' and 'Row 2, \"Moving checklist\": value \"Hidden\"… Draw this row only while the checklist is hidden for this viewer.' Artboard 1: 'Moved in Tue 29 Sep 2026, helper, status, legend, Moving checklist Hidden with Show again'. Design doc F6 sets up per-user dismissal ('just_moved_dismissed_at' on HomeOccupancy) and says 'the card hides for a home when dismissed on any device'.",
                    "fix": "Make the status line depend on the hidden state. While hidden, it reads e.g. \"Hidden from your place file · the 60 days end Sat 28 Nov\" (list it as an invented string). \"Showing in your place file until Sat 28 Nov\" appears only when the checklist is not hidden, e.g. in artboard 14 after Show again. Or keep artboard 1's status and drop the Hidden row from that frame. Spell out which one each artboard uses."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The prompt never gives the wrong date the app stamped at claim, which is the value this screen exists to correct. No frame shows it, and the save-error copy names the date Maya is trying to save as the old value. The error frame cannot match the story as written. The timing is also off: 'three weeks' after Tue 29 Sep is Tue 20 Oct, which is after TODAY (Mon 19 Oct).",
                    "evidence": "Prompt WHO AND WHEN: 'She claimed the address three weeks after moving in, so the app stamped the claim day as her move-in date… She wants the real date, Tue 29 Sep 2026'. COPY: 'Save error: \"We couldn't save your move-in date. Tue 29 Sep 2026 is still set.\"' EDGE CASES: 'keep the old value visible, and keep the date Maya typed in the sheet.' The inventory uxNote puts the whole purpose on this correction: 'a mover who claims their address three weeks after moving gets a window three weeks wrong'.",
                    "fix": "Add a fixture for the stamped value, e.g. \"Moved in: Mon 19 Oct 2026 (stamped when Maya claimed, 20 days after moving)\", and change 'three weeks' to 'about three weeks' or '20 days'. Artboard 2 opens the sheet from that stamped value. Artboards 11 and 19 show the error with the old value kept: \"We couldn't save your move-in date. Mon 19 Oct 2026 is still set.\" The sheet still holds the typed Tue 29 Sep 2026. Alternatively, say plainly that the error frame shows a later edit away from 29 Sep and name the date she typed."
                  },
