      {
        "ids": [
          "f3-members-roster",
          "f3-invite-composer",
          "f3-invite-banner"
        ],
        "prompts": [
          {
            "id": "f3-members-roster",
            "name": "Members roster",
            "platforms": [
              "web",
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": false,
            "frameCount": 24,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Who lives here (Members roster) · f3-members-roster\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Members\" (the home's Members & Security tab). This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed.\n- On web there must be exactly one members screen. The standalone members page and the dashboard's Members & Security tab become the same surface, so draw it once, as the tab. Keep the tab's existing security content below the roster, unchanged.\n- The old web \"Add guest\" page is deleted. It showed a success message without sending anything. Do not draw it anywhere.\n\nATTACH: the current Members screen on iOS, Android and web 1440 (the Members & Security tab, with the home header tabs Dashboard · Share · Members & Security · Settings); the place file's People section on iOS; the Foundations board from prompt 00.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852 (primary), Android 412x915, web 1440x900 (left sidebar) and 390x844 (bottom tab bar). Sheets: iOS sheets with detents; Android modal bottom sheets; web 1440 centred dialogs 480 wide; web 390 bottom sheets.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Place tab → place file for Larkspur Loop → People → Who lives here. On web the page is /app/homes/{id}/members, and it shows the same surface as the dashboard tab. Entry points:\n- the home dashboard Members card, quick action and Members & Security tab\n- the place file's People rows\n- the household block (\"Who lives here with you?\") once someone has joined\n- Today's member count\n- the Invite composer's Done, which returns here with the new Pending row highlighted once (\"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct · Resend\")\n- the Invite composer's Done after a Reissue, which returns here with that row highlighted once\n- the sender banner \"2 invitations need to be sent again · Fix\" and its in-app notification row, which land here scrolled to the Needs reissue rows, with a highlight that fades once\n- deep links /app/homes/{id}/members and their native equivalents.\nThe recipient banner \"You have 2 invitations\" does not come here. It opens the Invitations waiting for you list on Your places.\nWhat this screen hands on: Invite and \"Invite someone\" open the Invite composer with Email selected; Reissue opens it in its needs-reissue state; Resend on a pending or expired row works in place.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM. Maya Chen, owner of 2418 NE Larkspur Loop, has just sent an invitation to priya@example.com. She opens this screen to check it is really pending, and finds two older invitations that stopped working when the household's invite rules changed. Sam Ortega, a member, opens the same screen on his phone to see who lives there.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Let everyone in the household see who lives here, and let the people who manage the home fix invitations in one tap.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: (1) The role groups, each with its people. (2) The quieter Pending group underneath, where the two \"Needs reissue\" rows stand out by their glyph and their words. (3) The one primary action, \"Invite\", in the header. A member sees no Invite button; in its place is the line \"Maya Chen can invite people here.\"\n\nCONTENT: Use the FIXTURES. Deltas for this surface (list each on Notes):\n- Maya Chen (you) · Owner. Row: \"joined Thu 1 Oct 2026\". Person detail only: \"Address confirmed by postcard · Thu 8 Oct 2026\".\n- Sam Ortega · Member. Row: \"joined Sat 10 Oct 2026\". Person detail only: \"Joined by Maya Chen's invitation · Sat 10 Oct 2026\".\n- Lena Ortega · Guest. Row: \"access until Sun 1 Nov 2026\".\n- Pending, single-use link model: priya@example.com · \"Member · sent Mon 19 Oct · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · Resend. Invite link · \"Works once · Member · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · Turn off link.\n- Needs reissue: theo.park@example.com (\"Member · sent Mon 12 Oct\") and @rgarcia (\"Member · sent Tue 13 Oct\").\n- Expiring: noah.kim@example.com · \"Member · sent Tue 13 Oct · Expires tomorrow\".\n- Expired: ali.hassan@example.com · \"Member · sent Sun 11 Oct · Expired Sun 18 Oct\" · Resend. The expiry is words in text.secondary, with no red and no chip.\n- Declined: kai.brooks@example.com · StatusChip \"Declined · Thu 15 Oct\" · Remove.\n- Approval link model only: Invite link · \"Joiners wait for your OK · Member · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · Turn off link; Ana Ruiz, joined by link · \"Waiting for your OK\" · Approve / Remove.\n- Offline: FreshnessLine \"You're offline · as of 5:52 PM\".\n- Worst case (frame 18 only): 6 people — Maya Chen (Owner), Nora Patel (Admin), Sam Ortega, Ravi Shah, Elena Brooks (Members), Lena Ortega (Guest). 4 pending rows: margaret.oconnor-whitfield@example.com (38 characters; \"Member · sent Mon 19 Oct · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · Resend), theo.park@example.com and @rgarcia (Needs reissue), kai.brooks@example.com (Declined · Thu 15 Oct). Sam's member-view line in that household reads \"Maya Chen or Nora Patel can invite people here.\"\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION:\n- Header: title \"Who lives here\", the ScopeChip \"Your household\" beneath it, the primary \"Invite\", and a quiet secondary text action \"Visitor passes\". On web the tab label stays \"Members & Security\" as host chrome.\n- Role groups in this order, as overline labels: OWNER · ADMINS · MEMBERS · GUESTS. ADMINS, MEMBERS and GUESTS each carry a 44pt disclosure row: \"What can admins do?\", \"What can members do?\", \"What can guests do?\". Each expands in place into a GrantLimitList of verbs, not a permission matrix. OWNER carries \"What can owners do?\" as a proposed addition beyond MemberRow ⑦ (record it on Notes).\n- Under each label, one MemberRow per person: avatar, name, one caption (join date, or access-until for guests), overflow.\n- On every person row, including the viewer's own, draw no chip, badge, tick, caption or colour for how the person was verified. Verification appears in two places only: the person detail sheet (method and date), and a LockedActionRow on an action the viewer cannot use yet.\n- Pending group (owners and admins only), drawn last and quieter than the people, using InviteRow. Caption at its top: \"Only owners and admins see this.\"\n- A Needs reissue row: warning glyph, the text \"Needs reissue — your household's invite rules changed\" in text.primary, and an inline \"Reissue\".\n- An Expired row: the pending anatomy with its caption ending \"Expired Sun 18 Oct\" and an inline \"Resend\" (44pt). Record \"InviteRow expired variant\" on Notes as a proposed Foundations addition.\n- The two link models are alternatives, not a pair. Frames 1, 16, 17, 18, 19 and 21 draw the single-use model (the \"Works once\" link row). Frames 3, 4, 20 and 22 draw the approval model (the \"Joiners wait for your OK\" link row and Ana's \"Waiting for your OK\" row). Label each approval-model artboard, above the frame, \"approval variant, if links are not single-use\".\n- The roster is list-only; it has no chart. Missing data: a cold load over 1s shows WarmingSkeleton rows that keep the group structure; cached data shows FreshnessLine; a person with no join date shows only the role.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS:\n- A person row opens the person detail sheet with a visible \"Close\": name, role, join date and the verification line (method and date).\n- \"Confirm this person lives here\" appears only for a person who has not verified their address (they joined by invitation), in their detail and in their row overflow. For Maya viewing Sam, it opens the owner-attestation sheet in place of the detail (no stacked sheets). For anyone whose address is already confirmed, such as Maya, it is absent.\n- Row overflow on other people (owners and admins): Change role, Confirm this person lives here (only as above), Remove from Larkspur Loop. The viewer's own row holds only \"Leave Larkspur Loop\". Every overflow action is also a screen-reader custom action.\n- Change role opens a sheet titled \"Change Sam Ortega's role\": radio rows for Admin, Member and Guest, and two short columns, \"Member can\" and \"Admin can also\". When Guest is selected, an \"Access until\" row with a date control appears under the radio rows (platform date picker plus a typed alternative). Buttons \"Save role\" and \"Cancel\". On save, the sheet closes and \"Sam Ortega is now an admin\" is announced as a status message.\n- Remove and Leave use DestructiveConfirm.\n- Resend on a pending or expired row shows \"Sending…\" in place, then \"Sent again · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\". The row stays put. On an expired row, Resend issues a new 7-day expiry, and the row becomes a normal pending row.\n- Reissue opens the Invite composer in its needs-reissue state. After Done, this screen shows that row as a normal pending row: \"Sent again · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct · the old link no longer works\", highlighted once. Accessibility focus lands on that row.\n- Cancel invitation and Extend sit in the pending overflow. Extend appears only if the backend supports it (Notes); its result is \"Extended · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\". Cancel collapses the row to \"Cancelled invitation to priya@example.com · Undo\" (InlineUndo).\n- Turn off link collapses the link row to \"Link turned off · Undo\" (InlineUndo).\n- Approve moves Ana into MEMBERS and shows \"Ana Ruiz joined Larkspur Loop · Undo\" (InlineUndo). The \"Ana Ruiz joined\" notice to other members is sent only when Undo closes. Ana sees no household data until approved; only link joins need approval, and email and username invitations skip it.\n- Remove on a declined row uses InlineUndo. No InlineUndo has a timer.\n- \"Visitor passes\" opens the home's Share tab on web and the Share Center on iOS and Android, where visitor and service passes live. A household Guest is invited through Invite, by choosing Guest.\n- Motion: row insert and remove cross-fades of 300ms or less; the deep-link highlight fades once. Under Reduce Motion both are static.\n- Haptics: one light tick when Approve is confirmed, and nothing else on this screen.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED:\n- MemberRow: owner, admin, member, guest, you and empty variants. Draw the \"you\" variant without the ⑧ verification caption; method and date live only in the person detail sheet.\n- InviteRow: pending, expiring, needs reissue, declined, link active, awaiting approval, and the proposed expired variant; sending state; S3 offline reasons as published.\n- GrantLimitList: role disclosures; change-role columns.\n- LockedActionRow: names-who-can-act variant for members and legacy roles; verification variant in Sam's own detail.\n- ScopeChip (\"Your household\").\n- StatusChip: \"Declined · Thu 15 Oct\" and \"Waiting for your OK\", only on invitation rows, one per row.\n- DestructiveConfirm (Leave; Remove), InlineUndo, WarmingSkeleton (row skeleton), FreshnessLine, OfflineNotice, InlineErrorRow.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n- Reading order: title, scope chip, Invite, Visitor passes, each group label and its disclosure, the people, then Pending.\n- Each row is one element with a merged label, for example \"Sam Ortega, member, joined Saturday October 10 2026\" or \"Invitation to ali.hassan@example.com, member, expired Sunday 18 October. Resend.\" Row actions are custom actions.\n- Avatars are decorative.\n- Resend, Reissue, Approve, Remove, Undo and each overflow get 44pt / 48dp / 44px hit areas, even though they look like text.\n- Expiry, expired and reissue are stated in words, never by glyph or colour alone.\n- \"Sending\", \"Sent again\", \"Cancelled\", \"Link turned off\", \"Joined\", \"is now an admin\" and \"You're offline\" are polite status messages.\n- The Fix deep-link highlight moves accessibility focus to the first reissue row.\n- At AX5, captions wrap under names, group labels wrap, and the overflow stays reachable.\n\nCOPY:\n- Header \"Who lives here\" · ScopeChip \"Your household\" · button \"Invite\" · secondary \"Visitor passes\"\n- Member-view line \"Maya Chen can invite people here.\"\n- Pending caption \"Only owners and admins see this.\"\n- Disclosure rows \"What can owners do?\" · \"What can admins do?\" · \"What can members do?\" · \"What can guests do?\"\n- Members disclosure (exactly the shared GrantLimitList grants): \"Sees and edits the calendar\" · \"Sees bills and who paid\" · \"Sees who lives here\"\n- Guests disclosure: \"Same as Member until their access ends\"\n- Admins disclosure: \"Everything members can do\" · \"Invites people and resends invitations\" · \"Removes people and changes roles\" · \"Adds bills and marks them paid\"\n- Owners disclosure: \"Everything admins can do\" · \"Changes who can invite people here\"\n- Empty: \"Just you at Larkspur Loop\" · \"Invite someone\". In the empty state the header Invite is hidden; \"Invite someone\" is the single action.\n- Person detail: \"Close\" · \"Confirm this person lives here\"\n- Change role: \"Change Sam Ortega's role\" · \"Admin\" · \"Member\" · \"Guest\" · \"Member can\" · \"Admin can also\" · \"Access until\" · \"Save role\" / \"Cancel\" · status \"Sam Ortega is now an admin\"\n- Pending results: \"Sending…\" · \"Sent again · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · \"Cancelled invitation to priya@example.com · Undo\" · \"Link turned off · Undo\" · \"Extended · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · \"Ana Ruiz joined Larkspur Loop · Undo\"\n- LockedActionRow in Sam's own detail: \"Address verification needed to send neighbor messages · Verify address\"\n- Leave sheet: \"Leave Larkspur Loop?\" · \"You lose the household calendar, bills and tasks. Your saved places and private dates stay yours.\" · \"Leave Larkspur Loop\" / \"Stay\"\n- Remove sheet: \"Remove Sam Ortega from Larkspur Loop?\" · \"Sam loses the calendar, bills and tasks here. Bills Sam marked paid keep the note 'Sam (no longer here)'.\" · \"Remove Sam\" / \"Keep Sam\"\n- Sole owner, own row: \"You're the only owner. Make someone an admin and contact support to hand over ownership.\"\n- Access ended (revoked only): \"Your access to Larkspur Loop ended.\" · \"Your saved places and private dates are still yours.\" · \"Go to Your places\"\n- Legacy role without list access: \"Your role at Larkspur Loop doesn't include this list yet.\" · LockedActionRow \"Maya Chen can show you who lives here\"\n- Load error: \"We couldn't load who lives here. · Retry\"\n- Resend error: \"We couldn't resend to priya@example.com. · Retry\"\n- Offline: the Invite button shows the reason \"Inviting needs a connection.\" Pending rows use the published InviteRow S3 reasons (\"You're offline. You can resend when you're back.\" and the others). Person-row overflow uses the MemberRow S3 reason \"You're offline. You can change roles when you're back.\"\n\nEDGE CASES:\n- The 38-character email wraps to two lines and is never truncated before the @.\n- With 6 people and 4 pending rows, groups keep their labels and the page scrolls.\n- When an invitee accepts, their pending row is removed, and they appear in their role group for every member, with no status chip.\n- The sole owner's own row has no Leave; it shows the sole-owner line. Notes: product question on an owner-transfer control.\n- On Lena's end date her row leaves by itself; other members get the quiet row \"Lena's guest access ended\" (drawn in household notifications).\n- When someone joins, every member sees them; Pending stays owners-and-admins only.\n- Sam (member) sees no Pending group, no Invite, no role editing and no overflow on other people's rows. He sees Visitor passes only if his role allows Share; otherwise it is absent.\n- Revoked access gets the access-ended frame. A legacy role without list access gets the legacy frame: the household is still theirs, so it never says access ended.\n- Slow network: rows over 1s show skeletons; no full-page spinner.\n- Offline: the cached roster stays readable; actions are disabled with their reasons shown.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of \"Address-verified\" or \"Household member\" chips beside names, draw plain rows and put the method and date in the detail, because badging housemates reads as a ranking of the people you live with.\n- Instead of carrying over the green \"Household access\" chip that is being removed from iOS My Homes, draw nothing on roster rows, because that chip claims a verified status the member does not have.\n- Instead of an \"Add guest\" form that shows success, draw a secondary \"Visitor passes\" link that opens Share, because that page never sent anything and visitor passes already work there. A household Guest is chosen inside Invite.\n- Instead of a disabled Invite button for members, draw \"Maya Chen can invite people here.\", because a member can never invite, so name who can.\n- Instead of Resend on declined invitations, draw \"Declined · Thu 15 Oct\" with Remove only, so the sender is not prompted to nag. An expired invitation, which nobody answered, keeps Resend.\n- Instead of a red \"Expired\" chip, draw \"Expired Sun 18 Oct\" in the caption with Resend beside it, because the fix matters more than the alarm.\n- Instead of a per-person permission grid, draw coarse roles with a verb disclosure, because permission matrices lose non-expert members.\n- Instead of \"Your access ended\" for a legacy role, draw the reason and who can help, because that person still belongs to the household.\n\nDONE WHEN:\n- An invited member can list who lives here.\n- Maya can find a dead invitation (needs reissue or expired) and fix it in one tap per row, and afterwards she sees a pending row with \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct · Resend\".\n- An accepted invitation leaves Pending and the person appears in their role group.\n- No frame shows a verification chip or caption on a person, and no frame shows a control that does nothing.\n- The Members disclosure uses the same three grant strings the invitee reads.\n- Every frame reads correctly in greyscale.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f3-members-roster · ios · 01-owner-dense · light — Maya's view: header with scope chip, OWNER, MEMBERS, GUESTS, and Pending with theo.park@example.com and @rgarcia (Needs reissue · Reissue), priya@example.com (Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct · Resend) and the \"Works once\" link row.\n2. f3-members-roster · ios · 02-member-view · light — Sam's view: no Pending, no Invite, the names-who-can-act line.\n3. f3-members-roster · ios · 03-pending-states · light — labelled \"approval variant, if links are not single-use\": noah expiring, ali expired with Resend, kai declined, the \"Joiners wait for your OK\" link row, Ana waiting, priya's row mid \"Sending…\".\n4. f3-members-roster · ios · 04-after-reissue · light — labelled \"approval variant, if links are not single-use\": back from the composer, theo's row highlighted as \"Sent again … the old link no longer works\"; ali's row now \"Sent again · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\"; priya's row collapsed to the Cancelled Undo line; the link row collapsed to \"Link turned off · Undo\"; Ana's joined Undo line.\n5. f3-members-roster · ios · 05-person-detail-owner · light — Sam's detail as Maya sees it: method and date, Confirm this person lives here, Close.\n6. f3-members-roster · ios · 06-own-detail-locked · light — Sam's own detail with the verification LockedActionRow.\n7. f3-members-roster · ios · 07-change-role-sheet · light — Admin selected, the two capability columns, Save role / Cancel; inset below the sheet: the status \"Sam Ortega is now an admin\".\n8. f3-members-roster · ios · 08-leave-sheet · light — Sam leaving: what goes and what stays.\n9. f3-members-roster · ios · 09-remove-sheet · light — Maya removing Sam.\n10. f3-members-roster · ios · 10-empty-just-you · light — \"Just you at Larkspur Loop\" and Invite someone; header Invite hidden.\n11. f3-members-roster · ios · 11-loading · light — skeleton rows keeping the groups.\n12. f3-members-roster · ios · 12-error · light — load error row with Retry.\n13. f3-members-roster · ios · 13-offline · light — cached roster with FreshnessLine, Invite and row actions disabled with their reasons.\n14. f3-members-roster · ios · 14-access-ended · light — revoked access frame.\n15. f3-members-roster · ios · 15-legacy-no-list · light — legacy role: reason line and \"Maya Chen can show you who lives here\".\n16. f3-members-roster · android · 01-owner-dense · light — Material 3 version of frame 1.\n17. f3-members-roster · web-1440 · 01-owner-dense · light — the single Members & Security tab with frame 1's content, security content below.\n18. f3-members-roster · web-390 · 16-worst-case · light — Nora Patel, Ravi Shah, Elena Brooks and the others; 4 pending rows with the 38-character email wrapped.\n19. f3-members-roster · ios · 17-ax5 · light — frame 1 at AX5.\n20. f3-members-roster · android · 18-greyscale · light — frame 3 in greyscale, with the approval-variant label.\n21. f3-members-roster · ios · 01-owner-dense · dark — dark twin of frame 1.\n22. f3-members-roster · ios · 03-pending-states · dark — dark twin of frame 3, with the approval-variant label.\n23. f3-members-roster · web-1440 · 07-change-role-sheet · light — the change-role sheet as a centred 480-wide dialog with Guest selected and the \"Access until\" date row showing Sun 1 Nov 2026.\n24. f3-members-roster · ios · 99-Notes · light — every invented string (Nora Patel, Ravi Shah, Elena Brooks, margaret.oconnor-whitfield, noah, ali, kai, Ana, the approval link caption, all result lines, change-role strings, legacy and sole-owner copy); noah.kim replaces the earlier jordan.lee so no pending invitee shares a name with PLACE B's Jordan Lee; proposed Foundations additions: InviteRow expired variant, the owner disclosure (added beyond MemberRow ⑦), and the tasks grant (\"Proposed addition to the shared GrantLimitList set: 'Sees and edits tasks'. Add it to the composer caption, review and decision screen together, or not at all.\"); the \"you\" MemberRow is drawn without ⑧ here; the two link models (single-use vs approval is a backend choice; approval frames are labelled); Add guest page deleted, visitor passes live in Share; the recipient banner no longer lands here; product questions: Extend, owner transfer, owner-only powers, and whether admins as well as owners may use \"Confirm this person lives here\"; omitted states (Extend result drawn only as a string).\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 3: 13-18, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 4: 19-24.",
            "changeLog": [
              "Added an expired pending-invitation row (ali.hassan@example.com, 'Expired Sun 18 Oct', Resend issuing a new 7-day expiry) per flow-04 failure branch and research; drawn in frames 3 and 4; InviteRow expired variant recorded on Notes as a proposed addition (review majors).",
              "Artboard 1 (and dark twin 21) now show the two Needs reissue rows alongside priya and the link row so the hero frame shows the moment of truth (review major).",
              "Removed 'Sees and edits tasks' from the Members disclosure so it matches the three GrantLimitList contract strings; the tasks grant is recorded on Notes as a proposed shared addition (review major, doc confirms members have tasks.view/edit).",
              "Replaced the self-contradicting worst-case fixture with Nora Patel, Ravi Shah, Elena Brooks and four specified pending rows; member-view line 'Maya Chen or Nora Patel can invite people here.'; renamed jordan.lee to noah.kim to avoid clashing with PLACE B's Jordan Lee (review major).",
              "Added missing strings: change-role title, Save role / Cancel, Guest 'Access until' date row, 'Sam Ortega is now an admin', person detail 'Close', 'Link turned off · Undo', 'Extended · …' (review major + minor).",
              "Approval-model frames (3, 4, 20, 22) are explicitly labelled 'approval variant, if links are not single-use'; added the approval-model link row (derive proposal: active link is a pending row with Turn off link) (review minor).",
              "'Confirm this person lives here' now appears only for people who have not verified their address; Notes asks whether admins may confirm (review minor).",
              "Added edge case: an accepted invitation leaves Pending and the person appears in their role group, per flow-04 step 18 (review minor).",
              "Group labels changed to OWNER · ADMINS · MEMBERS · GUESTS per the published MemberRow board; owner disclosure kept as a proposed addition on Notes (review minor).",
              "MemberRow 'you' variant drawn without the ⑧ caption, stated explicitly (review minor).",
              "Offline copy aligned: Invite button reason plus published InviteRow S3 and MemberRow S3 reasons (review minor).",
              "Empty state: header Invite hidden so 'Invite someone' is the single action (review minor).",
              "Added the Fix notification row as an entry point and what this screen hands to the composer (flows-spec flow-12)."
            ]
