          {
            "id": "f3-invite-composer",
            "name": "Invite someone to your household",
            "platforms": [
              "web",
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": false,
            "frameCount": 24,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Invite someone to your household · f3-invite-composer\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Invite a co-resident\" (the household invitation composer). This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed.\n- Web already has all three channels: change only the captions, the review step, the needs-reissue state and the link limit there.\n- iOS is email-only today. It gains Username and \"Share instead\" (link and QR).\n- Android has Email and Username. It gains the QR code.\n\nATTACH: the current composer on web 1440 (modal), iOS (sheet) and Android (bottom sheet); the Who lives here screen behind it on iOS; the Foundations board from prompt 00.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS:\n- iOS 393x852: a sheet with medium and large detents, primary platform.\n- Android 412x915: a modal bottom sheet.\n- Web 1440x900: the existing invite modal, 560 wide.\n- Web 390x844: a bottom sheet.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Place tab → place file for Larkspur Loop → People → Who lives here → Invite. Entry points:\n- Who lives here \"Invite\": opens with Email selected.\n- Who lives here empty state \"Invite someone\": opens with Email selected.\n- The household block's \"Invite by email\" (Email selected) and \"Share a link\" (\"Share instead\" selected, warning already showing).\n- The place file's People row \"Add the people you live with\".\n- The home dashboard Members card's Invite action. This replaces the old floating button; the app has no floating button.\n- A Needs reissue row's \"Reissue\" in Who lives here, including after the sender banner's \"Fix\" opens it: the sheet opens straight on the needs-reissue state.\n- The web recovery page /app/homes/{id}/invitations.\nWho lives here no longer has an \"Add guest\" entry here; visitor passes live in Share.\nWhat it hands on: Done closes the sheet and returns to the entry surface. From Who lives here (either entry), the new Pending row reads \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct · Resend\" and is highlighted once. From the place file or household block, that row reads \"Invited priya@example.com · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\". After a Reissue, Done returns to Who lives here with that row highlighted once. The invitee's decision screen shows the same grant list the sender reviewed here.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM. Maya Chen is at 2418 NE Larkspur Loop. Priya is moving into the spare room next week. Maya has Priya's email but not her Pantopus username, and wants Priya to see the pickup day and the bills before she arrives.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Send one household invitation, by whichever channel you actually have for that person, knowing exactly what they will be able to see.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: (1) The channel chips with Email selected, and the one recipient field. (2) The role chips, with the capability caption under the selected role. (3) The single primary button \"Review invitation\", pinned at the foot of the sheet.\n\nCONTENT: Use the FIXTURES (HOME A; pending invite priya@example.com, expires Mon 26 Oct). Deltas (list each on Notes):\n- Username \"@priyar\", which resolves to the person row \"Priya Raman · @priyar\". Not-found example \"@priyra\".\n- Guest window \"Until Sun 1 Nov 2026\".\n- Note: \"You'll see our pickup day and the household calendar. I already added the lease end and the Clark Public Utilities bill.\"\n- Link: pantopus.com/j/7K4M-QD2X. Reissued link: pantopus.com/j/9R2T-HW4B.\n- Reissue rows: theo.park@example.com and @rgarcia.\n- Worst case: a 38-character email, margaret.oconnor-whitfield@example.com, and the note at its full length.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION:\n- Form, top to bottom: sheet title and the ScopeChip \"Your household\"; the channel radio group; ONE recipient slot; role ChoiceChips \"Member\" and \"Guest\" with a one-line caption under them; for Guest only, the access row \"Until Sun 1 Nov 2026\" with a date control; \"Add a note (optional)\"; the sticky primary button, with scroll padding reserved beneath it.\n- Channel group: three options in one radio group, \"Email\", \"Username\" and \"Share instead\". Draw all three as the standard ChoiceChip channel variant with the same outline and the same selected fill and check. \"Share instead\" is quieter only through its position (third). Selecting one deselects the others. iOS may use a segmented control if all three labels fit at default size; at AX sizes use radio rows.\n- Switching channel swaps only the recipient slot. Draw Email, Username and Share instead at the same total height, slot in the same position. The slot reserves room for one resolved person row or one two-line error, so at default text size the resolving, error and resolved states never move the role chips or the button.\n- Share instead asks for no recipient. The slot holds the exposure warning: a full body-size sentence with an info glyph, not a caption, shown the moment Share instead is chosen.\n- Review step: a plain manifest of label/value rows, no illustration, no celebration:\n  - Home — 2418 NE Larkspur Loop, Vancouver, WA\n  - Sent to — priya@example.com (Username path: \"Priya Raman · @priyar\"; link path: \"Link — Works once\"; approval model: \"Link — Whoever joins waits for your OK\")\n  - Role offered — Member, plus the GrantLimitList grant list and a collapsed \"What needs address verification (5)\" that expands to the five lock rows\n  - Access — Starts when accepted · no end date (Guest: \"Until Sun 1 Nov 2026\")\n  - Expires — in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\n  - Note — the text\n  - closing line \"Household access only. This invitation does not grant ownership.\"\n  The review's primary button is \"Send invitation\" on Email and Username, and \"Create link\" on the link path.\n- Sent panel: the status line, then (email and username) a quiet \"Resend\" text action, then the link in a copyable field, a QR block of at least 160pt (scannable from a phone held across a table), \"Copy link\" and \"Share\" as a TextActionRow using the system share sheet only, then the expiry, then \"Done\". The QR sits inside the panel and is never the hero.\n- Link-ready panel: same structure without Resend, with \"Link ready · Works once\" and \"You can turn it off later in Who lives here.\"\n- Needs-reissue state: the reason line at the top; then a compact manifest (Sent to — theo.park@example.com; Role offered — Member with the GrantLimitList grant list; Expires — in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct), read-only; then one primary \"Reissue\". The manifest is the confirmation; no extra dialog.\n- Reissued panel: the sent-panel structure: status line, the new link pantopus.com/j/9R2T-HW4B in the copyable field, its QR, Copy link / Share, the new expiry, Done.\n- The composer has no chart.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS:\n- The review replaces the form inside the same sheet, with a Back control. It never stacks a second sheet. The review is the confirmation; there is no separate confirm dialog.\n- Email field uses email autocomplete. Paste works everywhere.\n- Validation runs on \"Review invitation\" and on leaving the field, never on every keystroke. The typed value is always kept.\n- The username resolves after typing pauses: the slot shows \"Looking up @priyar…\", then the person row; not found shows the inline error inside the reserved slot space.\n- The Guest date opens the platform date picker, with a typed alternative.\n- Sending locks the review and shows \"Sending…\" on the Send invitation button. Success appears only after the server confirms.\n- Resend in the sent panel shows \"Sending…\" in place, then \"Sent again · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\".\n- \"Link copied\" is a status message.\n- Opened from Reissue, the sheet opens straight on the needs-reissue state, prefilled and read-only. Reissue shows \"Reissuing…\" on the button, re-sends on the same channel, and then shows the reissued panel: the old link stops working, and the new link and expiry are stated. Its Done returns to Who lives here with that row highlighted once.\n- Link joins: if links cannot be single-use, whoever joins by link waits for an owner or admin's OK and sees no household data until approved. Email and username invitations skip approval.\n- Motion: slot cross-fade on channel change (200ms); review slides in from the trailing edge (300ms). Under Reduce Motion both become cross-fades.\n- Haptics: one light tick when the send is confirmed, and nothing else.\n- \"Close\" (form) or \"Done\" (panels) is always visible. Android Back and web Escape step back from the review, then close the sheet.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: ChoiceChip (channel variant, all three options standard, with \"Share instead\" third; role variant with capability caption; selected = fill + check, distinct from focus), GrantLimitList (role caption under chips; \"Role offered\" expansion in the review and in the needs-reissue manifest), ScopeChip, InviteRow (the reissue row this sheet opens from), LockedActionRow (names-who-can-act variant, in the permission-denied frame), TextActionRow (Copy link / Share, copied state), InlineErrorRow (send failed, value kept), OfflineNotice.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n- Reading order: title, scope, channel, recipient, role and caption, note, primary button.\n- Channels read as one radio group, e.g. \"Share instead, 3 of 3, selected\". The role caption is read after its chip.\n- The exposure warning is announced when Share instead is selected.\n- QR label: \"QR code for the invitation link. The link is also below as text.\"\n- \"Looking up\", \"Sending\", \"Invitation sent\", \"Sent again\", \"Reissued\", \"Link copied\" and \"You're offline\" are polite live regions.\n- Errors are tied to their field; focus moves to the first error.\n- Chips and text actions are 44pt / 48dp / 44px.\n- At AX5 the chips become radio rows, manifest labels sit above values, and the sheet scrolls. Focus is never hidden under the sticky button.\n\nCOPY:\n- Title \"Invite someone to Larkspur Loop\" · \"Close\"\n- Channels \"Email\" · \"Username\" · \"Share instead\"\n- Field labels \"Email address\" · \"Pantopus username\" · resolving \"Looking up @priyar…\"\n- Member caption \"Sees and edits the calendar, sees bills and who paid, sees who lives here\"\n- Guest caption \"Same as Member until Sun 1 Nov\" · \"Need a visitor or service pass? Open visitor passes\"\n- Warning, single-use model: \"Anyone with this link can join your household until it expires. Send it to one person.\"\n- Warning, approval model (replaces the sentence above): \"Anyone with this link can ask to join until it expires. Whoever joins waits for your OK. Send it to one person.\"\n- Buttons \"Review invitation\" · \"Send invitation\" · \"Create link\" · \"Back\" · \"Reissue\" · \"Reissuing…\" · \"Done\"\n- Sent \"Invitation sent to priya@example.com\" · \"Resend\" · \"Copy link\" · \"Share\" · \"Link copied\" · \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\"\n- Link ready \"Link ready · Works once\" · \"You can turn it off later in Who lives here.\"\n- Errors: \"We can't find @priyra. Check the spelling, or send by email instead.\" · \"This email address looks incomplete. Check it and try again.\" · \"We couldn't send the invitation. Your details are still here. · Try again\"\n- Reissue \"This invitation stopped working when your household's invite rules changed. Send it again?\" · \"Sent again to theo.park@example.com. The old link no longer works. Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct.\"\n- Permission denied: \"Only owners and admins can invite people to Larkspur Loop.\" · LockedActionRow \"Maya Chen can invite people here.\" · \"Close\"\n- Offline \"You're offline. You can finish this, but sending needs a connection.\"\n- Slow send \"Still sending…\"\n\nEDGE CASES:\n- The 38-character email wraps inside the field and in the manifest.\n- The full-length note wraps; the manifest shows it in full.\n- @priyar already lives here: \"Priya Raman already lives here.\"\n- priya@example.com already pending: \"You invited this address on Mon 19 Oct. You can resend it from Who lives here.\"\n- Slow network: \"Sending…\" stays on the button, no full-screen spinner; after 10s add \"Still sending…\".\n- Sam (no invite rights) opening a stale link gets the permission-denied frame, with no form.\n- Link channel: if the backend cannot make links single-use, the approval-model warning and manifest line apply, joiners see nothing until approved, and Notes records the dependency.\n- Offline: the form stays editable; send is disabled with the reason.\n- No contact import, no bulk invite, no scheduled reminder sends.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of warning about link exposure in the sent panel, draw it in the recipient slot the moment Share instead is chosen, because the decision happens there.\n- Instead of a form that grows per channel, draw three equal-height states with a reserved slot, because the button must stay under the thumb.\n- Instead of making the QR or link the default, draw Email as the default, because the link widens exposure.\n- Instead of \"Role offered — Member\" alone, draw the grant list under it, because the sender is approving what someone else will see of the calendar and bills.\n- Instead of a bare \"Reissue\" button, draw the compact manifest with the grant list above it, because the invitation died when the role's permissions changed.\n- Instead of a success tick while the request is in flight, draw \"Sending…\" and show sent only after the server confirms.\n- Instead of \"Contacts\" import or \"Invite 5 people\", draw one recipient, because each invitation is a separate trust decision.\n- Instead of a free-standing or text-style \"Share instead\" link, draw it as the third standard chip in the group, so it is clear what is selected and how to go back.\n\nDONE WHEN:\n- The role explains itself where it is chosen.\n- The manifest, including the needs-reissue manifest, shows the same grant list the invitee reads, and always the expiry.\n- iOS has all three channels; Android has the QR code.\n- Switching channels, resolving a username, or showing an error moves nothing below the slot.\n- A reissue shows the new link and expiry, states that the old link stopped working, and returns to the highlighted row.\n- Every frame reads correctly in greyscale and at AX5.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f3-invite-composer · ios · 01-email-form · light — Email, priya@example.com, Member with caption, the note.\n2. f3-invite-composer · ios · 02-share-instead · light — Share instead selected, warning in the slot, same height as frame 1.\n3. f3-invite-composer · ios · 03-username-guest · light — @priyar resolved, Guest with the until-row and the visitor-passes line; small inset of the slot showing \"Looking up @priyar…\".\n4. f3-invite-composer · ios · 04-username-error · light — \"We can't find @priyra\", value kept, chips unmoved.\n5. f3-invite-composer · ios · 05-review · light — full manifest with grant list and collapsed verification list.\n6. f3-invite-composer · ios · 06-sending · light — review locked, \"Sending…\" on the Send invitation button.\n7. f3-invite-composer · ios · 07-sent-panel · light — sent status, Resend, link, QR, Copy link, Share, expiry, Done.\n8. f3-invite-composer · ios · 08-link-review · light — link path review with \"Link — Works once\" and \"Create link\".\n9. f3-invite-composer · ios · 09-link-ready · light — \"Link ready · Works once\", QR, turn-off hint.\n10. f3-invite-composer · ios · 10-needs-reissue · light — opened from Reissue: reason line, compact manifest for theo.park@example.com with the grant list and \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\", one Reissue.\n11. f3-invite-composer · ios · 11-reissued · light — sent-again status, old link stopped, new link pantopus.com/j/9R2T-HW4B, QR, Copy link / Share, new expiry, Done.\n12. f3-invite-composer · ios · 12-permission-denied · light — Sam: reason, who can invite, Close.\n13. f3-invite-composer · ios · 13-send-error · light — error row, all input kept.\n14. f3-invite-composer · ios · 14-offline · light — form editable, send disabled with reason.\n15. f3-invite-composer · android · 01-email-form · light — bottom sheet version.\n16. f3-invite-composer · android · 09-link-ready · light — the new Android QR panel.\n17. f3-invite-composer · web-1440 · 05-review · light — review in the 560 modal.\n18. f3-invite-composer · web-1440 · 02-share-instead · light — link warning and \"Works once\" in the 560 modal.\n19. f3-invite-composer · web-390 · 15-email-error · light — \"This email address looks incomplete…\"\n20. f3-invite-composer · ios · 16-ax5 · light — frame 1 at AX5, chips as radio rows.\n21. f3-invite-composer · ios · 17-greyscale · light — frame 2 in greyscale.\n22. f3-invite-composer · ios · 01-email-form · dark — dark twin of frame 1.\n23. f3-invite-composer · ios · 07-sent-panel · dark — dark twin of frame 7, QR keeping its contrast.\n24. f3-invite-composer · ios · 99-Notes · light — invented strings (@priyar, @priyra, the note, both links, \"Looking up @priyar…\", \"Reissuing…\", \"Still sending…\", the permission-denied reason, the approval-model warning and manifest line); single-use vs approval dependency and the rule that link joiners see nothing until approved while email and username skip approval; \"Guest = Member until the end date requires matching guest HomeRolePermission rows; confirm with backend.\"; Add guest entry removed (visitor passes live in Share); where \"Open visitor passes\" goes (web: the home's Share tab; native: the Share Center); Done destinations per entry; approval-model warning drawn only as a string; omitted states.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 3: 13-18, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 4: 19-24.",
            "changeLog": [
              "Needs-reissue state now shows a compact read-only manifest (Sent to, Role offered with GrantLimitList, Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct) above Reissue, because the invitation died when role permissions changed (review major; flow-12 step 6).",
              "Replaced 'Members' in user copy with 'Who lives here' ('You can turn it off later in Who lives here.', 'You can resend it from Who lives here.'), per the glossary and the roster title (review major).",
              "Reissued panel reuses the sent-panel structure with a new link, QR, Copy link / Share, new expiry and Done (review minor; flow-12 step 4).",
              "Added the Who lives here empty-state 'Invite someone' entry point (derive proposal f3-invite-wizard-channels) (review minor).",
              "Approval-model warning written in full and stated as a replacement: 'Anyone with this link can ask to join until it expires. Whoever joins waits for your OK. Send it to one person.' (review minor).",
              "Notes flags that Guest = Member depends on matching guest HomeRolePermission rows (review minor; doc F3 migration only adds member rows).",
              "Added the permission-denied reason string, LockedActionRow and Close (review minor).",
              "All three channel options drawn as the standard ChoiceChip; 'Share instead' quieter only by position; iOS segmented-control note from the contract (review minor).",
              "Removed FreshnessLine from the component list (unused) (review minor).",
              "Place-file handoff string now includes the relative count: 'Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct' (review minor).",
              "Added 'Looking up @priyar…' resolving caption (inset on frame 3), 'Close', 'Reissuing…', and a new web-1440 Share instead artboard; manifest grows to 24 (review minor)."
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "f3-invite-banner",
            "name": "Invitations waiting for you (landing banner)",
            "platforms": [
              "web",
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": false,
            "frameCount": 26,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Invitations waiting for you (landing banner) · f3-invite-banner\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Place tab landing\": Your places for someone with no claimed home, and the place file for someone with one. This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed. You are adding the invitation variants to the existing single banner slot, which already holds the \"from the card in your mailbox\" arrival pill, and one \"Invitations waiting for you\" section to Your places. Do not redesign the page.\n\nATTACH:\n- Your places on iOS, Android and web 1440, with one saved place and the mailbox-arrival pill visible.\n- The place file on iOS.\n- The setup and verify banners as they look today.\n- The Foundations board from prompt 00.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852 (primary), Android 412x915, web 1440x900 (left sidebar) and 390x844 (bottom tab bar).\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Place tab → top of the landing page, the first thing a signed-in person sees on every load.\n- Recipient push: a new invitation arrives as a push in the Account & security group, Time Sensitive on iOS and HIGH on Android, on by default. The push always opens that invitation's decision screen. If the invitation has since expired, been used or been cancelled, the decision screen shows its own expired, used or revoked frame naming the inviter and one next step. The push never falls back to this page.\n- Sender: the reissue variant appears here, and an in-app NotificationRow carries the same line. Tapping that NotificationRow opens Who lives here scrolled to the Needs reissue rows, the same as Fix.\n- A link opened while signed into a different account opens the decision screen's account-mismatch state, not this list.\nHand-offs:\n- One invitation: \"Review\" opens the invitation decision screen for it.\n- Two or more: \"Review\" opens Your places scrolled to \"Invitations waiting for you\". The durable list is where people decide.\n- Sender \"Fix\" opens Who lives here, scrolled to the Needs reissue rows.\n\nWHO AND WHEN:\n- Recipient: Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM. Priya Raman signed up yesterday. She saved 2418 NE Larkspur Loop as a saved place before moving in, has claimed nothing and verified nothing. Maya Chen invited her an hour ago. She opens Pantopus and lands on Place, not on any homes list.\n- Sender: Maya Chen, owner of Larkspur Loop. Two invitations she sent last week (Mon 12 and Tue 13 Oct) stopped working when the household's invite rules changed.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Make a waiting invitation, and a dead one the sender must send again, impossible to miss, on the screen people actually land on.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: (1) The inviter's name at the start of one line. (2) The home label. (3) The single trailing action \"Review\" (or \"Fix\" for a sender). Nothing else on the page changes.\n\nCONTENT: Use the FIXTURES (Maya Chen; HOME A, label \"Larkspur Loop\"; pending invite priya@example.com, expires Mon 26 Oct). Deltas (list each on Notes):\n- Recipient Priya Raman. Her saved-place row: title \"Larkspur Loop\" with the ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\".\n- Second live invitation: from Dana · a home in Camas · Guest · expires Thu 22 Oct. It also shows the fallback when a home has no label.\n- Dead rows in the list, from other inviters and homes:\n  - Stopped working: \"Marcus Hale · Hazel Dell Ave\" · \"Stopped working when Hazel Dell Ave changed who can invite. We've told Marcus Hale.\"\n  - Expired (an alternative state of Marcus Hale's row, drawn only in frame 12): StatusChip \"Expired Sun 18 Oct\" · caption \"Ask Marcus Hale to send a new one\".\n  - Cancelled by the sender: \"Owen Brandt · Lindell Rd\" · \"Owen Brandt cancelled this invitation\".\n- Expiring-soon frame only: Maya's invitation expires Tue 20 Oct.\n- Sender rows: theo.park@example.com and @rgarcia.\n- Offline time \"as of 5:52 PM\".\n- Worst case (frame 17 only): inviter \"Alexandria Montgomery-Ramirez\" (29 characters) and the home label \"the yellow house on NE 164th Avenue\". The line wraps to two lines, keeps the name whole, and keeps the action on the first line's trailing edge.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION:\n- Use LandingBannerSlot with the exact geometry of the existing mailbox pill: same height, radius, inset and 16pt leading glyph. One sentence with the actor's name first and one trailing 44pt action.\n- Only one banner ever shows. Use the published precedence ladder: invite > reissue > claim receipt > compare arrival > mailbox arrival > sync merge > setup > verify.\n- Dense frame: Priya has an invitation AND an unclaimed saved place AND an unverified profile. Show only the invitation banner. Outside the device frame, draw the suppressed setup and verify banners greyed, labelled \"suppressed by precedence\".\n- Two or more live invitations collapse into one count line. Dead invitations are not counted. Never draw stacked rows or an avatar cluster.\n- Expiring uses LandingBannerSlot V3 as published: line 1 \"Maya Chen invited you to Larkspur Loop\" · Review; line 2 caption \"Expires tomorrow\" in text.primary; the warning glyph replaces the envelope; radius 2xl shape. No badge, no warning-coloured text, no error red.\n- \"Invitations waiting for you\" is a section on Your places, above the saved places. It uses one InviteRow per invitation, received variant (proposed; record it on Notes as a Foundations addition): the same 56pt row, 16pt envelope glyph, bodySmall line 1 and caption line 2 as InviteRow.\n  - line 1: \"<inviter> · <home>\", inviter first\n  - line 2: role · expiry in words (\"Member · expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\"), or the dead row's reason and who can fix it\n  - trailing text action \"Review\" on live rows\n  - overflow: \"Not now\" and \"Decline\" on live rows; \"Remove\" only on dead rows\n  - StatusChip only on an expired row.\n  Dead rows (stopped working, expired, cancelled) stay listed and labelled, never silently dropped. A reissued invitation replaces its dead row.\n- No invitations: the section is absent, never an empty box.\n- Missing data: no inviter name → \"Someone invited you to Larkspur Loop\"; no home label → \"…to a home in Camas\" (the city).\n- Banner fetch failed or still loading: the slot falls through to the next eligible banner by precedence (here the mailbox pill), exactly as with no invitations, and nothing marks the failure or shifts.\n- List still loading after arriving from Review: the section heading shows with WarmingSkeleton rows at 56pt.\n- List fetch failed after arriving from Review: the section shows InlineErrorRow \"We couldn't load your invitations. · Retry\", and the rest of Your places stays usable.\n- The banner has no chart.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS:\n- The action is the only target on the banner; the whole banner is never a hidden second target.\n- The banner has no close glyph. It leaves when the invitation is accepted, declined or expires.\n- \"Not now\" hides that invitation from the banner until a new invitation arrives; the row stays in the list and it never re-asks on its own. With a single invitation, the decision screen's \"Not now\" has the same effect, so a person whose landing is the place file can still clear the banner and let setup and verify return.\n- \"Decline\" records the same decline as the decision screen, with no confirm. The row collapses to \"Declined Maya Chen's invitation. Maya Chen will see that you declined. · Undo\" (InlineUndo). The sender's roster shows \"Declined · Mon 19 Oct\" only after Undo closes.\n- \"Remove\" on a dead row collapses it to \"Removed Marcus Hale's invitation · Undo\" (InlineUndo). No Undo has a timer.\n- \"Retry\" on the list error reloads the section in place.\n- The banner never opens as a modal and never auto-opens the decision screen.\n- Motion: the banner fades in with the page (200ms). If invitations return after first paint, nothing is inserted: the banner appears on the next load or tab return, and the list section on Your places updates in place, below the fold. Under Reduce Motion there is no fade.\n- Arriving at the list from \"Review\" scrolls once and fades a highlight on the section; accessibility focus moves there.\n- No haptics.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: LandingBannerSlot (V1 one invite, V2 count, V3 expiring, V4 sender reissue, S3 offline, as published), InviteRow (received variant, proposed: live, expiring, dead with reason), InlineUndo (Decline, Remove), ScopeChip (\"Saved place · Only you\" on Priya's saved place, unchanged), StatusChip (\"Expired Sun 18 Oct\" on an expired row only), NotificationRow (sender reissue row), PushCopy (the invitation push tray preview), WarmingSkeleton (list rows), InlineErrorRow (list only), OfflineNotice, FreshnessLine (\"You're offline · as of 5:52 PM\" at the top of the page when offline).\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n- The banner is role=status on appearance and reads as one sentence then its action: \"Maya Chen invited you to Larkspur Loop. Review, button.\" Expiring: \"Expires tomorrow, Tuesday 20 October.\"\n- Expiry is in words.\n- Review, Fix, Retry and Undo are 44pt / 48dp / 44px.\n- Each list row is one element with Review as its default action. Not now and Decline (live rows) and Remove (dead rows) are custom actions and also visible in the overflow.\n- \"Declined\" and \"Removed\" are polite status messages; the loading section is announced once as \"Loading\".\n- Offline actions stay focusable and read their reason: \"Review, unavailable, You're offline. Review opens when you're back.\"\n- At AX5 the banner wraps as needed and the action moves below the sentence at full width.\n- The suppressed-banner annotation is outside the device frame and is not UI.\n\nCOPY:\n- Banners: \"Maya Chen invited you to Larkspur Loop\" · \"Review\" | \"You have 2 invitations\" · \"Review\" | expiring line 1 \"Maya Chen invited you to Larkspur Loop\" · \"Review\", line 2 \"Expires tomorrow\" | \"2 invitations need to be sent again\" · \"Fix\" | \"1 invitation needs to be sent again\" · \"Fix\"\n- Offline: page FreshnessLine \"You're offline · as of 5:52 PM\"; caption under the banner \"You're offline. Review opens when you're back.\" (recipient) or \"You're offline. Fix opens when you're back.\" (sender)\n- List: heading \"Invitations waiting for you\"; \"Maya Chen · Larkspur Loop\" · \"Member · expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · \"Review\"; \"Dana · a home in Camas\" · \"Guest · expires in 3 days · Thu 22 Oct\" · \"Review\"; \"Marcus Hale · Hazel Dell Ave\" · \"Stopped working when Hazel Dell Ave changed who can invite. We've told Marcus Hale.\"; expired StatusChip \"Expired Sun 18 Oct\" · \"Ask Marcus Hale to send a new one\"; \"Owen Brandt · Lindell Rd\" · \"Owen Brandt cancelled this invitation\"; overflow \"Not now\" · \"Decline\" (live) and \"Remove\" (dead); \"Declined Maya Chen's invitation. Maya Chen will see that you declined. · Undo\"; \"Declined Dana's invitation. Dana will see that you declined. · Undo\"; \"Removed Marcus Hale's invitation · Undo\"; \"We couldn't load your invitations. · Retry\"\n- Push: title \"Maya Chen invited you\" (21 characters); body \"Larkspur Loop · expires Mon 26 Oct\" (34 characters); hidden-preview placeholder \"Household invitation\".\n- Sender NotificationRow: \"2 invitations need to be sent again\" · \"Mon 19 Oct\" (the home label appears only for readers with more than one home).\n\nEDGE CASES:\n- The long name and long home label wrap and are never truncated.\n- 9 live invitations still show one count line: \"You have 9 invitations\".\n- No invitations: slot collapsed; the next banner by precedence (or none) shows.\n- Offline: the cached banner stays; Review is disabled with the reason.\n- A sender who can no longer invite never sees Fix; Who lives here shows who can.\n- Invitation email opened on a signed-in phone: the link opens the decision screen, not this banner.\n- Link opened while signed into a different account: the decision screen's account-mismatch state handles it; this list only holds invitations addressed to the signed-in account.\n- Priya's saved place makes the setup banner eligible, but it stays suppressed while an invitation waits and she has not chosen Not now.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of two or three stacked banners, draw one banner and the greyed suppressed ones outside the frame, because pile-up hides the one that matters.\n- Instead of an \"Invitations\" card on My Homes, draw the banner here plus the list on Your places, because a new invitee has no home and never opens My Homes.\n- Instead of a \"Couldn't load invitations\" banner, draw the next banner by precedence and keep the layout still, because a broken banner on the landing page reads as a broken app.\n- Instead of a new card style, draw the mailbox pill's geometry, so it reads as arrival context.\n- Instead of \"· Expires tomorrow\" squeezed onto one line in red or amber, draw the published two-line V3 with \"Expires tomorrow\" in text.primary and the warning glyph, because warning hues fail contrast as text and one line breaks the pill.\n- Instead of \"Review\" opening a list for a single invitation, draw it opening that invitation, because one invitation needs no list.\n- Instead of a silent \"Remove\" on a live invitation, or silently dropping a cancelled one, draw \"Decline\" and a labelled cancelled row, because both sides should know what happened.\n- Instead of a mock lock screen, draw the PushCopy tray preview inset, because the contract never mimics system UI.\n\nDONE WHEN:\n- A person with no home sees their invitation on first landing, without opening any homes list.\n- Two or more invitations lead to a durable list showing inviter, home, role and expiry, where declining is cheap, final and tells the person the inviter will know.\n- Dead invitations (stopped working, expired, cancelled) stay visible with their reason.\n- A sender learns that invitations died and can fix them in one tap per row.\n- Only one banner ever renders, and a fetch failure leaves no trace.\n- Every frame reads correctly in greyscale.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f3-invite-banner · ios · 01-densest-one-invite · light — Priya's Your places with the invitation banner; suppressed setup and verify banners greyed outside the frame.\n2. f3-invite-banner · ios · 02-multiple · light — \"You have 2 invitations\".\n3. f3-invite-banner · ios · 03-invitations-list · light — the section with Maya's live row (overflow open: Not now, Decline), Dana's row collapsed to its Declined Undo line, Marcus Hale's stopped-working row and Owen Brandt's cancelled row.\n4. f3-invite-banner · ios · 04-expiring · light — published V3: two lines, \"Expires tomorrow\" caption, warning glyph, radius 2xl.\n5. f3-invite-banner · ios · 05-sender-reissue · light — Maya's place file with \"2 invitations need to be sent again · Fix\", plus the NotificationRow inset annotated \"opens Who lives here at the Needs reissue rows\".\n6. f3-invite-banner · ios · 06-hidden · light — no invitations, slot showing the mailbox pill.\n7. f3-invite-banner · ios · 07-fetch-failed-fallthrough · light — same as frame 6: the mailbox pill renders by precedence; annotation outside the frame \"invitation fetch failed: falls through, nothing shifts\".\n8. f3-invite-banner · ios · 08-offline · light — FreshnessLine, cached banner, Review disabled, \"You're offline. Review opens when you're back.\"\n9. f3-invite-banner · ios · 09-degraded-name · light — \"Someone invited you to Larkspur Loop\".\n10. f3-invite-banner · ios · 10-push · light — PushCopy tray preview inset, collapsed and expanded, plus the hidden-preview \"Household invitation\", captioned \"This is the whole thing.\"\n11. f3-invite-banner · ios · 11-list-loading · light — arriving from Review: section heading with WarmingSkeleton rows.\n12. f3-invite-banner · ios · 12-list-error-and-expired · light — two side-by-side states: the section with InlineErrorRow above; and on retry, Marcus Hale's expired row with StatusChip \"Expired Sun 18 Oct\" and \"Ask Marcus Hale to send a new one\".\n13. f3-invite-banner · web-1440 · 01-densest-one-invite · light — web version of frame 1 with the sidebar.\n14. f3-invite-banner · web-1440 · 02-multiple · light — web version of frame 2.\n15. f3-invite-banner · web-1440 · 05-sender-reissue · light — web version of frame 5.\n16. f3-invite-banner · web-1440 · 03-invitations-list · light — web version of frame 3.\n17. f3-invite-banner · web-390 · 13-worst-case-long-name · light — \"Alexandria Montgomery-Ramirez invited you to the yellow house on NE 164th Avenue\", wrapped, radius 2xl, Review on the first line's trailing edge.\n18. f3-invite-banner · web-390 · 05-sender-reissue · light — frame 5 at 390.\n19. f3-invite-banner · android · 01-densest-one-invite · light — Material 3 version of frame 1.\n20. f3-invite-banner · android · 03-invitations-list · light — Material 3 version of frame 3.\n21. f3-invite-banner · android · 05-sender-reissue · light — Material 3 version of frame 5.\n22. f3-invite-banner · ios · 14-ax5 · light — frame 1 at AX5, action below the sentence.\n23. f3-invite-banner · ios · 15-greyscale · light — frame 4 in greyscale.\n24. f3-invite-banner · ios · 01-densest-one-invite · dark — dark twin of frame 1.\n25. f3-invite-banner · ios · 03-invitations-list · dark — dark twin of frame 3.\n26. f3-invite-banner · ios · 99-Notes · light — invented strings (Marcus Hale and Hazel Dell Ave, chosen because PLACE B is not claimed so Jordan Lee cannot invite; Owen Brandt and Lindell Rd; Alexandria Montgomery-Ramirez and \"the yellow house on NE 164th Avenue\"; the Decline and Remove Undo lines; list error; \"Household invitation\" as a proposed addition to PushCopy's hidden-preview placeholders); \"InviteRow received variant proposed\" as a Foundations addition; the full precedence ladder and fall-through rule; Not now vs Decline, and that the decision screen's Not now has the same effect as the list's; late results wait for the next load; push always opens the decision screen; a link opened under a different account opens the decision screen's account-mismatch state, not this list; omitted states.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: 7-12, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 3: 13-18, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 4: 19-24, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 5: 25-26.",
            "changeLog": [
              "Added a cancelled dead-row variant ('Owen Brandt · Lindell Rd' · 'Owen Brandt cancelled this invitation', Remove only), drawn in frame 3, per derive proposal f3-received-invitations (review major).",
              "Expiring banner now uses published LandingBannerSlot V3 (two lines, caption 'Expires tomorrow', warning glyph, radius 2xl); COPY, INSTEAD OF and artboard 4 updated (review major).",
              "List rows named explicitly as 'InviteRow, received variant (proposed)' with its anatomy, and recorded on Notes as a Foundations addition (review major).",
              "Removed the claim that a different-account link lands on this list; it now opens the decision screen's account-mismatch state, per flow-04 (review major).",
              "Decline line now tells the recipient the inviter will see it: 'Declined Maya Chen's invitation. Maya Chen will see that you declined. · Undo' (review minor; research).",
              "Added a list-loading state with WarmingSkeleton (new artboard 11) (review minor; derive proposal states).",
              "Worst case now uses a long home label, 'the yellow house on NE 164th Avenue', and the artboard is renamed '13-worst-case-long-name' (review minors).",
              "Sender NotificationRow tap destination stated: Who lives here scrolled to the Needs reissue rows (review minor; NotificationRow contract).",
              "Expired row keeps the StatusChip and shortens the caption to 'Ask Marcus Hale to send a new one' (review minor).",
              "Added artboard 12 for the list error and the expired row on retry (review minor).",
