                    "fix": "Name it explicitly: \"InviteRow, received variant (proposed; list on Notes as a Foundations addition): same 56pt row, 16pt envelope glyph, bodySmall line 1 and caption line 2 as InviteRow; line 1 '<inviter> · <home>'; trailing text action 'Review'; overflow Not now · Decline (live) or Remove (dead).\" Add \"InviteRow received variant proposed\" to the Notes artboard."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The prompt contradicts the flow on an invitation link opened while signed into a different account. flow-04 has the decision screen state the mismatch and offer to accept anyway or switch accounts. The prompt sends that case to the Invitations waiting for you list, which only holds invitations addressed to the signed-in account, so the person would land on a list without the invitation they tapped.",
                    "evidence": "prompt WHERE IT LIVES: \"The Invitations waiting for you list is also where an invitation link lands when it is opened while signed into a different account.\" vs flows-spec flow-04: \"Sam is signed in with a different email than the invite. The page states the mismatch and offers to accept anyway or switch accounts.\"",
                    "fix": "Delete that line. Replace it with: \"A link opened while signed into a different account opens the decision screen's account-mismatch state (f3b), not this list.\" Add the same sentence to Notes."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "States that are specified have no artboard: the list load error (InlineErrorRow) and the expired dead-row variant.",
                    "evidence": "LAYOUT: \"the section shows InlineErrorRow \"We couldn't load your invitations. · Retry\"\"; CONTENT: \"Expired variant: \"Expired Sun 18 Oct · Ask Marcus Hale to send a new one\"\". Neither appears in ARTBOARDS.",
                    "fix": "Change artboard 7 or 18 to add \"… · 13-list-error-and-expired · light — section with InlineErrorRow above, and on retry Marcus Hale's expired row with StatusChip 'Expired Sun 18 Oct'\"."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The offline strings differ from the published LandingBannerSlot S3 caption.",
                    "evidence": "prompt: \"Offline: \"You're offline · as of 5:52 PM\" · \"Review needs a connection.\"\" vs 00d S3: \"You're offline. Review opens when you're back.\" / \"You're offline. Fix opens when you're back.\"",
                    "fix": "Use the 00d captions under the banner. Keep \"You're offline · as of 5:52 PM\" only as the page's FreshnessLine."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The precedence list leaves out two steps from the published ladder (claim receipt, sync merge).",
                    "evidence": "prompt: \"invite > reissue > compare arrival > mailbox arrival > setup > verify\" vs 00d: \"invite > reissue > claim receipt > compare arrival > mailbox arrival > sync merge > setup > verify\"",
                    "fix": "Quote the full published ladder."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "Artboard 14 reuses the state name \"01-densest-one-invite\" for different content (the long-name worst case), which makes the manifest ambiguous.",
                    "evidence": "\"14. f3-invite-banner · web-390 · 01-densest-one-invite · light — worst case: \"Alexandria Montgomery-Ramirez…\"\"",
                    "fix": "Rename it to \"f3-invite-banner · web-390 · 13-worst-case-long-name · light\"."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "With a single invitation, the banner has no close control and Review opens the decision screen. A person whose landing is the place file then has no stated way to reach \"Not now\", so the banner suppresses setup and verify for up to 7 days.",
                    "evidence": "\"The banner has no close glyph.\" and \"One invitation: \"Review\" opens the invitation decision screen\"",
                    "fix": "Add: \"The decision screen's 'Not now' has the same effect as the list's Not now (hides it from the banner). Note this on Notes.\""
