                "issues": [
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The signed-out public page, which anyone with a forwarded link can open, prints the full street address with the house number. The inventory lists only the home label and city for this screen, and the prompt's own reason for showing a household count is that a forwarded link must not reveal who lives there. Printing the full address on that same page undercuts that reason, and the prompt never says this is new.",
                    "evidence": "inventory-entries/f3b-invitation-decision.json contents: \"Home, city, inviter, offered role, access window, expiry\"; derive-proposals.md [f3b-invitation-decision]: \"Home label, city, inviter\". The prompt's manifest reads: Home \"2418 NE Larkspur Loop, Vancouver, WA 98684\" and is drawn on frame 01-offer-signed-out. The prompt also says: \"because a forwarded link must not reveal who lives there\".",
                    "fix": "When signed out, show the home label and city (\"Larkspur Loop · Vancouver, WA\") and show the full street line only after sign-in. Otherwise, state on the Notes artboard that the existing public page already shows the full street, and give the reason."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The design doc's exact replacement copy is only partly used. Its second sentence was dropped in favour of the lists, and the Notes artboard doesn't say so. The doc's F3 and F3b sections also disagree: F3b replaces the ownership line, while F3 keeps it. The prompt keeps it as a footnote and doesn't mention the conflict.",
                    "evidence": "Design doc F3b: \"replacing the ownership line: 'This invitation gives you household access. To send neighbor messages or get a residency letter, verify the address yourself.'\" F3: \"keep the existing copy 'This invitation does not grant ownership.'\" The prompt uses only \"This invitation gives you household access.\" and the footnote.",
                    "fix": "Add a Notes line saying the second sentence is replaced by the two lists and the footnote is kept under F3. Alternatively, restore the sentence as the caption under the limits heading."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The secondary button's copy differs from the per-surface change and the flow, and the Notes artboard doesn't record the change.",
                    "evidence": "per-surface-changes and flows-spec flow-04 step 8: \"Start address verification — postcards take about a week\". The prompt has \"Start address verification — postcards take 5–10 days\".",
                    "fix": "Keep \"5–10 days\" so it matches the verify sheet, and list the change on the Notes artboard as a deliberate edit."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The prompt contradicts itself on Priya's account. It says she made an account yesterday and will sign in, but frame 7 is labelled \"after registration\", and the signed-out caption says \"You'll make an account next\".",
                    "evidence": "WHO AND WHEN: \"Priya made an account on her laptop yesterday\"; frame 7: \"the same state after registration, with the token kept\".",
                    "fix": "Relabel frame 7 as \"after sign-in, with the token kept\", or describe the caption as the default for people with no account and show the sign-in link as Priya's path."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
