        "prompts": [
          {
            "id": "f3-household-block",
            "name": "Who lives here with you (household block)",
            "platforms": [
              "web",
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": false,
            "frameCount": 18,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Who lives here with you (household block) · f3-household-block\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screens \"Your place file\" (its People section) and \"Home dashboard\". This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed. You add one card. It is the same card in both hosts, and one dismissal covers both.\n\nATTACH: (1) Your place file, People section, on iOS and web-1440, with the \"Verify this address to send neighbor messages\" banner visible above People. (2) Your place file, the T1 frame for PLACE B. (3) Home dashboard, web-1440, owner view. (4) The Foundations board rows for FactRow, MemberRow, InlineUndo, InviteRow, NotificationAsk, PushCopy and InlineErrorRow.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852 · Android 412x915, plus one frame with the card in a 320dp-wide column · web 390x844 and 1440x900.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: Place tab → Your place file → People section. Both native apps open on Place, and there is no Home tab. A card only on the Home dashboard would reach few new residents, so the place file is the main host. Ways in:\n(a) Scrolling the place file. No navigation is needed.\n(b) The mirror on the Home dashboard: Place → Larkspur Loop → Home dashboard (web /app/homes/:id/dashboard).\n(c) The Members roster's empty state \"Just you at Larkspur Loop · Invite someone\", which offers the ask again.\n(d) Today's \"Next: add the people you live with\" row. It opens the Place tab and scrolls once to this card, with the deep-link highlight. This card is the \"one person\" step of the first-week set.\nThere is no push and no deep link of its own, and the card never opens by itself.\nWhen it shows: only to someone who can invite, while exactly one person is active in the home, or within 7 days of the viewer's own start date if they are the only person who can invite. The 7-day window counts from the viewer's own start date, never the owner's move-in date. Anyone who cannot invite sees the read-only roster line instead (frame 06). It never shows after \"Just me\" or \"Not now\", and never to an inviter once a second person is active.\nHand-offs:\n- \"Invite by email\" opens the invite composer on Email (web modal, iOS wizard, Android bottom sheet).\n- \"Share a link\" opens the same composer on Link. The link warning appears there before any link exists.\n- The composer returns here in the sent state (frame 05).\n\nWHO AND WHEN:\n- Frames 01–05 and 12: Maya Chen, owner of HOME A, on the couch scrolling the Place tab, Mon 5 Oct 2026, 6:10 PM. Maya joined HOME A on Thu 1 Oct. Nobody else has joined or been invited yet. Her address is not verified yet, so the verify banner shows.\n- Frame 06: Sam Ortega on Tue 13 Oct. He joined through Maya's invitation on Sat 10 Oct, three days earlier.\n- Frame 07: Maya on TODAY (Mon 19 Oct). Sam has joined, and Priya's invitation is pending. Maya's address was confirmed by postcard on Thu 15 Oct, so there is no verify banner.\n- Frame 08: Jordan Lee at PLACE B on TODAY.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Ask a new resident once who else lives here, and make inviting them take two taps on the screen they actually see.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS:\n1. The title \"Who lives here with you?\".\n2. The sentence saying what gets shared and what never does.\n3. The filled \"Invite by email\" button. This is the single primary action.\nIn frames that show it, the verify banner above stays the loudest element on the screen.\n\nCONTENT (exact strings):\n- Title: \"Who lives here with you?\"\n- Body, one paragraph: \"Add the people you live with. They see the same pickup day, calendar and bills. Nothing about your home is shared with anyone else.\"\n- Primary button: \"Invite by email\". Secondary button: \"Share a link\". Declines: \"Just me\" and \"Not now\".\n- Host banner above the card in frames 01–05, 09–15. Draw it and leave it unchanged: \"Verify this address to send neighbor messages\".\n- Deltas:\n  - Frame 05 InviteRow caption: \"sam.ortega@example.com · Member · sent Today · Expires in 7 days · Mon 12 Oct\", with an inline \"Resend\".\n  - Frame 07 InviteRow caption: \"priya@example.com · Member · sent Mon 19 Oct · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\", with an inline \"Resend\".\n  - Frame dates Mon 5 Oct and Tue 13 Oct. Join dates Thu 1 Oct (Maya) and Sat 10 Oct (Sam) match the Members roster prompt.\n  - Example join notification: title \"Sam joined Larkspur Loop\" (24 characters), body \"Can see the calendar and bills\" (30 characters).\n- Worst case: the card in a 320dp column, with the full body wrapping to five lines.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION:\n- Card: one card on surface.raised, radius lg, shadow sm, with a visible card edge in dark mode. This is a two-button block, not a hero. No accent fill, no illustration and no avatar placeholders: nobody exists to draw yet.\n- Order inside the card:\n  1. The title, in h3.\n  2. The body, in bodySmall and text.secondary. It wraps and is never cut off.\n  3. \"Invite by email\" (filled, primary.700) and \"Share a link\" (outlined), side by side. In columns narrower than 360, stack them full width.\n  4. \"Just me\" and \"Not now\" on the last line, as two text buttons, left-aligned, 8dp apart. Both use the secondary button's label size and weight, in text.strong. They must not look greyed or muted, because declining is a real answer.\n- The card must not out-shout the banner above it. The banner keeps its tint and glyph. The card has neither.\n- If the member count cannot load, draw no card. The People section's own error row stays in place.\n- At T1 (frame 08), draw the FactRow in its not-at-this-tier variant instead of the card: label and reason in text.secondary (never text.muted), no chevron, no CTA.\n- Every InviteRow on this surface shows its full anatomy: mail glyph, recipient, the caption with sent date and expiry in words, the inline 44pt \"Resend\", and the overflow.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS:\n- \"Just me\", saving: while the choice saves, the full card stays exactly as it is: title, body and all four buttons. \"Just me\" shows its busy state. Nothing disappears before the server confirms the save.\n- \"Just me\", saved: once the server confirms, the card collapses in place to the InlineUndo \"Just you, then. · Undo\". The choice is saved on the server and synced to every device, and it also hides the dashboard mirror. Undo stays until Maya leaves the screen, with no timer.\n- \"Just me\", next visit: People shows the MemberRow empty variant \"Just you at Larkspur Loop · Invite someone\" (frame 04). This is a finished state, with no badge and no \"missing\" count.\n- \"Just me\", save fails: the card stays unchanged and retries quietly, with no toast. If the retries still fail, an InlineErrorRow in its save-failed variant appears directly under the unchanged card: \"We couldn't save 'Just me' · Retry\".\n- \"Not now\": the card collapses to a quiet FactRow, \"Add the people you live with · Add\". \"Not now\" is also saved on the server, syncs to every device and hides the dashboard mirror (one dismissal). The card never comes back by itself.\n- Sent state (frame 05): the card becomes the InviteRow for sam.ortega@example.com with its full caption and \"Resend\".\n  - Below the InviteRow sits a NotificationAsk card row: \"Hear when someone joins Larkspur Loop? Quiet notifications, no sound.\"\n  - Directly under that sentence, draw a PushCopy tray preview inset, captioned \"This is the whole thing.\" Title: \"Sam joined Larkspur Loop\". Body: \"Can see the calendar and bills\". Under the inset, annotate: \"Example — the name they sign up with appears here; the email address never does.\"\n  - Next to that inset, draw a small second inset labelled \"Lock screen, previews hidden\" with the title \"Household update\" and no body. This is the only place \"Household update\" appears.\n  - Buttons: \"Turn on\" and \"Not now\".\n  - If notifications have never been asked, \"Turn on\" goes straight to the OS prompt. There is never a second \"Yes\".\n  - If notifications are already allowed, \"Turn on\" switches household activity on with no OS prompt.\n  - Either way, the row then reads \"Household activity on · Undo\". Undo stays until Maya leaves the screen.\n- Motion: collapse is a height change plus a cross-fade, 200ms or less. With Reduce Motion, use a cross-fade only.\n- Haptics: none on this card. The light confirm tick belongs to the composer's Send.\n- Every action is a plain tap. Nothing uses swipe-to-dismiss.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED:\n- FactRow: missing; not-at-this-tier (\"Claim this address first\", label and reason in text.secondary, never text.muted, no chevron, no CTA); declined.\n- MemberRow: collapsed roster line; empty.\n- InlineUndo: declined ask; household activity turned on.\n- InviteRow: pending, with full caption and inline Resend.\n- NotificationAsk: card row; iOS denied; Android denied once; Android blocked.\n- PushCopy: tray preview inset (household join example) and the lock-screen public version (\"Household update\").\n- LockedActionRow: names who can act.\n- InlineErrorRow: save failed.\n- OfflineNotice: per-control reason caption.\n- WarmingSkeleton: row skeleton at the card's final height.\n- ScopeChip: host header only.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n- Reading order: People heading, title, body, Invite by email, Share a link, Just me, Not now.\n- Spoken labels: \"Invite someone by email\", \"Share an invite link\", \"Just me. No one else lives here\", \"Not now\", \"Resend invitation to sam.ortega@example.com\".\n- InviteRow expiry is read in words: \"expires in 7 days, Monday October 12\".\n- Polite live-region announcements: \"Just you, then. Undo available\", \"Invitation sent\", \"Household activity on\", and \"We couldn't save Just me. Retry available\".\n- The tray preview is read as \"Example notification: Sam joined Larkspur Loop, can see the calendar and bills.\" The lock-screen inset is read as \"Example with previews hidden: Household update.\"\n- Targets are 44pt, 48dp or 44px, with 8dp gaps.\n- At AX5, every button is full width and stacked, and the body wraps.\n- The primary button is told apart by its fill and position, never by hue alone.\n\nCOPY: Every string above, plus:\n- Offline caption under the disabled buttons: \"You're offline. Invites need a connection.\"\n- Error row in the People section, not in the card: \"We couldn't load who lives here · Retry\"\n- Member read-only roster (Sam): \"You and Maya live here · View\"\n- Locked row (Sam): \"Maya Chen can invite people here.\"\n- iOS, notifications denied, under the ask: \"Notifications are off for Pantopus · Open Settings\". This opens the notification settings page.\n- Android, denied once: \"Turn on\" asks again, one time only.\n- Android, blocked: \"Notifications are off for Pantopus · Open Settings\".\n\nEDGE CASES:\n- A 320dp column: frame 02.\n- T1 (PLACE B): no invite controls.\n- A pending invite and no one joined yet: only the InviteRow, no card.\n- Many residents, owner view: \"You, Sam and 3 others live here · View\", with Priya's InviteRow still below, because she has not joined.\n- Offline: all four buttons are disabled, show the offline reason and stay focusable.\n- Slow network: show the skeleton only after 1s.\n- A member who cannot manage people: no invite buttons and no card, even in their first 7 days. Draw the read-only roster line in its viewer-first form, \"You and Maya live here · View\". This form replaces the older \"You and 2 others live here\" wording after someone has joined: same meaning, with the other person named.\n- Save of \"Just me\" fails: the card stays unchanged, retries quietly and shows no toast. If that fails too, show the InlineErrorRow \"We couldn't save 'Just me' · Retry\".\n- Previews hidden on the lock screen: the join notice shows only \"Household update\".\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of a full-bleed onboarding hero, modal or coach mark, draw one quiet card in the People section — because asks belong inline, where they get completed.\n- Instead of ghost avatars or an illustration, draw text and buttons only — because there is nobody to show yet.\n- Instead of a greyed, shrunken \"Just me\", draw it at full label weight next to \"Not now\" — because living alone is a complete answer.\n- Instead of cutting the body to fit, let it wrap — because the privacy sentence is why people agree to invite.\n- Instead of a permanent \"Just me\", draw Undo plus the roster's \"Invite someone\" — because a mis-tap must not be a dead end.\n- Instead of collapsing the card the moment \"Just me\" is tapped, keep it whole until the save succeeds — because a choice that silently fails must not look done.\n- Instead of an email address in the notification, draw the joiner's name and the home — because the preview must match what arrives, and addresses do not belong on a lock screen.\n- Instead of \"Hear when Sam joins?\" in the ask, name the home — because an email invitation knows only an address until the person joins.\n- Instead of hiding the dashboard copy separately, share one dismissal — because two dismissals drift apart.\n\nDONE WHEN:\n- Maya sees the ask on Place without navigating.\n- Invite by email reaches the composer in one tap.\n- \"Just me\" is as easy to hit as Invite. It is undoable, never vanishes before it saves, and ends with no nag.\n- \"Just me\" and \"Not now\" each hide the card on every device and on the dashboard at once.\n- The card appears once per home per person, only to someone who can invite, and never after someone joins.\n- Sam never sees invite buttons, and his roster line starts with \"You\".\n- The notification ask shows the notification that would actually arrive, with no email address.\n- Every InviteRow shows its sent date, its expiry in words and Resend.\n- The privacy sentence survives 320dp intact.\n- Every frame reads in greyscale.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f3-household-block · ios · 01-visible · light — Maya's place file on Mon 5 Oct: verify banner above, full card.\n2. f3-household-block · android · 02-visible-320-column · light — the card in a 320dp column, with a five-line body and stacked buttons.\n3. f3-household-block · ios · 03-just-me-undo · light — after the server confirms: \"Just you, then. · Undo\" in place.\n4. f3-household-block · ios · 04-after-decline · light — two phone frames side by side inside this artboard. The left one is labelled \"After Just me\" and shows the next visit: \"Just you at Larkspur Loop · Invite someone\". The right one is labelled \"After Not now\" and shows the FactRow \"Add the people you live with · Add\". Annotate both: \"Saved on the server · same on every device and on the dashboard.\"\n5. f3-household-block · ios · 05-invite-sent-ask · light — the InviteRow \"sam.ortega@example.com · Member · sent Today · Expires in 7 days · Mon 12 Oct · Resend\", plus \"Hear when someone joins Larkspur Loop?\" with the example tray preview \"Sam joined Larkspur Loop / Can see the calendar and bills\", its annotation, the small \"Lock screen, previews hidden\" inset reading \"Household update\", and \"Turn on\" / \"Not now\". Annotate: \"Already allowed → Turn on switches on with no OS prompt.\"\n6. f3-household-block · ios · 06-member-read-only · light — Sam on Tue 13 Oct: \"You and Maya live here · View\" plus the LockedActionRow \"Maya Chen can invite people here.\"; no card and no verify banner above.\n7. f3-household-block · ios · 07-collapsed-roster · light — Maya on TODAY after Sam joined: \"You and Sam live here · View\", plus the InviteRow \"priya@example.com · Member · sent Mon 19 Oct · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct · Resend\" (owner view); no card, and no verify banner, because Maya's address was confirmed by postcard on Thu 15 Oct.\n8. f3-household-block · ios · 08-t1-saved-place · light — Jordan at PLACE B with \"Saved place · Only you\": the FactRow \"Add the people you live with / Claim this address first\" with label and reason in text.secondary, no chevron, no CTA.\n9. f3-household-block · ios · 09-loading · light — a skeleton at the card's real height.\n10. f3-household-block · android · 10-offline · light — the four buttons disabled, with \"You're offline. Invites need a connection.\" Annotate the Android notification rules: denied once, \"Turn on\" asks again one time; blocked, \"Notifications are off for Pantopus · Open Settings\".\n11. f3-household-block · ios · 11-save-retrying · light — two steps side by side. Step 1: the full card unchanged, \"Just me\" busy, annotated \"saving, quiet retry, no toast\". Step 2: the same card with the InlineErrorRow \"We couldn't save 'Just me' · Retry\" under it.\n12. f3-household-block · web-1440 · 12-dashboard-mirror · light — Maya on Mon 5 Oct, 6:10 PM (the same moment as frame 01): the same card on the Home dashboard, with no floating button.\n13. f3-household-block · web-390 · 13-visible · light — the place file on mobile web, verify banner above, full card.\n14. f3-household-block · ios · 14-ax5 · light — frame 01 at AX5, all buttons stacked full width.\n15. f3-household-block · ios · 15-greyscale · light — frame 01 in greyscale.\n16. f3-household-block · ios · 01-visible · dark — the dark twin of frame 01.\n17. f3-household-block · ios · 05-invite-sent-ask · dark — the dark twin of frame 05.\n18. Notes — four parts:\n- Assumptions:\n  - After someone joins, the viewer-first, named roster line (\"You and Maya live here\") replaces \"You and N others\". The invitation decision's accepted frame and the Members roster's collapsed line must use the same viewer-first, named form. The count-only form (\"Sam Ortega and 2 others live here\") stays only on the pre-acceptance invitation offer.\n  - The example join notification uses the name the person signs up with. \"Larkspur Loop\" in its title is the object of the sentence, not the multi-place label; the body carries no place label because Maya has one place.\n  - \"Household update\" is used only when previews are hidden on the lock screen.\n  - Join dates Thu 1 Oct / Sat 10 Oct differ from the Foundations MemberRow specimen dates (Mon 12 / Tue 13 Oct); the specimen dates are illustrative.\n  - Maya's address was confirmed by postcard on Thu 15 Oct, so frames on or after that date have no verify banner.\n- Every invented string (list each one):\n  - the frame dates Mon 5 Oct and Tue 13 Oct\n  - sam.ortega@example.com, \"sent Today\", \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 12 Oct\"\n  - \"sent Mon 19 Oct\" and \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" on Priya's row\n  - \"Hear when someone joins Larkspur Loop? Quiet notifications, no sound.\"\n  - \"Sam joined Larkspur Loop\" / \"Can see the calendar and bills\"\n  - \"Example — the name they sign up with appears here; the email address never does.\"\n  - \"Lock screen, previews hidden\"\n  - \"Turn on\"\n  - \"Household activity on · Undo\"\n  - \"You and Maya live here · View\", \"You and Sam live here · View\", \"You, Sam and 3 others live here · View\"\n  - \"Maya Chen can invite people here.\"\n  - \"We couldn't save 'Just me' · Retry\"\n  - \"You're offline. Invites need a connection.\" and \"We couldn't load who lives here · Retry\"\n  - \"Notifications are off for Pantopus · Open Settings\"\n  - any other string you add\n- Omitted states:\n  - The iOS-denied and Android denied-once and blocked notification variants are annotated, not drawn as frames.\n- Hand-off note: the one-time announcement that members can now see more lives on the Members roster, not on this card.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1–6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: artboards 7–12, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 3: artboards 13–18.",
            "changeLog": [
              "Tray preview now shows the real join notice 'Sam joined Larkspur Loop' / 'Can see the calendar and bills' labelled as an example, with no email address; 'Household update' kept only on an annotated lock-screen previews-hidden inset; spoken label, Notes and INSTEAD OF updated (review major, PushCopy, P6)",
              "'Not now' is saved on the server, synced across devices and hides the dashboard mirror (review minor, brief 2.7)",
              "Both InviteRows carry the full caption with sent date, relative expiry ('Expires in 7 days · Mon 12 Oct' / 'sent Mon 19 Oct · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct') and inline Resend; strings listed on Notes (review minor, contract InviteRow, house style dates, 00a)",
              "Added 'Turn on' behaviour when notifications are already allowed (review minor, NotificationAsk states)",
              "Notes now require the invitation decision's accepted frame and the roster collapsed line to use the same viewer-first named form; count-only wording kept for the pre-acceptance offer (review minor, research-findings 1025)",
              "Rewrote the trigger rule: only inviters see the card; non-inviters see the read-only roster line; never after a second person is active (review minor)",
              "Frame 07 has no verify banner (Maya confirmed by postcard Thu 15 Oct); Notes line reconciles join dates with 00c specimen dates (review minor)",
              "Offline caption changed to the Foundations wording 'You're offline. Invites need a connection.'; T1 row uses text.secondary, never text.muted (review minor, house style token usage)",
              "Removed internal flow step reference from Hand-offs (review minor)"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "f3-member-home-dashboard",
            "name": "Home dashboard, member view",
            "platforms": [
              "web",
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": false,
            "frameCount": 16,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Home dashboard, member view · f3-member-home-dashboard\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Home dashboard\". This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed.\n\nATTACH:\n1. Home dashboard, owner view, on iOS, Android and web-1440, showing all six cards in their current order.\n2. The Foundations board rows for LockedActionRow, MemberRow, InviteRow, BillRow, DateRow and ProvenanceMark.\n3. Invitation decision, accepted frame (the previous step).\n4. Nearby, neighbor-message compose (for the reference inset in frame 03).\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852 · Android 412x915 · web 390x844 and 1440x900.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE:\n- Path: Place tab → Your place file → \"Larkspur Loop\" → Home dashboard. Web URL: /app/homes/:id/dashboard.\n- Ways in:\n  - \"Open Home\" on the accepted invitation screen.\n  - The home row in Your places (this is the former My Homes list, now folded into Your places).\n  - Household notifications whose object has no page of its own.\n- What arrives: a person who has just joined. Today has already said once that it now uses Larkspur Loop.\n- Next steps:\n  - \"Open calendar\" goes to the household calendar, where Sam can add an event.\n  - \"View\" on Bills goes to the bills list.\n  - \"Verify address\" on a verification row opens the verify sheet with its reason.\n  - The neighbor-message lock lives in Nearby's compose, not on this dashboard.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Sam Ortega, a member of HOME A, on TODAY, Mon 19 Oct 2026, 6:10 PM. Maya Chen is the owner. Sam joined on Sat 10 Oct through Maya's invitation. This is a return visit: he is checking what he can do here.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Give a co-resident a useful, readable dashboard without manage rights, where every limit says who can act.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS:\n1. The Today card, with \"2 people live here\" and \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow\".\n2. The Calendar card, with its live footer.\n3. The Bills card total.\nThe single primary action is \"Open calendar\".\n\nCONTENT:\nMembers can now see the member list, read and edit the calendar, and read the bills. They could already read and edit tasks. So the Members, Calendar and Bills cards appear for members for the first time. Keep the six cards in the screenshot's order. Do not re-rank them for members. The one-time announcement of this wider access lives on the Members roster; do not draw it here.\n\nToday card:\n- The member count now shows for members: \"2 people live here\". It used to be blank for members.\n- Pickup line: \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow\".\n\nMembers card:\n- Heading: \"2 people live here\".\n- MemberRows: \"Maya Chen · Owner · joined Thu 1 Oct\" and \"Sam Ortega · You · joined Sat 10 Oct\".\n- Sam's own row has an overflow menu containing \"Leave Larkspur Loop\". The leave sheet belongs to the Members roster, so do not draw it here.\n- Owner view: adds the InviteRow \"priya@example.com · Member · sent Mon 19 Oct · Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" with its inline \"Resend\".\n\nCalendar card:\nThree DateRows from the household calendar, which is the only calendar. Delete the old separate 7-day household calendar that used to sit in this card.\n1. \"Recycling and garbage — Tomorrow\", with the hollow mark.\n   - Caption, identical for Sam and Maya: \"○ On record, not confirmed · Waste Connections · city pickup schedule\".\n   - Spoken mark name: \"on record, not confirmed\".\n2. \"Maya's parents visiting — in 3 days · Thu 22 Oct\".\n3. \"Online or mail voter registration for Tue 3 Nov must arrive by — in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\".\n   - Filled mark, with the first-occurrence word \"● Official\" printed beside it.\n   - ScopeChip \"Statewide — WA\".\n   - This filled mark assumes the row was checked by hand against the Washington Secretary of State. Beside the card, draw one small annotated inset of the same row in its unchecked form: hollow mark with \"○ On record, not confirmed\".\nThe first-occurrence mark words on this card are \"○ On record, not confirmed\" and \"● Official\". Print each word once, next to its first glyph.\n\nBills card:\n- Summary: \"3 upcoming · $306.17 through Mon 2 Nov\".\n- Caption: \"Everyone at Larkspur Loop can see these\".\n- BillRows: \"Clark Public Utilities · $142.18 · due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\" and \"City of Vancouver water · $84.00 · due in 9 days · Wed 28 Oct\".\n- Totals count only bills the household can see. Bills set to Only me are never counted on a member's card. This fixture has none, so both views show $306.17.\n\nTasks card:\n- Summary: \"2 open\".\n- Row: \"Change furnace filter · due in 5 days · Sat 24 Oct\".\n\nDocuments & Security card: keep its existing content, plus the verification row described below.\n\nRevoked panel:\n- \"Your access to Larkspur Loop ended.\"\n- \"Your saved places and private dates stay with you.\"\n- Button: \"Go to your places\".\n\nWorst case: all six cards, three role-lock footers (Members, Bills, Documents & Security), one verification row, and a partial error on Bills, at AX5.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION:\nDefine ONE member treatment and apply it to every card. Header, body and density stay pixel-identical to the owner's card. Only the footer action row changes, apart from viewer-relative captions and totals, and the verification row on Documents & Security.\n\nCards where the member lacks the action (Members, Bills, Documents & Security):\n- In the same row, replace the owner's control cluster with a LockedActionRow in its names-who-can-act variant, plus a quiet \"View\" right-aligned.\n- The reason text is plain text with no link. It uses one form:\n  - \"Maya Chen can invite people here.\"\n  - \"Maya Chen can add bills and mark them paid.\"\n  - \"Maya Chen can manage documents and security here.\"\n- Verifying the address never grants these, so these rows never link to verification.\n\nCards where the member holds the action (Calendar, Tasks):\n- The footer is identical to the owner's.\n- Calendar: \"Add an event\" is the left text action and \"Open calendar\" is the right-aligned text action. Both use the owner's existing footer styles, and neither is filled.\n- Tasks: \"Add a task · View\".\n\nOwner footers:\n- Members: \"Invite someone · View\".\n- Bills: \"Add a bill · View\". Mark paid lives on the bill itself, never on a dashboard card.\n- Documents & Security: keeps its existing cluster.\n\nFloating button: draw none in either view. The owner's invite lives in the Members card footer.\n\nThe iOS header: if the screenshot shows the green \"Household access\" chip, remove it. Nothing on the screen marks Sam's membership as a verification status.\n\nAccent: keep the identity.home accent the screenshot already uses.\n\nControls a member can see: each one is either live, or absent with a LockedActionRow stating the reason. None is ever visible and dead. This replaces the old Android behaviour where a member tapped a visible manage control and nothing happened.\n\nVerification:\n- Household members see no \"Verify this address\" banner at the top.\n- Address verification appears only on the actions that need it. On this dashboard, that is the Documents & Security card: \"Address verification needed to get a residency letter · Verify address\".\n- If the owner has turned off attestation and Sam has no other method, the row shows the reason with no link: \"Address verification isn't available for this home right now\".\n\nMarks:\n- The pickup row's mark is hollow because HOME A's pickup is on record from the city schedule and not yet confirmed as of TODAY. It matches the pickup card and Today's strip at this moment.\n- A tick appears only on a row the viewer added. Never draw a tick or the word \"confirmed\" on the pickup row.\n\nDegraded states:\n- A card whose data failed keeps its frame and shows an InlineErrorRow.\n- A card the viewer may not see is absent, with no ghost card.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS:\n- Each card header, and each \"View\", opens its full screen.\n- Role-limit rows: the reason text is not a target. Tapping it does nothing and announces nothing new. \"View\" is the row's only action.\n- Verification rows: only these open the verify sheet, and only through their \"Verify address\" link. The sheet shows that row's reason, the unchanged \"What this unlocks\" list as Sam's next step, and offers \"Ask Maya Chen to confirm\".\n- Tapping a DateRow opens that date. Tapping a BillRow opens the bill.\n- Sam's row overflow offers \"Leave Larkspur Loop\", which opens the roster's leave sheet.\n- Role change during the session:\n  - The footers re-render in place with no layout jump.\n  - The screen announces \"You're now an admin at Larkspur Loop.\"\n- Revoked access:\n  - The cards are replaced by one calm panel, and cached household data is removed.\n  - If a sheet is open, it closes first.\n- Motion: 200ms cross-fades only. With Reduce Motion, content swaps with no movement.\n- No haptics on this screen, and no gesture-only actions.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED:\n- LockedActionRow: names who can act, no link; verification, with the \"Verify address\" link; verification unavailable, no link; offline.\n- MemberRow: owner, member, you (with the \"Leave Larkspur Loop\" overflow).\n- InviteRow: pending, owner view only, with full caption and Resend.\n- BillRow: member. The list header states scope and total.\n- DateRow: pickup, deadline, home event.\n- ProvenanceMark: hollow and filled, each with its first-occurrence word.\n- ScopeChip: \"Statewide — WA\", and \"Larkspur Loop · Your household\" in the header.\n- WarmingSkeleton: card-shaped.\n- InlineErrorRow.\n- FreshnessLine.\n- OfflineNotice.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n- Reading order: the header and ScopeChip, then the cards in visual order. Each card is read as one group: heading, content, footer.\n- A role-limit footer reads as plain text followed by its button. Example: \"Maya Chen can add bills and mark them paid. View bills.\"\n- A verification row reads as: \"Address verification needed to get a residency letter. Verify address, button.\"\n- Pickup row, both views: \"Recycling and garbage, tomorrow, Waste Connections, on record, not confirmed.\"\n- Voter row: \"Online or mail voter registration for November 3 must arrive by Monday October 26, in 7 days, statewide, Washington, official.\"\n- Merged BillRow label: \"Clark Public Utilities, 142 dollars 18 cents, due in 4 days, Friday October 23, upcoming.\"\n- Polite live regions: the role change, the revoked panel, and \"You're offline\".\n- Targets are 44pt, 48dp or 44px.\n- At AX5, footers stack with \"View\" under the reason, and nothing truncates.\n- Lock and mark glyphs always sit next to words.\n\nCOPY: Every string above, plus:\n- Error: \"We couldn't load Larkspur Loop just now · Retry\"\n- Partial error: \"We couldn't load bills just now · Retry bills\"\n- Offline: \"You're offline · as of 6:04 PM\" and \"Adding needs a connection.\"\n- Loading: no text.\n\nEDGE CASES:\n- A long home label, \"Grandma's place on Larkspur Loop · Your household\": it wraps rather than truncating.\n- Six or more people: \"8 people live here\", with the first three rows and \"View\".\n- 14 upcoming bills: \"14 upcoming · $2,418.60 through Mon 30 Nov\".\n- No bills: \"Checked — no upcoming bills\".\n- An owner with one Only-me bill: her total includes it, Sam's does not.\n- A household with a guest who cannot see bills:\n  - The guest's Bills card is absent.\n  - On Maya's and Sam's cards, the caption names the people instead of \"Everyone\": \"Maya and Sam can see these\".\n- Attestation turned off by the owner: the verification row shows \"Address verification isn't available for this home right now\", with no link.\n- Seeded voter row not yet checked by hand: hollow mark, \"○ On record, not confirmed\".\n- Slow network: skeletons appear after 1s only.\n- Offline: cached cards stay. \"Add an event\" and \"Add a task\" are disabled and keep their reason.\n- Access revoked while a sheet is open: the sheet closes first.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of a different read-only look per card, draw one footer rule applied six times — because consistency teaches the rule once.\n- Instead of hiding Members, Calendar or Bills from members, draw them in full — because seeing them is the point of the change.\n- Instead of a greyed manage button with no reason, draw the LockedActionRow naming Maya Chen — because a silent dead tap reads as a broken app.\n- Instead of sending role limits to the verify sheet, draw them as plain text with only \"View\" — because verifying never lets Sam add bills or invite people.\n- Instead of a \"Request access\" flow, draw only the owner's name — because no such flow exists.\n- Instead of \"Mark paid\" on the Bills card, draw \"View\" — because a mis-tap there would notify the whole household.\n- Instead of a tick or \"confirmed\" on the pickup row, draw the hollow mark with \"On record, not confirmed\" — because nobody has confirmed HOME A's pickup yet, and the pickup card and strip say the same.\n- Instead of a verify banner or a \"Household access\" chip at the top, draw locked rows only on the actions that need verification — because Sam just joined and is not missing a setup step.\n\nDONE WHEN:\n- Sam can see who lives here, read and add to the calendar, and read the bills without asking Maya.\n- Every role limit names Maya Chen and offers \"View\".\n- Only verification rows lead to verification, and the verify sheet shows \"What this unlocks\".\n- Owner and member cards differ only in their footer row, plus the verification row on Documents & Security.\n- No card shows a visible control that does nothing.\n- No mark or caption claims more than the record shows, and none says Sam did something Maya did.\n- The dashboard's pickup mark matches the pickup card and Today's strip.\n- The revoked frame says what he keeps.\n- All of this reads in greyscale and at AX5.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f3-member-home-dashboard · ios · 01-member-view · light — Sam's six cards, with the locked footers, the live Calendar and Tasks footers, the hollow pickup row and the first-occurrence mark words; beside the Calendar card, the small annotated unchecked-voter-row inset.\n2. f3-member-home-dashboard · web-1440 · 02-owner-vs-member · light — the owner's and member's Members and Bills cards side by side, with the differing footer rows annotated. Owner footers: \"Invite someone · View\" and \"Add a bill · View\"; the owner's Members card also shows Priya's InviteRow. Annotate that the rest of the owner layout matches frame 11, and that Documents & Security also differs by its verification row.\n3. f3-member-home-dashboard · ios · 03-verification-locked · light — the residency-letter LockedActionRow in Documents & Security, plus a labelled inset \"Nearby · neighbor-message compose, for reference\" with \"Address verification needed to send neighbor messages · Verify address\".\n4. f3-member-home-dashboard · ios · 04-access-revoked · light — the calm panel with \"Go to your places\".\n5. f3-member-home-dashboard · ios · 05-role-changed · light — footers now showing owner-level controls, with the announcement line.\n6. f3-member-home-dashboard · ios · 06-loading · light — card-shaped skeletons in place.\n7. f3-member-home-dashboard · android · 07-member-view · light — frame 01 on Material 3. Annotation: \"Replaces the old Android behaviour where tapping a manage control did nothing; every former floating button or quick action is now absent or shows a LockedActionRow.\"\n8. f3-member-home-dashboard · android · 08-error · light — a cold-load error, and next to it a Bills-only InlineErrorRow.\n9. f3-member-home-dashboard · android · 09-offline · light — cached cards, the offline FreshnessLine, and the disabled adds with their reason.\n10. f3-member-home-dashboard · web-390 · 10-member-view · light — mobile web.\n11. f3-member-home-dashboard · web-1440 · 11-member-view · light — Sam's full dashboard in the host's primary web layout, with no floating button.\n12. f3-member-home-dashboard · ios · 12-ax5 · light — the worst case at AX5: six cards, three role-lock footers, one verification row and the Bills partial error.\n13. f3-member-home-dashboard · ios · 13-greyscale · light — frame 01 in greyscale.\n14. f3-member-home-dashboard · ios · 01-member-view · dark — the dark twin of frame 01.\n15. f3-member-home-dashboard · ios · 04-access-revoked · dark — the dark twin of frame 04.\n16. Notes — five parts:\n- Assumptions:\n  - The WA registration deadline row has been checked by hand against the Secretary of State. Until it is, draw the hollow mark with \"○ On record, not confirmed\" (inset on frame 01).\n  - HOME A's pickup is on record, not confirmed, as of TODAY, matching Foundations.\n  - My Homes is folded into Your places; its home row is the entry point.\n  - The one-time announcement that members can now see who lives here, the calendar and bills lives on the Members roster.\n  - The neighbor-message lock lives in Nearby compose, not on the Today card.\n  - Join dates Thu 1 Oct / Sat 10 Oct differ from the Foundations MemberRow specimen dates; the specimen dates are illustrative.\n- Every invented string (list each one):\n  - the join dates\n  - \"Leave Larkspur Loop\"\n  - \"Change furnace filter · due in 5 days · Sat 24 Oct\"\n  - \"Maya's parents visiting\"\n  - \"sent Mon 19 Oct\" on Priya's row\n  - \"Maya Chen can invite people here.\"\n  - \"Maya Chen can add bills and mark them paid.\"\n  - \"Maya Chen can manage documents and security here.\"\n  - \"Invite someone · View\"\n  - \"Go to your places\"\n  - \"city pickup schedule\"\n  - \"Address verification isn't available for this home right now\"\n  - \"Maya and Sam can see these\"\n  - \"Grandma's place on Larkspur Loop · Your household\"\n  - the role-change line\n  - the error, offline and \"Checked — no upcoming bills\" lines\n  - \"as of 6:04 PM\"\n  - the edge-case totals\n  - any other string you add\n- Omitted states:\n  - The phase-2 KeeperStrip, permission-limited: \"Ollie · On it\", whose mood line uses only facts the viewer may see.\n  - The leave sheet (belongs to the Members roster).\n- Engineering note, in plain words: on Android, remove the check that makes a member's tap on a manage control silently do nothing.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1–6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: artboards 7–12, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 3: artboards 13–16.",
            "changeLog": [
              "Pickup row now hollow with 'On record, not confirmed · Waste Connections · city pickup schedule' for both viewers; removed 'Maya confirmed this day', the tick rule paragraph, its spoken label, Notes entry and INSTEAD OF line; replaced with a hollow-mark INSTEAD OF (review major, 00c/00b fixtures, invariant 1)",
              "Voter registration row: filled mark conditioned on a hand check, with an annotated hollow unchecked inset and Notes assumption (review major, design doc F6 and 7.6)",
              "Noted that the widened-access announcement lives on the Members roster (review minor, research-findings 2222)",
              "Restored My Homes as folded into Your places, in entry points and Notes (review minor, inventory)",
              "Reworded owner/member diff: footer row only, apart from viewer-relative captions/totals and the Documents & Security verification row (review minor x2)",
              "Verify sheet now shows the unchanged 'What this unlocks' list (review minor, design doc F3b)",
              "Long-label edge case uses 'Grandma's place on Larkspur Loop · Your household', listed as invented (review minor)",
              "Bill and task dates now carry relative counts; BillRow spoken label updated (review minor, house style, 00a)",
              "Worst case restated: three role-lock footers, one verification row, Bills partial error, at AX5; frame 12 draws it (review minor)",
              "Removed code names and flow step numbers from drawn text; engineering note kept in plain words (review minor)",
              "Owner InviteRow given full caption with sent date, relative expiry and Resend for consistency with the household block and contract"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "f3-household-calendar",
            "name": "Household calendar",
            "platforms": [
              "web",
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": false,
            "frameCount": 20,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Household calendar · f3-household-calendar\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Household calendar\" (the home agenda). This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed. The screen already works, but nothing in the app links to it yet. Keep its existing member filter chip row and its existing \"Who's free\" link.\n\nATTACH:\n1. Household calendar on iOS, Android and web-1440, including its create-event sheet and its read-only mode.\n2. The home header tabs (web).\n3. The Home dashboard Calendar card.\n4. Your place file, Dates section.\n5. The Date sheet, in its view-mine and view-seeded states.\n6. The Foundations rows for DateRow, ProvenanceMark, LockedActionRow, InlineUndo, NotificationRow and QuietDayReceipt.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852 · Android 412x915 · web 390x844 and 1440x900.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE:\nPath: Place tab → Larkspur Loop → Calendar.\nDraw three new links as part of this work:\n- a \"Calendar\" tab in the home header, placed after Dashboard;\n- \"Open calendar\" on the dashboard Calendar card;\n- the place file Dates row \"Everyone here can see these\", with a chevron.\nOther ways in:\n- The household notification row \"Sam added 'Chimney sweep' for Sat 14 Nov\". It opens this screen scrolled to that event, with the event highlighted.\n- The deep link /app/homes/:id/calendar, on web and native.\n- \"Add as a separate calendar event\" from the Date sheet's duplicate warning. It opens this screen's create-event sheet.\n- A date-reminder push for a co-resident who cannot edit this home's dates lands here, in read-only mode (frame 05), scrolled to that date, instead of on Today.\nSam arrives from his dashboard's Calendar card and adds an event. The confirmation \"Saved to your household calendar.\" is only true because this screen shows the event. After Sam leaves the screen, Maya gets one quiet NotificationRow:\n- line 1: \"Sam added 'Chimney sweep' for Sat 14 Nov\"\n- line 2: \"Today · 6:22 PM\" (no home label, because Maya has one home)\nThis is now the only household calendar. The dashboard card previews this agenda and links here.\n\nWHO AND WHEN:\n- Frame 01: Maya Chen, owner of HOME A, on TODAY (Mon 19 Oct 2026, 6:10 PM), checking the next few weeks before her parents visit.\n- Frames 02–04: Sam Ortega, a member, adding the chimney sweep on TODAY.\n- Assumption: Maya tapped \"Share with the household\" on her claim receipt, so her lease, notice, warranty, smoke-alarm and HOA dates are household dates. Maya later set her renters insurance to Only you in the Date sheet; an Only-you date at a claimed home appears in the household calendar only for its owner.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Let everyone in the household read and add to one shared calendar, where a far-off lease date never looks like an overdue chore.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS:\n1. The \"Today\" marker and the \"Recycling and garbage — Tomorrow\" row.\n2. The month header with its count.\n3. The provenance legend.\nThe single primary action is \"Add an event\".\n\nCONTENT:\nHeader:\n- \"Larkspur Loop\", with ScopeChip \"Your household\".\n- Directly under it, show the exact legend once: \"● Official · ○ On record, not confirmed · ✓ You added this\".\n- In Sam's view only (frame 02 and other Sam frames), add one caption line under the legend: \"✓ on someone else's row names who added it\".\n\nMonth count rule: every month header counts only rows this viewer can see. Individual pickup rows inside the 14-day window count as items. A monthly pickup summary row is not counted and is shown as \"plus pickup\".\n\nOctober 2026 · 8 items (9 items in Maya's view, which adds her private row):\n- Tue 20 Oct: \"Recycling and garbage\" — Tomorrow — hollow mark — caption \"Waste Connections · city pickup schedule\" (same for Maya and Sam).\n- Thu 22 Oct, two rows:\n  - \"Maya's parents visiting\", a home event running to Sun 25 Oct — in 3 days.\n  - \"Package expected · replacement recycling cart\" — in 3 days · Thu 22 Oct — hollow mark.\n- Fri 23 Oct: \"Clark Public Utilities · $142.18\" — in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct — tick.\n  - Maya's caption: \"You added this\". Sam's caption: \"Maya added this\".\n- Sat 24 Oct: task \"Change furnace filter · Sam\" — in 5 days · Sat 24 Oct.\n- Mon 26 Oct: \"Online or mail voter registration for Tue 3 Nov must arrive by\" — in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct — filled mark.\n  - ScopeChip \"Statewide — WA\".\n  - Caption: \"Washington Secretary of State · statewide · as of Mon 19 Oct\".\n  - Maya's view only: a caption line with the person glyph, \"You marked this done · Only you will see this.\" Sam never sees Maya's done line.\n- Tue 27 Oct: \"Garbage only\" — in 8 days · Tue 27 Oct — hollow mark — \"Waste Connections · city pickup schedule\".\n- Wed 28 Oct: \"City of Vancouver water · $84.00\" — in 9 days · Wed 28 Oct — tick — \"You added this\" (\"Maya added this\" for Sam).\n- Fri 30 Oct, Maya's view only: \"Renters insurance renews\" — in 11 days · Fri 30 Oct — tick.\n  - Caption, with the person glyph: \"You entered this · Only you will see this.\"\n  - This row never appears in Sam's view, and nothing marks where it was.\n\nNovember 2026 · 5 items plus pickup (6 items plus pickup in frames 04 and 14):\n- One pickup summary row: \"Pickup every Tuesday · recycling Tue 3 and Tue 17 Nov\" — hollow mark — \"Waste Connections · city pickup schedule\".\n- Sun 1 Nov, two rows:\n  - \"HOA dues · $285\" — in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov — tick — recurrence caption \"every year · you entered this\".\n  - \"Smoke alarm batteries\" — in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov — tick — \"every year · you entered this\".\n- Mon 2 Nov, two rows:\n  - \"Property tax, 2nd half\" — in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov — filled — \"Clark County Treasurer · county-wide · 2026\". The Date sheet detail adds \"moved from Sat 31 Oct\".\n  - \"Comcast · $79.99\" — in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov — tick — \"You added this\".\n- Tue 3 Nov: \"Voter registration in person — until 8:00 PM\" — in 15 days · Tue 3 Nov — filled — no Statewide chip — caption \"Clark County Elections · county-wide · 2026\".\n- Frames 04 and 14 only: Sat 14 Nov, \"Chimney sweep · 9:00 AM\" — in 26 days · Sat 14 Nov — tick — \"Sam added this\" (\"You added this\" in Sam's view).\n\nDecember 2026 · 1 item plus pickup:\n- The pickup summary row (hollow).\n- Sat 12 Dec: \"Water-heater warranty ends\" — tick — \"one time · you entered this\".\n- The QuietDayReceipt line \"Checked — nothing else in December\".\n\nJanuary 2027 onward:\n- Pickup summary rows keep the same hollow mark as every HOME A pickup row.\n- Each carries the caption line \"Projected · Waste Connections hasn't published 2027 dates yet\".\n- June 2027: the Tue 1 Jun row stays on its usual day, hollow, captioned \"Projected · Memorial Day week · Waste Connections hasn't published 2027 dates yet\". Draw no moved row and no ghost for it.\n\nMarch 2027, both rows with a tick, the annual/self-entered left rule, and no urgency colour:\n- Mon 1 Mar: \"Tell your landlord in writing by Mon 1 Mar\".\n  - Caption: \"30 days before your lease ends · you entered this\".\n  - Reminder series: \"Reminders · Mon 15 Feb · Sun 28 Feb · Mon 1 Mar\".\n- Wed 31 Mar: \"Lease ends\", with the caption \"you entered this\".\n\nIn Sam's view, every \"you entered this\" caption on Maya's rows reads \"Maya entered this\".\n\nWorst case: Sun 1 Nov and Mon 2 Nov each hold two rows. Densest day, drawn as a labelled stress-test inset on the AX5 frame and not counted in frame 01's totals: Fri 23 Oct under the member filter chip row, holding \"Clark Public Utilities · $142.18\", the home event \"Pick up Maya's parents at PDX · 4:30 PM\", and two tasks, \"Clean gutters · Sam\" and \"Make up the guest bed · Maya\".\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION:\n\nThe agenda:\n- Keep the agenda: month headers with counts, then rows grouped by day. Do not use a month grid.\n- Every month header uses the noun \"items\" and follows the month count rule above.\n- Each month header has 44pt \"Previous month\" and \"Next month\" buttons.\n- Address rules and dates join as a fifth row type, alongside home events, tasks, bills and packages.\n- Every row is a DateRow: a leading KindGlyph, the title, a relative-plus-absolute date, a SourceCaption, and a trailing ProvenanceMark S at the same size everywhere.\n- \"You entered this\" and \"Maya entered this\" are the source for self-entered rows. The Date sheet shows the source as \"You\".\n\nThe \"Add an event\" button:\n- A filled primary.700 button, right-aligned in the header row under the legend. Height is 44pt on iOS, 48dp on Android and 44px on web.\n- iOS: it also appears as a labelled \"+\" top-bar button with the same spoken label.\n- Android: no FAB.\n- web-390: sticky, with scroll padding reserved.\n- In frame 05, this slot holds the LockedActionRow instead.\n\nVisual rule by row kind:\n- Annual or self-entered rows (lease, notice, warranty, smoke alarm, HOA, renters insurance) get the 2px identity.home left rule and their recurrence caption. They never take urgency or overdue treatment.\n- Derived near-term rows (pickup, bills, tasks, package) use the kind glyph and the relative day, and may use the existing due-soon treatment.\n\nMarks:\n- The mark follows provenance only. Filled = official or confirmed. Hollow = on record, not confirmed. Tick = added by a person in this household.\n- Every HOME A pickup row, summary row and projected row is hollow, because HOME A's pickup is on record from the city schedule and not confirmed as of TODAY. This matches the pickup card and Today's strip.\n- Projection is stated in words only, never by changing the mark.\n- Seeded civic rows (voter registration, in-person registration, property tax) are drawn filled on the assumption that each was checked by hand. A seeded row not yet checked is drawn hollow with the same caption. Frame 09 draws one such unchecked row, annotated.\n\nPickup:\n- For the next 14 days, each pickup is its own row, matching Today's strip.\n- After that, each month shows one summary row.\n- A holiday move is drawn only when a source has published it. It breaks out as its own row: the mark on the new day, a struck ghost row on the usual day labelled \"usual day\", and the source caption. The moved row's mark follows its source: filled for a city's published move. It is never a tick.\n- Founder check: HOME A's Tuesday route has no holiday move through Dec 2026, so frame 01 shows none.\n\nFrame 08 (holiday move):\n- Main content, labelled \"Specimen · a Camas Thursday route\", drawn in full agenda grammar: a November 2026 day group with the struck Thu 26 Nov ghost (\"usual day\") and the filled row \"Thanksgiving — moved to Fri 27 Nov\", caption \"City of Camas 2026 calendar\".\n- Beside it, a labelled inset \"Larkspur Loop · June 2027\" showing only the normal hollow row \"Garbage only · Tue 1 Jun\" with \"Projected · Memorial Day week · Waste Connections hasn't published 2027 dates yet\". No moved row, no ghost.\n- Annotate: \"If Waste Connections publishes a standing holiday-week policy, a projected move may be drawn with that policy named as its source. Otherwise, no move is drawn.\"\n\nScope and gaps:\n- Statewide rows carry \"Statewide — WA\", so they are clearly not a claim about this house. County rows say \"county-wide\" in their caption.\n- A quiet month reads as finished: its count, its rows and the \"Checked\" line.\n- When the viewer may not see bills or tasks, those rows are absent and the count drops. There is no ghost row, and the day keeps its dates and events.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS:\n\nRow taps and row actions. Each row kind has its own actions:\n- Household-entered dates: tapping opens the Date sheet in view-mine. Actions: Edit (opens the Date sheet), Remind me, Where this comes from, Mark done.\n- Pickup rows: tapping opens the pickup Date sheet. Actions: Change pickup day, Where this comes from.\n- Official seeded rows: tapping opens the Date sheet in view-seeded, with fields locked. Actions: Remind me, Where this comes from. Voter rows only also offer Mark done, which shows \"You marked this done\" to that person only.\n- Bill rows: tapping opens bill detail. Actions: Open bill, Where this comes from. There is no Mark done or Mark paid anywhere on this screen.\n- Task rows: tapping opens the task. Action: Open task.\n- Home events: tapping opens the existing event detail. Action: Open event.\nThe Date sheet is the one place dates are edited.\n\nThe mark:\n- The mark is never its own target. \"Where this comes from\" opens the ProvenanceSheet.\n\nAdding an event:\n- \"Add an event\" opens the existing create-event sheet.\n- For Sam, fill it in:\n  - Title: \"Chimney sweep\"\n  - Date: Sat 14 Nov\n  - Time: 9:00 AM\n  - Footer: \"Everyone in this household will see this.\"\n  - Buttons: \"Save event\" and a visible Close.\n- On save:\n  - One light haptic tick.\n  - The new row highlights once with a fading wash.\n  - The InlineUndo \"Saved to your household calendar. · Undo\" appears on that row and stays until Sam leaves the screen.\n  - The household notification goes out only after the undo closes.\n\nDeep-link landings: scroll once, highlight, and move focus to the row.\n\nReduce Motion: the highlight is static, and scrolling jumps instead of animating.\n\nMonth navigation: the \"Previous month\" / \"Next month\" buttons do the same as scrolling.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED:\n- DateRow: pickup; holiday moved (sourced); deadline; money row; done; permission-hidden; highlighted; Only-you private.\n- KindGlyph.\n- ProvenanceMark: the exact legend; hollow on pickup; filled on checked civic rows; tick with captions that name the actor.\n- SourceCaption.\n- ScopeChip: \"Your household\" and \"Statewide — WA\" chips, plus the sentence form \"Only you will see this.\" on Maya's private lines.\n- ProvenanceSheet.\n- DateSheet: view-mine, view-seeded, pickup.\n- NotificationRow: home_event_created (landing source, frame 14).\n- LockedActionRow: names who can act.\n- InlineUndo.\n- QuietDayReceipt.\n- WarmingSkeleton.\n- FreshnessLine.\n- OfflineNotice.\n- InlineErrorRow.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n\nRows:\n- Each row is one element, with the custom actions listed above for its kind.\n\nSpoken labels:\n- Pickup, both views: \"Recycling and garbage, tomorrow, Tuesday October 20, Waste Connections, on record, not confirmed.\"\n- Bill row, Sam's view: \"Clark Public Utilities, 142 dollars 18 cents, in 4 days, Friday October 23, added by Maya.\"\n- Holiday specimen: \"Pickup moved from Thursday November 26 to Friday November 27 for Thanksgiving. Official. City of Camas 2026 calendar.\" The struck ghost row is labelled \"usual day, Thursday November 26\".\n- June 2027 row: \"Garbage only, Tuesday June 1, projected, Memorial Day week, Waste Connections hasn't published 2027 dates yet, on record, not confirmed.\"\n\nMonth headers:\n- Month headers are headings.\n- Each is announced with a summary. Example: \"October: 8 items. Next: recycling and garbage tomorrow.\"\n- The month buttons are read as \"Previous month\" and \"Next month\".\n\nTargets and text size:\n- Targets are 44pt, 48dp or 44px.\n- At AX5, the date line wraps under the title and chips wrap.\n\nStatus messages:\n- The undo line, the error and the offline notice are live regions.\n\nCOPY: Every string above, plus:\n- Empty state: \"Checked — nothing from your household on the calendar\", with \"Add an event\" (filled) and \"Add a date\" (text button).\n- Read-only reason: \"Maya Chen can add and edit events here.\"\n- Error: \"We couldn't load the household calendar just now · Retry\"\n- Offline: \"You're offline · as of 6:04 PM\" and \"Adding events needs a connection.\"\n- Loading: no text.\n\nEDGE CASES:\n\nLong content:\n- A long title wraps to two lines and is never cut.\n- A multi-day event shows once, with its span.\n\nMore than one home:\n- The header reads \"Larkspur Loop · Your household\", and household notification rows add the home label on line 2.\n\nMany items:\n- November holds 20 items. The count reads \"November 2026 · 20 items plus pickup\".\n\nDensest day:\n- The Fri 23 Oct stress-test inset on frame 16.\n\nEmpty:\n- The seeded statewide rows still show, plus the empty line.\n\nUnchecked seeded rows:\n- Hollow mark, same caption (frame 09).\n\nUnpublished holiday weeks:\n- The usual day stays, hollow, with \"Projected\" in words. No predicted move.\n\nSlow network:\n- Skeletons appear after 1s.\n\nOffline:\n- The cached agenda stays.\n- Adding is disabled, with its reason.\n\nPrivate dates:\n- An Only-you date appears only in its owner's view.\n\nPermission variants:\n- Owner.\n- Member who can edit.\n- Legacy member who can only read: no add button, with the LockedActionRow in its place.\n- Guest without bill or task access: those rows are absent, and the counts drop.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n- Instead of a month grid, draw the day-grouped agenda — because rows carry source and scope.\n- Instead of red overdue styling on a lease or tax date, draw the green left rule and a recurrence caption — because annual dates are not late chores.\n- Instead of an even weekly pickup rhythm, draw one summary row per month plus a broken-out row only for a published holiday move — because moved weeks are what people need.\n- Instead of predicting a holiday move nobody has published, keep the usual day and say \"Projected\" — because a wrong moved day tells people to miss pickup.\n- Instead of changing the mark for projected pickups, keep the pickup's own mark and say \"Projected\" in words — because filled vs hollow means provenance only.\n- Instead of a FAB for \"Add an event\", draw a filled header button — because the house style has no FAB.\n- Instead of Mark done or Mark paid on bill rows, offer Open bill — because a mis-tap on a glanceable calendar must not notify the household.\n- Instead of showing Maya's private dates to Sam as ghost rows, draw nothing — because a private date stays private until she shares it.\n- Instead of making the mark tappable, make the whole row the target — because a 16pt mark is too small.\n\nDONE WHEN:\n- All three links reach this screen.\n- Sam adds the chimney sweep, sees it right away and can undo it. Maya gets one quiet row, \"Sam added 'Chimney sweep' for Sat 14 Nov\", after the undo closes.\n- A member can edit without the owner changing a role.\n- No bill can be marked paid from here.\n- The lease row never looks overdue.\n- December reads as finished.\n- The holiday move shown is a published one with its source, and no unpublished move is drawn.\n- Every HOME A pickup mark matches the pickup card and Today's strip.\n- Statewide rows are scoped.\n- Every row states its source.\n- Every month count matches its rows under the stated rule.\n- No mark says Sam did what Maya did, and the legend stays exact.\n- Every frame reads in greyscale and at AX5.\n\nARTBOARDS:\n1. f3-household-calendar · ios · 01-agenda-dense · light — Maya's view from Tue 20 Oct into early November, with hollow pickup rows, the private renters-insurance row and her done line; \"October 2026 · 9 items\".\n2. f3-household-calendar · ios · 02-member-can-edit · light — Sam's view: \"Add an event\" live; the legend plus \"✓ on someone else's row names who added it\"; \"October 2026 · 8 items\"; no done line and no renters-insurance row; Maya's rows read \"Maya entered this\" or \"Maya added this\"; pickup caption \"Waste Connections · city pickup schedule\".\n3. f3-household-calendar · ios · 03-create-event-sheet · light — the chimney sweep filled in.\n4. f3-household-calendar · ios · 04-saved-highlight · light — \"Saved to your household calendar. · Undo\" on the highlighted Sat 14 Nov row; \"November 2026 · 6 items plus pickup\".\n5. f3-household-calendar · ios · 05-legacy-read-only · light — no add button; the LockedActionRow \"Maya Chen can add and edit events here.\" in its slot. Annotate: \"Date-reminder pushes land here for co-residents who cannot edit.\"\n6. f3-household-calendar · ios · 06-derived-hidden · light — a guest without bill or task access: the same October days with no bill or task rows and no ghosts; \"October 2026 · 5 items\".\n7. f3-household-calendar · ios · 07-quiet-december · light — \"December 2026 · 1 item plus pickup\", the hollow pickup summary, the warranty row and the \"Checked\" line.\n8. f3-household-calendar · ios · 08-holiday-move-sourced · light — the \"Specimen · a Camas Thursday route\" day group with the struck Thu 26 Nov ghost and the filled \"Thanksgiving — moved to Fri 27 Nov\" row, plus the \"Larkspur Loop · June 2027\" inset with the plain projected Tue 1 Jun row and the policy annotation.\n9. f3-household-calendar · ios · 09-empty · light — the seeded statewide rows plus \"Checked — nothing from your household on the calendar\"; one seeded row drawn hollow, annotated \"Not yet checked by hand\".\n10. f3-household-calendar · ios · 10-loading · light — row skeletons.\n11. f3-household-calendar · android · 11-error · light — the InlineErrorRow with Retry.\n12. f3-household-calendar · android · 12-offline · light — the cached agenda and the disabled add button with its reason.\n13. f3-household-calendar · web-1440 · 13-entry-points · light — the agenda open at 1440 with the header Calendar tab selected. Beside it, two labelled inset crops: the dashboard Calendar card's \"Open calendar\", and the place file Dates row \"Everyone here can see these ›\". Each inset has an arrow to the agenda.\n14. f3-household-calendar · android · 14-notification-landing · light — Maya landed from the NotificationRow \"Sam added 'Chimney sweep' for Sat 14 Nov / Today · 6:22 PM\" (shown as a labelled inset), with the Sat 14 Nov row highlighted.\n15. f3-household-calendar · web-390 · 15-agenda-dense · light — frame 01 on mobile web, with the sticky \"Add an event\" button.\n16. f3-household-calendar · ios · 16-ax5 · light — frame 01 at AX5, plus the labelled Fri 23 Oct densest-day stress-test inset.\n17. f3-household-calendar · ios · 17-greyscale · light — frame 01 in greyscale.\n18. f3-household-calendar · ios · 01-agenda-dense · dark — the dark twin of frame 01.\n19. f3-household-calendar · ios · 08-holiday-move-sourced · dark — the dark twin of frame 08.\n20. Notes — five parts:\n- Assumptions for the founder to check:\n  - HOME A's Tuesday route has no holiday move through Dec 2026.\n  - Waste Connections has not published 2027 dates or a standing holiday-week policy, so no 2027 move is drawn.\n  - Filled marks on civic rows assume each row was checked by hand. Unchecked seeded rows use the hollow mark.\n  - The \"Washington Secretary of State\" and \"Clark County Elections\" sources.\n  - Maya shared her dates with the household, then set renters insurance to Only you in the Date sheet; an Only-you date at a claimed home appears in the household calendar only for its owner.\n  - HOA dues recur yearly (so December shows no HOA row).\n  - Maya has one home, so notification rows carry no home label.\n  - The pickup caption \"Waste Connections · city pickup schedule\" matches the dashboard's pickup row.\n- Contract conflict (recorded once): Drawn as: tick on a household member's entry, caption \"Maya added this\", spoken \"added by Maya\" — instead of contract: tick spoken only as \"you added this\". Proposed ProvenanceMark variant for prompt 00: household-added.\n- Every invented string (list each one):\n  - \"Maya's parents visiting\"\n  - \"Package expected · replacement recycling cart\"\n  - \"Change furnace filter\"\n  - \"Smoke alarm batteries\"\n  - \"Renters insurance renews\"\n  - \"city pickup schedule\"\n  - \"✓ on someone else's row names who added it\"\n  - \"Maya added this\", \"Maya entered this\", \"Sam added this\"\n  - the recurrence captions, including \"every year · you entered this\" and \"one time · you entered this\"\n  - \"Reminders · Mon 15 Feb · Sun 28 Feb · Mon 1 Mar\"\n  - the projected captions, including \"Memorial Day week\"\n  - \"Voter registration in person — until 8:00 PM\"\n  - \"Specimen · a Camas Thursday route\", \"Thanksgiving — moved to Fri 27 Nov\", \"usual day\"\n  - \"Chimney sweep · 9:00 AM\"\n  - \"Sam added 'Chimney sweep' for Sat 14 Nov\" and \"Today · 6:22 PM\"\n  - \"Saved to your household calendar. · Undo\"\n  - \"Pick up Maya's parents at PDX · 4:30 PM\", \"Clean gutters · Sam\", \"Make up the guest bed · Maya\"\n  - the empty, read-only, error and offline lines\n  - \"as of 6:04 PM\"\n  - \"20 items\"\n  - any other string you add\n- Omitted states: any not drawn.\n- Engineering note, in plain words: Android needs its own screen route for the household calendar link, or the notification lands on the dashboard.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1–6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: artboards 7–12, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 3: artboards 13–18, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 4: artboards 19–20.",
