                "issues": [
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The prompt gives Jordan's own address a different flood zone from the one the compare-sheet prompt in this same batch gives it. Jordan, at PLACE B on Mon 19 Oct, is drawn in Zone AE here. In f8-compare-sheet, the card minted from the same address on the same day reads Zone X. The house-style fixture also gives Zone X as the reading.",
                    "evidence": "This prompt, artboard 5: \"flood \\\"Different band\\\" (You in Zone AE)\" and WHO: \"For the signed-out and compare frames: Jordan Lee, new at PLACE B, 1107 NE Birchfield Ct\". f8-compare-sheet prompt: \"Made from 1107 NE Birchfield Ct\" … \"Flood zone \\\"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\\\"\". house-style-v2.txt FIXTURES: \"Readings: Flood Zone X (minimal flood hazard, FEMA, effective Sep 2021)\". (Zone AE for Jordan comes from flow-05, which used a different address: \"6207 NE 42nd Ave, Vancouver\".)",
                    "fix": "Make the 'You' column in frame 5 an explicitly different fixture. For example: \"a second viewer address in Zone AE (invented; list on Notes)\". Or keep Jordan at PLACE B in Zone X and show 'Different band' on the air row (frozen AQI 42 vs a live alert AQI 118) instead of flood. Either way, add a Notes line saying Jordan's PLACE B card in f8-compare-sheet reads Zone X."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The honesty rule about unconfirmed layers on the shared and compare sizes is never settled. The inventory says to add a confidence field to the token, or else drop unverified layers from the card. The prompt draws a HOLLOW row only at detail size. It says nothing about what a street-matched or unconfirmed layer looks like at compare size, share-card size or in a frozen token.",
                    "evidence": "inventory-entries/f8-scale-strips.json uxNote: \"Also add a confidence field to the compare token, or drop unverified layers from the card rather than shipping them as confident.\" critique-findings.md: \"nothing at all on the compare card or OG image — whose token schema has no confidence field, so a seeded unverified radon zone would unfurl in a chat thread as a confident grade\". Prompt EDGE CASES covers only the detail row: \"When our address match is only to the street, that one row is HOLLOW with \\\"On record, not confirmed\\\"\".",
                    "fix": "Add this to LAYOUT or EDGE CASES: \"At compare and share-card size, an unconfirmed layer keeps its HOLLOW mark with the printed words 'On record, not confirmed' (the token carries a per-layer confidence). It is never shown filled.\" Draw one such row in frame 2 (three sizes) and in frame 5."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The dark twins are incomplete. The research on the prompting method names the scale strips as one of the few surfaces that get a FULL dark set. This prompt twins only frames 1–5. There is no dark version of the HOLLOW/AE frame (where the ring's 3:1 contrast on the dark base matters most), the ProvenanceSheet, loading/error, offline, narrow, Android, desktop or AX5 frames.",
                    "evidence": "house-style-contradictions.md: \"default: the dense frame plus one state-coloured frame; full dark sets only for widgets, the provenance specimen and the scale strips\". Prompt ARTBOARDS: dark twins only 15–19 (of 1, 2, 3, 4, 5).",
                    "fix": "Add dark twins for at least 6 (flood AE and unconfirmed hollow), 7 (row tap with ProvenanceSheet), 8 (loading and partial error), 9 (offline) and 13 (AX5). Grow the batch plan to match, or state on the Notes artboard which dark frames were deliberately left out and why."
                  },
                  {
