                    "evidence": "f8-scale-strips prompt: \"Marker: 12pt, two-tone (text.primary core, 2px surface.base halo).\" · \"the band name printed beside the marker\" · Air: \"Print the category name in text.primary beside the track\". prompts-v2/00b.md ScaleStrip: \"Marker: a vertical capsule 4pt wide × 20pt tall … It is never a disc, so it cannot be read as the 'Official' mark.\" · \"Band names under the track … The occupied band's name is always in captionMedium 12/16/500 text.primary, directly under the marker.\" · \"The Air row prints the AqiBand range labels ('0–50' … '301+') instead of band names\"",
                    "fix": "In LAYOUT & VISUALIZATION, replace the \"Flood, wildfire and radon tracks\", \"Air row\" and \"Marker\" bullets with: \"Draw every track exactly as ScaleStrip on the Foundations board: the capsule marker, a 2px text.primary outline on the occupied band, and band names under the track (Wildfire prints only the two end names plus the occupied name). The Air row is AqiBand's instrument-row variant, with range labels under the segments and the category in the value line ('AQI 42 · Good'), never on a fill. Wildfire keeps '3 of 5'. Radon is described in words only.\" Delete the words \"beside the marker\" and \"beside the track\" wherever they appear."
