              {
                "id": "f8-og-compare-card",
                "pass": false,
                "issues": [
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The card silently redefines the published ScaleStrip 05-og-column recipe: a 780px column where the recipe allows at most 640, different value strings, a per-row \"Official\" word, a different sources line and a different Air label. Claude Design will see both definitions. The prompt calls its version \"OG column size\" as if it were the contract's.",
                    "evidence": "Prompt: \"ScaleStrip at OG column size, 780px wide on this card\"; rows \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\", \"● Official\" at each track's end; sources \"FEMA · USFS · AirNow · EPA\". prompts-v2/00b.md 05-og-column: \"a 520px-wide text-and-track column … may widen to at most 640px\"; rows \"Flood · Zone X — minimal\" … \"Radon · Zone 1 (county)\"; sources \"● Official · FEMA Sep 2021 · USFS 2023 · AirNow Sat 12 Sep · EPA county-wide\". component-contract.md: \"OG column (520 of 1200)\".",
                    "fix": "Under FOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED, write: \"ScaleStrip, following the published 05-og-column recipe (capsule marker 8×40 with a 4px halo, 30px track, no band names, no per-row captions) with these declared overrides: column 780px (not 520–640); value strings are the approved in-app strings; layer labels Flood / Wildfire / Air on <date> / Radon; a 28px '● Official' after each track; sources line 'FEMA · USFS · AirNow · EPA'.\" Keep the Notes entry proposing the contract update."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The title-length rules contradict each other, and the reciprocal title shown in frame 03 breaks the prompt's own accessibility rule.",
                    "evidence": "EDGE CASES: \"when the named og:title would pass 45 characters, use 'What's on record at a place in <city>. Yours?'; if that passes 50 characters, use … a friend's place\". ACCESSIBILITY: \"'Yours?' stays in the first 45 characters\". The reciprocal og:title \"What's on record at a place in Camas, WA. Yours?\" is 48 characters.",
                    "fix": "Use one limit: \"Every og:title is 45 characters or fewer. Try the named form, then 'On record at a place in <city>. Yours?', then 'What's on record at a friend's place. Yours?'.\" Set the reciprocal og:title to \"On record at a place in Camas, WA. Yours?\" (41 characters)."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The crop rule can't be met. A left-aligned sender line at x=40 and a right-hand \"Yours?\" column can't both sit inside the central band of a near-square crop. The research also marks crop safe areas as unverified.",
                    "evidence": "LAYOUT: \"The sender line and 'Yours?' sit inside the central band, so a near-square or 2:1 crop never cuts them.\" research-findings.md:2407 calls this a \"hedge, not a verified spec\", and :2566 lists \"any 'safe-area' percentage for OG crops\" as unverified.",
                    "fix": "Replace with: \"Keep the sender line and 'Yours?' at least 40px from the top and bottom edges so a 2:1 crop (1200x600) never cuts them. Square crops are not designed for; record this on Notes as unverified.\" Rename frame 06 to \"06-scaled-400\" and describe it as \"frame 1 scaled to 400x210\", because it is not a crop."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The contract and research set a 40px cap-height floor, but the prompt redefines it as a 40px font size, about 30% smaller at bubble size. The brief's \"≥40 px type\" allows this reading, but the choice should be a flagged question, not a silent reinterpretation.",
                    "evidence": "component-contract.md ScaleStrip: \"text is at least 40px cap\". research-findings.md:2401: \"Cap height should be at least ~40 px at 1200 wide\". Prompt: \"have a font size of at least 40px (about 13px when the card is shown 400 wide)\".",
                    "fix": "Keep the 40px font floor but require proof: \"In frame 06, measure the rendered band words and 'Yours?' and print the sizes. 'Yours?' and the sender line use at least 40px cap height (about 56px font).\" Keep the Notes question about the contract."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "No size is given for the text inside the \"Yours?\" column (\"Enter your address\", \"pantopus.com\"). The type rule allows only three strings to drop below 40px, and \"Enter your address\" at 40px doesn't fit in the roughly 308px column.",
                    "evidence": "\"Only 'as of', 'Official' and the sources line may drop, to 28px or more.\" \"Right column about 300px\". The slot reads \"Enter your address\".",
                    "fix": "Add \"the address slot text and 'pantopus.com'\" to the list allowed to drop to 28px, and state the width: \"Right column 308px (1120 − 780 − 32).\""
                  },
                  {
