                    "issue": "\"● Official\" at the track's right end doesn't say whether the track shortens to make room. Claude Design may draw the word over the Very high or 301+ band.",
                    "evidence": "\"Each row: layer name, value, then the track with '● Official' at the track's right end.\"",
                    "fix": "Write: \"The track is 620px, then a 12px gap, then a 28px mark and 'Official' at 28px (about 148px), inside the 780px column.\""
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The glossary requires spelling out \"air quality index (AQI)\" once, but the image and title never do.",
                    "evidence": "component-contract.md glossary: \"spell out 'air quality index (AQI)' once per surface.\" The image label is \"Air on Sat 12 Sep\"; og:image:alt says \"air quality index 42\".",
                    "fix": "Change og:image:alt to \"…air quality index (AQI) 42, Good…\" and record on Notes that the image uses the short form because of space."
