        "prompts": [
          {
            "id": "f8-native-share-compare",
            "name": "Share + compare actions on the native address preview",
            "platforms": [
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": false,
            "frameCount": 19,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Share + compare actions on the native address preview · f8-native-share-compare\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Place launch / T0 address preview\" (iOS and Android). This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed.\n- Keep the hero and the section groups exactly as they are.\n- Aha card: draw the f8-seasonal-aha content described under CONTENT.\n- Add one action row under the aha card.\n- iOS: both buttons are new. The screen has no share control today.\n- Android: the existing \"Share this address\" link currently sits inside the sticky wall, under \"Continue\". Remove it from the wall. Drop its share icon. Re-home it as the left button of the new pair under the aha card. Apart from that removal, draw the wall exactly as in the screenshot.\n\nATTACH: (1) The iOS address preview, scrolled so the aha card and the sticky wall are both visible. (2) The Android address preview at the same scroll, showing the existing \"Share this address\" link in the wall. (3) The finished f8-seasonal-aha iOS and Android frames, which supply the aha card content. (4) The f8-og-compare-card no-name frame, used as the share-sheet thumbnail.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393×852 and Android 412×915 only. Web has its own compare sheet, so draw no web frames here.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE\n- Tab and parent: the Place tab. On both apps the address preview is the Place tab's root for anyone who is signed out, or signed in with no saved place.\n- Arrival: the person types an address into the Place launch field and taps \"See your place\".\n- Position: the new row sits directly under the aha card (\"What stands out\"), about one screen down.\n- Entry points: only the aha card on this preview. No push, widget or deep link lands here.\n- What it receives: the typed address and the finished preview.\n- Hand-off 1, \"Compare with a friend\": the link is made, then the system share sheet opens with https://pantopus.com/start?vs=<token>. The friend sees the compare share card \"A place in Camas, WA · Yours?\" in the chat and taps it. They land on the web compare arrival page in the browser. In v1 the link does not open the app.\n- Hand-off 2, \"Share this address\": the system share sheet opens with the address link the Android app already sends.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Someone new at PLACE B: a signed-out visitor who moved to Camas this month. On the fixture TODAY (Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM) they type 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas, WA 98607 into the iPhone app. They want to send the readings to a friend without sending their address.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Let someone send this reading to a friend in one tap, with no native compare screen and without competing with the save.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: The eye lands on the aha card first, then on the two text buttons and their caption, then on the sticky wall. The screen's single primary action stays \"Continue\" in the sticky wall. The new row has no primary.\n\nCONTENT (deltas to the fixtures)\n- Header address: PLACE B.\n- The aha card above the row is f8-seasonal-aha's Mon 19 Oct default, drawn exactly as that prompt specifies. It contains:\n  - the voter-registration headline;\n  - the StatusChip deadline chip \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\";\n  - the hollow mark with its source caption \"Washington Secretary of State · statewide · as of Mon 19 Oct\";\n  - the sunken follow-up row \"Keep this address handy to see what changes here\";\n  - inside the card, the bordered outbound row \"Check or update at VoteWA ↗\".\n- New row: \"Share this address\" · \"Compare with a friend\".\n- Caption under the row: \"The compare card shows your city, your readings and the headline above — never your address, and no name. Anyone with the link can see it.\"\n- Sticky wall, drawn exactly as in the screenshot apart from the Android link removal: \"Keep this address handy. Choose whether to save it privately after sign-in.\", the caption \"Your preview stays on this device for up to 24 hours while you sign in.\", and \"Continue\".\n- iOS compare share-sheet header: title \"A place in Camas, WA · Yours?\", the compare card as the thumbnail, subtitle \"pantopus.com\".\n- iOS share-address header: title \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas, WA 98607\", subtitle \"pantopus.com\".\n- Android compare Sharesheet: title \"Compare your place with mine\", with the card thumbnail in the preview.\n- Android share-address Sharesheet: title \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas, WA 98607\", no thumbnail.\n- Worst case: iOS AX5 text. The two buttons stack, and the caption, with its future expiry clause, wraps to five or more lines above the sticky wall.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\n- Put a TextActionRow on the page surface, 16pt below the aha card's bottom edge. Do not give it a card of its own.\n- The VoteWA outbound row stays inside the aha card. The share/compare pair sits outside the card, on the page surface, so the card edge separates the two rows.\n- The pair has no border and no glyph, so nobody can mistake it for the bordered outbound row inside the card.\n- Draw two text buttons side by side, with no fill, no border and no icon. Separate them with spacing only: at least 8pt on iOS and 8dp on Android.\n- Each button is 44pt tall on iOS and 48dp tall on Android.\n- Set the labels in primary.700; in dark mode use the dark focus/link token (border.focus, #38BDF8).\n- Put the caption under the row, in caption type and text.secondary.\n- Emphasis runs top to bottom: aha card, text row, sections, sticky primary. Sharing is always available but never outranks the save.\n- v1 has no name field, so the card is always anonymous. The caption says so in words, so the button never suggests a personalised card.\n- If the compare link cannot be made, only the Compare button changes. \"Share this address\" stays live.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- Make the link when the row first scrolls into view, so the tap usually opens the sheet at once. The minting state appears only if that link is not ready yet or failed; a failed early attempt retries on tap.\n- \"Compare with a friend\" opens the system share sheet. On iOS this is the system share sheet, with its header filled from the card's link preview (title and image). On Android it is the system Sharesheet.\n- Minting (TextActionRow minting state): a 12pt spinner replaces the start of the Compare label, which reads \"Making a link…\". The button is not re-tappable. The spinner appears only if the wait reaches 1s. Under Reduce Motion there is no spinner and the words stay. Share stays live.\n- Cancelling the iOS sheet returns to idle with no message. Android reports no cancel, so draw no cancelled state there.\n- On Android with no share targets, show an inline line with \"Copy link\". Copying announces \"Link copied\".\n- Haptics: one light tick on \"Link copied\" only.\n- Motion: sheets use the system transition. Under Reduce Motion, use a cross-fade.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED\n- TextActionRow: the share/compare pair, with states idle, minting, copied and offline.\n- OfflineNotice: the host's FreshnessLine offline line plus a reason caption under Compare.\n- InlineErrorRow: link failed, with its \"Retry\" text button (44pt).\n- ProvenanceMark, SourceCaption, StatusChip and TextActionRow (outbound variant): the aha card, exactly as drawn in f8-seasonal-aha.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Reading order: the aha card, ending with its follow-up row and then \"Check or update at VoteWA, opens website\". Then \"Share this address\", \"Compare with a friend\", the caption, the sections and the sticky wall.\n- Keep scroll padding so the sticky wall never hides focus.\n- Spoken labels: \"Share this address, opens share sheet\" and \"Compare with a friend, sends a card without your address, opens share sheet\".\n- While the link is being made, Compare reads \"Making a link\". When disabled, it stays focusable and reads its reason.\n- The error's retry button reads \"Retry making the compare link\".\n- \"Link copied\" and the error are polite announcements.\n- The share-sheet thumbnail has a description of the readings with no address: \"Camas, WA: flood zone X, minimal flood hazard (FEMA); wildfire hazard moderate, 3 of 5 (USFS); air on Mon 19 Oct good, AQI 42, observed 7:00 AM (AirNow); radon zone 1, highest potential for the county (EPA). Yours?\"\n- When the share sheet closes, focus returns to the button that opened it.\n- At AX5 and Android 200% the buttons stack full-width and the text wraps.\n- Every frame must read correctly in greyscale. No state is shown by colour alone.\n\nCOPY\n- Buttons: \"Share this address\" · \"Compare with a friend\".\n- Minting label: \"Making a link…\".\n- Caption: \"The compare card shows your city, your readings and the headline above — never your address, and no name. Anyone with the link can see it.\"\n- Error line: \"We couldn't make a compare link just now.\"\n- Error button: \"Retry\".\n- Offline reason: \"You're offline. Compare needs a connection. You can still share the address.\"\n- Android, no targets, line: \"No apps to share with. Copy the link instead.\"\n- Android, no targets, button: \"Copy link\".\n- Status: \"Link copied\".\n\nEDGE CASES\n- Longest address: PLACE B in the iOS share-address header, wrapping to two lines.\n- AX5 and 200%: the buttons stack.\n- Expiry: once the token lifetime is fixed, the caption gains \"until {date}\" at the end of its last sentence; frame 14 tests that wrap.\n- Slow network: the spinner appears only after 1s, and Share stays live.\n- Offline: the host's FreshnessLine reads \"You're offline · as of 6:04 PM\". Compare is disabled with its reason. Share still works.\n- No share targets: Android only.\n- Audience: the row appears wherever the address preview appears, whether the person is signed out or signed in with no saved place. It never appears on Today or on a saved place's Place file.\n- Measurement: sends from the apps are not counted in the spread metric yet. Nothing on screen changes because of this. List it on Notes.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of filled or outlined buttons, draw plain text buttons at full target size — because \"Continue\" must stay the only primary at the moment of sign-up.\n- Instead of putting the pair inside the sticky wall, or leaving Android's old link there, draw the pair under the aha card and draw the wall without the link — because the contract puts no actions in the wall, and a third control there becomes a crowded 3-up row.\n- Instead of lining the share pair up with the VoteWA row, keep the pair outside the card with no border or glyph — because the outbound row leaves the app and the pair opens the share sheet.\n- Instead of an app-drawn Material 3 chooser, draw the system Android Sharesheet with its title — because Android guidance forbids custom share lists.\n- Instead of a bare URL in the iOS sheet header, draw the card title and image — because the header is what the sender checks before sending.\n- Instead of copy such as \"Send your card\", write the anonymous caption — because the recipient sees \"A place in Camas, WA\", with no name.\n- Instead of a red error banner, draw the InlineErrorRow under the row — because only one control failed.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- Each frame without a sheet shows exactly one filled primary (\"Continue\"). Sheet frames show the preview dimmed behind the system sheet.\n- The Android wall no longer holds \"Share this address\".\n- Both buttons measure 44pt/48dp, with an 8pt/8dp gap.\n- Before the tap, the caption says what the card shows (city, readings, headline), that it is anonymous, and that anyone with the link can see it.\n- When the token lifetime is fixed, the caption ends \"until {date}\" in the same line with no layout change.\n- The iOS header shows the card title and image. Android shows the system Sharesheet titled \"Compare your place with mine\".\n- The aha card's chip reads \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\", matching StatusChip.\n- Offline and error frames keep \"Share this address\" usable.\n- The VoteWA row and the share pair cannot be confused.\n- A viewer can tell, without reading code, that the compare card never carries the address.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f8-native-share-compare · ios · 01-idle · light — the dense default: the aha card (including the VoteWA row), the text row, the caption and the full sticky wall in one viewport.\n2. f8-native-share-compare · ios · 02-minting · light — the link is not ready: 12pt spinner and \"Making a link…\" on Compare; Share live.\n3. f8-native-share-compare · ios · 03-compare-share-sheet · light — the system sheet at medium detent, with the header \"A place in Camas, WA · Yours?\" and the card image; the preview is dimmed behind it.\n4. f8-native-share-compare · ios · 04-link-error · light — the InlineErrorRow \"We couldn't make a compare link just now.\" with \"Retry\"; both buttons enabled.\n5. f8-native-share-compare · ios · 05-offline · light — the FreshnessLine \"You're offline · as of 6:04 PM\" under the header; Compare disabled with its reason; Share enabled.\n6. f8-native-share-compare · ios · 06-share-address-sheet · light — the system sheet whose header names 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, wrapped to two lines.\n7. f8-native-share-compare · android · 07-idle · light — the pair under the aha card, with the caption; the sticky wall without the old link.\n8. f8-native-share-compare · android · 08-minting · light — spinner and \"Making a link…\" on Compare; Share live.\n9. f8-native-share-compare · android · 09-sharesheet · light — the system Sharesheet titled \"Compare your place with mine\", with the thumbnail.\n10. f8-native-share-compare · android · 10-share-address-sharesheet · light — the system Sharesheet titled \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas, WA 98607\", no thumbnail.\n11. f8-native-share-compare · android · 11-no-targets · light — the inline \"No apps to share with. Copy the link instead.\" and \"Copy link\".\n12. f8-native-share-compare · android · 12-link-copied · light — the \"Link copied\" status line.\n13. f8-native-share-compare · android · 13-offline · light — the FreshnessLine offline line; Compare disabled with its reason; Share live.\n14. f8-native-share-compare · ios · 14-ax5 · light — the buttons stacked; the longer caption \"…Anyone with the link can see it until Mon 16 Nov.\" wrapped; the sticky wall with scroll padding.\n15. f8-native-share-compare · android · 15-link-error · light — the Android version of frame 4, with \"Retry\".\n16. f8-native-share-compare · ios · 16-greyscale · light — frame 1 in greyscale.\n17. f8-native-share-compare · ios · 17-idle · dark — dark twin of frame 1, with the labels in the dark focus/link token (border.focus, #38BDF8).\n18. f8-native-share-compare · android · 18-offline · dark — dark twin of frame 13: Compare disabled with its reason; Share live.\n19. f8-native-share-compare · ios · 19-notes · light — the Notes artboard. List every invented string: the iOS header titles, the Android share-address Sharesheet title, the no-targets line, \"Making a link…\", \"Link copied\", 6:04 PM, the AX5 expiry date \"Mon 16 Nov\", and the thumbnail description, which comes from the compare card's image description. Record these decisions:\n- The Android link moved out of the wall and lost its icon.\n- The caption names the headline because the compare card carries the aha headline as well as the readings.\n- Making the link when the row scrolls into view is new on native (the design doc makes it on tap; the web makes it when its sheet opens). It spends the compare-card rate limit, which matches the address preview's, only for visitors who reach the row.\n- The error button reads \"Retry\", per InlineErrorRow.\nFlag these open items:\n- Sends from the apps are not counted in the spread metric until the app event recorder ships. This understates spread rather than inflating it, which is the acceptable direction. Adding the recorder is F7's job, since the widget needs it too.\n- /start?vs= links open in the browser, not the app, so the web compare pages must carry the app download link.\n- Add the expiry date to the caption (\"…until {date}\") once the token lifetime is fixed. Until then, native consent is weaker than the web sheet's.\n- The aha follow-up now uses \"Keep\", matching the wall. See f8-seasonal-aha.\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: artboards 7-12, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 3: artboards 13-18, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 4: artboard 19.",
            "changeLog": [
              "Replaced the Jordan Lee / Sat 10 Oct persona with a signed-out newcomer at PLACE B on the fixture TODAY Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM; removed the date-difference Notes line (major review finding; PLACE B is saved on Sat 10 Oct so the saver never sees this screen).",
              "Thumbnail description now dates the frozen air reading and names every authority: 'air on Mon 19 Oct good, AQI 42, observed 7:00 AM (AirNow)', 'wildfire ... (USFS)' (major + minor findings; P15 frozen readings carry their date; derive f8-9).",
              "Aha deadline chip changed to count-first 'in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct' and source caption to '... · as of Mon 19 Oct', matching published StatusChip/SourceCaption and the revised f8-seasonal-aha (major finding).",
              "Minting state now uses the TextActionRow minting anatomy: 12pt spinner, 'Making a link…', Reduce Motion keeps the words; spoken 'Making a link'; string added to COPY (00c S2).",
              "Error button renamed 'Retry' with spoken label 'Retry making the compare link'; COPY split into one string per line (InlineErrorRow contract).",
              "Caption now names the headline: 'your city, your readings and the headline above' (token carries h; TextActionRow copy rule).",
              "Link is made when the row first scrolls into view instead of on every preview load; Notes records this as a new native decision and its rate-limit cost (design doc: mint on tap; research: web mints on sheet open).",
              "Sticky wall strings quoted in full from the host, and told to draw it exactly as in the screenshot.",
              "Dark label colour named as a token (border.focus) in LAYOUT and the dark artboard.",
              "Added Android share-address Sharesheet title in CONTENT and a new artboard 10; frame count 18 -> 19, batch plan now 4 turns.",
              "Added the expiry-clause DONE WHEN line and made the AX5 artboard draw the longer caption '...until Mon 16 Nov.' (invented, listed on Notes); edge case notes the expiry wrap.",
              "Notes invented-string list extended; all v1 substance (hand-offs, audience, measurement gap, browser-only links, no-name card, offline and no-targets states) kept."
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "f8-seasonal-aha",
            "name": "Rotating seasonal aha card",
            "platforms": [
              "web",
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": false,
            "frameCount": 23,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Rotating seasonal aha card · f8-seasonal-aha\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Aha card (What stands out)\". This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed. Keep these parts as they are:\n- the overline \"WHAT STANDS OUT\" on the left of the header row;\n- the chip slot on the right of the header row;\n- the 42pt rounded icon tile;\n- the headline, the detail and the source caption;\n- one sunken follow-up row with a chevron.\nThe host's reading badge is now called the \"reading chip\".\n\nATTACH: (1) The aha card on web /start at 390 and 1440. (2) The iOS and Android address previews, showing the aha card. (3) The Foundations board frames for ProvenanceMark, SourceCaption, StatusChip and TextActionRow. (4) One frame each of f8-compare-arrival-header and f8-og-compare-card, for the crops in frame 15.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: Web 390×844 and 1440×900, iOS 393×852, Android 412×915.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE\n- Tab and parent: Place tab → address preview. On web this is /start. On iOS and Android it is the Place launch preview. The card is the first card under the hero.\n- Entry points:\n  - typing an address and tapping \"See your place\";\n  - a shared https://pantopus.com/start?address= link;\n  - a friend's https://pantopus.com/start?vs=<token> link, whose sender column shows the token's headline (90 characters at most);\n  - the compare reveal, which shows the recipient's own aha;\n  - the compare share card.\n- What it receives: the typed address, today's date and the address's state.\n- Hand-off 1: the follow-up row scrolls to the sticky wall (\"Keep this address handy\").\n- Hand-off 2: \"Compare with a friend\", below the card, opens the compare sheet on web or the system share sheet on the apps.\n- Hand-off 3: the source caption row opens ProvenanceSheet in the app.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Someone new at PLACE B, a mover like Jordan Lee. He moved from Oregon, so his registration does not carry over. On Mon 19 Oct at 6:10 PM Pacific, a signed-out visitor types 1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas, WA 98607. The Oregon detail is scenario context only. It must never appear in copy, and no copy may imply anyone's registration status.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Make the one headline on the anonymous preview the fact that is actually urgent this month at this address.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: The eye lands on the headline first, then on the date chip, then on the source caption with its mark. The card's primary action is the sunken follow-up row, which leads to the save. The outbound row is visibly secondary.\n\nCONTENT (deltas to the fixtures; the default frame is dated Mon 19 Oct)\n\nVoter card (the default)\n- Chip: \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\".\n- Headline: \"Online or mail voter registration for Nov 3 must arrive by Oct 26 in Washington.\"\n- Detail, line 1: \"In person: until 8:00 PM Tue 3 Nov at your county elections office.\"\n- Detail, line 2: \"Moved recently? Registration is per address.\"\n- Source: \"Washington Secretary of State · statewide · as of Mon 19 Oct\". The data is loaded but not yet checked, so draw a HOLLOW mark with the words \"On record, not confirmed\".\n- Follow-up row: \"Keep this address handy to see what changes here\".\n- Outbound row: \"Check or update at VoteWA ↗\".\n\nOther voter dates\n- Thu 8 Oct: chip \"in 18 days · Mon 26 Oct\".\n- Mon 26 Oct: chip \"Today\".\n\nIn-person phase, from Tue 27 Oct until 8:00 PM Tue 3 Nov\n- Fri 30 Oct: chip \"in 4 days · Tue 3 Nov\".\n- Headline: \"You can still register in person for Nov 3 — until 8:00 PM on Election Day.\"\n- Detail, line 1: \"Go to your county elections office.\"\n- Detail, line 2: \"Moved recently? Registration is per address.\"\n- Remove the online/mail line.\n- Source (\"as of\" the frame's date), outbound row and follow-up row are the same as the voter card, with a HOLLOW mark.\n- Tue 3 Nov: chip \"Today\".\n\nRadon in January (Mon 11 Jan 2027)\n- Reading chip: \"Zone 1\".\n- Headline: \"Clark County is EPA Radon Zone 1 — highest potential (county).\"\n- Detail: \"EPA recommends testing every home. A test kit takes a few days.\"\n- Source: \"EPA · county-wide estimate — only a test tells you about this home\", with a FILLED mark.\n- Outbound row: \"Get a free test kit · Washington Dept of Health ↗\".\n\nRanked aha with no seasonal match (Wed 4 Nov)\n- The same radon card, without the outbound row.\n\nSummer air (Tue 8 Sep)\n- Reading chip: \"Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups · AQI 118\".\n- Headline: \"Air is Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups here today · air quality index (AQI) 118\".\n- Detail (EPA's health message for this category, verbatim): \"Members of sensitive groups may experience health effects. The general public is less likely to be affected.\"\n- Source: \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 4:00 PM\", with a FILLED mark.\n\nTax, when no election rule is loaded (Mon 19 Oct)\n- Chip: \"in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov\".\n- Headline: \"Property tax, second half, is due Mon 2 Nov in Clark County.\"\n- Detail: \"Moved from Sat 31 Oct because that date is a Saturday.\"\n- Source: \"Clark County Treasurer · county-wide · as of Mon 19 Oct\", with a HOLLOW mark and \"On record, not confirmed\".\n\nCalm fallback (no chip)\n- Use a hypothetical address outside radon Zone 1. Crop the header out and draw no address.\n- Headline: \"No active alerts · Air Good today (AirNow) · Outside FEMA's mapped floodplain\".\n- Detail: \"Air: Good · air quality index (AQI) 42, observed 5:00 PM.\"\n- Source: \"AirNow, FEMA, NWS · this area · checked 6:00 PM\", with a FILLED mark. Each clause's authority is named in the headline or the caption (NWS).\n\nWorst case: the 90-character token limit (a synthetic stress string)\n- Full headline (112 characters): \"Clark County property tax, second half, is due Mon 2 Nov — moved from Sat 31 Oct because that date is a weekend.\"\n- Cut version (89 characters): \"Clark County property tax, second half, is due Mon 2 Nov — moved from Sat 31 Oct because…\"\n- The cut falls at a word boundary. The mark, its word and the short source stay.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\n- Chip slot, on the right of the header row:\n  - Deadline headlines use StatusChip, deadline variant, exactly as published: 24pt pill, surface.sunken fill, 12pt calendar-outline glyph, captionMedium label in text.strong, no border.\n  - In light mode the glyph is text.strong at every count. In dark mode the glyph is semantic.warning at 14 days or fewer and on \"Today\".\n  - The chip is the relative count, then the date. On the deadline day it shows \"Today\" alone. Urgency is carried by the printed count.\n- Hazard headlines use the reading chip: the host's existing badge, restyled to StatusChip anatomy (surface.sunken fill, captionMedium label in text.strong, no border), the plain word before the number, no AQI hue fill, one per header row.\n- The calm fallback has no chip.\n- Source: a SourceCaption with ProvenanceMark (S) at its head. Print the mark's word once, next to the mark.\n- The caption row (44pt) opens ProvenanceSheet in the app and shows no external-link glyph, with or without a URL. ProvenanceSheet has its own no-URL state; when a URL exists it lives in the sheet's source row. The only ↗ on the card is the outbound row's.\n- Actions: two follow-up actions that must never look alike.\n  - First, the existing sunken internal row, which keeps its chevron-right. It is the card's primary action.\n  - Under it, inside the card, the TextActionRow outbound variant as published: 48pt/dp/px minimum height, radius md 8, 1px text.secondary edge, no fill, bodySmall text.primary label that names the destination, trailing 16pt external-link glyph.\n  - The ↗ in copy strings stands for that glyph. Draw it once, at the row's trailing edge, and do not also print it as text.\n- Graceful degradation:\n  - If the state has no program link, the outbound row is absent. Leave no empty slot.\n  - When a method's deadline passes, remove that method's line. After 8:00 PM Tue 3 Nov, draw the ranked aha instead.\n  - A failed preview is handled by the host's error screen. Draw the host error screen in that case, not an empty card shell.\n- Wildfire: when promoted in summer, show it as a standing fact (\"Wildfire hazard potential: High · 4 of 5 · USFS\"), paired with today's AirNow reading. Present it as a standing hazard rating, never as current fire danger.\n- Loading: the WarmingSkeleton matches the card's final geometry: the icon tile, two headline bars, a caption bar and the chip outline, at the card's final height. It is shown only if the load takes 1s or longer.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- The follow-up row scrolls to the wall. On a deep-link landing, scroll once and fade the highlight.\n- The outbound row opens a new tab on web, an in-app Safari view on iOS and a Custom Tab on Android, so the preview stays open.\n- The caption row opens ProvenanceSheet: a web modal, an iOS medium detent or an Android bottom sheet. Focus returns to the caption row when it closes.\n- The chip is not interactive.\n- The chip and its count do not animate. Under Reduce Motion everything is static, and the highlight fade becomes a cross-fade.\n- No haptics.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED\n- StatusChip (deadline variant, as published)\n- Reading chip = the host's existing badge, restyled to StatusChip anatomy (surface.sunken, text.strong), one per header row\n- ProvenanceMark (S)\n- SourceCaption (here a trigger for ProvenanceSheet, not a link)\n- ProvenanceSheet\n- TextActionRow (outbound variant, as published)\n- WarmingSkeleton (card-shaped, as described above)\n- OfflineNotice (with the host's FreshnessLine offline variant)\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Reading order: overline, headline, chip, detail, source with its mark word, follow-up row, outbound row.\n- The chip reads \"Deadline in 7 days, Monday 26 October\". On the day it reads \"Deadline today, Monday 26 October\".\n- Mark names: \"on record, not confirmed\" and \"official\".\n- The caption row reads \"Source: Washington Secretary of State, on record, not confirmed, opens source details\".\n- The outbound rows read \"Check or update at VoteWA, opens website\" and \"Get a free test kit from Washington Department of Health, opens website\". The glyph is not read.\n- Chip label contrast is at least 4.5:1. The chip glyph and the outbound edge are at least 3:1.\n- Urgency is never shown by hue alone; the count is always printed.\n- AX5: the header row stacks, with the chip under the overline, and the headline wraps fully.\n- Every frame must read correctly in greyscale.\n\nCOPY: Every string above, plus these:\n- \"Check or update at VoteWA ↗\" and \"Get a free test kit · Washington Dept of Health ↗\" (the ↗ is the glyph).\n- Offline reason: \"You're offline. VoteWA needs a connection. You can still read this card.\"\n- Mark words: \"On record, not confirmed\" and \"Official\".\n- The follow-up row says \"Keep this address handy…\", not \"Claim this address\", because the row leads to a save, not a claim.\n- The radon detail is the EPA testing line; the host's \"one in four homes\" statistic is removed because it has no named source and sits under an official mark.\n- On the deadline day the chip says \"Today\", never a zero count. Times are written \"8:00 PM\"; deadlines are never described as midnight.\n- Say how rare a reading is only with a named source; otherwise state the reading and its authority.\n- No string says or implies whether the person is registered.\n- Never write \"closes Oct 26\" or \"Quiet on every layer\".\n\nEDGE CASES\n- The longest headline: the 90-character cut.\n- The in-person phase.\n- A deadline that falls today.\n- Two seasonal rules that match at once: the election rule wins by table order.\n- No program link for the state.\n- Data not yet checked (hollow) vs checked (filled).\n- Offline: the host's FreshnessLine reads \"You're offline · as of 6:04 PM\" above the card; the outbound row is disabled with its reason.\n- Loading: the card-shaped skeleton at final height, only for loads of 1s or longer.\n- At 390, if the overline and the reading chip do not fit on one line, the chip moves under the overline, as at AX5.\n- A device outside Pacific time: add \"Pacific\" after 8:00 PM.\n- Signed in or out: the card looks the same to signed-in and signed-out visitors on /start. Signed-in visitors who arrive through a compare link see the same card, and the follow-up still scrolls to the wall.\n- Rules table, for checking the delta dates:\n  - From Sep 20: the state's election deadline rows, when 30 days or fewer remain.\n  - Apr 1–30 and Oct 1–31: property tax or appeal rows within 30 days.\n  - Jan 1–31: radon Zone 1, with the state's free-kit link.\n  - Jun 15 – Sep 30: AQI 101 or higher today, or wildfire hazard High.\n  - Otherwise: the existing ranking, then the calm fallback.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of \"Voter registration … closes October 26\", write the online-or-mail line plus the in-person line — because in-person registration stays open until 8:00 PM on Election Day.\n- Instead of hiding the card on Tue 27 Oct, switch to the in-person headline — because that is the last open path for a late mover.\n- Instead of warning-coloured chip text, glyph or border in light mode, draw the published StatusChip with a text.strong glyph and the count printed — because warning on the sunken fill fails 3:1.\n- Instead of a \"Quiet\" chip over all layers, name only what is calm, with sources — because radon is Zone 1 here.\n- Instead of reusing the follow-up row for the kit link, draw a separate bordered outbound row — because one control that does two things depending on the month misleads.\n- Instead of an external-link glyph on the source caption, draw the caption with no glyph and keep ↗ for the outbound row only — because the caption opens a sheet in the app and the outbound row leaves it.\n- Instead of dropping the mark in the 90-character version, keep the mark and the short source — because an unchecked deadline shown as fact is the honesty failure the pilot counts.\n- Instead of a countdown ring or bar, draw the dated chip — because urgency is shown as a date.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- In October, a Washington address shows the method-specific headline, sourced to the Washington Secretary of State. In January, a Zone 1 county shows the kit link.\n- Every loaded, unchecked deadline (voter, tax) is hollow and says so at every size, including the token version. Official datasets (EPA, AirNow) are filled.\n- No frame shows a past deadline for any method.\n- Every deadline chip reads count first, then date, and matches StatusChip on the Foundations board.\n- The follow-up row and the outbound row cannot be confused, and the card has exactly one ↗.\n- Every frame names its mark.\n- The card is fully readable while signed out.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f8-seasonal-aha · web-390 · 01-voter-7-days-unconfirmed · light — the dense default on Mon 19 Oct: chip \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\", hollow mark, the \"Keep\" follow-up row and the bordered VoteWA row.\n2. f8-seasonal-aha · web-390 · 02-voter-official · light — the same card with a filled \"Official\" mark.\n3. f8-seasonal-aha · web-390 · 03-voter-18-days · light — Thu 8 Oct, chip \"in 18 days · Mon 26 Oct\".\n4. f8-seasonal-aha · web-390 · 04-voter-today · light — Mon 26 Oct, chip \"Today\".\n5. f8-seasonal-aha · web-390 · 05-in-person-phase · light — Fri 30 Oct, chip \"in 4 days · Tue 3 Nov\", the in-person detail lines and a hollow mark.\n6. f8-seasonal-aha · web-390 · 06-in-person-today · light — Tue 3 Nov, chip \"Today\", hollow mark.\n7. f8-seasonal-aha · web-390 · 07-radon-january-kit · light — the radon card with the testing detail, a filled mark and the outbound row \"Get a free test kit · Washington Dept of Health ↗\".\n8. f8-seasonal-aha · web-390 · 08-deadline-passed-ranked · light — Wed 4 Nov: the radon card with no outbound row, filled mark.\n9. f8-seasonal-aha · web-390 · 09-no-program-link · light — the voter card with no outbound row, hollow mark.\n10. f8-seasonal-aha · web-390 · 10-summer-air · light — Tue 8 Sep: the reading chip \"Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups · AQI 118\" moved under the overline because it does not fit beside it, the EPA health detail, filled mark.\n11. f8-seasonal-aha · web-390 · 11-tax-due · light — the tax card, chip \"in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov\", hollow mark.\n12. f8-seasonal-aha · web-390 · 12-calm-fallback · light — no chip, filled mark; a hypothetical address outside radon Zone 1 with the header cropped out.\n13. f8-seasonal-aha · web-390 · 13-loading · light — the card-shaped skeleton at final height (shown for loads of 1s or longer).\n14. f8-seasonal-aha · web-390 · 14-offline · light — the host's FreshnessLine \"You're offline · as of 6:04 PM\" above the card; the outbound row disabled, with its reason.\n15. f8-seasonal-aha · web-390 · 15-token-90 · light — two labelled crops, stacked: (a) the f8-compare-arrival-header sender strip at 390 wide; (b) the f8-og-compare-card sender column, scaled from 520 of 1200 wide, with the mark at 28px or larger. Label each crop with its host surface name. Both show the cut headline, the mark, its word and the short source.\n16. f8-seasonal-aha · web-1440 · 16-voter-7-days · light — the default at desktop width.\n17. f8-seasonal-aha · ios · 17-voter-7-days · light — the default in the iOS preview.\n18. f8-seasonal-aha · android · 18-voter-7-days · light — the default in the Android preview, with a 48dp outbound row.\n19. f8-seasonal-aha · ios · 19-ax5 · light — the header row stacked, the headline wrapped.\n20. f8-seasonal-aha · web-390 · 20-greyscale · light — frame 1 in greyscale.\n21. f8-seasonal-aha · web-390 · 21-voter-7-days · dark — dark twin of frame 1 (chip glyph semantic.warning at 7 days).\n22. f8-seasonal-aha · ios · 22-in-person-phase · dark — dark twin of the in-person phase.\n23. f8-seasonal-aha · web-390 · 23-notes · light — the Notes artboard. List:\n- every invented string and delta date: 8 Oct, 30 Oct, 3 Nov, 4 Nov, 8 Sep, 11 Jan;\n- the tax and voter as-of dates \"as of Mon 19 Oct\" (the tax caption previously ended \"2026 second half\");\n- the calm-fallback caption \"checked 6:00 PM\", the air time \"observed 5:00 PM\" and its hypothetical address;\n- the radon testing line;\n- the reading-chip strings and the quoted EPA health message;\n- the 90-character worst case, labelled as a synthetic stress string.\nRecord these deltas from the host:\n- The follow-up now matches the wall (\"Keep\"). \"Claim this address\" stays for T1→T3 only. The inventory's intent that the follow-up stays primary is kept.\n- The host's radon statistic is removed until it has a named source.\n- Ranked radon headline reworded to authority wording (\"highest potential\", county scope).\n- Calm fallback headline and detail replaced; no \"Quiet\" chip (radon Zone 1).\n- The chip uses the published StatusChip: count first, text.strong label and glyph. The per-surface request for hue on the glyph and border is replaced because warning on sunken fails 3:1.\n- The host badge is restyled to StatusChip anatomy as the reading chip.\n- SourceCaption here is a sheet trigger, not a link; the contract's no-URL rule is read as \"no outbound link\".\nOmitted state: no tax-appeal headline is drawn. Clark County's window (\"Closes July 1, or 60 days after your value notice was mailed\") has no fixed date inside the Apr and Oct rule windows, so its wording stays conditional.\nFlag these open items:\n- The compare token needs a confidence field, so the hollow mark can survive into frame 15's crops.\n- Signed-in visitors have no in-app civic destination from this card. The proposed target is /app/place/civic?focus=registration.\n- Whether the free-kit link should appear on every radon aha, not only in January (research calls it the step from county estimate to house).\n\nBATCH PLAN: Turn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 2: artboards 7-12, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 3: artboards 13-18, then wait for \"continue\". Turn 4: artboards 19-23.",
            "changeLog": [
              "All deadline chips now count first ('in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct', 'in 18 days', 'in 4 days · Tue 3 Nov', 'in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov'); LAYOUT says count then date; spoken label 'Deadline in 7 days, Monday 26 October'; deleted the date-first Notes line (major finding; 00a StatusChip and house style).",
              "Chip anatomy replaced by the published StatusChip deadline variant (12pt glyph, no border, text.strong glyph in light, semantic.warning in dark at <=14 days/Today); artboards 3 and 11 now describe count and date only; Notes records why the hue request was dropped (major finding; warning on sunken 2.89:1).",
              "Source caption row now opens ProvenanceSheet with no external-link glyph; the only ↗ is the outbound row's; new INSTEAD OF line and Notes entry on reading the contract's no-URL rule (major finding).",
              "Outbound row uses the published TextActionRow outbound measurements (48 min, radius md 8, 1px text.secondary, bodySmall).",
              "Kit link renamed 'Get a free test kit · Washington Dept of Health ↗' with spoken label, matching 00b.",
              "Reading chip added to FOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED as the host badge restyled to StatusChip anatomy (text.strong); air chip now 'Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups · AQI 118' with EPA casing matching the headline; 390 fit edge case added and shown in artboard 10.",
              "Summer air headline leads with the plain meaning and gains EPA's verbatim health message as detail (P13).",
              "Calm fallback air time changed to 'observed 5:00 PM' (invented); justification now says authorities are named in headline or caption (NWS); offline artboard and edge case gain the host FreshnessLine 'You're offline · as of 6:04 PM'.",
              "Tax detail reworded ('because that date is a Saturday'); worst case replaced with a 112-char synthetic string cut at a word boundary to 89 chars, labelled on Notes.",
              "Voter and tax source captions end with 'as of Mon 19 Oct' (SourceCaption authority · scope · as-of; matches 00a crop c); the old tax as-of noted on Notes.",
              "WarmingSkeleton shown only for loads of 1s or longer (contract platform note), in Loading, edge cases and artboard 13.",
              "INSTEAD OF split to 8 lines (countdown ring separated; ↗ line added); 'Claim' and 'one in four' moved into COPY notes; other prohibitions rewritten as positive COPY rules; Never list kept only for 'closes Oct 26' and 'Quiet on every layer'.",
              "Notes deltas added: ranked radon headline rewording, calm fallback replacement, chip anatomy decision, reading-chip restyle; new open item on showing the kit link on every radon aha."
            ]
          }
        ],
        "history": [
          {
            "round": 1,
            "substance": [
