                "id": "f8-native-share-compare",
                "pass": false,
                "issues": [
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "On Android, the existing 'Share this address' link sits inside the sticky wall today, directly under 'Continue'. The prompt says to keep the sticky wall 'exactly as they are' and also to turn that link into a pair under the aha card. It never says the link must be taken out of the wall, so the designer could leave a copy in the wall or never move it. The contract bans actions inside the WallBar. The prompt also never says the link's existing share icon must go, although the new row has 'no icon'.",
                    "evidence": "PlaceLaunchScreen.kt:470-483: the bottom sticky Column holds 'Keep this address handy…', PrimaryButton 'Continue', the 24-hour caption, then `ShareAddressLink(place)`. Lines 494-523: ShareAddressLink draws PantopusIcon.Share (14dp) and the 13sp 'Share this address'. component-contract.md TextActionRow doNot: 'No actions inside the sticky WallBar.' The prompt says: 'Keep the hero, the aha card, the section groups and the sticky wall exactly as they are... On Android, turn the existing single \"Share this address\" link into a pair.'",
                    "fix": "In TYPE, write: 'On Android the existing Share this address link currently sits inside the sticky wall under Continue. Remove it from the wall, drop its share icon, and re-home it as the left button of the new pair under the aha card. Apart from that removal, the wall is unchanged.' Frame 7 should show the wall without the link."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The aha card's contents are listed without its VoteWA outbound row. In f8-seasonal-aha the Mon 19 Oct default has an outbound TextActionRow ('Check or update at VoteWA ↗') under the follow-up row. With that row back, the share pair sits 16pt below a second TextActionRow, and the prompt never says how the two stay distinct. The designer may drop the VoteWA row, or draw two text rows that look alike.",
                    "evidence": "The prompt says: 'draw f8-seasonal-aha's Mon 19 Oct default exactly as that prompt specifies (voter-registration headline, date chip \"Mon 26 Oct · 7 days\", hollow mark with its source caption, and the follow-up row)'. f8-seasonal-aha CONTENT includes 'Outbound row: \"Check or update at VoteWA ↗\"', and its LAYOUT puts 'the TextActionRow outbound variant: border only... external-link glyph' under the follow-up row.",
                    "fix": "Add the outbound row to the enumeration ('…the follow-up row, and the bordered outbound row \"Check or update at VoteWA ↗\" inside the card'). Add one layout line: the share pair sits outside the card on the page surface, with no border and no glyph, so it cannot be mistaken for the in-card bordered outbound row. Add the VoteWA row to the reading order after the follow-up row."
                  },
                  {
