                    "issue": "The flow and the prompt disagree on the day-word change, and on when 'Bins out tonight' becomes true.",
                    "evidence": "flow-07 step 6: \"'Tomorrow' has become 'Tonight'\". research-findings: timeline entries \"at the evening boundary where 'Bins out tonight' becomes true\". Prompt shows \"Bins out tonight\" at 7:40 AM and DONE WHEN says \"'Tomorrow' becomes 'Today' at midnight\".",
                    "fix": "State what the evening-before entry changes (for example, the caption switches to 'Bins out tonight' from 5:00 PM) and what the midnight entry changes, and list both day-word sequences on Notes."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "Several smaller research and inventory points were dropped: 'no keeper text' on the widget; no-place copy only where the add-a-place sheet exists; if the large year band isn't legible at 338x354, ship small and medium only; the Android equivalent of midnight timeline entries (the doc has updatePeriodMillis 1800000); the optional accessoryRectangular.",
                    "evidence": "per-surface: \"no logo; no keeper overdue text\". Inventory state: \"no place ('Save an address to see today here' — only where the add-a-place sheet exists)\". research-findings: \"If the large year strip cannot be made legible at 338x354pt ... leave large out instead of filling it with extra text rows.\"",
                    "fix": "Add 'no keeper line' to SMALL/LARGE. Add the add-a-place dependency and the large-size go/no-go check to Notes. Name the Android update mechanism for midnight day-word changes."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "In the air-hero delta, the lower pickup line breaks the date rule for dates beyond tomorrow, and in the large widget the air line opens section=strip instead of section=air.",
                    "evidence": "house-style MICROCOPY: \"beyond tomorrow, add the relative count: 'in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct'\". Prompt: \"Garbage only · Tue 27 Oct\" on Thu 22 Oct. \"The two lower lines open section=strip.\"",
                    "fix": "Use 'Garbage only · in 5 days · Tue 27 Oct'. Either give the large air line its own section=air region or explain on Notes why it shares the strip region."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "Dark coverage is thin for a widget. The research says widgets get full dark sets, and the dimmed stale and past-horizon states are exactly where dark-mode contrast can fail.",
                    "evidence": "house-style-contradictions: \"full dark sets only for widgets, the provenance specimen and the scale strips\". The prompt's dark frames are only 11, 12, 19 (01), 20 (04) and 21 (13).",
                    "fix": "Add dark twins of 08-stale-air and 09-past-horizon at least."
                  }
