                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The large widget's year-band tap (section=year) goes straight to the place file and skips this landing. So that tap gets no forced refresh, no snapshot write and no session_open{trigger:widget}. A past-horizon widget tapped on its year band stays on 'Open to refresh', and widget attribution is undercounted. That breaks this surface's job for 'any tap'.",
                    "evidence": "Inventory entryPoints: \"Any tap on either widget size\". Purpose: \"refresh it so the snapshot is rewritten, and record that this open came from the widget\". flow-07 step 8: \"A forced refresh writes the snapshot, so 'Open to refresh' can never leave the widget grey.\" Prompt: \"section=year does not come here. It opens Place → Your place file at its year band.\"",
                    "fix": "State that section=year also triggers the forced Today refresh in the background, the snapshot write and session_open{trigger:widget} before or while it routes to the place file. List this on Notes as behaviour."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The research asks for session_open to be measured separately from snapshot writes, and activation counts a snapshot write reported as its own event. The prompt lists the behaviours without that separation.",
