                "id": "f7-widget-howto-sheet",
                "pass": false,
                "issues": [
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The prompt asks Notes to cover 'how the app learns a widget is placed' but never gives the mechanism, although the flow spec and derive proposal do. This is the exact handoff gap the critique flagged. On iOS there is no pin callback, so the success state and the removal of the place-file row depend on a read the prompt never names.",
                    "evidence": "flow-07 step 12: \"The app knows a widget is placed (a snapshot read or a pin callback) and stops asking.\" derive-proposals f7-add-widget-nudge: \"Suppressed automatically once a widget is placed (iOS WidgetCenter.getCurrentConfigurations, Android AppWidgetManager.getAppWidgetIds for TodayWidgetProvider)\". critique handoff gap: \"no prompt says how the app learns a widget was placed\".",
                    "fix": "State it: 'Android: the pin success callback, plus AppWidgetManager.getAppWidgetIds on each foreground. iOS: WidgetCenter.getCurrentConfigurations on each foreground (no callback, so iOS has no success line and the row disappears on the next app open).' Add an iOS frame or Notes line for the return-from-gallery case."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The merge of the Today nudge row into the place-file row isn't acknowledged, and that row's own states are dropped: dismissible, and hidden while the person has no place.",
                    "evidence": "critique: \"f7-add-widget-nudge becomes a row in it rather than a promo on Today.\" derive-proposals states: \"dismissed ... · already placed — hidden · no place — hidden\".",
                    "fix": "Add one line: the old Today nudge row now lives in the place file; it is dismissible, hidden with no place and hidden once placed, and the Notifications settings row keeps the sheet reachable after a dismissal."
