                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The finished-state line claims every piece has a decision, but the prompt lets Maya press Finish day with 9 pieces still undecided. In that case the line is false. The completeness honesty rule forbids it.",
                    "evidence": "Prompt footer: \"Finish day\" with caption \"9 still need a call. They'll be here tomorrow.\" and \"'Finish day' closes undo and collapses the page to the finished state.\" Prompt COPY: \"Finished: 'Day finished. Every piece you added today has a decision.'\" research-findings.md (capture): \"Copy says 'the mail you've added today', never 'all of today's mail'\" and \"Copy never claims completeness.\" flows-spec.md flow-08 step 8: \"the copy never claims 'all your mail'.\"",
                    "fix": "Split the finished state in two. (a) Only when Needs a call is empty: \"Day finished. Every piece you added today has a decision.\" (b) When pieces remain: \"Day finished. 9 pieces still need a call. They'll be here tomorrow.\" Draw 05-day-finished with 9 remaining, since that is the case the dense fixture produces, and list both strings in COPY."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
