                    "fix": "Add body variants under COPY → Confirm. Keep the bill variant as written. Filed or unclassified: body \"The mail record stays in Mail; only the photo is removed.\", live region \"Photo deleted. The mail record stays.\", deleted-state line \"The photo was deleted on <date>. The mail record stays.\" Not confirmed yet: body \"What we read stays unconfirmed in Needs a call; only the photo is removed.\" Add artboard \"f10-mail-piece-photo · ios · 08b-delete-confirm-filed · light\" showing the Riverview variant."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The drawer rows use provenance marks inconsistently. The HOA row gets the ring mark, but nothing on the drawer prints its legend word. The Clark Public Utilities row has no tick mark drawn, yet its spoken label says 'you added this'. A screen-reader user hears a mark that a sighted user never sees, and the ring has no word on this surface, which breaks the one-legend-per-surface invariant.",
                    "evidence": "Drawer list: 'Photographed rows get a ThumbnailRail ... and key facts on line 2, e.g. \"$142.18 · due Fri 23 Oct · Added to bills\"' (no mark) and 'Larkspur Loop HOA line 2: ... with the ring mark'. Accessibility: 'A drawer row is one element: \"Clark Public Utilities, 142 dollars 18 cents, due Friday 23 October, you added this, ...\"'. House style invariant 1: 'Each surface shows the matching word once (a legend or first-occurrence label).'",
                    "fix": "In the Drawer list section, add: \"Committed rows draw ProvenanceMark S (you-added) after the amount; the HOA row draws the read-from-your-photo ring. Print the legend once, under the filter row: '✓ You added this · ○ On record, not confirmed'.\" Change the HOA spoken label to end \"…due Sunday 1 November, on record, not confirmed, still in Needs a call.\" so the phrase is not said twice."
