                    "issue": "The prompt contradicts itself about sheet detents, and the default frame hides either the letter or the primary action. The sheet is given only peek and medium, but AX5 uses a 'large' detent. Frame 1 opens at medium, which covers the lower half of the page, while the peek detent leaves out the primary link row.",
                    "evidence": "'a bottom sheet with two detents: the peek shows payee, amount and due date; medium shows everything' vs 'At AX5 the facts panel opens at its large detent'. FIRST FIVE SECONDS: '(1) The letter itself, readable at fit-to-width ... Primary action: that link.'",
                    "fix": "Define three detents: \"peek (payee, amount and due date, plus the link row or 'Confirm what we read'), medium (stops at 45% of the height; the page is top-aligned so the letterhead and account line stay visible above it), large (AX sizes only).\""
                  },
