      {
        "ids": [
          "f11-keeper-strip",
          "f11-keeper-naming"
        ],
        "prompts": [
          {
            "id": "f11-keeper-strip",
            "name": "Keeper strip on Today",
            "platforms": [
              "web",
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": false,
            "frameCount": 29,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Keeper strip on Today · f11-keeper-strip\n\nTYPE: EXTENSION of the existing designed screen \"Today\". This screen already exists in the Pantopus design system. The attached screenshot is exact. Keep everything and change only what is listed. The only change is one strip in Today's keeper slot, between the 14-day strip and the weather block. Every other section keeps its order and look.\n\nATTACH: Today on iOS 393x852 for HOME A (dense, light and dark); Today on Android 412x915, web 1440x900 and web 390x844; Today with the air alert pinned; Today for PLACE B with the \"Saved place · Only you\" chip; the top section of the place file (Place tab); the Bills list on iOS for HOME A (Maya, owner), including a BillRow in its highlighted-from-notification state.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS: iOS 393x852 (primary), Android 412x915, web 1440x900 (left sidebar, main column) and web 390x844 (bottom tab bar).\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: The strip lives on the Today tab (bottom bar on phones, sidebar on desktop). There is one Today per platform; briefing pushes land on it, so this strip is the only place a keeper appears on Today. People reach it from:\n- the Today tab\n- the deep links /app/today and pantopus://today\n- the pickup and briefing push landings\n- a widget tap (pantopus://today?src=widget)\n- coming back from the naming sheet, which hands over a name and species. The pose settles in place, and the status line \"Ollie is on Today now.\" shows under the strip until the user leaves Today.\nAfter a claim, the same keeper appears at home scope (see the claim receipt). Ollie is still Ollie, and the claim receipt states the change in who can see it.\nThe strip hands off in three places:\n- The mood line opens the item it summarises, and that item offers the correction.\n- The count opens the place file, which shows the same number.\n- The name opens the keeper menu.\n\nWHO AND WHEN: Maya Chen at HOME A on Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM, checking whether the bins go out tonight. She named the River otter \"Ollie\" last week. Sam Ortega is a member and sees the same keeper. Jordan Lee, new at PLACE B, named a Red fox \"Pepper\".\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Put a calm face on what is really due at this address in the next 7 days, in words first.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: The eye hits the mood line (the fact) first, the avatar's pose and name second, and \"11 on file\" third. There is no primary action, because the strip asks for nothing. Its only tap targets are the mood line, the count and the name.\n\nCONTENT (fixture deltas only; list every invented string on Notes)\n- Keeper: Ollie, River otter. The species set is Octopus, River otter, Great blue heron, Red fox, Raccoon and Douglas squirrel.\n- Mood inputs at HOME A: bills, tasks and dates this household added that are overdue or due in the next 7 days (rolling, not a calendar week), plus pickup on the day before. Mood never comes from app opens, time away or mail counts. Seeded civic deadlines (voter registration, property tax) stay on the 14-day strip and do not move the mood unless the household added them, so the keeper never implies whether anyone is registered.\n- Mood inputs at PLACE B: only the dates Jordan added plus pickup (calendar only).\n- Permission-limited: mood, pose, caption and line are all computed only from data the viewer is allowed to see.\n- Mood rule (count every input item; pickup counts once, on the day before):\n  - calm = 0 items.\n  - on it = exactly 1 item, not overdue.\n  - busy = 2 or more items, none overdue.\n  - needs you = any item overdue.\n  - The line names up to 2 items. With 3 or more it reads \"N things due in the next 7 days.\" In needs you, the overdue item is always named first and the rest are counted.\n- calm, on it, busy and needs you are internal variant and pose names only. They never appear on screen. The visible caption beside the name describes the week, never the keeper:\n  - calm → \"Quiet week\"\n  - on it → \"Pickup soon\" when the one item is pickup; \"One thing due\" when it is a bill, task or date\n  - busy → \"Busy week\"\n  - needs you → \"Past due\"\n- Frames and lines:\n  1. calm, Wed 21 Oct, 8:00 AM, with both utility bills marked paid by Sam · Sun 18 Oct. Caption \"Quiet week\". Line \"Nothing due in the next 7 days.\" Calm requires every mood input (bills, tasks, dates, pickup) to return successfully. Pose: sitting, settled.\n  2. on it, Mon 19 Oct, with Clark Public Utilities marked paid by Sam · Sun 18 Oct. Caption \"Pickup soon\". Line \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow.\" Pose: upright, looking toward the line.\n  3. busy (the dense default, drawn on TODAY exactly; 2 items: pickup and Clark Public Utilities; the water bill on Wed 28 Oct is outside the window). Caption \"Busy week\". Line \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow. Clark Public Utilities is due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct.\" Pose: holding a small stack of papers.\n  4. busy with 3 items, Fri 30 Oct, 6:10 PM, with both utility bills marked paid and property tax added by the household: HOA dues Sun 1 Nov, Comcast Mon 2 Nov, property tax 2nd half Mon 2 Nov. Caption \"Busy week\". Line \"3 things due in the next 7 days.\"\n  5. needs you, Sat 24 Oct, 9:00 AM, Clark Public Utilities not marked paid (the water bill Wed 28 Oct is the 1 more). Caption \"Past due\". Line \"The Clark Public Utilities bill was due Fri 23 Oct. 1 more due in the next 7 days.\" Pose: holding up an envelope toward the line.\n- Unavailable: no caption, the neutral pose, InlineErrorRow and \"Retry\". When one input failed, name it: \"Couldn't check your bills.\" When more than one failed: \"Couldn't check what's due.\"\n- HOME A's pickup day was confirmed by Maya, so its line has no hollow mark.\n- Offline: \"Pickup soon · as of 7:04 AM\". The line is kept and the avatar is desaturated.\n- Count: \"11 on file\", with pips Place · Dates · Money · People. Proof is unknown, so draw nothing for it. PLACE B: \"6 on file\", with Place · Dates only.\n- PLACE B, Wed 21 Oct, 6:10 PM: on it pose, caption \"Pickup soon\", line \"Pickup tomorrow.\", then a hollow ProvenanceMark and \"City schedule, not yet confirmed\".\n- Worst case: the 24-character name \"Captain Wigglebottom the\" with the needs you line, at 393pt and at AX5.\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\n- Phones (iOS, Android, web-390): draw one row plus 12pt vertical padding at full content width. Add no card chrome beyond the host's section spacing. Place a 44pt avatar on the leading side. Beside it goes the text column:\n  - the name in bodyMedium, then the caption word in text.secondary, then a small chevron-down glyph\n  - the mood line in bodySmall text.primary, wrapping to two lines and never truncating\n  - FactCount on its own line under the mood line, left-aligned to the text column, with a 44pt-tall target\n- Web-1440 only: FactCount sits trailing in the same row.\n- Pose carries mood; colour never does. Draw every species in 4 clearly different postures that read at 44pt. Add a separate neutral front-facing pose for Unavailable, drawn as a single text.secondary outline with no fill. Draw nothing sad: no tears, drooping, illness, cowering or darker scenery.\n- FactCount is the integer plus one small labelled pip per known category. It is an open row, never a closed shape, so nothing reads as a share of a goal. A saved place shows a smaller set that is still complete.\n- The mood line is always one target. With one named item it opens that item. With 2 or more non-overdue items it scrolls Today up to the FourteenDayStrip rows and highlights them. In needs you it opens the overdue item.\n- Missing data:\n  - A failed input gives Unavailable, never calm.\n  - Offline keeps the last-known state with its time.\n  - With no keeper, draw Today exactly as it is today.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- Needs you landing: the line switches to the Place tab and opens the Bills list (from the place file's Money section), scrolled to the Clark Public Utilities BillRow in its highlighted-from-notification state, with focus on it. Back returns to Today.\n  - The correction goes through the row's existing overflow (Mark paid / I paid this) or bill detail. Draw no buttons on the row face. Under the highlighted row, draw one caption line, \"Already paid?\", that opens the row's overflow.\n- The PLACE B pickup line lands on the PickupCard. There, \"Yes, Tuesday is right\" becomes \"Yes, Thursday is right\" / \"Change pickup day\".\n- FactCount opens the place file.\n- The name opens a native menu: an iOS menu, an M3 dropdown, or a web popover. Owner items: Rename · Change species · Hide keeper for now · Remove keeper. Each item is also a screen-reader custom action.\n- Hide keeper for now applies only to the viewer. It opens a submenu (iOS menu submenu, M3 nested dropdown, web popover list) with \"Hide for 7 days · until Mon 26 Oct\" and \"Hide for a month · until Thu 19 Nov\". The slot closes and the InlineUndo line reads \"Keeper hidden until Mon 26 Oct (in 7 days) · Undo\".\n- While hidden, the place file's Keeper row carries the text action \"Show Ollie on Today\". The keeper also returns by itself on its date.\n- Remove keeper happens at once, with no dialog, on every tier.\n  - HOME A (affects Sam): the slot collapses to the InlineUndo line \"Keeper removed for everyone in this household · Undo\". The first half is the consequence prefix. Focus moves to Undo.\n  - PLACE B: \"Keeper removed · Undo\".\n  - None of the remove copy carries creature emotion.\n- The unnamed invitation appears only after a first value moment (a confirmed pickup day or a saved date) and after the first-week row has gone. It stays at most 14 days.\n  - It is a row with an outline silhouette in text.secondary, the invitation text and a 44pt \"Skip\" button.\n  - Invitation text: \"Give your place a keeper\" at HOME A, \"Give this place a keeper\" at PLACE B.\n  - Tapping the row opens the naming sheet.\n  - Skip closes the slot for good. Today then looks as it does with no keeper, with the InlineUndo line \"Skipped. You can add a keeper from your place file. · Undo\".\n- Motion: a pose change is one transition of 300ms or less. The idle loop lasts 5s or less, then the avatar holds still. The count changes silently, with no count-up and no \"+1\". Under Reduce Motion, use static poses and a cross-fade. This strip has no haptics.\n- Push: a mood change never sends a push, and no push carries the keeper's name, avatar or voice.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED: KeeperStrip (variants calm, on it, busy, needs you, unavailable, offline; states loading, hidden after Skip, suppressed under an active alert, permission-limited; FactCount on its own line on phones) · FactCount (keeper strip variant; T1 variant for PLACE B) · ProvenanceMark (S, unconfirmed; PLACE B pickup only) · InlineErrorRow (Unavailable) · WarmingSkeleton (avatar circle, two bars, count bar) · FreshnessLine and OfflineNotice (host) · InlineUndo (skipped, hidden, removed) · FactRow (place-file Keeper row with \"Show Ollie on Today\") · PickupCard, FourteenDayStrip, BillRow (highlighted from notification) and QuietDayReceipt (landings and host context) · ScopeChip (host location row). The strip uses no DestructiveConfirm and no LockedActionRow.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- The strip is a group labelled \"Ollie\" with three elements in this order. The avatar is decorative.\n  1. Name button: \"Ollie, keeper options\", with the value \"Busy week\".\n  2. Mood-line button: label is the fact line, \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow. Clark Public Utilities is due in 4 days, Friday 23 October.\" Hint: \"Shows these on Today.\" (needs you: \"Opens the bill.\")\n  3. Count button: \"11 things on file: place, dates, money, people. Opens your place file.\"\n- Targets: 44pt on iOS, 48dp on Android, 44px on web, with 8dp gaps between the line, the count and the name.\n- At AX5 or 200% text, the avatar sits on top and everything else stacks full width.\n- Mood is carried by words and pose, never hue, so the greyscale frame must read fully.\n- Retry's spoken label is \"Retry checking your bills\" (or \"Retry checking what's due\"). Announce Unavailable and offline politely. The status line \"Ollie is on Today now.\" is role=status.\n\nCOPY: \"Quiet week\" · \"Pickup soon\" · \"One thing due\" · \"Busy week\" · \"Past due\" · \"Nothing due in the next 7 days.\" · \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow.\" · \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow. Clark Public Utilities is due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct.\" · \"3 things due in the next 7 days.\" · \"5 things due in the next 7 days.\" · \"The Clark Public Utilities bill was due Fri 23 Oct. 1 more due in the next 7 days.\" · \"Already paid?\" · \"Couldn't check your bills.\" · \"Couldn't check what's due.\" · \"Retry\" · \"Pickup soon · as of 7:04 AM\" · \"11 on file\" · \"6 on file\" · \"Ollie is on Today now.\" · \"Give your place a keeper\" · \"Give this place a keeper\" · \"Skip\" · \"Skipped. You can add a keeper from your place file. · Undo\" · \"Rename\" · \"Change species\" · \"Hide keeper for now\" · \"Hide for 7 days · until Mon 26 Oct\" · \"Hide for a month · until Thu 19 Nov\" · \"Keeper hidden until Mon 26 Oct (in 7 days) · Undo\" · \"Show Ollie on Today\" · \"Remove keeper\" · \"Keeper removed for everyone in this household · Undo\" · \"Keeper removed · Undo\" · \"Only Maya can rename, change or remove this keeper.\" · \"Pickup tomorrow.\" · \"City schedule, not yet confirmed\".\n\nEDGE CASES\n- At AX5 the worst-case name and the needs you line wrap onto as many lines as they need (about 8), at full AX5 size, with no ellipsis, and Today scrolls.\n- A count of 128 on file keeps its pips on one line, on the count's own line.\n- Five items due: the line reads \"5 things due in the next 7 days.\" and opens the strip rows.\n- No place: the strip is absent.\n- Slow network: the skeleton reserves the exact height, so the weather block never jumps.\n- Air alert pinned (AQI 118, Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups, 4:00 PM): the whole slot collapses and the alert owns the screen. The keeper never sits beside an alert.\n- Sam (member) sees the same keeper. His menu shows \"Hide keeper for now\" (which hides it only for Sam) plus a disabled menu item \"Rename\" with the subtitle \"Only Maya can rename, change or remove this keeper.\" Only the owner can rename, change species or remove.\n- A guest without bill access gets pose, caption and line all computed only from what they can see: on it pose, \"Pickup soon\", \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow.\", even while Maya sees busy.\n- Invitation unanswered after 14 days: the slot closes silently, as after Skip but with no Undo line.\n- Way back after Skip, expiry or Remove: the place file's Place row \"Give your place a keeper\", and the Keeper row in account Settings, which opens the naming sheet.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a five-segment ring with outlined empty slots, draw \"11 on file\" plus labelled pips for known categories only — because a closed shape with gaps reads as \"almost done\".\n- Instead of a worried or tearful creature for an overdue bill, draw it holding up the envelope — because distress makes people avoid the display.\n- Instead of \"Needs you\" or \"On it\" next to the name, write a word about the week (\"Past due\", \"Pickup soon\") — because the keeper never asks for or does anything.\n- Instead of a cheerful calm face when any check fails, draw the neutral outline pose with \"Couldn't check your bills.\" — because a quiet face on an overdue day is a lie.\n- Instead of a hollow provenance mark on the Unavailable state, draw the InlineErrorRow glyph — because hollow means only \"on record, not confirmed\".\n- Instead of \"Mark paid\" buttons on the landed BillRow's face, highlight the row and put \"Already paid?\" as a caption that opens its overflow — because BillRow keeps Mark paid in the overflow.\n- Instead of a \"Remove Ollie?\" dialog, remove at once and show the Undo line that says who is affected — because Undo is cheaper than a confirm.\n- Instead of a badge, dot, push or \"check in\" button, draw nothing that asks — because the strip is ambient, and a mood change never sends a push.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- Every mood traces to named records, and the item count in the line matches the mood rule for that frame's date.\n- Calm appears only when every mood input succeeded, and Unavailable can never be mistaken for it.\n- The count reads 11 (HOME A) and 6 (PLACE B) on both the strip and the place file.\n- A guest's pose, caption and line reveal nothing they cannot see.\n- The greyscale and AX5 frames read without loss.\n- After Skip or Remove, Today matches a no-keeper Today, and Remove can be undone.\n- The keeper never sits beside an alert, never appears in a push, and never sends one.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 01-busy-dense · light — HOME A Today on Mon 19 Oct, busy pose, \"Busy week\", full host context, FactCount on its own line.\n2. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 02-on-it · light — \"Pickup soon\", \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow.\"\n3. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 03-busy-three · light — Fri 30 Oct, \"3 things due in the next 7 days.\", with the FourteenDayStrip rows for HOA dues, Comcast and property tax highlighted after the tap.\n4. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 04-needs-you · light — Sat 24 Oct, \"Past due\", envelope pose, the overdue line.\n5. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 05-needs-you-landing · light — Place tab, Bills list scrolled to the Clark Public Utilities BillRow, highlighted, focus on it, \"Already paid?\" caption under it, no buttons on the row face, Back to Today.\n6. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 06-calm · light — Wed 21 Oct, \"Quiet week\", \"Nothing due in the next 7 days.\"; every input succeeded.\n7. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 07-unavailable · light — the bills input failed (calendar and pickup succeeded), so the host receipt stays fully ticked; neutral outline pose, \"Couldn't check your bills.\" with Retry.\n8. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 08-invitation · light — HOME A in week 3, before Ollie was named: silhouette row \"Give your place a keeper\" with Skip.\n9. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 09-skipped · light — slot closed, the Skip InlineUndo line.\n10. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 10-named-return · light — back from naming: busy pose settled, \"Ollie is on Today now.\" as a one-line status under the strip.\n11. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 11-menu-open · light — the four owner menu items.\n12. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 12-hide-submenu · light — the two hide options as a submenu.\n13. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 13-hidden · light — slot closed, \"Keeper hidden until Mon 26 Oct (in 7 days) · Undo\"; inset of the place-file Keeper row with \"Show Ollie on Today\".\n14. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 14-removed-undo · light — HOME A right after Remove keeper: \"Keeper removed for everyone in this household · Undo\", focus on Undo.\n15. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 15-member-view · light — Sam's menu: \"Hide keeper for now\" plus disabled \"Rename\" with its subtitle; guest inset: on it pose, \"Pickup soon\" and the pickup-only line.\n16. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 16-saved-place · light — PLACE B: Pepper, on it pose, \"Pickup soon\", \"Pickup tomorrow.\" with the hollow mark, \"6 on file\". Insets: \"Give this place a keeper\" invitation; \"Keeper removed · Undo\".\n17. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 17-alert-suppressed · light — AQI 118 pinned, no strip.\n18. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 18-loading · light — skeleton at the exact height.\n19. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 19-offline · light — \"Pickup soon · as of 7:04 AM\", desaturated avatar.\n20. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 20-no-place · light — Today with no strip.\n21. f11-keeper-strip · android · 21-busy-dense · light — M3 dropdown menu anchor, 48dp targets, count on its own line.\n22. f11-keeper-strip · web-1440 · 22-busy-dense · light — main column, FactCount trailing in the row, popover menu.\n23. f11-keeper-strip · web-390 · 23-busy-dense · light — bottom tab bar, count on its own line.\n24. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 24-ax5 · light — worst-case name plus the needs you line; avatar on top, everything stacked full width, about 8 lines, Today scrolling.\n25. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 25-greyscale · light — needs you and calm side by side.\n26. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 26-pose-sheet · light — 6 species x 4 poses (labelled with the internal names), plus each species' neutral pose, at 44pt and 88pt.\n27. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 27-busy-dense · dark — dark twin of 01.\n28. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 28-unavailable · dark — dark twin of 07.\n29. f11-keeper-strip · Notes — record the following:\n- Assumptions and omitted states.\n- Invented strings: the captions \"Quiet week\" / \"Pickup soon\" / \"One thing due\" / \"Busy week\" / \"Past due\"; \"3 things due in the next 7 days.\"; \"5 things due in the next 7 days.\"; the needs you line; \"Couldn't check your bills.\"; \"Retry checking your bills\"; \"Retry checking what's due\"; both hide options; \"Keeper hidden until Mon 26 Oct (in 7 days) · Undo\"; \"Show Ollie on Today\"; \"Keeper removed · Undo\"; \"Keeper removed for everyone in this household · Undo\"; \"Already paid?\"; \"Ollie, keeper options\"; \"Shows these on Today.\"; \"Opens the bill.\"; \"Pickup tomorrow.\"; \"Give this place a keeper\"; \"Only Maya can rename, change or remove this keeper.\"; \"6 on file\"; Sam's paid dates; the Sat 24, Wed 21 and Fri 30 frame times; property tax as household-added on Fri 30; Pepper; the guest inset; the 14-day invitation window.\n- Mood rule: calm 0 items · on it exactly 1, not overdue · busy 2 or more, none overdue · needs you any overdue. The line names up to 2; 3 or more reads \"N things due in the next 7 days.\" Pickup counts once, on the day before.\n- Rename rule: only the owner can rename, change species or remove. flows-spec flow-09 has the names reversed (\"Only Sam can rename\").\n- Doc → prompt mapping: relaxed→calm (\"Quiet week\"), attentive→on it (\"Pickup soon\"; the contract's \"Attentive · as of 7:04 AM\" becomes \"Pickup soon · as of 7:04 AM\"), fidgeting→busy (\"Busy week\"), worried→needs you (\"Past due\"). Internal names are never shown. The strings changed per research: rolling 7 days, the thing as the subject, and the glossary's \"Recycling and garbage\". The doc's \"knows N things\" growth line is dropped, because FactCount never says \"knows\". The briefing-screen kicker keeper (f11-keeper-briefing-kicker) is merged away; briefing pushes land on this one Today, so the strip is the only keeper placement.\n- Deviations needing a contract decision:\n  - KeeperStrip on phones puts FactCount on its own line under the mood line so the fact line never truncates. Update the anatomy to: trailing at 1440, own line under 600pt.\n  - The caption beside the name is a week word, not the mood name; the name button carries it as its value, and the mood-line button's label is the fact line.\n  - Unavailable names the failed input (\"Couldn't check your bills.\") when only one failed, per invariant 4.\n  - \"Already paid?\" caption under a highlighted BillRow.\n  - Keeper removal is immediate with InlineUndo per the MERGES decision. Retire the DestructiveConfirm variant \"Remove Ollie? Today goes back to no keeper. You can add one again any time.\" from the contract.\n  - The contract's FactCount place-file example \"14 on file\" is stale. Change it to 11.\n- Open items:\n  - The species list differs from design doc §F11 (otter, owl, fox, heron, cat, dog).\n  - The art may be cut to three species.\n  - Mood inputs differ from design doc §F11: mail counts are not an input, and seeded civic/tax rows are excluded unless the household added them. The doc's single-item \"Tax due in 3 days.\" is now on it, not busy; Fri 30 Oct at HOME A has 3 items. Update the doc.\n  - flows-spec flow-09 step 6 reads \"Recycling tomorrow.\" and step 8 \"Nothing due this week.\"; update to the strings here.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 2: artboards 7-12, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 3: artboards 13-18, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 4: artboards 19-24, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 5: artboard 25, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 6: artboard 26 (pose sheet) alone, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 7: artboards 27-29.",
            "changeLog": [
              "Visible mood captions changed to week words (Quiet week / Pickup soon or One thing due / Busy week / Past due); calm/on it/busy/needs you kept as internal pose names only; offline string now 'Pickup soon · as of 7:04 AM'; new INSTEAD OF line (review major, contract copyRules, glossary)",
              "Added an explicit mood rule (0 / exactly 1 / 2+ / any overdue; names up to 2, else 'N things due in the next 7 days.') and recorded it on Notes (review major)",
              "Replaced the false Fri 30 Oct single-item line with the honest '3 things due in the next 7 days.' (HOA, Comcast, property tax, utilities paid) and gave it its own artboard 03 (review major x2)",
              "Permission-limited rule now covers pose, caption and line; guest inset shows on it pose + 'Pickup soon' (review major, research-findings)",
              "Needs you landing now names its host: Place tab > Bills list scrolled to the Clark row, highlighted, focus, Back to Today; Bills list added to ATTACH (review major)",
              "Removal follows MERGES/flow-09: immediate remove + InlineUndo with consequence prefix, no dialog; DestructiveConfirm artboard dropped and its variant marked 'retire from contract' on Notes (review minor, MERGES, critique)",
              "Accessibility restructured: group 'Ollie' with three ordered elements; the mood-line label is the fact line per contract, week word exposed as the name button's value; deviation recorded (review minor x2)",
