          {
            "id": "f11-keeper-naming",
            "name": "Give your place a keeper (naming)",
            "platforms": [
              "web",
              "ios",
              "android"
            ],
            "isNew": true,
            "frameCount": 23,
            "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components from prompt 00, by exact name.\n\nSCREEN: Give your place a keeper · f11-keeper-naming\n\nTYPE: NEW. This is one sheet with no steps. It opens over whatever screen invoked it, with that screen's real content visible behind the scrim: over Today (invitation, Rename, Change species from the strip menu), over the place file (the Place section row, the read-only mode), or over account Settings (the Keeper row).\n\nATTACH: Today on iOS 393x852 for HOME A, with the keeper invitation row (from the keeper strip project); Today for PLACE B; Today on Android 412x915, web 1440x900 and web 390x844; the Place section of the place file; the account Settings index.\n\nPLATFORMS & VIEWPORTS\n- iOS 393x852 (primary): a sheet with a grabber that opens at the large detent (content height). It scrolls if content exceeds it, with the button row pinned.\n- Android 412x915: an M3 modal bottom sheet.\n- Web 1440x900: a centred modal, 480 wide.\n- Web 390x844: a bottom sheet that grows to full height with the keyboard.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES & HOW PEOPLE ARRIVE: The sheet opens only from a tap. It never opens on its own: not at launch, not on a second open, not in the first session.\n\nEntry points:\n1. The keeper invitation row on Today. The row appears only after a first value moment (a confirmed pickup day or a saved date).\n2. Rename or Change species in the keeper menu on the strip.\n3. The place file's Place section. With no keeper, the FactRow (missing variant) reads \"Give your place a keeper\"; this is the way back after Skip. With a keeper, the FactRow (known variant) shows label \"Keeper\" and value \"Ollie, River otter\". For Maya (owner) it opens Change species mode, which includes the name field. For Sam (member) it opens read-only mode. While the keeper is hidden, the row also carries the text action \"Show Ollie on Today\".\n4. The Keeper row in account Settings, listed per place, so it also serves PLACE B. With no keeper it opens the default sheet; with a keeper it opens Change species mode (owner) or read-only mode (member).\n\nWhat the sheet hands on, by entry:\n- From the Today invitation or the strip menu: the sheet closes to Today, the strip's pose settles into its current state, the status line shows under the strip, and focus moves to the strip's name.\n- From the place file or Settings: the sheet closes back to that screen, the row now reads label \"Keeper\" with value \"Ollie, River otter\", the status line \"Ollie is on Today now.\" shows under the row, and focus moves to that row.\n- Skip returns to Today with the keeper slot closed and the InlineUndo line showing.\n- Close leaves everything as it was.\n- At a later claim, the keeper carries over and the scope sentence changes to the household form.\n\nWHO AND WHEN\n- Maya Chen at HOME A, in week 3, on her iPhone. She checked that recycling and garbage go out tomorrow, then tapped the invitation.\n- Jordan Lee, new at PLACE B, does the same for a saved place.\n- Sam Ortega is a member. He opens the sheet from the place file's Keeper row and can only view it.\n\nTHE ONE JOB: Let someone name a keeper in two taps (an animal, then save), or skip it for good at no cost.\n\nFIRST FIVE SECONDS: The eye lands first on the title, then on the six species tiles, then on the button row. The primary action is \"Name the keeper\". It is enabled once a species is picked.\n\nCONTENT (fixture deltas only; list every invented string on Notes)\n- Title: \"Give your place a keeper\" for HOME A, \"Give this place a keeper\" for PLACE B.\n- Body: \"A small face on Today, so the address feels like somewhere.\"\n- Second line: \"It sums up what's due. You can rename or remove it any time.\"\n- Six tiles, in this order, each with its suggested name:\n  - Octopus: Otto\n  - River otter: Ollie\n  - Great blue heron: Stilt\n  - Red fox: Pepper\n  - Raccoon: Bandit\n  - Douglas squirrel: Doug\n- Each tile shows the species' calm pose and its name.\n- The name field has the visible label \"Keeper's name\", a 24-character limit and a live counter (\"5 / 24\").\n- Scope sentence, exactly:\n  - HOME A: \"Everyone in this household will see this.\" plus \"What it says is based on what each person can see.\"\n  - PLACE B: \"Only you will see this.\"\n- Buttons from the Today invitation: \"Name the keeper\" and \"Skip\", equal.\n- Buttons from the place file or Settings (user-started): only \"Name the keeper\", full width, plus the visible Close in the header.\n- PLACE B delta: Jordan picks Red fox, and the field fills with \"Pepper\".\n- Status lines after save: first naming \"Ollie is on Today now.\"; rename (Maya renames Ollie to Olive) \"Renamed to Olive.\"; change species \"Ollie is a Red fox now.\"\n- Read-only mode (Sam):\n  - Title: \"Ollie\"\n  - Body line: \"Maya named this place's keeper Ollie.\"\n- Worst case: pasting \"Captain Wigglebottom the Third\" keeps \"Captain Wigglebottom the\" (24 characters).\n\nLAYOUT & VISUALIZATION\n- Draw one screen with no steps.\n- Top to bottom: header (the title and a visible Close), the body lines, a 3x2 tile grid, the name field directly below the grid, the scope sentence, then the button row.\n- Button row from the Today invitation: two buttons with identical height, width and type weight.\n  - \"Name the keeper\": filled, primary.700.\n  - \"Skip\": outlined, with a text.secondary-strength border.\n- Button row from the place file or Settings: \"Name the keeper\" alone, full width.\n- Each tile is a target of at least 44pt, with a 56pt pose and a label.\n- The selected tile uses the KindGlyph selected-tile treatment only: a filled radio dot and a bold label. Draw no outline, tick or check badge on selection.\n- Draw the focus ring offset outside the tile, so focus and selection never look alike.\n- Draw no pronouns, traits, colours, quiz or preview carousel.\n- At AX5 or 200% text, the tiles become a single-column list, the sheet scrolls, and the buttons stack full width with \"Name the keeper\" first.\n\nINTERACTION, MOTION & HAPTICS\n- Picking a tile\n  - Picking a tile fills the field with that species' suggested name. Focus stays on the tile.\n  - Tapping the field selects the whole name, so typing replaces it.\n  - Picking another species replaces the name only if it is still an unedited suggestion.\n- Saving\n  - On save, the sheet closes to its host (see the handoff above) and the status line is announced. This is the only feedback: no confetti, no sound.\n  - Play one light haptic tick on iOS and Android, on a successful save only.\n  - Close during saving closes the sheet; the save finishes and its status line appears on the host (or the error appears on the host if it fails).\n  - While saving, Skip is disabled, so a Skip cannot race a save.\n- Skip and Close\n  - Skip appears only when the sheet opens from the Today invitation. It persists on the server. The sheet closes, the Today slot closes, and the InlineUndo line reads \"Skipped. You can add a keeper from your place file. · Undo\".\n  - Close, Escape, Back and swipe-down all leave everything as it was. Swipe-down works only when nothing was typed.\n- Rename mode (from the strip menu)\n  - Title: \"Rename Ollie\"\n  - Content: only the name field, pre-filled\n  - Primary: \"Save name\"\n  - Also: Close\n- Change species mode (strip menu, owner's place-file row, owner's Settings row)\n  - Title: \"Choose a different animal\"\n  - Content: the tiles, with the current species selected, and the name field, keeping \"Ollie\"\n  - A saved name is never replaced by a suggestion in this mode.\n  - Primary: \"Save\"\n  - Also: Close\n- Read-only mode (members)\n  - Title: \"Ollie\"\n  - Body: \"Maya named this place's keeper Ollie.\"\n  - The Ollie tile is shown selected and locked. No name field.\n  - Draw the LockedActionRow \"Only Maya can rename, change or remove this keeper.\" and a single Close.\n- Remove and Hide are handled on the strip's menu, drawn in the keeper strip project: Remove is immediate with an Undo line, no dialog.\n- Motion: use the native sheet transition. The pose settles in 300ms or less. Under Reduce Motion, use a cross-fade and a static pose.\n\nFOUNDATIONS COMPONENTS USED\n- ScopeChip: the footer sentence form, both tiers.\n- KindGlyph: only its selected-tile state (filled radio dot plus bold label), borrowed for the species tiles. The species tile itself (56pt pose plus label) is a new variant to add to the contract; it is not a ChoiceChip.\n- InlineErrorRow: save failed, value kept. Visible button \"Retry\", spoken label \"Retry saving the name\".\n- InlineUndo: Skip.\n- OfflineNotice: form offline.\n- LockedActionRow: read-only mode only.\n- KeeperStrip: the Today landing after save.\n- FactRow: the place-file rows (missing \"Give your place a keeper\"; known label \"Keeper\", value \"Ollie, River otter\") and the Settings Keeper row.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- The sheet has a unique title and traps focus.\n- Focus after closing:\n  - After Close, focus returns to the invoking row.\n  - After Skip, focus moves to the InlineUndo line.\n  - After save from Today or the strip menu, focus moves to the KeeperStrip name. After save from the place file or Settings, focus moves to the updated Keeper row.\n- The tiles are a radio group. Each reads as \"River otter, suggested name Ollie\", with the selected trait. Focus never jumps to the field on its own.\n- The counter is a polite live region, but only at 20 characters and above.\n- Errors sit under the field and say what to do.\n- The save status line is role=status.\n- A disabled \"Name the keeper\" stays focusable, with the hint \"Pick an animal first\".\n- Selection must still read in greyscale, from the dot and the bold label.\n\nCOPY: \"Give your place a keeper\" · \"Give this place a keeper\" · \"A small face on Today, so the address feels like somewhere.\" · \"It sums up what's due. You can rename or remove it any time.\" · \"Keeper's name\" · \"5 / 24\" · \"24 / 24\" · \"Everyone in this household will see this.\" · \"What it says is based on what each person can see.\" · \"Only you will see this.\" · \"Name the keeper\" · \"Skip\" · \"Close\" · \"Pick an animal first\" · \"24 characters is the limit.\" · \"Give it a name, or tap Skip.\" · \"Give it a name, or tap Close.\" · \"Saving…\" · \"We couldn't save that. Your name is still here.\" · \"Retry\" (spoken \"Retry saving the name\") · \"You're offline. You can name it when you're back.\" · \"Ollie\" · \"Keeper\" · \"Ollie, River otter\" · \"Show Ollie on Today\" · \"Maya named this place's keeper Ollie.\" · \"Only Maya can rename, change or remove this keeper.\" · \"Ollie is on Today now.\" · \"Renamed to Olive.\" · \"Ollie is a Red fox now.\" · \"Skipped. You can add a keeper from your place file. · Undo\" · \"Rename Ollie\" · \"Save name\" · \"Choose a different animal\" · \"Save\".\n\nEDGE CASES\n- Too long: after a paste, the counter reads \"24 / 24\" in text.primary with a warning glyph, and the helper reads \"24 characters is the limit.\"\n- Empty or spaces only: the helper reads \"Give it a name, or tap Skip.\" from the Today invitation, or \"Give it a name, or tap Close.\" from every other entry, and the primary is disabled.\n- Emoji count as one character each.\n- Slow network: after 1s, the primary shows \"Saving…\", and the tiles, field and Skip are disabled. Close stays available and does not cancel the save.\n- Save error: InlineErrorRow \"We couldn't save that. Your name is still here.\" with the visible button \"Retry\", and the typed name kept.\n- Offline: OfflineNotice \"You're offline. You can name it when you're back.\" \"Name the keeper\" and \"Skip\" are both disabled with that reason. Close still works.\n- Member (Sam), read-only: opened from the place-file Keeper row or the Settings Keeper row, as described in Read-only mode.\n- PLACE B from Settings: the Keeper row sits under PLACE B's name in account Settings, since a saved place has no per-home settings.\n- After a claim: Change species at the claimed home shows the household scope sentence.\n- A claim that merges into a home that already has a keeper: the claim receipt, not this sheet, says which keeper is kept.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of auto-presenting this on a second open, open it only from a tap after a value moment — because someone checking recycling should not be interrupted by a naming ask.\n- Instead of a grey \"Skip\" link, draw Skip as an outlined button matching \"Name the keeper\" in size and weight — because a decline must be one easy, neutral tap.\n- Instead of \"Not now\" beside the button when the user opened the sheet themselves, show only \"Name the keeper\" and Close — because Close already declines, and \"Not now\" needs a permanent decline beside it.\n- Instead of an outline or focus-coloured ring as the selection, draw a filled radio dot and a bold label — because selection must look different from focus.\n- Instead of moving focus into the field after a pick, keep focus on the tile — because a jump disorients screen-reader users.\n- Instead of confetti, sound, a badge or \"Level 1 keeper\", let the pose settle and show one factual line — because celebration turns a choice into a game.\n- Instead of sending every save to Today, close back to the screen that opened the sheet — because jumping tabs loses the user's place.\n- Instead of \"Ollie will miss you\" on Skip or remove, use plain verbs — because the keeper never uses guilt.\n- Instead of reusing \"Give your place a keeper\" for Sam, draw the read-only \"Ollie\" sheet — because a viewer who can't act should not be asked.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- Naming takes two taps: a species, then save.\n- Skip takes one tap, is permanent, can be undone, and can be reversed later from the place file or Settings.\n- Nothing is gated behind naming.\n- The scope sentence matches the tier exactly.\n- Every save returns to the screen that opened the sheet, with a matching status line.\n- Rename, Change species, read-only and Remove all exist (Remove is drawn on the strip).\n- The sheet never opens on its own.\n- The AX5 and greyscale frames read correctly, and focus and selection look different.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. f11-keeper-naming · ios · 01-otter-picked · light — HOME A from the invitation, River otter selected, \"Ollie\", \"5 / 24\", primary enabled, Skip equal.\n2. f11-keeper-naming · ios · 02-default · light — HOME A, nothing picked, primary disabled.\n3. f11-keeper-naming · ios · 03-name-too-long · light — pasted name cut to 24, helper shown.\n4. f11-keeper-naming · ios · 04-name-empty · light — \"Give it a name, or tap Skip.\"\n5. f11-keeper-naming · ios · 05-saving · light — \"Saving…\"; tiles, field and Skip disabled; Close available.\n6. f11-keeper-naming · ios · 06-save-error · light — InlineErrorRow with the visible \"Retry\", name kept.\n7. f11-keeper-naming · ios · 07-named-landing · light — Today, Mon 19 Oct: busy pose settles; \"Ollie is on Today now.\" drawn as a one-line status under the strip (role=status); focus on the strip name.\n8. f11-keeper-naming · ios · 08-skipped-landing · light — Today with the slot closed and the InlineUndo line.\n9. f11-keeper-naming · ios · 09-saved-place · light — PLACE B: \"Give this place a keeper\", Red fox, \"Pepper\", \"Only you will see this.\"\n10. f11-keeper-naming · ios · 10-member-read-only · light — Sam's \"Ollie\" sheet over the place file, LockedActionRow, single Close.\n11. f11-keeper-naming · ios · 11-rename · light — Rename mode with the keyboard up, \"Olive\" typed.\n12. f11-keeper-naming · ios · 12-change-species · light — Change species mode over the place file, \"Ollie\" kept, Red fox selected.\n13. f11-keeper-naming · ios · 13-change-species-after-claim · light — PLACE B after Jordan claims it: Pepper kept, the scope sentence now reads \"Everyone in this household will see this.\"\n14. f11-keeper-naming · ios · 14-offline · light — OfflineNotice; both buttons disabled with the reason.\n15. f11-keeper-naming · ios · 15-reentry · light — the place-file row \"Give your place a keeper\", the Settings Keeper row, an inset of the sheet footer with \"Name the keeper\" full width and Close in the header, and an inset of the place file after save: Keeper row \"Ollie, River otter\" with \"Ollie is on Today now.\" under it and focus on the row.\n16. f11-keeper-naming · android · 16-otter-picked · light — M3 bottom sheet, 48dp targets.\n17. f11-keeper-naming · web-1440 · 17-otter-picked · light — 480-wide modal over Today; keyboard focus ring on Great blue heron while River otter is selected.\n18. f11-keeper-naming · web-390 · 18-otter-picked · light — bottom sheet.\n19. f11-keeper-naming · ios · 19-ax5 · light — one-column tiles, stacked buttons, scrolling.\n20. f11-keeper-naming · ios · 20-greyscale · light — selection readable without hue.\n21. f11-keeper-naming · ios · 21-otter-picked · dark — dark twin of 01.\n22. f11-keeper-naming · ios · 22-save-error · dark — dark twin of 06.\n23. f11-keeper-naming · Notes — record the following:\n- Assumptions and omitted states.\n- Invented strings: Otto, Stilt, Bandit, Doug; Olive; the first body line; the second body line; the second scope line; \"Keeper's name\"; the mode titles; \"Ollie\" as the read-only title; the Keeper row label and value; \"Show Ollie on Today\"; \"Maya named this place's keeper Ollie.\"; \"Only Maya can rename, change or remove this keeper.\"; \"Give this place a keeper\"; \"24 characters is the limit.\"; both empty-name helpers; \"Saving…\"; \"We couldn't save that. Your name is still here.\"; \"Retry saving the name\"; \"You're offline. You can name it when you're back.\"; the three status lines; the Skip line; the \"Pick an animal first\" hint.\n- Decisions:\n  - Skip is disabled while saving, so a Skip cannot undo a save that then succeeds.\n  - Offline disables both buttons with one reason. The queued \"Will save when you're back online\" is dropped.\n  - Skip exists only from the Today invitation. User-started entries (place file, Settings) show only \"Name the keeper\" plus Close; \"Not now\" is dropped there, per the glossary.\n  - Saves return to the screen that opened the sheet.\n  - The save-error button is InlineErrorRow's \"Retry\" instead of \"Try again\".\n  - Only the owner can rename, change species or remove. flows-spec flow-09 has the names reversed.\n  - Ollie is the River otter per the HOME A fixture \"Ollie (otter)\".\n- Contract additions: the species tile (56pt pose plus label, borrowing KindGlyph's selected-tile treatment) is a new variant to add to the contract. Retire the DestructiveConfirm keeper-removal variant; removal is immediate with Undo.\n- Open items:\n  - This overrides design doc §F11's auto-present on the second Today open; the sheet opens only from a tap. Update the doc.\n  - flows-spec flow-09 step 4 pairs Octopus with \"Ollie\" and step 3 reads \"Only you see this.\"; this prompt uses River otter → Ollie and \"Only you will see this.\" Update the flow.\n  - The doc lists otter, owl, fox, heron, cat and dog.\n  - The species art may be cut to three.\n  - Saved-place naming depends on the claim receipt carrying the keeper.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 2: artboards 7-12, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 3: artboards 13-18, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 4: artboards 19-23.",
            "changeLog": [
