                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "Removing the keeper at HOME A can't be undone, and the confirm dialog never says the household loses the keeper too. The merge decision, flow-09 and the v1 prompt all make keeper removal optimistic with Undo. Where other people are affected, the merge asks for a one-line consequence prefix instead. The prompt swaps that for a dialog with no Undo afterwards, and the dialog copy never mentions Sam.",
                    "evidence": "FINAL-screen-inventory.md MERGES: \"Three destructive confirmation dialogs (remove saved place, remove date, remove keeper) → optimistic delete + Undo everywhere, with a one-line consequence prefix only where someone beyond the actor is affected.\" flows-spec.md flow-09: \"Remove. Optimistic with Undo, and the copy carries no creature emotion.\" prompts-v1/f11-keeper-naming.md: \"Remove confirm: ... — optimistic remove with Undo.\" research-findings.md: \"Removing it is the user's choice and can be undone.\" The prompt says: \"at HOME A the household loses it too, so show DestructiveConfirm 'Remove Ollie? Today goes back to no keeper. You can add one again any time.' with 'Remove keeper' and 'Keep Ollie'.\" No Undo is given for HOME A.",
                    "fix": "After 'Remove keeper' at HOME A, collapse the slot to the InlineUndo line \"Keeper removed · Undo\", the same as PLACE B. Make sure the confirm (or a consequence prefix) names who else is affected, e.g. \"Sam will no longer see Ollie on Today.\" Add a frame after the confirm that shows the Undo line. On Notes, record that the contract's DestructiveConfirm variant sits in tension with the MERGES decision, which said no dialogs."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "major",
