                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The mood inputs differ from the design doc, and Notes doesn't record it. The doc computes mood from dueBills, dueTasks, statusItems and the calendar, including mail ('so the mail half of the mood is real'), and uses a tax deadline as its fidgeting example. The prompt drops mail entirely and leaves seeded civic and tax deadlines out of the mood. Both may be the right call (research limits mood to obligations; HOME A rents), but the doc isn't corrected anywhere.",
                    "evidence": "Design doc §F11: \"Mood, computed in GET /api/hub from already-loaded dueBills, dueTasks, statusItems and the calendar: ... fidgeting ('Tax due in 3 days.') ... Fix the invalid Mail column names at hub.js:221-260 first so the mail half of the mood is real.\" The prompt says: \"Mood comes only from bills, tasks and dates this household added ... Seeded civic deadlines (voter registration, property tax) stay on the 14-day strip and do not move the mood\". The Notes open items list only the species list, the three-species cut and the count.",
                    "fix": "Add a Notes open item: \"Mood inputs differ from design doc §F11: mail counts are not an input, and seeded civic/tax rows are excluded unless the household added them (the doc's 'Tax due in 3 days.' becomes the household-added 'Property tax 2nd half is due in 3 days · Mon 2 Nov.'). Update the doc.\" Also say that at PLACE B the inputs are the dates Jordan added plus pickup (calendar-only, per the inventory's T1 state), not 'this household'."
                  },
