                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The trailing FactCount cannot fit on a 393pt phone row. A 44pt avatar, the name and mood line, and four labelled pips plus the count do not fit in 361pt of content width. The pips alone take about 200pt, which leaves the mood line about 35pt, so Claude Design will either truncate the fact line (forbidden) or improvise a layout. The 128-count edge case makes this worse.",
                    "evidence": "Prompt LAYOUT: \"Trailing: FactCount, with a 44pt minimum target.\" plus CONTENT \"'11 on file' with pips Place · Dates · Money · People\" and EDGE CASES \"A count of 128 on file keeps the pips on one line.\" component-contract.md FactCount: \"one small labelled pip per category that has anything known\".",
                    "fix": "Replace the 'Trailing: FactCount' sentence with: \"On phones (iOS, Android, web-390), FactCount sits on its own line under the mood line, aligned to the text column, left-aligned, with a 44pt-tall target. Only on web-1440 does it sit trailing in the same row.\" Update the AX5 line to \"the avatar sits on top and everything else stacks full width\". Change artboard 01 to show the two-line arrangement."
                  },
