                  {
                    "severity": "major",
                    "issue": "The save handoff is wrong for the place-file and Settings entries. Every save returns to Today and moves focus to the strip, even when the sheet was opened over the place file or Settings, where no strip exists. The user is thrown to another tab.",
                    "evidence": "WHERE: \"A save returns to Today. The strip's pose settles, and the status line 'Ollie is on Today now.' appears.\" ACCESSIBILITY: \"After save, focus moves to the new KeeperStrip name.\" TYPE: \"The read-only mode and the place-file entry open over the place file.\" Entry 4: \"The 'Keeper' row in Settings.\"",
                    "fix": "Split the handoff by entry. From the Today invitation or the strip menu: close to Today, the pose settles, the status line shows, and focus moves to the strip name. From the place file or Settings: close back to that screen, the row now reads label \"Keeper\" with value \"Ollie, River otter\", the status line \"Ollie is on Today now.\" shows under the row, and focus moves to that row. Add an inset of that return to artboard 15."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The iOS medium detent cannot hold the layout. The title, two body lines, a 3x2 grid of 56pt tiles, the field, a two-line scope sentence and the buttons will not fit in about 50% of 852pt, so Claude Design will clip or shrink the content.",
                    "evidence": "PLATFORMS: \"a sheet with a grabber. It opens at medium height and grows to large when the keyboard is up.\" LAYOUT: \"header ..., the body lines, a 3x2 tile grid, the name field ..., the scope sentence, then a button row.\"",
                    "fix": "Change to: \"opens at the large detent (content height), with a grabber\". Alternatively, allow the medium detent to scroll with the button row pinned and scroll padding reserved."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The glossary's rule for \"Not now\" is broken. The place-file and Settings entries pair \"Not now\" with no permanent decline, and it only repeats what Close already does.",
                    "evidence": "CONTENT: \"Buttons from the place file or Settings: 'Name the keeper' and 'Not now'. 'Not now' closes the sheet and stores nothing.\" Glossary: \"Not now — ... Always paired with a permanent decline (Just me / Skip / No thanks).\"",
                    "fix": "For user-started entries (place file, Settings), show only \"Name the keeper\" full width plus the visible Close. Drop \"Not now\" and the helper \"Give it a name, or tap Not now.\" (use \"Give it a name, or tap Close.\")."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "When the owner taps the known place-file row, which mode opens is not defined. The FactRow string is also written as one line, although FactRow's anatomy is a label above a value.",
                    "evidence": "Entry 3: \"With a keeper, the FactRow (known variant) reads 'Keeper · Ollie, River otter'.\" component-contract FactRow: \"Label (bodySmall text.secondary) above the value (body text.primary)\".",
                    "fix": "Write: \"FactRow known: label 'Keeper', value 'Ollie, River otter'. For Maya it opens Change species mode, which includes the name field. For Sam it opens read-only.\" Update COPY to match."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The selected-tile treatment adds a 2px ink outline that the contract's KindGlyph selected state does not have. Since the focus ring is also an outline, the two cues may look alike, and no frame shows focus and selection together to prove they differ.",
                    "evidence": "\"a filled radio dot, a bold label and a 2px ink outline\"; contract KindGlyph: \"selected tile (filled radio dot + bold label, distinct from focus)\". The ARTBOARDS have no focus frame.",
                    "fix": "Drop the 2px ink outline and use only the dot plus the bold label, per the contract. On artboard 17 (web-1440), add: \"keyboard focus ring on Great blue heron while River otter is selected\"."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "Rename and Change species reuse the first-naming status line, which is wrong after a rename. What Close does while a save is in flight is also undefined.",
                    "evidence": "INTERACTION: \"On save, the sheet closes ... and the status line is announced\" (only \"Ollie is on Today now.\" exists). \"Close stays available\" during Saving.",
                    "fix": "Add the status lines \"Renamed to Pepper.\" and \"Ollie is a Red fox now.\" to COPY and Notes. State: \"Close during saving closes the sheet; the save finishes and its status line appears on the host.\""
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The species-to-name mapping contradicts flow-09, which pre-fills \"Ollie\" for Octopus. Notes do not record the discrepancy, and they carry process history that is useless to Claude Design.",
                    "evidence": "flows-spec flow-09 step 4: \"She picks Octopus, and 'Ollie' is pre-filled\". Prompt: \"Octopus: Otto · River otter: Ollie\". Notes: \"(v1 disabled it too; the round-1 draft had kept it live.)\"",
                    "fix": "Under Notes > Open items, add \"flows-spec flow-09 step 4 pairs Octopus with 'Ollie'; this prompt uses River otter → Ollie per the fixture 'Ollie (otter)'. Update the flow.\" Delete the parenthetical v1/round-1 history."
                  },
                  {
                    "severity": "minor",
                    "issue": "The save-error Retry has no stated visible label, only the spoken one, so Claude Design may print the long spoken label on the button.",
                    "evidence": "COPY lists \"Retry saving the name\"; EDGE CASES: \"InlineErrorRow ... with 'Retry saving the name'\". The contract's InlineErrorRow shows the visible \"Retry\", and \"Retry names its target\" is an accessibility rule.",
                    "fix": "Write: \"visible button 'Retry', spoken label 'Retry saving the name'\"."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "clean": false
      }
    ]
  },
